translate chinese strings:

    old "After several weeks of agonizing pain, she finally succumbed to the disease. The fact that her body was so strong only made it worse since it forced Herza to endure the pain for a long time."
    new "After several weeks of agonizing pain, she finally succumbed to the disease. The fact that her body was so strong only made it worse since it forced Herza to endure the pain for a long time.\n在数周令人煎熬的痛苦之后，她最终还是没能扛过这场疾病。她的身体太过强壮，反而让情况更糟——因为这迫使 Herza 承受了很长一段时间的痛苦。"

    old "And that was all time the elders could have used to change their minds too..."
    new "And that was all time the elders could have used to change their minds too...\n而那段时间，本也是长者们可以用来改变主意的……"

    old "It's hard for a person to admit that they're wrong. It's even harder for a group of people to do the same. For them, it was easier to cite tradition and use it to wash their hands of any actual responsibility. And Herza died needlessly for that."
    new "It's hard for a person to admit that they're wrong. It's even harder for a group of people to do the same. For them, it was easier to cite tradition and use it to wash their hands of any actual responsibility. And Herza died needlessly for that.\n一个人很难承认自己错了，一群人就更难做到同样的事。对他们来说，搬出传统、借此撇清自己的实际责任要容易得多。而 Herza 就这样白白死去了。"

    old "Anyway, this particular story was kept secret for a long time because it brings shame to the amazons. It's only resurfaced recently."
    new "Anyway, this particular story was kept secret for a long time because it brings shame to the amazons. It's only resurfaced recently.\n总之，这件事被隐瞒了很久，因为它给 Amazons 带来了耻辱。直到最近才重新浮出水面。"

    old "Well... Maybe now they can learn from their predecessors' mistakes. Do you think Queen Karen would have let the healer help Herza if she was put in the same situation?"
    new "Well... Maybe now they can learn from their predecessors' mistakes. Do you think Queen Karen would have let the healer help Herza if she was put in the same situation?\n嗯……也许现在他们能从先辈的错误中吸取教训了。你觉得如果 Queen Karen 身处同样的境地，她会允许治疗师去救 Herza 吗？"

    old "I'd like to think that Queen Karen would be smart enough to overcome her prejudice and help whoever was put in Herza's position."
    new "I'd like to think that Queen Karen would be smart enough to overcome her prejudice and help whoever was put in Herza's position.\n我愿意相信 Queen Karen 足够聪明，能够克服自己的偏见，去帮助任何处于 Herza 那种处境的人。"

    old "If it was Leena or someone else she cared about I know that she wouldn't repeat the same mistake. If it was someone of a lower rank though... I'm not quite as certain."
    new "If it was Leena or someone else she cared about I know that she wouldn't repeat the same mistake. If it was someone of a lower rank though... I'm not quite as certain.\n如果是 Leena 或她关心的其他人，我知道她不会再犯同样的错误。但如果是个地位更低的人……我就不那么确定了。"

    old "And that's not because I think that Queen Karen wouldn't care. It's just... when you're part of a large group that all adhere to a certain belief it can be hard to oppose them. Even if you disagree, sometimes it's just easier to go with the crowd."
    new "And that's not because I think that Queen Karen wouldn't care. It's just... when you're part of a large group that all adhere to a certain belief it can be hard to oppose them. Even if you disagree, sometimes it's just easier to go with the crowd.\n这并不是因为我觉得 Queen Karen 会不在乎。只是……当你身处一个所有人都信奉某种信念的大群体中时，要反对他们是很难的。即使你不认同，有时随大流反而更省事。"

    old "I get what you're trying to say, [protag]. And, I guess that on a certain level, it does make sense. A society's beliefs can be hard to abandon."
    new "I get what you're trying to say, [protag]. And, I guess that on a certain level, it does make sense. A society's beliefs can be hard to abandon.\n我明白你的意思，[protag]。而且我想，从某种程度上说，这确实有道理。一个社会的信念是很难被舍弃的。"

    old "Still, that's not the way it should be. If something is wrong, it should be changed."
    new "Still, that's not the way it should be. If something is wrong, it should be changed.\n不过，事情本不该如此。如果有什么是错的，就应该去改变它。"

    old "I know that's idealistic, but still... I hope that in time more nagas will become like me and Sylrissa."
    new "I know that's idealistic, but still... I hope that in time more nagas will become like me and Sylrissa.\n我知道这太理想化了，不过……我希望随着时间推移，会有更多的 Nagas 变得像我和 Sylrissa 一样。"

    old "I guess I can hope for that too, as impossible as it seems."
    new "I guess I can hope for that too, as impossible as it seems.\n尽管看起来希望渺茫，我想我也可以抱有这样的期待。"

    old "Enok flexes his muscles. Sometimes I forget that besides being a powerful magic user, he can still hold his own in a brawl using his sheer strength."
    new "Enok flexes his muscles. Sometimes I forget that besides being a powerful magic user, he can still hold his own in a brawl using his sheer strength.\nEnok 绷了绷他的肌肉。有时我会忘记，他除了是一名强大的魔法使用者，还能凭借纯粹的力量在一场肉搏中不落下风。"

    old "Excuse me now, [protag], but I'd like to get some more work done on my little home over there. I want to try building a table and some chairs so I need to go get more wood."
    new "Excuse me now, [protag], but I'd like to get some more work done on my little home over there. I want to try building a table and some chairs so I need to go get more wood.\n先失陪了，[protag]，我想去那边我那间小屋子里再干点活。我想试着做一张桌子和几把椅子，所以得再去弄点木头。"

    old "Sure, good luck with your endeavour, Enok. See you soon."
    new "Sure, good luck with your endeavour, Enok. See you soon.\n好的，祝你顺利，Enok。回头见。"

    old "I'm on my way back to Grimoire after a short reconnaissance mission when I hear a commotion coming from the main gate nearby. I quicken my step and move closer to find Enok being held by two guards!"
    new "I'm on my way back to Grimoire after a short reconnaissance mission when I hear a commotion coming from the main gate nearby. I quicken my step and move closer to find Enok being held by two guards!\n我完成一次短暂的侦察任务，正在返回 Grimoire 的路上，忽然听到附近正门传来一阵骚动。我加快脚步走近，发现 Enok 正被两名守卫抓着！"

    old "Hey! Stop! He's with me!"
    new "Hey! Stop! He's with me!\n喂！住手！他是我的人！"

    old "This one? With you?"
    new "This one? With you?\n就这个？跟你一起的？"

    old "Yes. What happened here?"
    new "Yes. What happened here?\n是的。这里发生什么了？"

    old "He was trying to infiltrate Grimoire and-"
    new "He was trying to infiltrate Grimoire and-\n他企图潜入 Grimoire，而且——"

    old "Infiltrate!? I was coming to meet with Apolimesho and [protag]. I'm one of the people [heshe] recruited to fight at N'Mar! Don't you recognize me?"
    new "Infiltrate!? I was coming to meet with Apolimesho and [protag]. I'm one of the people [heshe] recruited to fight at N'Mar! Don't you recognize me?\n潜入！？我是来见 Apolimesho 和 [protag] 的。我是 [heshe] 招募来去 N'Mar 作战的人之一！你们认不出我吗？"

    old "Oh. I-I suppose that your face does look familiar after all..."
    new "Oh. I-I suppose that your face does look familiar after all...\n哦。我、我想你的脸看起来确实有点眼熟……"

    old "Our apologies. The situation here in the city is tense and they told us to be extra careful, but we've clearly made a terrible mistake."
    new "Our apologies. The situation here in the city is tense and they told us to be extra careful, but we've clearly made a terrible mistake.\n我们很抱歉。城里现在局势紧张，上头让我们格外小心，但我们显然犯了个严重的错误。"

    old "It's alright. We understand that you were just trying to do your job. I'm sure that Enok has already forgiven you both anyway, right Enok?"
    new "It's alright. We understand that you were just trying to do your job. I'm sure that Enok has already forgiven you both anyway, right Enok?\n没关系。我们明白你们只是在履行职责。反正我相信 Enok 已经原谅你们俩了，对吧，Enok？"

    old "Hmph. I suppose."
    new "Hmph. I suppose.\n哼。算是吧。"

    old "I wave my hand, gesturing for Enok to follow me into the city. Once we've left the guards a fair distance behind, I ask the question foremost on my mind."
    new "I wave my hand, gesturing for Enok to follow me into the city. Once we've left the guards a fair distance behind, I ask the question foremost on my mind.\n我挥了挥手，示意 Enok 跟我进城。等我们把守卫远远甩在身后，我才问出那个最想问的问题。"

    old "So what's this about a meeting with me and Apolimesho? This is the first I've heard about it."
    new "So what's this about a meeting with me and Apolimesho? This is the first I've heard about it.\n那么，我和 Apolimesho 要会面是怎么回事？这是我头一次听说。"

    old "Hm. Really? I guess he forgot to tell you then."
    new "Hm. Really? I guess he forgot to tell you then.\n嗯？是吗？那我猜他是忘了告诉你了。"

    old "At that exact moment, I see Apolimesho crossing the main square towards my temporary home. I catch his attention and he changes course to approach us."
    new "At that exact moment, I see Apolimesho crossing the main square towards my temporary home. I catch his attention and he changes course to approach us.\n就在那一刻，我看到 Apolimesho 穿过主广场，朝我临时的住处走来。我引起他的注意，他便改变方向朝我们走来。"

    old "Ah, good. I see that you've already met with Enok. I assume he told you about the meeting?"
    new "Ah, good. I see that you've already met with Enok. I assume he told you about the meeting?\n啊，很好。看来你已经见过 Enok 了。我猜他跟你提过会面的事了吧？"

    old "Well, he told me of a meeting. I still have no idea what this is about."
    new "Well, he told me of a meeting. I still have no idea what this is about.\n嗯，他确实跟我说有个会面。但我还是完全不知道是为了什么。"

    old "Come. Let's go to my room inside the Wizards Guild. I will explain everything there."
    new "Come. Let's go to my room inside the Wizards Guild. I will explain everything there.\n来吧。我们去 Wizards Guild 里我的房间。我会在那里把一切都解释清楚。"

    old "Upon hearing the words 'Wizards Guild', Enok's face lights up. His eyes are positively beaming and the less than subtle smile makes him look like a child that's just won a lifetime supply of Dingirran Chocolate."
    new "Upon hearing the words 'Wizards Guild', Enok's face lights up. His eyes are positively beaming and the less than subtle smile makes him look like a child that's just won a lifetime supply of Dingirran Chocolate.\n一听到 Wizards Guild 这几个字，Enok 的脸就亮了起来。他的眼睛闪闪发光，那毫不掩饰的笑容让他看起来像个刚刚赢得了一辈子都吃不完的 Dingirran Chocolate 的孩子。"

    old "Once we get inside, Apolimesho turns to us and clears his throat before speaking."
    new "Once we get inside, Apolimesho turns to us and clears his throat before speaking.\n进去之后，Apolimesho 转向我们，清了清嗓子，然后开口说话。"

    old "As I am sure you are aware, Enok here is an exceedingly skilled caster..."
    new "As I am sure you are aware, Enok here is an exceedingly skilled caster...\n我相信你们都知道，Enok 这位是一位技艺极其高超的施法者……"

    old "I didn't think it was possible, but somehow Enok's smile manages to grow even bigger. A little more and I don't think his face we'll be able to safely support it."
    new "I didn't think it was possible, but somehow Enok's smile manages to grow even bigger. A little more and I don't think his face we'll be able to safely support it.\n我本来以为不可能，但不知怎的，Enok 的笑容竟然还能咧得更大。再大一点，我怕他的脸都要撑不住了。"

    old "But what is even more interesting to me are his physical abilities-- the fact that he is a battlemage. It's a very odd specialization. I can count the people I know who chose the same path on one hand."
    new "But what is even more interesting to me are his physical abilities-- the fact that he is a battlemage. It's a very odd specialization. I can count the people I know who chose the same path on one hand.\n但更让我感兴趣的是他的体能——他是名战斗法师这一事实。这是个非常罕见的专精方向。我认识的人里选择同样道路的，一只手就数得过来。"

    old "That isn't exactly news to me. It's been clear from the first time that we met that Enok is special. Why is that important?"
    new "That isn't exactly news to me. It's been clear from the first time that we met that Enok is special. Why is that important?\n这对我来说不算什么新鲜事。从我们第一次见面起，Enok 的特别之处就很明显了。这有什么重要的？"

    old "[protag], you're making me blush in front of Apolimesho."
    new "[protag], you're making me blush in front of Apolimesho.\n[protag]，你让我在 Apolimesho 面前脸红了。"

    old "Enok is good, but so is everyone else on my team. It's our combined efforts that makes us such a formidable strike team."
    new "Enok is good, but so is everyone else on my team. It's our combined efforts that makes us such a formidable strike team.\nEnok 很出色，但我队伍里的其他人也一样。正是大家的齐心协力，才让我们成为一支如此强大的突击小队。"

    old "Enok sighs."
    new "Enok sighs.\nEnok 叹了口气。"

    old "And I was really enjoying all of the flattery too. Why'd you have to go and ruin it, [protag]?"
    new "And I was really enjoying all of the flattery too. Why'd you have to go and ruin it, [protag]?\n我还正享受这些恭维呢。你干嘛非得来搅和，[protag]？"

    old "Apolimesho clears his throat and continues, not allowing us to get too far away from the point."
    new "Apolimesho clears his throat and continues, not allowing us to get too far away from the point.\nApolimesho 清了清嗓子，继续往下说，不让我们把话题扯得太远。"

    old "I was curious, so I asked around for more information about Enok and the battlemage specialization..."
    new "I was curious, so I asked around for more information about Enok and the battlemage specialization...\n我很好奇，所以四处打听了一些关于 Enok 和战斗法师这个专精的信息……"

    old "I have a feeling that I'm not going to like where this is heading."
    new "I have a feeling that I'm not going to like where this is heading.\n我有种预感，事情的发展方向不会让我喜欢。"

    old "And my inquiries revealed that battlemages are well known for making use of dark magic whenever they get the chance. It was also brought to my attention that Enok here is no exception. So, tell me Enok, is this information correct? Do you use dark magic?"
    new "And my inquiries revealed that battlemages are well known for making use of dark magic whenever they get the chance. It was also brought to my attention that Enok here is no exception. So, tell me Enok, is this information correct? Do you use dark magic?\n我的调查显示，战斗法师以只要一有机会就使用黑暗魔法而闻名。我还得知，这里的 Enok 也不例外。那么告诉我，Enok，这消息属实吗？你使用黑暗魔法吗？"

    old "I... maybe, sometimes. But it's harmless!"
    new "I... maybe, sometimes. But it's harmless!\n我……也许，偶尔吧。但它是无害的！"

    old "Apolimesho's face becomes furious as he slams his palms on the table. Enok instinctively backs up. I've never seen him afraid of anything before, but he certainly seems terrified now. Not that I can blame him. Even though Apolimesho's anger isn't directed at me, I jumped a bit too."
    new "Apolimesho's face becomes furious as he slams his palms on the table. Enok instinctively backs up. I've never seen him afraid of anything before, but he certainly seems terrified now. Not that I can blame him. Even though Apolimesho's anger isn't directed at me, I jumped a bit too.\nApolimesho 双手猛地拍在桌上，脸上满是怒意。Enok 本能地向后退去。我从没见过他害怕什么，但此刻他显然吓坏了。这也不能怪他。尽管 Apolimesho 的怒火不是冲我来的，我也还是被吓了一跳。"

    old "I lost countless men-- good men-- during 'The Old War' against the demons and Fost. Do either of you even know who Fost was?"
    new "I lost countless men-- good men-- during 'The Old War' against the demons and Fost. Do either of you even know who Fost was?\n在与恶魔和 Fost 对抗的 The Old War 中，我失去了数不清的人——那些都是好人。你们俩有谁知道 Fost 是谁吗？"

    old "Fost was a Death Knight. He used dark magic to summon all of those demons to crush our armies. So much was lost during that war. My Gwendylin..."
    new "Fost was a Death Knight. He used dark magic to summon all of those demons to crush our armies. So much was lost during that war. My Gwendylin...\nFost 是一名 Death Knight。他用黑暗魔法召唤出那些恶魔，来摧毁我们的军队。那场战争让我们失去了太多。我的 Gwendylin……"

    old "Apolimesho has never told me much about his past. Frankly, I'm surprised he's bringing it up now, albeit due to a burst of anger. He doesn't elaborate as to who exactly Gwendylin is but I can tell that she must have been someone very dear to him. Perhaps his daughter or wife?"
    new "Apolimesho has never told me much about his past. Frankly, I'm surprised he's bringing it up now, albeit due to a burst of anger. He doesn't elaborate as to who exactly Gwendylin is but I can tell that she must have been someone very dear to him. Perhaps his daughter or wife?\nApolimesho 从没跟我多讲过他的过去。说真的，我很惊讶他现在会提起这些，尽管是一时怒气所致。他没有细说 Gwendylin 究竟是谁，但我看得出，她一定是他极为珍视的人。也许是他的女儿或妻子？"

    old "Dark magic is forbidden here and in all other magic schools across Aravorn. Did you not think that there was a clear reason for that? Dark magic is dangerous and it corrupts peoples' minds."
    new "Dark magic is forbidden here and in all other magic schools across Aravorn. Did you not think that there was a clear reason for that? Dark magic is dangerous and it corrupts peoples' minds.\n黑暗魔法在这里以及 Aravorn 所有其他魔法学院都是被禁止的。你难道没想过这背后有明确的原因吗？黑暗魔法很危险，它会腐蚀人的心智。"

    old "Apolimesho, sir... with all due respect, I am a naga. I don't react the same way to dark magic as humans do. Nagas have a much higher tolerance for dark magic than other races and--"
    new "Apolimesho, sir... with all due respect, I am a naga. I don't react the same way to dark magic as humans do. Nagas have a much higher tolerance for dark magic than other races and--\nApolimesho 先生……恕我直言，我是 naga。我对黑暗魔法的反应和人类不一样。Nagas 对黑暗魔法的耐受性比其他种族高得多，而且——"

    old "Silence! I won't allow someone practicing dark magic to be a part of our battle against the undead. Have I made myself clear, [protag]?"
    new "Silence! I won't allow someone practicing dark magic to be a part of our battle against the undead. Have I made myself clear, [protag]?\n住口！我不会允许一个修习黑暗魔法的人参与我们对抗亡灵的作战。我说清楚了吗，[protag]？"

    old "What? You would turn your back on your mission and all of the people who are counting on you to succeed for one individual?"
    new "What? You would turn your back on your mission and all of the people who are counting on you to succeed for one individual?\n什么？你会为了一个人，就背弃你的使命和所有指望你成功的人们？"

    old "If the alternative is turning my back on a friend then yes. Without question or hesitation."
    new "If the alternative is turning my back on a friend then yes. Without question or hesitation.\n如果另一个选择是背弃一位朋友，那么是的。毫无疑问，也毫不犹豫。"

    old "I cannot see Enok from where I'm standing, but I imagine that he's at least relieved at my response."
    new "I cannot see Enok from where I'm standing, but I imagine that he's at least relieved at my response.\n从我站的位置看不到 Enok，但我想他听了我的回答后，至少松了口气。"

    old "Wait. What if we found another solution?"
    new "Wait. What if we found another solution?\n等等。如果我们能找到别的解决办法呢？"

    old "An alternative? No. My verdict is final."
    new "An alternative? No. My verdict is final.\n别的办法？不。我的裁决是最终的。"

    old "We can't trust Enok's word, despite how convinced he seems to be of what he's said. Corruption isn't something you're supposed to notice yourself."
    new "We can't trust Enok's word, despite how convinced he seems to be of what he's said. Corruption isn't something you're supposed to notice yourself.\n我们不能相信 Enok 的一面之词，尽管他似乎对自己说的话深信不疑。腐化这种东西，本来就不是你自己能察觉到的。"

    old "I might have a solution."
    new "I might have a solution.\n我也许有个办法。"

    old "What kind of solution?"
    new "What kind of solution?\n什么样的办法？"

    old "What if I brought you incontrovertible proof that I am immune to the side effects of dark magic? Would that convince you to let me stay?"
    new "What if I brought you incontrovertible proof that I am immune to the side effects of dark magic? Would that convince you to let me stay?\n如果我给你带来无可辩驳的证据，证明我对黑暗魔法的副作用免疫呢？那样能说服你让我留下吗？"

    old "And what that proof might be?"
    new "And what that proof might be?\n那又会是什么样的证据呢？"

    old "Have you ever heard of Divine Juice?"
    new "Have you ever heard of Divine Juice?\n你听说过 Divine Juice 吗？"

    old "I'm an alchemist and a rather skilled one at that. Of course I've heard of Divine Juice. Now, what does that have to do with-- oh, I see."
    new "I'm an alchemist and a rather skilled one at that. Of course I've heard of Divine Juice. Now, what does that have to do with-- oh, I see.\n我是炼金术师，而且技艺相当娴熟。我当然听说过 Divine Juice。那么，这跟……哦，我明白了。"

    old "Divine Juice, huh? I know I've heard of it before, but it might take me a minute to recall the information."
    new "Divine Juice, huh? I know I've heard of it before, but it might take me a minute to recall the information.\nDivine Juice，嗯？我知道我以前听说过，但可能要花点时间才能回想起来。"

    old "Well, being a [pCharProf], I can safely say I've never heard of Divine Juice before. What is it?"
    new "Well, being a [pCharProf], I can safely say I've never heard of Divine Juice before. What is it?\n嗯，作为一个 [pCharProf]，我可以肯定地说，我以前从没听说过 Divine Juice。它是什么？"

    old "Enok opens his mouth to speak but, once he notices that Apolimesho has done the same, he stops and allows Apolimesho to do the explaining."
    new "Enok opens his mouth to speak but, once he notices that Apolimesho has done the same, he stops and allows Apolimesho to do the explaining.\nEnok 张嘴想说话，但一看到 Apolimesho 也开了口，他便停了下来，让 Apolimesho 来解释。"

    old "Divine Juice is a concentrated version of Divine Essence. It's the purest thing you can hope to find here in Aravorn. It's also a very rare and valuable alchemy ingredient. While it has several notable properties, the one that suits our purposes is that it reacts to demons and dark magic."
    new "Divine Juice is a concentrated version of Divine Essence. It's the purest thing you can hope to find here in Aravorn. It's also a very rare and valuable alchemy ingredient. While it has several notable properties, the one that suits our purposes is that it reacts to demons and dark magic.\nDivine Juice 是 Divine Essence 的浓缩形态。它是你在 Aravorn 这里所能找到的最纯净之物。它同时也是一种非常稀有、珍贵的炼金原料。它有若干显著特性，其中适合我们用途的一点是：它会对恶魔和黑暗魔法产生反应。"

    old "So you're saying that it can be used to test for dark magic?"
    new "So you're saying that it can be used to test for dark magic?\n所以你是说，它能用来检测黑暗魔法？"

    old "Exactly. If something, an item, a place, or even your body, is corrupted by dark magic, the juice will react to it. The stronger the corruption, the stronger the Divine Juice's reaction."
    new "Exactly. If something, an item, a place, or even your body, is corrupted by dark magic, the juice will react to it. The stronger the corruption, the stronger the Divine Juice's reaction.\n没错。如果某样东西——一件物品、一个地方，甚至你的身体——被黑暗魔法腐蚀了，Divine Juice 就会对它产生反应。腐化越严重，Divine Juice 的反应就越强烈。"

    old "Interesting. So, if you use this Divine Juice on Enok you'll be able to tell if he's been corrupted by dark magic or not?"
    new "Interesting. So, if you use this Divine Juice on Enok you'll be able to tell if he's been corrupted by dark magic or not?\n有意思。那么，如果你把这个 Divine Juice 用在 Enok 身上，你就能判断出他有没有被黑暗魔法腐蚀了？"

    old "Yes. That should be the case."
    new "Yes. That should be the case.\n是的。应该是这样。"

    old "I imagine that the Guild has some Divine Juice on hand, correct?"
    new "I imagine that the Guild has some Divine Juice on hand, correct?\n我想 Guild 里应该备有 Divine Juice 吧？"

    old "Naturally. I even have some I made myself hidden away in a safe place. I distilled it using some archangel feathers a few months ago. I must say, it came out splendidly. I don't mean to sound egotistical, but I truly believe that it is the highest quality Divine Juice I've ever the pleasure of laying my eyes on."
    new "Naturally. I even have some I made myself hidden away in a safe place. I distilled it using some archangel feathers a few months ago. I must say, it came out splendidly. I don't mean to sound egotistical, but I truly believe that it is the highest quality Divine Juice I've ever the pleasure of laying my eyes on.\n自然。我自己也做了一些，藏在一个安全的地方。几个月前，我用一些大天使的羽毛把它蒸馏了出来。不得不说，成品极佳。我并不想显得自大，但我真心认为，这是我有幸亲眼见过的品质最高的 Divine Juice。"

    old "He strokes his beard happily at the memory before eventually realizing that he's gone off on a tangent."
    new "He strokes his beard happily at the memory before eventually realizing that he's gone off on a tangent.\n他回想着，愉快地捋了捋胡子，随后才意识到自己扯远了。"

    old "Ahem. Forgive me. I let my enthusiasm carry me away. Please continue, Enok."
    new "Ahem. Forgive me. I let my enthusiasm carry me away. Please continue, Enok.\n咳咳。抱歉。我一时激动，扯远了。请继续，Enok。"

    old "Well, I could take the 'test' now if you want, but I'd like to do this as thoroughly as possible. So..."
    new "Well, I could take the 'test' now if you want, but I'd like to do this as thoroughly as possible. So...\n嗯，如果你想的话，我现在就可以做这个测试，但我想尽量做得彻底一些。所以……"

    old "I'll go to the Everburn Mountains, kill some hellhounds, cook them, eat them, and then come back to take the test!"
    new "I'll go to the Everburn Mountains, kill some hellhounds, cook them, eat them, and then come back to take the test!\n我要去 Everburn Mountains，杀掉几只地狱犬，把它们煮了吃掉，然后再回来做测试！"

    old "Uh, Enok, I'm not sure it's such a good idea-"
    new "Uh, Enok, I'm not sure it's such a good idea-\n呃，Enok，我不确定这是个好主意——"

    old "Hmm. It is an interesting proposition. If, after doing what you said, the Divine Juice still won't react to your presence, then I'll have no choice but to accept the fact that you are capable of absorbing dark magic in high quantities without any negative side effects."
    new "Hmm. It is an interesting proposition. If, after doing what you said, the Divine Juice still won't react to your presence, then I'll have no choice but to accept the fact that you are capable of absorbing dark magic in high quantities without any negative side effects.\n嗯。这是个有趣的提议。如果你照你说的做了之后，Divine Juice 仍然不会对你的存在产生反应，那我就只能接受这一事实：你能够大量吸收黑暗魔法而不产生任何负面副作用。"

    old "Hold on! Wait just a moment. Don't I get a say in this?"
    new "Hold on! Wait just a moment. Don't I get a say in this?\n等一下！稍等一下。这件事我就没有发言权吗？"

    old "Of course, [protag]. What are your concerns?"
    new "Of course, [protag]. What are your concerns?\n当然有，[protag]。你有什么顾虑？"

    old "First of all, the Everburn Mountains aren't exactly close by. It'd take up time we don't really have to get there. Secondly, kill some hellhounds, cook their meat, and eat them? I'm sorry, but that's... just insane."
    new "First of all, the Everburn Mountains aren't exactly close by. It'd take up time we don't really have to get there. Secondly, kill some hellhounds, cook their meat, and eat them? I'm sorry, but that's... just insane.\n首先，Everburn Mountains 可不算近。去那里会耗费我们本就不宽裕的时间。其次，杀几只地狱犬，煮它们的肉，然后吃掉？抱歉，但那……简直疯了。"

    old "I'm going to be the only one who eats the Hellhound meat, [protag]. For you, it'd probably be deadly."
    new "I'm going to be the only one who eats the Hellhound meat, [protag]. For you, it'd probably be deadly.\n吃地狱犬肉的只有我一个，[protag]。对你来说，那多半是致命的。"

    old "I wasn't talking about the eating part! The problem is killing them! Hellhounds are dangerous beasts, you know?"
    new "I wasn't talking about the eating part! The problem is killing them! Hellhounds are dangerous beasts, you know?\n我说的不是吃那部分！问题是杀掉它们！地狱犬可是危险的野兽，你知道吗？"

    old "You probably don't need to go all the way to Everburn. Hellhound sightings are fairly common in the area around Hammerhands. They're not as strong as the hellhounds you find in Everburn, but they're still imbued with dark magic so eating their meat would still work for the test."
    new "You probably don't need to go all the way to Everburn. Hellhound sightings are fairly common in the area around Hammerhands. They're not as strong as the hellhounds you find in Everburn, but they're still imbued with dark magic so eating their meat would still work for the test.\n你大概不必跑那么远去 Everburn。在 Hammerhands 一带，目击地狱犬是相当常见的事。它们虽然没有 Everburn 那边的地狱犬那么强，但同样浸染着黑暗魔法，所以吃它们的肉照样能用来做测试。"

    old "Sorry, Apolimesho, but I'm not willing to waste precious time doing this stupid test. Enok is a valuable member of my team. He stays and that's that."
    new "Sorry, Apolimesho, but I'm not willing to waste precious time doing this stupid test. Enok is a valuable member of my team. He stays and that's that.\n抱歉，Apolimesho，但我不愿意把宝贵的时间浪费在这个愚蠢的测试上。Enok 是我队伍里重要的一员。他留下，就这么定了。"

    old "If you want to test his resistance to dark magic, that's fine but do it in a way that doesn't require us running all around Aravorn."
    new "If you want to test his resistance to dark magic, that's fine but do it in a way that doesn't require us running all around Aravorn.\n如果你想测试他对黑暗魔法的抵抗力，那没问题，但请用一种不需要我们在 Aravorn 到处奔波的方式。"

    old "Ah, but..."
    new "Ah, but...\n啊，可是……"

    old "Apolimesho sighs."
    new "Apolimesho sighs.\nApolimesho 叹了口气。"

    old "I guess you're probably right. It would be silly to waste time when we already have such pressing matters to attend to. I still want to test him with the Divine Juice though. It'll just have to be after he casts a dark magic spell instead."
    new "I guess you're probably right. It would be silly to waste time when we already have such pressing matters to attend to. I still want to test him with the Divine Juice though. It'll just have to be after he casts a dark magic spell instead.\n我想你说得大概没错。既然已经有这么紧迫的事情要处理，再浪费时间确实很愚蠢。不过我还是想用 Divine Juice 测试他。只是得改成等他施放一个黑暗魔法之后再进行。"

    old "I'm ready anytime you want to do it. Even now."
    new "I'm ready anytime you want to do it. Even now.\n你什么时候想做，我都准备好了。现在也行。"

    old "Good, at least this will be quick."
    new "Good, at least this will be quick.\n好，至少这样会很快。"

    old "Follow me then, please."
    new "Follow me then, please.\n那么，请跟我来。"

    old "I wait, alone, in Apolimesho's room while they perform the test. They didn't ask me to follow and, honestly, I have very little interest in seeing Apolimesho's surprised face when he sees that Enok really is immune. Because Enok is immune, right?"
    new "I wait, alone, in Apolimesho's room while they perform the test. They didn't ask me to follow and, honestly, I have very little interest in seeing Apolimesho's surprised face when he sees that Enok really is immune. Because Enok is immune, right?\n他们去做测试时，我一个人待在 Apolimesho 的房间里等候。他们没有叫我跟着去，而说真的，我也没什么兴趣去看 Apolimesho 发现 Enok 真的免疫时那副惊讶的表情。因为 Enok 是免疫的，对吧？"

    old "The longer they take, the more I end up doubting myself."
    new "The longer they take, the more I end up doubting myself.\n他们拖得越久，我就越怀疑自己。"

    old "Luckily, a few minutes later, I hear footsteps and look in the direction of the door. As they enter, I notice that Apolimesho seems visibly embarrassed. He is the first to speak."
    new "Luckily, a few minutes later, I hear footsteps and look in the direction of the door. As they enter, I notice that Apolimesho seems visibly embarrassed. He is the first to speak.\n幸运的是，几分钟后，我听到了脚步声，便朝门口看去。他们进来时，我注意到 Apolimesho 显然有些难为情。他先开了口。"

    old "So, it seems that what Enok was saying is actually true. He really is capable of using dark magic without consequences."
    new "So, it seems that what Enok was saying is actually true. He really is capable of using dark magic without consequences.\n那么，看来 Enok 说的都是真的。他真的能够使用黑暗魔法而不受任何影响。"

    old "Told you so."
    new "Told you so.\n我早跟你说了吧。"

    old "Of course, it wasn't exactly an exhaustive test so I might ask you to come back again in future so we can gather more data about this peculiar resistance to dark magic you nagas have. For now though, you have my blessing, [protag]. Enok can remain on your team."
    new "Of course, it wasn't exactly an exhaustive test so I might ask you to come back again in future so we can gather more data about this peculiar resistance to dark magic you nagas have. For now though, you have my blessing, [protag]. Enok can remain on your team.\n当然，这算不上一次彻底的测试，所以将来我也许还会请你再来，好让我们收集更多关于你们 Nagas 这种奇特黑暗魔法抗性的数据。不过眼下，我同意了，[protag]。Enok 可以留在你的队伍里。"

    old "We politely depart from Apolimesho and begin walking out of the Wizards Guild."
    new "We politely depart from Apolimesho and begin walking out of the Wizards Guild.\n我们礼貌地向 Apolimesho 告辞，然后开始走出 Wizards Guild。"

    old "Pfft. Hahahaha!"
    new "Pfft. Hahahaha!\n噗。哈哈哈哈哈！"

    old "What's so funny?"
    new "What's so funny?\n有什么好笑的？"

    old "I was just thinking... The archwizard. If he knew about Bambara he'd have a heart attack."
    new "I was just thinking... The archwizard. If he knew about Bambara he'd have a heart attack.\n我只是在想……那位大法师。要是他知道 Bambara 的事，非得心脏病发作不可。"

    old "Who?"
    new "Who?\n谁？"

    old "That witch living in the swamps, I told you about her, remember? She is a human and she can definitely use dark magic better than me. Without consequences, too."
    new "That witch living in the swamps, I told you about her, remember? She is a human and she can definitely use dark magic better than me. Without consequences, too.\n就是住在沼泽里的那个女巫，我跟你说过她，记得吗？她是人类，而且用起黑暗魔法来肯定比我厉害。同样也没有任何后果。"

    old "I'm still not entirely convinced that this person is real. Or that Bambara is an actual name. Still, it's not like I'm going to argue about it with Enok."
    new "I'm still not entirely convinced that this person is real. Or that Bambara is an actual name. Still, it's not like I'm going to argue about it with Enok.\n我仍然不太相信这个人真的存在。也不太相信 Bambara 是个真名。不过，我倒也没打算为此跟 Enok 争辩。"

    old "Well, I hope you aren't disappointed that you don't get to go hunting hellhounds."
    new "Well, I hope you aren't disappointed that you don't get to go hunting hellhounds.\n嗯，我希望你没因为去不成猎地狱犬而感到失望。"

    old "I must confess that I'd have liked to try that. In case you didn't already guess, my idea was mostly an excuse to try some new forbidden recipes I found in a book that was apparently written by a demon who liked cooking."
    new "I must confess that I'd have liked to try that. In case you didn't already guess, my idea was mostly an excuse to try some new forbidden recipes I found in a book that was apparently written by a demon who liked cooking.\n我得承认，我本来挺想试试的。也许你已经猜到了，我的主意主要是个借口，想尝试一些新的禁忌食谱——那是我在一本书里找到的，那本书显然是一个喜欢烹饪的恶魔写的。"

    old "I knew it!"
    new "I knew it!\n我就知道！"

    old "It was a pretty crazy idea in retrospect. I think you made the right call."
    new "It was a pretty crazy idea in retrospect. I think you made the right call.\n现在回想起来，那主意确实挺疯狂的。我觉得你做得对。"

    old "Even though he says that, he still seems a little disappointed."
    new "Even though he says that, he still seems a little disappointed.\n尽管他这么说，看起来还是有点失望。"

    old "I'm sorry Enok, but for now we have more important things to think about."
    new "I'm sorry Enok, but for now we have more important things to think about.\n抱歉，Enok，但眼下我们有更重要的事情要考虑。"

    old "I understand, [protag]. Maybe when everything is taken care of at N'Mar we can revisit the idea."
    new "I understand, [protag]. Maybe when everything is taken care of at N'Mar we can revisit the idea.\n我理解，[protag]。也许等 N'Mar 那边的事情都处理完了，我们可以再考虑这个主意。"

    old "I'm still not sure I want to, but I go ahead and agree for now to make Enok happy."
    new "I'm still not sure I want to, but I go ahead and agree for now to make Enok happy.\n我其实还是不太想，但为了哄 Enok 开心，我暂且先答应了。"

    old "I give up and let out a long sigh."
    new "I give up and let out a long sigh.\n我放弃了，长长地叹了口气。"

    old "Of course the one thing that both Enok and Apolimesho ended up agreeing on would be something this stupid. I don't exactly feel like arguing with them though."
    new "Of course the one thing that both Enok and Apolimesho ended up agreeing on would be something this stupid. I don't exactly feel like arguing with them though.\nEnok 和 Apolimesho 最终达成一致的，偏偏就是这种蠢事。不过我也实在懒得再跟他们争了。"

    old "I guess we can do it, but only when I have the time, understand? Until then, nobody can say anything about Enok being on my team, understood?"
    new "I guess we can do it, but only when I have the time, understand? Until then, nobody can say anything about Enok being on my team, understood?\n我想这事可以做，但只能等我有时间的时候，明白吗？在那之前，谁也不能对 Enok 留在我队里说三道四，听明白了吗？"

    old "Very well. I agree to your condition."
    new "Very well. I agree to your condition.\n很好。我同意你的条件。"

    old "Good. We'll contact you again when we're ready to do that test."
    new "Good. We'll contact you again when we're ready to do that test.\n好。等我们准备好做那个测试时，会再联系你的。"

    old "Enok and I make the preparations to travel to Hammerhands in order to hunt minor hellhounds."
    new "Enok and I make the preparations to travel to Hammerhands in order to hunt minor hellhounds.\nEnok 和我开始为前往 Hammerhands 猎杀低级地狱犬做准备。"

    old "I still can't believe I agreed to go along with this crazy plan. It'd be one thing if I seriously thought he wanted to go solely to prove he's immune to dark magic, but his idea was so specific I feel like he has ulterior motives."
    new "I still can't believe I agreed to go along with this crazy plan. It'd be one thing if I seriously thought he wanted to go solely to prove he's immune to dark magic, but his idea was so specific I feel like he has ulterior motives.\n我还是不敢相信自己竟同意了这个疯狂的计划。如果我真以为他只是想证明自己对黑暗魔法免疫，那倒还说得过去，可他的主意实在太具体了，让我觉得他另有所图。"

    old "Enok, be honest with me, is there any other reason why you wanted to do this? Besides proving that you can use dark magic without consequences to Apolimesho, of course."
    new "Enok, be honest with me, is there any other reason why you wanted to do this? Besides proving that you can use dark magic without consequences to Apolimesho, of course.\nEnok，跟我说实话，你想做这件事，除了向 Apolimesho 证明你能无后果地使用黑暗魔法之外，还有别的理由吗？"

    old "Uh? No? That is absolutely the only reason. Why do you ask?"
    new "Uh? No? That is absolutely the only reason. Why do you ask?\n呃？没有啊？绝对只有这一个理由。你为什么这么问？"

    old "W-what?"
    new "W-what?\n怎、怎么？"

    old "Is it just me or are you getting worse at lying as time passes?"
    new "Is it just me or are you getting worse at lying as time passes?\n是我的错觉，还是你的撒谎水平随着时间越来越差了？"

    old "I mean, normally, the more someone does something, the better they get at it, but in this case... You're so terrible. Like, really, really bad. I don't understand how you can be so awful at it."
    new "I mean, normally, the more someone does something, the better they get at it, but in this case... You're so terrible. Like, really, really bad. I don't understand how you can be so awful at it.\n我的意思是，一般说来，一件事做得越多就越熟练，可你这情况……你实在太差了。真的，特别特别差。我都不明白你怎么能烂成这样。"

    old "How rude."
    new "How rude.\n真没礼貌。"

    old "Come on, Enok? Can you really stand there and tell me you aren't lying to me?"
    new "Come on, Enok? Can you really stand there and tell me you aren't lying to me?\n得了吧，Enok。你真能站在这儿跟我说你没有在骗我？"

    old "That's what I thought. But why lie in the first place? I think about it for a few seconds before realizing that the answer is really obvious and really dumb."
    new "That's what I thought. But why lie in the first place? I think about it for a few seconds before realizing that the answer is really obvious and really dumb.\n我想也是。可你一开始为什么要撒谎呢？我想了几秒钟，才意识到答案既明显又愚蠢。"

    old "Please don't tell me this is about cooking..."
    new "Please don't tell me this is about cooking...\n拜托别告诉我，这跟做饭有关……"

    old "Why aren't you talking?"
    new "Why aren't you talking?\n你为什么不说话？"

    old "You told me not to tell you that it was about cooking."
    new "You told me not to tell you that it was about cooking.\n是你叫我别告诉你这事跟做饭有关的。"

    old "If you read that book, you'd understand! The description of that hellhound pot roast... It sounded so good, [protag]. My mouth got all watery just reading it!"
    new "If you read that book, you'd understand! The description of that hellhound pot roast... It sounded so good, [protag]. My mouth got all watery just reading it!\n你要是读了那本书就明白了！那道地狱犬炖烤肉的描述……听起来太香了，[protag]。光是读着，我口水都要流下来了！"

    old "Then again, it's probably best that you don't read about it since eating it would probably instantly kill you. Or drive you insane."
    new "Then again, it's probably best that you don't read about it since eating it would probably instantly kill you. Or drive you insane.\n不过话说回来，你最好还是别去读它，因为吃下那东西多半会立刻要了你的命。或者让你发疯。"

    old "In that case it might be worth it though. Hmm..."
    new "In that case it might be worth it though. Hmm...\n不过那样的话，也许还挺值的。嗯……"

    old "That's it."
    new "That's it.\n够了。"

    old "What!? But-"
    new "What!? But-\n什么！？可是——"

    old "Enok! If you can prove your theory to Apolimesho without having us travel all the way to Hammerhands and spend hours tracking and hunting hellhounds, that is what you're going to do!"
    new "Enok! If you can prove your theory to Apolimesho without having us travel all the way to Hammerhands and spend hours tracking and hunting hellhounds, that is what you're going to do!\nEnok！如果你能在不让我们大老远跑去 Hammerhands、再花好几个小时追踪猎杀地狱犬的情况下，向 Apolimesho 证明你的理论，那你就得那么做！"

    old "Enok pouts and looks at me with a set of hurt eyes. The expression is a little too dramatic though so I know he's just trying to get me to change my mind. He's not actually hurt, at least, not to the degree he'd like me to believe."
    new "Enok pouts and looks at me with a set of hurt eyes. The expression is a little too dramatic though so I know he's just trying to get me to change my mind. He's not actually hurt, at least, not to the degree he'd like me to believe.\nEnok 撅起嘴，用一双委屈的眼睛看着我。不过那表情有点太夸张了，所以我知道他只是想让我改变主意。他并没有真的受伤，至少没到他希望我相信的那种程度。"

    old "Not working."
    new "Not working.\n这招没用。"

    old "All right, all right. I guess those hellhounds will still be there after we finish up our business at N'Mar. I'll just have to go then."
    new "All right, all right. I guess those hellhounds will still be there after we finish up our business at N'Mar. I'll just have to go then.\n好吧，好吧。我想等我们在 N'Mar 把事情办完之后，那些地狱犬应该还在那儿。到时候我再去就是了。"

    old "And I'd gladly accompany you at that time, assuming you still want my help."
    new "And I'd gladly accompany you at that time, assuming you still want my help.\n到那时我也很乐意陪你去，前提是你还需要我帮忙。"

    old "I'd like that."
    new "I'd like that.\n那我很乐意。"

    old "I chat with Enok a bit more before taking my leave. I know he would have liked it if I humored him and went on this crazy mission, but it really is a waste of time that we can't really afford right now."
    new "I chat with Enok a bit more before taking my leave. I know he would have liked it if I humored him and went on this crazy mission, but it really is a waste of time that we can't really afford right now.\n我和 Enok 又聊了一会儿，然后告辞离开。我知道如果我顺着他的意思、陪他去干这趟疯狂的差事，他会很高兴，但那真的是我们眼下负担不起的时间浪费。"

    old "He'll just have to patiently wait until we've finished our main mission at N'Mar."
    new "He'll just have to patiently wait until we've finished our main mission at N'Mar.\n他只能耐心等到我们在 N'Mar 完成主要任务了。"

    old "I let out a sigh and then give in."
    new "I let out a sigh and then give in.\n我叹了口气，然后还是让步了。"

    old "I'm going to need some kind of reward for putting up with this. And I obviously can't eat hellhound meat so, if you want my help, you're going to owe me dinner for this, got it?"
    new "I'm going to need some kind of reward for putting up with this. And I obviously can't eat hellhound meat so, if you want my help, you're going to owe me dinner for this, got it?\n要我忍受这些，总得给我点报酬。而且我显然不能吃地狱犬肉，所以，如果你想让我帮忙，你就得因此欠我一顿晚饭，明白吗？"

    old "Oh! I would love to cook dinner for you! That little spot near the river is so lovely at night. You can see the stars, hear the crickets. It's very romantic--"
    new "Oh! I would love to cook dinner for you! That little spot near the river is so lovely at night. You can see the stars, hear the crickets. It's very romantic--\n哦！我很乐意给你做晚饭！河边那个小地方，晚上美极了。你能看到星星，听到蟋蟀的叫声。特别浪漫——"

    old "Enok stops as if to think about what he just said."
    new "Enok stops as if to think about what he just said.\nEnok 停了下来，仿佛在回想自己刚才说的话。"

    old "N-not that it would be a romantic dinner, of course! I was just saying!"
    new "N-not that it would be a romantic dinner, of course! I was just saying!\n当、当然不是说那会是一顿浪漫晚餐！我只是随口一说！"

    old "I smile at him and he cautiously smiles back. I don't push the topic any further. Instead, I notice that he's carrying a bag that looks like it's stuffed with various books."
    new "I smile at him and he cautiously smiles back. I don't push the topic any further. Instead, I notice that he's carrying a bag that looks like it's stuffed with various books.\n我对他笑了笑，他也小心翼翼地回以一笑。我没有再继续这个话题。转而，我注意到他背着一个包，里面像是塞满了各种书。"

    old "Do you have the recipe book with you?"
    new "Do you have the recipe book with you?\n你把那本食谱带在身上了吗？"

    old "Yes! Here, take a look. Page 102. Hellhound Pot Roast."
    new "Yes! Here, take a look. Page 102. Hellhound Pot Roast.\n带了！来，你看看。第 102 页。Hellhound Pot Roast。"

    old "He digs around in his bag for a moment before pulling out the right book and handing it over to me."
    new "He digs around in his bag for a moment before pulling out the right book and handing it over to me.\n他在包里翻找了一会儿，然后掏出那本正确的书递给我。"

    old "Wanting to see what the fuss is all about, I end up reading the recipe as we travel towards Hammerhands. Between the description and the drawing of the dish, I can kind of understand why Enok wants to try it so badly."
    new "Wanting to see what the fuss is all about, I end up reading the recipe as we travel towards Hammerhands. Between the description and the drawing of the dish, I can kind of understand why Enok wants to try it so badly.\n出于好奇，我想看看这究竟有什么好大惊小怪的，于是在前往 Hammerhands 的路上读起了那份食谱。看到那道菜的描述和插图，我多少能理解 Enok 为什么那么想尝一尝了。"

    old "I just wish I could eat it too."
    new "I just wish I could eat it too.\n我只是希望自己也能吃到。"

    old "You really do enjoy cooking, don't you? You sure seem to have a lot of books on the subject."
    new "You really do enjoy cooking, don't you? You sure seem to have a lot of books on the subject.\n你真的很喜欢烹饪，对吧？关于这个，你的书可真不少。"

    old "Oh, not all of these books are recipe books. I do like cooking, but I also just like reading in general. I'll read any book I can get my hands on."
    new "Oh, not all of these books are recipe books. I do like cooking, but I also just like reading in general. I'll read any book I can get my hands on.\n哦，这些书并不都是食谱。我确实喜欢烹饪，但我也只是单纯喜欢阅读。只要能弄到手的书，我都会读。"

    old "Back when I was being a 'bad naga', I used to take all of the books we'd find in the caravans we assaulted. None of the other nagas were really interested in them either so I didn't have to worry about sharing them. I got to keep them all to myself."
    new "Back when I was being a 'bad naga', I used to take all of the books we'd find in the caravans we assaulted. None of the other nagas were really interested in them either so I didn't have to worry about sharing them. I got to keep them all to myself.\n想当年我还是个坏 naga 的时候，我们袭击商队，凡是在车队里找到的书，我都会拿走。其他 naga 对书也都没什么兴趣，所以我不用担心要跟人分享，可以全据为己有。"

    old "Anyway, because of that I ended up reading about all sorts of things and decided that cooking seemed like a worthwhile art to pursue."
    new "Anyway, because of that I ended up reading about all sorts of things and decided that cooking seemed like a worthwhile art to pursue.\n总之，正因如此，我最后读到了各种五花八门的东西，并且认定烹饪似乎是一门值得钻研的技艺。"

    old "In general, nagas don't have a very developed sense of taste. Most of my companions were content just eating raw meat. Of course, that's probably mostly due to the fact that they never bothered trying anything else."
    new "In general, nagas don't have a very developed sense of taste. Most of my companions were content just eating raw meat. Of course, that's probably mostly due to the fact that they never bothered trying anything else.\n一般来说，naga 的味觉并不发达。我的同伴大多只吃生肉就很满足了。当然，这多半是因为他们压根懒得去尝试别的东西。"

    old "It's like what you were getting at before: when people stop asking questions and blindly follow the rules set by others, ignorance prevails. And that unquestioning attitude can be surprisingly harmful."
    new "It's like what you were getting at before: when people stop asking questions and blindly follow the rules set by others, ignorance prevails. And that unquestioning attitude can be surprisingly harmful.\n这就像你之前说的：当人们不再提问，盲目遵从他人定下的规矩时，无知就会占上风。而这种毫不质疑的态度，危害之大往往出人意料。"

    old "In a way, this all relates to our mission. We need to get out there and get more information, be more curious, more hungry. Why are the vampires doing this? What is this mysterious mist? Is there some higher magic at work here? Those are all good questions that we still need to find the answers to."
    new "In a way, this all relates to our mission. We need to get out there and get more information, be more curious, more hungry. Why are the vampires doing this? What is this mysterious mist? Is there some higher magic at work here? Those are all good questions that we still need to find the answers to.\n从某种意义上说，这一切都与我们的任务相关。我们需要走出去，获取更多信息，保持更多的好奇心，更多的渴求。吸血鬼为什么要这么做？这神秘的雾气是什么？这里是不是有某种更高深的魔法在起作用？这些都是好问题，而我们仍然需要找到答案。"

    old "I look at him and smile as I take his hand in mine and squeeze it gently to show my support. He blushes shyly for a moment before looking me in the eyes."
    new "I look at him and smile as I take his hand in mine and squeeze it gently to show my support. He blushes shyly for a moment before looking me in the eyes.\n我看着他，微笑着，握住他的手，轻轻捏了捏以表示支持。他害羞地脸红了一瞬，然后直视着我的眼睛。"

    old "You're right. Knowledge is power, but not only in the way we're used to thinking of it. There's definitely merit in the search for it."
    new "You're right. Knowledge is power, but not only in the way we're used to thinking of it. There's definitely merit in the search for it.\n你说得对。知识就是力量，但不仅仅是我们惯常理解的那种方式。追求知识本身，就确有价值。"

    old "We're going to end up getting close to the mist. Maybe hunting hellhounds might inadvertently lead us to some new information. This trip may end up being more productive than I originally thought."
    new "We're going to end up getting close to the mist. Maybe hunting hellhounds might inadvertently lead us to some new information. This trip may end up being more productive than I originally thought.\n我们终究会接近那片雾气。也许猎杀地狱犬会意外地让我们获得一些新信息。这趟行程最终可能比我原先想的更有收获。"

    old "And, even if we don't find out anything useful, I'll still get a good meal out of it."
    new "And, even if we don't find out anything useful, I'll still get a good meal out of it.\n而且，即便我们一无所获，我也能从中得到一顿美餐。"

    old "Enok's grin widens as he says the last sentence."
    new "Enok's grin widens as he says the last sentence.\nEnok 说出最后一句时，咧嘴笑得更开了。"

    old "Eventually, we arrive on the outskirts of Hammerhands and immediately start scouting our surroundings for any signs of hellhounds."
    new "Eventually, we arrive on the outskirts of Hammerhands and immediately start scouting our surroundings for any signs of hellhounds.\n最终，我们抵达了 Hammerhands 的郊外，随即开始侦查四周，寻找地狱犬的踪迹。"

    old "Do you have an actual plan to find the hellhounds or..."
    new "Do you have an actual plan to find the hellhounds or...\n你有找到地狱犬的具体计划吗，还是……"

    old "Finding them should be quite simple, actually. Hellhounds are like big dogs. The adult ones are roughly the size of horses. The ones in this area probably don't grow quite as big the ones in the Everburn Mountains, but they should still be quite heavy. When such a heavy animal goes through a place, it's bound to leave large tracks."
    new "Finding them should be quite simple, actually. Hellhounds are like big dogs. The adult ones are roughly the size of horses. The ones in this area probably don't grow quite as big the ones in the Everburn Mountains, but they should still be quite heavy. When such a heavy animal goes through a place, it's bound to leave large tracks.\n其实要找到它们相当简单。地狱犬就像大狗，成年的大约有马那么大。这一带的个头大概长不到 Everburn Mountains 那边那么大，但应该也相当沉。这么沉的动物经过一个地方，必然会留下很大的足迹。"

    old "So, you're saying that you're just going to follow their tracks like a normal hunter?"
    new "So, you're saying that you're just going to follow their tracks like a normal hunter?\n所以你是说，你就像个普通猎人那样，跟着它们的足迹走？"

    old "Exactly. Sorry if you were expecting something more grand. Maybe a dark magic ritual to locate the hellhounds? If you want I can pretend to cast some obscure spell and-- ah!"
    new "Exactly. Sorry if you were expecting something more grand. Maybe a dark magic ritual to locate the hellhounds? If you want I can pretend to cast some obscure spell and-- ah!\n没错。抱歉，如果你期待的是更了不起的法子。也许是某个用来定位地狱犬的黑暗魔法仪式？如果你想的话，我可以假装念一段晦涩的咒语，然后——哎哟！"

    old "I punch him in the shoulder. Considering his muscles, he probably barely felt the blow but, as always, he does like to exaggerate."
    new "I punch him in the shoulder. Considering his muscles, he probably barely felt the blow but, as always, he does like to exaggerate.\n我一拳打在他肩膀上。以他那身肌肉，他大概几乎没感觉到这一下，但一如往常，他就爱夸张。"

    old "Anyway, try to keep up, [protag]. I think I've found some fresh tracks. I'm going to try following them."
    new "Anyway, try to keep up, [protag]. I think I've found some fresh tracks. I'm going to try following them.\n总之，尽量跟上，[protag]。我想我找到了一些新鲜的足迹，我要试着跟过去。"

    old "Already? That was fast."
    new "Already? That was fast.\n这就找到了？真够快的。"

    old "Us nagas have to hunt for food to survive. We're a nomadic race and we don't do any farming. It's only natural that we'd end up being skilled hunters, no? Ahem, when we aren't robbing trade caravans, of course."
    new "Us nagas have to hunt for food to survive. We're a nomadic race and we don't do any farming. It's only natural that we'd end up being skilled hunters, no? Ahem, when we aren't robbing trade caravans, of course.\n我们 naga 为了生存，必须捕猎觅食。我们是游牧种族，不事农耕。最后自然就成了熟练的猎人，不是吗？咳咳，当然，是在我们不去抢劫商队的时候。"

    old "Hm. I guess it would be hard to start up a farm in the middle of the swamp. I can see how hunting would be your best option."
    new "Hm. I guess it would be hard to start up a farm in the middle of the swamp. I can see how hunting would be your best option.\n嗯。我想在沼泽中央开垦农田确实很难。我能理解捕猎为什么是你们最好的选择。"

    old "Still, I doubt Enok's skill is due exclusively to him being a naga. I imagine all of the extreme things he's done in order to get ingredients for his recipes has given him more experience than your average naga."
    new "Still, I doubt Enok's skill is due exclusively to him being a naga. I imagine all of the extreme things he's done in order to get ingredients for his recipes has given him more experience than your average naga.\n不过，我怀疑 Enok 的本事并非完全源于他是 naga。我猜他为了给食谱弄到食材所做过的那些极端之举，已经让他比一般 naga 更有经验了。"

    old "I follow his lead and, after a few short minutes of searching, we reach a small cave."
    new "I follow his lead and, after a few short minutes of searching, we reach a small cave.\n我跟着他，经过短短几分钟的搜寻，我们来到一个小洞穴前。"

    old "Do you think there are hellhounds inside?"
    new "Do you think there are hellhounds inside?\n你觉得里面有地狱犬吗？"

    old "Probably. Let's investigate it more closely."
    new "Probably. Let's investigate it more closely.\n很可能。我们再靠近点探一探。"

    old "Isn't it dangerous to go inside?"
    new "Isn't it dangerous to go inside?\n进去不危险吗？"

    old "It is. That's why I'm going to cast my ice shard spell inside the cave. The cold should draw out whatever is inside. It should give us a fairly significant advantage."
    new "It is. That's why I'm going to cast my ice shard spell inside the cave. The cold should draw out whatever is inside. It should give us a fairly significant advantage.\n危险。所以我要往洞里施放我的 Ice Shard 法术。寒冷应该能把里面的东西逼出来，那会给我们带来相当大的优势。"

    old "Clever. I guess I should have expected something like this from Enok. I'm sure he's come up with all sorts of fascinating ways to hunt. It might be interesting to tag along on more of them in the future."
    new "Clever. I guess I should have expected something like this from Enok. I'm sure he's come up with all sorts of fascinating ways to hunt. It might be interesting to tag along on more of them in the future.\n聪明。我早该料到 Enok 会来这一手。我相信他想出了各种各样有趣的捕猎法子。将来跟着他多见识几次，也许挺有意思的。"

    old "I prepare myself for a fight as Enok starts casting the ice shard spell. As soon as it hits the inside of the cave, we see a big flash of ice and then three smaller hellhounds come rushing out from it!"
    new "I prepare myself for a fight as Enok starts casting the ice shard spell. As soon as it hits the inside of the cave, we see a big flash of ice and then three smaller hellhounds come rushing out from it!\nEnok 开始施放 Ice Shard 法术时，我做好了战斗准备。法术一打进洞内，我们就看到一大片冰光闪过，接着三只个头小一些的地狱犬从洞里冲了出来！"

    old "There are three of them!"
    new "There are three of them!\n有三只！"

    old "Uh, yeah. Sorry. I didn't consider the possibility that they might be traveling in a group."
    new "Uh, yeah. Sorry. I didn't consider the possibility that they might be traveling in a group.\n呃，是啊。抱歉。我没考虑到它们可能结伴而行。"

    old "Maybe I was giving Enok too much credit earlier..."
    new "Maybe I was giving Enok too much credit earlier...\n也许我之前把 Enok 捧得太高了……"

    old "Phew. I'm glad that's over. All that's left is to collect the meat I need."
    new "Phew. I'm glad that's over. All that's left is to collect the meat I need.\n呼。真高兴这事结束了。剩下的就是采集我需要的肉了。"

    old "Alright. I'll go keep watch up on that hill over there to make sure we don't run into any more surprises. The last thing we need is another fight."
    new "Alright. I'll go keep watch up on that hill over there to make sure we don't run into any more surprises. The last thing we need is another fight.\n好。我去那边的小山上放哨，确保我们不会再遇到什么意外。我们最不需要的就是再打一架。"

    old "Good idea, [protag]. I'll try to keep this quick."
    new "Good idea, [protag]. I'll try to keep this quick.\n好主意，[protag]。我会尽量快一点。"

    old "I head over to the hill and keep an eye out for trouble for a few minutes before Enok approaches me carrying a bag full of meat. Blood is dripping out of the bottom of it, giving the whole thing a very macabre vibe."
    new "I head over to the hill and keep an eye out for trouble for a few minutes before Enok approaches me carrying a bag full of meat. Blood is dripping out of the bottom of it, giving the whole thing a very macabre vibe.\n我走到小山那里，留神观察了几分钟，随后 Enok 提着一满袋肉朝我走来。袋底还在滴血，让整个画面透着一股阴森的气息。"

    old "Wait. We need to cook it or it will be rancid by the time we reach Grimoire!"
    new "Wait. We need to cook it or it will be rancid by the time we reach Grimoire!\n等等。我们得把它做熟，不然等回到 Grimoire，肉都该坏了！"

    old "Ah, don't worry. That shouldn't be an issue."
    new "Ah, don't worry. That shouldn't be an issue.\n啊，别担心。这不成问题。"

    old "Enok snaps his fingers and a minor version of his ice spell freezes the meat instantly. It also happens to solve the blood dripping problem."
    new "Enok snaps his fingers and a minor version of his ice spell freezes the meat instantly. It also happens to solve the blood dripping problem.\nEnok 打了个响指，一个缩小版的冰系法术立刻把肉冻住了。顺便也解决了滴血的问题。"

    old "Nice idea."
    new "Nice idea.\n好主意。"

    old "This way, we can cook the meat right in front of Apolimesho."
    new "This way, we can cook the meat right in front of Apolimesho.\n这样，我们就可以在 Apolimesho 面前直接烹制这些肉了。"

    old "Then he'll have no choice but to admit that you're immune."
    new "Then he'll have no choice but to admit that you're immune.\n那样他就别无选择，只能承认你免疫了。"

    old "That is the idea."
    new "That is the idea.\n正是这个意思。"

    old "Enok and I continue chatting as we start our way back to Grimoire."
    new "Enok and I continue chatting as we start our way back to Grimoire.\n我们启程返回 Grimoire 时，Enok 和我继续聊着天。"

    old "Well, I've held up my end of the bargain. You'd better start thinking about what amazing dish you're going to make to pay me back."
    new "Well, I've held up my end of the bargain. You'd better start thinking about what amazing dish you're going to make to pay me back.\n好了，我这边说到做到了。你最好开始想想，要做一道什么了不起的菜来回报我。"

    old "Hmm. That's going to be a difficult decision to make. There are so many options to consider. Do you have any requests, [protag]?"
    new "Hmm. That's going to be a difficult decision to make. There are so many options to consider. Do you have any requests, [protag]?\n嗯。这可是个难做的决定。有太多选择了。你有什么想吃的吗，[protag]？"

    old "Oh, no. I'm not helping you with this decision. I want it to be a surprise. Besides, I'm sure I'll enjoy whatever you make no matter what it ends up being."
    new "Oh, no. I'm not helping you with this decision. I want it to be a surprise. Besides, I'm sure I'll enjoy whatever you make no matter what it ends up being.\n哦，不。这个决定我可不帮你做。我想保留点惊喜。再说了，无论你最后做出来的是什么，我相信我都会喜欢。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]. I'll be sure to surpass your expectations."
    new "Thank you, [protag]. I'll be sure to surpass your expectations.\n谢谢你，[protag]。我一定会超出你的期待。"

    old "That's some confidence. Still, I'm sure he will."
    new "That's some confidence. Still, I'm sure he will.\n还挺有自信。不过，我相信他能做到。"

    old "We drift into silence for a bit before Enok eventually speaks up again."
    new "We drift into silence for a bit before Enok eventually speaks up again.\n我们沉默了一会儿，随后 Enok 又开口了。"

    old "You know... I guess it's kind of pointless to tell you this now, but I would have made you dinner even if you didn't help me with this mission. All you had to do was ask."
    new "You know... I guess it's kind of pointless to tell you this now, but I would have made you dinner even if you didn't help me with this mission. All you had to do was ask.\n你知道吗……我想现在说这些也没什么意义了，但即便你没帮我这趟任务，我也会给你做晚饭的。你只要开口就行了。"

    old "I know."
    new "I know.\n我知道。"

    old "Then why did you ask me to make you something as a reward?"
    new "Then why did you ask me to make you something as a reward?\n那你为什么还要我以做菜作为回报？"

    old "I guess it just seemed better this way. I mean, it wouldn't be fair to you if you cooked for me all the time and I didn't do anything for you in return."
    new "I guess it just seemed better this way. I mean, it wouldn't be fair to you if you cooked for me all the time and I didn't do anything for you in return.\n我想，这样似乎更好。我是说，要是你总是给我做饭，而我却什么都不为你做，那对你不公平。"

    old "Enok flashes me a smile."
    new "Enok flashes me a smile.\nEnok 冲我一笑。"

    old "I wouldn't mind."
    new "I wouldn't mind.\n我不会介意的。"

    old "After a few hours of travel, we're back. Enok and I then go find Apolimesho and get started. Enok cooks the hellhound meat in front of Aplimesho who looks surprisingly bemused. It's a nice change from his usual, annoyed expression."
    new "After a few hours of travel, we're back. Enok and I then go find Apolimesho and get started. Enok cooks the hellhound meat in front of Aplimesho who looks surprisingly bemused. It's a nice change from his usual, annoyed expression.\n经过几个小时的赶路，我们回来了。随后 Enok 和我去找 Apolimesho，开始正事。Enok 当着 Apolimesho 的面烹制地狱犬肉，对方竟露出了一副饶有兴味的神情。这可比他平时那副不耐烦的样子好多了。"

    old "Once the dish is done, Enok digs in. I can't help but be a little envious as I take note of the euphoric look on his face. The Hellhound Pot Roast looks and smells delicious, but I know I can't eat it myself-- unless I'm ready to die or go insane, which I'm not. Life can be cruel."
    new "Once the dish is done, Enok digs in. I can't help but be a little envious as I take note of the euphoric look on his face. The Hellhound Pot Roast looks and smells delicious, but I know I can't eat it myself-- unless I'm ready to die or go insane, which I'm not. Life can be cruel.\n菜一做好，Enok 就大快朵颐起来。看着他脸上那陶醉的神情，我忍不住有点羡慕。Hellhound Pot Roast 看起来、闻起来都美味极了，可我知道自己不能吃——除非我准备好去死或者发疯，而我没有。生活有时真残酷。"

    old "The dish eaten, Apolimesho proceeds to administer the test. The Divine Juice trembles ever so slightly, but grows still shortly after."
    new "The dish eaten, Apolimesho proceeds to administer the test. The Divine Juice trembles ever so slightly, but grows still shortly after.\n菜吃完后，Apolimesho 便开始进行测试。Divine Juice 微微颤动了一下，但很快就恢复了平静。"

    old "Well, it looks like you were right, Enok. It's true that the juice moved a little, but considering how much dark magic you just ingested... It's nothing short of incredible. A man, elf, or dwarf would arleady be suffering severely."
    new "Well, it looks like you were right, Enok. It's true that the juice moved a little, but considering how much dark magic you just ingested... It's nothing short of incredible. A man, elf, or dwarf would arleady be suffering severely.\n嗯，看来你是对的，Enok。诚然，那汁液确实动了一下，但考虑到你刚刚摄入了那么多黑暗魔法……这简直不可思议。换成人类、精灵或矮人，早就痛苦不堪了。"

    old "I suppose you're satisfied now?"
    new "I suppose you're satisfied now?\n我想你现在满意了吧？"

    old "Yes. While I still don't approve of the use of dark magic, I can say with absolute certainty that it won't drive you mad, Enok. I am comfortable with you remaining on [protag]'s team."
    new "Yes. While I still don't approve of the use of dark magic, I can say with absolute certainty that it won't drive you mad, Enok. I am comfortable with you remaining on [protag]'s team.\n是的。虽然我仍然不赞成使用黑暗魔法，但我可以绝对肯定地说，它不会让你发疯，Enok。我放心让你留在 [protag] 的队伍里。"

    old "We leave Apolimesho's room shortly after and, when we do, Enok turns to me and grins broadly."
    new "We leave Apolimesho's room shortly after and, when we do, Enok turns to me and grins broadly.\n不久后我们离开了 Apolimesho 的房间，一出房门，Enok 就转向我，咧开嘴笑了。"

    old "What an adventure, eh?"
    new "What an adventure, eh?\n真是场冒险，对吧？"

    old "As interesting as it was, you can't deny that it was a waste of time. I'm honestly still surprised that Apolimesho was so insistent about it. He knows how vital our quest at N'Mar is."
    new "As interesting as it was, you can't deny that it was a waste of time. I'm honestly still surprised that Apolimesho was so insistent about it. He knows how vital our quest at N'Mar is.\n虽然挺有意思，但你也不能否认这是浪费时间。说真的，我仍惊讶 Apolimesho 竟如此坚持。他明明知道我们在 N'Mar 的使命有多重要。"

    old "Hmm... I guess it was important for him to know wether he could trust me with you or not."
    new "Hmm... I guess it was important for him to know wether he could trust me with you or not.\n嗯……我想，对他来说，弄清能否把我托付给你是很重要的。"

    old "Trust isn't something that comes easily to him, is it? Maybe he was betrayed in the past-- not that he would tell us if he was. I guess we can't really know."
    new "Trust isn't something that comes easily to him, is it? Maybe he was betrayed in the past-- not that he would tell us if he was. I guess we can't really know.\n信任对他来说来之不易，对吧？也许他过去曾被背叛过——不过就算如此，他也不会告诉我们。我想我们是无从知道了。"

    old "True. A man in his position can't really afford to take anything for granted. It makes sense that he's cautious."
    new "True. A man in his position can't really afford to take anything for granted. It makes sense that he's cautious.\n没错。处在他那个位置的人，实在不敢把任何事视作理所当然。他如此谨慎也说得通。"

    old "It ended up being a pleasant diversion. I mean, I don't like that Apolimesho couldn't trust my judgement when it came to you, but it did give me a good excuse to spend time with you."
    new "It ended up being a pleasant diversion. I mean, I don't like that Apolimesho couldn't trust my judgement when it came to you, but it did give me a good excuse to spend time with you.\n到头来这倒成了次愉快的消遣。我是说，我不喜欢 Apolimesho 在有关你的事上不信任我的判断，不过这确实给了我一个和你相处的正当理由。"

    old "And... You really are an amazing cook, Enok. All that reading paid off."
    new "And... You really are an amazing cook, Enok. All that reading paid off.\n而且……你真的是个了不起的厨师，Enok。读那么多书没有白费。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]. But how can you say that when you didn't even get to taste the dish?"
    new "Thank you, [protag]. But how can you say that when you didn't even get to taste the dish?\n谢谢你，[protag]。可你连菜都没尝到，怎么这么说？"

    old "Well, experience with your cooking for one thing. And, I may not have been able to taste it, but I could definitely smell it. The aroma was nothing short of amazing. I'm sure it tasted fantastic."
    new "Well, experience with your cooking for one thing. And, I may not have been able to taste it, but I could definitely smell it. The aroma was nothing short of amazing. I'm sure it tasted fantastic.\n嗯，首先是因为见识过你的厨艺。而且，我虽然没能尝到，但绝对闻到了。那香气简直妙不可言。我敢肯定它味道好极了。"

    old "This may be insensitive to say, but yes. It really was."
    new "This may be insensitive to say, but yes. It really was.\n这么说也许有点不顾你的感受，但确实如此。真的。"

    old "Anyway, I've taken up enough of your time today. I need to start heading back to the swamps and I know you have your own tasks to get back to."
    new "Anyway, I've taken up enough of your time today. I need to start heading back to the swamps and I know you have your own tasks to get back to.\n总之，我今天占用你的时间够多了。我得动身回沼泽去了，我知道你也有自己的事情要回去忙。"

    old "Oh, before I go! Don't forget that I owe you dinner. I'll let you know when I have the time to make something really good."
    new "Oh, before I go! Don't forget that I owe you dinner. I'll let you know when I have the time to make something really good.\n哦，临走前说一句！别忘了我还欠你一顿晚饭。等我有时间做点真正的好菜时，会通知你的。"

    old "Naturally. I'm looking forward to it."
    new "Naturally. I'm looking forward to it.\n当然。我很期待。"

    old "Enok flashes me one last smile before taking his leave. Well, I guess that's my cue to get going myself."
    new "Enok flashes me one last smile before taking his leave. Well, I guess that's my cue to get going myself.\nEnok 临走前朝我最后一笑。好吧，那我也该动身了。"

    old "Enok formally invited me to dinner and I happen to think he's a very talented cook so, naturally, the only option was to accept. Still, more than the food, I'm looking forward to spending more time with Enok."
    new "Enok formally invited me to dinner and I happen to think he's a very talented cook so, naturally, the only option was to accept. Still, more than the food, I'm looking forward to spending more time with Enok.\nEnok 正式邀请我共进晚餐，而我恰好觉得他是个极有天赋的厨师，所以自然只有接受这一个选项。不过，比起食物，我更期待和 Enok 多相处些时光。"

    old "I reach the river around sunset and approach Enok. However, to my surprise, Sylrissa is there too. I mean, I guess that this wasn't technically a date or anything, but... it seems kind of weird somehow."
    new "I reach the river around sunset and approach Enok. However, to my surprise, Sylrissa is there too. I mean, I guess that this wasn't technically a date or anything, but... it seems kind of weird somehow.\n我在日落时分来到河边，走向 Enok。然而出乎我意料的是，Sylrissa 也在那里。我是说，严格来说这也不算什么约会之类的，但……总觉得有点怪怪的。"

    old "Oh, [protag], you have arrived!"
    new "Oh, [protag], you have arrived!\n哦，[protag]，你来了！"

    old "Hi Sylrissa, I didn't know you would be here too."
    new "Hi Sylrissa, I didn't know you would be here too.\n嗨，Sylrissa，我不知道你也会来。"

    old "I'm always here, [protag]. You don't know this, but I frequently hide behind the bushes hoping to catch a good view of you and Enok making out."
    new "I'm always here, [protag]. You don't know this, but I frequently hide behind the bushes hoping to catch a good view of you and Enok making out.\n我一直都在这里，[protag]。你不知道吧，我经常躲在灌木丛后面，就盼着能好好看一场你和 Enok 亲热的戏码。"

    old "Sylrissa! Stop that. It's not funny."
    new "Sylrissa! Stop that. It's not funny.\nSylrissa！别闹了。这一点也不好笑。"

    old "My face burns a bright red but, as red as it is, it's comforting to know that Enok cheeks are an even darker shade than mine."
    new "My face burns a bright red but, as red as it is, it's comforting to know that Enok cheeks are an even darker shade than mine.\n我的脸烧得通红，但尽管已经很红了，得知 Enok 的脸颊比我还要红上一分，倒也让我心里好受些。"

    old "Allright, allright. I'll stop with the teasing. For now at least. The food was exquisite as always, Enok."
    new "Allright, allright. I'll stop with the teasing. For now at least. The food was exquisite as always, Enok.\n好了，好了。我不逗你们了。至少暂时不逗了。饭菜还是一如既往地精美，Enok。"

    old "You're leaving?"
    new "You're leaving?\n你要走了？"

    old "Hm? Oh, yes. Sorry. I have this very urgent thing I need to go do that simply can not be delayed."
    new "Hm? Oh, yes. Sorry. I have this very urgent thing I need to go do that simply can not be delayed.\n嗯？哦，是的。抱歉。我有一件非常紧急的事要去做，实在耽误不得。"

    old "I can't think of many things in the swamp that would have a strict time limit. I get the impression that she isn't telling me the truth. I don't stop her from leaving though. Enok is the one I came to spend time with today."
    new "I can't think of many things in the swamp that would have a strict time limit. I get the impression that she isn't telling me the truth. I don't stop her from leaving though. Enok is the one I came to spend time with today.\n我想不出沼泽里有多少事会这么有时间限制。我觉得她没有对我说实话。不过我也没有拦她。今天我来，本来就是想和 Enok 一起度过。"

    old "Sorry about that. Anyway, if you'll follow me..."
    new "Sorry about that. Anyway, if you'll follow me...\n抱歉啊。总之，请跟我来……"

    old "I thought we were eating near the river?"
    new "I thought we were eating near the river?\n我还以为我们在河边吃饭？"

    old "We are, but not on the ground. We're going to use the small shelter I made."
    new "We are, but not on the ground. We're going to use the small shelter I made.\n是在河边，但不是席地而坐。我们要用我搭的那个小棚子。"

    old "Ah, I see. Thank you. I appreciate it."
    new "Ah, I see. Thank you. I appreciate it.\n啊，我明白了。谢谢。我很感激。"

    old "I imagined you would. For us nagas, most places are comfortable enough because of our tails. That's not quite the case for you though, is it?"
    new "I imagined you would. For us nagas, most places are comfortable enough because of our tails. That's not quite the case for you though, is it?\n我想你会的。对我们 naga 来说，大多数地方因为有尾巴，坐着都挺舒服。但对你来说就不太一样了，对吧？"

    old "No, it is not. The more I hear about your tails, the more advantageous I think they are."
    new "No, it is not. The more I hear about your tails, the more advantageous I think they are.\n不，确实不一样。关于你们的尾巴，我听得越多，就越觉得它们优势多多。"

    old "Oh? Thinking about getting one for yourself?"
    new "Oh? Thinking about getting one for yourself?\n哦？你也想给自己弄一条？"

    old "I laugh."
    new "I laugh.\n我笑了。"

    old "I'm afraid I've gotten to used to my [prace] legs. I wouldn't know what to do with a naga tail."
    new "I'm afraid I've gotten to used to my [prace] legs. I wouldn't know what to do with a naga tail.\n恐怕我已经太习惯自己这双 [prace] 腿了。有了 naga 尾巴，我还真不知道该怎么用。"

    old "Seriously though, you and Sylrissa never get tired of standing still?"
    new "Seriously though, you and Sylrissa never get tired of standing still?\n不过说真的，你和 Sylrissa 一直那么站着，就不会累吗？"

    old "Well, no. We get tired of 'standing' too. We can do a lot more before getting exhausted than other races, but it still happens. That's not exactly what I'd call a disadvantage though."
    new "Well, no. We get tired of 'standing' too. We can do a lot more before getting exhausted than other races, but it still happens. That's not exactly what I'd call a disadvantage though.\n嗯，也会累的。我们也会因为站着而累。只是比起其他种族，我们能坚持得久得多，不过终究还是会累的。但这也算不上什么劣势就是了。"

    old "Oh! Another cool thing about our tails is that we can cross rough terrain and feel almost nothing."
    new "Oh! Another cool thing about our tails is that we can cross rough terrain and feel almost nothing.\n哦！我们尾巴还有个很酷的地方，就是能穿越崎岖的地形，却几乎毫无感觉。"

    old "You also move quietly and can use your tail to grip things. Really, your tail grants you a pretty significant advantage in a lot of situations. Hunting, fighting. Even escaping."
    new "You also move quietly and can use your tail to grip things. Really, your tail grants you a pretty significant advantage in a lot of situations. Hunting, fighting. Even escaping.\n你们行动时还很安静，还能用尾巴抓握东西。真的，在很多情况下，尾巴都给了你们相当大的优势。捕猎、战斗，甚至逃跑。"

    old "True enough. My tail is pretty great."
    new "True enough. My tail is pretty great.\n说得没错。我的尾巴确实很棒。"

    old "Enok lets out an amused chuckle and then shows me to a wooden stool. There's another one on the opposite side that looks just as well made."
    new "Enok lets out an amused chuckle and then shows me to a wooden stool. There's another one on the opposite side that looks just as well made.\nEnok 发出一声被逗乐的笑，然后领我坐到一张木凳旁。对面还有一张，看起来做工同样精良。"

    old "I hope it's comfortable enough. Let me know if there's anything that feels off. I'll try to adjust it before your next visit."
    new "I hope it's comfortable enough. Let me know if there's anything that feels off. I'll try to adjust it before your next visit.\n希望它够舒服。如果有哪里不对劲就告诉我。我会在你下次来之前试着调整。"

    old "You... crafted these yourself?"
    new "You... crafted these yourself?\n这些……是你自己做的？"

    old "Yes! I found a carpentry book and figured I'd give it a try."
    new "Yes! I found a carpentry book and figured I'd give it a try.\n是啊！我找到一本木工书，就想着试试看。"

    old "Enok: give him a book and he can learn to do anything."
    new "Enok: give him a book and he can learn to do anything.\nEnok 此人：给他一本书，他就能学会任何事。"

    old "Enok laughs."
    new "Enok laughs.\nEnok 笑了起来。"

    old "It's not like that! At least, not always. For instance, I once found a book on fishing. I read it and tried to follow its advice, but after awhile I got bored. I jumped into the river and, a few minutes later, I'd already caught three big fish."
    new "It's not like that! At least, not always. For instance, I once found a book on fishing. I read it and tried to follow its advice, but after awhile I got bored. I jumped into the river and, a few minutes later, I'd already caught three big fish.\n也不是那样啦！至少不总是。比如说，我曾经找到一本讲钓鱼的书。我读了，也试着照它说的做，可没过多久就烦了。我跳进河里，几分钟后，已经抓到了三条大鱼。"

    old "I take my seat and wait as Enok reveals what he ended up making for the occasion. As it turns out, he didn't just make one dish. He made several of them. They aren't exactly simple dishes either. Sometimes I wonder where Enok finds all the ingredients he needs. Then I remind myself that it's probably better not to ask too many questions."
    new "I take my seat and wait as Enok reveals what he ended up making for the occasion. As it turns out, he didn't just make one dish. He made several of them. They aren't exactly simple dishes either. Sometimes I wonder where Enok finds all the ingredients he needs. Then I remind myself that it's probably better not to ask too many questions.\n我坐了下来，等着 Enok 揭晓他这次到底做了什么。原来他不只做了一道菜，而是做了好几道。而且这些菜也都不算简单。有时我会好奇 Enok 是从哪儿弄到所有需要的食材的。随后我又提醒自己，最好还是别问太多。"

    old "I take my time sampling each dish and discussing all sorts of things with Enok."
    new "I take my time sampling each dish and discussing all sorts of things with Enok.\n我不慌不忙地逐一品尝每道菜，和 Enok 聊着各种话题。"

    old "Once we finish eating, we move closer to the river and relax as we admire the flow of the water."
    new "Once we finish eating, we move closer to the river and relax as we admire the flow of the water.\n吃完饭后，我们挪到河边，一边欣赏着水流，一边放松休息。"

    old "I really enjoyed the dinner you prepared, Enok. Thank you."
    new "I really enjoyed the dinner you prepared, Enok. Thank you.\n你准备的这顿晚餐我真的很喜欢，Enok。谢谢你。"

    old "You're quite welcome. I enjoyed making it for you."
    new "You're quite welcome. I enjoyed making it for you.\n不客气。为你做这顿饭，我也很开心。"

    old "You know... I make a point of visiting all of our team members as frequently as I can, but this time was special. I was really looking forward to it. And it's also the first time I've gotten something in exchange for my time. I mean, it's not like any of you owe me anything, but..."
    new "You know... I make a point of visiting all of our team members as frequently as I can, but this time was special. I was really looking forward to it. And it's also the first time I've gotten something in exchange for my time. I mean, it's not like any of you owe me anything, but...\n你知道吗……我总会尽量频繁地去看望我们队里的每个人，但这次很特别。我真的很期待。而且这也是第一次，我付出的时间得到了回馈。我是说，并不是说你们谁欠我什么，只是……"

    old "But it's nice to talk and unwind after a nice dinner, isn't it?"
    new "But it's nice to talk and unwind after a nice dinner, isn't it?\n但在一顿美餐之后聊聊天、放松一下，是件很惬意的事，不是吗？"

    old "Yes. It most definitely is."
    new "Yes. It most definitely is.\n是的。绝对如此。"

    old "So, what do you think? You said you enjoyed it but was this a proper 'culinary reward' for helping me out with the whole hellhound incident?"
    new "So, what do you think? You said you enjoyed it but was this a proper 'culinary reward' for helping me out with the whole hellhound incident?\n那么，你觉得怎么样？你说你喜欢，但这一顿算不算对我那场地狱犬风波帮了忙的合格烹饪奖赏？"

    old "'Culinary reward'?"
    new "'Culinary reward'?\n烹饪奖赏？"

    old "I come up with the best new terms, don't I?"
    new "I come up with the best new terms, don't I?\n我总能造出最棒的新词，不是吗？"

    old "I chuckle and then answer his first question."
    new "I chuckle and then answer his first question.\n我轻笑一声，然后回答了他的第一个问题。"

    old "You surpassed all of my expectations."
    new "You surpassed all of my expectations.\n你超出了我所有的期待。"

    old "It's a pity I couldn't try the hellhound recipe."
    new "It's a pity I couldn't try the hellhound recipe.\n真可惜，我没法尝尝那道地狱犬食谱。"

    old "You're still thinking about that, huh?"
    new "You're still thinking about that, huh?\n你还在惦记那个呢，嗯？"

    old "Yeah. I know that might be a little insensitive to bring up in front of you since you can't eat it, but... it sounded so good. I bet that dish is really something."
    new "Yeah. I know that might be a little insensitive to bring up in front of you since you can't eat it, but... it sounded so good. I bet that dish is really something.\n是啊。我知道在你面前提这个可能有点不体贴，毕竟你不能吃，但……那听起来实在太诱人了。我打赌那道菜肯定不一般。"

    old "You'll get to try it one day. As soon as the N'Mar threat is over we can go fight as many hellhounds as you want."
    new "You'll get to try it one day. As soon as the N'Mar threat is over we can go fight as many hellhounds as you want.\n总有一天你会尝到的。等 N'Mar 的威胁一结束，我们就可以去猎杀地狱犬，你想打多少就打多少。"

    old "I hear a noise coming from the bushes behind us and instinctively get up. Enok, on the other hand, responds calmly, taking my hand in his and holding it reassuringly."
    new "I hear a noise coming from the bushes behind us and instinctively get up. Enok, on the other hand, responds calmly, taking my hand in his and holding it reassuringly.\n我听到身后灌木丛里传来声响，本能地站起身来。Enok 则显得很平静，他握住我的手，安慰般地轻轻按着。"

    old "Calm down. It's just a bird or some other small creature."
    new "Calm down. It's just a bird or some other small creature.\n冷静点。只是只鸟，或别的什么小动物罢了。"

    old "How do you know that?"
    new "How do you know that?\n你怎么知道？"

    old "Because Sylrissa is guarding the perimeter. She wouldn't let anything bigger than a rabbit pass, believe me."
    new "Because Sylrissa is guarding the perimeter. She wouldn't let anything bigger than a rabbit pass, believe me.\n因为 Sylrissa 在守着外围。她绝不会放任何比兔子大的东西过去，相信我。"

    old "Sylrissa? Why would she be upset?"
    new "Sylrissa? Why would she be upset?\nSylrissa？她为什么会不高兴？"

    old "Well, you know... because we had a romantic dinner alone and..."
    new "Well, you know... because we had a romantic dinner alone and...\n嗯，你知道的……因为我们俩单独吃了顿浪漫晚餐，然后……"

    old "I turn a bright red. Do I really have to explain this?"
    new "I turn a bright red. Do I really have to explain this?\n我的脸涨得通红。这真的要我来解释吗？"

    old "Oh! I see what you mean now. I didn't think that you would consider this dinner romantic-"
    new "Oh! I see what you mean now. I didn't think that you would consider this dinner romantic-\n哦！我现在明白你的意思了。我没想到你会把这顿晚餐当作浪漫的——"

    old "Sorry, maybe I chose the wrong words!"
    new "Sorry, maybe I chose the wrong words!\n抱歉，也许我用词不当！"

    old "No, not at all. It's fine. I mean... Well, this is something new for me. Nagas aren't exactly known for being romantic, you know?"
    new "No, not at all. It's fine. I mean... Well, this is something new for me. Nagas aren't exactly known for being romantic, you know?\n不，完全不会。没关系。我是说……嗯，这对我来说是新鲜事。Nagas 可不算以浪漫著称的种族，你知道吗？"

    old "I don't know. Maybe you can go ask her yourself."
    new "I don't know. Maybe you can go ask her yourself.\n我不知道。也许你可以自己去问问她。"

    old "Is it just my imagination, or did Enok look slightly annoyed at what I just said? I guess I'd better backtrack a bit."
    new "Is it just my imagination, or did Enok look slightly annoyed at what I just said? I guess I'd better backtrack a bit.\n是我的错觉吗，还是 Enok 听了我刚才的话，似乎有点不高兴？我想我还是把话收回来一点比较好。"

    old "I'm sure it's fine. I want to stay here with you a bit longer. This place... it's very romantic."
    new "I'm sure it's fine. I want to stay here with you a bit longer. This place... it's very romantic.\n我相信没事的。我想在这里和你多待一会儿。这个地方……非常浪漫。"

    old "Romantic?"
    new "Romantic?\n浪漫？"

    old "I think Sylrissa mentioned that before: that you nagas aren't a romantic race. The concept is a bit strange to me to be completely honest, but it's not like nagas are the only race that lack that sense of romanticism."
    new "I think Sylrissa mentioned that before: that you nagas aren't a romantic race. The concept is a bit strange to me to be completely honest, but it's not like nagas are the only race that lack that sense of romanticism.\n我想 Sylrissa 之前提过：你们 naga 不是个浪漫的种族。老实说，这个概念对我来说有点陌生，不过也并非只有 naga 缺乏那种浪漫情调。"

    old "Oh? There are others? I thought it was just us nagas."
    new "Oh? There are others? I thought it was just us nagas.\n哦？还有别的种族也这样？我还以为只有我们 naga 呢。"

    old "It's not. For example, the orc way of courting consists of bashing their potential partner's head with a giant club until they agree to go out on a date."
    new "It's not. For example, the orc way of courting consists of bashing their potential partner's head with a giant club until they agree to go out on a date.\n不是的。比如说，Orcs 的求偶方式，就是用一根大棒猛敲潜在伴侣的脑袋，直到对方答应约会为止。"

    old "That's not real! It can't be. You had to have made that up."
    new "That's not real! It can't be. You had to have made that up.\n这不可能！怎么可能是真的。你一定是编的。"

    old "I may have exaggerated a bit but, believe me, it's not as far from the truth as it should be."
    new "I may have exaggerated a bit but, believe me, it's not as far from the truth as it should be.\n我也许夸张了一点，但相信我，它离真相并不像你想的那么远。"

    old "Hm. Interesting. You really know a lot of things, [protag]. I could stay and listen to you for hours."
    new "Hm. Interesting. You really know a lot of things, [protag]. I could stay and listen to you for hours.\n嗯。有意思。你真的懂得很多，[protag]。我能待在这儿听你讲上几个小时。"

    old "Enok blushes but remains silent as his eyes remain fixed on mine. The longer it goes on, the more uncomfortable I get so I decide to break the silence."
    new "Enok blushes but remains silent as his eyes remain fixed on mine. The longer it goes on, the more uncomfortable I get so I decide to break the silence.\nEnok 脸红了，却仍沉默着，目光一直停留在我眼睛上。这样越久，我越不自在，于是我决定打破沉默。"

    old "Err, anyway, I really must go now. Tomorrow is going to be another busy day."
    new "Err, anyway, I really must go now. Tomorrow is going to be another busy day.\n呃，总之，我现在真的得走了。明天又会是忙碌的一天。"

    old "I understand. Have a nice trip back to Grimoire."
    new "I understand. Have a nice trip back to Grimoire.\n我明白。祝你回 Grimoire 一路顺风。"

    old "Enok stands up before me and offers to help me up by extending his hand. I take it, but his grip is so strong that he accidentally pulls me up too fast. I end up bumping gently into his chest."
    new "Enok stands up before me and offers to help me up by extending his hand. I take it, but his grip is so strong that he accidentally pulls me up too fast. I end up bumping gently into his chest.\nEnok 先站起身来，然后伸出手要拉我起来。我握住他的手，但他的力气太大，一不小心把我拽得太快，结果我轻轻撞进了他怀里。"

    old "Oh, sorry, I-"
    new "Oh, sorry, I-\n哦，抱歉，我——"

    old "I place my hand on his chest and, for a moment, I can feel his well developed pectoral muscles under my fingers. It's a nice feeling, but I don't dare overstay my welcome."
    new "I place my hand on his chest and, for a moment, I can feel his well developed pectoral muscles under my fingers. It's a nice feeling, but I don't dare overstay my welcome.\n我把手按在他胸口，一瞬间，我能隔着手指感觉到他那发达的胸肌。那感觉很好，但我可不敢贪恋。"

    old "There's nothing to be sorry about."
    new "There's nothing to be sorry about.\n没什么好道歉的。"

    old "Oh, already?"
    new "Oh, already?\n哦，这就要走了？"

    old "Enok looks a bit disappointed. Unfortunately, I really do have to go. But I think I know something that will perk him up."
    new "Enok looks a bit disappointed. Unfortunately, I really do have to go. But I think I know something that will perk him up.\nEnok 看起来有点失望。可惜我真的得走了。不过我想，我知道该怎么让他打起精神来。"

    old "I take his hand in mine and hold it as I offer him a smile."
    new "I take his hand in mine and hold it as I offer him a smile.\n我握住他的手，朝他微微一笑。"

    old "Yes, but if you keep cooking like this I'll have no choice but to come back."
    new "Yes, but if you keep cooking like this I'll have no choice but to come back.\n是的，但你要是一直像这样做饭，我就别无选择，只能再回来了。"

    old "That's good because I have many more recipes I want to try!"
    new "That's good because I have many more recipes I want to try!\n那太好了，因为我还有好多食谱想试呢！"

    old "I say my goodbyes and leave the river behind. As I go, I can feel Enok's eyes on me. I don't turn around to see him, but I don't have to look to know that he's staring at me."
    new "I say my goodbyes and leave the river behind. As I go, I can feel Enok's eyes on me. I don't turn around to see him, but I don't have to look to know that he's staring at me.\n我道了别，离开了河边。一路上，我能感觉到 Enok 的目光追随着我。我没有回头看他，但不用看我也知道，他一直在注视着我。"

    old "I head to the river again to meet up with Enok. Today, I find him swimming in it."
    new "I head to the river again to meet up with Enok. Today, I find him swimming in it.\n我再次前往河边与 Enok 会面。今天，我发现他正在河里游泳。"

    old "Oh hey, [protag]! I was just trying to catch a few fish before you came!"
    new "Oh hey, [protag]! I was just trying to catch a few fish before you came!\n哦嘿，[protag]！我正想赶在你来之前抓几条鱼呢！"

    old "I can wait a bit if you need another minute."
    new "I can wait a bit if you need another minute.\n如果你还需要点时间，我可以等一会儿。"

    old "Oh no, it's not a problem. I can always catch them later. I'll join you on the shore."
    new "Oh no, it's not a problem. I can always catch them later. I'll join you on the shore.\n哦不，没关系的。我随时可以再抓。我上岸来陪你。"

    old "Anyway, I'm going to soak my feet in the river for a bit if you don't mind. I walked a lot today and my feet are kind of sore."
    new "Anyway, I'm going to soak my feet in the river for a bit if you don't mind. I walked a lot today and my feet are kind of sore.\n总之，如果你不介意的话，我想去河里泡一会儿脚。今天走了很多路，脚有点酸。"

    old "Enok looks at me with a curious expression."
    new "Enok looks at me with a curious expression.\nEnok 一脸好奇地看着我。"

    old "I don't mind, but... why do that? Do you get some kind of relief out of it?"
    new "I don't mind, but... why do that? Do you get some kind of relief out of it?\n我不介意，可是……为什么要这么做？那样能让你得到某种缓解吗？"

    old "Yes. Walking for a long time fatigues our feet. Putting them in cold water feels good and reactivates the circulatory system. Basically, it gives those of us with feet a spark of energy."
    new "Yes. Walking for a long time fatigues our feet. Putting them in cold water feels good and reactivates the circulatory system. Basically, it gives those of us with feet a spark of energy.\n是的。走久了会让我们的脚疲惫。把脚放进冷水里很舒服，还能促进血液循环。基本上，就是给像我们这种有脚的人注入一点活力。"

    old "I take my shoes off as I answer Enok's question and walk into the water until it reaches my ankles. The river water is so cold that it sends a shiver up my spine, but I can already feel its soothing effects."
    new "I take my shoes off as I answer Enok's question and walk into the water until it reaches my ankles. The river water is so cold that it sends a shiver up my spine, but I can already feel its soothing effects.\n我一边回答 Enok 的问题，一边脱掉鞋子，走进水里，直到水没到脚踝。河水冷得我脊背一激灵，但我已经能感觉到它舒缓的效果了。"

    old "I see. Interesting. I didn't know that."
    new "I see. Interesting. I didn't know that.\n我明白了。有意思。我以前不知道。"

    old "So you've never done anything similar with your tail? I mean, I know that it's quite strong, but that still seems kind of odd to me."
    new "So you've never done anything similar with your tail? I mean, I know that it's quite strong, but that still seems kind of odd to me.\n所以你们从来没对尾巴做过类似的事吗？我是说，我知道尾巴很强壮，但总觉得还是有点不可思议。"

    old "Hmm... I guess we just don't really need to."
    new "Hmm... I guess we just don't really need to.\n嗯……我想我们就是不太需要吧。"

    old "Our tails are sturdy and we can walk long distances without feeling any sort of pain, even if we do get tired overall like you do. And, like snakes, we shed our whole tail skin regularly. I'd say around two or three times a year. When that happens, the skin on our tails gets renewed and any small imperfection we may have had goes away."
    new "Our tails are sturdy and we can walk long distances without feeling any sort of pain, even if we do get tired overall like you do. And, like snakes, we shed our whole tail skin regularly. I'd say around two or three times a year. When that happens, the skin on our tails gets renewed and any small imperfection we may have had goes away.\n我们的尾巴很结实，走再远的路也不会感到任何疼痛，虽然整体上也会像你们一样累。而且，像蛇一样，我们会定期蜕掉整条尾巴上的皮。我想一年大概两三次吧。蜕皮之后，尾巴上的皮肤焕然一新，之前可能有过的任何小瑕疵都会消失。"

    old "That's very int-- aah!"
    new "That's very int-- aah!\n那真的非常……啊！"

    old "[protag]? What happened?"
    new "[protag]? What happened?\n[protag]？怎么了？"

    old "I-I think I cut my right foot on something in the river."
    new "I-I think I cut my right foot on something in the river.\n我、我想我的右脚被河里的什么东西割伤了。"

    old "I grit my teeth as a sharp pain shoots through my body."
    new "I grit my teeth as a sharp pain shoots through my body.\n一阵剧痛贯穿全身，我咬紧了牙关。"

    old "I head back to shore, trying not to set my right foot down flat as I go. Once I'm there, I sit down on the ground and inspect my foot. There is a bit of blood and it looks like something got lodged inside. A thorn of some kind?"
    new "I head back to shore, trying not to set my right foot down flat as I go. Once I'm there, I sit down on the ground and inspect my foot. There is a bit of blood and it looks like something got lodged inside. A thorn of some kind?\n我朝岸边走去，尽量不让右脚平着着地。到了之后，我坐在地上查看自己的脚。有点血，看起来像是有什么东西扎进去了。某种刺？"

    old "Enok rushes to my side, a worried expression on his face. It's kind of cute that he's so concerned, but I'd appreciate it if he didn't make me feel like I was dying over something minor like this."
    new "Enok rushes to my side, a worried expression on his face. It's kind of cute that he's so concerned, but I'd appreciate it if he didn't make me feel like I was dying over something minor like this.\nEnok 冲到我身边，脸上写满担忧。他这么关心我，是挺可爱的，不过我倒希望他别为这点小伤就摆出我快死了一样的架势。"

    old "First of all, relax. It's not that big of a deal."
    new "First of all, relax. It's not that big of a deal.\n首先，放轻松。这没什么大不了的。"

    old "Yes. I promise, I'm not dying."
    new "Yes. I promise, I'm not dying.\n是的。我保证，我不会死的。"

    old "Enok lets out a small laugh."
    new "Enok lets out a small laugh.\nEnok 轻轻笑了一声。"

    old "I guess it would be pretty ironic if this is what ended up killing the Envoy of Grimoire after all we've been through."
    new "I guess it would be pretty ironic if this is what ended up killing the Envoy of Grimoire after all we've been through.\n我想，要是经历了这么多之后，最后竟然是这点小伤要了 Grimoire 使节的命，那也太讽刺了。"

    old "Still, I would like to take a look at it if you don't mind."
    new "Still, I would like to take a look at it if you don't mind.\n不过，如果你不介意的话，我还是想看看。"

    old "Alright, but, as I said, it's nothing."
    new "Alright, but, as I said, it's nothing.\n好吧，但正如我说的，没什么。"

    old "Enok gently takes my foot into his hands and carefully examines it. I may be overthinking it, but I get the impression that he's indulging himself a bit as his fingertips brush against my skin."
    new "Enok gently takes my foot into his hands and carefully examines it. I may be overthinking it, but I get the impression that he's indulging himself a bit as his fingertips brush against my skin.\nEnok 轻轻地把我的脚捧在手里，仔细查看。也许是我多想了，但我觉得当他的指尖擦过我的皮肤时，他有点在趁机享受。"

    old "His thumb caresses the side of my foot as he extracts the thorn from my foot with his free hand and throws it away."
    new "His thumb caresses the side of my foot as he extracts the thorn from my foot with his free hand and throws it away.\n他的拇指抚过我的脚侧，另一只手把刺拔了出来，随手扔掉。"

    old "Ouch!"
    new "Ouch!\n哎哟！"

    old "Sorry. Let me massage it a little to ease your pain..."
    new "Sorry. Let me massage it a little to ease your pain...\n抱歉。让我给你揉一揉，减轻点疼痛……"

    old "Enok blushes a bright red, leading me to believe that his intentions aren't completely innocent. This situation is starting to get kind of intimate. If I want our friendship to become something more, this is probably the moment to do something about it."
    new "Enok blushes a bright red, leading me to believe that his intentions aren't completely innocent. This situation is starting to get kind of intimate. If I want our friendship to become something more, this is probably the moment to do something about it.\nEnok 脸红得厉害，这让我觉得他的心思并不完全单纯。眼下的气氛开始变得有些暧昧。如果我想让我们的友谊更进一步，现在大概就是采取行动的时候了。"

    old "Oh! I- I-"
    new "Oh! I- I-\n哦！我、我——"

    old "I pull my foot away from him quickly-- perhaps a little too quickly. Enok's face pales as he continues sputtering awkwardly."
    new "I pull my foot away from him quickly-- perhaps a little too quickly. Enok's face pales as he continues sputtering awkwardly.\n我飞快地把脚从他手里抽回来——也许抽得太快了。Enok 脸色一白，仍在尴尬地支支吾吾。"

    old "I'm sorry, Enok, but... I only see you as a friend."
    new "I'm sorry, Enok, but... I only see you as a friend.\n对不起，Enok，但是……我只把你当朋友。"

    old "O-oh. I was so obvious, wasn't I?"
    new "O-oh. I was so obvious, wasn't I?\n哦、哦。我表现得太明显了，对吧？"

    old "You were. And, I don't want to hurt your feelings, but..."
    new "You were. And, I don't want to hurt your feelings, but...\n确实。而且，我也不想伤害你的感情，可是……"

    old "I understand. It's good that you said something. I... might have ended up doing something even more embarrassing if you didn't."
    new "I understand. It's good that you said something. I... might have ended up doing something even more embarrassing if you didn't.\n我明白。你说出来是好事。不然的话，我……说不定会做出更丢脸的事。"

    old "Are we okay?"
    new "Are we okay?\n我们之间还好吗？"

    old "Yes, yes. Of course. You can count on my help as always."
    new "Yes, yes. Of course. You can count on my help as always.\n还好，还好。当然。你还是可以像往常一样指望我帮忙。"

    old "And your friendship?"
    new "And your friendship?\n那你的友谊呢？"

    old "He says yes quietly, with a sad look on his face. He does mean it. I can tell that much. It's just that it'll take him a little while to get over this."
    new "He says yes quietly, with a sad look on his face. He does mean it. I can tell that much. It's just that it'll take him a little while to get over this.\n他面带哀伤，轻声应了声好。他是真心的，这一点我看得出来。只是他还需要一点时间才能走出来。"

    old "I decide that it's probably best to leave for now, to give him some time to think about it."
    new "I decide that it's probably best to leave for now, to give him some time to think about it.\n我决定眼下最好还是先离开，给他一点时间去消化。"

    old "I think you'll find that I'm very skilled!"
    new "I think you'll find that I'm very skilled!\n我想你会发现，我手法非常娴熟！"

    old "Let me guess: you learned how to give massages from a book?"
    new "Let me guess: you learned how to give massages from a book?\n让我猜猜：你又是从书上学来的按摩？"

    old "What? Don't be ridiculous! This sort of thing comes naturally with practice. You don't need to read a book to learn how to give a good massage."
    new "What? Don't be ridiculous! This sort of thing comes naturally with practice. You don't need to read a book to learn how to give a good massage.\n什么？别胡说了！这种事靠练习自然就会。学按摩哪用得着看书。"

    old "Right. Just like you don't need to read a book to do... other things..."
    new "Right. Just like you don't need to read a book to do... other things...\n对。就像做……别的事……也不用看书一样。"

    old "Enok's cheeks turn a darker shade of red, telling me that he understood my meaning."
    new "Enok's cheeks turn a darker shade of red, telling me that he understood my meaning.\nEnok 的脸颊红得更深了，这告诉我他听懂了我的言外之意。"

    old "I withdraw my foot. Enok looks a bit confused at first, but relaxes when I scoot closer and take his hand in mine."
    new "I withdraw my foot. Enok looks a bit confused at first, but relaxes when I scoot closer and take his hand in mine.\n我把脚收了回来。Enok 起初有点困惑，但当我凑近他、握住他的手时，他便放松了下来。"

    old "He stares at me for a moment before leaning in and stealing a cautious kiss."
    new "He stares at me for a moment before leaning in and stealing a cautious kiss.\n他凝视了我片刻，然后凑过来，试探性地偷来一吻。"

    old "I return it, my own kiss being anything but cautious. From there, it turns into a furious exchange of increasingly passionate kisses."
    new "I return it, my own kiss being anything but cautious. From there, it turns into a furious exchange of increasingly passionate kisses.\n我回吻了他，而且我的吻可一点也不试探。从那里开始，就演变成一场愈发炽热的激吻。"

    old "Enok eventually breaks the pattern and pulls me up from the ground."
    new "Enok eventually breaks the pattern and pulls me up from the ground.\n最终 Enok 打破了节奏，把我从地上拉了起来。"

    old "Not here. It's too rocky. You won't be comfortable when we... do what we're planning to do. Come, follow me."
    new "Not here. It's too rocky. You won't be comfortable when we... do what we're planning to do. Come, follow me.\n别在这里。这里太硌了。等我们……做打算要做的事时，你会不舒服的。来，跟我走。"

    old "I want you now, Enok."
    new "I want you now, Enok.\n我现在就想要你，Enok。"

    old "There's a good place nearby. I promise it's not far."
    new "There's a good place nearby. I promise it's not far.\n附近就有个好地方。我保证不远。"

    old "It only takes us a minute or so to reach the spot Enok was talking about but, in my current state, that still feels too long."
    new "It only takes us a minute or so to reach the spot Enok was talking about but, in my current state, that still feels too long.\n我们只用了一分钟左右就到了 Enok 说的那个地方，但以我现在的状态，这仍然感觉太久了。"

    old "Here, in this pond. The water is calm and not too cold."
    new "Here, in this pond. The water is calm and not too cold.\n就是这里，这片池塘。水面平静，也不算太冷。"

    old "How do you know it's not too cold?"
    new "How do you know it's not too cold?\n你怎么知道不冷？"

    old "Because I'm going to cast my fire spell on it. That should raise the temperature to a comfortable level quickly."
    new "Because I'm going to cast my fire spell on it. That should raise the temperature to a comfortable level quickly.\n因为我要对它施放我的火焰法术。那样应该很快就能把水温升到舒适的程度。"

    old "I should have known."
    new "I should have known.\n我早该想到的。"

    old "Enok gets to work quickly, just as eager to get started as I am."
    new "Enok gets to work quickly, just as eager to get started as I am.\nEnok 很快动起手来，和我一样迫不及待地想开始。"

    old "Once it's ready, we both dive into the small pond and face each other. As I work to steady myself, I take note of the water's warmth all around me. I don't know how much of it was skill and how much of it was luck, but Enok made it the perfect temperature."
    new "Once it's ready, we both dive into the small pond and face each other. As I work to steady myself, I take note of the water's warmth all around me. I don't know how much of it was skill and how much of it was luck, but Enok made it the perfect temperature.\n一切就绪后，我们俩潜入小池塘，面对面站着。我一边稳住身子，一边感受着周身的水温。我不知道这其中有多少是技巧、多少是运气，但 Enok 把水温调得恰到好处。"

    old "I then take a moment to just stare at Enok. Small bubbles glide up the surface of his skin, drawing my attention from his stomach upward. He smiles at me as his hair flows gently around his face, guided by the water's whims."
    new "I then take a moment to just stare at Enok. Small bubbles glide up the surface of his skin, drawing my attention from his stomach upward. He smiles at me as his hair flows gently around his face, guided by the water's whims.\n随后我花了一会儿工夫，只是凝视着 Enok。细小的气泡沿着他的皮肤向上滑去，把我的目光从他的腹部一路引向上方。他朝我微笑，头发随着水的流动，轻柔地拂过他的脸庞。"

    old "He really is beautiful. I've thought that many times before but, once again, I'm striken by how true that thought really is."
    new "He really is beautiful. I've thought that many times before but, once again, I'm striken by how true that thought really is.\n他真的很美。这个想法我此前已有过许多次，但此刻，我再一次被它的真实所震撼。"

    old "As I watch, Enok slowly undresses and lets his clothes float away."
    new "As I watch, Enok slowly undresses and lets his clothes float away.\n在我的注视下，Enok 慢慢脱下衣服，任它们随水漂走。"

    old "My gaze lingers on his chest, slowly taking in the definition of his pectoral musles among other things as my heart beat steadily increases."
    new "My gaze lingers on his chest, slowly taking in the definition of his pectoral musles among other things as my heart beat steadily increases.\n我的目光流连在他的胸膛上，慢慢欣赏着他胸肌的轮廓以及其他种种，心跳也随之稳步加快。"

    old "Enok smirks, giving him a playful look. He definitely has something mischievous going on in his mind."
    new "Enok smirks, giving him a playful look. He definitely has something mischievous going on in his mind.\nEnok 坏坏一笑，冲我投来一个俏皮的眼神。他心里肯定在打着什么鬼主意。"

    old "As I meet his eyes, he swims towards me, closing the distance quickly as if he was going after prey."
    new "As I meet his eyes, he swims towards me, closing the distance quickly as if he was going after prey.\n当我的目光与他相接，他朝我游了过来，飞快地拉近距离，仿佛在追逐猎物一般。"

    old "I wince instinctively, but instead of experiencing anything resembling an attack, he wraps his arms around me gently and lays a kiss on forehead."
    new "I wince instinctively, but instead of experiencing anything resembling an attack, he wraps his arms around me gently and lays a kiss on forehead.\n我本能地缩了一下，但等待我的并非什么攻击，他轻柔地搂住我，在我的额头上落下一吻。"

    old "I open my eyes once more and stare up at him as my fingers touch the stretch of skin just above his belly button."
    new "I open my eyes once more and stare up at him as my fingers touch the stretch of skin just above his belly button.\n我再次睁开眼睛，抬头凝视着他，手指触到他肚脐上方的那片皮肤。"

    old "Enok blushes slightly. I smile to myself and go lower, watching him carefully to see how he reacts. However, Enok doesn't let me play that game."
    new "Enok blushes slightly. I smile to myself and go lower, watching him carefully to see how he reacts. However, Enok doesn't let me play that game.\nEnok 微微脸红。我暗自一笑，手继续向下，一边小心地观察他的反应。然而，Enok 并不让我玩这套把戏。"

    old "We kiss and then we kiss again."
    new "We kiss and then we kiss again.\n我们接吻，然后又一次接吻。"

    old "It's a good thing that Enok remembers that, unlike him, I eventually need to breathe because I almost manage to forget that basic necessity as our bodies press against each other."
    new "It's a good thing that Enok remembers that, unlike him, I eventually need to breathe because I almost manage to forget that basic necessity as our bodies press against each other.\n幸好 Enok 还记得，我不像他，终究需要呼吸——因为当我们的身体紧贴在一起时，我几乎要把这最基本的需要给忘了。"

    old "We eventually find a good rhythm and are able to break up our vortex of pleasure and passion less and less as we continue."
    new "We eventually find a good rhythm and are able to break up our vortex of pleasure and passion less and less as we continue.\n我们最终找到了合拍的节奏，随着继续，我们越来越少地从那欢愉与激情的漩涡中分开。"

    old "This won't be a day I easily forget."
    new "This won't be a day I easily forget.\n这不会是我轻易忘记的一天。"

    old "When I reach the swamps, Enok greets me with an excited smile. An expression like that can only mean one thing, right? Maybe he's found a new recipe."
    new "When I reach the swamps, Enok greets me with an excited smile. An expression like that can only mean one thing, right? Maybe he's found a new recipe.\n我到达沼泽时，Enok 一脸兴奋地笑着迎接我。那样的表情只能说明一件事，对吧？也许他发现了新食谱。"

    old "Hey, friend! Come here! I have great news!"
    new "Hey, friend! Come here! I have great news!\n嘿，朋友！过来！我有个好消息！"

    old "Oh? What happened? Is it a new recipe?"
    new "Oh? What happened? Is it a new recipe?\n哦？怎么了？是新食谱吗？"

    old "Well, yes, but... let me explain. After you left the last time, I was a bit sad."
    new "Well, yes, but... let me explain. After you left the last time, I was a bit sad.\n嗯，是，不过……让我解释一下。你上次离开之后，我有点难过。"

    old "I know, I know! There's no need to say anything. I'm over it now. But, before I came to terms with everything, I ended up wandering around the swamp."
    new "I know, I know! There's no need to say anything. I'm over it now. But, before I came to terms with everything, I ended up wandering around the swamp.\n我知道，我知道！你什么都不用说。我现在已经想开了。不过，在我彻底想通之前，我一直在沼泽里四处游荡。"

    old "My emotions were a mess. I had a hard time figuring out what I wanted to do about them too. Still, despite all the confusion, I did remember that I swore to help you so... Once I'd calmed down, I started to think about how I could use my love of cooking for something more than making you delicious meals."
    new "My emotions were a mess. I had a hard time figuring out what I wanted to do about them too. Still, despite all the confusion, I did remember that I swore to help you so... Once I'd calmed down, I started to think about how I could use my love of cooking for something more than making you delicious meals.\n我当时情绪一团糟，也不知道该怎么面对它们。不过，尽管混乱，我仍记得自己发誓要帮你，所以……冷静下来之后，我开始思考，怎样能让我对烹饪的热爱，不只是用来给你做美味佳肴。"

    old "My dear! I have great news!"
    new "My dear! I have great news!\n亲爱的！我有个好消息！"

    old "Enok quickly closes the gap between us and plants a kiss on my lips. I'm a bit taken by surprise so I remain frozen in place."
    new "Enok quickly closes the gap between us and plants a kiss on my lips. I'm a bit taken by surprise so I remain frozen in place.\nEnok 飞快地拉近我们之间的距离，在我唇上印下一吻。我有点猝不及防，于是僵在了原地。"

    old "You... what news?"
    new "You... what news?\n你……什么消息？"

    old "After what happened last time, I was so happy that I couldn't stand still. I started wandering the swamps, looking for more ingredients that I could use to prepare more dishes for you. Then, I got an enlightening idea: why not do something more?"
    new "After what happened last time, I was so happy that I couldn't stand still. I started wandering the swamps, looking for more ingredients that I could use to prepare more dishes for you. Then, I got an enlightening idea: why not do something more?\n上次那件事之后，我高兴得坐立不安。我开始在沼泽里四处游荡，寻找更多食材，好为你做更多菜。然后，我有了个豁然开朗的想法：为什么不做得更多一点呢？"

    old "More than... what? Food?"
    new "More than... what? Food?\n更多……什么？不只是食物？"

    old "Yes. I decided to try to apply my skills to something new."
    new "Yes. I decided to try to apply my skills to something new.\n是的。我决定试着把我的本事用在新东西上。"

    old "I remembered that I had a few alchemy books. I know I'm not as skilled as Apolimesho-- that would take years of practice-- but, I am a skilled cook. Cooking is actually pretty similar to alchemy: you take a set of ingredients and turn it into something different through various processes. That made me think."
    new "I remembered that I had a few alchemy books. I know I'm not as skilled as Apolimesho-- that would take years of practice-- but, I am a skilled cook. Cooking is actually pretty similar to alchemy: you take a set of ingredients and turn it into something different through various processes. That made me think.\n我想起自己有几本炼金术的书。我知道我不如 Apolimesho 熟练——那需要多年练习——不过，我是个熟练的厨师。烹饪其实和炼金术相当相似：取一组原料，通过各种工序，把它变成不同的东西。这让我动了心思。"

    old "And, as I was thinking, I was scouting the swamps, observing every tree, every bush, every abandoned caravan... It's incredible how many goods are still left out there because bandits and nagas don't know what they are or how to use them."
    new "And, as I was thinking, I was scouting the swamps, observing every tree, every bush, every abandoned caravan... It's incredible how many goods are still left out there because bandits and nagas don't know what they are or how to use them.\n于是，我一边想，一边在沼泽里搜寻，观察每一棵树、每一丛灌木、每一辆被遗弃的大篷车……真是难以置信，外面还留着那么多货物，就因为强盗和 naga 不知道它们是什么、该怎么用。"

    old "At one point, I found a caravan that had been on it's way to Icesilia. I don't even know where that is, but my guess is that they were lost since I don't think you can get there quickly by passing through the swamp."
    new "At one point, I found a caravan that had been on it's way to Icesilia. I don't even know where that is, but my guess is that they were lost since I don't think you can get there quickly by passing through the swamp.\n有一回，我发现一辆原本要前往 Icesilia 的大篷车。我甚至不知道那地方在哪儿，但我猜他们是迷路了，因为我觉得穿过沼泽不可能很快到得了那里。"

    old "I know where it is. It's on the eastern part of Issanis, past the Everburn Mountains. It's quite far from here to be honest. What was in the caravan?"
    new "I know where it is. It's on the eastern part of Issanis, past the Everburn Mountains. It's quite far from here to be honest. What was in the caravan?\n我知道那地方。它在 Issanis 东部，要越过 Everburn Mountains。说实话离这里相当远。车里装的是什么？"

    old "That's what's incredible! I found a whole crate full of rare alchemy ingredients! The recipient was supposed to be someone named Haros. Anyway, I took the ingredients since I figured it'd be better than letting them rot out in the swamp."
    new "That's what's incredible! I found a whole crate full of rare alchemy ingredients! The recipient was supposed to be someone named Haros. Anyway, I took the ingredients since I figured it'd be better than letting them rot out in the swamp.\n这正是最不可思议的地方！我找到整整一箱稀有炼金原料！收货人本该是个叫 Haros 的人。总之，我把原料拿走了，因为我想总比让它们在沼泽里烂掉强。"

    old "Well... technically that is theft, but it's not like we have the time to send them back to whoever this Haros is. We have a war to fight here."
    new "Well... technically that is theft, but it's not like we have the time to send them back to whoever this Haros is. We have a war to fight here.\n嗯……严格说这算是偷窃，但我们也没时间把它们送还给这个叫 Haros 的人。我们这儿还有仗要打呢。"

    old "That's the spirit!"
    new "That's the spirit!\n就是这个劲头！"

    old "Of course he'd agree with me on this. Still, it's not like I was lying. We really don't have the time to deliver missing crates right now. Besides, who knows how long those ingredients were out in the swamp? They might not have survived the journey in the first place."
    new "Of course he'd agree with me on this. Still, it's not like I was lying. We really don't have the time to deliver missing crates right now. Besides, who knows how long those ingredients were out in the swamp? They might not have survived the journey in the first place.\n他当然会同意我的看法。不过，我也没在说谎。我们现在确实没时间去送还丢失的货箱。再说，谁知道那些原料在沼泽里放了多久？它们说不定本来就没能撑过那段路程。"

    old "I kind of already used the ingredients anyway."
    new "I kind of already used the ingredients anyway.\n反正我差不多已经把原料给用了。"

    old "I rub my forehead and attempt to alleviate my oncoming headache. I'm not going to bother arguing with him right now."
    new "I rub my forehead and attempt to alleviate my oncoming headache. I'm not going to bother arguing with him right now.\n我揉了揉额头，想缓解正在升起的头疼。我现在不打算跟他争辩。"

    old "So, I started mixing the edible ingredients with some other ones I already had in my shelter and ended up creating this!"
    new "So, I started mixing the edible ingredients with some other ones I already had in my shelter and ended up creating this!\n于是，我开始把这些可食用的原料，和我棚子里已有的另一些东西混在一起，最后做出了这个！"

    old "Ta-dah! I mixed the ingredients with some strawberries and created Enok's Strawberry Delice!"
    new "Ta-dah! I mixed the ingredients with some strawberries and created Enok's Strawberry Delice!\n锵锵！我把那些原料和草莓混合，做出了 Enok's Strawberry Delice！"

    old "Enok's Strawberry Delice?"
    new "Enok's Strawberry Delice?\nEnok's Strawberry Delice？"

    old "Well, it sounds better than 'Regenerating Strawberry Jam', don't you think? Anyway, eating a spoon of this will grant the consumer a powerful regenerating effect. It's as powerful as my magic, but without the need for me to cast any kind of spell!"
    new "Well, it sounds better than 'Regenerating Strawberry Jam', don't you think? Anyway, eating a spoon of this will grant the consumer a powerful regenerating effect. It's as powerful as my magic, but without the need for me to cast any kind of spell!\n嗯，这名字总比 Regenerating Strawberry Jam 好听吧，你不觉得吗？总之，吃一勺这个，就能给食用者带来强大的再生效果。它和我的魔法一样强，却不需要我施任何法术！"

    old "Voilà! Heart shaped chocolates! But please, don't eat them now, as tempting as that may be!"
    new "Voilà! Heart shaped chocolates! But please, don't eat them now, as tempting as that may be!\n瞧！心形巧克力！不过，请别现在吃，虽然它们确实很诱人！"

    old "Come on, Enok. Can't I have just one?"
    new "Come on, Enok. Can't I have just one?\n拜托，Enok。就不能让我吃一颗吗？"

    old "Well... I mean, you can, but it'd be a waste. Just one of these chocolates will fully restore your health, defense and vigor! It'd be better to save them for a tough battle."
    new "Well... I mean, you can, but it'd be a waste. Just one of these chocolates will fully restore your health, defense and vigor! It'd be better to save them for a tough battle.\n嗯……我是说，可以是可以，但那就浪费了。只要一颗这样的巧克力，就能完全恢复你的生命、防御和活力！最好还是留着等硬仗时再用。"

    old "I guess you're right, Enok. They just look so good and-- wait! They seriously restore your health, defense and vigor?"
    new "I guess you're right, Enok. They just look so good and-- wait! They seriously restore your health, defense and vigor?\n我想你说得对，Enok。它们只是看起来太诱人了，而且——等等！它们真能恢复生命、防御和活力？"

    old "That sounds too good to be true. Is there a downside? There must be one."
    new "That sounds too good to be true. Is there a downside? There must be one.\n这好得有点不真实。有什么缺点吗？肯定有吧。"

    old "Eh, yes. Sadly, the alchemy ingredients I used were very rare and, because of that, there was a limited quantity of them. There isn't enough left over to make anything else. We need to use what we have sparingly, but I think there's more than enough to help us win several battles, don't you think?"
    new "Eh, yes. Sadly, the alchemy ingredients I used were very rare and, because of that, there was a limited quantity of them. There isn't enough left over to make anything else. We need to use what we have sparingly, but I think there's more than enough to help us win several battles, don't you think?\n呃，是的。可惜的是，我用的炼金原料非常稀有，因此数量有限。剩下的已经不够再做别的了。我们得省着用，不过我想，这些也足够帮我们打赢好几场战斗了，你不觉得吗？"

    old "I agree. A weapon or a piece of armor would have lasted longer, but these can give us a vital boost in battle when we need it most. And they can be used by anyone. Your dish may end up being the key to our survival in our upcoming battles."
    new "I agree. A weapon or a piece of armor would have lasted longer, but these can give us a vital boost in battle when we need it most. And they can be used by anyone. Your dish may end up being the key to our survival in our upcoming battles.\n我同意。一把武器或一件护甲能撑更久，但这些能在我们最需要的时候，在战斗中给我们关键的增益。而且谁都能用。你做的这东西，说不定会成为我们接下来几场战斗里活下来的关键。"

    old "You did a great job, Enok."
    new "You did a great job, Enok.\n你干得漂亮，Enok。"

    old "Enok seems to be positively glowing at the praise."
    new "Enok seems to be positively glowing at the praise.\nEnok 被夸得似乎整个人都在发光。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]."
    new "Thank you, [protag].\n谢谢你，[protag]。"

    old "Oh, and... let's not tell Apolimesho about this. For two reasons: first, the crate's contents didn't technically belong to you and, second, if he learns that you used rare alchemy incredients in such an unorthodox way, he might be even more furious."
    new "Oh, and... let's not tell Apolimesho about this. For two reasons: first, the crate's contents didn't technically belong to you and, second, if he learns that you used rare alchemy incredients in such an unorthodox way, he might be even more furious.\n哦，还有……这件事我们别告诉 Apolimesho。原因有二：第一，那箱东西严格来说并不属于你；第二，要是他得知你用这么离经叛道的方式用掉了稀有炼金原料，他可能会更生气。"

    old "I'll be as quiet as a fish."
    new "I'll be as quiet as a fish.\n我会像鱼一样安静。"

    old "I leave the swamp, taking Enok's gift with me. It's bound to come in handy in future battles against the undead."
    new "I leave the swamp, taking Enok's gift with me. It's bound to come in handy in future battles against the undead.\n我带着 Enok 的礼物离开了沼泽。在将来对抗亡灵的战斗中，它一定会派上用场。"

    old "I unconsciously end up skipping as I make my way to the swamp today. Just seeing Enok makes me feel really happy lately."
    new "I unconsciously end up skipping as I make my way to the swamp today. Just seeing Enok makes me feel really happy lately.\n今天去沼泽的路上，我不自觉地蹦跳了起来。近来，光是见到 Enok，就让我感到特别开心。"

    old "I slow down when I see Enok's face. His expression is oddly serious and his greeting is colder than I expected. Something is going on."
    new "I slow down when I see Enok's face. His expression is oddly serious and his greeting is colder than I expected. Something is going on.\n看到 Enok 的脸，我放慢了脚步。他的表情异常严肃，问候也比我想象的冷淡。一定出了什么事。"

    old "Enok? What happened? Is Sylrissa okay?"
    new "Enok? What happened? Is Sylrissa okay?\nEnok？怎么了？Sylrissa 还好吗？"

    old "Sylrissa? It's interesting that you're asking me about her."
    new "Sylrissa? It's interesting that you're asking me about her.\nSylrissa？你居然问我她的情况，真有意思。"

    old "Why...?"
    new "Why...?\n为什么……？"

    old "I know what happened between you and Sylrissa, [protag]. And, to be completely honest, I can understand why you would be attracted to her. I am-- ahem-- was too."
    new "I know what happened between you and Sylrissa, [protag]. And, to be completely honest, I can understand why you would be attracted to her. I am-- ahem-- was too.\n我知道你和 Sylrissa 之间发生了什么，[protag]。而且，说句实在话，我能理解你为什么会被她吸引。我也——咳咳——曾经也是。"

    old "I suspected as much. You two always seemed close. Closer than people who are just friends usually are. I often wondered if there was something more going on between the two of you."
    new "I suspected as much. You two always seemed close. Closer than people who are just friends usually are. I often wondered if there was something more going on between the two of you.\n我早就隐约猜到了。你们俩一直很亲近，比一般朋友要亲近得多。我常常想，你们俩之间是不是有更深的什么。"

    old "Nice try, [protag]. But we're not talking about me right now. We're talking about you and how you slept with my best friend behind my back. Don't try to change the topic again."
    new "Nice try, [protag]. But we're not talking about me right now. We're talking about you and how you slept with my best friend behind my back. Don't try to change the topic again.\n转移得不错，[protag]。但我们现在说的不是我。说的是你，以及你怎么背着我跟我最好的朋友上了床。别又想转移话题。"

    old "Err... I hope I didn't ruin anything?"
    new "Err... I hope I didn't ruin anything?\n呃……希望我没有毁掉什么？"

    old "You need to be more specific. Ruin my friendship with Sylrissa? Ruin our blooming relationship? Ruin the mood?"
    new "You need to be more specific. Ruin my friendship with Sylrissa? Ruin our blooming relationship? Ruin the mood?\n你得说具体点。是毁掉我和 Sylrissa 的友谊？还是毁掉我们正萌芽的感情？还是毁了这气氛？"

    old "I am sorry, Enok. I knew it was wrong, but I... Sylrissa was..."
    new "I am sorry, Enok. I knew it was wrong, but I... Sylrissa was...\n对不起，Enok。我知道那不对，可我……Sylrissa 她……"

    old "I'm digging myself in deep with that last bit. I pull back a bit and try something a little less likely to get me killed."
    new "I'm digging myself in deep with that last bit. I pull back a bit and try something a little less likely to get me killed.\n我最后那句话越描越黑。我收敛了一点，换了个更不容易送命的说法。"

    old "It just happened. I'm sorry."
    new "It just happened. I'm sorry.\n事情就那么发生了。对不起。"

    old "Enok remains silent. However, as much as I try, I'm unable to spot any traces of anger or disappointment on his face. He almost seems... relaxed? But that's impossible, isn't it?"
    new "Enok remains silent. However, as much as I try, I'm unable to spot any traces of anger or disappointment on his face. He almost seems... relaxed? But that's impossible, isn't it?\nEnok 仍沉默着。然而，无论我怎么找，都没法在他脸上看到一丝愤怒或失望的痕迹。他看起来甚至有点……平静？但那不可能吧，不是吗？"

    old "Enok? Say something."
    new "Enok? Say something.\nEnok？说句话吧。"

    old "I think the best solution is for us all to be open with each other. Sylrissa is not here at the moment, but I think that what we should do now is meet, the three of us, face to face, and talk about all of this. I don't want anyone to be hurt."
    new "I think the best solution is for us all to be open with each other. Sylrissa is not here at the moment, but I think that what we should do now is meet, the three of us, face to face, and talk about all of this. I don't want anyone to be hurt.\n我想最好的办法，是我们彼此都坦诚相待。Sylrissa 现在不在这里，但我想我们现在该做的，是我们三个当面见一面，把这些事都摊开来说。我不想任何人受到伤害。"

    old "I don't want anyone to be hurt either."
    new "I don't want anyone to be hurt either.\n我也不想任何人受伤害。"

    old "I'm sure that's easier said than done though."
    new "I'm sure that's easier said than done though.\n不过我敢说，这说起来容易做起来难。"

    old "Good. Now, please go. The next time we meet we'll talk this situation over and find a solution."
    new "Good. Now, please go. The next time we meet we'll talk this situation over and find a solution.\n好。现在，请先走吧。下次见面时，我们再好好谈这件事，找出解决办法。"

    old "I take my leave, unsure what will await me the next time I set foot in this place."
    new "I take my leave, unsure what will await me the next time I set foot in this place.\n我告辞离开，不知道下次踏进这里时，等待我的会是什么。"

    old "She is fine. We did just have a bit of an argument though."
    new "She is fine. We did just have a bit of an argument though.\n她没事。我们只是刚刚吵了一架。"

    old "About what?"
    new "About what?\n吵什么？"

    old "She insisted that you're sleeping with someone else on our team because we're nagas... which means we're too different from the others. Our exterior appearence for one thing. Then, the beast-like aura that surrounds us, even when we're completely calm. It makes you uncomfortable, doesn't it? Maybe even a little afraid?"
    new "She insisted that you're sleeping with someone else on our team because we're nagas... which means we're too different from the others. Our exterior appearence for one thing. Then, the beast-like aura that surrounds us, even when we're completely calm. It makes you uncomfortable, doesn't it? Maybe even a little afraid?\n她坚持说，你和队里的别人上床，是因为我们是 naga……也就是说，我们和别人太不一样了。光是外表就是一方面。还有，即便我们完全平静时，周身也笼罩着一种野兽般的气息。这让你很不自在，不是吗？也许还有点害怕？"

    old "I remain speechless for a few seconds, needing time to process all of the information that Enok just dumped on me. What the hell?"
    new "I remain speechless for a few seconds, needing time to process all of the information that Enok just dumped on me. What the hell?\n我哑口无言了几秒，需要时间来消化 Enok 刚刚一股脑倒给我的这些信息。搞什么啊？"

    old "Hold on, Enok! That's absolutely not true!"
    new "Hold on, Enok! That's absolutely not true!\n等等，Enok！这绝对不是真的！"

    old "So you're claiming that you didn't sleep with someone else?"
    new "So you're claiming that you didn't sleep with someone else?\n所以你的意思是，你没有和别人上床？"

    old "Ah, no... That is true and I am sorry."
    new "Ah, no... That is true and I am sorry.\n啊，不是……那倒是真的，我很抱歉。"

    old "But Enok! You being a naga has nothing to do with it. I think both you and Sylrissa are great. I can't deny that you look different from the other races I've encountered so far and maybe I do get a little scared when you make a sudden movement I wasn't ready for, but I also know that you're both good people."
    new "But Enok! You being a naga has nothing to do with it. I think both you and Sylrissa are great. I can't deny that you look different from the other races I've encountered so far and maybe I do get a little scared when you make a sudden movement I wasn't ready for, but I also know that you're both good people.\n但是 Enok！你是 naga 这件事跟那毫无关系。我觉得你和 Sylrissa 都很棒。我不否认，你们看起来和我迄今遇到的其他种族不一样，也许当你做出我没防备的突然动作时，我确实会有点害怕，但我也知道，你们俩都是好人。"

    old "That's what I told Sylrissa too."
    new "That's what I told Sylrissa too.\n我也是这么跟 Sylrissa 说的。"

    old "Really? Then why bring it up?"
    new "Really? Then why bring it up?\n是吗？那为什么要提？"

    old "Because you still slept with someone else even though I thought... I thought we had something special going on. I told you how rare it is for us nagas to have stable relationships, right? I thought I'd found mine but, apparently, I was wrong."
    new "Because you still slept with someone else even though I thought... I thought we had something special going on. I told you how rare it is for us nagas to have stable relationships, right? I thought I'd found mine but, apparently, I was wrong.\n因为你还是和别人上了床，即便我以为……我以为我们之间有某种特别的东西。我跟你说过，我们 naga 之间稳定的感情有多罕见，对吧？我以为我找到了属于我的那份，但显然，我错了。"

    old "This hurt me, [protag]. It hurt me a lot."
    new "This hurt me, [protag]. It hurt me a lot.\n这伤害了我，[protag]。伤得很深。"

    old "Damn it. I should have known my past actions would come back to haunt me. There was no way it could have stayed a secret forever."
    new "Damn it. I should have known my past actions would come back to haunt me. There was no way it could have stayed a secret forever.\n该死。我早该知道，我过去的所作所为会回来纠缠我。这种事不可能永远瞒得住。"

    old "I guess I need to make a decision. Is Enok the one I want to be with? Sharing me with someone doesn't seem to be an option so I need to answer a hard question. Do I love him?"
    new "I guess I need to make a decision. Is Enok the one I want to be with? Sharing me with someone doesn't seem to be an option so I need to answer a hard question. Do I love him?\n我想我需要做个决定。Enok 是我想在一起的人吗？和别人分享我，似乎不是一个选项，所以我必须回答一个艰难的问题。我爱他吗？"

    old "I'm sorry, Enok. I guess I mistook what we had for love, but... now that I'm forced to commit to the idea, I can't."
    new "I'm sorry, Enok. I guess I mistook what we had for love, but... now that I'm forced to commit to the idea, I can't.\n对不起，Enok。我想我把我们之间的感情错当成了爱，但……如今被逼着要作出承诺时，我做不到。"

    old "Everything that happend between us... It was fun. I enjoyed it, but..."
    new "Everything that happend between us... It was fun. I enjoyed it, but...\n我们之间发生的一切……都很快乐。我很享受，可是……"

    old "It was fun. Like always. Good sex, but nothing more besides that. Kind of how it was back with our tribe."
    new "It was fun. Like always. Good sex, but nothing more besides that. Kind of how it was back with our tribe.\n确实很快乐。一如既往。性很美好，但也仅此而已。有点像当年在我们部落里的样子。"

    old "It's fine. I mean, it's not, but... I prefer knowing now, before I grew any more attached to you. It hurts, but it could have ended up hurting much worse."
    new "It's fine. I mean, it's not, but... I prefer knowing now, before I grew any more attached to you. It hurts, but it could have ended up hurting much worse.\n没关系。我是说，其实并不好受，但……我宁愿现在知道，趁我对你陷得还不算太深。虽然痛，但总比将来痛得更厉害要好。"

    old "I'll... give you some space. I can't imagine you want to see my face right now."
    new "I'll... give you some space. I can't imagine you want to see my face right now.\n我……给你一些空间。我想你现在大概不想看到我这张脸。"

    old "That'd probably be for the best. Thank you."
    new "That'd probably be for the best. Thank you.\n那样大概最好。谢谢。"

    old "Before I go though... I can still count on you for our mission, right?"
    new "Before I go though... I can still count on you for our mission, right?\n不过在我走之前……我们的任务，我还是能指望你的，对吧？"

    old "Yes. Of course. I should be fine when I'm with the others. Staying alone with you is what hurts."
    new "Yes. Of course. I should be fine when I'm with the others. Staying alone with you is what hurts.\n当然。和别人在一起时，我应该没事。只有和你单独相处才让我难过。"

    old "I nod and take my leave. I feel sorry for Enok but, as he said, it's probably better that I was clear about my intentions now, before things became too serious."
    new "I nod and take my leave. I feel sorry for Enok but, as he said, it's probably better that I was clear about my intentions now, before things became too serious.\n我点点头，告辞离开。我为 Enok 感到难过，但正如他所说，趁事情还没变得太严重，现在就把我的想法说清楚，大概更好。"

    old "Look, I know this is not an excuse. But everything happened so fast. This whole thing. Not long ago, I was just a normal person, living my life."
    new "Look, I know this is not an excuse. But everything happened so fast. This whole thing. Not long ago, I was just a normal person, living my life.\n听着，我知道这不是借口。但一切都发生得太快了。这整件事。不久之前，我还只是个普通人，过着自己的日子。"

    old "A [pCharProf], right?"
    new "A [pCharProf], right?\n一个 [pCharProf]，对吧？"

    old "Yes. Nothing more. Then suddenly I got involved in all of this. I mean, it was my choice, but sometimes I feel like I didn't really have a choice. But about us, I know I have one. I know the right choice is you, Enok."
    new "Yes. Nothing more. Then suddenly I got involved in all of this. I mean, it was my choice, but sometimes I feel like I didn't really have a choice. But about us, I know I have one. I know the right choice is you, Enok.\n是的。仅此而已。然后我忽然就卷进了这一切。我是说，那是我自己的选择，但有时我又觉得，自己其实别无选择。可关于我们，我知道我是有选择的。我知道正确的选择是你，Enok。"

    old "Enok looks at me dubiously but doesn't say anything in return."
    new "Enok looks at me dubiously but doesn't say anything in return.\nEnok 半信半疑地看着我，却没有回话。"

    old "I know it probably sounds like a lie after everything I've done, but it's true. I... I need you to believe me."
    new "I know it probably sounds like a lie after everything I've done, but it's true. I... I need you to believe me.\n我知道，在我做了那么多事之后，这话听起来大概像谎言，但它是真的。我……我需要你相信我。"

    old "I know, I know, it's just... you don't understand. I have never been this close to anyone else in my entire life, except maybe Sylrissa. I don't know how this works. It's all so new to me, and-"
    new "I know, I know, it's just... you don't understand. I have never been this close to anyone else in my entire life, except maybe Sylrissa. I don't know how this works. It's all so new to me, and-\n我知道，我知道，只是……你不明白。我这辈子从没和任何人这么亲近过，也许除了 Sylrissa。我不知道这种事该怎么处理。这一切对我来说都太新鲜了，而且——"

    old "I silence him by kissing him on his mouth. He seems a bit reluctant at first, but he eventually lets himself go and puts a hand tenderly on my back."
    new "I silence him by kissing him on his mouth. He seems a bit reluctant at first, but he eventually lets himself go and puts a hand tenderly on my back.\n我吻上他的唇，止住了他的话。起初他有些迟疑，但最终还是放任了自己，温柔地把一只手搭在我背上。"

    old "It's just the beginning of another wonderful moment with Enok. One of the many I hope the future has reserved us."
    new "It's just the beginning of another wonderful moment with Enok. One of the many I hope the future has reserved us.\n这只是与 Enok 共度的又一个美妙时刻的开端。我希望，未来还为我们预备了更多这样的时刻。"

    old "I head to the swamps to visit Enok, but when I arrive I can't seem to find him. Sylrissa isn't here either so I'm not sure what's going on."
    new "I head to the swamps to visit Enok, but when I arrive I can't seem to find him. Sylrissa isn't here either so I'm not sure what's going on.\n我前往沼泽去看望 Enok，但到了之后却找不到他。Sylrissa 也不在，所以我不清楚出了什么事。"

    old "Suddenly, I hear a voice coming from the direction of the shelter that Enok built. I move closer but I still can't see him. Luckily, he calls for me again."
    new "Suddenly, I hear a voice coming from the direction of the shelter that Enok built. I move closer but I still can't see him. Luckily, he calls for me again.\n突然，我听到 Enok 搭的那个棚子方向传来声音。我走近一些，却还是看不到他。幸好，他又喊了我一声。"

    old "Here, inside the tent!"
    new "Here, inside the tent!\n在这儿，帐篷里面！"

    old "I enter the tent, which looks much bigger than I remember it being, and find Enok intently reading a book."
    new "I enter the tent, which looks much bigger than I remember it being, and find Enok intently reading a book.\n我走进帐篷——它看起来比我印象中大了不少——发现 Enok 正专心地读着一本书。"

    old "Enok is relaxing on his side, a comfortable looking blanket underneath him so that he's not lying on the ground."
    new "Enok is relaxing on his side, a comfortable looking blanket underneath him so that he's not lying on the ground.\nEnok 侧身躺着休息，身下垫着一条看起来很舒服的毯子，这样他就不用直接躺在地上。"

    old "I can't help but notice that he's not wearing anything, leaving his perfectly defined chest muscles fully exposed."
    new "I can't help but notice that he's not wearing anything, leaving his perfectly defined chest muscles fully exposed.\n我不由注意到他身上什么都没穿，那线条分明的胸肌完全暴露在外。"

    old "Something about the relaxed nature of the scene strikes me as cute. This is a side of Enok I haven't gotten to see yet."
    new "Something about the relaxed nature of the scene strikes me as cute. This is a side of Enok I haven't gotten to see yet.\n这场景的闲适气息，让我觉得有点可爱。这是我还没见过的 Enok 的另一面。"

    old "I've never seen you reading before."
    new "I've never seen you reading before.\n我以前从没见过你读书的样子。"

    old "I told you that I read a lot of books."
    new "I told you that I read a lot of books.\n我跟你说过，我读过很多书。"

    old "True. Several times, in fact. I just... Well, this the first time I've seen it. I guess what I'm trying to say is that you look cute when you're reading."
    new "True. Several times, in fact. I just... Well, this the first time I've seen it. I guess what I'm trying to say is that you look cute when you're reading.\n没错。其实你还说过好几次。我只是……嗯，这是我头一回亲眼见到。我想说的是，你读书的样子很可爱。"

    old "Heh. I see. Thank you, [protag]."
    new "Heh. I see. Thank you, [protag].\n嘿。我明白了。谢谢你，[protag]。"

    old "A playful smirk crosses Enok's face suddenly as he changes up the subject up a bit."
    new "A playful smirk crosses Enok's face suddenly as he changes up the subject up a bit.\nEnok 脸上忽然闪过一丝俏皮的笑，然后把话题换了一换。"

    old "You'll never guess what kind of book I'm reading."
    new "You'll never guess what kind of book I'm reading.\n你绝对猜不到我在读什么书。"

    old "I suppose that means I'd better placate Enok with a guess."
    new "I suppose that means I'd better placate Enok with a guess.\n我想这意味着我最好还是猜一猜，哄哄 Enok。"

    old "Let's see. You're reading..."
    new "Let's see. You're reading...\n让我想想。你在读……"

    old "No. That is a good guess though. Of course, it'd also be a bit too predictable, don't you think?"
    new "No. That is a good guess though. Of course, it'd also be a bit too predictable, don't you think?\n不对。不过猜得不错。当然，那样也太容易猜了，你不觉得吗？"

    old "Fair enough. It was a little silly to think it'd be that easy."
    new "Fair enough. It was a little silly to think it'd be that easy.\n有道理。指望这么简单就能猜中，是有点傻。"

    old "Exactly, I wouldn't have asked you to guess if I was just reading another cook book."
    new "Exactly, I wouldn't have asked you to guess if I was just reading another cook book.\n正是。如果我只是在读又一本食谱，就不会让你猜了。"

    old "Enok lets out a longing sigh."
    new "Enok lets out a longing sigh.\nEnok 发出一声向往的叹息。"

    old "I wish. Those books are incredibly rare and difficult to find. I do have a couple but I've already read all of them several times. I can probably recite all the information in them off the top of my head at this point."
    new "I wish. Those books are incredibly rare and difficult to find. I do have a couple but I've already read all of them several times. I can probably recite all the information in them off the top of my head at this point.\n但愿如此。那种书极其稀有，很难找。我确实有几本，但每本都已经读了好几遍。事到如今，里面的内容我大概都能倒背如流了。"

    old "Can't you ask that...witch? The one living in the swamps?"
    new "Can't you ask that...witch? The one living in the swamps?\n你不能去问问那个……女巫吗？住在沼泽里的那个？"

    old "The one that I'm pretty sure isn't actually named Bambara."
    new "The one that I'm pretty sure isn't actually named Bambara.\n就是我相当肯定其实并不叫 Bambara 的那个。"

    old "I doubt she has any books. I did find an interesting book talking about the witches of the unforgiving swamps awhile back though."
    new "I doubt she has any books. I did find an interesting book talking about the witches of the unforgiving swamps awhile back though.\n我怀疑她手上根本没什么书。不过前阵子，我确实找到了一本讲那些无赦沼泽女巫的有趣的书。"

    old "That actually does sound kind of intriguing."
    new "That actually does sound kind of intriguing.\n那听起来确实挺有意思。"

    old "Yes, apparently in the past there were a lot of witches living in these swamps. Then the nagas, the bandits, and the witch hunters killed or drove most of them away."
    new "Yes, apparently in the past there were a lot of witches living in these swamps. Then the nagas, the bandits, and the witch hunters killed or drove most of them away.\n是啊，据说过去这些沼泽里住着许多女巫。后来，naga、强盗和猎巫人把她们大多杀掉或赶走了。"

    old "Ugh, no. I've had my fill of undead related things lately considering how many we meet every day on the battlefield."
    new "Ugh, no. I've had my fill of undead related things lately considering how many we meet every day on the battlefield.\n呃，算了。鉴于我们每天在战场上要碰到多少亡灵，最近和亡灵有关的事我已经受够了。"

    old "Oh yeah? I thought you might be interested in finding out more about our enemies."
    new "Oh yeah? I thought you might be interested in finding out more about our enemies.\n哦，是吗？我还以为你会有兴趣多了解了解我们的敌人。"

    old "Not really. Besides, it isn't like there are that many books to read on them. A good majority of what we know about the undead, vampires, zombies, and so on is from folklore. When we kill vampires, they vanish into dust. It's no wonder that they're hard to study properly."
    new "Not really. Besides, it isn't like there are that many books to read on them. A good majority of what we know about the undead, vampires, zombies, and so on is from folklore. When we kill vampires, they vanish into dust. It's no wonder that they're hard to study properly.\n并不太想。再说，关于它们的书本来也不多。我们对亡灵、吸血鬼、僵尸之类的了解，大部分都来自民间传说。我们杀死吸血鬼时，它们会化作尘土消失。难怪很难正经研究它们。"

    old "All right, I give up. What is that book about?"
    new "All right, I give up. What is that book about?\n好吧，我认输。那本书是讲什么的？"

    old "Enok lifts the book up so that I can read the title. Uh... 'How to Please your Lover' by Lilith Gorgo."
    new "Enok lifts the book up so that I can read the title. Uh... 'How to Please your Lover' by Lilith Gorgo.\nEnok 把书举起来，好让我看清书名。呃……Lilith Gorgo 写的 How to Please your Lover。"

    old "Who's Lilith Gorgo?"
    new "Who's Lilith Gorgo?\nLilith Gorgo 是谁？"

    old "Really? That's the first thing you notice after taking a look at this book's cover?"
    new "Really? That's the first thing you notice after taking a look at this book's cover?\n真的吗？你看了这本书的封面，最先注意到的就是这个？"

    old "Okay, fine. That's not the first thing I noticed. I was just trying to avoid bringing up that title. Why are you reading that anyway? You're already a good lover, Enok, trust me!"
    new "Okay, fine. That's not the first thing I noticed. I was just trying to avoid bringing up that title. Why are you reading that anyway? You're already a good lover, Enok, trust me!\n好吧，好。那不是我首先注意到的。我只是想避开那个书名。话说你干嘛读这个？你已经是个很好的情人了，Enok，相信我！"

    old "Of course I am. But there's always room for improvement, right?"
    new "Of course I am. But there's always room for improvement, right?\n我当然好。但人总有进步的空间，对吧？"

    old "You know, Sylrissa used to say I was a terrible cook."
    new "You know, Sylrissa used to say I was a terrible cook.\n你知道吗，Sylrissa 以前常说我是个糟糕透顶的厨子。"

    old "Really? I have a hard time believing that."
    new "Really? I have a hard time believing that.\n真的吗？这我很难相信。"

    old "It's true. That was a really long time ago though. Before we met. And she was right. I was a terrible cook. But then, book after book, attempt after attempt... I got better."
    new "It's true. That was a really long time ago though. Before we met. And she was right. I was a terrible cook. But then, book after book, attempt after attempt... I got better.\n是真的。不过那是很久以前了。在我们相遇之前。而且她说得没错。我当时确实是个糟糕的厨子。但后来，一本接一本书，一次又一次尝试……我越来越好。"

    old "My point is, why should I settle for 'good' when I can be better?"
    new "My point is, why should I settle for 'good' when I can be better?\n我想说的是，既然我能更好，为什么要满足于好呢？"

    old "That's a good point. I'd say that's the right attitude to have."
    new "That's a good point. I'd say that's the right attitude to have.\n说得好。要我说，这种态度很正确。"

    old "Indeed. Now, please undress yourself and lay down here next to me."
    new "Indeed. Now, please undress yourself and lay down here next to me.\n确实。那么，请你脱掉衣服，躺到我旁边来。"

    old "Huh?"
    new "Huh?\n啊？"

    old "Book learning is all well and good, but nothing beats actual experience, right?"
    new "Book learning is all well and good, but nothing beats actual experience, right?\n书本知识固然很好，但什么都比不上亲身实践，对吧？"

    old "I clear my throat as I take a seat next to him."
    new "I clear my throat as I take a seat next to him.\n我清了清嗓子，在他身旁坐下。"

    old "So, um, you want to put what you just learned into practice already?"
    new "So, um, you want to put what you just learned into practice already?\n那么，呃，你想把刚学到的东西马上付诸实践？"

    old "You catch on quickly, [protag]. As a reward, I'll be sure to share all I've learned."
    new "You catch on quickly, [protag]. As a reward, I'll be sure to share all I've learned.\n你领悟得真快，[protag]。作为奖励，我一定会把我学到的一切都分享给你。"

    old "For instance..."
    new "For instance...\n比如说……"

    old "He gingerly touches me along the neck."
    new "He gingerly touches me along the neck.\n他小心翼翼地沿着我的脖颈抚摸。"

    old "Okay, that does actually feel kind of good."
    new "Okay, that does actually feel kind of good.\n好吧，这感觉确实还挺舒服。"

    old "Enok keeps up the motion, gradually applying more force as he goes. The more pressure he applies, the better I feel."
    new "Enok keeps up the motion, gradually applying more force as he goes. The more pressure he applies, the better I feel.\nEnok 继续着动作，力道逐渐加大。他按得越用力，我就越舒服。"

    old "Supposedly, the neck is a very sensual spot for both men and women."
    new "Supposedly, the neck is a very sensual spot for both men and women.\n据说，脖颈对男人和女人来说都是个很敏感的部位。"

    old "Of course, if I really want to make you feel something I should try combining it with another spot."
    new "Of course, if I really want to make you feel something I should try combining it with another spot.\n当然，如果我真想让你感受到什么，就应该试着把它和另一个部位结合起来。"

    old "I don't know how much time passes. At a certain point I lose sense of anything that isn't Enok or the pleasure he's giving me."
    new "I don't know how much time passes. At a certain point I lose sense of anything that isn't Enok or the pleasure he's giving me.\n我不知道过了多久。到了某个时刻，除了 Enok 和他带给我的欢愉，我对一切都失去了感知。"

    old "It seems reading that book was a good idea after all."
    new "It seems reading that book was a good idea after all.\n看来读那本书到底还是个好主意。"

    old "We're quickly approaching the end of our mission. Soon, we'll launch the final assault and everything will be settled one way or another. I should be excited that it's almost over, but..."
    new "We're quickly approaching the end of our mission. Soon, we'll launch the final assault and everything will be settled one way or another. I should be excited that it's almost over, but...\n我们的任务正迅速接近尾声。很快，我们就要发动最后的进攻，一切终将以这样或那样的方式了结。我本该为即将结束而兴奋，可是……"

    old "Lately I've had trouble sleeping. I believe in myself and the team I've assembled, but there's still a nagging dread at the back of my mind. What if we fail? Or... What if we win but we end up losing someone?"
    new "Lately I've had trouble sleeping. I believe in myself and the team I've assembled, but there's still a nagging dread at the back of my mind. What if we fail? Or... What if we win but we end up losing someone?\n最近我一直难以入睡。我信得过自己，也信得过我组建的这支队伍，但脑海深处仍盘踞着一丝挥之不去的恐惧。万一我们失败了呢？或者……万一我们赢了，却失去了某个人呢？"

    old "Of course, I hope that everyone survives the final battle, but if I had to choose survivors..."
    new "Of course, I hope that everyone survives the final battle, but if I had to choose survivors...\n我当然希望每个人都能在最终之战中活下来，但如果非要我选择谁活下来……"

    old "Enok and Sylrissa. They're a formidable duo and they know how to defend themselves. Even so, this battle will be hard. It's likely that we'll be facing our most powerful enemy yet."
    new "Enok and Sylrissa. They're a formidable duo and they know how to defend themselves. Even so, this battle will be hard. It's likely that we'll be facing our most powerful enemy yet.\nEnok 和 Sylrissa。他们是一对令人敬畏的搭档，也知道如何自保。即便如此，这场仗也会很艰难。我们很可能要面对迄今为止最强大的敌人。"

    old "[protag]! You won't get rid of us so easily-- no matter what monster you send us to fight!"
    new "[protag]! You won't get rid of us so easily-- no matter what monster you send us to fight!\n[protag]！你休想这么轻易甩掉我们——不管你派我们去打什么怪物！"

    old "Yes. Know that we're bonded to you now, forever. We have no intention of letting you face this evil alone."
    new "Yes. Know that we're bonded to you now, forever. We have no intention of letting you face this evil alone.\n是的。你要知道，我们现在已与你紧紧相连，直到永远。我们无意让你独自面对这邪恶。"

    old "Enok. I know choosing favorites is horrible, but... More than anyone, I want him to be okay. I don't know what I would do without him."
    new "Enok. I know choosing favorites is horrible, but... More than anyone, I want him to be okay. I don't know what I would do without him.\nEnok。我知道偏心很糟糕，可是……比起任何人，我最希望他能平安。没有他，我真不知该如何是好。"

    old "Don't worry, [protag]. I am not easily killed. You should know that much by now."
    new "Don't worry, [protag]. I am not easily killed. You should know that much by now.\n别担心，[protag]。我可不是那么容易死的。这一点你现在也该知道了。"

    old "Thank you. I know I shouldn't doubt your skills, but... this time, for the first time, I'm afraid of what might happen."
    new "Thank you. I know I shouldn't doubt your skills, but... this time, for the first time, I'm afraid of what might happen.\n谢谢。我知道我不该怀疑你的本事，可是……这一次，是头一回，我害怕可能发生的事。"

    old "No, don't be afraid! Fear is exactly what our enemies want us to feel. Don't let them shake your resolve."
    new "No, don't be afraid! Fear is exactly what our enemies want us to feel. Don't let them shake your resolve.\n不，别害怕！恐惧正是我们的敌人想让我们感受到的。别让他们动摇你的决心。"

    old "You don't need to be afraid when we're with you. Together, nobody can harm us!"
    new "You don't need to be afraid when we're with you. Together, nobody can harm us!\n有我们陪着你，你就不必害怕。只要我们在一起，谁也伤不了我们！"

    old "Fear is natural when you care about someone. But, that doesn't have to be a weakness. It can be a strength too. It makes you careful, alert... It gives you something to fight for."
    new "Fear is natural when you care about someone. But, that doesn't have to be a weakness. It can be a strength too. It makes you careful, alert... It gives you something to fight for.\n在乎一个人的时候，恐惧是自然的。但它不一定就是弱点，也可以是一种力量。它让你谨慎、警觉……它给了你为之奋战的理由。"

    old "Thank you. Maybe you're right..."
    new "Thank you. Maybe you're right...\n谢谢。也许你说得对……"

    old "I know I'm dreaming, but I keep wondering if it's a regular one or if Enok has something to do with it. Can dark magic do something like this? I have no idea what he is really capable of."
    new "I know I'm dreaming, but I keep wondering if it's a regular one or if Enok has something to do with it. Can dark magic do something like this? I have no idea what he is really capable of.\n我知道自己在做梦，却忍不住想，这到底是寻常的梦，还是和 Enok 有关。黑暗魔法能做到这种事吗？我完全不知道他究竟有多大能耐。"

    old "What do you think, Enok? Maybe [protag] would like us to help relax [himher] a bit?"
    new "What do you think, Enok? Maybe [protag] would like us to help relax [himher] a bit?\n你觉得呢，Enok？也许 [protag] 希望我们帮 [himher] 放松一下？"

    old "Oh, yes. I think that's a fine idea. Sit back and let us do our magic, [protag]..."
    new "Oh, yes. I think that's a fine idea. Sit back and let us do our magic, [protag]...\n哦，是的。我觉得这主意不错。坐好，让我们施展我们的魔法吧，[protag]……"

    old "You're wondering if this is a dream, right? Who knows? Maybe it is. Or maybe I'm using dark magic to trick you into thinking about me."
    new "You're wondering if this is a dream, right? Who knows? Maybe it is. Or maybe I'm using dark magic to trick you into thinking about me.\n你在想这是不是梦，对吧？谁知道呢？也许确实是梦。又或者，是我在用黑暗魔法诱你想着我。"

    old "It doesn't matter. What matters is that I want you to feel better. Think about me, imagine that I'm fishing in the river..."
    new "It doesn't matter. What matters is that I want you to feel better. Think about me, imagine that I'm fishing in the river...\n这不重要。重要的是，我想让你感觉好起来。想着我，想象我正在河里钓鱼……"

    old "I imagine Enok. He is holding a fish in his mouth, his sharp teeth holding it firmly in place. He could kill it in an instant, but instead he just holds it still."
    new "I imagine Enok. He is holding a fish in his mouth, his sharp teeth holding it firmly in place. He could kill it in an instant, but instead he just holds it still.\n我想象着 Enok。他嘴里衔着一条鱼，尖利的牙齿牢牢地把它固定住。他本可以一瞬间将它咬死，却只是那样静静衔着。"

    old "And, of course, probably because it's my dream, he wears nothing, revealing those chest muscles I love."
    new "And, of course, probably because it's my dream, he wears nothing, revealing those chest muscles I love.\n当然，大概因为这是我的梦，他一丝不挂，露出那些我心爱的胸肌。"

    old "Seeing him like this excites me. I know how those teeth feel against my own skin and how skillfully Enok can use them."
    new "Seeing him like this excites me. I know how those teeth feel against my own skin and how skillfully Enok can use them.\n看到他这副样子，我兴奋了起来。我知道那些牙齿贴着自己皮肤的感觉，也知道 Enok 能用得多娴熟。"

    old "Enok pulls the fish from his mouth and then begins licking it suggestively. He watches me carefully as he runs his tongue slowly along its surface. I feel myself getting warmer and warmer."
    new "Enok pulls the fish from his mouth and then begins licking it suggestively. He watches me carefully as he runs his tongue slowly along its surface. I feel myself getting warmer and warmer.\nEnok 把鱼从嘴里拿出来，然后开始挑逗般地舔舐它。他一边缓缓地把舌头滑过鱼的表面，一边仔细地看着我。我觉得自己越来越热。"

    old "I'm going to prepare an exquisite dinner with this. But first... I think I'll play with it a little."
    new "I'm going to prepare an exquisite dinner with this. But first... I think I'll play with it a little.\n我要用这个做一顿精美的晚餐。不过首先……我想先拿它玩一会儿。"

    old "Yes..."
    new "Yes...\n好……"

    old "I don't know if you've noticed already, but us nagas have a longer tongue than most other races."
    new "I don't know if you've noticed already, but us nagas have a longer tongue than most other races.\n不知道你有没有注意到，我们 naga 的舌头比大多数种族都要长。"

    old "Now, Imagine all the nice things I could do to you with my long tongue. I'm sure you can come up with a few ideas."
    new "Now, Imagine all the nice things I could do to you with my long tongue. I'm sure you can come up with a few ideas.\n现在，想象一下，我能用这条长舌头对你做多少美妙的事。我相信你自己也能想出几个来。"

    old "Enok puts the fish back in his mouth and lets out a small moan. I can't hold back any longer. I reach down and begin touching myself."
    new "Enok puts the fish back in his mouth and lets out a small moan. I can't hold back any longer. I reach down and begin touching myself.\nEnok 把鱼放回嘴里，发出一声轻吟。我再也忍不住了，把手伸下去，开始抚摸自己。"

    old "After a few glorious moments of pleasure, I'm exhausted. Was it really only a dream? It seemed so real!"
    new "After a few glorious moments of pleasure, I'm exhausted. Was it really only a dream? It seemed so real!\n经过几段酣畅淋漓的欢愉，我筋疲力尽。这真的只是一场梦吗？它太真实了！"

    old "I think Enok really did use some sort of dark magic trick. Yes, that must be the only explanation. My dreams aren't that creative, right? Anyway, I do feel relaxed now. I don't think I'll have any more trouble sleeping tonight."
    new "I think Enok really did use some sort of dark magic trick. Yes, that must be the only explanation. My dreams aren't that creative, right? Anyway, I do feel relaxed now. I don't think I'll have any more trouble sleeping tonight.\n我想 Enok 真的用了某种黑暗魔法的把戏。对，这一定是唯一的解释。我的梦可没这么有想象力，对吧？总之，我现在确实放松了。今晚应该不会再睡不着了。"

    old "I find Galan in Grimoire, where we last met."
    new "I find Galan in Grimoire, where we last met.\n我在 Grimoire 找到了 Galan，就在我们上次见面的地方。"

    old "Galan. I hope you've been well."
    new "Galan. I hope you've been well.\nGalan。希望你一切安好。"

    old "Well enough. I'm not hungry and I'm free to move about. I suppose I should count those as blessings. Not everyone can say the same."
    new "Well enough. I'm not hungry and I'm free to move about. I suppose I should count those as blessings. Not everyone can say the same.\n还算好。我不饿，也能自由走动。我想这些该算是福气了。不是人人都能这么说的。"

    old "Were you thinking of someone in particular?"
    new "Were you thinking of someone in particular?\n你心里想到某个特定的人了吗？"

    old "Well, seeing you does bring up some memories. There were three of us in that cell, remember. Now there's one. It makes me feel discontent, knowing that all but one of us made it out."
    new "Well, seeing you does bring up some memories. There were three of us in that cell, remember. Now there's one. It makes me feel discontent, knowing that all but one of us made it out.\n嗯，看到你确实勾起了些回忆。那间牢房里原本关着我们三个，记得吗。现在只剩下一个了。一想到我们三个里只有一个活着出来，我就满心不是滋味。"

    old "Even if Dasyra was guilty of the crime she was accused of, Edgar Arasmas will do her far worse than she deserves. He's a wretched man. Words like 'honesty' and 'mercy' are foreign to him."
    new "Even if Dasyra was guilty of the crime she was accused of, Edgar Arasmas will do her far worse than she deserves. He's a wretched man. Words like 'honesty' and 'mercy' are foreign to him.\n就算 Dasyra 真犯了被指控的罪，Edgar Arasmas 也会让她落得远不该有的下场。他是个卑鄙的人。诚实、仁慈这类字眼，对他而言完全是陌生的。"

    old "Both you and I have personal experience to speak to that."
    new "Both you and I have personal experience to speak to that.\n这一点，你我都深有体会。"

    old "True, true. You have spent a night in his dungeon. But you haven't experienced the corruption that man has wrought in Hammerhands."
    new "True, true. You have spent a night in his dungeon. But you haven't experienced the corruption that man has wrought in Hammerhands.\n没错，没错。你曾在他的地牢里待过一夜。但你没有经历过那个人在 Hammerhands 造成的腐败。"

    old "I take it that you have."
    new "I take it that you have.\n看来你经历过。"

    old "[protag], I fear for Dasyra's life. If we go back to Hammerhands, we risk arrest. But this will continue to gnaw at me if I don't have a chance to see for myself what's become of her."
    new "[protag], I fear for Dasyra's life. If we go back to Hammerhands, we risk arrest. But this will continue to gnaw at me if I don't have a chance to see for myself what's become of her.\n[protag]，我担心 Dasyra 的性命。如果我们回 Hammerhands，就有被捕的风险。但若没有机会亲眼看看她如今怎样了，这件事会一直啃噬我的心。"

    old "I feel the same way, Galan. Let's go back to Hammerhands and see what we can discover. When would you be ready to head back?"
    new "I feel the same way, Galan. Let's go back to Hammerhands and see what we can discover. When would you be ready to head back?\n我也有同感，Galan。我们回 Hammerhands 去，看看能查出些什么。你什么时候能出发？"

    old "No time like the present. I can leave right now if that's what you want."
    new "No time like the present. I can leave right now if that's what you want.\n择日不如撞日。如果你想，我现在就可以走。"

    old "Let's get going, then."
    new "Let's get going, then.\n那我们动身吧。"

    old "First order of business, let's discover whether you and I are still wanted for arrest. If we are wanted, then we'll have a tough time investigating around the business districts of Hammerhands. But here, we're among friends."
    new "First order of business, let's discover whether you and I are still wanted for arrest. If we are wanted, then we'll have a tough time investigating around the business districts of Hammerhands. But here, we're among friends.\n第一件事，先弄清楚你我是否还在被通缉。如果还在，那我们在 Hammerhands 的商业区一带调查起来会很困难。不过在这里，我们周围都是朋友。"

    old "Friends?"
    new "Friends?\n朋友？"

    old "Didn't I tell you, [protag]? I grew up in the basin. Stin!"
    new "Didn't I tell you, [protag]? I grew up in the basin. Stin!\n我没告诉过你吗，[protag]？我是在盆地长大的。Stin！"

    old "The bartender looks up and smiles at Galan."
    new "The bartender looks up and smiles at Galan.\n酒保抬起头，冲 Galan 笑了笑。"

    old "Galan, my man! What brings you out to these parts?"
    new "Galan, my man! What brings you out to these parts?\nGalan，好兄弟！什么风把你吹到这边来了？"

    old "I wanted information, and you're my favorite person to get it from."
    new "I wanted information, and you're my favorite person to get it from.\n我想打听点消息，而你是我最愿意来打听的人。"

    old "Information, you got it. I'll get you and your friend a couple of ales to go along with it."
    new "Information, you got it. I'll get you and your friend a couple of ales to go along with it.\n打听消息，没问题。我给你和你朋友来两杯麦酒，边喝边聊。"

    old "Information, you got it. I'll get you and your lady friend a couple of ales to go along with it."
    new "Information, you got it. I'll get you and your lady friend a couple of ales to go along with it.\n打听消息，没问题。我给你和这位女士朋友来两杯麦酒，边喝边聊。"

    old "Thanks, Stin, but I've been off the ale."
    new "Thanks, Stin, but I've been off the ale.\n谢了，Stin，不过我已经戒酒了。"

    old "Is Crazy Galan finally sobering up? I never thought I'd see the day. What about your friend over there?"
    new "Is Crazy Galan finally sobering up? I never thought I'd see the day. What about your friend over there?\nCrazy Galan 终于开始清醒了？真没想到有生之年还能见到。那你这位朋友呢？"

    old "Thanks for the offer, but I'll pass. I need to stay frosty."
    new "Thanks for the offer, but I'll pass. I need to stay frosty.\n谢谢好意，不过算了。我得保持清醒。"

    old "Fair enough, fair enough. So what do you fellows to know about?"
    new "Fair enough, fair enough. So what do you fellows to know about?\n行吧，行吧。那么你们几位想打听点什么？"

    old "Fair enough, fair enough. What do you two need to know about?"
    new "Fair enough, fair enough. What do you two need to know about?\n行吧，行吧。你们两位想打听点什么？"

    old "Any news out of Arasmas? Any recent arrest warrants, things of that nature?"
    new "Any news out of Arasmas? Any recent arrest warrants, things of that nature?\nArasmas 那边有什么消息吗？最近有什么逮捕令之类的？"

    old "As a matter of fact, yes. Two thieves were seen recently fleeing the Arasmas estate. Haven't heard about what it was they made off with, but there's a reward for anyone who can provide details leading to their capture."
    new "As a matter of fact, yes. Two thieves were seen recently fleeing the Arasmas estate. Haven't heard about what it was they made off with, but there's a reward for anyone who can provide details leading to their capture.\n还真有。最近有人看到两个贼从 Arasmas 庄园逃出来。没听说他们顺走了什么，但只要能提供线索帮人抓到他俩，就有赏金。"

    old "Do you have a description of the two thieves?"
    new "Do you have a description of the two thieves?\n那两个贼有什么特征描述吗？"

    old "All I've heard is that it was a dwarf and an elf. Not much to go on, I know. Odds are those two are going to get away with it."
    new "All I've heard is that it was a dwarf and an elf. Not much to go on, I know. Odds are those two are going to get away with it.\n我只听说是一个矮人和一个精灵。我知道这线索没什么用。那俩人多半能逃掉。"

    old "All I've heard is that it was two dwarves. Not much to go on, I know. Only several thousand people in Hammerhands matching that description. Odds are those two are going to get away with it."
    new "All I've heard is that it was two dwarves. Not much to go on, I know. Only several thousand people in Hammerhands matching that description. Odds are those two are going to get away with it.\n我只听说是两个矮人。我知道这线索没什么用。Hammerhands 里符合这描述的少说也有几千人。那俩人多半能逃掉。"

    old "All I've heard is that it was a dwarf and a human. Not much to go on, I know. Odds are those two are going to get away with it."
    new "All I've heard is that it was a dwarf and a human. Not much to go on, I know. Odds are those two are going to get away with it.\n我只听说是一个矮人和一个人类。我知道这线索没什么用。那俩人多半能逃掉。"

    old "Anyway, what's it to you, Galan? After that reward money?"
    new "Anyway, what's it to you, Galan? After that reward money?\n话说，Galan，这跟你有什么关系？冲着那赏金去的？"

    old "I might be."
    new "I might be.\n也许吧。"

    old "I never thought I'd see the day when Galan would start chasing Arasmas money. But hey, I suppose Arasmas money can buy the finer things in life just as well as honest money. At a point you lose the luxury of being able to pick and choose."
    new "I never thought I'd see the day when Galan would start chasing Arasmas money. But hey, I suppose Arasmas money can buy the finer things in life just as well as honest money. At a point you lose the luxury of being able to pick and choose.\n真没想到有生之年还能看到 Galan 追着 Arasmas 的钱跑。不过嘿，我想 Arasmas 的钱买起好东西来，跟干净钱也是一样好使。人到某个份上，就没资格挑三拣四了。"

    old "Anything else you think I should know?"
    new "Anything else you think I should know?\n还有什么你觉得我该知道的吗？"

    old "Well, Missy Horner is having another baby. That's news, I suppose. And Nandy got a job working at the mine. Apart from that, it's been the same old same old."
    new "Well, Missy Horner is having another baby. That's news, I suppose. And Nandy got a job working at the mine. Apart from that, it's been the same old same old.\n嗯，Missy Horner 又要生孩子了。这算条新闻吧。还有 Nandy 在矿上找到活儿干了。除此之外，还是老样子。"

    old "Thanks for the update, Stin. I wish I could stick around, but I've got business to take care of."
    new "Thanks for the update, Stin. I wish I could stick around, but I've got business to take care of.\n谢谢你的消息，Stin。我也想多待会儿，可我还有事要办。"

    old "Don't we all, don't we all. Come by any time, Galan."
    new "Don't we all, don't we all. Come by any time, Galan.\n谁说不是呢，谁说不是呢。随时过来，Galan。"

    old "I follow Galan outside."
    new "I follow Galan outside.\n我跟着 Galan 走了出去。"

    old "So, apparently I'm an elf now?"
    new "So, apparently I'm an elf now?\n那么，我现在居然成了精灵？"

    old "Isn't it funny how they managed to flub up the most basic detail? Well, I am a dwarf. They did get that half right. Still, looking at you...I'm really not seeing how someone could mistake you for an elf."
    new "Isn't it funny how they managed to flub up the most basic detail? Well, I am a dwarf. They did get that half right. Still, looking at you...I'm really not seeing how someone could mistake you for an elf.\n他们竟能把最基本的特征都给搞错，你不觉得好笑吗？嗯，我确实是矮人。这一半他们算说对了。可再看看你……我实在看不出有谁会把你误认成精灵。"

    old "I know some dwarves think that all foreigners look the same, but this is taking it to a different level."
    new "I know some dwarves think that all foreigners look the same, but this is taking it to a different level.\n我知道有些矮人觉得所有外族人都长一个样，可这也太离谱了。"

    old "This is actually pretty fortunate. If they're looking for an elf and a dwarf traveling together, you and I should be free to move about the city."
    new "This is actually pretty fortunate. If they're looking for an elf and a dwarf traveling together, you and I should be free to move about the city.\n这其实是好事。如果他们在找一起赶路的一个精灵和一个矮人，那你我应该就能在城里自由活动了。"

    old "So, they're out looking for two dwarves."
    new "So, they're out looking for two dwarves.\n那么，他们要找的是两个矮人。"

    old "You and I answer to that description, I'm afraid. But somehow, I get the feeling that we aren't going to be found based on that description alone."
    new "You and I answer to that description, I'm afraid. But somehow, I get the feeling that we aren't going to be found based on that description alone.\n恐怕你我都符合这描述。但不知怎的，我有种感觉，光凭这描述是找不到我们的。"

    old "If they haven't been circulating any details about us apart from the fact that we're dwarves, I think we should be free to move about the city."
    new "If they haven't been circulating any details about us apart from the fact that we're dwarves, I think we should be free to move about the city.\n如果他们除了我们是矮人这一点之外，没有散布任何关于我们的细节，我想我们应该能在城里自由活动。"

    old "So, apparently I'm a human now?"
    new "So, apparently I'm a human now?\n那么，我现在居然成了人类？"

    old "Isn't it funny how they managed to flub up the most basic detail? Well, I am a dwarf. They did get that half right. Still, looking at you...I'm really not seeing how someone could mistake you for a human."
    new "Isn't it funny how they managed to flub up the most basic detail? Well, I am a dwarf. They did get that half right. Still, looking at you...I'm really not seeing how someone could mistake you for a human.\n他们竟能把最基本的特征都给搞错，你不觉得好笑吗？嗯，我确实是矮人。这一半他们算说对了。可再看看你……我实在看不出有谁会把你误认成人类。"

    old "This is actually pretty fortunate. If they're looking for a human and a dwarf traveling together, you and I should be free to move about the city."
    new "This is actually pretty fortunate. If they're looking for a human and a dwarf traveling together, you and I should be free to move about the city.\n这其实是好事。如果他们在找一起赶路的一个人类和一个矮人，那你我应该就能在城里自由活动了。"

    old "[protag], knowing that, I'm thinking maybe we just rock on up to the Arasmas grounds and see what's up. What do you think?"
    new "[protag], knowing that, I'm thinking maybe we just rock on up to the Arasmas grounds and see what's up. What do you think?\n[protag]，既然这样，我想也许我们干脆直接到 Arasmas 庄园去，看看情况。你觉得呢？"

    old "Sounds like a good idea. There were a few guards who saw our faces, but as long as we stay outside the grounds, we should be fine."
    new "Sounds like a good idea. There were a few guards who saw our faces, but as long as we stay outside the grounds, we should be fine.\n听起来不错。有几个守卫见过我们的脸，但只要我们待在庄园外面，应该就没事。"

    old "I don't know, Galan. Even if they got our description wrong, there were more than a few guards that saw both of our faces. What if we run into one who recognizes us?"
    new "I don't know, Galan. Even if they got our description wrong, there were more than a few guards that saw both of our faces. What if we run into one who recognizes us?\n我不太确定，Galan。就算他们把我们的描述搞错了，可看到我们俩脸的可不止几个守卫。要是碰上认得出我们的呢？"

    old "How about this: we'll get as close as we can while feeling safe, and then pay someone to get closer on our behalf if we think we need a closer eye on what's happening. Is that good enough for you?"
    new "How about this: we'll get as close as we can while feeling safe, and then pay someone to get closer on our behalf if we think we need a closer eye on what's happening. Is that good enough for you?\n这样如何：我们先在确保安全的前提下尽量靠近，如果觉得需要更近距离盯着，就花钱雇人替我们靠近。这样你满意吗？"

    old "That'll do, Galan."
    new "That'll do, Galan.\n可以，Galan。"

    old "I think that we should investigate when the streets are crowded. We're less likely to draw attention to ourselves that way, and if we do get spotted and recognized, crowds can prove a good distraction."
    new "I think that we should investigate when the streets are crowded. We're less likely to draw attention to ourselves that way, and if we do get spotted and recognized, crowds can prove a good distraction.\n我觉得我们应该趁街道拥挤时去调查。那样比较不容易引人注意，而且就算被发现、被认出来，人群也能起到很好的掩护作用。"

    old "In that case, we should head there shortly after daybreak. The crowds will be thick with people on their way to work."
    new "In that case, we should head there shortly after daybreak. The crowds will be thick with people on their way to work.\n那样的话，我们应该在天亮后不久过去。那时候街上满是要去上工的人，会很拥挤。"

    old "Isn't there an evening crowd of people returning home from work?"
    new "Isn't there an evening crowd of people returning home from work?\n傍晚不是也有下班回家的人群吗？"

    old "Nothing like the morning crowd. Nearly everyone in Hammerhands starts their day at the crack of dawn, but everyone goes home at different times. Some craftsmen have shorter work days than the laborers. And not everyone goes straight home after their day's work is done. Some linger in the areas around the business for fine dining and drinks."
    new "Nothing like the morning crowd. Nearly everyone in Hammerhands starts their day at the crack of dawn, but everyone goes home at different times. Some craftsmen have shorter work days than the laborers. And not everyone goes straight home after their day's work is done. Some linger in the areas around the business for fine dining and drinks.\n那可比不上早晨的人群。Hammerhands 几乎人人天一亮就开工，但大家回家的时间却各不相同。有些工匠比苦力的工作时间短。而且也不是人人干完活就直接回家。有些人会在商业区一带流连，吃顿好饭、喝点小酒。"

    old "If you want a dense crowd to hide in, we should come back another day in the morning."
    new "If you want a dense crowd to hide in, we should come back another day in the morning.\n如果你想躲在密集的人群里，那我们最好改天早上再来。"

    old "Well then. Let's make it happen. See you soon, Galan."
    new "Well then. Let's make it happen. See you soon, Galan.\n那好。就这么办。回头见，Galan。"

    old "[protag], before you go, there's something I think I should tell you. About my relationship with Edgar Arasmas."
    new "[protag], before you go, there's something I think I should tell you. About my relationship with Edgar Arasmas.\n[protag]，你走之前，有件事我想应该告诉你。是关于我和 Edgar Arasmas 的关系。"

    old "You have an existing relationship with Edgar?"
    new "You have an existing relationship with Edgar?\n你之前就跟 Edgar 认识？"

    old "Do you remember our discussion when we were trapped together in that cell? I shared a story with you, a rather somber one, about the sins of my past. About the lives that I took which can never be restored."
    new "Do you remember our discussion when we were trapped together in that cell? I shared a story with you, a rather somber one, about the sins of my past. About the lives that I took which can never be restored.\n还记得我们被一起困在那间牢房里时的谈话吗？我跟你讲过一个故事，一个相当沉重，关于我过往罪孽的故事。关于那些被我夺走、再也无法挽回的生命。"

    old "There's a small detail of the story that I left out. I flew into that...fury, because I thought that I had been cheated. I was lied to by a corrupt appraiser who had been bribed by the buyer of the jewels."
    new "There's a small detail of the story that I left out. I flew into that...fury, because I thought that I had been cheated. I was lied to by a corrupt appraiser who had been bribed by the buyer of the jewels.\n那故事里有个小细节我漏掉了。我之所以陷入那场……暴怒，是因为我以为自己被骗了。一个收了珠宝买家贿赂的腐败估价师对我撒了谎。"

    old "That man...the man who attempted to cheat that merchant, the merchant that I killed...his name was Edgar Arasmas."
    new "That man...the man who attempted to cheat that merchant, the merchant that I killed...his name was Edgar Arasmas.\n那个人……那个企图欺骗那名商人的人——那名商人正是后来被我杀死的那位——他的名字叫 Edgar Arasmas。"

    old "That's one hell of a coincidence."
    new "That's one hell of a coincidence.\n这也太巧了吧。"

    old "As it turns out, yes, it is all a massive coincidence. When I joined the fight with you and Dasyra and attacked those guards, I had no idea that they were subjects of the Arasmas estate. It's a weird quirk of fate that our paths managed to cross in that way."
    new "As it turns out, yes, it is all a massive coincidence. When I joined the fight with you and Dasyra and attacked those guards, I had no idea that they were subjects of the Arasmas estate. It's a weird quirk of fate that our paths managed to cross in that way.\n事实证明，是的，这一切都是个巨大的巧合。当我和你们、和 Dasyra 一起战斗，攻击那些守卫时，我完全不知道他们是 Arasmas 庄园的人。我们的命运竟以那种方式再次交错，真是命运的怪癖。"

    old "You have an existing relationship with Edgar Arasmas?"
    new "You have an existing relationship with Edgar Arasmas?\n你之前就跟 Edgar Arasmas 认识？"

    old "You've extended me the courtesy of not prying too much into my past, but I feel like I should share at least this much. Several years ago, I was part of a business deal between a merchant and Edgar Arasmas. I was the merchant's escort, helping him to transport some gems."
    new "You've extended me the courtesy of not prying too much into my past, but I feel like I should share at least this much. Several years ago, I was part of a business deal between a merchant and Edgar Arasmas. I was the merchant's escort, helping him to transport some gems.\n你一直很体谅我，没有过多打探我的过去，但我觉得至少该分享这些。几年前，我参与了一桩商人与 Edgar Arasmas 之间的交易。我是那名商人的护卫，帮他运送一些宝石。"

    old "The ultimate result of the deal was that Edgar defrauded the merchant, leaving me without a way to get paid."
    new "The ultimate result of the deal was that Edgar defrauded the merchant, leaving me without a way to get paid.\n那笔交易的最终结果是，Edgar 骗了那名商人，害得我连酬劳都拿不到。"

    old "Things after that went quite sour. I'll spare you the details. Suffice to say, I had little fondness for Edgar Arasmas even before this whole ordeal began."
    new "Things after that went quite sour. I'll spare you the details. Suffice to say, I had little fondness for Edgar Arasmas even before this whole ordeal began.\n之后事情就变得很不妙。细节我就不提了。总之，早在这一切开始之前，我就对 Edgar Arasmas 没什么好感了。"

    old "I hoped to avoid him my entire life. And then one day my attempt to rescue a damsel in distress led to another unfortunate encounter with Edgar Arasmas."
    new "I hoped to avoid him my entire life. And then one day my attempt to rescue a damsel in distress led to another unfortunate encounter with Edgar Arasmas.\n我原本希望这辈子都躲着他。结果有一天，我试图搭救一位落难的少女，却又一次不幸地撞上了 Edgar Arasmas。"

    old "I'm sorry for not bringing this up sooner. At the time, the connection between my past and the present hadn't even occurred to me."
    new "I'm sorry for not bringing this up sooner. At the time, the connection between my past and the present hadn't even occurred to me.\n抱歉我没有早点提起。当时我甚至都没意识到，我的过去和现在竟有这层关联。"

    old "I know, it must seem like I was hiding something, as it seems quite obvious looking back. But my mind was occupied with much bigger problems at the time."
    new "I know, it must seem like I was hiding something, as it seems quite obvious looking back. But my mind was occupied with much bigger problems at the time.\n我知道，事后回想起来这似乎很明显，我看起来像是在隐瞒什么。但当时我的心思全被更大的麻烦占据了。"

    old "That's understandable."
    new "That's understandable.\n这可以理解。"

    old "I never held a grudge against Edgar. I presumed he was doing what nobles do: exploiting the system for his own gain. He did it before, and now he's done it again. But now, it's become something more personal."
    new "I never held a grudge against Edgar. I presumed he was doing what nobles do: exploiting the system for his own gain. He did it before, and now he's done it again. But now, it's become something more personal.\n我从未对 Edgar 怀恨在心。我原以为他不过是做了贵族常做的事：钻制度的空子为自己谋利。他以前就这么干过，如今又故技重施。但这一次，事情变得更私人了。"

    old "We're going to rescue Dasyra, Galan. Hopefully that's will be enough for you in terms of closure."
    new "We're going to rescue Dasyra, Galan. Hopefully that's will be enough for you in terms of closure.\n我们一定会救出 Dasyra，Galan。希望到那时，你心里能就此放下。"

    old "I meet Galan in Hammerhands at the crack of dawn."
    new "I meet Galan in Hammerhands at the crack of dawn.\n天刚破晓，我在 Hammerhands 与 Galan 会合。"

    old "[protag], good to see you made it."
    new "[protag], good to see you made it.\n[protag]，真高兴你赶到了。"

    old "Hello, Galan. I hope I didn't keep you waiting."
    new "Hello, Galan. I hope I didn't keep you waiting.\n你好，Galan。希望没让你久等。"

    old "I haven't been waiting long. Progress through early morning traffic is always slow, anyway."
    new "I haven't been waiting long. Progress through early morning traffic is always slow, anyway.\n我没等多久。反正清晨的人流总是走不快。"

    old "These streets certainly are bustling."
    new "These streets certainly are bustling.\n这些街道果然熙熙攘攘。"

    old "Makes you feel at ease, doesn't it? Crowds are easy to get lost in if you ever find yourself being pursued."
    new "Makes you feel at ease, doesn't it? Crowds are easy to get lost in if you ever find yourself being pursued.\n让人安心不少，对吧？要是被人追赶，人群里很容易就能甩掉对方。"

    old "Hopefully that won't be relevant in our case, but it never hurts to have a backup plan."
    new "Hopefully that won't be relevant in our case, but it never hurts to have a backup plan.\n希望我们不至于用到，但有个备用计划总没坏处。"

    old "So what are we here to do?"
    new "So what are we here to do?\n那我们到这里来做什么？"

    old "I was thinking we might plan a different way to get in. I don't get the feeling things will go too well for us if we charge through the Arasmas front gate looking for a fight. Slinking around in the shadows isn't really my style, but it might be our best bet at getting to Dasyra."
    new "I was thinking we might plan a different way to get in. I don't get the feeling things will go too well for us if we charge through the Arasmas front gate looking for a fight. Slinking around in the shadows isn't really my style, but it might be our best bet at getting to Dasyra.\n我在想，也许我们该另想办法进去。如果我们硬闯 Arasmas 的正门去找茬，我感觉不会有好果子吃。偷偷摸摸躲在暗处不是我的风格，但那可能是我们找到 Dasyra 的最佳选择。"

    old "How do we sneak in?"
    new "How do we sneak in?\n我们怎么潜进去？"

    old "That's what we're here to find out. I believe this is what burglars refer to as 'casing the joint.' The question is, should we split up, or search together?"
    new "That's what we're here to find out. I believe this is what burglars refer to as 'casing the joint.' The question is, should we split up, or search together?\n这就是我们来这儿要弄清的。我想这就是窃贼所谓的踩点。问题是，我们该分头行动，还是一起搜寻？"

    old "If we split up, we can cover the area twice as fast. Faster searching means a smaller window of time for us to get caught or run into trouble."
    new "If we split up, we can cover the area twice as fast. Faster searching means a smaller window of time for us to get caught or run into trouble.\n如果分头行动，我们能以两倍速度摸清这一带。搜得越快，我们被抓或碰上麻烦的时间窗口就越小。"

    old "Alright. I'll head around the west side, and you take a look at things from the east."
    new "Alright. I'll head around the west side, and you take a look at things from the east.\n好。我绕西边去，你从东边看看情况。"

    old "If we split up, we double our chances of getting caught. Plus, there's safety in numbers, as the saying goes. If worse comes to worse, I'd prefer to have you by my side."
    new "If we split up, we double our chances of getting caught. Plus, there's safety in numbers, as the saying goes. If worse comes to worse, I'd prefer to have you by my side.\n如果分头行动，被抓的几率就翻倍了。而且俗话说，人多更安全。真到了最糟的地步，我更希望有你在我身边。"

    old "Alright. You lead the way."
    new "Alright. You lead the way.\n好。你带路。"

    old "I walk along the road that runs parallel to the Arasmas estate, and Galan tails close behind me."
    new "I walk along the road that runs parallel to the Arasmas estate, and Galan tails close behind me.\n我沿着与 Arasmas 庄园平行的路往前走，Galan 紧随其后。"

    old "It doesn't look like we'll get entry from the main road. Arasmas is a noble house, and like any noble house, they're concerned about appearances. But perhaps the side roads are less closely guarded."
    new "It doesn't look like we'll get entry from the main road. Arasmas is a noble house, and like any noble house, they're concerned about appearances. But perhaps the side roads are less closely guarded.\n看样子从大路是进不去的。Arasmas 是贵族府邸，像所有贵族府邸一样，他们很在意门面。但也许侧面的小路戒备会松一些。"

    old "I wrap my way around the estate wall, looking the less crowded roads. I do my best to tread lightly, but as I move forward, I hear a hollow ringing sound under my feet."
    new "I wrap my way around the estate wall, looking the less crowded roads. I do my best to tread lightly, but as I move forward, I hear a hollow ringing sound under my feet.\n我沿着庄园围墙绕行，寻找人少的小路。我尽量放轻脚步，可向前走时，脚下却传来一声空洞的回响。"

    old "I freeze."
    new "I freeze.\n我僵住了。"

    old "I turn around and lock eyes with Galan, who is stopped dead in his tracks. We both look down at the ground beneath my feet."
    new "I turn around and lock eyes with Galan, who is stopped dead in his tracks. We both look down at the ground beneath my feet.\n我转过身，与 Galan 四目相对，他也僵在了原地。我们俩都朝我脚下的地面看去。"

    old "A thin layer of dirt covers the ground. I bend down and gently scrape at the dirt around my feet, slowly revealing a large metal sheet with slitted holes."
    new "A thin layer of dirt covers the ground. I bend down and gently scrape at the dirt around my feet, slowly revealing a large metal sheet with slitted holes.\n地面上覆着一层薄薄的泥土。我弯下腰，轻轻刮开脚边的泥土，一块带长条形孔洞的大金属板慢慢显露出来。"

    old "This certainly seems like a point of interest. I should come back here when I have Galan in tow."
    new "This certainly seems like a point of interest. I should come back here when I have Galan in tow.\n这地方看来确实值得注意。我应该等带上 Galan 再回来看。"

    old "I make my way back to the street and check the remainder of the estate's perimeter, but find nothing else notable."
    new "I make my way back to the street and check the remainder of the estate's perimeter, but find nothing else notable.\n我回到街上，把庄园周边其余部分都检查了一遍，但没再发现什么值得注意的东西。"

    old "My search didn't turn up anything notable. The guards don't seem very attentive, but there doesn't seem to be any way for us to actually get in without making a scene."
    new "My search didn't turn up anything notable. The guards don't seem very attentive, but there doesn't seem to be any way for us to actually get in without making a scene.\n我的搜寻没发现什么值得注意的东西。守卫看起来不太警觉，但似乎也没有办法能让我们不闹出动静就进去。"

    old "I found something more promising. Perhaps it's best if I show you."
    new "I found something more promising. Perhaps it's best if I show you.\n我发现了个更有希望的东西。也许最好还是带你去看。"

    old "I lead Galan back to where I found the metal sheet with slitted holes."
    new "I lead Galan back to where I found the metal sheet with slitted holes.\n我领着 Galan 回到我找到那块带孔金属板的地方。"

    old "Galan leans in and speaks softly."
    new "Galan leans in and speaks softly.\nGalan 凑近，轻声说道。"

    old "Sewers. Of course an estate this big has to have drainage. This could be our way in."
    new "Sewers. Of course an estate this big has to have drainage. This could be our way in.\n下水道。这么大的庄园当然得有排水系统。这可能就是我们进去的路。"

    old "We're going to go wading through their waste?"
    new "We're going to go wading through their waste?\n我们得从他们的污物里蹚过去？"

    old "It's not as bad as it sounds. The city is actually well irrigated, so waste doesn't have a chance to build up. The nobles figured out that waste spreads disease, so they made these drainage systems to take the waste away as far and fast as possible."
    new "It's not as bad as it sounds. The city is actually well irrigated, so waste doesn't have a chance to build up. The nobles figured out that waste spreads disease, so they made these drainage systems to take the waste away as far and fast as possible.\n没听起来那么糟。这城市其实排水做得很好，污物不会堆积起来。贵族们早就明白污物会传播疾病，所以造了这些排水系统，好把污物尽快、尽量远地排走。"

    old "It's mostly just water. There will be some fresh waste, but it'll be no worse than the inside of that jail cell we were in together, plus a lot of wetness."
    new "It's mostly just water. There will be some fresh waste, but it'll be no worse than the inside of that jail cell we were in together, plus a lot of wetness.\n里面大部分只是水。会有一些新鲜的污物，但也不会比我们一起待过的那间牢房更糟，只是湿得多。"

    old "What's it like down there? Will we be able to get to Dasyra?"
    new "What's it like down there? Will we be able to get to Dasyra?\n下面是什么样子？我们能找到 Dasyra 吗？"

    old "Only one way to find out."
    new "Only one way to find out.\n只有下去才能知道。"

    old "Galan begins scraping away at the dirt beneath us, and I join him. I glance down toward the main street, but the shadow of the estate wall is covering us."
    new "Galan begins scraping away at the dirt beneath us, and I join him. I glance down toward the main street, but the shadow of the estate wall is covering us.\nGalan 开始刮开我们脚下的泥土，我也跟着帮忙。我朝大街方向瞥了一眼，好在庄园围墙的阴影遮住了我们。"

    old "Galan finally unearths what looks like a handle, and he lifts the metal cover off."
    new "Galan finally unearths what looks like a handle, and he lifts the metal cover off.\nGalan 终于挖出了一个像是把手的东西，他把金属盖板掀了起来。"

    old "Looks big enough for a dwarf to fit in. In the mood for some spelunking?"
    new "Looks big enough for a dwarf to fit in. In the mood for some spelunking?\n看起来够一个矮人钻进去。有兴趣来点地底探险吗？"

    old "Big enough for a dwarf to fit inside. You, on the other hand...you're a bit bigger. Not saying you wouldn't fit, but it might not be too comfortable down there."
    new "Big enough for a dwarf to fit inside. You, on the other hand...you're a bit bigger. Not saying you wouldn't fit, but it might not be too comfortable down there.\n够一个矮人钻进去。至于你嘛……你就稍微大只了点。倒不是说你进不去，只是下面可能不会太舒服。"

    old "I'm going to go down there and check things out. Keep vigilant up here while I'm poking around, will you?"
    new "I'm going to go down there and check things out. Keep vigilant up here while I'm poking around, will you?\n我下去探探情况。我在下面摸索的时候，你留在这上面保持警觉，好吗？"

    old "I descend into the drainage."
    new "I descend into the drainage.\n我下到了排水道里。"

    old "The water is knee-deep, and it quickly soaks through my boots and into the fabric of my clothes. It's freezing down here. I suppose I shouldn't be surprised that it's cold down where the sun doesn't shine."
    new "The water is knee-deep, and it quickly soaks through my boots and into the fabric of my clothes. It's freezing down here. I suppose I shouldn't be surprised that it's cold down where the sun doesn't shine.\n水没到膝盖，很快就浸透了我的靴子，渗进衣服的布料里。这里冷得要命。我想我也不该惊讶，阳光照不到的地方当然会冷。"

    old "I tredge through the drain channel in the direction of the Arasmas estate and encounter a fork, where two channels leading from the estate meet. I try to approximate the location of the cell where we were held as best I can in my minds eye. It was near the edge of the buildings..."
    new "I tredge through the drain channel in the direction of the Arasmas estate and encounter a fork, where two channels leading from the estate meet. I try to approximate the location of the cell where we were held as best I can in my minds eye. It was near the edge of the buildings...\n我蹚着排水道，朝 Arasmas 庄园的方向前进，遇到一个岔口，两条从庄园通出的水道在此汇合。我尽量在脑海中估摸着我们被关押的那间牢房的位置。它就在建筑群的边缘附近……"

    old "As best I can tell, the channel to my left should take me to below the holding cells."
    new "As best I can tell, the channel to my left should take me to below the holding cells.\n据我判断，左侧那条水道应该能通到关押牢房的下方。"

    old "I continue down the channel. Above my head, small pipes scarcely wider than my arm empty into the channel. I give one of them a tap, and the tap echoes through the pipe."
    new "I continue down the channel. Above my head, small pipes scarcely wider than my arm empty into the channel. I give one of them a tap, and the tap echoes through the pipe.\n我继续沿着水道前进。头顶上方，一些比我的手臂粗不了多少的小管子排入水道。我敲了敲其中一根，敲击声顺着管子回荡开去。"

    old "I hear the sound of grunting through the pipe. Whether that's the grunt of a guard or another prisoner, I probably don't want someone knowing I'm down here. I continue plodding."
    new "I hear the sound of grunting through the pipe. Whether that's the grunt of a guard or another prisoner, I probably don't want someone knowing I'm down here. I continue plodding.\n我透过管子听到一声闷哼。不管那是守卫还是别的囚犯发出的，我大概都不希望有人知道我在这下面。我继续蹚水前行。"

    old "As I count the pipes, I visualize in my mind the layout of the dungeon as we passed by it on our way to the holding cell. We were at the end, and I stop at the pipe at the end. Perhaps Dasyra's still being held above."
    new "As I count the pipes, I visualize in my mind the layout of the dungeon as we passed by it on our way to the holding cell. We were at the end, and I stop at the pipe at the end. Perhaps Dasyra's still being held above.\n我一边数着管子，一边在脑中回想我们去关押牢房时经过的地牢布局。我们当时在最尽头，于是我在最尽头那根管子前停下。也许 Dasyra 仍被关在上方。"

    old "I give the pipe a tap."
    new "I give the pipe a tap.\n我敲了敲管子。"

    old "Hello?"
    new "Hello?\n喂？"

    old "I recognize that voice."
    new "I recognize that voice.\n我认得这个声音。"

    old "Dasyra, is that you?"
    new "Dasyra, is that you?\nDasyra，是你吗？"

    old "Don't say my name so loud."
    new "Don't say my name so loud.\n别那么大声喊我的名字。"

    old "Don't worry, I'm alone up here."
    new "Don't worry, I'm alone up here.\n别担心，我这边就我一个人。"

    old "Better to bide my time for now. No telling who's up there with her."
    new "Better to bide my time for now. No telling who's up there with her.\n眼下最好还是先等等。谁知道她身边还有谁。"

    old "Hello? Is anyone down there?"
    new "Hello? Is anyone down there?\n喂？下面有人吗？"

    old "I hear only Dasyra's voice. Surely she wouldn't be calling out if there was a guard there with her."
    new "I hear only Dasyra's voice. Surely she wouldn't be calling out if there was a guard there with her.\n我只听到 Dasyra 一个人的声音。要是旁边有守卫，她肯定不会这样喊话的。"

    old "Dasyra, can you hear me?"
    new "Dasyra, can you hear me?\nDasyra，你能听到我吗？"

    old "It's you!"
    new "It's you!\n是你！"

    old "Don't say my name."
    new "Don't say my name.\n别说我的名字。"

    old "It's alright. I'm alone."
    new "It's alright. I'm alone.\n没事的。就我一个人。"

    old "They've put me in the corner where I'm furthest from the other prisoners. I think Edgar likes that I can hear him walking down the long corridor when he comes to visit me."
    new "They've put me in the corner where I'm furthest from the other prisoners. I think Edgar likes that I can hear him walking down the long corridor when he comes to visit me.\n他们把我关在最靠里的角落，离其他囚犯最远。我想 Edgar 喜欢这样——这样他来看我的时候，我就能听见他沿着长长的走廊走过来的脚步声。"

    old "Edgar has been visiting you?"
    new "Edgar has been visiting you?\nEdgar 一直来看你？"

    old "Yes, he and I have known each other since childhood. I think he enjoys taunting me."
    new "Yes, he and I have known each other since childhood. I think he enjoys taunting me.\n是的，他和我从小就认识。我想他乐在其中地嘲弄我。"

    old "What are you doing down there?"
    new "What are you doing down there?\n你在下面做什么？"

    old "We came to break you out. We're gathering information right now."
    new "We came to break you out. We're gathering information right now.\n我们是来救你出去的。眼下正在收集情报。"

    old "I'm afraid you won't be rescuing me through these sewers. These pipes can carry sound, but I can scarce fit an arm into this pipe, let alone my entire body."
    new "I'm afraid you won't be rescuing me through these sewers. These pipes can carry sound, but I can scarce fit an arm into this pipe, let alone my entire body.\n恐怕你们没法从这些下水道把我救出去。这些管子能传声，但别说整个人了，我连一只手臂都很难塞进去。"

    old "That's alright, we'll figure something else out. You said that Edgar came to taunt you. Have you managed to get anything useful out of him?"
    new "That's alright, we'll figure something else out. You said that Edgar came to taunt you. Have you managed to get anything useful out of him?\n没关系，我们会另想办法。你说 Edgar 来嘲弄你。你有没有从他嘴里套出什么有用的消息？"

    old "I did manage to provide a bit of misinformation. I told him I was escaping with a dwarf and an elf, and somehow none of the guards that actually saw you thought to correct me."
    new "I did manage to provide a bit of misinformation. I told him I was escaping with a dwarf and an elf, and somehow none of the guards that actually saw you thought to correct me.\n我倒是设法散布了点假消息。我告诉他，我是和一个矮人、一个精灵一起逃的，而不知怎的，真正见过你们的守卫竟没有一个想着纠正我。"

    old "Your false rumors have spread outside the estate walls. I was surprised to hear myself described as an elf, but it may prove advantageous. Good work, Dasyra."
    new "Your false rumors have spread outside the estate walls. I was surprised to hear myself described as an elf, but it may prove advantageous. Good work, Dasyra.\n你的假消息已经传到了庄园围墙之外。我听到自己被说成精灵，还吃了一惊，不过这可能反而是好事。干得好，Dasyra。"

    old "Has Edgar told you anything that might help in your escape?"
    new "Has Edgar told you anything that might help in your escape?\nEdgar 有没有跟你说过什么，可能对你的逃跑有帮助？"

    old "I did manage to provide a bit of misinformation. I told him I was escaping with a dwarf and a human, and somehow none of the guards that actually saw you thought to correct me."
    new "I did manage to provide a bit of misinformation. I told him I was escaping with a dwarf and a human, and somehow none of the guards that actually saw you thought to correct me.\n我倒是设法散布了点假消息。我告诉他，我是和一个矮人、一个人类一起逃的，而不知怎的，真正见过你们的守卫竟没有一个想着纠正我。"

    old "Your false rumors have spread outside the estate walls. I was surprised to hear myself described as an human, but it may prove advantageous. Good work, Dasyra."
    new "Your false rumors have spread outside the estate walls. I was surprised to hear myself described as an human, but it may prove advantageous. Good work, Dasyra.\n你的假消息已经传到了庄园围墙之外。我听到自己被说成人类，还吃了一惊，不过这可能反而是好事。干得好，Dasyra。"

    old "Edgar is going to be attending the negotiation summit during the coming weeks. Knowing Edgar, he'll be taking most of his guards with him to put on a show for the other nobles. It might be a good chance to—ah!"
    new "Edgar is going to be attending the negotiation summit during the coming weeks. Knowing Edgar, he'll be taking most of his guards with him to put on a show for the other nobles. It might be a good chance to—ah!\n接下来几周，Edgar 要去参加谈判峰会。以我对 Edgar 的了解，他会带上大部分守卫，好在其他贵族面前显摆。这可能是个好机会，可以——啊！"

    old "What's going on in here? Who are you talking to?"
    new "What's going on in here? Who are you talking to?\n这里面在干什么？你在跟谁说话？"

    old "I'm just talking to myself. It gets lonely in here, you know. Who else would I be talking to?"
    new "I'm just talking to myself. It gets lonely in here, you know. Who else would I be talking to?\n我只是在自言自语。这里很寂寞，你知道的。不然我还能跟谁说话？"

    old "Don't think you can get away with badmouthing Lord Arasmas, even if you are just talking to yourself. I think you need to spend more time closer to the guard post. The lord wants us to teach you some proper manners."
    new "Don't think you can get away with badmouthing Lord Arasmas, even if you are just talking to yourself. I think you need to spend more time closer to the guard post. The lord wants us to teach you some proper manners.\n别以为只是在自言自语，就能随便说 Lord Arasmas 的坏话。我看你需要搬得离岗哨更近一点，多待些时间。领主大人要我们教你学点规矩。"

    old "I think you should go now."
    new "I think you should go now.\n我想你现在该走了。"

    old "Again with that mouth of yours. I'll go whenever I damn please."
    new "Again with that mouth of yours. I'll go whenever I damn please.\n又是你这张嘴。我他妈想什么时候走就什么时候走。"

    old "She said 'I think you should go now.' It seems pretty obvious that Dasyra intended that for me. I should follow her advice. If Arasmas does decide to start a manhunt, I don't want to be trapped down here when it happens."
    new "She said 'I think you should go now.' It seems pretty obvious that Dasyra intended that for me. I should follow her advice. If Arasmas does decide to start a manhunt, I don't want to be trapped down here when it happens.\n她说了句我想你现在该走了。很明显，Dasyra 那句话是说给我听的。我应该听她的。要是 Arasmas 真决定展开搜捕，我可不想事发时被困在这下面。"

    old "I plod back through the channel as quietly as I can. Galan is waiting for me when I reach the surface."
    new "I plod back through the channel as quietly as I can. Galan is waiting for me when I reach the surface.\n我尽可能悄无声息地沿着水道蹚了回去。等我回到地面时，Galan 正在等我。"

    old "Holy hell, [protag]. I hope you feel better than you smell."
    new "Holy hell, [protag]. I hope you feel better than you smell.\n天哪，[protag]。希望你闻起来比感觉上要好。"

    old "My legs are soaked and freezing, but I'm feeling pretty good right about now. I managed to find Dasyra."
    new "My legs are soaked and freezing, but I'm feeling pretty good right about now. I managed to find Dasyra.\n我的腿湿透了，冻得发僵，不过眼下我感觉相当好。我设法找到了 Dasyra。"

    old "Is she..."
    new "Is she...\n她……"

    old "Galan looks down the hole, and I shake my head."
    new "Galan looks down the hole, and I shake my head.\nGalan 朝洞口下方望去，我摇了摇头。"

    old "There's no way we're getting her out through there, but I did manage to exchange some words with her. She said something about Edgar being at the negotiation summit. And from the sounds of things, she's being moved closer to the main estate."
    new "There's no way we're getting her out through there, but I did manage to exchange some words with her. She said something about Edgar being at the negotiation summit. And from the sounds of things, she's being moved closer to the main estate.\n我们没法从那里把她救出来，不过我确实和她说了几句话。她提到 Edgar 会去谈判峰会之类的事。而且听动静，她正被转移到更靠近主宅的地方。"

    old "Sounds like good information. What do you reckon we should do with it?"
    new "Sounds like good information. What do you reckon we should do with it?\n听起来是条有用的情报。你觉得我们该怎么利用？"

    old "We need a plan. And I have a friend in Grimoire who might be able to help us consider our best options."
    new "We need a plan. And I have a friend in Grimoire who might be able to help us consider our best options.\n我们需要一个计划。我在 Grimoire 有位朋友，也许能帮我们斟酌出最佳方案。"

    old "But right now, what I really want is to get out of these stinking wet clothes. Let's leave it until another day to meet back in Grimoire and plan our next move."
    new "But right now, what I really want is to get out of these stinking wet clothes. Let's leave it until another day to meet back in Grimoire and plan our next move.\n不过眼下，我最想做的就是脱掉这身又臭又湿的衣服。我们改天在 Grimoire 碰头，再计划下一步吧。"

    old "Galan, I'll keep watch up here. Go down and investigate."
    new "Galan, I'll keep watch up here. Go down and investigate.\nGalan，我在上面放哨。你下去调查。"

    old "What do you want me to do down there?"
    new "What do you want me to do down there?\n你想让我在下面做什么？"

    old "Just try to get as much information as you can. See what you can see. We're not here to break Dasyra out just yet; we need more information before we can do that."
    new "Just try to get as much information as you can. See what you can see. We're not here to break Dasyra out just yet; we need more information before we can do that.\n尽量多收集信息。看看能发现什么。我们还不是来救 Dasyra 出去的；在行动之前，我们还需要更多情报。"

    old "Alright. Cover the hole once I'm down there. I'll knock on the grate when I'm ready to come up."
    new "Alright. Cover the hole once I'm down there. I'll knock on the grate when I'm ready to come up.\n好。我下去之后把洞口盖好。等我要上来时，会敲栅栏给你信号。"

    old "Galan lowers himself into the hole."
    new "Galan lowers himself into the hole.\nGalan 把自己下放进洞口。"

    old "Ugh."
    new "Ugh.\n呃。"

    old "You okay down there?"
    new "You okay down there?\n下面还好吗？"

    old "Just a little wet. I'll survive."
    new "Just a little wet. I'll survive.\n只是有点湿。我撑得住。"

    old "Good luck, Galan."
    new "Good luck, Galan.\n祝你好运，Galan。"

    old "I slide the cover over the hole and kick some dirt over it to make it less obvious that it was recently disturbed."
    new "I slide the cover over the hole and kick some dirt over it to make it less obvious that it was recently disturbed.\n我把盖板滑回洞口，又踢了些泥土盖上去，好让它看起来不那么像刚被人动过。"

    old "I stand in the shadows and lean against the wall with my arms crossed, trying to look both inconspicuous and nonchalant. Somehow, being unassuming and nonchalant is a task that becomes more difficult the harder you try."
    new "I stand in the shadows and lean against the wall with my arms crossed, trying to look both inconspicuous and nonchalant. Somehow, being unassuming and nonchalant is a task that becomes more difficult the harder you try.\n我站在阴影里，双臂交叉靠着墙，努力装出一副不起眼又若无其事的样子。不知怎的，越是努力显得低调随意，这事反而越难。"

    old "Minutes pass, and eventually I hear a tapping. I crouch down, remove the cover, and lift Galan out of the hole."
    new "Minutes pass, and eventually I hear a tapping. I crouch down, remove the cover, and lift Galan out of the hole.\n几分钟过去了，我终于听到一阵敲击声。我蹲下身，掀开盖板，把 Galan 从洞里拉了上来。"

    old "I'm fine. And, from the sound of things, so is Dasyra. I managed to find a pipe leading up to her cell."
    new "I'm fine. And, from the sound of things, so is Dasyra. I managed to find a pipe leading up to her cell.\n我没事。而且听动静，Dasyra 也没事。我设法找到了通往她牢房的一根管子。"

    old "What? Is there any way she can crawl out?"
    new "What? Is there any way she can crawl out?\n什么？她有办法爬出来吗？"

    old "I'm afraid not. The pipe is barely big enough to fit a hand inside, let alone an entire person. But I did exchange a few words with her before the guards showed up."
    new "I'm afraid not. The pipe is barely big enough to fit a hand inside, let alone an entire person. But I did exchange a few words with her before the guards showed up.\n恐怕不行。那管子勉强够塞进一只手，更别提整个人了。不过在守卫出现之前，我确实和她说了几句话。"

    old "What's happening?"
    new "What's happening?\n现在什么情况？"

    old "Dasyra says that in the coming weeks, Edgar Arasmas will be attending the Hammerhands negotiation summit with most of his guards in tow. He's the type who likes to make a big appearance."
    new "Dasyra says that in the coming weeks, Edgar Arasmas will be attending the Hammerhands negotiation summit with most of his guards in tow. He's the type who likes to make a big appearance.\nDasyra 说，接下来几周，Edgar Arasmas 会带着大部分守卫去参加 Hammerhands 的谈判峰会。他是那种喜欢大摆排场的人。"

    old "That sounds like a potential opportunity."
    new "That sounds like a potential opportunity.\n那听起来可能是个机会。"

    old "Right now? You and I are going to get out of here. We came here to get information, and we got it. We need to plan our next course of action. Let's meet back at Grimoire. I've got a friend there who I think can help us figure out what to do next."
    new "Right now? You and I are going to get out of here. We came here to get information, and we got it. We need to plan our next course of action. Let's meet back at Grimoire. I've got a friend there who I think can help us figure out what to do next.\n眼下？你和我先离开这里。我们此行的目的是搞情报，情报已经拿到了。我们得规划下一步行动。回 Grimoire 碰头吧。我那边有位朋友，我想他能帮我们理清接下来该怎么办。"

    old "Apolimesho, thank you for taking the time to see us."
    new "Apolimesho, thank you for taking the time to see us.\nApolimesho，谢谢你抽空见我们。"

    old "Of course, [protag]. My attention is yours whenever you need it."
    new "Of course, [protag]. My attention is yours whenever you need it.\n当然，[protag]。只要你有需要，我随时听候差遣。"

    old "I hope you don't mind, but I've brought a friend. I've come to discuss a matter that concerns both me and him."
    new "I hope you don't mind, but I've brought a friend. I've come to discuss a matter that concerns both me and him.\n希望你不介意，我带了一位朋友来。我来是想商量一件关乎我们俩的事。"

    old "Hello. I'm Galan."
    new "Hello. I'm Galan.\n你好。我是 Galan。"

    old "It's a pleasure to meet you, Galan."
    new "It's a pleasure to meet you, Galan.\n幸会，Galan。"

    old "Now, what matter brings you two here today?"
    new "Now, what matter brings you two here today?\n那么，今天你们两位来，是为了什么事？"

    old "It concerns Edgar Arasmas. He's holding a friend of ours captive."
    new "It concerns Edgar Arasmas. He's holding a friend of ours captive.\n是关于 Edgar Arasmas 的。他囚禁了我们的一位朋友。"

    old "A dwarven nobleman, holding someone captive. I presume he has a reason."
    new "A dwarven nobleman, holding someone captive. I presume he has a reason.\n一位矮人贵族，囚禁他人。我想他自有他的理由。"

    old "Yes, he does have a reason, but it's a flimsy one. Edgar Arasmas stole from this woman. She attempted to steal back what he'd taken from her. Unfortunately, noblemen have ways of committing theft legally."
    new "Yes, he does have a reason, but it's a flimsy one. Edgar Arasmas stole from this woman. She attempted to steal back what he'd taken from her. Unfortunately, noblemen have ways of committing theft legally.\n是的，他确实有理由，只是那理由站不住脚。Edgar Arasmas 偷了这个女人的东西。她想把被他夺走的东西偷回来。可惜的是，贵族们有的是办法让偷窃变得合法。"

    old "I see. Quite a dilemma. How do you convict someone of wrongdoing when the law is the instrument that they use for wrongdoing?"
    new "I see. Quite a dilemma. How do you convict someone of wrongdoing when the law is the instrument that they use for wrongdoing?\n我明白了。这确实是个两难。当法律沦为作恶者手中的工具时，你又如何给一个人定罪呢？"

    old "We've discovered something of an opportunity."
    new "We've discovered something of an opportunity.\n我们发现了一个机会。"

    old "Go on."
    new "Go on.\n说下去。"

    old "Edgar Arasmas is attending the negotiation summit in Hammerhands. It's an annual event where nobles come to shake hands and broker deals. Some use the summit as an opportunity to commit to deals they've arranged ahead of time, but Edgar is apparently attending to attend the summit for its entire duration."
    new "Edgar Arasmas is attending the negotiation summit in Hammerhands. It's an annual event where nobles come to shake hands and broker deals. Some use the summit as an opportunity to commit to deals they've arranged ahead of time, but Edgar is apparently attending to attend the summit for its entire duration.\nEdgar Arasmas 将出席 Hammerhands 的谈判峰会。那是贵族们前来握手言和、敲定交易的一年一度的活动。有些人利用峰会，把事先谈好的交易敲定下来，而 Edgar 显然会全程出席这场峰会。"

    old "I see. He's going in expecting to make deals without knowing what they are."
    new "I see. He's going in expecting to make deals without knowing what they are.\n我明白了。他打算到场去谈交易，却还不知道具体是些什么交易。"

    old "It makes sense for a man of Edgar's wealth to do so. He does business in many industries, and he wants to make himself available to people who might want to do business with him."
    new "It makes sense for a man of Edgar's wealth to do so. He does business in many industries, and he wants to make himself available to people who might want to do business with him.\n以 Edgar 的财富，这么做也说得通。他在许多行业都有生意，他想让自己随时可供那些想与他做生意的人接洽。"

    old "However, I think pride is also part of it. The Arasmas name is well known, but Edgar is among the younger nobles. It seems like he is trying to make a reputation for himself. He wants to put on appearances."
    new "However, I think pride is also part of it. The Arasmas name is well known, but Edgar is among the younger nobles. It seems like he is trying to make a reputation for himself. He wants to put on appearances.\n不过，我觉得虚荣也是原因之一。Arasmas 这个姓氏固然赫赫有名，但 Edgar 在贵族中还属年轻一辈。他似乎在努力为自己挣名声。他想撑足场面。"

    old "Interesting. I wonder if you might be able to pressure him into meeting with you two for private mediation at the summit. He is, after all, attending the summit to make deals. You could be among them."
    new "Interesting. I wonder if you might be able to pressure him into meeting with you two for private mediation at the summit. He is, after all, attending the summit to make deals. You could be among them.\n有意思。我在想，你们也许能施压让他在峰会上与你们两位进行私下调停。毕竟，他去参加峰会就是为了谈交易。你们也可以成为其中之一。"

    old "You really think that Edgar would meet with us?"
    new "You really think that Edgar would meet with us?\n你真觉得 Edgar 会愿意见我们？"

    old "Don't forget that you represent the interests of the Grimoire council, [protag]. For all the skulking and sneaking you do, your title still has some prestige. If you were to confront him in public and ask for private mediation, it would put him at great risk of public embarrassment to refuse."
    new "Don't forget that you represent the interests of the Grimoire council, [protag]. For all the skulking and sneaking you do, your title still has some prestige. If you were to confront him in public and ask for private mediation, it would put him at great risk of public embarrassment to refuse.\n别忘了，你代表的是 Grimoire 议会的利益，[protag]。尽管你总干些偷偷摸摸的勾当，你的头衔还是有些分量的。你若在公开场合与他当面对质、要求私下调停，他要是拒绝，就会冒上在众人面前难堪的巨大风险。"

    old "Edgar does care a great deal about appearances. According to our friend, Edgar is planning to bring most of his guards along with him as a show of strength at the summit."
    new "Edgar does care a great deal about appearances. According to our friend, Edgar is planning to bring most of his guards along with him as a show of strength at the summit.\nEdgar 确实极其在意排场。据我们那位朋友说，Edgar 打算带大部分守卫随行，好在峰会上炫耀武力。"

    old "I see, I see. The negotiation summit seems like a very safe and well-guarded event already. I wonder if perhaps his decision to bring his own guards with him may come across as a display of paranoia rather than strength."
    new "I see, I see. The negotiation summit seems like a very safe and well-guarded event already. I wonder if perhaps his decision to bring his own guards with him may come across as a display of paranoia rather than strength.\n原来如此，原来如此。谈判峰会本已是个戒备森严、十分安全的场合。我在想，他决定自带守卫随行，说不定反而会显得多疑，而非强大。"

    old "In fact, it seems quite foolish for him to do such a thing. The guards are employed to guard the estate. If they travel with him to the summit, they're scarce doing the job they were intended for."
    new "In fact, it seems quite foolish for him to do such a thing. The guards are employed to guard the estate. If they travel with him to the summit, they're scarce doing the job they were intended for.\n事实上，他这么做相当愚蠢。那些守卫是雇来守卫庄园的。要是他们随他去峰会，就几乎没法履行他们本该做的工作了。"

    old "Apolimesho strokes his beard thoughtfully for a moment."
    new "Apolimesho strokes his beard thoughtfully for a moment.\nApolimesho 若有所思地捋了一会儿胡子。"

    old "So, knowing what you know, which option seems better?"
    new "So, knowing what you know, which option seems better?\n那么，就你所掌握的情况，哪种方案更好？"

    old "If Edgar is going to pull guards away from his estate to boast about how impressive his escort is, I say we make him pay for it. The estate will still be guarded, but security will be much weaker. That will be our chance to sneak into the estate, and if push comes to shove we can force our way through."
    new "If Edgar is going to pull guards away from his estate to boast about how impressive his escort is, I say we make him pay for it. The estate will still be guarded, but security will be much weaker. That will be our chance to sneak into the estate, and if push comes to shove we can force our way through.\n如果 Edgar 要把守卫从庄园调走，好吹嘘自己的随行队伍有多气派，那我建议让他为此付出代价。庄园仍会有守卫，但戒备会薄弱得多。那将是我们潜入庄园的机会，万不得已时，我们也可以强闯进去。"

    old "Interesting. Does Galan agree with this idea?"
    new "Interesting. Does Galan agree with this idea?\n有意思。Galan 同意这个想法吗？"

    old "I am hesitant about going in and freeing Dasyra by force."
    new "I am hesitant about going in and freeing Dasyra by force.\n对于强行闯入去救 Dasyra，我有些犹豫。"

    old "I find myself thinking about the first time the three of us met. [protag] and I charged in with weapons drawn to liberate Dasyra from the clutches of Edgar's guards. Things didn't go so well for us."
    new "I find myself thinking about the first time the three of us met. [protag] and I charged in with weapons drawn to liberate Dasyra from the clutches of Edgar's guards. Things didn't go so well for us.\n我不由想起我们三个初次见面的情景。[protag] 和我拔刀冲进去，想把 Dasyra 从 Edgar 那些守卫的魔爪下解救出来。结果我们的下场并不太好。"

    old "I'd be wary of making the same mistake twice. If we charge in with 'might makes right' as our banner, we may find that Edgar's might exceeds our own."
    new "I'd be wary of making the same mistake twice. If we charge in with 'might makes right' as our banner, we may find that Edgar's might exceeds our own.\n我提防着别再犯同样的错误。如果我们高举强权即公理的旗帜冲进去，可能会发现 Edgar 的力量更胜我们一筹。"

    old "It may seem odd for me, as a wizard, to agree with the notion that might makes right. But that is the very premise of your business with the council, [protag]. We are fighting the evil of N'Mar, but we're not defeating them with morals and rhetoric. We're defeating them with staves and spears."
    new "It may seem odd for me, as a wizard, to agree with the notion that might makes right. But that is the very premise of your business with the council, [protag]. We are fighting the evil of N'Mar, but we're not defeating them with morals and rhetoric. We're defeating them with staves and spears.\n我身为巫师，却赞同强权即公理的观念，也许显得奇怪。但这正是你与议会所行之事的根本前提，[protag]。我们在与 N'Mar 的邪恶作战，却不是靠道德与说辞去战胜他们，而是靠法杖与长矛。"

    old "You two are both competent combatants. Realize that physical might is also a tool at your disposal."
    new "You two are both competent combatants. Realize that physical might is also a tool at your disposal.\n你们两位都是能干的战士。要明白，武力也是你们可资利用的工具。"

    old "Of course. And strategic planned infiltration is a far cry from running in with passionate fury. [protag], the choice is yours to make. I'll trust your judgment over my own misgivings."
    new "Of course. And strategic planned infiltration is a far cry from running in with passionate fury. [protag], the choice is yours to make. I'll trust your judgment over my own misgivings.\n当然。而经过周密谋划的潜入，与凭一腔怒火冲进去完全不是一回事。[protag]，选择权在你。比起我自己的顾虑，我更相信你的判断。"

    old "What about the others? We could use some help."
    new "What about the others? We could use some help.\n其他人呢？我们可以找些帮手。"

    old "I'd rather not, [protag]. This is my personal fight."
    new "I'd rather not, [protag]. This is my personal fight.\n还是不要了，[protag]。这是我个人的战斗。"

    old "Besides, you'll have more chances to infiltrate with a small group than a larger one."
    new "Besides, you'll have more chances to infiltrate with a small group than a larger one.\n再说，小队伍潜入的机会比大队伍更多。"

    old "Fair point."
    new "Fair point.\n说得有道理。"

    old "So [protag]. Are we going to invade Edgar's estate while he is absent?"
    new "So [protag]. Are we going to invade Edgar's estate while he is absent?\n那么，[protag]。我们要趁 Edgar 不在时潜入他的庄园吗？"

    old "Yes, Galan. If you can support that course of action, then I'm going to commit to it."
    new "Yes, Galan. If you can support that course of action, then I'm going to commit to it.\n是的，Galan。如果你支持这个行动方案，那我就下定决心去做了。"

    old "Very well. When the negotiation summit begins, we'll pay a visit to our 'friend'."
    new "Very well. When the negotiation summit begins, we'll pay a visit to our 'friend'.\n很好。等谈判峰会开始，我们就去拜访我们那位朋友。"

    old "Perhaps it's best to let cooler heads prevail. Let's meet Edgar head on and fight using words, not fists."
    new "Perhaps it's best to let cooler heads prevail. Let's meet Edgar head on and fight using words, not fists.\n也许最好还是让冷静的头脑占上风。我们正面去会一会 Edgar，用言辞而非拳头来较量。"

    old "That's all well and good, but you need more than just words to win a negotiation. You need to have leverage."
    new "That's all well and good, but you need more than just words to win a negotiation. You need to have leverage.\n这固然很好，但要赢得谈判，光靠言辞是不够的。你得有筹码。"

    old "I think that we should force Edgar to sit down with us at the negotiation summit. We can broker an agreement there. If I show up in my capacity as representative of Grimoire's council, he has to give me an audience."
    new "I think that we should force Edgar to sit down with us at the negotiation summit. We can broker an agreement there. If I show up in my capacity as representative of Grimoire's council, he has to give me an audience.\n我认为我们应该迫使 Edgar 在谈判峰会上与我们坐下来谈。我们可以在那里达成协议。如果我以 Grimoire 议会代表的身份出面，他就必须接见我。"

    old "I see. What leverage do you have?"
    new "I see. What leverage do you have?\n我明白了。你有什么筹码？"

    old "Leverage?"
    new "Leverage?\n筹码？"

    old "Edgar has something you want. How do you intend to get it from him once he sits down at the negotiation table with you? You have to offer him something."
    new "Edgar has something you want. How do you intend to get it from him once he sits down at the negotiation table with you? You have to offer him something.\nEdgar 手上有你想要的东西。等他坐到谈判桌前，你打算怎么从他那里得到它？你得拿点什么来换。"

    old "What do you have that Edgar wants?"
    new "What do you have that Edgar wants?\n你有什么是 Edgar 想要的？"

    old "We have the brooch."
    new "We have the brooch.\n我们有那枚胸针。"

    old "Is this item of particular worth to Edgar Arasmas?"
    new "Is this item of particular worth to Edgar Arasmas?\n这东西对 Edgar Arasmas 有特别的价值吗？"

    old "He wanted it enough to steal it from Dasyra once and then arrest her for stealing it back. I'd say it's an item of some importance to him."
    new "He wanted it enough to steal it from Dasyra once and then arrest her for stealing it back. I'd say it's an item of some importance to him.\n他想要它，想要到不惜先从 Dasyra 那里偷走一次，又因她偷回去而将她逮捕。要我说，这东西对他相当重要。"

    old "If that's the case, perhaps you should leave the item here in Grimoire for safekeeping. If you carry it on your person, you risk having it pilfered. Don't think Edgar too dumb to hire a pickpocket."
    new "If that's the case, perhaps you should leave the item here in Grimoire for safekeeping. If you carry it on your person, you risk having it pilfered. Don't think Edgar too dumb to hire a pickpocket.\n若真如此，也许你该把那东西留在 Grimoire 妥善保管。随身携带，就有被扒走的危险。别以为 Edgar 笨到不会雇个扒手。"

    old "I don't have it on me. Dasyra still has it."
    new "I don't have it on me. Dasyra still has it.\n它不在我身上。还在 Dasyra 手里。"

    old "That is an interesting wrinkle. How, then, do you intend to use the brooch has a bargaining chip?"
    new "That is an interesting wrinkle. How, then, do you intend to use the brooch has a bargaining chip?\n这倒是个有趣的变数。那么，你打算怎么用这枚胸针当谈判筹码呢？"

    old "We'll have to bluff long enough to make contact with Dasyra. We can demand to see her in person, in order to ensure that she's not been injured, and at that point we can get it from her and trade it for her freedom."
    new "We'll have to bluff long enough to make contact with Dasyra. We can demand to see her in person, in order to ensure that she's not been injured, and at that point we can get it from her and trade it for her freedom.\n我们得先虚张声势，撑到能和 Dasyra 接触为止。我们可以要求当面见她，好确认她没有受伤，到那时再从她那里拿到胸针，用它来交换她的自由。"

    old "An interesting plan. Perhaps you have the ability to make it work."
    new "An interesting plan. Perhaps you have the ability to make it work.\n有趣的计划。也许你有本事让它成真。"

    old "Very well. All those who attend the negotiation summit are required to wear some piece of clothing bearing their emblem. A bracer is customary. I'll have one prepared for you. And you as well, Galan."
    new "Very well. All those who attend the negotiation summit are required to wear some piece of clothing bearing their emblem. A bracer is customary. I'll have one prepared for you. And you as well, Galan.\n很好。所有出席谈判峰会的人，都须穿戴一件带有徽记的衣物。按惯例是一副护腕。我会为你准备一副。你也一样，Galan。"

    old "Apart from that, I can only wish you the best of luck. And do be careful what you do and say publicly while wearing the emblem of the Grimoire council, [protag]. You are our representative, after all. We don't want a scandal on our hands."
    new "Apart from that, I can only wish you the best of luck. And do be careful what you do and say publicly while wearing the emblem of the Grimoire council, [protag]. You are our representative, after all. We don't want a scandal on our hands.\n除此之外，我只能祝你们好运。还有，[protag]，佩戴 Grimoire 议会徽记时，你在公开场合的言行举止要多加小心。毕竟你是我们的代表。我们可不想惹上什么丑闻。"

    old "I meet with Galan in Hammerhands, and together we walk to Arasmas Estate. As expected, a guard approaches us at the main gate."
    new "I meet with Galan in Hammerhands, and together we walk to Arasmas Estate. As expected, a guard approaches us at the main gate.\n我在 Hammerhands 与 Galan 会合，一同走向 Arasmas 庄园。不出所料，一名守卫在正门朝我们走来。"

    old "What is it you want?"
    new "What is it you want?\n你们想干什么？"

    old "Hello. We've come to see Lord Arasmas."
    new "Hello. We've come to see Lord Arasmas.\n你好。我们是来求见 Lord Arasmas 的。"

    old "You've come to the wrong place. Lord Arasmas is out at the courthouse for the negotiation summit."
    new "You've come to the wrong place. Lord Arasmas is out at the courthouse for the negotiation summit.\n你们来错地方了。Lord Arasmas 到法院那边参加谈判峰会去了。"

    old "How unfortunate. Could you please pass him this note?"
    new "How unfortunate. Could you please pass him this note?\n真不凑巧。能否请你把这封便条转交给他？"

    old "I pull out an envelope, and the guard extends his hand to take it. At the last moment, I drop the note, grab the guard's arm, and pull it toward me."
    new "I pull out an envelope, and the guard extends his hand to take it. At the last moment, I drop the note, grab the guard's arm, and pull it toward me.\n我掏出一个信封，守卫伸出手来接。就在最后一刻，我丢下便条，抓住守卫的手臂，一把拽向自己。"

    old "Galan strikes the guard on the back of the head with his hammer."
    new "Galan strikes the guard on the back of the head with his hammer.\nGalan 用锤子敲在守卫的后脑上。"

    old "Cripes, Galan. That turned out more violently than I expected."
    new "Cripes, Galan. That turned out more violently than I expected.\n天啊，Galan。这比我预想的要粗暴多了。"

    old "What did you expect me to do?"
    new "What did you expect me to do?\n你指望我怎么做？"

    old "Restrain him, I suppose. Was it really necessary to knock him out?"
    new "Restrain him, I suppose. Was it really necessary to knock him out?\n我想是制服他吧。真的有必要把他打晕吗？"

    old "This is quicker."
    new "This is quicker.\n这样更快。"

    old "Galan picks up the guard's body and slings it over his shoulder before marching through the front gate."
    new "Galan picks up the guard's body and slings it over his shoulder before marching through the front gate.\nGalan 扛起守卫的身体，甩到肩上，然后迈步穿过正门。"

    old "Won't do to leave bodies lying about. Wouldn't want a passerby to notice something is up."
    new "Won't do to leave bodies lying about. Wouldn't want a passerby to notice something is up.\n总不能把尸体随便丢在地上。可不想让路人看出什么异样。"

    old "I survey the front courtyard, taking notice of the trees and colored plants."
    new "I survey the front courtyard, taking notice of the trees and colored plants.\n我环视前院，留意着那些树木和色彩斑斓的花草。"

    old "You know, seeing this place in broad daylight makes me realize just how nice it looks. The courtyard has a certain charm to it, if you're not running toward the wall and fleeing for your life."
    new "You know, seeing this place in broad daylight makes me realize just how nice it looks. The courtyard has a certain charm to it, if you're not running toward the wall and fleeing for your life.\n你知道吗，大白天的看到这地方，我才发觉它有多漂亮。若不是正朝围墙狂奔逃命，这庭院倒也别有一番韵味。"

    old "Too bad we don't have time to stop and smell the roses. We'd better get moving."
    new "Too bad we don't have time to stop and smell the roses. We'd better get moving.\n可惜我们没时间停下来闻闻花香。还是快点走吧。"

    old "We head to the containment facility, treading the same path we did the first time we were incarcerated here."
    new "We head to the containment facility, treading the same path we did the first time we were incarcerated here.\n我们朝关押设施走去，走的是我们第一次被关进这里时同样的路。"

    old "Do you think we should knock? Maybe try to draw one of them out?"
    new "Do you think we should knock? Maybe try to draw one of them out?\n你觉得我们该敲门吗？也许引一个出来？"

    old "I'd rather charge in and have the element of surprise to our advantage, but the choice is yours."
    new "I'd rather charge in and have the element of surprise to our advantage, but the choice is yours.\n我倒宁愿冲进去，占个出其不意的先机，不过由你决定。"

    old "It would be bad manners to just march in. Let's let them know we're here."
    new "It would be bad manners to just march in. Let's let them know we're here.\n直接闯进去太失礼了。让他们知道我们来了。"

    old "I give the door three consecutive raps, and I hear the sound of movement inside."
    new "I give the door three consecutive raps, and I hear the sound of movement inside.\n我在门上连敲三下，听到里面传来响动。"

    old "Who the hell?"
    new "Who the hell?\n他妈的谁啊？"

    old "Go check on it, Dimli."
    new "Go check on it, Dimli.\n去看看吧，Dimli。"

    old "The door opens, and we're greeted by the shocked expression of a dwarven guard."
    new "The door opens, and we're greeted by the shocked expression of a dwarven guard.\n门开了，迎接我们的是一名矮人守卫惊愕的表情。"

    old "Galan smacks him in the chest with his hammer, sending him to the floor."
    new "Galan smacks him in the chest with his hammer, sending him to the floor.\nGalan 一锤子砸在他胸口，把他打翻在地。"

    old "See, Galan? Show good manners, get rewarded."
    new "See, Galan? Show good manners, get rewarded.\n瞧见没，Galan？懂礼貌，就有回报。"

    old "These guys are a lot easier when you fight them one at a time."
    new "These guys are a lot easier when you fight them one at a time.\n这些家伙，一次只打一个，就容易多了。"

    old "Surprise."
    new "Surprise.\n惊喜吧。"

    old "Is that all of them?"
    new "Is that all of them?\n就这些了吗？"

    old "Galan calls out."
    new "Galan calls out.\nGalan 高声喊道。"

    old "Hey, any guards down here? We have intruders here!"
    new "Hey, any guards down here? We have intruders here!\n嘿，下面还有守卫吗？这里有入侵者！"

    old "I think that's all of them."
    new "I think that's all of them.\n我想就这些了。"

    old "Alright, search these two for keys."
    new "Alright, search these two for keys.\n好，搜搜这两个家伙身上有没有钥匙。"

    old "Found them."
    new "Found them.\n找到了。"

    old "Galan dangles a key ring."
    new "Galan dangles a key ring.\nGalan 晃了晃一串钥匙。"

    old "We located Dasyra's on the third door we try. Her startled face looks up at us as the door opens."
    new "We located Dasyra's on the third door we try. Her startled face looks up at us as the door opens.\n我们试到第三扇门时，找到了 Dasyra 的牢房。门一开，她那张惊愕的脸便抬头看向我们。"

    old "Galan! [protag]!"
    new "Galan! [protag]!\nGalan！[protag]！"

    old "Hello, Dasyra. Ready to go home?"
    new "Hello, Dasyra. Ready to go home?\n你好，Dasyra。准备好回家了吗？"

    old "Am I ever."
    new "Am I ever.\n那还用说。"

    old "Dasyra stands up and dusts herself off."
    new "Dasyra stands up and dusts herself off.\nDasyra 站起身，拍了拍身上的灰。"

    old "Dasyra, do you think you could run if we had to?"
    new "Dasyra, do you think you could run if we had to?\nDasyra，万不得已时，你能跑吗？"

    old "Yes, I can run if I have to. I could even fight if it came to that. I still have my health, Edgar's certainly been feeding me well enough."
    new "Yes, I can run if I have to. I could even fight if it came to that. I still have my health, Edgar's certainly been feeding me well enough.\n能，必要的话我可以跑。真要打起来，我也能打。我身体还不错，Edgar 确实把我喂得挺饱的。"

    old "Wonderful. There's a staff right here that I think would look great in your hands."
    new "Wonderful. There's a staff right here that I think would look great in your hands.\n好极了。这儿正好有根法杖，我想它在你手里会很称手。"

    old "We leave Dasyra's cell and reach the entrance of the containment. There are three guards waiting for us in the courtyard."
    new "We leave Dasyra's cell and reach the entrance of the containment. There are three guards waiting for us in the courtyard.\n我们离开 Dasyra 的牢房，来到关押区的入口。院子里已有三名守卫在等着我们。"

    old "I told you!"
    new "I told you!\n我早跟你说过！"

    old "Let's not waste any more time getting the hell out of here."
    new "Let's not waste any more time getting the hell out of here.\n别再浪费时间了，赶紧离开这鬼地方。"

    old "I don't think it needs to be said, but we probably want to leave this city immediately. Let's get to Grimoire, I have friends there."
    new "I don't think it needs to be said, but we probably want to leave this city immediately. Let's get to Grimoire, I have friends there.\n我想这话不必多说，但我们最好立刻离开这座城市。去 Grimoire 吧，我在那里有朋友。"

    old "We leave the estate without being noticed, and leave the city undisturbed."
    new "We leave the estate without being noticed, and leave the city undisturbed.\n我们神不知鬼不觉地离开了庄园，又安然无恙地出了城。"

    old "I can't believe you two came back for me."
    new "I can't believe you two came back for me.\n真不敢相信，你们俩竟回来救我了。"

    old "And I can't believe we got away with it. It feels unreal that we just waltzed in the front gate, got what we came for, and left."
    new "And I can't believe we got away with it. It feels unreal that we just waltzed in the front gate, got what we came for, and left.\n我也真不敢相信我们居然得手了。我们大摇大摆走进正门，拿到想要的东西，又离开了，这感觉真不真实。"

    old "Edgar left behind as many men as he thought necessary to protect the estate in his absence. Evidently he estimated wrongly."
    new "Edgar left behind as many men as he thought necessary to protect the estate in his absence. Evidently he estimated wrongly.\nEdgar 在离开时，留下了他认为足以守护庄园的人手。显然，他估算错了。"

    old "It wouldn't be the first time a nobleman was undone by his hubris."
    new "It wouldn't be the first time a nobleman was undone by his hubris.\n贵族因傲慢而栽跟头，这也不是头一回了。"

    old "I wish I could see Edgar's face when he returns and realizes what happened."
    new "I wish I could see Edgar's face when he returns and realizes what happened.\n我真希望能看到 Edgar 回来、明白发生了什么时的那张脸。"

    old "And I'll be happy if I never see his face again."
    new "And I'll be happy if I never see his face again.\n而我只要再也不用见到他那张脸，就很开心了。"

    old "Amen to that."
    new "Amen to that.\n说得太对了。"

    old "Well, Galan and I go back to our mission. You're free to do whatever you like."
    new "Well, Galan and I go back to our mission. You're free to do whatever you like.\n好了，我和 Galan 要回去执行任务了。你想做什么都行。"

    old "Your mission? What is it?"
    new "Your mission? What is it?\n你们的任务？是什么？"

    old "You're aware of the mists that have been covering the plains of N'Mar as of late, correct?"
    new "You're aware of the mists that have been covering the plains of N'Mar as of late, correct?\n你应该知道，近来一直笼罩着 N'Mar 平原的那片雾气吧？"

    old "The Grimoire council has determined that the mists are the manifestation of some evil emanating from the castle of N'Mar. We intend to invade the castle and put an end to that."
    new "The Grimoire council has determined that the mists are the manifestation of some evil emanating from the castle of N'Mar. We intend to invade the castle and put an end to that.\nGrimoire 议会已经断定，那片雾气是从 N'Mar 城堡中散逸出来的某种邪恶的显现。我们打算攻入城堡，了结这一切。"

    old "Well, you've certainly proven yourself capable of invading strongholds."
    new "Well, you've certainly proven yourself capable of invading strongholds.\n嗯，你们确实已经证明了自己有攻入要塞的本事。"

    old "If only the castle were as vulnerable a target as Edgar Arasmas's estate. Unfortunately, a fortress patrolled by skeletons and vampires is a great deal more difficult than catching dwarf guards by surprise."
    new "If only the castle were as vulnerable a target as Edgar Arasmas's estate. Unfortunately, a fortress patrolled by skeletons and vampires is a great deal more difficult than catching dwarf guards by surprise.\n要是那城堡像 Edgar Arasmas 的庄园一样容易得手就好了。可惜，一座由骷髅和吸血鬼巡逻的要塞，可比出其不意地拿下几个矮人守卫难太多了。"

    old "Sounds like you need all the help you can get. Think a healer might come in handy?"
    new "Sounds like you need all the help you can get. Think a healer might come in handy?\n听起来你们需要所有能得到的帮助。觉得一个治疗师能派上用场吗？"

    old "A healer? Now there's an idea. If only we knew of someone with those talents..."
    new "A healer? Now there's an idea. If only we knew of someone with those talents...\n治疗师？这倒是个好主意。要是我们认识有这本事的人就好了……"

    old "I know I might not be an experienced combatant, but I think I have what it takes."
    new "I know I might not be an experienced combatant, but I think I have what it takes.\n我知道自己也许不是个经验丰富的战士，但我想我够格。"

    old "What do you think, [protag]? I've fought alongside this woman twice, and I can tell you from experience she's no slouch."
    new "What do you think, [protag]? I've fought alongside this woman twice, and I can tell you from experience she's no slouch.\n你怎么看，[protag]？我和这个女人并肩战斗过两次，凭经验可以告诉你，她绝非等闲之辈。"

    old "You know what? I think we make a good team. Dasyra, if you're willing to join us in our quest, we're happy to have your help."
    new "You know what? I think we make a good team. Dasyra, if you're willing to join us in our quest, we're happy to have your help.\n你知道吗？我觉得我们会是个好团队。Dasyra，如果你愿意加入我们的征途，我们很乐意有你的帮助。"

    old "Welcome aboard."
    new "Welcome aboard.\n欢迎加入。"

    old "I meet Galan at Hammerhands for the negotiation summit. I enter the courtroom wearing the emblem of."
    new "I meet Galan at Hammerhands for the negotiation summit. I enter the courtroom wearing the emblem of.\n我在 Hammerhands 与 Galan 会合，前去参加谈判峰会。我佩戴着 Grimoire 议会的徽记走进法庭。"

    old "Somehow, this place has a much more dignified air about it than I might have expected. I imagined it much more as a marketplace, a loud place filled with people making deals."
    new "Somehow, this place has a much more dignified air about it than I might have expected. I imagined it much more as a marketplace, a loud place filled with people making deals.\n不知怎的，这地方比我预想的要庄重得多。我原本想象它更像一个市场，一个挤满谈交易的人、嘈杂喧闹的地方。"

    old "This place is actually a courtroom under ordinary circumstances. It's a setting with a certain gravitas to it, with lots of individual courtrooms to serve as chambers for negotiation, and there are judges on call to serve as legal witness whenever a contract or legal document needs to be notarized."
    new "This place is actually a courtroom under ordinary circumstances. It's a setting with a certain gravitas to it, with lots of individual courtrooms to serve as chambers for negotiation, and there are judges on call to serve as legal witness whenever a contract or legal document needs to be notarized.\n其实，这地方平日里就是一间法院。它自有一种庄严肃穆的氛围，有许多独立的法庭可充当谈判室，还有法官随时待命，每当合同或法律文件需要公证时，便担任法律见证人。"

    old "The officers of the court also serve as a protective security for the event. It makes sense as a location for deals to be made."
    new "The officers of the court also serve as a protective security for the event. It makes sense as a location for deals to be made.\n法院的官员也同时承担着这场活动的安保工作。作为缔结交易的地点，这很合理。"

    old "In fact, the negotiation summit is so central to the function of these courtrooms that they've specifically trained and hired some bailiffs who are deaf, for the purpose of presiding by discussions between nobles without risk of eavesdropping."
    new "In fact, the negotiation summit is so central to the function of these courtrooms that they've specifically trained and hired some bailiffs who are deaf, for the purpose of presiding by discussions between nobles without risk of eavesdropping.\n事实上，谈判峰会对这些法庭的职能如此核心，以至于他们专门训练并雇用了一些失聪的法警，为的是在贵族之间的会谈中充当主持，而不必担心有人偷听。"

    old "That does sound practical, I suppose. Having someone who's deaf to serve as a neutral presiding officer ensures that information about ongoing deals can never leak out."
    new "That does sound practical, I suppose. Having someone who's deaf to serve as a neutral presiding officer ensures that information about ongoing deals can never leak out.\n我想，这听起来确实很务实。让一位听不见的人担任中立主持人，就能确保正在进行的交易信息绝不会泄露出去。"

    old "Employing someone specifically because of their inability to hear sounds somehow morbid. I only hope that they get deaf bailiffs by taking deaf people and training them to be bailiffs, rather than approaching things the other way around."
    new "Employing someone specifically because of their inability to hear sounds somehow morbid. I only hope that they get deaf bailiffs by taking deaf people and training them to be bailiffs, rather than approaching things the other way around.\n因为一个人听不见就专门雇用他，总让人觉得有点病态。我只希望，他们找失聪法警，是招募失聪者再训练成法警，而不是反过来。"

    old "Truth be told, I don't know which is the case. Sometimes I wonder if their aren't those who cauterize their own ears in order to be allowed to serve as bailiffs at the negotiation summit. It's something I try not to think about too much."
    new "Truth be told, I don't know which is the case. Sometimes I wonder if their aren't those who cauterize their own ears in order to be allowed to serve as bailiffs at the negotiation summit. It's something I try not to think about too much.\n说真的，我也不知道是哪种情况。有时我会想，会不会真有人为了获准在谈判峰会上当法警，而烧聋自己的耳朵。这事我尽量不多想。"

    old "Wheeling and dealing noblemen are always concerned with appearances. They value dignity above scruples. That's what makes them nobles."
    new "Wheeling and dealing noblemen are always concerned with appearances. They value dignity above scruples. That's what makes them nobles.\n那些尔虞我诈的贵族总在意排场。他们把体面看得比良知更重。这正是他们身为贵族的原因。"

    old "Remember, any deal we get that involves promises from Edgar is only good if we can get it in writing. Don't ever take him at his word."
    new "Remember, any deal we get that involves promises from Edgar is only good if we can get it in writing. Don't ever take him at his word.\n记住，任何涉及 Edgar 承诺的交易，只有落到纸面上才算数。千万别只信他空口说的话。"

    old "Don't worry, Galan. I'm not that naive."
    new "Don't worry, Galan. I'm not that naive.\n别担心，Galan。我没那么天真。"

    old "Those soldiers over there are wearing the Arasmas family emblem. Edgar must be nearby."
    new "Those soldiers over there are wearing the Arasmas family emblem. Edgar must be nearby.\n那边那些士兵戴着 Arasmas 家族的徽记。Edgar 一定就在附近。"

    old "Bear in mind, we're in public, so we'd better address him as lord."
    new "Bear in mind, we're in public, so we'd better address him as lord.\n记住，我们是在公开场合，所以最好称他为大人。"

    old "Lord Arasmas."
    new "Lord Arasmas.\nArasmas 大人。"

    old "Yes?"
    new "Yes?\n嗯？"

    old "I'm [protag]. I represent the interests of the council in Grimoire."
    new "I'm [protag]. I represent the interests of the council in Grimoire.\n我是 [protag]。我代表 Grimoire 议会的利益。"

    old "Edgar begins smiling with a toothy grin that looks phonier than anything I've ever seen."
    new "Edgar begins smiling with a toothy grin that looks phonier than anything I've ever seen.\nEdgar 咧开嘴笑起来，那笑容比我见过的任何表情都要虚假。"

    old "A pleasure, [protag]. What can I do for you?"
    new "A pleasure, [protag]. What can I do for you?\n幸会，[protag]。有什么能为你效劳的？"

    old "I was wondering if you might be able to assist me with a missing person incident."
    new "I was wondering if you might be able to assist me with a missing person incident.\n我想请问，你能否帮我处理一起人员失踪的事件。"

    old "I'm sorry, [protag], but perhaps this issue is best left to the city patrols. My men never venture far from my own estate, excepting occasions such as this one. Now if you'll excuse me..."
    new "I'm sorry, [protag], but perhaps this issue is best left to the city patrols. My men never venture far from my own estate, excepting occasions such as this one. Now if you'll excuse me...\n抱歉，[protag]，但这种事也许最好交给城里的巡逻队。除了今天这种场合，我的人从不远离我的庄园。那么，恕我失陪了……"

    old "Dasyra was her name."
    new "Dasyra was her name.\n她叫 Dasyra。"

    old "Edgar's fake smile breaks and I see an involuntary scowl creep onto his face for a moment."
    new "Edgar's fake smile breaks and I see an involuntary scowl creep onto his face for a moment.\nEdgar 的假笑僵住了，我看见一丝不由自主的怒容在他脸上掠过一瞬。"

    old "Perhaps we could speak privately regarding this matter."
    new "Perhaps we could speak privately regarding this matter.\n也许这件事，我们可以私下谈谈。"

    old "Yes, let's. Someone, fetch a bailiff!"
    new "Yes, let's. Someone, fetch a bailiff!\n好，就这么办。来人，去请一位法警！"

    old "Edgar leads us into a private negotiation chamber. He takes one of his guards with him, and the guard stands in the corner of the room, next to the bailiff. Galan takes a place beside them."
    new "Edgar leads us into a private negotiation chamber. He takes one of his guards with him, and the guard stands in the corner of the room, next to the bailiff. Galan takes a place beside them.\nEdgar 把我们领进一间私密谈判室。他带了一名守卫随行，那名守卫站在房间角落里，挨着法警。Galan 也在他们旁边找了个位置。"

    old "You're the ones. I know it, but I can't prove it."
    new "You're the ones. I know it, but I can't prove it.\n就是你们。我知道，但我没法证明。"

    old "I'm sure I don't know what you're talking about."
    new "I'm sure I don't know what you're talking about.\n我想我完全不明白你在说什么。"

    old "Oh, you don't have to play dumb with me. We're in private. You and I both know that you two are the ones who tried to flee with Dasyra."
    new "Oh, you don't have to play dumb with me. We're in private. You and I both know that you two are the ones who tried to flee with Dasyra.\n哦，你不必跟我装傻。这里没外人。你我都清楚，你们俩就是想带着 Dasyra 逃走的那两个人。"

    old "You're right, there is nothing you can do to prove it was us. Let's stop agonizing about the past and take a few moments to discuss what comes next, shall we?"
    new "You're right, there is nothing you can do to prove it was us. Let's stop agonizing about the past and take a few moments to discuss what comes next, shall we?\n你说得对，你没法证明那是我们。那我们就别再为过去的事纠结，花点时间谈谈接下来该怎么办，好吗？"

    old "I wish I knew what you were talking about, Edgar. I'm just interested in securing the release of a certain missing person."
    new "I wish I knew what you were talking about, Edgar. I'm just interested in securing the release of a certain missing person.\n我真希望自己知道你在说什么，Edgar。我只是想促成某个失踪者获释而已。"

    old "Alright, tell me what you want."
    new "Alright, tell me what you want.\n好吧，说说你想要什么。"

    old "You have Dasyra locked up. We want her freed."
    new "You have Dasyra locked up. We want her freed.\n你把 Dasyra 关了起来。我们要你放了她。"

    old "And why should I kowtow to your demands?"
    new "And why should I kowtow to your demands?\n我又凭什么要对你们的要求低头？"

    old "Because you want the brooch."
    new "Because you want the brooch.\n因为你想要那枚胸针。"

    old "Edgar tenses up."
    new "Edgar tenses up.\nEdgar 身子一僵。"

    old "What are you proposing?"
    new "What are you proposing?\n你们在提议什么？"

    old "You free Dasyra, and we give you the brooch."
    new "You free Dasyra, and we give you the brooch.\n你放了 Dasyra，我们就把胸针给你。"

    old "You're insane."
    new "You're insane.\n你们疯了。"

    old "That's the only offer we're going to make."
    new "That's the only offer we're going to make.\n这是我们唯一会开出的条件。"

    old "That brooch belonged to my mother, you bastard. It should be mine by right. It {i}is{/i} mine by right."
    new "That brooch belonged to my mother, you bastard. It should be mine by right. It {i}is{/i} mine by right.\n那枚胸针是我母亲的，你这混蛋。它按理就该是我的。它{i}就{/i}该是我的。"

    old "Yes, you've made quite sure of that. You want that brooch, and we want to see a woman released from captivity. You can have what you want if we get what we want."
    new "Yes, you've made quite sure of that. You want that brooch, and we want to see a woman released from captivity. You can have what you want if we get what we want.\n是啊，这一点你可确保得很到位。你想要那枚胸针，我们想看到一位女子重获自由。只要我们得到想要的，你也能得到你想要的。"

    old "Show me the brooch."
    new "Show me the brooch.\n把胸针给我看看。"

    old "Bring us Dasyra and show us she's unharmed."
    new "Bring us Dasyra and show us she's unharmed.\n把 Dasyra 带过来，让我们看看她安然无恙。"

    old "You bloody...fine. Meet me back here in three hours time."
    new "You bloody...fine. Meet me back here in three hours time.\n你们这些该死的……行吧。三个小时后回这里见我。"

    old "Edgar storms toward the exit, but pauses in front of Galan."
    new "Edgar storms toward the exit, but pauses in front of Galan.\nEdgar 怒气冲冲地朝出口走去，却在 Galan 面前停了下来。"

    old "Your retainer. There's something familiar about him. I feel like we've met."
    new "Your retainer. There's something familiar about him. I feel like we've met.\n你的这位随从。他有点眼熟。我感觉我们见过。"

    old "You know, I have a wonderful memory for faces. I seem to recall you and I once were part of a deal together. You were with some merchant who tried to defraud me with counterfeit goods. A pity that things didn't go as you'd hoped."
    new "You know, I have a wonderful memory for faces. I seem to recall you and I once were part of a deal together. You were with some merchant who tried to defraud me with counterfeit goods. A pity that things didn't go as you'd hoped.\n你知道吗，我对人的面孔记性极好。我似乎记得，你我曾经共同参与过一桩交易。当时你跟着某个想用假货坑我的商人。可惜，事情没能如你所愿。"

    old "You wouldn't tell by looking, but this one's got an even temper. I like that."
    new "You wouldn't tell by looking, but this one's got an even temper. I like that.\n光看可看不出来，这家伙脾气倒是很稳。我喜欢。"

    old "Edgar pats Galan on the shoulder. Galan doesn't flinch."
    new "Edgar pats Galan on the shoulder. Galan doesn't flinch.\nEdgar 拍了拍 Galan 的肩膀。Galan 纹丝不动。"

    old "Keep being stoic. It's a good look for you."
    new "Keep being stoic. It's a good look for you.\n继续保持这副淡定的样子。很适合你。"

    old "Edgar marches out of the room, retainer in tow."
    new "Edgar marches out of the room, retainer in tow.\nEdgar 大步走出房间，随从跟在身后。"

    old "Remember, this room, three hours from now. Don't keep me waiting."
    new "Remember, this room, three hours from now. Don't keep me waiting.\n记住，这间屋子，三个小时后。别让我等。"

    old "Three and a half hours later, Edgar is nowhere to be seen."
    new "Three and a half hours later, Edgar is nowhere to be seen.\n三个半小时过去了，Edgar 仍不见踪影。"

    old "Edgar told us not to keep him waiting. I wish he'd take his own advice."
    new "Edgar told us not to keep him waiting. I wish he'd take his own advice.\nEdgar 叫我们别让他等。我倒希望他自己也能说到做到。"

    old "It's a power play. He's sub-communicating that his time is more valuable than ours."
    new "It's a power play. He's sub-communicating that his time is more valuable than ours.\n这是场权力游戏。他在暗示，他的时间比我们的更宝贵。"

    old "You think? He did have to go out and retrieve Dasyra, while we've just been waiting here for him to bring the brooch to us."
    new "You think? He did have to go out and retrieve Dasyra, while we've just been waiting here for him to bring the brooch to us.\n你这么觉得？他确实得出去把 Dasyra 带过来，而我们只是在这儿等着他拿着胸针来见我们。"

    old "If Edgar wanted to be on time, he'd have no trouble being on time. He wants us to be fully aware just how much contempt he has for us."
    new "If Edgar wanted to be on time, he'd have no trouble being on time. He wants us to be fully aware just how much contempt he has for us.\n要是 Edgar 想准时，他准能轻松做到。他就是想让我们彻底明白，他有多么看不起我们。"

    old "The door to the room swings open, and a bailiff holds the door as Edgar marches through. Behind him, two guards escort Dasyra."
    new "The door to the room swings open, and a bailiff holds the door as Edgar marches through. Behind him, two guards escort Dasyra.\n房门被推开，一名法警扶着门，Edgar 大步走了进来。他身后，两名守卫押着 Dasyra。"

    old "Hello, boys!"
    new "Hello, boys!\n你们好呀，伙计们！"

    old "Dasyra, are you alright?"
    new "Dasyra, are you alright?\nDasyra，你没事吧？"

    old "I'm right here, you nit. When a lord enters the room, you show respect."
    new "I'm right here, you nit. When a lord enters the room, you show respect.\n我就在这儿呢，你个蠢货。领主进屋时，你得表现出敬意。"

    old "We're in private, Edgar. You said it yourself, no need for formalities behind closed doors."
    new "We're in private, Edgar. You said it yourself, no need for formalities behind closed doors.\n我们这是私下场合，Edgar。你自己也说了，关起门来不必讲究那些礼数。"

    old "I've brought the girl. Now show me the brooch."
    new "I've brought the girl. Now show me the brooch.\n我把人带来了。现在把胸针给我看看。"

    old "Let us check her to make sure you haven't injured her in any way."
    new "Let us check her to make sure you haven't injured her in any way.\n先让我们检查一下，确认你没有以任何方式伤害她。"

    old "Be my guest."
    new "Be my guest.\n请便。"

    old "The guards shove Dasyra toward us, and she collapses into my arms."
    new "The guards shove Dasyra toward us, and she collapses into my arms.\n守卫们把 Dasyra 朝我们推来，她倒进了我怀里。"

    old "As okay as a woman can be after spending days and nights in captivity."
    new "As okay as a woman can be after spending days and nights in captivity.\n一个被囚禁了数个昼夜的女人，能好到哪儿去。"

    old "I whisper into her ear."
    new "I whisper into her ear.\n我凑到她耳边低语。"

    old "Do you have the brooch on you?"
    new "Do you have the brooch on you?\n胸针在你身上吗？"

    old "Ah, was that the deal? My freedom for the brooch?"
    new "Ah, was that the deal? My freedom for the brooch?\n啊，这就是那桩交易吗？用我的自由换胸针？"

    old "I know it hurts to give it up, but if we make the trade, it can be as if this all never happened."
    new "I know it hurts to give it up, but if we make the trade, it can be as if this all never happened.\n我知道放弃它很痛苦，但只要我们完成交易，这一切就能当作从未发生过。"

    old "That's fine. I'm sorry for getting you mixed up in all of this."
    new "That's fine. I'm sorry for getting you mixed up in all of this.\n没关系。抱歉把你也卷进了这一切。"

    old "Dasyra reaches into her blouse and produces the brooch. I hold it up for Edgar to see."
    new "Dasyra reaches into her blouse and produces the brooch. I hold it up for Edgar to see.\nDasyra 伸手探进上衣，取出胸针。我把它举起来，好让 Edgar 看到。"

    old "This is what you wanted, is it not?"
    new "This is what you wanted, is it not?\n这就是你想要的，不是吗？"

    old "Let me see that."
    new "Let me see that.\n让我看看。"

    old "Edgar reaches for the brooch, and I snatch it away."
    new "Edgar reaches for the brooch, and I snatch it away.\nEdgar 伸手来拿胸针，我一把收了回来。"

    old "You can look, but no touching."
    new "You can look, but no touching.\n你可以看，但不能碰。"

    old "I hold up the brooch, making it clear so that the bailiff can see what I'm doing. Edgar takes note of the bailiff and inspects the brooch, then nods, evidently satisfied."
    new "I hold up the brooch, making it clear so that the bailiff can see what I'm doing. Edgar takes note of the bailiff and inspects the brooch, then nods, evidently satisfied.\n我举起胸针，动作明明白白，好让法警看清我在做什么。Edgar 留意到法警，检查了胸针，然后点了点头，显然满意了。"

    old "Alright. Let's get this in writing to make it official. Can someone call in a judge? Does anyone know how to communicate with this bailiff?"
    new "Alright. Let's get this in writing to make it official. Can someone call in a judge? Does anyone know how to communicate with this bailiff?\n好。我们把这事落到纸面上，让它正式生效。有人能请一位法官来吗？有没有人知道怎么和这位法警沟通？"

    old "I do."
    new "I do.\n我会。"

    old "Dasyra makes several signs with her hands, and the bailiff nods and signs back."
    new "Dasyra makes several signs with her hands, and the bailiff nods and signs back.\nDasyra 用手比划了几个手势，法警点点头，也用手语回应。"

    old "Since the brooch and I are both items in the exchange, the bailiff is going to take, ah, custody of both of us until the contract is signed."
    new "Since the brooch and I are both items in the exchange, the bailiff is going to take, ah, custody of both of us until the contract is signed.\n既然我和胸针都是这笔交易中的交换物，在合同签署之前，法警会先，呃，把我们都看管起来。"

    old "Fine, fine."
    new "Fine, fine.\n行，行。"

    old "I hand the brooch to the bailiff, and one of the Arasmas guards leaves the room with him, escorting Dasyra out. The door shuts behind them, leaving Galan and me alone with Edgar and the remaining Arasmas guard. Edgar turns to me with a scowl."
    new "I hand the brooch to the bailiff, and one of the Arasmas guards leaves the room with him, escorting Dasyra out. The door shuts behind them, leaving Galan and me alone with Edgar and the remaining Arasmas guard. Edgar turns to me with a scowl.\n我把胸针交给法警，一名 Arasmas 守卫随他一起离开了房间，押送 Dasyra 出去。门在他们身后关上，屋里只剩下我和 Galan，以及 Edgar 和另一名 Arasmas 守卫。Edgar 板着脸转向我。"

    old "You've been a tremendous pain in my side ever since you first came to Hammerhands."
    new "You've been a tremendous pain in my side ever since you first came to Hammerhands.\n自从你第一次踏进 Hammerhands，你就一直是我肋下的一根巨刺。"

    old "Suddenly, I feel someone grab my hands, and I'm pulled back as my arms are restrained."
    new "Suddenly, I feel someone grab my hands, and I'm pulled back as my arms are restrained.\n突然，我感觉有人抓住了我的手，我的双臂被反扭住，整个人被向后拽去。"

    old "I struggle in the Arasmas guard's grasp, but he keeps me restrained as Edgar steps closer to my face."
    new "I struggle in the Arasmas guard's grasp, but he keeps me restrained as Edgar steps closer to my face.\n我在那名 Arasmas 守卫的钳制下挣扎，但他死死按住我，而 Edgar 则凑近了我的脸。"

    old "Never turn your back to an enemy, [protag]. You should know that."
    new "Never turn your back to an enemy, [protag]. You should know that.\n永远别把后背亮给敌人，[protag]。你该明白这一点。"

    old "Edgar swings his arm, hitting my face with the back of his hand. I try to pull away, but his guard's restraining grip makes it impossible for me to escape the blow."
    new "Edgar swings his arm, hitting my face with the back of his hand. I try to pull away, but his guard's restraining grip makes it impossible for me to escape the blow.\nEdgar 挥起手臂，用手背抽在我脸上。我想躲开，可那守卫的钳制让我根本躲不开这一下。"

    old "You never should have come to Hammerhands. You should know when you're not welcome."
    new "You never should have come to Hammerhands. You should know when you're not welcome.\n你压根就不该来 Hammerhands。你该明白什么时候自己不受欢迎。"

    old "Edgar draws his hand back and strikes again, this time hitting me with even greater force."
    new "Edgar draws his hand back and strikes again, this time hitting me with even greater force.\nEdgar 又扬起手，再次抽下来，这次力道更重。"

    old "Edgar looks at me with a sinister grin."
    new "Edgar looks at me with a sinister grin.\nEdgar 冲我露出一个阴险的笑。"

    old "What's the matter? Aren't you going to beg for help?"
    new "What's the matter? Aren't you going to beg for help?\n怎么了？不打算求饶吗？"

    old "Galan, help!"
    new "Galan, help!\nGalan，救我！"

    old "Galan looks at Edgar with hateful eyes."
    new "Galan looks at Edgar with hateful eyes.\nGalan 用满是恨意的目光瞪着 Edgar。"

    old "Stop it."
    new "Stop it.\n住手。"

    old "Come and make me."
    new "Come and make me.\n有本事你来拦啊。"

    old "Edgar turns his attention back to me, and pulls his arm back for another slap, but it never comes. Galan grabs Edgar from behind and wraps his arms around the nobleman, restraining him."
    new "Edgar turns his attention back to me, and pulls his arm back for another slap, but it never comes. Galan grabs Edgar from behind and wraps his arms around the nobleman, restraining him.\nEdgar 把注意力转回我身上，又一次扬起手臂准备再抽，但那一下终究没有落下。Galan 从背后抓住 Edgar，双臂环住这位贵族，把他制住了。"

    old "Oh, come on, you brute. You've got more than that in you."
    new "Oh, come on, you brute. You've got more than that in you.\n哦，来啊，你这莽汉。你身上可不只这点本事。"

    old "Galan tightens his grip on Edgar."
    new "Galan tightens his grip on Edgar.\nGalan 收紧了抓住 Edgar 的力道。"

    old "Come on, I know you want to rough me up. Go ahead and do it."
    new "Come on, I know you want to rough me up. Go ahead and do it.\n来啊，我知道你想揍我一顿。尽管动手啊。"

    old "I'm but a dainty nobleman, and you seem to hate me so. A dwarf like you could snap me like a twig. You know you want to."
    new "I'm but a dainty nobleman, and you seem to hate me so. A dwarf like you could snap me like a twig. You know you want to.\n我不过是个娇贵的贵族，而你似乎恨我入骨。像你这样的矮人，把我像根小树枝一样折断都行。你心里清楚你想动手。"

    old "Restrain him, Galan. Don't let him taunt you into fighting him."
    new "Restrain him, Galan. Don't let him taunt you into fighting him.\n制住他就行，Galan。别被他激得跟他动手。"

    old "Rough him up, Galan. A broken bone or two ought to shut him up."
    new "Rough him up, Galan. A broken bone or two ought to shut him up.\n揍他，Galan。断他一两根骨头，他自然就闭嘴了。"

    old "At that moment, the door swings open and the judge walks in."
    new "At that moment, the door swings open and the judge walks in.\n就在这时，门被推开，法官走了进来。"

    old "What the devil is going on in here?"
    new "What the devil is going on in here?\n这里他妈的到底在闹什么？"

    old "This [manwoman] assaulted me!"
    new "This [manwoman] assaulted me!\n这个 [manwoman] 袭击了我！"

    old "What? He assaulted me!"
    new "What? He assaulted me!\n什么？是他袭击了我！"

    old "Sounds to me like a case of mutual assault. Outside the courts of Hammerhands, we call that a 'fight.' The courthouse is where we settle our disputes with words, not fists. Shame on both of you. At least your retainers had the good sense to restrain you before you could do each other any harm."
    new "Sounds to me like a case of mutual assault. Outside the courts of Hammerhands, we call that a 'fight.' The courthouse is where we settle our disputes with words, not fists. Shame on both of you. At least your retainers had the good sense to restrain you before you could do each other any harm.\n依我看，这像是双方互殴。在 Hammerhands 的法庭之外，我们管这叫打架。法院是用言语而非拳头解决争端的地方。你们俩都该感到羞愧。至少你们的随从还算有分寸，在你们互相造成伤害之前把你们拉开了。"

    old "Now, I was called here to notarize a contract. Let's get this over with as quickly as possible."
    new "Now, I was called here to notarize a contract. Let's get this over with as quickly as possible.\n好了，我是被请来公证一份合同的。让我们尽快办完吧。"

    old "Thank you for coming back for me. Somehow, we all managed to make it out."
    new "Thank you for coming back for me. Somehow, we all managed to make it out.\n谢谢你们回来救我。不知怎的，我们居然都平安出来了。"

    old "I can't believe it's all come to this. When you two came to my rescue in the street, I never imagined that you'd turn out to be emissaries of Grimoire."
    new "I can't believe it's all come to this. When you two came to my rescue in the street, I never imagined that you'd turn out to be emissaries of Grimoire.\n真不敢相信事情会走到这一步。你们俩在街上救我的时候，我做梦也没想到，你们竟会是 Grimoire 的使节。"

    old "[HeShe]'s an emissary, I'm just tagging along. A good diplomat needs some muscle behind [himher], especially when [heshe]'s negotiating with zombies and vampires, which are almost as unpleasant as Hammerhands noblemen."
    new "[HeShe]'s an emissary, I'm just tagging along. A good diplomat needs some muscle behind [himher], especially when [heshe]'s negotiating with zombies and vampires, which are almost as unpleasant as Hammerhands noblemen.\n[HeShe] 才是使节，我只是跟着凑数的。一个好外交官身后总得有些武力撑腰，尤其是当 [heshe] 要跟僵尸和吸血鬼谈判时——那些家伙几乎和 Hammerhands 的贵族一样讨人厌。"

    old "Vampires?"
    new "Vampires?\n吸血鬼？"

    old "Surely you've heard of mists around the plains of N'Mar. There's evil sequestered in the castle, and it's leaking."
    new "Surely you've heard of mists around the plains of N'Mar. There's evil sequestered in the castle, and it's leaking.\n你肯定听说过 N'Mar 平原周围的雾气吧。城堡里蛰伏着邪恶，而它正在外泄。"

    old "And you intend to march on up to those monsters and give them what for."
    new "And you intend to march on up to those monsters and give them what for.\n而你们打算一路杀到那些怪物面前，好好教训它们一顿。"

    old "Yes, that's one way of putting it."
    new "Yes, that's one way of putting it.\n是的，也可以这么说。"

    old "Do you think that you might want the company of a healer when you go to confront evil incarnate?"
    new "Do you think that you might want the company of a healer when you go to confront evil incarnate?\n你们去直面那邪恶的化身时，会不会想要一位治疗师随行呢？"

    old "What do you think, Galan? Should we let her join us?"
    new "What do you think, Galan? Should we let her join us?\n你觉得呢，Galan？我们该让她加入吗？"

    old "If one thing has been born out of all of this, it's that Dasyra is a survivor. And don't forget how it all started. She knows how to handle a staff."
    new "If one thing has been born out of all of this, it's that Dasyra is a survivor. And don't forget how it all started. She knows how to handle a staff.\n要说这一切带来了什么，那就是证明了 Dasyra 是个能活下去的人。而且别忘了这一切是怎么开始的。她使法杖很在行。"

    old "Dasyra smiles and takes a bow."
    new "Dasyra smiles and takes a bow.\nDasyra 微笑着，欠身行了一礼。"

    old "I guess it's unanimous, Dasyra. I don't know what would compel someone to volunteer to fight the undead, but who am I to refuse the offer?"
    new "I guess it's unanimous, Dasyra. I don't know what would compel someone to volunteer to fight the undead, but who am I to refuse the offer?\n我想这是全体通过了，Dasyra。我不知道是什么促使一个人自愿去与亡灵作战，但我又有什么资格拒绝这份好意呢？"

    old "You know, it's odd. Moments ago I was thinking about how with Dasyra freed, we're all back to where we started."
    new "You know, it's odd. Moments ago I was thinking about how with Dasyra freed, we're all back to where we started.\n你知道吗，说来也怪。片刻之前我还在想，随着 Dasyra 获救，我们所有人又回到了起点。"

    old "But I think we've actually gained something more. When I first came to this city, I came in search of allies. It would seem as though fate as connected me to them."
    new "But I think we've actually gained something more. When I first came to this city, I came in search of allies. It would seem as though fate as connected me to them.\n但我想，我们其实收获了更多。当初我来到这座城市，就是为了寻找盟友。如今看来，命运似乎已将我和他们连在了一起。"

    old "Galan, wait!"
    new "Galan, wait!\nGalan，等等！"

    old "What's the matter? Aren't you going to help your friend?"
    new "What's the matter? Aren't you going to help your friend?\n怎么了？你不打算帮帮你的朋友吗？"

    old "Don't do it, Galan. He's trying to provoke you."
    new "Don't do it, Galan. He's trying to provoke you.\n别动手，Galan。他是在故意激你。"

    old "Quiet, you."
    new "Quiet, you.\n你给我闭嘴。"

    old "Edgar turns and backhands me in the face again."
    new "Edgar turns and backhands me in the face again.\nEdgar 转过身，又反手抽了我一记耳光。"

    old "What a terrible companion you are, watching as your friend is beaten senseless."
    new "What a terrible companion you are, watching as your friend is beaten senseless.\n你这同伴可真够差劲的，眼睁睁看着朋友被打得神志不清。"

    old "It's not worth it, Galan. Edgar's a weakling anyway. His slaps don't even hurt."
    new "It's not worth it, Galan. Edgar's a weakling anyway. His slaps don't even hurt.\n这不值得，Galan。反正Edgar就是个软蛋。他扇的巴掌连疼都不疼。"

    old "You just don't know when to keep quiet, do you?"
    new "You just don't know when to keep quiet, do you?\n你就是不知道什么时候该闭嘴，是吧？"

    old "Edgar makes a fist and slams it into my face."
    new "Edgar makes a fist and slams it into my face.\nEdgar握紧拳头，狠狠砸在我脸上。"

    old "Is that all you've got?"
    new "Is that all you've got?\n你就这点本事吗？"

    old "Shut up!"
    new "Shut up!\n闭嘴！"

    old "Edgar throws another punch at my face, but this time I lower my head. His fist collides with my forehead, and I hear the sound of crackling knuckles."
    new "Edgar throws another punch at my face, but this time I lower my head. His fist collides with my forehead, and I hear the sound of crackling knuckles.\nEdgar又朝我脸上挥了一拳，但这次我低下了头。他的拳头撞上我的额头，我听见指关节咔咔作响。"

    old "Bloody hell!"
    new "Bloody hell!\n该死的！"

    old "Edgar holds his hand, wringing it gingerly."
    new "Edgar holds his hand, wringing it gingerly.\nEdgar握着自己那只手，小心翼翼地揉着。"

    old "Hope you didn't break any fingers there, Edgar."
    new "Hope you didn't break any fingers there, Edgar.\n希望你那儿没断手指，Edgar。"

    old "To hell with you!"
    new "To hell with you!\n去你的！"

    old "Edgar rears up for another punch, and it connects just as the door swings open."
    new "Edgar rears up for another punch, and it connects just as the door swings open.\nEdgar直起身子又抡起一拳，就在门被推开的那一刻，这一拳落了下来。"

    old "What in Irijo's name is going on here?"
    new "What in Irijo's name is going on here?\n以Irijo之名，这里到底在闹什么？"

    old "Edgar freezes and turns toward the judge with a look of horror."
    new "Edgar freezes and turns toward the judge with a look of horror.\nEdgar僵住了，一脸惊恐地转向法官。"

    old "Your Honor, I, ah..."
    new "Your Honor, I, ah...\n法官大人，我，呃……"

    old "It's exactly what it looks like, Your Honor."
    new "It's exactly what it looks like, Your Honor.\n就是您看到的这样，法官大人。"

    old "Get your hands off of that [manwoman]!"
    new "Get your hands off of that [manwoman]!\n把你的手从那个[manwoman]身上拿开！"

    old "The Arasmas guard loosens his grip on me, and I make a show of falling forward onto the floor."
    new "The Arasmas guard loosens his grip on me, and I make a show of falling forward onto the floor.\nArasmas守卫松开了抓我的手，我便顺势朝前一扑，摔倒在地板上。"

    old "You'd better start explaining this, Arasmas."
    new "You'd better start explaining this, Arasmas.\n你最好开始解释一下，Arasmas。"

    old "Y-your Honor, this [manwoman] insulted my, ah, father. I had to defend my family's name."
    new "Y-your Honor, this [manwoman] insulted my, ah, father. I had to defend my family's name.\n法、法官大人，这个[manwoman]侮辱了我的，呃，父亲。我不得不捍卫我家族的名声。"

    old "And so you responded by having your man restrain [himher] while you savagely beat [himher]? Arasmas, were this [manwoman] a noble of Hammerhands, this would be a capital offense."
    new "And so you responded by having your man restrain [himher] while you savagely beat [himher]? Arasmas, were this [manwoman] a noble of Hammerhands, this would be a capital offense.\n所以你回应他的方式，就是让你的手下按住[himher]，然后自己野蛮地殴打[himher]？Arasmas，倘若这个[manwoman]是Hammerhands的贵族，这可是死罪。"

    old "But [heshe]'s not, Your Honor."
    new "But [heshe]'s not, Your Honor.\n但[heshe]不是，法官大人。"

    old "Yes, which is why I'm willing to consider leniency."
    new "Yes, which is why I'm willing to consider leniency.\n没错，正因如此，我才愿意考虑从轻发落。"

    old "Now, the representative from Grimoire. What was your name?"
    new "Now, the representative from Grimoire. What was your name?\n那么，来自Grimoire的代表。你叫什么名字？"

    old "My name is [protag], Your Honor."
    new "My name is [protag], Your Honor.\n我叫[protag]，法官大人。"

    old "Do you have anything to say? What do you think would be an appropriate punishment for this man?"
    new "Do you have anything to say? What do you think would be an appropriate punishment for this man?\n你有什么要说的吗？你觉得对这个男人来说，怎样惩罚才算合适？"

    old "Your Honor, if I may be so bold as to make a suggestion..."
    new "Your Honor, if I may be so bold as to make a suggestion...\n法官大人，如果我能斗胆提个建议……"

    old "By all means."
    new "By all means.\n请讲。"

    old "Give us your bracer."
    new "Give us your bracer.\n把你的护腕交出来。"

    old "My what?"
    new "My what?\n我的什么？"

    old "Your studded bracer. Give it to us."
    new "Your studded bracer. Give it to us.\n你的镶钉护腕。交给我们。"

    old "This is my family's emblem. I require this to do business here at the summit. I can't surrender it. If I leave this room without it and am seen walking about without my own family's emblem, I'll be disgraced."
    new "This is my family's emblem. I require this to do business here at the summit. I can't surrender it. If I leave this room without it and am seen walking about without my own family's emblem, I'll be disgraced.\n这是我家族的徽记。我在这峰会上做生意需要它。我不能交出去。如果我离开这房间时没带着它，被人看到我四处走动却没佩戴自己家族的徽记，我会颜面扫地。"

    old "I think that is exactly what he intended, Arasmas."
    new "I think that is exactly what he intended, Arasmas.\n我想那正是他的意图，Arasmas。"

    old "What you've done here is disgraceful. It seems only appropriate that you should be disgraced as a consequence."
    new "What you've done here is disgraceful. It seems only appropriate that you should be disgraced as a consequence.\n你在这里的所作所为实在可耻。让你因此蒙羞，似乎再合适不过了。"

    old "But I—"
    new "But I—\n可我——"

    old "Do you really not understand the situation you are in, Edgar? You are being offered leniency here. For your own benefit, I hope you don't decline it."
    new "Do you really not understand the situation you are in, Edgar? You are being offered leniency here. For your own benefit, I hope you don't decline it.\n你真的不明白自己现在的处境吗，Edgar？这里给你的可是从轻发落。为了你自己好，我希望你别拒绝。"

    old "Edgar rips the bracer off his arm, throwing it onto the floor."
    new "Edgar rips the bracer off his arm, throwing it onto the floor.\nEdgar从手臂上扯下护腕，扔到了地上。"

    old "Edgar hangs his head and turns away. I see his shoulders rise and fall, and hear what sounds like a sob. Is Edgar crying?"
    new "Edgar hangs his head and turns away. I see his shoulders rise and fall, and hear what sounds like a sob. Is Edgar crying?\nEdgar垂下头，转过身去。我看见他的肩膀起伏着，还听见一声像是抽泣的声音。Edgar哭了吗？"

    old "The judge looks at Edgar and shakes his head, then turns to me."
    new "The judge looks at Edgar and shakes his head, then turns to me.\n法官看了看Edgar，摇了摇头，然后转向我。"

    old "I'm truly sorry about what happened here today. I don't know how this started, but nothing excuses his behavior. When Grimoire's council sent their representative to the Hammerhands summit, they surely didn't expect for them to be battered as you were."
    new "I'm truly sorry about what happened here today. I don't know how this started, but nothing excuses his behavior. When Grimoire's council sent their representative to the Hammerhands summit, they surely didn't expect for them to be battered as you were.\n今天发生的事，我由衷地感到抱歉。我不知道事情是怎么闹起来的，但无论如何都不能为他的行为开脱。Grimoire议会派代表出席Hammerhands峰会时，他们肯定没料到派来的代表会像你一样挨打。"

    old "I wish I had the words to extend you a proper apology. This man has made an incredibly poor example of this city."
    new "I wish I had the words to extend you a proper apology. This man has made an incredibly poor example of this city.\n真希望我能找到合适的措辞向你正式道歉。这个人给这座城市树立了一个糟糕透顶的榜样。"

    old "It's alright, Your Honor. I understand that not all the people of Hammerhands are as rude as this man here."
    new "It's alright, Your Honor. I understand that not all the people of Hammerhands are as rude as this man here.\n没关系，法官大人。我知道Hammerhands并非所有人都像这个男人一样粗鲁。"

    old "Calling him 'rude' is being far too charitable. I often find myself sickened by the dealings of nobles, but this is a new low."
    new "Calling him 'rude' is being far too charitable. I often find myself sickened by the dealings of nobles, but this is a new low.\n说他“粗鲁”实在太客气了。我常常被贵族的那些勾当恶心到，但这次又刷新了下限。"

    old "Now, I was called here to notarize a contract. Let's get that done and over with, shall we?"
    new "Now, I was called here to notarize a contract. Let's get that done and over with, shall we?\n好了，我被叫来是给一份契约做公证的。我们把这事办完就散了吧？"

    old "I know it was my idea, but I still can't believe I got to see a nobleman escorted out of the summit stripped of his emblem."
    new "I know it was my idea, but I still can't believe I got to see a nobleman escorted out of the summit stripped of his emblem.\n我知道这是我的主意，可我还是不敢相信，竟然能看到一个贵族被剥掉徽记、护送着赶出峰会。"

    old "I can't believe I got to see Edgar crying as he was led out."
    new "I can't believe I got to see Edgar crying as he was led out.\n真不敢相信，我居然看到Edgar被带出去时在哭。"

    old "I can't believe I managed to survive that assault without so much as a bloody nose. For a man who likes to slap people, Edgar sure has weak arms."
    new "I can't believe I managed to survive that assault without so much as a bloody nose. For a man who likes to slap people, Edgar sure has weak arms.\n真不敢相信，我挺过那场袭击，居然连鼻子都没流血。对于一个喜欢扇人巴掌的人来说，Edgar的胳膊还真是没力气。"

    old "Dasyra begins laughing, and Galan and I join in her infectious laughter."
    new "Dasyra begins laughing, and Galan and I join in her infectious laughter.\nDasyra笑了起来，Galan和我也被她那富有感染力的笑声带动，跟着笑了。"

    old "[HeShe]'s an emissary, I'm just tagging along. A good diplomat needs some muscle behind [himher], especially when [heshe]'s negotiating with zombies and vampires."
    new "[HeShe]'s an emissary, I'm just tagging along. A good diplomat needs some muscle behind [himher], especially when [heshe]'s negotiating with zombies and vampires.\n[HeShe]是使者，我只是跟着来的。一个好外交官身后总得有点武力撑腰，尤其是在[heshe]跟僵尸和吸血鬼谈判的时候。"

    old "You know, it's odd. Moments ago I was thinking about how with Dasyra freed, we're all back to where we started. But I think we've actually gained something more. When I first came to this city, I came in search of allies. It would seem as though fate as connected me to them."
    new "You know, it's odd. Moments ago I was thinking about how with Dasyra freed, we're all back to where we started. But I think we've actually gained something more. When I first came to this city, I came in search of allies. It would seem as though fate as connected me to them.\n你知道吗，说来也怪。刚才我还在想，Dasyra既然已经自由了，我们岂不是又回到了起点。但我觉得，我们其实还收获了更多。当初我来这座城市，是为了寻找盟友。如今看来，命运似乎把我同他们紧紧连在了一起。"

    old "Don't forget, we're now also richer to the tune of one Arasmas emblem."
    new "Don't forget, we're now also richer to the tune of one Arasmas emblem.\n别忘了，我们现在还多了一枚Arasmas徽记，身家更丰厚了。"

    old "Galan holds up the bracer."
    new "Galan holds up the bracer.\nGalan举起了那只护腕。"

    old "What do you reckon we ought to do with that thing, Galan?"
    new "What do you reckon we ought to do with that thing, Galan?\n你觉得我们该怎么处理那玩意儿，Galan？"

    old "Well, it just happens to fit me. Fine Faberge Arasmas craftsmanship, this one. I feel stronger just wearing it. Edgar's old man knew how to make armor as elegant as it is functional."
    new "Well, it just happens to fit me. Fine Faberge Arasmas craftsmanship, this one. I feel stronger just wearing it. Edgar's old man knew how to make armor as elegant as it is functional.\n嗯，它恰好正合我戴。这可是Arasmas上等的Faberge工艺。戴上它我就觉得更有力气了。Edgar的老爹懂得打造既优雅又实用的盔甲。"

    old "It's not every day that you get to take a noble family's emblem as your trophy. I think I may as well see what mileage I can get out of it."
    new "It's not every day that you get to take a noble family's emblem as your trophy. I think I may as well see what mileage I can get out of it.\n能拿贵族家族的徽记当战利品，可不是天天都有的事。我想我不妨看看它能给我带来多少好处。"

    old "It looks good on you, Galan. I'm sure it would vex Edgar to see you walking around Hammerhands with his family's emblem, so don't be shy about wearing it in public."
    new "It looks good on you, Galan. I'm sure it would vex Edgar to see you walking around Hammerhands with his family's emblem, so don't be shy about wearing it in public.\n你戴着很好看，Galan。我敢肯定，Edgar看到你戴着他家的徽记在Hammerhands晃悠，肯定气得够呛，所以你尽管大胆在公开场合戴着。"

    old "I see a familiar-looking dwarf sitting on a rock by the Grimoire town gates. His legs are crossed, and his hands are placed deliberately on his knees, as if he's about to prostrate himself in a bow."
    new "I see a familiar-looking dwarf sitting on a rock by the Grimoire town gates. His legs are crossed, and his hands are placed deliberately on his knees, as if he's about to prostrate himself in a bow.\n我看见一个眼熟的矮人坐在Grimoire城门旁的一块石头上。他盘着腿，双手刻意地搭在膝盖上，仿佛正要俯身行个大礼。"

    old "Both his eyes are closed, and he wears an expression of relaxed concentration."
    new "Both his eyes are closed, and he wears an expression of relaxed concentration.\n他双目紧闭，脸上是一副放松而专注的神情。"

    old "Ho, Galan!"
    new "Ho, Galan!\n嚯，Galan！"

    old "Galan opens his eyes and blinks several times. His eyes settle on me, and he smiles."
    new "Galan opens his eyes and blinks several times. His eyes settle on me, and he smiles.\nGalan睁开眼睛，连眨了几下。他的目光落到我身上，随即笑了起来。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. What brings you here?"
    new "Ah, [protag]. What brings you here?\n啊，[protag]。什么风把你吹来了？"

    old "I could ask you the same thing. It's not every day that you see a dwarf like you perched outside the entrance to Grimoire."
    new "I could ask you the same thing. It's not every day that you see a dwarf like you perched outside the entrance to Grimoire.\n我正想问你同样的问题。能看到像你这样的矮人坐在Grimoire入口外头，可不是天天都有的事。"

    old "Galan seems to be deep in thought, and whatever it is, I feel like it would be rude to interrupt him."
    new "Galan seems to be deep in thought, and whatever it is, I feel like it would be rude to interrupt him.\nGalan似乎陷入了沉思，不管在想什么，我都觉得打断他不太礼貌。"

    old "A fly buzzes around his head, but Galan makes no motion to swat it away. The fly lands on his hand. I see the muscles in his hand tense, but a moment later they relax, and Galan remains sitting, eyes shut, with the fly on his arm."
    new "A fly buzzes around his head, but Galan makes no motion to swat it away. The fly lands on his hand. I see the muscles in his hand tense, but a moment later they relax, and Galan remains sitting, eyes shut, with the fly on his arm.\n一只苍蝇在他脑袋周围嗡嗡转，Galan却没有任何挥手赶它的动作。苍蝇落在他手上。我看见他手上的肌肉绷紧了，但片刻后又放松下来，Galan依旧坐着，双目紧闭，任由苍蝇停在他的手臂上。"

    old "The fly takes off and lands again, this time choosing his nose as a landing spot. His nose wrinkles, but the fly doesn't move. I watch as Galan scrunches and contorts his face, until finally he snaps."
    new "The fly takes off and lands again, this time choosing his nose as a landing spot. His nose wrinkles, but the fly doesn't move. I watch as Galan scrunches and contorts his face, until finally he snaps.\n苍蝇飞起来又落下，这次选了他的鼻子当落脚点。他的鼻子皱了皱，苍蝇却纹丝不动。我眼看着Galan把脸挤成一团、扭来扭去，直到最后他忍无可忍。"

    old "Blast it!"
    new "Blast it!\n见鬼！"

    old "Galan raises a hand and smacks himself in the face, missing the fly by a hair."
    new "Galan raises a hand and smacks himself in the face, missing the fly by a hair.\nGalan抬起一只手，一巴掌拍在自己脸上，只差一丝就打着苍蝇了。"

    old "Whoa there, don't hurt yourself."
    new "Whoa there, don't hurt yourself.\n喂喂，别伤着自己。"

    old "Galan looks up at me and smiles."
    new "Galan looks up at me and smiles.\nGalan抬头看我，笑了笑。"

    old "Ah, [protag], you were watching that?"
    new "Ah, [protag], you were watching that?\n啊，[protag]，你都看到了？"

    old "What are you doing? Some kind of prayer?"
    new "What are you doing? Some kind of prayer?\n你在干什么？某种祷告吗？"

    old "I was meditating. Or trying to, at any rate. It's a habit I've been trying to develop."
    new "I was meditating. Or trying to, at any rate. It's a habit I've been trying to develop.\n我在冥想。或者说，在试着冥想。这是我一直想养成的一个习惯。"

    old "Why meditate here, of all places? With people constantly walking by to enter the city, it's not exactly the most private spot. I mean, I found you. Why not pick some place more secluded?"
    new "Why meditate here, of all places? With people constantly walking by to enter the city, it's not exactly the most private spot. I mean, I found you. Why not pick some place more secluded?\n怎么会偏偏在这儿冥想？人们进进出出不停地从这儿经过，这可不是最私密的地方。我是说，我都找到你了。为什么不挑个更僻静点的地方？"

    old "Meditating is a bit of a skill. Learning to be mindful, regardless of your surrounding circumstances, is a big part of the exercise."
    new "Meditating is a bit of a skill. Learning to be mindful, regardless of your surrounding circumstances, is a big part of the exercise.\n冥想是一门技巧。学会保持专注，不受周围环境影响，是这门练习里很重要的一部分。"

    old "Did someone teach you this?"
    new "Did someone teach you this?\n是有人教你的吗？"

    old "I once served as an escort for a traveling monk. He tried to persuade me to try meditating with him."
    new "I once served as an escort for a traveling monk. He tried to persuade me to try meditating with him.\n我曾经给一位云游僧当过护卫。他试图说服我，让我试着跟他一起冥想。"

    old "Looks like he succeeded."
    new "Looks like he succeeded.\n看来他成功了。"

    old "No, he failed miserably. At the time, I thought the practice was silly. Sitting alone and just thinking, it seemed a mix of boredom and pointlessness. It wasn't until years after that I tried to recall what the monk had tried to teach me."
    new "No, he failed miserably. At the time, I thought the practice was silly. Sitting alone and just thinking, it seemed a mix of boredom and pointlessness. It wasn't until years after that I tried to recall what the monk had tried to teach me.\n不，他败得一塌糊涂。当时我觉得这练习很傻。一个人干坐着，光顾着想东想西，既无聊又没意义。直到多年以后，我才试着回忆起当年那位僧人想教我的东西。"

    old "So what changed?"
    new "So what changed?\n那是什么让你变了？"

    old "I'm trying to control my temper. A berserker's rage, when focused, can be a powerful tool. But when unfocused...I can easily hurt people I don't intend to hurt."
    new "I'm trying to control my temper. A berserker's rage, when focused, can be a powerful tool. But when unfocused...I can easily hurt people I don't intend to hurt.\n我在试着控制自己的脾气。狂暴者的怒火，若能收放自如，会是很强大的武器。但若失控……我很容易伤到本不想伤的人。"

    old "I thought that practicing mindfulness and meditation would give me a greater sense of inner peace?"
    new "I thought that practicing mindfulness and meditation would give me a greater sense of inner peace?\n我本来以为，练习正念和冥想能给我带来更强的内心平静？"

    old "Has it worked?"
    new "Has it worked?\n有效果吗？"

    old "Yes, it has. But it's not an overnight transformation. I still lose my temper now and then. It's a slow process."
    new "Yes, it has. But it's not an overnight transformation. I still lose my temper now and then. It's a slow process.\n有。但这不是一夜之间就能转变的事。我偶尔还是会发脾气。这是个缓慢的过程。"

    old "I always thought the idea of meditating seemed really dull and boring. But it's actually quite intense."
    new "I always thought the idea of meditating seemed really dull and boring. But it's actually quite intense.\n我一直觉得冥想这主意又闷又无聊。但其实还挺激烈的。"

    old "What exactly is meditation? Just sitting still and focusing your mind on something?"
    new "What exactly is meditation? Just sitting still and focusing your mind on something?\n冥想到底是什么？就是一动不动地坐着，把心思集中到某样东西上？"

    old "I could try to explain it to you. But I think that doing something can be more informative than hearing about it."
    new "I could try to explain it to you. But I think that doing something can be more informative than hearing about it.\n我可以试着跟你解释。但我觉得，亲身做一遍，比光听别人讲更有启发。"

    old "Would you like to try meditating? I'm by no means an expert, but I think I could help guide you through a session."
    new "Would you like to try meditating? I'm by no means an expert, but I think I could help guide you through a session.\n你想试试冥想吗？我绝不是专家，不过我想我多少能带你做一次。"

    old "Sure, I'll give it a try. What am I supposed to do?"
    new "Sure, I'll give it a try. What am I supposed to do?\n好啊，我试试。我该怎么做？"

    old "Can you be comfortable sitting on a rock?"
    new "Can you be comfortable sitting on a rock?\n坐在石头上，你能舒服吗？"

    old "I've learned how to be comfortable in lots of positions and places. Sitting on a rock is no problem for me."
    new "I've learned how to be comfortable in lots of positions and places. Sitting on a rock is no problem for me.\n我在各种姿势、各种地方都能待得舒服。坐在石头上对我完全不是问题。"

    old "Galan stands up and gestures to the stone where he was sitting. I take a seat."
    new "Galan stands up and gestures to the stone where he was sitting. I take a seat.\nGalan站起身，朝他刚才坐的那块石头比了比。我坐了下来。"

    old "Get comfortable in a position that you won't mind holding for the next few minutes."
    new "Get comfortable in a position that you won't mind holding for the next few minutes.\n找个舒服的姿势，接下来几分钟你都得保持住，得找个你不会难受的坐法。"

    old "I'm not allowed to move?"
    new "I'm not allowed to move?\n我不能动吗？"

    old "If you do it right, you won't want to move."
    new "If you do it right, you won't want to move.\n做得对的话，你根本就不会想动。"

    old "Start by taking deep breaths."
    new "Start by taking deep breaths.\n先开始深呼吸。"

    old "I breathe several times."
    new "I breathe several times.\n我呼吸了几次。"

    old "Deep breaths means breathing so loudly that the people around you could hear, if they bothered to listen."
    new "Deep breaths means breathing so loudly that the people around you could hear, if they bothered to listen.\n深呼吸的意思，是呼吸声要大到让周围的人都能听见——如果他们愿意听的话。"

    old "I heave several more heavy breaths."
    new "I heave several more heavy breaths.\n我又重重地喘了几口气。"

    old "Now, close your eyes."
    new "Now, close your eyes.\n现在，闭上眼睛。"

    old "Focus on the sounds around you. Don't try to concentrate on any individual sound. Just hear what's around you. Try to paint a picture in your head of your surroundings."
    new "Focus on the sounds around you. Don't try to concentrate on any individual sound. Just hear what's around you. Try to paint a picture in your head of your surroundings.\n把注意力放在你周围的声音上。别试图去专注某一个声音。只要去听你周遭的一切。试着在脑中描绘出你四周的画面。"

    old "I listen. I hear the chatter of several women on the other side of the city gate. I can't make out the individual words, but based on their hushed tones, it must be some kind of gossip."
    new "I listen. I hear the chatter of several women on the other side of the city gate. I can't make out the individual words, but based on their hushed tones, it must be some kind of gossip.\n我听着。我听见城门另一边几个女人在窃窃私语。我听不清具体每个字，但从她们压低的声音来看，一定是某种闲话。"

    old "There are several birds chirping. They seem to be stationary. Below me. Birds not in flight, but on the ground."
    new "There are several birds chirping. They seem to be stationary. Below me. Birds not in flight, but on the ground.\n有几只鸟在啁啾。它们似乎停着不动。在我下方。鸟儿没有在飞，而是落在地上。"

    old "Come to think of it, I wonder if the birds around the planes of N'Mar have been disturbed any. The plague has ravaged the landscape. I suppose it's no surprise seeing crows when there's so much rot around, but what about the other birds, like jays and sparrows?"
    new "Come to think of it, I wonder if the birds around the planes of N'Mar have been disturbed any. The plague has ravaged the landscape. I suppose it's no surprise seeing crows when there's so much rot around, but what about the other birds, like jays and sparrows?\n说起来，我倒想知道，N'Mar平原一带的鸟儿有没有受到什么惊扰。瘟疫已经把这片土地摧残得不成样子。周围有这么多腐烂的东西，看到乌鸦倒也不稀奇，可其他鸟呢，比如松鸦和麻雀？"

    old "Remember, focus on the sounds and sensations around you. If you find your mind wandering and turning to other thoughts, let those thoughts pass and turn your attention back to what's around you."
    new "Remember, focus on the sounds and sensations around you. If you find your mind wandering and turning to other thoughts, let those thoughts pass and turn your attention back to what's around you.\n记住，把注意力放在你周围的声音和感受上。如果你发现思绪飘走、转到了别的念头上，就让那些念头过去，再把注意力拉回到你周遭的事物上。"

    old "I take another deep breath and try to concentrate again on the things around me."
    new "I take another deep breath and try to concentrate again on the things around me.\n我又深吸一口气，试着再次把注意力集中到周围的事物上。"

    old "I hear the sound of a wheeled cart moving through the streets. There's a rhythmic nature to the sound, with a slight 'thunk' every second or so. The wheel must be damaged."
    new "I hear the sound of a wheeled cart moving through the streets. There's a rhythmic nature to the sound, with a slight 'thunk' every second or so. The wheel must be damaged.\n我听见一辆带轮子的货车驶过街道的声音。这声音很有节奏，每隔一秒左右就有一声轻微的“咯噔”。车轮肯定是坏了。"

    old "Whoever owns that wagon really should get that wheel fixed. An uneven wheel puts stress on the...no, don't get distracted. Just try to take everything in."
    new "Whoever owns that wagon really should get that wheel fixed. An uneven wheel puts stress on the...no, don't get distracted. Just try to take everything in.\n不管那辆货车是谁的，真该把车轮修好。车轮不平会给……不，别分心。就试着把一切都收进来。"

    old "I shut my eyes tighter. I hear a soft pattering on the ground, like the sound of children's footsteps."
    new "I shut my eyes tighter. I hear a soft pattering on the ground, like the sound of children's footsteps.\n我把眼睛闭得更紧了些。我听见地面上有轻轻的啪嗒声，像是小孩子的脚步声。"

    old "Boo!"
    new "Boo!\n哇！"

    old "I open my eyes, just in time to see a small boy who starts giggling and runs off."
    new "I open my eyes, just in time to see a small boy who starts giggling and runs off.\n我睁开眼睛，正好看到一个小男孩咯咯笑着跑开了。"

    old "I think that's enough for today."
    new "I think that's enough for today.\n我想今天就到这儿吧。"

    old "Does that happen often? Mischievous children coming up and disturbing your meditation?"
    new "Does that happen often? Mischievous children coming up and disturbing your meditation?\n这种事经常发生吗？调皮的孩子们凑上来打扰你冥想？"

    old "Not really, no. But I have noticed some children staring at me on occasion. I guess I look too intimidating for them to want to bother me."
    new "Not really, no. But I have noticed some children staring at me on occasion. I guess I look too intimidating for them to want to bother me.\n倒也不是。不过我倒是有时注意到，有些孩子会盯着我看。估计我长得太吓人，他们不敢来烦我。"

    old "I don't look intimidating to you?"
    new "I don't look intimidating to you?\n我看起来不可怕吗？"

    old "Not as intimidating as I am, apparently."
    new "Not as intimidating as I am, apparently.\n显然没我这么可怕。"

    old "Anyway, what did you think of your meditation session? It was only a few minutes, but what you did is similar to what I try to do."
    new "Anyway, what did you think of your meditation session? It was only a few minutes, but what you did is similar to what I try to do.\n话说回来，你觉得这次冥想怎么样？虽然只有几分钟，但你所做的，跟我一直试着做的差不多。"

    old "It was actually a lot more intense than I expected. Trying to focus on your surroundings and not let your mind wander...it's harder than I thought it would be. And that was with you constantly reminding me. How do you manage to do it alone, with no one else to keep you on track?"
    new "It was actually a lot more intense than I expected. Trying to focus on your surroundings and not let your mind wander...it's harder than I thought it would be. And that was with you constantly reminding me. How do you manage to do it alone, with no one else to keep you on track?\n其实比我预想的激烈多了。要努力专注于周围，又不让思绪飘走……比我想象中难。而且这还是在你不断提醒我的情况下。你一个人，没人盯着你，是怎么做到的？"

    old "It's not easy. Especially for someone like me. But it does get easier when you make it a daily practice."
    new "It's not easy. Especially for someone like me. But it does get easier when you make it a daily practice.\n不容易。尤其对我这样的人来说。不过当你把它变成每天的习惯后，确实会变得容易些。"

    old "How about you just tell me what meditation is? I'm not really in the mood to start trying."
    new "How about you just tell me what meditation is? I'm not really in the mood to start trying.\n你就直接告诉我冥想是什么吧？我现在没心情开始尝试。"

    old "Meditation is, in a sense, about emptying your mind."
    new "Meditation is, in a sense, about emptying your mind.\n从某种意义上说，冥想就是放空你的心。"

    old "What's the point of that?"
    new "What's the point of that?\n那有什么意义？"

    old "Many people carry burdens and thoughts in their mind. Simply clearing the mind for a few minutes out of the day can allow you to re-orient yourself. In a way, it helps you get a fresh start on things."
    new "Many people carry burdens and thoughts in their mind. Simply clearing the mind for a few minutes out of the day can allow you to re-orient yourself. In a way, it helps you get a fresh start on things.\n很多人心里都背负着重担和思绪。一天当中，哪怕只是放空几分钟，也能让你重新找准方向。从某种程度上说，它能帮你对事情有个全新的开始。"

    old "Like when you wake up?"
    new "Like when you wake up?\n就像你醒来的时候那样？"

    old "Sort of like that, yes."
    new "Sort of like that, yes.\n差不多就是那样，是的。"

    old "How exactly do you enter your mind? Do you just...think about nothing?"
    new "How exactly do you enter your mind? Do you just...think about nothing?\n你究竟是怎么进入自己内心的？难道你就……什么都不想？"

    old "Well, trying to empty your mind and not think about things is impossible. You can't really truly empty your mind. You have to replace it with something. And I replace it with being present-minded. In the moment."
    new "Well, trying to empty your mind and not think about things is impossible. You can't really truly empty your mind. You have to replace it with something. And I replace it with being present-minded. In the moment.\n嗯，试图放空心思、什么都不想，是不可能的。你没法真正把心彻底放空。你得用别的东西去填补它。而我用来填补的，是专注当下。就在此刻。"

    old "It means being aware of your surroundings. Taking in the world around you, but not dwelling on it or judging it."
    new "It means being aware of your surroundings. Taking in the world around you, but not dwelling on it or judging it.\n意思是了解你周围的环境。去感受你周遭的世界，但不沉溺其中，也不评判它。"

    old "If the purpose of meditation is to take in your surroundings, then why close your eyes when you meditate?"
    new "If the purpose of meditation is to take in your surroundings, then why close your eyes when you meditate?\n如果冥想的目的是感受周围环境，那冥想时为什么还要闭眼？"

    old "Meditating with your eyes open can be quite overwhelming. There's just so much to take in. If you close your eyes, it's easier to just focus on the sounds and physical sensations around you."
    new "Meditating with your eyes open can be quite overwhelming. There's just so much to take in. If you close your eyes, it's easier to just focus on the sounds and physical sensations around you.\n睁着眼冥想会让人应接不暇。要接收的东西实在太多了。闭上眼睛，就更容易只专注于周围的声音和身体感受。"

    old "That's what you're doing? Listening really intently to the things around you?"
    new "That's what you're doing? Listening really intently to the things around you?\n这就是你在做的事？全神贯注地倾听周遭的一切？"

    old "In a way, I try to paint a picture in my mind of the world around me, just based on what I can take in."
    new "In a way, I try to paint a picture in my mind of the world around me, just based on what I can take in.\n从某种意义上说，我试着仅凭能接收到的信息，在脑中勾勒出周遭世界的画面。"

    old "That's actually really interesting. It sounds like...a bit of a challenge."
    new "That's actually really interesting. It sounds like...a bit of a challenge.\n那确实很有意思。听起来……像是一种挑战。"

    old "Meditation isn't easy."
    new "Meditation isn't easy.\n冥想并不容易。"

    old "It's weird. When you look at someone meditating, it doesn't seem hard at all. But the way that you describe it, it sounds almost like exercising your mind."
    new "It's weird. When you look at someone meditating, it doesn't seem hard at all. But the way that you describe it, it sounds almost like exercising your mind.\n很奇怪。看着一个人冥想时，觉得一点都不难。但听你这么一说，倒像是在锻炼自己的心智。"

    old "It is like exercise. And like any exercise, the key is to practice it regularly and maintain a habit. That's what I've been trying to do since we arrived in Grimoire."
    new "It is like exercise. And like any exercise, the key is to practice it regularly and maintain a habit. That's what I've been trying to do since we arrived in Grimoire.\n它就像是锻炼。跟任何锻炼一样，关键在于定期练习、保持习惯。自从我们到Grimoire以来，我一直在努力这么做。"

    old "How's that been going?"
    new "How's that been going?\n进展如何？"

    old "So far, so good."
    new "So far, so good.\n目前为止，还不错。"

    old "This has been really interesting, Galan. I never imagined that a hammer-toting dwarf with a unique talent for losing his temper would be the one to teach me about meditation."
    new "This has been really interesting, Galan. I never imagined that a hammer-toting dwarf with a unique talent for losing his temper would be the one to teach me about meditation.\n这真的很有意思，Galan。我从没想过，一个扛着锤子、动不动就发脾气的矮人，居然会来教我冥想。"

    old "If you really want to understand meditation, I recommend finding someone more practiced than I am. Perhaps a monk could assist you."
    new "If you really want to understand meditation, I recommend finding someone more practiced than I am. Perhaps a monk could assist you.\n如果你真想弄懂冥想，我建议你去找个比我更有修为的人。也许一位僧人能帮到你。"

    old "Honestly, I'm not that interested in meditation. But I think now I understand you a little bit better than I did before. Thanks for sharing this with me, Galan."
    new "Honestly, I'm not that interested in meditation. But I think now I understand you a little bit better than I did before. Thanks for sharing this with me, Galan.\n说实话，我对冥想没那么感兴趣。但我想，现在我比以前更了解你一点了。谢谢你跟我分享这些，Galan。"

    old "Hey, Galan. Still in Grimoire?"
    new "Hey, Galan. Still in Grimoire?\n嘿，Galan。还在Grimoire？"

    old "Yes, and I suspect I'll continue to stay here. I've taken a liking to this city."
    new "Yes, and I suspect I'll continue to stay here. I've taken a liking to this city.\n是的，而且我估计会继续待下去。我已经喜欢上这座城市了。"

    old "Really? What about Grimoire is it that you like so much?"
    new "Really? What about Grimoire is it that you like so much?\n真的吗？Grimoire有什么让你这么喜欢？"

    old "It feels a bit silly for me to say this, but it's the air."
    new "It feels a bit silly for me to say this, but it's the air.\n我说出来有点傻，是空气。"

    old "It's good to be in a city that's not Hammerhands. The air feels cleaner."
    new "It's good to be in a city that's not Hammerhands. The air feels cleaner.\n能待在一座不是Hammerhands的城市真好。空气感觉更干净。"

    old "There's something nice about being able to stand outside and take deep, full breaths without filling your throat and nose with soot. It's easy to spend time in Hammerhands without realizing it, but over the months and years, the ashy dust and soot around the mountains takes its toll on your lungs."
    new "There's something nice about being able to stand outside and take deep, full breaths without filling your throat and nose with soot. It's easy to spend time in Hammerhands without realizing it, but over the months and years, the ashy dust and soot around the mountains takes its toll on your lungs.\n能站在外面，深吸几口饱满的空气，而不用让喉咙和鼻子灌满煤灰，真是件舒服的事。待在Hammerhands时，你很容易不知不觉就忘了，但经年累月下来，群山间那灰扑扑的尘土和煤灰会一点点侵蚀你的肺。"

    old "Every time you cough up that soot, it takes something out of you. It scratches your throat. Spend enough years scratching your throat like that, and soon you start coughing up blood like it's a regular thing. That, or your throat gets calloused and hard."
    new "Every time you cough up that soot, it takes something out of you. It scratches your throat. Spend enough years scratching your throat like that, and soon you start coughing up blood like it's a regular thing. That, or your throat gets calloused and hard.\n每次你咳出那些煤灰，都会损耗你。它刮着你的喉咙。像这样刮上足够多年，很快你就会开始咳血，就跟家常便饭一样。不然，你的喉咙就会变得粗糙发硬。"

    old "Have you ever wondered why every older dwarf speaks with such a deep, gruff voice? They weren't born that way. Dwarf children don't have deeper voices than human or elf children. No, it's the air in Hammerhands. Anyone who grows old in a place like that will find themselves speaking like an old, ornery dwarf."
    new "Have you ever wondered why every older dwarf speaks with such a deep, gruff voice? They weren't born that way. Dwarf children don't have deeper voices than human or elf children. No, it's the air in Hammerhands. Anyone who grows old in a place like that will find themselves speaking like an old, ornery dwarf.\n你有没有想过，为什么年长的矮人说话都那么低沉沙哑？他们天生不是这样的。矮人小孩的声音并不比人类或精灵孩子低沉。不，是Hammerhands的空气。任何在那种地方变老的人，都会发现自己说话像个又老又倔的矮人。"

    old "I don't intend to grow old in a city like Hammerhands."
    new "I don't intend to grow old in a city like Hammerhands.\n我不打算在Hammerhands这样的城市里变老。"

    old "I can understand you'd want to get away from Hammerhands, but what is it about Grimoire specifically that's caught your fancy? t I'm sure you'd find cleaner air if you headed to places nearer to the Great Forest. Or coastal cities."
    new "I can understand you'd want to get away from Hammerhands, but what is it about Grimoire specifically that's caught your fancy? t I'm sure you'd find cleaner air if you headed to places nearer to the Great Forest. Or coastal cities.\n我能理解你想离开Hammerhands，但具体是Grimoire的什么让你动心？我敢肯定，如果你往大森林附近的地方去，或者去沿海城市，能找到更干净的空气。"

    old "I've found that I like living in cities. The hustle and bustle...living out on the frontier can get quite lonely, as I've learned. I want to be woken up in the morning by the sound of people in the street pushing their cards and carrying about their business."
    new "I've found that I like living in cities. The hustle and bustle...living out on the frontier can get quite lonely, as I've learned. I want to be woken up in the morning by the sound of people in the street pushing their cards and carrying about their business.\n我发现我喜欢住在城市里。车水马龙、熙熙攘攘……在边境上生活其实相当孤单，这一点我是领教过的。我想在清晨被街上人们推着车、忙着自己营生的声音吵醒。"

    old "As for the coast, something in the ocean breeze doesn't sit well with me. Soot-filled air is bad, and I'm not sure that salty air is much better. It makes me fill nauseous. I've endured it on more than one occasion, but I wouldn't want to live in a place like that."
    new "As for the coast, something in the ocean breeze doesn't sit well with me. Soot-filled air is bad, and I'm not sure that salty air is much better. It makes me fill nauseous. I've endured it on more than one occasion, but I wouldn't want to live in a place like that.\n至于海边，海风里有种东西让我不太舒服。充满煤灰的空气不好，可我也不确定咸空气能好到哪儿去。它让我觉得恶心。我不止一次忍受过，但我不想住在那种地方。"

    old "So, you're going to make Grimoire your new home?"
    new "So, you're going to make Grimoire your new home?\n所以，你打算把Grimoire当成新家？"

    old "Grimoire, Horus, maybe a place like Triberg. I'm not that particular. But some place in the human empire, I reckon. And I'm already in Grimoire. I know I might seem a bit out of place in a city like this, but I think it suits me."
    new "Grimoire, Horus, maybe a place like Triberg. I'm not that particular. But some place in the human empire, I reckon. And I'm already in Grimoire. I know I might seem a bit out of place in a city like this, but I think it suits me.\nGrimoire、Horus，也许还有Triberg这样的地方。我不是那么挑剔。不过我想，总归是人类帝国的某个地方。而且我已经在Grimoire了。我知道自己在这座城市里可能显得有点格格不入，但我觉得它很适合我。"

    old "You don't really strike me as the type of dwarf to settle down."
    new "You don't really strike me as the type of dwarf to settle down.\n你可不像是那种会安顿下来的矮人。"

    old "I know what you mean. I feel like you and I are somehow kindred spirits."
    new "I know what you mean. I feel like you and I are somehow kindred spirits.\n我明白你的意思。我觉得你我某种程度上是同类人。"

    old "Even when we were in Hammerhands, you struck me as unusual. Just something in the way that you walked and talked made you seem more worldly than most dwarves."
    new "Even when we were in Hammerhands, you struck me as unusual. Just something in the way that you walked and talked made you seem more worldly than most dwarves.\n即使在Hammerhands时，你也让我觉得不同寻常。光是你的走路和谈吐，就让你显得比大多数矮人都更见多识广。"

    old "When we first met in Hammerhands, I wondered, what could someone like you be doing in a city like that? It was obvious that you were a traveler of some sort."
    new "When we first met in Hammerhands, I wondered, what could someone like you be doing in a city like that? It was obvious that you were a traveler of some sort.\n我们第一次在Hammerhands见面时，我就在想，像你这样的人待在那样的城市里做什么？很明显，你是某种旅行者。"

    old "I've always thought that being a traveler was part of my identity. Even before I ventured outside of Hammerhands for the first time, I felt like it was my destiny to wander the earth. But now, I wonder if that compulsion to travel wasn't something else."
    new "I've always thought that being a traveler was part of my identity. Even before I ventured outside of Hammerhands for the first time, I felt like it was my destiny to wander the earth. But now, I wonder if that compulsion to travel wasn't something else.\n我一直觉得，做旅行者是我身份的一部分。即便是在我第一次踏出Hammerhands之前，我就觉得漫游大地是我的宿命。但现在，我有点怀疑，那股想旅行的冲动，会不会其实是别的东西。"

    old "Maybe I was just discontent with my life, and I thought that if I changed scenery, I might happen into a life that I could be happy with."
    new "Maybe I was just discontent with my life, and I thought that if I changed scenery, I might happen into a life that I could be happy with.\n也许我只是对生活不满，以为换个环境，就能撞上一种能让我幸福的生活。"

    old "I traveled and traveled, spending time in different cities and different places. The familiarity of Hammerhands kept drawing me back, and I tried to make life work there, but I always felt that happiness was just over the horizon. Until now."
    new "I traveled and traveled, spending time in different cities and different places. The familiarity of Hammerhands kept drawing me back, and I tried to make life work there, but I always felt that happiness was just over the horizon. Until now.\n我不停地旅行，在不同的城市、不同的地方待过。对Hammerhands的熟悉总把我往回拽，我也试着在那儿把日子过下去，却总觉得幸福就在地平线那头，触不可及。直到现在。"

    old "[protag], for the first time in my life...I feel a sense of purpose. I feel like I'm doing the right thing in my life."
    new "[protag], for the first time in my life...I feel a sense of purpose. I feel like I'm doing the right thing in my life.\n[protag]，这是我一生中第一次……我感到一种使命感。我觉得自己正在做人生中正确的事。"

    old "Grimoire has been good to you?"
    new "Grimoire has been good to you?\nGrimoire待你不薄吧？"

    old "That's what I'm unsure of. Maybe it's Grimoire. But maybe it's our mission. The business with N'Mar, I mean."
    new "That's what I'm unsure of. Maybe it's Grimoire. But maybe it's our mission. The business with N'Mar, I mean.\n这正是我不确定的。也许是Grimoire。但也许是我们这场任务。我是说N'Mar这档子事。"

    old "I find myself wondering if I'll still have this same sense of purpose once we've accomplished our mission. Will I still find living in Grimoire just as fulfilling then as I do now?"
    new "I find myself wondering if I'll still have this same sense of purpose once we've accomplished our mission. Will I still find living in Grimoire just as fulfilling then as I do now?\n我不由得想，等我们完成任务后，我是否还会有这同样的使命感。到那时，住在Grimoire会不会还像现在这样让我感到充实？"

    old "Anyway, I feel like I've rambled for long enough. Thanks for hearing me out, [protag]."
    new "Anyway, I feel like I've rambled for long enough. Thanks for hearing me out, [protag].\n算了，我啰嗦得够久了。谢谢你听我讲完，[protag]。"

    old "Hey, Galan."
    new "Hey, Galan.\n嘿，Galan。"

    old "Ah, hello, [protag]. It's good to see you."
    new "Ah, hello, [protag]. It's good to see you.\n啊，你好，[protag]。见到你真好。"

    old "Galan, I hope you don't mind if I ask, but...what's it like, living in Grimoire?"
    new "Galan, I hope you don't mind if I ask, but...what's it like, living in Grimoire?\nGalan，希望你不介意我问一下，不过……住在Grimoire是什么感觉？"

    old "That's a very broad question. Did you want to ask me about some specific part of Grimoire living?"
    new "That's a very broad question. Did you want to ask me about some specific part of Grimoire living?\n这问题太宽泛了。你是想问Grimoire生活里某个具体的方面吗？"

    old "Well, there aren't very many dwarves in Grimoire. That makes you a bit..."
    new "Well, there aren't very many dwarves in Grimoire. That makes you a bit...\n嗯，Grimoire里矮人不多。这让你有点……"

    old "Unusual?"
    new "Unusual?\n与众不同？"

    old "Yes, that's one way to put it."
    new "Yes, that's one way to put it.\n对，可以这么说。"

    old "[protag], I've always felt a bit unusual. Even when I lived in Hammerhands, I marched to the beat of a different drum. As a dwarf, I may have looked a bit more 'normal' in a city of dwarves, but I've always felt like an outsider. In that sense, being in Grimoire isn't too much of a change of pace."
    new "[protag], I've always felt a bit unusual. Even when I lived in Hammerhands, I marched to the beat of a different drum. As a dwarf, I may have looked a bit more 'normal' in a city of dwarves, but I've always felt like an outsider. In that sense, being in Grimoire isn't too much of a change of pace.\n[protag]，我一直都觉得自己有点与众不同。即便住在Hammerhands，我也是踩着另一种节拍走路的。作为矮人，在满城矮人的地方，我看起来也许更“正常”些，但我始终觉得自己像个外人。从这个意义上说，待在Grimoire也不算多大的改变。"

    old "But you did have friends in Hammerhands, didn't you?"
    new "But you did have friends in Hammerhands, didn't you?\n但你在Hammerhands确实有朋友，不是吗？"

    old "Yes, I had friends in Hammerhands, and I've managed to make some friends in Grimoire as well. But in both cities, the friends I've made tend to be from the fringes, the dregs of society. That seems to be where I fit best."
    new "Yes, I had friends in Hammerhands, and I've managed to make some friends in Grimoire as well. But in both cities, the friends I've made tend to be from the fringes, the dregs of society. That seems to be where I fit best.\n是的，我在Hammerhands有朋友，在Grimoire也交到了一些。不过在这两座城市里，我交到的朋友往往来自边缘，是社会的底层渣滓。那似乎就是我最合得来的地方。"

    old "Have I ever met any of your friends?"
    new "Have I ever met any of your friends?\n我见过你那些朋友吗？"

    old "Probably not. They are, after all, the dregs. The kind of people who see very little daylight, who spend their days sleeping and their nights toiling, hidden from the public eye."
    new "Probably not. They are, after all, the dregs. The kind of people who see very little daylight, who spend their days sleeping and their nights toiling, hidden from the public eye.\n大概没有。毕竟他们是底层。那种很少见天日的人，白天睡觉，夜里劳作，避开公众视线。"

    old "Galan, you're not...getting into any trouble, are you?"
    new "Galan, you're not...getting into any trouble, are you?\nGalan，你该不会……惹上什么麻烦了吧？"

    old "No, no. I don't want you to get the wrong idea. Let me explain. One of the best friends I've made since coming to Grimoire, his name is Kav. He's one quarter elf."
    new "No, no. I don't want you to get the wrong idea. Let me explain. One of the best friends I've made since coming to Grimoire, his name is Kav. He's one quarter elf.\n不，不。我不想让你误会。让我解释一下。我来到Grimoire后交到的最好的朋友之一，他叫Kav。他有四分之一的精灵血统。"

    old "Half a half elf?"
    new "Half a half elf?\n半个半精灵？"

    old "Yes, that's exactly how he describes himself, in fact. Anyway, Kav's job is going around after dark and shoveling shit."
    new "Yes, that's exactly how he describes himself, in fact. Anyway, Kav's job is going around after dark and shoveling shit.\n对，事实上他正是这么形容自己的。总之，Kav的工作是在天黑后四处转悠，铲粪。"

    old "That's...a job?"
    new "That's...a job?\n那……算一份工作吗？"

    old "[protag], look at the streets. Lots of people transport their goods around the city using horse-drawn cards. Lots of horses means lots of horse shit. Someone has to scoop it up."
    new "[protag], look at the streets. Lots of people transport their goods around the city using horse-drawn cards. Lots of horses means lots of horse shit. Someone has to scoop it up.\n[protag]，看看这些街道。很多人用马拉的车在城里运送货物。马多就意味着马粪多。总得有人去铲起来。"

    old "I guess you're right. I never really thought about it."
    new "I guess you're right. I never really thought about it.\n我想你说得对。我还真没想过这个。"

    old "Anyway, that's what I mean when I talk about the 'dregs.' People who do work that needs to get done, but don't do jobs that most people would be proud to have."
    new "Anyway, that's what I mean when I talk about the 'dregs.' People who do work that needs to get done, but don't do jobs that most people would be proud to have.\n总之，这就是我说“底层”的意思。他们干的是必须有人干的活，但不是大多数人引以为傲的差事。"

    old "That's...kind of unfortunate. Kav's profession, I mean."
    new "That's...kind of unfortunate. Kav's profession, I mean.\n那……有点不幸。我是说Kav的职业。"

    old "Why is it unfortunate? Shoveling shit might sound miserable to you, but to Kav, it's a living. He doesn't have a sense of smell, you see, and he's more than happy to clean up after other people's horses."
    new "Why is it unfortunate? Shoveling shit might sound miserable to you, but to Kav, it's a living. He doesn't have a sense of smell, you see, and he's more than happy to clean up after other people's horses.\n为什么不幸？铲粪对你来说可能听上去很惨，但对Kav来说，那是生计。你瞧，他没有嗅觉，而且很乐意跟在别人的马后头清理。"

    old "He's paid a fair wage for the work he does, and at the end of his work day, he can wipe his brow and feel like he's performed a valuable service for the city. He knows how to drink and be merry when he's not working."
    new "He's paid a fair wage for the work he does, and at the end of his work day, he can wipe his brow and feel like he's performed a valuable service for the city. He knows how to drink and be merry when he's not working.\n他干活拿的是公平的工钱，一天工作结束时，他可以擦擦额头，觉得自己为这座城市做了有价值的服务。不工作的时候，他也懂得喝酒寻乐。"

    old "He's recently found a girl likes him well enough that he'll probably marry her some day, and odds are, he'll grow old in this city having enjoyed most of his life."
    new "He's recently found a girl likes him well enough that he'll probably marry her some day, and odds are, he'll grow old in this city having enjoyed most of his life.\n他最近找到一个挺喜欢他的姑娘，说不定哪天就会娶她。而且不出意外的话，他会在这座城市里安享晚年，好好享受大半辈子的人生。"

    old "Is that the kind of life you see for yourself?"
    new "Is that the kind of life you see for yourself?\n这是你为自己设想的那种生活吗？"

    old "Perhaps it is. You know, I never really thought about it. Maybe I thought that I didn't deserve happiness. But living in Grimoire...it's pleasant."
    new "Perhaps it is. You know, I never really thought about it. Maybe I thought that I didn't deserve happiness. But living in Grimoire...it's pleasant.\n也许是。你知道，我从没真正想过这个。也许我觉得自己不配得到幸福。但住在Grimoire……很惬意。"

    old "Right now I'm a bit preoccupied with, you know, Grimoire's present peril. Vampires, and ghouls, and their ilk. I can't very well think of retiring in Grimoire when the city itself is in danger. But one day...perhaps I'll develop a tolerance for the smell of shit, and grab a shovel and join Kav in the streets."
    new "Right now I'm a bit preoccupied with, you know, Grimoire's present peril. Vampires, and ghouls, and their ilk. I can't very well think of retiring in Grimoire when the city itself is in danger. But one day...perhaps I'll develop a tolerance for the smell of shit, and grab a shovel and join Kav in the streets.\n眼下我有点心神不宁，你知道的，Grimoire正面临危险。吸血鬼、食尸鬼，还有它们那一类东西。当这座城市自身都危在旦夕时，我没法好好考虑在Grimoire养老。但总有一天……也许我会习惯粪臭，抄起一把铲子，跟Kav一起上街去。"

    old "Are you serious about that?"
    new "Are you serious about that?\n你这话是认真的吗？"

    old "Galan smiles and shrugs."
    new "Galan smiles and shrugs.\nGalan笑着耸了耸肩。"

    old "Who knows? Years ago, that kind of thinking would have been absurd to me. I wanted excitement. I wanted to fight. But maybe...maybe one day I'll grow out of this life."
    new "Who knows? Years ago, that kind of thinking would have been absurd to me. I wanted excitement. I wanted to fight. But maybe...maybe one day I'll grow out of this life.\n谁知道呢？几年前，那种想法对我来说很荒谬。我想要刺激。我想要战斗。但也许……也许有一天我会从这种生活里走出来。"

    old "Swinging a hammer feels right. But eventually my bones will grow too brittle to hold up in combat, and then what?"
    new "Swinging a hammer feels right. But eventually my bones will grow too brittle to hold up in combat, and then what?\n挥锤子的感觉才对味。但终有一天，我的骨头会脆得撑不住战斗，到那时又怎么办？"

    old "When I was young, the idea frightened me. Part of me actually hoped that I would die in combat, so that I would never have to live to see the day that I was too old to fight."
    new "When I was young, the idea frightened me. Part of me actually hoped that I would die in combat, so that I would never have to live to see the day that I was too old to fight.\n年轻时，这个念头吓坏了我。我甚至有点希望自己战死沙场，那样就永远不用活到自己老得打不动的那一天。"

    old "But if I will eventually become a gray-haired elderly dwarf, what's the harm in getting a head start on that?"
    new "But if I will eventually become a gray-haired elderly dwarf, what's the harm in getting a head start on that?\n但如果我终究会变成一个白发苍苍的老矮人，提前朝那一步走走又有什么坏处？"

    old "Wow, you really are serious about this."
    new "Wow, you really are serious about this.\n哇，你还真是认真的。"

    old "Yes, I am. Though, knowing me, I'll probably spend the next years talking about how much I hate fighting while continuing to fight. Or maybe I'll retire as soon as this business with N'Mar is done and over with."
    new "Yes, I am. Though, knowing me, I'll probably spend the next years talking about how much I hate fighting while continuing to fight. Or maybe I'll retire as soon as this business with N'Mar is done and over with.\n是的。不过，以我对我自己的了解，接下来几年我大概还会一边继续打，一边抱怨自己有多讨厌打架。又或者，等N'Mar这档子事一了结，我就退休。"

    old "I've never really been good at doing things in moderation."
    new "I've never really been good at doing things in moderation.\n我从来不太擅长做事有节制。"

    old "What do you think I should do when we're done working together, [protag]? Should I keep fighting, or look for some other line of work?"
    new "What do you think I should do when we're done working together, [protag]? Should I keep fighting, or look for some other line of work?\n你觉得等我们一起干完后，我该做什么，[protag]？是继续战斗，还是找点别的营生？"

    old "Galan, I know talent when I see it. And you've got a talent for fighting."
    new "Galan, I know talent when I see it. And you've got a talent for fighting.\nGalan，我看人一向准。你有战斗的天赋。"

    old "There's other things you could do. A man with your brawn, you could just as easily work a job as a stone mason, or doing heavy lifting in a construction job. But that's not what you want to do, is it?"
    new "There's other things you could do. A man with your brawn, you could just as easily work a job as a stone mason, or doing heavy lifting in a construction job. But that's not what you want to do, is it?\n你还能做别的。以你这副身板，去当个石匠，或者去建筑工地干重活，都绰绰有余。但那不是你想做的，对吧？"

    old "No, you've got a fire in your eyes. A fire that says, 'I want to fight.' I think you see it, too. Maybe that scares you. After all, if everyone was a fighter, we'd have a very unruly society."
    new "No, you've got a fire in your eyes. A fire that says, 'I want to fight.' I think you see it, too. Maybe that scares you. After all, if everyone was a fighter, we'd have a very unruly society.\n不，你眼里有团火。一团说着“我想战斗”的火。我想你自己也看得到。也许这让你害怕。毕竟，要是人人都当战士，社会可就乱套了。"

    old "But we'll always have need for fighters. This world is filled with horrors and threats. Today, it's vampires and ghouls. Next year, it may be an invading army from an enemy nation. Sometimes, it's as simple as a mugger who preys on the weak, stealing from them."
    new "But we'll always have need for fighters. This world is filled with horrors and threats. Today, it's vampires and ghouls. Next year, it may be an invading army from an enemy nation. Sometimes, it's as simple as a mugger who preys on the weak, stealing from them.\n但世界永远需要战士。这世上充满了恐怖和威胁。今天是吸血鬼和食尸鬼。明年，也许是敌国来犯的军队。有时候，事情简单到就是一个专门欺负弱小的劫匪，从他们手里抢东西。"

    old "We need people who can protect us from the dangers of the world. We need people like you."
    new "We need people who can protect us from the dangers of the world. We need people like you.\n我们需要能保护大家、抵御世间危险的人。我们需要你这样的人。"

    old "You are your own man. You make your own decisions. But you have a gift. And I wouldn't want to see it go to waste."
    new "You are your own man. You make your own decisions. But you have a gift. And I wouldn't want to see it go to waste.\n你是你自己的主人。你自己拿主意。但你有天赋。我可不想看到它被白白浪费。"

    old "There's more to life than fighting, Galan. I think that you'll find something else to do."
    new "There's more to life than fighting, Galan. I think that you'll find something else to do.\n人生不只是战斗，Galan。我想你会找到别的事情做的。"

    old "After all, I'm not exactly a fighter either."
    new "After all, I'm not exactly a fighter either.\n毕竟，我也算不上真正的战士。"

    old "That's funny to hear, coming from someone who's building an army."
    new "That's funny to hear, coming from someone who's building an army.\n这话从一个正在组建军队的人嘴里说出来，可真有意思。"

    old "Before I got wrapped up in this business, I was a [i]. After this is all done and over with, I may very well go back to doing that."
    new "Before I got wrapped up in this business, I was a [i]. After this is all done and over with, I may very well go back to doing that.\n在我卷进这档子事之前，我是个[i]。等这一切了结之后，我很可能又会回去干那个。"

    old "But what about me?"
    new "But what about me?\n那我呢？"

    old "That's for you to decide. You've got time to figure it out, right? And you don't have to decide right away. You don't have to one day declare, 'I want to be a farmer,' and then commit to living on a farm for the rest of your life."
    new "That's for you to decide. You've got time to figure it out, right? And you don't have to decide right away. You don't have to one day declare, 'I want to be a farmer,' and then commit to living on a farm for the rest of your life.\n那要由你自己决定。你有时间慢慢想，对吧？而且你也不必马上决定。你不用某天宣布“我想当农民”，然后就发誓余生都守着农场过活。"

    old "I say, mull it over. You fight, but I think there may be more enjoyable and more fulfilling ways to spend your life."
    new "I say, mull it over. You fight, but I think there may be more enjoyable and more fulfilling ways to spend your life.\n要我说，你就慢慢琢磨。你是会战斗，但我觉得，也许还有更愉快、更充实的方式度过你的人生。"

    old "I guess so. Well, thanks, [protag]. I hope my uncertainty about the future doesn't make me appear irresolute when I accompany you on the battlefield. Right now I am focused on assisting you in your mission."
    new "I guess so. Well, thanks, [protag]. I hope my uncertainty about the future doesn't make me appear irresolute when I accompany you on the battlefield. Right now I am focused on assisting you in your mission.\n我想也是。那，谢谢了，[protag]。希望我对未来的犹疑，不会让我在战场上陪着你时显得不坚定。眼下我专心协助你完成使命。"

    old "But the days are long, and they've given me a lot of time to contemplate what lies ahead for me."
    new "But the days are long, and they've given me a lot of time to contemplate what lies ahead for me.\n但日子很长，这也给了我很多时间去思考前面等待我的路。"

    old "Of course, Galan. You are your own person. You've pledged your loyalty to me, but that doesn't mean that you're accountable to me for every waking moment of your day. It's comforting to know that when I'll need you, you'll be at my side."
    new "Of course, Galan. You are your own person. You've pledged your loyalty to me, but that doesn't mean that you're accountable to me for every waking moment of your day. It's comforting to know that when I'll need you, you'll be at my side.\n当然，Galan。你是你自己的主人。你向我宣誓效忠，但这并不意味着你醒着的每一刻都要对我负责。知道在我需要你时，你会守在我身边，这让我很安心。"

    old "Of course. It's been a pleasure, [protag]. And it will continue to be my pleasure to serve you for as long as needed to achieve our goals."
    new "Of course. It's been a pleasure, [protag]. And it will continue to be my pleasure to serve you for as long as needed to achieve our goals.\n当然。这是我的荣幸，[protag]。为了达成我们的目标，我会继续为你效力，多久都行。"

    old "I walk up to Galan. He's sitting outside the city gates, sitting on the ground with both of his hands wrapped around the handle of his hammer."
    new "I walk up to Galan. He's sitting outside the city gates, sitting on the ground with both of his hands wrapped around the handle of his hammer.\n我走到Galan身边。他坐在城门外，坐在地上，双手都握在锤柄上。"

    old "Galan looks up at me, blinking."
    new "Galan looks up at me, blinking.\nGalan抬头看我，眨了眨眼。"

    old "Ah, sorry. Did I interrupt something?"
    new "Ah, sorry. Did I interrupt something?\n啊，抱歉。我打扰到你了吗？"

    old "I was meditating."
    new "I was meditating.\n我刚才在冥想。"

    old "Sorry, I didn't realize. I saw you holding your weapon and thought you were repairing it or something."
    new "Sorry, I didn't realize. I saw you holding your weapon and thought you were repairing it or something.\n对不起，我没注意到。我看到你握着武器，还以为你在修理它之类的。"

    old "If you don't mind my asking, why do you have your hammer out while meditating?"
    new "If you don't mind my asking, why do you have your hammer out while meditating?\n如果你不介意我问一句，为什么冥想时要把锤子拿出来？"

    old "Ah, I can understand your confusion. The truth is, I've been thinking of ways to apply my meditation techniques more directly."
    new "Ah, I can understand your confusion. The truth is, I've been thinking of ways to apply my meditation techniques more directly.\n啊，我能理解你的疑惑。其实，我一直在琢磨，怎么才能更直接地运用我的冥想技巧。"

    old "Fundamentally, meditation is about mindfulness. Being in the present, and fully aware of the space around you. That includes physical sensations, even things as simple as the feel of a chair underneath you as you sit, or the sensation of your own weight pressing down on your heels as you stand."
    new "Fundamentally, meditation is about mindfulness. Being in the present, and fully aware of the space around you. That includes physical sensations, even things as simple as the feel of a chair underneath you as you sit, or the sensation of your own weight pressing down on your heels as you stand.\n从根本上说，冥想关乎正念。活在当下，充分感知你周围的空间。这包括身体的感受，哪怕简单到你坐下时身下椅子的触感，或者站立时自己身体的重量压在脚跟上的感觉。"

    old "That sounds...really intense."
    new "That sounds...really intense.\n听起来……真的很专注。"

    old "In my recent meditations, I've been focusing on the sensation of this handle. Just forcing myself to be present-minded as I hold this hammer has made me more comfortable handling it."
    new "In my recent meditations, I've been focusing on the sensation of this handle. Just forcing myself to be present-minded as I hold this hammer has made me more comfortable handling it.\n最近几次冥想，我一直在专注于这锤柄的触感。光是逼自己在握锤时保持专注当下，就已经让我握锤时更顺手了。"

    old "Are you sure? The idea that you could get better at wielding a hammer just from mental exercise seems a bit far-fetched."
    new "Are you sure? The idea that you could get better at wielding a hammer just from mental exercise seems a bit far-fetched.\n你确定吗？光靠精神练习就能让挥锤更厉害，这说法听起来有点牵强。"

    old "Oh, I don't mean to exaggerate the significance of this meditation practice. It's not as if I suddenly became better at swinging a hammer just because I concentrated a lot on the feel of the grip. But it has made me more consistent."
    new "Oh, I don't mean to exaggerate the significance of this meditation practice. It's not as if I suddenly became better at swinging a hammer just because I concentrated a lot on the feel of the grip. But it has made me more consistent.\n哦，我并不是想夸大这种冥想练习的作用。我并不是说，只要把注意力集中到握柄的手感上，我就突然更会挥锤了。但它让我更稳定了。"

    old "What's that supposed to mean?"
    new "What's that supposed to mean?\n这话什么意思？"

    old "Have you ever had that feeling in battle, where you just feel like you are in the zone? There are moments where you just feel supreme clarity, when you feel mentally energized, almost like you're in a trance that is letting you do all the things you want to do."
    new "Have you ever had that feeling in battle, where you just feel like you are in the zone? There are moments where you just feel supreme clarity, when you feel mentally energized, almost like you're in a trance that is letting you do all the things you want to do.\n你在战斗中有没有过那种感觉，就是觉得自己进入了状态？有些时刻，你会感到格外清明，精神充沛，几乎像进入了某种出神的状态，让你想做什么都能做到。"

    old "No doubts in your mind, no misgivings, just pure focus on the exact thing that you are doing, whether that's swinging a weapon or parrying a blow. Do you know what I mean?"
    new "No doubts in your mind, no misgivings, just pure focus on the exact thing that you are doing, whether that's swinging a weapon or parrying a blow. Do you know what I mean?\n心里没有疑虑，没有杂念，只是纯粹地专注于你正在做的那件事，无论是挥动武器还是格挡一击。你懂我的意思吗？"

    old "Yes. It's hard to describe exactly what it is, but there are some days when I just feel 'on.' Just like there are some days when I feel a bit 'off.'"
    new "Yes. It's hard to describe exactly what it is, but there are some days when I just feel 'on.' Just like there are some days when I feel a bit 'off.'\n懂。那种感觉很难准确形容，但有些日子我就是觉得“在状态”。就像有些日子会有点“不在状态”一样。"

    old "Exactly. For me, being present-minded makes me feel like I am always 'on' when I pick up this hammer. That focus isn't going to magically allow me to perform feats that I wouldn't otherwise be capable of. But it does feel like I can fight to my full potential all of the time."
    new "Exactly. For me, being present-minded makes me feel like I am always 'on' when I pick up this hammer. That focus isn't going to magically allow me to perform feats that I wouldn't otherwise be capable of. But it does feel like I can fight to my full potential all of the time.\n没错。对我来说，保持专注当下，让我在拿起这把锤子时，总觉得自己时刻“在状态”。这种专注不会神奇地让我做到本做不到的事。但它确实让我觉得，自己随时都能发挥出全部实力。"

    old "I'm just a little bit better at handling this hammer than I was before. But when you're fighting for your life, sometimes being just a little bit better can make all the difference."
    new "I'm just a little bit better at handling this hammer than I was before. But when you're fighting for your life, sometimes being just a little bit better can make all the difference.\n我握这把锤子只是比以前稍微顺手了一点点。但当你为活命而战时，有时仅仅是好上那么一点点，就能改变一切。"

    old "That sounds great, Galan. I'm glad that your meditative practice seems to be paying off for you."
    new "That sounds great, Galan. I'm glad that your meditative practice seems to be paying off for you.\n听起来很棒，Galan。很高兴你的冥想练习似乎有了回报。"

    old "I walk up to Galan. He's sitting outside the city gates, perched on a rock with his legs folded in the lotus position."
    new "I walk up to Galan. He's sitting outside the city gates, perched on a rock with his legs folded in the lotus position.\n我走到Galan身边。他坐在城门外，盘腿坐在一块石头上，摆着莲花坐姿。"

    old "I give him a wave before I realize that his eyes are closed. I walk up to him and watch him for a moment as he silently meditates."
    new "I give him a wave before I realize that his eyes are closed. I walk up to him and watch him for a moment as he silently meditates.\n我朝他挥了挥手，才意识到他闭着眼睛。我走到他跟前，静静看他冥想了一会儿。"

    old "Galan speaks with his eyes still closed."
    new "Galan speaks with his eyes still closed.\nGalan眼睛仍闭着，开了口。"

    old "Whoa. How did you know it was me?"
    new "Whoa. How did you know it was me?\n嚯。你怎么知道是我？"

    old "The rhythm of your breathing, the pace of your gait as you approached. That, and the fact that you decided to stand there watching me."
    new "The rhythm of your breathing, the pace of your gait as you approached. That, and the fact that you decided to stand there watching me.\n你呼吸的节奏，你走近时步子的快慢。再加上你决定站在这儿看我的这个事实。"

    old "I assumed you were someone I knew, and the number of people who come to visit me while I meditate is actually quite small. So really, recognizing you without looking isn't as impressive as it looks."
    new "I assumed you were someone I knew, and the number of people who come to visit me while I meditate is actually quite small. So really, recognizing you without looking isn't as impressive as it looks.\n我猜你是我认识的人，而在我冥想时会来看我的人其实很少。所以，不睁眼就认出你，其实没看上去那么厉害。"

    old "It's still impressive. I don't think many people could do the same thing."
    new "It's still impressive. I don't think many people could do the same thing.\n还是很厉害。我觉得没多少人能做到。"

    old "I've found that being present-minded has allowed me to pick up small details that I might otherwise miss. It makes me just a little bit more reactive to the things around me."
    new "I've found that being present-minded has allowed me to pick up small details that I might otherwise miss. It makes me just a little bit more reactive to the things around me.\n我发现，保持专注当下，能让我捕捉到一些本可能错过的小细节。这让我对周围的事物反应稍微快了一点。"

    old "You've got better reflexes?"
    new "You've got better reflexes?\n你的反应变快了？"

    old "That would be over-stating it, I think. I've noticed it in combat, too. Being just a little bit more reactive hasn't allowed me to dodge blows. But if I can recognize a blow is coming just a fraction of a second before it hits me, I can brace for it and lessen the impact."
    new "That would be over-stating it, I think. I've noticed it in combat, too. Being just a little bit more reactive hasn't allowed me to dodge blows. But if I can recognize a blow is coming just a fraction of a second before it hits me, I can brace for it and lessen the impact.\n我觉得这么说有点夸张了。我在战斗中也注意到了。反应稍微快一点，并没有让我躲开攻击。但如果我能在攻击打中我之前提早哪怕零点几秒察觉，我就能绷紧身体，减轻冲击。"

    old "Sort of like a boxer, who learns how to roll with his opponent's punches."
    new "Sort of like a boxer, who learns how to roll with his opponent's punches.\n有点像拳击手，学着顺着对手的拳头卸力。"

    old "Yes, it's quite similar to that. I find myself flinching and reacting in ways that allow me to take just a little bit less damage whenever I absorb a blow."
    new "Yes, it's quite similar to that. I find myself flinching and reacting in ways that allow me to take just a little bit less damage whenever I absorb a blow.\n对，跟那很像。我发现自己会本能地闪避、做出反应，让我在挨打时能少受那么一点点伤害。"

    old "You say 'just a little bit.' But when it comes to a crisis situation, sometimes just a little bit can make all the difference."
    new "You say 'just a little bit.' But when it comes to a crisis situation, sometimes just a little bit can make all the difference.\n你总说“一点点”。但到了危急关头，有时仅仅是一点点，就能改变一切。"

    old "I hope that we triumph over our foes by more than just the skin of our teeth. But yes, in a dire situation, it could mean the difference between living and dying."
    new "I hope that we triumph over our foes by more than just the skin of our teeth. But yes, in a dire situation, it could mean the difference between living and dying.\n我希望我们战胜敌人，靠的不只是险胜。但没错，在绝境中，这可能意味着生与死的差别。"

    old "All this, from your meditation practice."
    new "All this, from your meditation practice.\n这一切，都来自你的冥想练习。"

    old "Yes. Training myself to be mindful has had more tangible benefits in my life, though."
    new "Yes. Training myself to be mindful has had more tangible benefits in my life, though.\n是的。不过，训练自己保持正念，给我生活带来的好处更实在。"

    old "I feel a greater sense of serenity and contentment. I used to find that even small things could trigger my anger. Someone bumping into me on the street, or someone not quite hearing me correctly when I spoke to them. My temper was a problem."
    new "I feel a greater sense of serenity and contentment. I used to find that even small things could trigger my anger. Someone bumping into me on the street, or someone not quite hearing me correctly when I spoke to them. My temper was a problem.\n我感到一种更强烈的平静与满足。过去我发现，哪怕一点小事也能惹火我。有人在街上撞到我，或者有人跟我说话时没听清我的话。我的脾气是个问题。"

    old "Now, I find it just easier to accept the things that happen to me. I find myself observing and accepting the things around, me rather than judging them."
    new "Now, I find it just easier to accept the things that happen to me. I find myself observing and accepting the things around, me rather than judging them.\n现在，我觉得接受发生在我身上的事更容易了。我发现自己只是在观察、接受周遭的一切，而不是去评判它们。"

    old "I'm glad that you've found peace, Galan. I hope that calling you into combat doesn't undermine that."
    new "I'm glad that you've found peace, Galan. I hope that calling you into combat doesn't undermine that.\n很高兴你找到了内心的平静，Galan。希望我召你上战场不会破坏它。"

    old "Don't worry, [protag]. When it comes to being violent and frenzied, I'm more than capable of doing damage with this hammer if the situation requires it. But it only happens when I want it to."
    new "Don't worry, [protag]. When it comes to being violent and frenzied, I'm more than capable of doing damage with this hammer if the situation requires it. But it only happens when I want it to.\n别担心，[protag]。到了需要暴力狂怒的时候，只要情况需要，我完全有能力用这把锤子造成杀伤。但那只会在我愿意的时候发生。"

    old "When you need a crazed dwarf to start wailing on a bunch of zombies, I'll be there. But now, I'm in control of when it happens."
    new "When you need a crazed dwarf to start wailing on a bunch of zombies, I'll be there. But now, I'm in control of when it happens.\n当你需要一个发狂的矮人去痛揍一群僵尸时，我会到场。但现在，什么时候发作由我自己掌控。"

    old "I've been thinking of what I'll do when this whole business with N'Mar is over and done with."
    new "I've been thinking of what I'll do when this whole business with N'Mar is over and done with.\n我一直在想，等N'Mar这整档子事结束之后，我该做什么。"

    old "Already decided on a new career?"
    new "Already decided on a new career?\n已经决定好新职业了？"

    old "I've been thinking about the monk that introduced me to meditative practice in the first place. I've learned to achieve a better state of present-mindedness, but truth be told, I think that I know very little when it comes to meditative practice."
    new "I've been thinking about the monk that introduced me to meditative practice in the first place. I've learned to achieve a better state of present-mindedness, but truth be told, I think that I know very little when it comes to meditative practice.\n我一直在想最初引导我接触冥想的那位僧人。我已经学会了达到更好的专注状态，但说句实话，在冥想这门功课上，我觉得自己懂得还很少。"

    old "Furthermore, most of my meditation has been focused on being present-minded. It's an exercise in trying to take in the world around me. But there's more to this world than the things that we can see with our eyes and touch with our hands. Lately, my mind has been turning to matters of the everlasting."
    new "Furthermore, most of my meditation has been focused on being present-minded. It's an exercise in trying to take in the world around me. But there's more to this world than the things that we can see with our eyes and touch with our hands. Lately, my mind has been turning to matters of the everlasting.\n而且，我大部分冥想都专注于活在当下。这是一种尝试去感知周遭世界的练习。但这世上除了我们能用眼睛看到、用手触摸到的东西之外，还有更多。最近，我的心思渐渐转向了永恒之事。"

    old "Are you thinking of joining a monastery?"
    new "Are you thinking of joining a monastery?\n你在考虑加入修道院吗？"

    old "I've thought about it. However, joining any order of monks is a massive commitment. It's not the kind of decision I'd make lightly."
    new "I've thought about it. However, joining any order of monks is a massive commitment. It's not the kind of decision I'd make lightly.\n我想过。不过，加入任何僧团都是巨大的承诺。这不是我会草率做出的决定。"

    old "Do I really want to devote the rest of my life to that kind of practice? The idea frightens me a little."
    new "Do I really want to devote the rest of my life to that kind of practice? The idea frightens me a little.\n我真的想把余生都献给那种修行吗？这念头让我有点害怕。"

    old "And the more that I learn about such things, the more I realize that I really am content with the way my life is right now. I'm not looking to massively change who I am or what I do."
    new "And the more that I learn about such things, the more I realize that I really am content with the way my life is right now. I'm not looking to massively change who I am or what I do.\n而我越是了解这些事，就越意识到，我其实对现在的生活很满足。我并不想大幅改变我是谁、我做什么。"

    old "What I do know is that right now, my life has a purpose. And that purpose is slaying the undead."
    new "What I do know is that right now, my life has a purpose. And that purpose is slaying the undead.\n我所知道的是，眼下，我的生活有了目标。那个目标就是斩杀亡灵。"

    old "Then let's work together and make that come to fruition."
    new "Then let's work together and make that come to fruition.\n那我们就一起努力，让这个目标开花结果。"

    old "Of course, [protag]. Of course."
    new "Of course, [protag]. Of course.\n当然，[protag]。当然。"

    old "I spot Galan walking from the town gate with a folded paper in his hand."
    new "I spot Galan walking from the town gate with a folded paper in his hand.\n我看见Galan从城门走来，手里拿着一张折起来的纸。"

    old "Hey there, Galan. What are you up to?"
    new "Hey there, Galan. What are you up to?\n嘿，Galan。你在忙什么？"

    old "Ah, me? Just getting some mail."
    new "Ah, me? Just getting some mail.\n啊，我？就是去取个信。"

    old "Mail, huh? News from your friends in Hammerhands?"
    new "Mail, huh? News from your friends in Hammerhands?\n信？是Hammerhands的朋友来的消息吗？"

    old "No, actually. I've been corresponding with an order of monks."
    new "No, actually. I've been corresponding with an order of monks.\n不，其实不是。我一直在和一群僧侣通信。"

    old "Are you getting more serious about pursuing a life of religious study?"
    new "Are you getting more serious about pursuing a life of religious study?\n你是越来越认真，想要投身宗教修行了吗？"

    old "In a sense. But this order of monks is somewhat unique."
    new "In a sense. But this order of monks is somewhat unique.\n从某种意义上说，是的。但这个僧团有些特别。"

    old "What about them is unique?"
    new "What about them is unique?\n他们有什么特别的？"

    old "They're located on Mount Kronos. Are you familiar with it?"
    new "They're located on Mount Kronos. Are you familiar with it?\n他们驻扎在Mount Kronos。你熟悉那儿吗？"

    old "Mount Kronos? Yes, I've heard of it. It's out east, on the direction of Icesilia."
    new "Mount Kronos? Yes, I've heard of it. It's out east, on the direction of Icesilia.\nMount Kronos？是的，我听说过。它在东方，朝Icesilia的方向。"

    old "I can't say I'm familiar with it."
    new "I can't say I'm familiar with it.\n我对它不太熟悉。"

    old "It's east of here, on the road to Icesilia. I presume you're familiar with the history of The Old War."
    new "It's east of here, on the road to Icesilia. I presume you're familiar with the history of The Old War.\n它就在这里的东边，通往Icesilia的路上。我想你应该熟悉The Old War的历史吧。"

    old "During The Old War, many humans and elves died around Mount Kronos. The frost has preserved many of their remains through the decades. And that seems to have made the mountain a popular target for necromancers."
    new "During The Old War, many humans and elves died around Mount Kronos. The frost has preserved many of their remains through the decades. And that seems to have made the mountain a popular target for necromancers.\n在The Old War期间，无数人类和精灵在Mount Kronos周围丧生。霜雪几十年来一直保存着他们的遗骸。这似乎也使得那座山成了死灵法师们热衷的目标。"

    old "There are dark magicians trying to animate the remains of those who were killed during the war?"
    new "There are dark magicians trying to animate the remains of those who were killed during the war?\n有邪恶法师试图唤醒那些在战争中遇难者的遗骸？"

    old "That seems to be the case."
    new "That seems to be the case.\n情况似乎正是如此。"

    old "What does this have to do with the monk you've been corresponding with?"
    new "What does this have to do with the monk you've been corresponding with?\n这跟你一直在通信的那位僧人有什么关系？"

    old "The monks hail from the Order of Irijo. They occupy a temple at the top of Mount Kronos, and they've taken it upon themselves to combat the undead that walk that region."
    new "The monks hail from the Order of Irijo. They occupy a temple at the top of Mount Kronos, and they've taken it upon themselves to combat the undead that walk that region.\n那些僧人来自Order of Irijo。他们占据着Mount Kronos山顶的一座神庙，并主动承担起与那一带游荡的亡灵作战的使命。"

    old "Prayers in the morning, followed by combat in the afternoon?"
    new "Prayers in the morning, followed by combat in the afternoon?\n早上祈祷，下午接着战斗？"

    old "Yes, actually, at least when circumstances call for it. The monks have made it their mission to eradicate the undead around the mountain."
    new "Yes, actually, at least when circumstances call for it. The monks have made it their mission to eradicate the undead around the mountain.\n是的，事实上确实如此，至少在情况需要的时候。僧人们已经把消灭山周围的亡灵当作自己的使命。"

    old "Considering the number of people who were killed during that war, those monks may be there for a very, very long time."
    new "Considering the number of people who were killed during that war, those monks may be there for a very, very long time.\n考虑到那场战争中阵亡的人数，那些僧人恐怕得在那儿待上很久很久。"

    old "Yes, I imagine so. But it seems like a noble cause. And more importantly, it seems like a cause that matches my talents."
    new "Yes, I imagine so. But it seems like a noble cause. And more importantly, it seems like a cause that matches my talents.\n是的，我想也是。但这似乎是一项崇高的事业。更重要的是，这似乎是一项与我的才能相称的事业。"

    old "My focus has been on ending the undead menace in N'Mar. When we're done here, perhaps I can put those skills to use on Mount Kronos."
    new "My focus has been on ending the undead menace in N'Mar. When we're done here, perhaps I can put those skills to use on Mount Kronos.\n我关注的重点一直是终结N'Mar的亡灵之祸。等这里的事了结之后，也许我可以把那些本领用到Mount Kronos上去。"

    old "Well, you've proven yourself to be a capable fighter. I appreciate your devotion to our cause, Galan. But I'm well aware that there are other causes in this world that are just as deserving of your talents."
    new "Well, you've proven yourself to be a capable fighter. I appreciate your devotion to our cause, Galan. But I'm well aware that there are other causes in this world that are just as deserving of your talents.\n嗯，你已经证明了自己是个能干的战士。我很感激你对我们事业的奉献，Galan。但我很清楚，这世上还有其他事业，同样值得你的才能。"

    old "If your destiny is to become a monk and devote yourself to a life of eradicating another part of the world of evil, then I applaud you for recognizing that and committing yourself to it."
    new "If your destiny is to become a monk and devote yourself to a life of eradicating another part of the world of evil, then I applaud you for recognizing that and committing yourself to it.\n如果你的宿命是成为一名僧侣，投身于为世界清除另一片邪恶的人生，那我为你能认清这一点并为之献身而喝彩。"

    old "It does seem like it's my destiny to continue fighting the undead. A year from now, I may be meditating in a temple, preparing for the next appearance of the undead. But right now, I'm at your side."
    new "It does seem like it's my destiny to continue fighting the undead. A year from now, I may be meditating in a temple, preparing for the next appearance of the undead. But right now, I'm at your side.\n看起来，继续与亡灵作战确实是我的宿命。一年后，我也许会在某座神庙里冥想，为亡灵的下一次现身做准备。但现在，我守在你身边。"

    old "[protag], I must confess, when I met you, I joined your fight on a whim. I didn't know what I was getting into, but I jumped into the fray."
    new "[protag], I must confess, when I met you, I joined your fight on a whim. I didn't know what I was getting into, but I jumped into the fray.\n[protag]，我必须坦白，当初遇见你时，我是一时冲动加入了你的战斗。我不知道自己会卷进什么，但我跳进了战局。"

    old "Then, I joined your troupe of fighters, and began fighting for a greater cause. At the time, I wasn't sure what the consequences of that would be, exactly. But it seemed like the right idea at the time."
    new "Then, I joined your troupe of fighters, and began fighting for a greater cause. At the time, I wasn't sure what the consequences of that would be, exactly. But it seemed like the right idea at the time.\n后来，我加入了你的战士队伍，开始为更伟大的事业而战。当时我还不确定那会带来什么后果，确切地说。但当时看来，那似乎是个正确的决定。"

    old "My whole life has been filled with uncertainty, even as I fought side-by-side with you for the first time. But as I've spent more time with you, I find myself convinced now more than ever that joining you was the right decision."
    new "My whole life has been filled with uncertainty, even as I fought side-by-side with you for the first time. But as I've spent more time with you, I find myself convinced now more than ever that joining you was the right decision.\n我这一生充满了不确定，哪怕在我第一次与你并肩作战时也是如此。但与你相处越久，我就越确信，加入你是正确的决定。"

    old "One day, with your permission, I'd like to join the monks atop Mount Kronos in their fight against evil. But right now, you have my complete devotion. I feel like my life has gained new purpose since I joined your cause, and giving you my loyalty seems like such a small thing to offer in return."
    new "One day, with your permission, I'd like to join the monks atop Mount Kronos in their fight against evil. But right now, you have my complete devotion. I feel like my life has gained new purpose since I joined your cause, and giving you my loyalty seems like such a small thing to offer in return.\n总有一天，若你准许，我想去加入Mount Kronos山顶的那些僧人，与他们一同对抗邪恶。但现在，我全心效忠于你。我觉得自从加入你的事业以来，我的生命有了新的意义，而献上我的忠诚，作为回报实在是微不足道。"

    old "Having your loyalty is a generous reward, Galan. I won't ever take it for granted."
    new "Having your loyalty is a generous reward, Galan. I won't ever take it for granted.\n能得到你的忠诚，是一份慷慨的回报，Galan。我永远不会视为理所当然。"

    old "I stumble into Galan on Grimoire's main square."
    new "I stumble into Galan on Grimoire's main square.\n我在Grimoire的中心广场上撞见了Galan。"

    old "[protag], I just came back from the Citadel."
    new "[protag], I just came back from the Citadel.\n[protag]，我刚从Citadel回来。"

    old "The Citadel?"
    new "The Citadel?\nCitadel？"

    old "Yes. Queen Karen wanted to see me in private."
    new "Yes. Queen Karen wanted to see me in private.\n是的。Karen女王想私下见我。"

    old "Galan stays silent and grins. It's like if he's waiting for me to say something."
    new "Galan stays silent and grins. It's like if he's waiting for me to say something.\nGalan默不作声，咧嘴笑着。就好像在等我开口说点什么。"

    old "Hey, hey. When you say it like that, it sounds like you doubt I'd have anything of value to offer."
    new "Hey, hey. When you say it like that, it sounds like you doubt I'd have anything of value to offer.\n喂喂。你这么一说，搞得好像你怀疑我拿不出什么有价值的东西似的。"

    old "Sorry, Galan. You're right. There are many reasons why Karen could want to see you."
    new "Sorry, Galan. You're right. There are many reasons why Karen could want to see you.\n抱歉，Galan。你说得对。Karen想见你，可以有很多原因。"

    old "Indeed it was."
    new "Indeed it was.\n的确如此。"

    old "Galan goes silent again."
    new "Galan goes silent again.\nGalan又不说话了。"

    old "Aren't you going to ask me what was it about?"
    new "Aren't you going to ask me what was it about?\n你不想问我那是怎么回事吗？"

    old "I let out an exasperated sigh."
    new "I let out an exasperated sigh.\n我无奈地叹了口气。"

    old "I thought it was a secret meeting or something! All right, what is it that Karen wanted from you?"
    new "I thought it was a secret meeting or something! All right, what is it that Karen wanted from you?\n我还以为是秘密会面什么的呢！好了，Karen到底想从你这儿得到什么？"

    old "You see, it's about the Queen's daughter, Loren."
    new "You see, it's about the Queen's daughter, Loren.\n你瞧，是关于女王的女儿Loren。"

    old "What about her?"
    new "What about her?\n她怎么了？"

    old "Karen told me that Loren tends to be... hot tempered, both in and outside combat. Leena is training her well, but Karen feels that her impulsiveness could become her biggest weakness."
    new "Karen told me that Loren tends to be... hot tempered, both in and outside combat. Leena is training her well, but Karen feels that her impulsiveness could become her biggest weakness.\nKaren告诉我，Loren的性子……很暴躁，不管是在战斗中还是战斗外。Leena把她训练得很好，但Karen觉得，她的冲动可能会成为她最大的弱点。"

    old "And so she decided to ask the master of impulsiveness."
    new "And so she decided to ask the master of impulsiveness.\n于是她就决定向“冲动”的大师请教。"

    old "If that was an attempt at humor, it's a poor one, [protag]. But yes, she thought that I was the right person to tell the young princess about the necessity of not allowing yourself lose control in and outside combat."
    new "If that was an attempt at humor, it's a poor one, [protag]. But yes, she thought that I was the right person to tell the young princess about the necessity of not allowing yourself lose control in and outside combat.\n如果那算是在开玩笑，这玩笑可不怎么样，[protag]。不过，是的，她认为我是最合适的人选，去告诉年轻的公主，在战斗中和战斗外都不能让自己失控。"

    old "True fighters know when to stop and think, observe the opponent, and devise a strategy."
    new "True fighters know when to stop and think, observe the opponent, and devise a strategy.\n真正的战士知道什么时候该停下来思考，观察对手，制定策略。"

    old "And how did your training session with Loren go? Did she immediately adopt the calmness you suggested?"
    new "And how did your training session with Loren go? Did she immediately adopt the calmness you suggested?\n那你给Loren上的这堂课怎么样？她立刻就接受了你建议的冷静吗？"

    old "Sadly not. After a short while, we grow tired of talking and we started sparring. That girl is going to be a hell of a fighter in a few years."
    new "Sadly not. After a short while, we grow tired of talking and we started sparring. That girl is going to be a hell of a fighter in a few years.\n可惜没有。没过多久，我们就说腻了，开始对练。那姑娘再过几年，会是个了不得的战士。"

    old "Yes. Of course, right now she is no match for someone like me. However, I've never seen someone of her age fight so well. She told me that she wants to learn dual wielding in future."
    new "Yes. Of course, right now she is no match for someone like me. However, I've never seen someone of her age fight so well. She told me that she wants to learn dual wielding in future.\n是啊。当然，眼下她还不是我这种人的对手。不过，我从没见过她这个年纪的人打得这么好。她告诉我，她将来想学双持。"

    old "I think Sylrissa might be able to teach her a thing or two about that."
    new "I think Sylrissa might be able to teach her a thing or two about that.\n我想Sylrissa也许能在这方面教她一两手。"

    old "True, but I doubt Karen would allow a Naga inside the Citadel. Don't get me wrong, Sylrissa can be trusted, however..."
    new "True, but I doubt Karen would allow a Naga inside the Citadel. Don't get me wrong, Sylrissa can be trusted, however...\n没错，但我怀疑Karen不会允许一个Naga进入Citadel。别误会，Sylrissa是可以信任的，不过……"

    old "Yes, that's probably not going to happen."
    new "Yes, that's probably not going to happen.\n是的，那大概不会发生。"

    old "Excuse me now, [protag]. But after the training session with Loren I'm all sweaty, and I can't wait to get back home and have a proper bath."
    new "Excuse me now, [protag]. But after the training session with Loren I'm all sweaty, and I can't wait to get back home and have a proper bath.\n先失陪了，[protag]。跟Loren训练完，我浑身是汗，等不及回家好好洗个澡。"

    old "Sure, talk to you soon, Galan."
    new "Sure, talk to you soon, Galan.\n好，回头聊，Galan。"

    old "I arrive at the docks and spot Jasper sitting on the pier. He waves me over."
    new "I arrive at the docks and spot Jasper sitting on the pier. He waves me over.\n我来到码头，看见Jasper坐在栈桥上。他招手让我过去。"

    old "Hello, [protag]. Do you have business with the captain?"
    new "Hello, [protag]. Do you have business with the captain?\n你好，[protag]。你找船长有事吗？"

    old "No, I just came to see you."
    new "No, I just came to see you.\n不，我就是来看看你。"

    old "I'm very flattered. Would you care to join me in my rowboat?"
    new "I'm very flattered. Would you care to join me in my rowboat?\n真是受宠若惊。愿意上我的小划艇坐坐吗？"

    old "Why the rowboat?"
    new "Why the rowboat?\n为什么是划艇？"

    old "I feel more comfortable on the water. Less risk of someone listening in on your conversation."
    new "I feel more comfortable on the water. Less risk of someone listening in on your conversation.\n在水上我更自在。别人偷听你谈话的风险也更小。"

    old "Why would eavesdroppers be a concern? Are we going to be discussing something sensitive?"
    new "Why would eavesdroppers be a concern? Are we going to be discussing something sensitive?\n为什么会担心有人偷听？我们要谈什么敏感的事吗？"

    old "Not necessarily, but why not give ourselves that freedom, if the impulse strikes?"
    new "Not necessarily, but why not give ourselves that freedom, if the impulse strikes?\n倒也未必，但何不给自己这份自由呢，万一兴致来了？"

    old "Are you expecting eavesdroppers? You're the type who follows people around, but you don't strike me as the type who'd have followers."
    new "Are you expecting eavesdroppers? You're the type who follows people around, but you don't strike me as the type who'd have followers.\n你在等偷听的人出现吗？你是那种会跟踪别人的人，但你可不像那种会被人跟着的人。"

    old "Perhaps I'm just paranoid. But I'd rather be too cautious than not cautious enough."
    new "Perhaps I'm just paranoid. But I'd rather be too cautious than not cautious enough.\n也许我只是多疑。但我宁愿过于谨慎，也不愿不够谨慎。"

    old "Alright, Jasper. If it will put you at ease, I'll put out to sea."
    new "Alright, Jasper. If it will put you at ease, I'll put out to sea.\n好吧，Jasper。既然这样能让你安心，那我们就出海。"

    old "I get in after Jasper, and he rows us out to the edge of the harbor."
    new "I get in after Jasper, and he rows us out to the edge of the harbor.\n我跟着Jasper上了船，他把我们划到了港湾边缘。"

    old "You're an odd man, Jasper."
    new "You're an odd man, Jasper.\n你真是个怪人，Jasper。"

    old "Odd in what way?"
    new "Odd in what way?\n怪在哪儿？"

    old "I guess now is my opportunity to find that out."
    new "I guess now is my opportunity to find that out.\n我想现在正是我弄明白的机会。"

    old "You're presuming I'm willing to tell."
    new "You're presuming I'm willing to tell.\n你这是在假定我愿意告诉你。"

    old "Well, are you?"
    new "Well, are you?\n那你愿意吗？"

    old "How about I ask you a question first?"
    new "How about I ask you a question first?\n不如我先问你个问题？"

    old "You can ask the question, but I can't be sure I'll have the answer."
    new "You can ask the question, but I can't be sure I'll have the answer.\n你可以问，但我不能保证一定答得上来。"

    old "It's a subjective matter. There are no wrong answers here."
    new "It's a subjective matter. There are no wrong answers here.\n这是个主观问题。这里没有错误答案。"

    old "You're a representative of the Grimoire council. You do their bidding. You're assembling a task force to take on N'Mar's horrors. Why do all this?"
    new "You're a representative of the Grimoire council. You do their bidding. You're assembling a task force to take on N'Mar's horrors. Why do all this?\n你是Grimoire议会的代表。你替他们办事。你在组建一支特遣队去对付N'Mar的恐怖。为什么要做这一切？"

    old "I serve the leadership of Grimoire. They want me to take on N'Mar's horrors, so I oblige."
    new "I serve the leadership of Grimoire. They want me to take on N'Mar's horrors, so I oblige.\n我为Grimoire的领导层效力。他们要我对付N'Mar的恐怖，我便从命。"

    old "So your loyalty is to the leadership, then. But what if the leadership wanted something else?"
    new "So your loyalty is to the leadership, then. But what if the leadership wanted something else?\n那么，你忠诚的是领导层。可如果领导层想要的是别的事呢？"

    old "Right now, the leadership wants you to eliminate the source of N'Mar's mists. But suppose they wanted you to do something else, like assassinate a nobleman for political purposes. Or invade the lands of a rival nation, say the dwarves or the elves, and sabotage their cities' infrastructure. Would you still do their bidding, unconditionally?"
    new "Right now, the leadership wants you to eliminate the source of N'Mar's mists. But suppose they wanted you to do something else, like assassinate a nobleman for political purposes. Or invade the lands of a rival nation, say the dwarves or the elves, and sabotage their cities' infrastructure. Would you still do their bidding, unconditionally?\n眼下，领导层要你们去铲除N'Mar迷雾的源头。但假设他们要你去做别的，比如出于政治目的刺杀一名贵族。或者入侵一个敌对国家的领土，比如矮人或精灵的地盘，破坏他们城市的基础设施。你还会无条件地照办吗？"

    old "Yes, I would. The nature of commitment is that it's immutable. If you serve someone only when it suits you, you're not really serving them at all. You're just serving yourself."
    new "Yes, I would. The nature of commitment is that it's immutable. If you serve someone only when it suits you, you're not really serving them at all. You're just serving yourself.\n会的。承诺的本质就在于它不可改变。如果你只在合适的时候才为某人效力，那你根本不是真正在为他效力。你只是在为自己效力。"

    old "What if the council of Grimoire told you that your next mission was to serve the next forty years of your life working hard manual labor in a field, eating nothing but barley and drinking nothing but water? Would you still follow their orders?"
    new "What if the council of Grimoire told you that your next mission was to serve the next forty years of your life working hard manual labor in a field, eating nothing but barley and drinking nothing but water? Would you still follow their orders?\n如果Grimoire议会告诉你，你的下一个任务，是在往后的四十年里，在田里做繁重的体力活，只吃大麦、只喝水，你还会听从他们的命令吗？"

    old "Yes, I would."
    new "Yes, I would.\n会的。"

    old "I'm impressed. Few would be so unwavering in their loyalty."
    new "I'm impressed. Few would be so unwavering in their loyalty.\n真让人印象深刻。很少有人能如此毫不动摇地忠诚。"

    old "No, I wouldn't."
    new "No, I wouldn't.\n不，我不会。"

    old "But you just said that you were willing to do the bidding of Grimoire's council unconditionally."
    new "But you just said that you were willing to do the bidding of Grimoire's council unconditionally.\n可你刚才还说你愿意无条件地为Grimoire议会办事。"

    old "Laboring forty years in a field is not comparable to the mission I'm doing right now."
    new "Laboring forty years in a field is not comparable to the mission I'm doing right now.\n在田里劳作四十年，跟我现在做的任务没法比。"

    old "That's not what I asked, [protag]. You said your loyalty was unconditional. What we've just established now is that your loyalty to the council does have certain conditions."
    new "That's not what I asked, [protag]. You said your loyalty was unconditional. What we've just established now is that your loyalty to the council does have certain conditions.\n这不是我问你的，[protag]。你说你的忠诚是无条件的。而我们刚刚才确认，你对议会的忠诚其实是有条件的。"

    old "For example, one such condition might be, 'I will serve the Grimoire council, as long as their orders do not involved decades of manual labor and a life of poverty.'"
    new "For example, one such condition might be, 'I will serve the Grimoire council, as long as their orders do not involved decades of manual labor and a life of poverty.'\n比如说，其中一个条件可能是：“只要他们的命令不涉及几十年的体力劳动和贫穷的生活，我就为Grimoire议会效力。”"

    old "That's a healthy admission to make, and if you aren't willing to admit it to me, then at least admit it to yourself. There are certain things you're unwilling to do for Grimoire's council."
    new "That's a healthy admission to make, and if you aren't willing to admit it to me, then at least admit it to yourself. There are certain things you're unwilling to do for Grimoire's council.\n这么坦诚是件好事，如果你不愿向我承认，那至少向自己承认。有些事你是不愿意为Grimoire议会做的。"

    old "Interesting. What I gather from this is that you're willing to serve Grimoire's leadership only when it suits you."
    new "Interesting. What I gather from this is that you're willing to serve Grimoire's leadership only when it suits you.\n有意思。我从中听出来的是，你只愿意在自己觉得合适的时候为Grimoire领导层效力。"

    old "There are limits to what I'm willing to do."
    new "There are limits to what I'm willing to do.\n我愿意做的事是有底线的。"

    old "But you do the bidding of Grimoire's council conditionally. You do it when it suits you. So when you say that you serve the leadership of Grimoire, you're not really telling the full truth. For you to be running around on their behalf, there must be something else compelling you to do their bidding."
    new "But you do the bidding of Grimoire's council conditionally. You do it when it suits you. So when you say that you serve the leadership of Grimoire, you're not really telling the full truth. For you to be running around on their behalf, there must be something else compelling you to do their bidding.\n但你是附条件地为Grimoire议会办事。你在觉得合适的时候才去做。所以当你说你为Grimoire领导层效力时，你并没有说出全部实情。你会替他们四处奔波，一定还有别的东西在驱使你为他们办事。"

    old "You're right."
    new "You're right.\n你说得对。"

    old "I won't speculate as to why that is. You dodged my question with a non-response, and I won't try to pressure you into giving me another half-truth to answer the same question. I ask the question not so much because I want an answer from you, but because I want to give you something to ponder upon."
    new "I won't speculate as to why that is. You dodged my question with a non-response, and I won't try to pressure you into giving me another half-truth to answer the same question. I ask the question not so much because I want an answer from you, but because I want to give you something to ponder upon.\n我不会去猜那是什么原因。你用避而不答躲开了我的问题，我也不会逼你再用另一个半真半假的回答来应付同一个问题。我问这个问题，与其说是想从你那儿得到答案，不如说是想给你一点东西去琢磨。"

    old "There are certain missions Grimoire might task you with that you'd refuse. Yet, you didn't refuse this one. Think about why that is. It may be a complicated answer, or it may be a simple one. Whatever the case, it's something you may wish to dwell upon the next time you're called upon to make a difficult decision."
    new "There are certain missions Grimoire might task you with that you'd refuse. Yet, you didn't refuse this one. Think about why that is. It may be a complicated answer, or it may be a simple one. Whatever the case, it's something you may wish to dwell upon the next time you're called upon to make a difficult decision.\nGrimoire可能会交给你某些你会拒绝的任务。然而，你却没有拒绝这一个。想想这是为什么。答案可能很复杂，也可能很简单。无论如何，下次你被叫去做艰难决定时，这或许值得你好好想想。"

    old "I serve the people of Grimoire."
    new "I serve the people of Grimoire.\n我为Grimoire的人民效力。"

    old "So, you fancy yourself a messiah?"
    new "So, you fancy yourself a messiah?\n这么说，你觉得自己是个救世主？"

    old "I suppose, in a manner of speaking, that the fate of the people of Grimoire rests on my shoulders. After all, the mists around N'Mar threaten to envelop the human empire, and may one day threaten the entire continent."
    new "I suppose, in a manner of speaking, that the fate of the people of Grimoire rests on my shoulders. After all, the mists around N'Mar threaten to envelop the human empire, and may one day threaten the entire continent.\n我想，从某种意义上说，Grimoire人民的命运就压在我的肩上。毕竟，N'Mar周围的迷雾威胁着要吞没人类帝国，也许有朝一日会威胁到整片大陆。"

    old "If I fail in my mission, all those people may die. If I succeed, then they live to see another day. Wouldn't you say that makes me a messiah of sorts?"
    new "If I fail in my mission, all those people may die. If I succeed, then they live to see another day. Wouldn't you say that makes me a messiah of sorts?\n如果我任务失败，那些人可能都会死。如果我成功，他们就能活到明天。你难道不说这让我算是个救世主吗？"

    old "Only if you succeed, and only if we presume that the job you're doing couldn't be done by someone else in your absence. After all, there is a difference between being an architect and being a handyman. What's to say you couldn't be replaced?"
    new "Only if you succeed, and only if we presume that the job you're doing couldn't be done by someone else in your absence. After all, there is a difference between being an architect and being a handyman. What's to say you couldn't be replaced?\n只有在你成功的前提下，而且前提是假定你不在时，这份工作就没有别人能做。毕竟，建筑师和杂工是有区别的。凭什么说你就不可替代呢？"

    old "Even if I am replaceable, I wouldn't say that makes me any less of a hero."
    new "Even if I am replaceable, I wouldn't say that makes me any less of a hero.\n就算我可以被替代，我也不觉得那会让我少算一分英雄。"

    old "In that case, I'd say that the Grimoire council is lucky to have you. Unwavering enthusiasm, that's what they need when it comes to the really tough tasks that require both physical and mental fortitude."
    new "In that case, I'd say that the Grimoire council is lucky to have you. Unwavering enthusiasm, that's what they need when it comes to the really tough tasks that require both physical and mental fortitude.\n那样的话，我会说，Grimoire议会能拥有你是它的幸运。毫不动摇的热忱，正是他们在那些既需要体魄又需要意志的真正艰巨任务上所需要的。"

    old "I'm no messiah. Just a [manwoman] doing [hisher] part to defeat a menace that threatens the human empire."
    new "I'm no messiah. Just a [manwoman] doing [hisher] part to defeat a menace that threatens the human empire.\n我不是什么救世主。只是一个[manwoman]，尽[hisher]的本分，去击败威胁人类帝国的灾祸。"

    old "That's odd. You do so much for Grimoire, and yet you're so humble. That mixture of drive and humility must make you quite a favorite with Grimoire's council members."
    new "That's odd. You do so much for Grimoire, and yet you're so humble. That mixture of drive and humility must make you quite a favorite with Grimoire's council members.\n真奇怪。你为Grimoire做了那么多，却又如此谦逊。那种干劲与谦逊的混合，一定让你很受Grimoire议员们的青睐。"

    old "They need loyal foot soldiers, men and women who will carry out their mission without demanding recognition or praise. The fact that you consider the mission's success to be its own reward simplifies matters for them greatly."
    new "They need loyal foot soldiers, men and women who will carry out their mission without demanding recognition or praise. The fact that you consider the mission's success to be its own reward simplifies matters for them greatly.\n他们需要忠诚的步兵，无论男女，那些会不图认可、不求赞美地执行任务的男男女女。你觉得任务的成功本身就是回报，这一点大大简化了他们的事。"

    old "Messiah?"
    new "Messiah?\n救世主？"

    old "It means a savior of the people. If you profess to serve the people of Grimoire, it must mean that you fancy yourself their savior. After all, you're doing a job that no one else is willing to do."
    new "It means a savior of the people. If you profess to serve the people of Grimoire, it must mean that you fancy yourself their savior. After all, you're doing a job that no one else is willing to do.\n意思是人民的救星。如果你宣称你为Grimoire人民服务，那必然意味着你自认是他们的救星。毕竟，你在做一件没人愿意做的工作。"

    old "Maybe so, maybe not. It could be that I'm one of a kind. It could also be that if I were absent, someone else would take on the same set of responsibilities and see the mission through to its conclusion."
    new "Maybe so, maybe not. It could be that I'm one of a kind. It could also be that if I were absent, someone else would take on the same set of responsibilities and see the mission through to its conclusion.\n也许是，也许不是。可能我是独一无二的。也可能，如果我不在，别人会承担起同样的责任，把任务贯彻到底。"

    old "Well, if we're lucky, we won't have to find out the answer to that question."
    new "Well, if we're lucky, we won't have to find out the answer to that question.\n嗯，如果运气好，我们就不必去弄清那个问题的答案了。"

    old "I think the real question is, what happens to you when this is all over?"
    new "I think the real question is, what happens to you when this is all over?\n我觉得真正的问题是，当这一切结束时，你会怎么样？"

    old "I'm not sure I understand your question."
    new "I'm not sure I understand your question.\n我不太明白你的问题。"

    old "Clearly, the council is using you for some purpose. What happens when they're done with you?"
    new "Clearly, the council is using you for some purpose. What happens when they're done with you?\n很明显，议会是在利用你达成某种目的。等他们用完你之后，会怎样？"

    old "I haven't given that much thought. I suppose cared more about the people of Grimoire as a whole more than I care about the Grimoire council."
    new "I haven't given that much thought. I suppose cared more about the people of Grimoire as a whole more than I care about the Grimoire council.\n我没想那么多。我想，比起Grimoire议会，我更在乎的是Grimoire的全体人民。"

    old "But your deal is with the council, not the people. You serve the council, and the council ostensibly serves the interests of the people. The people of Grimoire don't know who you are. If you're going to get thanks and recognition from anyone, it will be the council."
    new "But your deal is with the council, not the people. You serve the council, and the council ostensibly serves the interests of the people. The people of Grimoire don't know who you are. If you're going to get thanks and recognition from anyone, it will be the council.\n但与你达成交易的是议会，不是人民。你为议会效力，而议会表面上为人民的利益效力。Grimoire的人民并不知道你是谁。如果你能从谁那里得到感谢和认可，那只会是议会。"

    old "I'll ask the question again: what do you suppose the council intends to do when they're done with you?"
    new "I'll ask the question again: what do you suppose the council intends to do when they're done with you?\n我再问一次：你觉得议会用完你之后，打算做什么？"

    old "You probably don't know the answer to that question, which is fine. I asked it not because I wanted you to give me an answer, but because I wanted to give you an idea to ponder."
    new "You probably don't know the answer to that question, which is fine. I asked it not because I wanted you to give me an answer, but because I wanted to give you an idea to ponder.\n你大概不知道那个问题的答案，这没关系。我问它，不是想让你给我答案，而是想给你个想法去琢磨。"

    old "However, I will say this. The Grimoire council is a powerful group full of powerful people. They decided to form a partnership of sorts with you. Which of you is winning in this deal you've struck? Because it certainly doesn't seem like the council is the one losing."
    new "However, I will say this. The Grimoire council is a powerful group full of powerful people. They decided to form a partnership of sorts with you. Which of you is winning in this deal you've struck? Because it certainly doesn't seem like the council is the one losing.\n不过，我要说一句。Grimoire议会是一个由有权有势之人组成的强大团体。他们决定与你结成某种伙伴关系。在你们达成的这笔交易里，谁占了上风？因为输的那一方显然不是议会。"

    old "Maybe we both win."
    new "Maybe we both win.\n也许我们双赢。"

    old "'Maybe' isn't something most people are comfortable staking their future on. But then, you're not 'most people,' are you?"
    new "'Maybe' isn't something most people are comfortable staking their future on. But then, you're not 'most people,' are you?\n“也许”这两个字，大多数人可不敢拿它去押自己的未来。不过话说回来，你又不是“大多数人”，对吧？"

    old "My first loyalty is to myself. I do what I do because I believe it's in my own best interest."
    new "My first loyalty is to myself. I do what I do because I believe it's in my own best interest.\n我的首要忠诚是忠于自己。我这么做，是因为我相信这符合我自己的最大利益。"

    old "Interesting. That's not a noble reason, but it feels honest somehow. Not honest just in the sense of being frank, but the sense that serving one's own self-interest seems like the most predictable course of action."
    new "Interesting. That's not a noble reason, but it feels honest somehow. Not honest just in the sense of being frank, but the sense that serving one's own self-interest seems like the most predictable course of action.\n有意思。这不是个崇高的理由，但不知怎的，它让人觉得诚实。诚实不光是指坦率，而是说，为自己的私利服务，似乎是最可预测的一种行为方式。"

    old "A selfish man can always be counted on to be selfish. It's the ones who profess to be selfless that you have to keep an eye on, because they're either liars, or worse still, actually trying to do what they think is best for other people."
    new "A selfish man can always be counted on to be selfish. It's the ones who profess to be selfless that you have to keep an eye on, because they're either liars, or worse still, actually trying to do what they think is best for other people.\n自私的人，你永远能指望他继续自私。需要提防的，是那些宣称自己无私的人，因为他们要么是骗子，要么更糟——真的在试图做他们认为对别人最有利的事。"

    old "Are you saying that vice is better than virtue?"
    new "Are you saying that vice is better than virtue?\n你是说，恶习比美德更好？"

    old "Let me point the question back at you, [protag]. Would you rather deal with an adversary driven by virtue, or one driven by vice?"
    new "Let me point the question back at you, [protag]. Would you rather deal with an adversary driven by virtue, or one driven by vice?\n让我把问题抛回给你，[protag]。你更愿意对付一个被美德驱使的对手，还是一个被恶习驱使的对手？"

    old "Jasper looks over his shoulder, toward the open sea. A wry grin creeps onto his face, and in his eyes I can sense a calm contentment."
    new "Jasper looks over his shoulder, toward the open sea. A wry grin creeps onto his face, and in his eyes I can sense a calm contentment.\nJasper越过肩头，望向开阔的海面。一丝揶揄的笑意爬上他的脸，从他的眼里，我能感到一种平静的满足。"

    old "I feel like I've gotten to know you better, [protag]. I hope you feel the same way."
    new "I feel like I've gotten to know you better, [protag]. I hope you feel the same way.\n我觉得我更了解你了，[protag]。希望你也这么觉得。"

    old "Well, I've learned that you enjoy asking strange rhetorical and philosophical questions."
    new "Well, I've learned that you enjoy asking strange rhetorical and philosophical questions.\n嗯，我了解到，你喜欢问些奇奇怪怪的修辞和哲学问题。"

    old "Oh, I wasn't talking about you getting to know me better. I was talking about you getting to know yourself better. Our conversation has mostly been centered on you, after all."
    new "Oh, I wasn't talking about you getting to know me better. I was talking about you getting to know yourself better. Our conversation has mostly been centered on you, after all.\n哦，我说的可不是你更了解我。我说的是你更了解自己。毕竟，我们的谈话大多都围绕着你。"

    old "I know myself pretty well. Me, myself, and I have a long history together."
    new "I know myself pretty well. Me, myself, and I have a long history together.\n我挺了解自己的。我、我自己、还有我自己，我们三个可是老交情了。"

    old "That's good. 'Know thyself' is a piece of wisdom as old as time itself, but I think it's still pertinent to this day. Just make sure that you don't take your own self-understanding for granted."
    new "That's good. 'Know thyself' is a piece of wisdom as old as time itself, but I think it's still pertinent to this day. Just make sure that you don't take your own self-understanding for granted.\n很好。“认识你自己”是句和时光一样古老的智慧，但我认为它至今仍不过时。只是要确保，你别把自己的自我认知当成理所当然。"

    old "There are fewer things more important than questions of the self. What matters most to you? What are you willing to do to achieve that goal? A lot of people assume that they know the answers to these questions, but far too often I've seen people realize in retrospect that they've betrayed themselves."
    new "There are fewer things more important than questions of the self. What matters most to you? What are you willing to do to achieve that goal? A lot of people assume that they know the answers to these questions, but far too often I've seen people realize in retrospect that they've betrayed themselves.\n没什么比关于自我的问题更重要了。你最在乎什么？你愿意付出什么去达成那个目标？很多人自以为知道这些问题的答案，但我见过太多人在回顾时才意识到，他们背叛了自己。"

    old "I'm not sure I've ever met someone who betrayed himself."
    new "I'm not sure I've ever met someone who betrayed himself.\n我不确定自己有没有见过背叛自己的人。"

    old "Oh, but you have. You're looking at him right now."
    new "Oh, but you have. You're looking at him right now.\n哦，你见过。你此刻正看着他呢。"

    old "You? How exactly did you betray yourself?"
    new "You? How exactly did you betray yourself?\n你？你究竟是怎么背叛自己的？"

    old "That's a good question. Ask me again another day, and I may have an answer for you."
    new "That's a good question. Ask me again another day, and I may have an answer for you.\n问得好。改天再问我，我也许能给你个答案。"

    old "I'd rather deal with someone driven by virtue."
    new "I'd rather deal with someone driven by virtue.\n我宁愿对付一个被美德驱使的人。"

    old "That's...an interesting position to take."
    new "That's...an interesting position to take.\n那……倒是个有意思的立场。"

    old "I take it you view things differently."
    new "I take it you view things differently.\n看来你对事情的看法不同。"

    old "Let me pose it to you like this. Suppose you have a neighbor who has a penchant for stealing alcohol."
    new "Let me pose it to you like this. Suppose you have a neighbor who has a penchant for stealing alcohol.\n让我这么跟你说吧。假设你有个邻居，嗜好偷酒。"

    old "He's a drunkard, you see, a selfish drunkard with no regard for the rights of others. Any time he catches wind of the fact that you have some ale, or a bottle of wine in your home, he sneaks in to snatch it."
    new "He's a drunkard, you see, a selfish drunkard with no regard for the rights of others. Any time he catches wind of the fact that you have some ale, or a bottle of wine in your home, he sneaks in to snatch it.\n你瞧，他是个酒鬼，一个自私的酒鬼，全然不顾别人的权利。每当他嗅到你家里有些麦芽酒、或者一瓶葡萄酒的风声，就会溜进去偷走。"

    old "In fact, some days, he might break in to look for wine to steal, even when you have none of it."
    new "In fact, some days, he might break in to look for wine to steal, even when you have none of it.\n事实上，有些日子，哪怕你家里根本没有酒，他也可能闯进来找酒偷。"

    old "Now, this would be quite the vexing situation, having your home broken into constantly. However, you could tale consolation in the fact that your neighbor is motivated by selfishness. On days when he thirsted for the drink, he would break into your house in search of ale."
    new "Now, this would be quite the vexing situation, having your home broken into constantly. However, you could tale consolation in the fact that your neighbor is motivated by selfishness. On days when he thirsted for the drink, he would break into your house in search of ale.\n那么，家里隔三差五被人闯进来，这情况可够烦人的。不过，你倒是可以从这件事里找点安慰：你的邻居是出于自私。他馋酒的那几天，才会闯进你家找麦芽酒。"

    old "However, there might be some days when he was too drunk, or too lazy, or too tired to break into your house. This hypothetical neighbor is a selfish man, remember, and driven by his own impulses, like the desire to sleep."
    new "However, there might be some days when he was too drunk, or too lazy, or too tired to break into your house. This hypothetical neighbor is a selfish man, remember, and driven by his own impulses, like the desire to sleep.\n然而，有些日子他可能醉得太厉害，或者太懒、太累，就不会闯进你家。别忘了，这个假想中的邻居是个自私的人，被自己的冲动驱使着，比如想睡觉的欲望。"

    old "Perhaps every now and then he spends a day at the brothel, and can't be bothered to spend time breaking into your home."
    new "Perhaps every now and then he spends a day at the brothel, and can't be bothered to spend time breaking into your home.\n也许他时不时会在妓院里待上一天，也就懒得花时间闯进你家了。"

    old "Let's consider an alternate example. Let's suppose your neighbor is not an alcoholic, but a moral man. A priest, with extreme views on vice. A fanatic who fancies himself so moral that he is adamantly opposed to the consumption of alcohol."
    new "Let's consider an alternate example. Let's suppose your neighbor is not an alcoholic, but a moral man. A priest, with extreme views on vice. A fanatic who fancies himself so moral that he is adamantly opposed to the consumption of alcohol.\n我们再来考虑另一个例子。假设你的邻居不是酒鬼，而是一个有道德的人。一个对恶习抱有极端看法的牧师。一个自以为道德高尚到坚决反对饮酒的狂热分子。"

    old "This priest is so uncompromisingly hostile to alcohol, that he won't permit his neighbors to have it. If he catches wind of the fact that you might have some ale or a bottle of wine in your home, he breaks in, steals the drink, and pours it out onto the ground to ensure that it can't be consumed."
    new "This priest is so uncompromisingly hostile to alcohol, that he won't permit his neighbors to have it. If he catches wind of the fact that you might have some ale or a bottle of wine in your home, he breaks in, steals the drink, and pours it out onto the ground to ensure that it can't be consumed.\n这位牧师对酒精怀有如此毫不妥协的敌意，以至于他绝不容许邻居拥有酒。他一旦嗅到你家里可能有些麦芽酒或一瓶葡萄酒的风声，就会闯进去，偷走酒，然后倒在地上，确保没人能喝到。"

    old "Sometimes he breaks into your home, even when you have no alcohol, just to make sure that you don't."
    new "Sometimes he breaks into your home, even when you have no alcohol, just to make sure that you don't.\n有时候，哪怕你家里没有酒，他也会闯进去，只是为了确认你真的没有。"

    old "This priest's transgression toward you might similar to that of the drunkard: he has an agenda which demands that he break into your home and steal your drinks. However, unlike the drunkard, he is not driven by selfishness. He is driven by his conscience."
    new "This priest's transgression toward you might similar to that of the drunkard: he has an agenda which demands that he break into your home and steal your drinks. However, unlike the drunkard, he is not driven by selfishness. He is driven by his conscience.\n这位牧师对你的侵犯，也许跟酒鬼差不多：他有个非做不可的议程，逼他闯进你家、偷走你的酒。然而，和酒鬼不同，他不是被自私驱使的。他是被自己的良心驱使的。"

    old "The drunkard may some days decide that it is not worth the effort to break into your home, and so out of selfishness, elect not to bother you. Perhaps on some days, he will find alcohol somewhere other than your home, and thus feel no compulsion to break into your home."
    new "The drunkard may some days decide that it is not worth the effort to break into your home, and so out of selfishness, elect not to bother you. Perhaps on some days, he will find alcohol somewhere other than your home, and thus feel no compulsion to break into your home.\n酒鬼可能有些日子觉得，闯进你家不值得费那番力气，于是出于自私，选择不来打扰你。也许有些日子，他会在你家以外的地方找到酒，也就没有闯进你家的冲动。"

    old "However, the priest is driven by his convictions. Every day, he will break into your home, driven by a moral fervor and a determination to ensure that you have no alcohol in your home. No amount of tiredness will stop him. The priest will endure fatigue and physical struggle, because he feels compelled to break into your home not by impulse, but by some higher calling."
    new "However, the priest is driven by his convictions. Every day, he will break into your home, driven by a moral fervor and a determination to ensure that you have no alcohol in your home. No amount of tiredness will stop him. The priest will endure fatigue and physical struggle, because he feels compelled to break into your home not by impulse, but by some higher calling.\n然而，牧师是被他的信念驱使的。他每天都会闯进你家，被一种道德狂热和决心所驱使，非要确保你家里没有酒。再累也拦不住他。牧师会忍受疲惫和身体的挣扎，因为驱使他闯进你家的不是冲动，而是某种更高的召唤。"

    old "So, I ask you this: which makes the worse neighbor, the drunkard or the priest?"
    new "So, I ask you this: which makes the worse neighbor, the drunkard or the priest?\n所以，我问你：哪个邻居更糟糕，酒鬼还是牧师？"

    old "It's worse to live next to the drunkard. The priest may be a nuisance, but at least he has scruples and sticks to them."
    new "It's worse to live next to the drunkard. The priest may be a nuisance, but at least he has scruples and sticks to them.\n住在酒鬼隔壁更糟。牧师可能很烦人，但至少他有原则，并且坚守原则。"

    old "Even as he invades your home."
    new "Even as he invades your home.\n即便他闯进你的家。"

    old "It's better than dealing with the derelict drunkard."
    new "It's better than dealing with the derelict drunkard.\n那也比对付那个堕落的酒鬼强。"

    old "Alright, [protag]. You seem fairly convinced of your position. I can respect that. But I would like to provide one last example to illustrate my point."
    new "Alright, [protag]. You seem fairly convinced of your position. I can respect that. But I would like to provide one last example to illustrate my point.\n好吧，[protag]。你似乎相当确信自己的立场。我尊重这一点。不过，我想再举最后一个例子来说明我的观点。"

    old "Suppose you are the ruler of a kingdom. The king of a neighboring land declares war on you. 'We want your riches for ourselves,' he says. 'We will kill your people and take your land, and plunder the gold from your castle.'"
    new "Suppose you are the ruler of a kingdom. The king of a neighboring land declares war on you. 'We want your riches for ourselves,' he says. 'We will kill your people and take your land, and plunder the gold from your castle.'\n假设你是一个王国的统治者。邻国的国王向你宣战。他说：“我们想要你们的财富。我们要杀死你们的人民，夺走你们的土地，从你们的城堡里抢走黄金。”"

    old "This is a terrifying thing to hear. But you can imagine that because he is selfish, he performed an analysis of the benefits and costs of invading your kingdom."
    new "This is a terrifying thing to hear. But you can imagine that because he is selfish, he performed an analysis of the benefits and costs of invading your kingdom.\n这话听起来很吓人。但你可以想象，因为他自私，他会对入侵你王国的收益和代价做一番分析。"

    old "He is willing to sacrifice the lives of some of his soldiers to plunder your lands, but if you can mount a sufficient resistance, he may decide that the cost of invading is too high. His selfishness may cause him to retreat from your lands at some point."
    new "He is willing to sacrifice the lives of some of his soldiers to plunder your lands, but if you can mount a sufficient resistance, he may decide that the cost of invading is too high. His selfishness may cause him to retreat from your lands at some point.\n他愿意牺牲自己的一些士兵去掠夺你的土地，但如果你能组织起足够的抵抗，他可能会认定入侵的代价太高。他的自私，也许会让他在某个时候从你的土地上撤退。"

    old "Now, imagine a different king of a different kingdom declares war on you. 'The almighty have declared that the lands of your kingdom belong to us,' he says. 'The existence of your people is an affront to the gods. They demand that we exterminate every person within your kingdom.'"
    new "Now, imagine a different king of a different kingdom declares war on you. 'The almighty have declared that the lands of your kingdom belong to us,' he says. 'The existence of your people is an affront to the gods. They demand that we exterminate every person within your kingdom.'\n现在，再想象另一个王国的一位不同的国王向你宣战。他说：“全能的神已经宣告，你们王国的土地属于我们。你们人民的存在是对诸神的冒犯。他们命令我们，将你们王国内的每一个人斩尽杀绝。”"

    old "How much more horrifying is this than the invasion by the selfish king? A selfish invader may be repelled, but an invader who believes that he is morally obligated to invade you will never cease in his assault. He may even do things which a selfish invader wouldn't, like killing women and children."
    new "How much more horrifying is this than the invasion by the selfish king? A selfish invader may be repelled, but an invader who believes that he is morally obligated to invade you will never cease in his assault. He may even do things which a selfish invader wouldn't, like killing women and children.\n这比那个自私国王的入侵要可怕多少？一个自私的侵略者或许能被击退，但一个相信自己道义上有义务入侵你的侵略者，绝不会停止进攻。他甚至可能做出自私的侵略者不会做的事，比如杀害妇孺。"

    old "Are you done lecturing me?"
    new "Are you done lecturing me?\n你教训够了吗？"

    old "Forgive me, [protag]. My intent is not to tell you how to think, but to give you questions to think upon."
    new "Forgive me, [protag]. My intent is not to tell you how to think, but to give you questions to think upon.\n原谅我，[protag]。我的本意不是告诉你怎么思考，而是给你些问题去思索。"

    old "I suppose it would be worst to live next to the priest."
    new "I suppose it would be worst to live next to the priest.\n我想，住在牧师隔壁会更糟。"

    old "So you understand my point. There is something comforting about selfishness. A man who fancies himself a paragon of virtue is relentless. A selfish man, conversely, may sometimes relent in his assault on your rights."
    new "So you understand my point. There is something comforting about selfishness. A man who fancies himself a paragon of virtue is relentless. A selfish man, conversely, may sometimes relent in his assault on your rights.\n所以你就明白我的意思了。自私自利之中，自有一种让人安心之处。一个自诩道德楷模的人会不留余地。而一个自私的人，反而有时会对你权利的侵犯有所收敛。"

    old "By the same token, a man who plots to kill you and steal everything from you may, in some circumstances, be persuaded not to kill you if he believes that it is in his best interests not to kill you. On the other hand, a zealot who believes that you are evil and must be killed to satisfy some moral agenda cannot be similarly persuaded."
    new "By the same token, a man who plots to kill you and steal everything from you may, in some circumstances, be persuaded not to kill you if he believes that it is in his best interests not to kill you. On the other hand, a zealot who believes that you are evil and must be killed to satisfy some moral agenda cannot be similarly persuaded.\n同理，一个密谋杀害你、抢光你一切的人，在某些情况下，如果他认为不杀你才最符合他的利益，是可以被说服不杀你的。另一方面，一个认为你是邪恶的、必须为满足某种道德议程而杀你的狂热分子，是无法同样被说服的。"

    old "Exactly. I'm glad to hear you understand."
    new "Exactly. I'm glad to hear you understand.\n没错。很高兴你听明白了。"

    old "It's preferable to deal with a foe driven by vice. If someone plots against you out of selfishness, he may be persuaded against carrying out his plan if he believes it to be in his best interest. Conversely, someone who plots against you out of a sense of virtue will be unrelenting in their assault, as they do so with a sense of moral obligation."
    new "It's preferable to deal with a foe driven by vice. If someone plots against you out of selfishness, he may be persuaded against carrying out his plan if he believes it to be in his best interest. Conversely, someone who plots against you out of a sense of virtue will be unrelenting in their assault, as they do so with a sense of moral obligation.\n对付一个被恶习驱使的敌人更可取。如果有人出于自私密谋害你，当他相信收手才最符合自身利益时，他或许会被说服放弃计划。相反，出于道德感而密谋害你的人，会毫不留情地攻击你，因为他们这么做是出于道德义务。"

    old "Exactly. The power of conscience is greater than the power of greed. If my foes are driven by greed, I know many ways to deal with that. But when they are driven by conscience..."
    new "Exactly. The power of conscience is greater than the power of greed. If my foes are driven by greed, I know many ways to deal with that. But when they are driven by conscience...\n没错。良心的力量比贪婪的力量更大。如果我的敌人被贪婪驱使，我知道很多对付的办法。但当他们被良心驱使时……"

    old "Hello, Jasper."
    new "Hello, Jasper.\n你好，Jasper。"

    old "Come to entertain me again, have you?"
    new "Come to entertain me again, have you?\n又来找我消遣了，是吗？"

    old "Maybe I came here so that you could entertain me."
    new "Maybe I came here so that you could entertain me.\n也许我来，是为了让你消遣我。"

    old "How about we entertain each other?"
    new "How about we entertain each other?\n那我们互相消遣如何？"

    old "Sounds fair to me. Are we going out to sea again?"
    new "Sounds fair to me. Are we going out to sea again?\n听起来公平。我们又要出海吗？"

    old "Let's stick to the docks. I've been trying to get my land legs back, now that I expect to do more fighting on land than at sea."
    new "Let's stick to the docks. I've been trying to get my land legs back, now that I expect to do more fighting on land than at sea.\n就待在码头吧。我一直想把陆地上的腿劲找回来，毕竟我估计接下来在陆地上作战会比在海上多。"

    old "You've been working with the Grimoire council, haven't you?"
    new "You've been working with the Grimoire council, haven't you?\n你一直在跟Grimoire议会合作，对吧？"

    old "Indeed I have."
    new "Indeed I have.\n没错。"

    old "Tell me, what's the council like? What do you think of them?"
    new "Tell me, what's the council like? What do you think of them?\n告诉我，议会是什么样的？你觉得他们如何？"

    old "They've been easy to work with. Actually, to say that I work with them would be putting it rather generously. For the most part, they leave me to my own devices."
    new "They've been easy to work with. Actually, to say that I work with them would be putting it rather generously. For the most part, they leave me to my own devices.\n跟他们合作很省心。其实，说我跟他们合作，已经是往大了说。大部分时候，他们都放手让我自己干。"

    old "I do have directions from the council, but they tend to be very vague. I have a lot of autonomy. For example, I can do things like ask for the assistance of pirates."
    new "I do have directions from the council, but they tend to be very vague. I have a lot of autonomy. For example, I can do things like ask for the assistance of pirates.\n我确实会收到议会的指示，但往往都很含糊。我有很大的自主权。比如，我可以做出向海盗求助之类的事。"

    old "And they're fine with the way you do things?"
    new "And they're fine with the way you do things?\n他们对你做事的方式也没意见？"

    old "It might be more accurate to say that I don't inform them of the way I do things. And they can't object to something when they don't know about it."
    new "It might be more accurate to say that I don't inform them of the way I do things. And they can't object to something when they don't know about it.\n更准确的说法或许是，我并不把我的做事方式告诉他们。他们不知道的事，自然就没法反对。"

    old "So, the thing that makes the council easy to work with is the fact that they don't give you too much scrutiny."
    new "So, the thing that makes the council easy to work with is the fact that they don't give you too much scrutiny.\n所以说，让议会省心的，是他们不会对你盯得太紧。"

    old "That seems fair to say."
    new "That seems fair to say.\n这么说倒也公平。"

    old "Would you say that they willingly turn a blind eye to the way you do things? Or are you actively concealing your activity from them?"
    new "Would you say that they willingly turn a blind eye to the way you do things? Or are you actively concealing your activity from them?\n你觉得，他们是对你的做法自愿睁一只眼闭一只眼，还是你在主动对他们隐瞒你的行动？"

    old "I'm just asking, what if the council knew everything that you were doing in the pursuit of your mission? What if they knew about every part of every conversation you ever had, the people you were working with and the things you had to do to enlist their help."
    new "I'm just asking, what if the council knew everything that you were doing in the pursuit of your mission? What if they knew about every part of every conversation you ever had, the people you were working with and the things you had to do to enlist their help.\n我只是想问，如果议会知道你执行任务时所做的一切呢？如果他们知道你每一场对话的每一个细节，你合作的那些人，以及你为了争取他们帮助而不得不做的那些事呢？"

    old "Do you think they would be approve? Or would they be displeased?"
    new "Do you think they would be approve? Or would they be displeased?\n你觉得他们会赞成吗？还是会不高兴？"

    old "They'd approve. I'm a representative of the council, and I'd like to think that I do them proud."
    new "They'd approve. I'm a representative of the council, and I'd like to think that I do them proud.\n他们会赞成。我是议会的代表，我想我做得没让他们丢脸。"

    old "My understanding is that you've assembled a very...multicultural task force, as it were."
    new "My understanding is that you've assembled a very...multicultural task force, as it were.\n据我了解，你组建了一支非常……多元文化的特遣队，可以这么说。"

    old "Yes. The people who I've recruited to help me come from all walks of life and all regions of Aravorn."
    new "Yes. The people who I've recruited to help me come from all walks of life and all regions of Aravorn.\n是的。我招募来帮我的人，来自Aravorn各行各业、各个地区。"

    old "I wonder, how does the council of the human empire feel about foreigners coming in to fight their battles for them?"
    new "I wonder, how does the council of the human empire feel about foreigners coming in to fight their battles for them?\n我想知道，人类帝国的议会，对外国人来替他们打仗，是什么感觉？"

    old "It was Grimoire's council who decided to strike an alliance with the Amazons, not me. I'm simply carrying out their will."
    new "It was Grimoire's council who decided to strike an alliance with the Amazons, not me. I'm simply carrying out their will.\n决定与Amazons结盟的是Grimoire议会，不是我。我只是在执行他们的意志。"

    old "But what about the others you've met? Did the council explicitly approve every one of those arrangements as well?"
    new "But what about the others you've met? Did the council explicitly approve every one of those arrangements as well?\n那你遇见的其他人呢？议会也明确批准了每一个安排吗？"

    old "Some alliances are explicit, others are tacit. That doesn't mean they're not valid."
    new "Some alliances are explicit, others are tacit. That doesn't mean they're not valid.\n有些联盟是明面上的，有些是心照不宣的。这并不代表它们无效。"

    old "I'd be concerned that any alliance formed without a formal declaration could also be broken without a formal declaration."
    new "I'd be concerned that any alliance formed without a formal declaration could also be broken without a formal declaration.\n我会担心，任何没有正式宣告就结成的联盟，也可能在没有正式宣告的情况下破裂。"

    old "I think that we share a common enemy in all of this. My job is to defeat the evil of N'Mar by any means necessary. And that's exactly what I intend to do."
    new "I think that we share a common enemy in all of this. My job is to defeat the evil of N'Mar by any means necessary. And that's exactly what I intend to do.\n我觉得，在这一切里，我们有一个共同的敌人。我的工作，就是用一切必要手段击败N'Mar的邪恶。而这正是我打算做的。"

    old "That's...a difficult question to answer."
    new "That's...a difficult question to answer.\n那……是个很难回答的问题。"

    old "That's why I asked it."
    new "That's why I asked it.\n所以我才问。"

    old "I think it would fair to say that I play a bit fast and loose when it comes to getting things done. There are some things that don't look all that great when you pull them into the sunlight."
    new "I think it would fair to say that I play a bit fast and loose when it comes to getting things done. There are some things that don't look all that great when you pull them into the sunlight.\n我想可以这么说，在把事情办成这件事上，我有点我行我素。有些事情，一旦摊到阳光下，看起来并不那么光彩。"

    old "But the real question is, what does the council think of me? Not in some hypothetical scenario, but what do they think of me now? And the answer to that question is that they're pleased. I'm accomplishing the goals they lay out. I'm getting things done. That's what matters."
    new "But the real question is, what does the council think of me? Not in some hypothetical scenario, but what do they think of me now? And the answer to that question is that they're pleased. I'm accomplishing the goals they lay out. I'm getting things done. That's what matters.\n但真正的问题是，议会怎么看我？不是在某些假设情境下，而是他们现在怎么看我。这个问题的答案是，他们很满意。我在完成他们定下的目标。我在把事情办成。这才是关键。"

    old "That may be the case, [protag]. But be wary that the questions and scenarios that seem hypothetical today may not seem so hypothetical tomorrow."
    new "That may be the case, [protag]. But be wary that the questions and scenarios that seem hypothetical today may not seem so hypothetical tomorrow.\n也许是这么回事，[protag]。但要当心，今天看来是假设的问题和情形，明天可能就不再是假设了。"

    old "The council hasn't exactly been easy to work with."
    new "The council hasn't exactly been easy to work with.\n议会其实并不怎么好合作。"

    old "Oh? How so?"
    new "Oh? How so?\n哦？怎么说？"

    old "Most of what they do is shrouded in mystery. It's very seldom that I convene with the entire council. Mostly, I report to them, and wait for orders to come in."
    new "Most of what they do is shrouded in mystery. It's very seldom that I convene with the entire council. Mostly, I report to them, and wait for orders to come in.\n他们做的绝大多数事都蒙着神秘的面纱。我很少能和整个议会一起开会。大多数时候，我向他们汇报，然后等命令下来。"

    old "Actually, most of what I do is done without the specific directive of the council. I think part of my job is to take the council's instructions, which are sometimes vague, and translate them into more concrete and actionable goals."
    new "Actually, most of what I do is done without the specific directive of the council. I think part of my job is to take the council's instructions, which are sometimes vague, and translate them into more concrete and actionable goals.\n其实，我做的大部分事情，都不是在议会的具体指示下完成的。我想我工作的一部分，就是接过议会那些有时含糊不清的指示，把它们转化为更具体、可执行的目标。"

    old "Most of the direct and explicit advice I've gotten has come from people working outside the council."
    new "Most of the direct and explicit advice I've gotten has come from people working outside the council.\n我得到的大部分直接、明确的建议，都来自议会之外的人。"

    old "I am guessing that the council never formally came to you and instructed you to form an alliance with pirates."
    new "I am guessing that the council never formally came to you and instructed you to form an alliance with pirates.\n我猜，议会从来没有正式来找你，指示你去和海盗结盟。"

    old "No, that was my decision, more or less."
    new "No, that was my decision, more or less.\n没有，那或多或少是我自己的决定。"

    old "I wonder, what would the council's reaction be to such an alliance?"
    new "I wonder, what would the council's reaction be to such an alliance?\n我想知道，议会对这种联盟会作何反应？"

    old "Grimoire wants the evil of N'Mar to be put to rest. If working with pirates will get them closer to that goal, they'll do it."
    new "Grimoire wants the evil of N'Mar to be put to rest. If working with pirates will get them closer to that goal, they'll do it.\nGrimoire想让N'Mar的邪恶得到安息。如果和海盗合作能让他们离那个目标更近，他们就会这么做。"

    old "They might not be so receptive to the idea at first. They'll have to learn to like it, I suppose."
    new "They might not be so receptive to the idea at first. They'll have to learn to like it, I suppose.\n他们一开始可能不太接受这个想法。我想，他们得学着去接受。"

    old "They'll have to learn to like it?"
    new "They'll have to learn to like it?\n他们得学着去接受？"

    old "What choice do we have? Grimoire is at war with the evil of N'Mar, and in times of war you don't always get to do your favorite thing. I'm sure the council is aware of that. They're willing to do what is necessary."
    new "What choice do we have? Grimoire is at war with the evil of N'Mar, and in times of war you don't always get to do your favorite thing. I'm sure the council is aware of that. They're willing to do what is necessary.\n我们还有什么选择？Grimoire正在和N'Mar的邪恶开战，而战争时期，你并不总能去做自己喜欢的事。我相信议会明白这一点。他们愿意做必要的事。"

    old "Honestly? I'm not sure I have an answer to that question. I've never really thought about the council that much. I guess you could say I have no strong feelings one way or the other."
    new "Honestly? I'm not sure I have an answer to that question. I've never really thought about the council that much. I guess you could say I have no strong feelings one way or the other.\n老实说？我不确定自己有没有答案。我从来没怎么想过议会。我想你可以说，我对他们没有特别强烈的感受，无论好坏。"

    old "Well, it sounds like you don't have any bad things to say about them."
    new "Well, it sounds like you don't have any bad things to say about them.\n嗯，听起来你对他们没什么坏话可说。"

    old "It could also be that I don't have any good things to say about them."
    new "It could also be that I don't have any good things to say about them.\n也可能是因为我对他们没什么好话可说。"

    old "Yes, you could put it like that. But I think what it tells us most is that you interact very little with the council. Most of your time is spent outside of Grimoire, roaming around Aravorn, and occasionally reporting back to them."
    new "Yes, you could put it like that. But I think what it tells us most is that you interact very little with the council. Most of your time is spent outside of Grimoire, roaming around Aravorn, and occasionally reporting back to them.\n对，你可以这么说。但我想，这最说明的一点是，你和议会的互动很少。你大部分时间都待在Grimoire之外，在Aravorn四处奔走，偶尔才向他们汇报。"

    old "That sounds about right."
    new "That sounds about right.\n听起来差不多是这样。"

    old "In other words, you're doing a lot of work for the council, without a lot of assistance."
    new "In other words, you're doing a lot of work for the council, without a lot of assistance.\n换句话说，你在为议会做很多工作，却没什么援助。"

    old "You could also say that I'm getting to do that work without a lot of meddling."
    new "You could also say that I'm getting to do that work without a lot of meddling.\n你也可以说，我做那些工作，却没太多人指手画脚。"

    old "Yes, you could put it like that."
    new "Yes, you could put it like that.\n对，你可以这么说。"

    old "What I'm gathering from all of this is that the council holds you at arm's length, and mostly allows you to do what is necessary to achieve their goals."
    new "What I'm gathering from all of this is that the council holds you at arm's length, and mostly allows you to do what is necessary to achieve their goals.\n我从这一切里得出的结论是，议会对你保持距离，大体上放手让你去做达成他们目标所必需的事。"

    old "Which conveniently absolves them of having to dirty their hands with whatever it is that you're doing."
    new "Which conveniently absolves them of having to dirty their hands with whatever it is that you're doing.\n这样他们就方便地不必亲自动手，去沾上你正在做的那些脏活。"

    old "I think it would be fair to say that the council delegates responsibilities. There are many things that need to be done. The council makes the decision, but the task of carrying out those decisions is left to people like me."
    new "I think it would be fair to say that the council delegates responsibilities. There are many things that need to be done. The council makes the decision, but the task of carrying out those decisions is left to people like me.\n我想可以公平地说，议会是在委派责任。有很多事情需要做。议会做决定，但执行这些决定的任务，落到像我这样的人身上。"

    old "The council may declare war, but it isn't the council members who will march out on the front lines to fight it."
    new "The council may declare war, but it isn't the council members who will march out on the front lines to fight it.\n议会可以宣战，但真正开赴前线作战的，不是议员们。"

    old "True, true. The council chambers may be the mind of Grimoire, but people like you are its arms and legs."
    new "True, true. The council chambers may be the mind of Grimoire, but people like you are its arms and legs.\n没错，没错。议会大厅也许是Grimoire的大脑，但像你这样的人，是它的手臂和腿。"

    old "Tell me, [protag]. What would you say the job of the council is? What is their reason for being?"
    new "Tell me, [protag]. What would you say the job of the council is? What is their reason for being?\n告诉我，[protag]。你觉得议会的职责是什么？他们存在的理由是什么？"

    old "The council's job is to protect the people of Grimorie."
    new "The council's job is to protect the people of Grimorie.\n议会的职责是保护Grimoire的人民。"

    old "Protect the people? Protect them from whom?"
    new "Protect the people? Protect them from whom?\n保护人民？保护他们免受谁的伤害？"

    old "The blight of N'Mar, for one thing."
    new "The blight of N'Mar, for one thing.\nN'Mar的瘟疫，就是其中之一。"

    old "I mean more generally. The N'Mar vampires weren't around when the council was created."
    new "I mean more generally. The N'Mar vampires weren't around when the council was created.\n我是更笼统地问。议会成立的时候，N'Mar的吸血鬼还不存在。"

    old "They protect the people from whatever threatens them. Enemies of the human empire."
    new "They protect the people from whatever threatens them. Enemies of the human empire.\n他们保护人民，免受任何威胁。人类帝国的敌人。"

    old "And who decides what is and isn't an enemy of the human empire?"
    new "And who decides what is and isn't an enemy of the human empire?\n那么，由谁来决定什么算是、什么不算是人类帝国的敌人？"

    old "The council decides."
    new "The council decides.\n由议会决定。"

    old "So, the council's job is to carry out a responsibility, and that responsibility is decided by the council. Is that what you're saying?"
    new "So, the council's job is to carry out a responsibility, and that responsibility is decided by the council. Is that what you're saying?\n所以，议会的职责是履行一份责任，而这份责任由议会自己决定。你是这个意思吗？"

    old "I'm not sure I understand."
    new "I'm not sure I understand.\n我不太明白。"

    old "Suppose tomorrow, the council decides that you are an enemy of the human empire. Then they send someone to kill you. That's a justified use of power, is it not?"
    new "Suppose tomorrow, the council decides that you are an enemy of the human empire. Then they send someone to kill you. That's a justified use of power, is it not?\n假设明天，议会认定你是人类帝国的敌人。然后他们派人来杀你。这是对权力的正当运用，不是吗？"

    old "That's an outrageous idea. They have no reason to do such a thing."
    new "That's an outrageous idea. They have no reason to do such a thing.\n这想法太离谱了。他们没有理由这么做。"

    old "But they could, if they wanted to."
    new "But they could, if they wanted to.\n但只要他们想，他们就能。"

    old "I don't think the council would do that."
    new "I don't think the council would do that.\n我不认为议会会那么做。"

    old "How confident are you? Would you bet your life on it?"
    new "How confident are you? Would you bet your life on it?\n你有多自信？你愿意拿命去赌吗？"

    old "Well, you already are."
    new "Well, you already are.\n嗯，你已经赌上了。"

    old "But you already are."
    new "But you already are.\n可你早就已经赌上了。"

    old "Do you have a point?"
    new "Do you have a point?\n你到底想说什么？"

    old "Jasper shrugs and gives me a wry grin."
    new "Jasper shrugs and gives me a wry grin.\nJasper耸耸肩，冲我露出一丝揶揄的笑。"

    old "Me? Have a point? I'm just doing my best here to entertain you, [protag]. Don't you like philosophical discussions about the role of government?"
    new "Me? Have a point? I'm just doing my best here to entertain you, [protag]. Don't you like philosophical discussions about the role of government?\n我？想说什么？我不过是尽力逗你开心罢了，[protag]。你不喜欢关于政府角色的哲学讨论吗？"

    old "The reason the council exists is to govern the people. To tell them how to behave, and enforce the law."
    new "The reason the council exists is to govern the people. To tell them how to behave, and enforce the law.\n议会之所以存在，是为了治理人民。告诉他们如何行事，并执行法律。"

    old "The council's job is to tell people how to behave? That sounds awfully paternalistic."
    new "The council's job is to tell people how to behave? That sounds awfully paternalistic.\n议会的工作是告诉人们如何行事？这听起来可太家长式了。"

    old "The council needs to law down laws that the people obey. Don't kill your neighbor or steal from him, for example."
    new "The council needs to law down laws that the people obey. Don't kill your neighbor or steal from him, for example.\n议会需要制定人们要遵守的法律。比如，别杀你的邻居，也别偷他的东西。"

    old "I see, and if it weren't for the city rulers to tell us 'thou shalt not kill,' people would be completely unable to answer the moral question for themselves of whether murder is okay or not."
    new "I see, and if it weren't for the city rulers to tell us 'thou shalt not kill,' people would be completely unable to answer the moral question for themselves of whether murder is okay or not.\n我明白了。如果不是城里的统治者告诉我们“不可杀人”，人们就完全没法自己去判断，杀人到底对不对。"

    old "I'm not sure your sarcasm is warranted here, Jasper. The rulers create laws, but they also enforce them. One of the things that helps to keep people in line is that consequences await them if they don't."
    new "I'm not sure your sarcasm is warranted here, Jasper. The rulers create laws, but they also enforce them. One of the things that helps to keep people in line is that consequences await them if they don't.\n我不确定你的讽刺在这里合适，Jasper。统治者制定法律，但他们也执行法律。让人们守规矩的原因之一，就是如果不守，后果在等着他们。"

    old "Even if someone feels the impulse to kill, its in his best interest to let his victim be, because he doesn't want to be convicted for murder."
    new "Even if someone feels the impulse to kill, its in his best interest to let his victim be, because he doesn't want to be convicted for murder.\n即使有人起了杀心，让受害者活着也符合他的最大利益，因为他不想因谋杀被定罪。"

    old "So what you're saying is that the council needs to exist because people are evil."
    new "So what you're saying is that the council needs to exist because people are evil.\n所以你的意思是，议会必须存在，因为人是邪恶的。"

    old "Not all people, but yes, some people are evil and needs to be controlled. Even if you take an optimistic view of the world, there will always be bad apples out there. The council is there to protect us, because people aren't perfect."
    new "Not all people, but yes, some people are evil and needs to be controlled. Even if you take an optimistic view of the world, there will always be bad apples out there. The council is there to protect us, because people aren't perfect.\n不全是，但没错，有些人是邪恶的，需要被约束。即使你对世界抱乐观态度，也总会有些坏家伙存在。议会是来保护我们的，因为人并不完美。"

    old "You say the council needs to exist to protect us from people, because people aren't perfect. But the council is made up of people."
    new "You say the council needs to exist to protect us from people, because people aren't perfect. But the council is made up of people.\n你说议会必须存在，是为了保护我们不受人的伤害，因为人并不完美。但议会本身就是由人组成的。"

    old "You said that there are evil people in the world. What happens when one of those people gets onto the council and begins using its power to enact his evil?"
    new "You said that there are evil people in the world. What happens when one of those people gets onto the council and begins using its power to enact his evil?\n你说这世上有邪恶的人。当其中一个进了议会，开始利用其权力施行他的邪恶时，会怎样？"

    old "The other council members would keep him in check."
    new "The other council members would keep him in check.\n其他议员会约束他。"

    old "What if the other council members are also evil? I know you presume them not to be, but just humor the thought. Let's play out an experiment in our heads."
    new "What if the other council members are also evil? I know you presume them not to be, but just humor the thought. Let's play out an experiment in our heads.\n如果其他议员也是邪恶的呢？我知道你假定他们不是，但姑且顺着这个想法想想。让我们在脑子里做个实验。"

    old "Well, for one thing, the council isn't made up of ordinary people. The kind of people that are appointed to lead a city aren't the same kinds of people who walk its streets."
    new "Well, for one thing, the council isn't made up of ordinary people. The kind of people that are appointed to lead a city aren't the same kinds of people who walk its streets.\n嗯，首先，议会不是由普通人组成的。被任命来领导一座城市的人，跟走在这座城市街头的人不一样。"

    old "No, you're right. They're not normal people. They happen to be those who have the ability to rule through might. And we all know that power and morality go hand in hand, for there is none more immoral than the babe who has no means to defend itself."
    new "No, you're right. They're not normal people. They happen to be those who have the ability to rule through might. And we all know that power and morality go hand in hand, for there is none more immoral than the babe who has no means to defend itself.\n不，你说得对。他们不是普通人。他们恰好是那些有能力靠武力统治的人。而我们都知道，权力和道德是相伴而行的，因为没有谁比一个毫无自卫之力的婴儿更不道德了。"

    old "Again with the sarcasm."
    new "Again with the sarcasm.\n又是讽刺。"

    old "But the point stands. Might makes right, does it not?"
    new "But the point stands. Might makes right, does it not?\n但道理依然成立。强权即公理，不是吗？"

    old "Yes, might does make right. It's why we're building an army to take down the evil of N'Mar's castle. We need force to back our words up."
    new "Yes, might does make right. It's why we're building an army to take down the evil of N'Mar's castle. We need force to back our words up.\n是的，强权确实即公理。这正是我们要组建一支军队，去击垮N'Mar城堡的邪恶的原因。我们需要武力为我们的言辞撑腰。"

    old "Then we're in agreement."
    new "Then we're in agreement.\n那我们就达成一致了。"

    old "No, of course not."
    new "No, of course not.\n不，当然不是。"

    old "Riddle me this. When we go to war against the evils of N'Mar, what do we expect to win the day? What are you in the process of doing right now?"
    new "Riddle me this. When we go to war against the evils of N'Mar, what do we expect to win the day? What are you in the process of doing right now?\n我问你一个谜题。当我们去和N'Mar的邪恶开战时，我们指望靠什么赢得胜利？你现在正在做的又是什么？"

    old "We're building an army."
    new "We're building an army.\n我们在组建一支军队。"

    old "Then I think you've laid out a very compelling argument for why might does make right. You're not building an army because you believe that concentrated virtue is the key to winning this battle."
    new "Then I think you've laid out a very compelling argument for why might does make right. You're not building an army because you believe that concentrated virtue is the key to winning this battle.\n那我认为，你已经为“强权即公理”提出了一个非常有说服力的论证。你组建军队，并不是因为你相信纯粹的道德是赢得这场战斗的关键。"

    old "No, you want fighters. You want those adept with weapons and magic, those who can stab or slice or bludgeon or burn or flay those ghouls and vampires into submission."
    new "No, you want fighters. You want those adept with weapons and magic, those who can stab or slice or bludgeon or burn or flay those ghouls and vampires into submission.\n不，你要的是战士。你要的是那些精通武器和魔法的人，那些能刺、能砍、能砸、能烧，或者能把那些食尸鬼和吸血鬼打得服服帖帖的人。"

    old "So if we're in agreement that might and power is what will ultimately allow us to triumph over the evils of N'Mar, it stands to reason that any ruling government that exists in the world must have come to power through roughly the same means."
    new "So if we're in agreement that might and power is what will ultimately allow us to triumph over the evils of N'Mar, it stands to reason that any ruling government that exists in the world must have come to power through roughly the same means.\n所以，如果我们一致认为，强权和力量才是最终让我们战胜N'Mar的邪恶的东西，那么顺理成章地，世上任何一个执政的政府，都必然是靠着大致相同的手段上台的。"

    old "That's different. They need the will of the people to rule."
    new "That's different. They need the will of the people to rule.\n那不一样。他们需要人民的意志才能统治。"

    old "I thought you said that the purpose of the government was to rule the people and tell them how to behave, not the other way around."
    new "I thought you said that the purpose of the government was to rule the people and tell them how to behave, not the other way around.\n我还以为你说的是，政府的目的是统治人民、告诉他们如何行事，而不是反过来。"

    old "I think you're being obtuse."
    new "I think you're being obtuse.\n我觉得你在故意装糊涂。"

    old "You're right, I am being deliberately obtuse to make a point. I'd just like to leave you with one thought. Grimoire's council can lay down any mandate they wish."
    new "You're right, I am being deliberately obtuse to make a point. I'd just like to leave you with one thought. Grimoire's council can lay down any mandate they wish.\n你说得对，我是在故意装糊涂，好说明一个道理。我只想给你留一个念头。Grimoire议会可以颁布任何他们想要的命令。"

    old "'No elves allowed,' for example, in the event that they decide that elves are unwanted in the city. 'Kill Jasper the pirate on sight if you happen to see him' would be another example of such a mandate."
    new "'No elves allowed,' for example, in the event that they decide that elves are unwanted in the city. 'Kill Jasper the pirate on sight if you happen to see him' would be another example of such a mandate.\n比如“禁止精灵入内”，前提是他们认定精灵在这座城市不受欢迎。“要是碰巧见到海盗Jasper，就当场杀死他”，也会是这种命令的另一个例子。"

    old "Is there a bounty on your head?"
    new "Is there a bounty on your head?\n你头上挂着悬赏吗？"

    old "I'm just talking in hypotheticals, [protag]. After all, Grimoire does allow elves to dwell within its limits, even though they may be treated as second-class citizens."
    new "I'm just talking in hypotheticals, [protag]. After all, Grimoire does allow elves to dwell within its limits, even though they may be treated as second-class citizens.\n我只是在打比方，[protag]。毕竟，Grimoire确实允许精灵住在城内，尽管他们可能被当作二等公民对待。"

    old "Your point?"
    new "Your point?\n你到底想说什么？"

    old "Today, you agree with Grimoire's mandate. 'Slay the vampires,' or something to that effect. But today's mandate will not last forever. What happens when the vampires are gone?"
    new "Today, you agree with Grimoire's mandate. 'Slay the vampires,' or something to that effect. But today's mandate will not last forever. What happens when the vampires are gone?\n今天，你赞同Grimoire的命令。“斩杀吸血鬼”，诸如此类。但今天的命令不会永远有效。等吸血鬼消失了，会怎样？"

    old "You mean, what happens to me?"
    new "You mean, what happens to me?\n你是说，我会怎么样？"

    old "...maybe. The question is up to you to interpret. I don't expect an answer out of you right now."
    new "...maybe. The question is up to you to interpret. I don't expect an answer out of you right now.\n……也许吧。这个问题留给你自己去解读。我现在不指望你给出答案。"

    old "The role of the council is to represent the interests of the people of the empire."
    new "The role of the council is to represent the interests of the people of the empire.\n议会的作用是代表帝国人民的利益。"

    old "Interesting. What do you mean by that?"
    new "Interesting. What do you mean by that?\n有意思。你这话是什么意思？"

    old "Any time agreements need to be brokered between nations, it would be simply infeasible for every individual of the empire to take part in the negotiation."
    new "Any time agreements need to be brokered between nations, it would be simply infeasible for every individual of the empire to take part in the negotiation.\n任何时候，当国家之间需要斡旋达成协议，让帝国的每一个人都参与谈判，是根本不可行的。"

    old "So if an agreement needs to be made between the city of Hammerhands and the city of Grimoire, the rulers of each city meet with each other, and relay the concerns of their people to each other."
    new "So if an agreement needs to be made between the city of Hammerhands and the city of Grimoire, the rulers of each city meet with each other, and relay the concerns of their people to each other.\n所以，如果Hammerhands城和Grimoire城之间需要达成协议，两座城市的统治者就彼此会面，把各自人民关切的问题转达给对方。"

    old "That's an optimistic view of how the council works. But it does seem realistic."
    new "That's an optimistic view of how the council works. But it does seem realistic.\n这是对议会运作方式的一种乐观看法。但确实显得很现实。"

    old "How does an envoy like you fit into all of this?"
    new "How does an envoy like you fit into all of this?\n像你这样的特使，是怎么融入这一切的？"

    old "You represent the interests of the council. The council represents the interests of the people."
    new "You represent the interests of the council. The council represents the interests of the people.\n你代表议会的利益。议会代表人民的利益。"

    old "Yes, and?"
    new "Yes, and?\n是，然后呢？"

    old "In a way, the council is a middleman. In reality, negotiations between two nations would probably be done through diplomatic channels. I cannot envision a scenario in which every member of the Grimoire council would travel to Hammerhands to negotiate, nor could I envision the reverse scenario."
    new "In a way, the council is a middleman. In reality, negotiations between two nations would probably be done through diplomatic channels. I cannot envision a scenario in which every member of the Grimoire council would travel to Hammerhands to negotiate, nor could I envision the reverse scenario.\n从某种程度上说，议会是个中间人。现实中，两国之间的谈判大概会通过外交渠道进行。我无法想象这样的场景：Grimoire议会的每个成员都跑到Hammerhands去谈判，反过来也一样无法想象。"

    old "I suppose that's true."
    new "I suppose that's true.\n我想那倒是真的。"

    old "The difference between you and the council is that the council's mission, to represent the people, is immutable. The people will always be in need of representation. You, on the other hand, have a mission that is much more temporary."
    new "The difference between you and the council is that the council's mission, to represent the people, is immutable. The people will always be in need of representation. You, on the other hand, have a mission that is much more temporary.\n你和议会的区别在于，议会的使命——代表人民——是不可改变的。人民永远需要代表。而你，你的使命要临时得多。"

    old "One of these days, either N'Mar or the human empire will fall, and you will have outlived your usefulness."
    new "One of these days, either N'Mar or the human empire will fall, and you will have outlived your usefulness.\n总有一天，要么N'Mar，要么人类帝国会倒下，而到那时，你的用处就到头了。"

    old "This isn't the first time you've expressed this idea."
    new "This isn't the first time you've expressed this idea.\n这不是你第一次表达这个想法了。"

    old "Is it? Well, shame on me for failing to give you a new question to think on today."
    new "Is it? Well, shame on me for failing to give you a new question to think on today.\n是吗？嗯，今天没能给你个新问题去琢磨，真是我的不是。"

    old "Jasper, you seem to have somewhat cynical views regarding the council."
    new "Jasper, you seem to have somewhat cynical views regarding the council.\nJasper，你对议会似乎抱着相当愤世嫉俗的看法。"

    old "I guess my view is that the council is only as good as the people who make it up. That's the bigger question, I think. How many of them do you know personally? How many do you think you could vouch for?"
    new "I guess my view is that the council is only as good as the people who make it up. That's the bigger question, I think. How many of them do you know personally? How many do you think you could vouch for?\n我想我的看法是，议会的好坏，只取决于组成它的人。这才是更大的问题，我觉得。他们当中你认识几个？你觉得你能为几个人担保？"

    old "There's only one that I really know. His name is Apolimesho."
    new "There's only one that I really know. His name is Apolimesho.\n我真正认识的只有一个。他叫Apolimesho。"

    old "Apolimesho is on the council?"
    new "Apolimesho is on the council?\nApolimesho在议会里？"

    old "Yes. You say that like you've met him before."
    new "Yes. You say that like you've met him before.\n是的。你这话听起来，好像你以前见过他。"

    old "We may have rubbed shoulders once or twice. What's your relationship with Apolimesho?"
    new "We may have rubbed shoulders once or twice. What's your relationship with Apolimesho?\n我们也许打过一两次照面。你和Apolimesho是什么关系？"

    old "I communicate with him lot in an unofficial capacity. He has, on occasion, offered me advice and guidance on my various escapades. To be honest, I get the impression that has some skepticism for the council as a whole, though not nearly to the extent that you seem to."
    new "I communicate with him lot in an unofficial capacity. He has, on occasion, offered me advice and guidance on my various escapades. To be honest, I get the impression that has some skepticism for the council as a whole, though not nearly to the extent that you seem to.\n我经常以非官方的身份跟他沟通。有时，他会就我的各种冒险行动给我建议和指点。说实话，我得到的印象是，他对整个议会有些怀疑，尽管远没有你表现出的那么强烈。"

    old "I'd like to meet with Apolimesho some time. Do you think you could arrange that?"
    new "I'd like to meet with Apolimesho some time. Do you think you could arrange that?\n我想找个时间见见Apolimesho。你觉得你能安排一下吗？"

    old "Saying hello to an old friend?"
    new "Saying hello to an old friend?\n跟老朋友打个招呼？"

    old "Something like that."
    new "Something like that.\n差不多吧。"

    old "Well, I'll see what I can do."
    new "Well, I'll see what I can do.\n好，我看看能怎么办。"

    old "I managed to arrange a meeting with Apolimesho, and I'm bringing Jasper with me today. We head to Apolimesho's chambers."
    new "I managed to arrange a meeting with Apolimesho, and I'm bringing Jasper with me today. We head to Apolimesho's chambers.\n我设法安排了一次与Apolimesho的会面，今天我把Jasper也带来了。我们前往Apolimesho的房间。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. What brings you here today?"
    new "Ah, [protag]. What brings you here today?\n啊，[protag]。今天什么风把你吹来了？"

    old "Hello, Apolimesho. I've brought a friend."
    new "Hello, Apolimesho. I've brought a friend.\n你好，Apolimesho。我带了个朋友来。"

    old "Hello, Apolimesho. It's been awhile."
    new "Hello, Apolimesho. It's been awhile.\n你好，Apolimesho。好久不见。"

    old "Jasper and Apolimesho stare at each other, and moments pass. I feel like I've been forgotten."
    new "Jasper and Apolimesho stare at each other, and moments pass. I feel like I've been forgotten.\nJasper和Apolimesho互相凝视着，好一会儿过去。我觉得自己像是被遗忘了。"

    old "Zaccheus. What brings you here?"
    new "Zaccheus. What brings you here?\nZaccheus。什么风把你吹来了？"

    old "Our mutual acquaintance brought me here. Oh, and I'm called Jasper now."
    new "Our mutual acquaintance brought me here. Oh, and I'm called Jasper now.\n是我们共同的熟人带我来的。哦，对了，我现在叫Jasper。"

    old "Jasper. Is that a name you gave yourself?"
    new "Jasper. Is that a name you gave yourself?\nJasper。这是你自己给自己起的名字吗？"

    old "It is. I think it fits me better now. New man, new name. Though, Zaccheus wasn't such a bad name either."
    new "It is. I think it fits me better now. New man, new name. Though, Zaccheus wasn't such a bad name either.\n是的。我觉得它现在更适合我。新人，新名字。不过，Zaccheus这名字也不赖。"

    old "My mother gave me that name. Do you know what it means? 'Innocent.' What a perfect name for a young and naive boy."
    new "My mother gave me that name. Do you know what it means? 'Innocent.' What a perfect name for a young and naive boy.\n那名字是我母亲起的。你知道它什么意思吗？“无辜”。对一个年轻天真的男孩来说，真是个好名字。"

    old "Jasper, well, that means 'treasurer,' or so I'm told. A bit ironic, considering my new profession."
    new "Jasper, well, that means 'treasurer,' or so I'm told. A bit ironic, considering my new profession.\nJasper嘛，意思是“司库”，至少别人是这么告诉我的。考虑到我的新职业，有点讽刺。"

    old "Your new profession?"
    new "Your new profession?\n你的新职业？"

    old "Ah, [protag] hasn't told you? I'm a pirate now. You know, I used to hate the water. But then, I also used to love the council, so that's two things that have changed about me, probably for the better."
    new "Ah, [protag] hasn't told you? I'm a pirate now. You know, I used to hate the water. But then, I also used to love the council, so that's two things that have changed about me, probably for the better.\n啊，[protag]没告诉你吗？我现在是个海盗了。你知道吗，我以前讨厌水。不过，我以前也热爱议会，所以我已经有两样东西变了，多半是越变越好。"

    old "I never intended for things to happen as they did, Zaccheus."
    new "I never intended for things to happen as they did, Zaccheus.\n我从没想过事情会变成那样，Zaccheus。"

    old "I'm sure of that. You were just as young and naive as I was. Well, not quite so young, but an idealist nonetheless."
    new "I'm sure of that. You were just as young and naive as I was. Well, not quite so young, but an idealist nonetheless.\n我相信。你当年跟我一样年轻天真。嗯，没那么年轻，但终究是个理想主义者。"

    old "Things are different now."
    new "Things are different now.\n现在情况不同了。"

    old "I'm sure of it, seeing you here now."
    new "I'm sure of it, seeing you here now.\n如今在这里见到你，我确信如此。"

    old "I suppose you've come to give me a piece of your mind."
    new "I suppose you've come to give me a piece of your mind.\n我想，你是来数落我的吧。"

    old "Indeed I have. Apolimesho, there's something that I never got to tell you before I left."
    new "Indeed I have. Apolimesho, there's something that I never got to tell you before I left.\n确实。Apolimesho，有些事，我离开之前一直没来得及告诉你。"

    old "I forgive you. I accept my part in all of this. I can see you didn't fall victim to the same fate I did, and if I had been a better man, today I might be standing where you are right now."
    new "I forgive you. I accept my part in all of this. I can see you didn't fall victim to the same fate I did, and if I had been a better man, today I might be standing where you are right now.\n我原谅你。我接受自己在这整件事里的角色。我看得出，你没有落得和我一样的下场。如果我当年是个更好的人，今天站在你这个位置的，也许就是我。"

    old "I was just the right mix of willing, trusting, and stupid. Willing to do whatever they sent me out for, stupid enough to admit it when pulled before a committee, and trusting enough to assume that there would be a reward waiting for me when the dust settled."
    new "I was just the right mix of willing, trusting, and stupid. Willing to do whatever they sent me out for, stupid enough to admit it when pulled before a committee, and trusting enough to assume that there would be a reward waiting for me when the dust settled.\n我不过是自愿、轻信和愚蠢的正确组合。愿意去做他们派我去的任何事，被拉到委员会面前时又蠢到照实承认，还天真到以为尘埃落定后会有奖赏等着我。"

    old "I just have one request. [protag] here. Look out for [himher], would you? I'd hate to see [himher] fall victim to the same fate."
    new "I just have one request. [protag] here. Look out for [himher], would you? I'd hate to see [himher] fall victim to the same fate.\n我只有一个请求。这位是[protag]。替我照看[himher]，好吗？我不想看到[himher]落得和我一样的下场。"

    old "Apolimesho turns to me with a look of hesitation."
    new "Apolimesho turns to me with a look of hesitation.\nApolimesho转向我，一脸犹豫。"

    old "I feel like you want some answers. I say this assuming Zac—Jasper hasn't already told you, which he hasn't, because he's charitable sort of man to allow others to tell their own half of the story. I assume that's why he brought you here as well."
    new "I feel like you want some answers. I say this assuming Zac—Jasper hasn't already told you, which he hasn't, because he's charitable sort of man to allow others to tell their own half of the story. I assume that's why he brought you here as well.\n我觉得你想要些答案。我这么说，是假定Zac——Jasper还没告诉过你，而他确实没有，因为他是个好心人，愿意让别人讲自己那半边故事。我想，这也是他把你带到这儿来的原因。"

    old "What exactly happened between you and Jasper?"
    new "What exactly happened between you and Jasper?\n你和Jasper之间到底发生了什么？"

    old "[protag], you may feel like something of an anomaly. You were quickly deputized in an hour of need. The council needed someone to exterminate and expunge the threat of N'Mar, you were conveniently within arm's reach, and thus you were recruited for the job."
    new "[protag], you may feel like something of an anomaly. You were quickly deputized in an hour of need. The council needed someone to exterminate and expunge the threat of N'Mar, you were conveniently within arm's reach, and thus you were recruited for the job.\n[protag]，你也许会觉得自己有点像个异数。你是在危急关头被迅速任命的。议会需要有人去剿灭、清除N'Mar的威胁，你恰好近在咫尺，于是你被招募来做这份差事。"

    old "The empire of man has numerous soldiers who are loyal to Grimoire. Yet you were chosen for the job. Part of this was due to your qualifications—and mostly it was because you are outside of the system. You don't depend on the council for support. You make many of your own decisions."
    new "The empire of man has numerous soldiers who are loyal to Grimoire. Yet you were chosen for the job. Part of this was due to your qualifications—and mostly it was because you are outside of the system. You don't depend on the council for support. You make many of your own decisions.\n人类帝国有无数忠于Grimoire的士兵。然而，被选中的人是你。这一部分是因为你的资质——但更主要是因为，你在体制之外。你不依赖议会的支持。你的许多决定都由自己做出。"

    old "This confers many advantages to the council. It allows you to do what needs to be done, without having to have every one of your actions and decisions ratified by committee. In times of emergency, we don't have time for bureaucracy."
    new "This confers many advantages to the council. It allows you to do what needs to be done, without having to have every one of your actions and decisions ratified by committee. In times of emergency, we don't have time for bureaucracy.\n这给议会带来了许多好处。它让你去做该做的事，而不必让你的每个行动、每个决定都经委员会批准。紧急关头，我们没有时间搞官僚程序。"

    old "This isn't the first time this has happened. It's rare that the need for such deputizing to occur comes up, but I've seen it happen once before. In fact, I was one such person, plucked in a moment of need to run missions for the empire. So was your friend here."
    new "This isn't the first time this has happened. It's rare that the need for such deputizing to occur comes up, but I've seen it happen once before. In fact, I was one such person, plucked in a moment of need to run missions for the empire. So was your friend here.\n这并非第一次发生这种事。需要这样任命的情况很少出现，但我以前见过一次。事实上，我就是那样一个人，在需要时被挑出来为帝国执行任务。你这位朋友也是。"

    old "Yes, Apolimesho and I used to be colleagues. Surprised?"
    new "Yes, Apolimesho and I used to be colleagues. Surprised?\n是的，Apolimesho和我以前是同事。意外吗？"

    old "I'm not sure if I should be. For a simple pirate, you seemed to know a lot about the operations of the council. I assumed you had some kind of insider information, maybe as a spy."
    new "I'm not sure if I should be. For a simple pirate, you seemed to know a lot about the operations of the council. I assumed you had some kind of insider information, maybe as a spy.\n我不确定该不该意外。一个普通的海盗，居然对议会的运作了解那么多。我还以为你有什么内幕消息，也许是当间谍。"

    old "As a matter of fact, I was a spy. But not in the way that you might think."
    new "As a matter of fact, I was a spy. But not in the way that you might think.\n事实上，我确实是个间谍。但可能不是你想的那种。"

    old "Zaccheus—sorry, Jasper—did not spy on the human empire. Quite the opposite—he did spying on the empire's behalf. He infiltrated rival nations and provided information back to Grimoire's council."
    new "Zaccheus—sorry, Jasper—did not spy on the human empire. Quite the opposite—he did spying on the empire's behalf. He infiltrated rival nations and provided information back to Grimoire's council.\nZaccheus——抱歉，Jasper——并没有监视人类帝国。恰恰相反，他替帝国做间谍活动。他潜入敌国，把情报传回Grimoire议会。"

    old "What about you, Apolimesho?"
    new "What about you, Apolimesho?\n那你呢，Apolimesho？"

    old "I wasn't a spy. My duties were much more domestic in nature. But the two of us were quite close. There's a fine line between the man who intercepts letters and communications, and the people who process that information."
    new "I wasn't a spy. My duties were much more domestic in nature. But the two of us were quite close. There's a fine line between the man who intercepts letters and communications, and the people who process that information.\n我不是间谍。我的职责更偏国内。但我们俩关系相当密切。拦截信件和通讯的人，与处理这些情报的人之间，只有一线之隔。"

    old "Before, I said there were advantages to the council, having someone like you or Jasper involved, as an outsider doing their bidding. You can work at an expedited pace. You can do things with an efficiency that the council might not be able to manage. And you can do things in a manner that they might not approve of—just so long as you have the sense to keep it secret."
    new "Before, I said there were advantages to the council, having someone like you or Jasper involved, as an outsider doing their bidding. You can work at an expedited pace. You can do things with an efficiency that the council might not be able to manage. And you can do things in a manner that they might not approve of—just so long as you have the sense to keep it secret.\n之前我说过，有像你或Jasper这样的人参与其中，对议会有好处——以一个外人的身份替他们办事。你可以加快工作速度。你可以高效地做议会可能办不到的事。你还可以以他们可能不赞成的方式办事——只要你有心保密。"

    old "The icing on the cake is that, with all you do for the empire, you're operating under your own jurisdiction. Your decisions aren't checked by the council. That's convenient for you—and it's convenient for them. It means that they can disavow any action you take."
    new "The icing on the cake is that, with all you do for the empire, you're operating under your own jurisdiction. Your decisions aren't checked by the council. That's convenient for you—and it's convenient for them. It means that they can disavow any action you take.\n锦上添花的是，你为帝国所做的一切，都是在自己的管辖下运作的。你的决定不受议会审核。这对你方便，对他们也方便。这意味着，他们可以否认你采取的任何行动。"

    old "And sometimes, disavowing an action means disavowing a person."
    new "And sometimes, disavowing an action means disavowing a person.\n而有时候，否认一个行动，就意味着否认一个人。"

    old "Do you understand now, [protag]? How it is that I became what I am today?"
    new "Do you understand now, [protag]? How it is that I became what I am today?\n你现在明白了吗，[protag]？我是怎么变成今天这样的？"

    old "I think I have a good idea."
    new "I think I have a good idea.\n我想我大致明白了。"

    old "I don't mean for either of you to feel any pity for me or what happened to me. The truth is, I'm quite happy where things eventually led me. The life of a seafaring man fits me much better. Living in exile isn't so bad, and considering that I was able to enter these chambers unmolested, that exile is virtually meaningless at this point."
    new "I don't mean for either of you to feel any pity for me or what happened to me. The truth is, I'm quite happy where things eventually led me. The life of a seafaring man fits me much better. Living in exile isn't so bad, and considering that I was able to enter these chambers unmolested, that exile is virtually meaningless at this point.\n我并不想让你们任何一个同情我，或者同情我的遭遇。事实是，我很满意事情最终走到的地方。海上生活更适合我。流亡也没那么糟，考虑到我能不受打扰地走进这间议事厅，那流亡如今已经几乎毫无意义了。"

    old "But you might not be the same. [protag], I made the mistake of assuming that by working for the empire, I was currying favor with them. In my mind, I was putting coins into a bank account, one that would eventually allow me to buy favors from the council. I thought one day I would be rewarded by them."
    new "But you might not be the same. [protag], I made the mistake of assuming that by working for the empire, I was currying favor with them. In my mind, I was putting coins into a bank account, one that would eventually allow me to buy favors from the council. I thought one day I would be rewarded by them.\n但你也许不一样。[protag]，我犯了个错误，以为为帝国工作就是在讨好他们。在我心里，我像是在往一个银行账户里存硬币，终有一天能让我从议会那里换来好处。我以为有一天会得到他们的回报。"

    old "Things didn't turn out quite as I expected. As I said, I'm not in a bad place right now, but I don't want you to fall victim to the same fate I did."
    new "Things didn't turn out quite as I expected. As I said, I'm not in a bad place right now, but I don't want you to fall victim to the same fate I did.\n事情并没有完全如我预期。正如我所说，我现在的处境并不差，但我不想让你落得和我一样的下场。"

    old "You've done a good job of making friends with different people around Aravorn. I'm sure the council is quite happy about that. But there may come a day when you find yourself making enemies, rather than friends, quite possibly through no fault of your own. And if Grimoire's council believes that have more to gain than lose by disavowing you, they're likely to do it."
    new "You've done a good job of making friends with different people around Aravorn. I'm sure the council is quite happy about that. But there may come a day when you find yourself making enemies, rather than friends, quite possibly through no fault of your own. And if Grimoire's council believes that have more to gain than lose by disavowing you, they're likely to do it.\n你在Aravorn四处结交了不少朋友，干得很漂亮。我相信议会对此很满意。但也许有一天，你会发现自己树敌，而不是交友，而且很可能并非你的过错。如果Grimoire议会认为，否认你对他们利大于弊，他们很可能会这么做。"

    old "I appreciate your words of advice, Jasper. But I'm not concerned about falling victim to the same fate you did."
    new "I appreciate your words of advice, Jasper. But I'm not concerned about falling victim to the same fate you did.\n我感激你的忠告，Jasper。但我不担心会落得和你一样的下场。"

    old "You told me that you spent all of your time working for Grimoire's council, hoping to curry favor with them. You had built up an imagined trove of favors, and you never got to cash those in. When the council disavowed you, it must have seemed like the ultimate betrayal."
    new "You told me that you spent all of your time working for Grimoire's council, hoping to curry favor with them. You had built up an imagined trove of favors, and you never got to cash those in. When the council disavowed you, it must have seemed like the ultimate betrayal.\n你告诉过我，你把所有时间都花在为Grimoire议会工作上，指望讨好他们。你攒下了一堆想象中的恩情，却从没机会兑现。当议会否认你时，那一定像是终极的背叛。"

    old "I'm a bit different. In all of my dealings on behalf of the council, I've built up favor with many people. As you said, I've made friends around Aravorn. They're friends of Grimoire. But they're also friends of mine. I've earned personal loyalties. Perhaps you're among them."
    new "I'm a bit different. In all of my dealings on behalf of the council, I've built up favor with many people. As you said, I've made friends around Aravorn. They're friends of Grimoire. But they're also friends of mine. I've earned personal loyalties. Perhaps you're among them.\n我有点不同。在我代表议会的所有往来中，我赢得了许多人的好感。正如你所说，我在Aravorn四处结交了朋友。他们是Grimoire的朋友，但也是我的朋友。我赢得了私人的忠诚。也许你也是其中之一。"

    old "Even if, one day, one of them decides to betray me, even if I never get to cash in the favors that I have been earning, even if I am one day exiled from the empire of man, my efforts will not have been for naught."
    new "Even if, one day, one of them decides to betray me, even if I never get to cash in the favors that I have been earning, even if I am one day exiled from the empire of man, my efforts will not have been for naught.\n即便有一天，他们中的某个决定背叛我，即便我永远没机会兑现我积攒的那些恩情，即便有一天我被逐出人类帝国，我的努力也不会白费。"

    old "The council recruited me in part because I am a wanderer. And I believe that, should my relationship with them end, I will resume being a wanderer. I don't think it's such a bad existence."
    new "The council recruited me in part because I am a wanderer. And I believe that, should my relationship with them end, I will resume being a wanderer. I don't think it's such a bad existence.\n议会招募我，部分原因是因为我是个流浪者。而我相信，倘若我和他们的关系终结，我会重新做回流浪者。我觉得那也不失为一种不错的人生。"

    old "I'm glad to hear that you have a reasonable view of things. I think that's all I wanted. When I look at you, I see certain aspects of myself. I just wanted to make sure you didn't experience the same sense of betrayal I did."
    new "I'm glad to hear that you have a reasonable view of things. I think that's all I wanted. When I look at you, I see certain aspects of myself. I just wanted to make sure you didn't experience the same sense of betrayal I did.\n很高兴你对事情有清醒的看法。我想，我要的就是这个。看着你，我看到了自己的某些影子。我只想确保，你不会经历我经历过的那种背叛感。"

    old "Looking at what happened to me, it can be easy to draw a pessimistic conclusion about the council and the way they operate, but the truth is that most people who do right by the council find themselves rewarded for it. I present my story as a cautionary tale, but also understand that I am quite a rarity."
    new "Looking at what happened to me, it can be easy to draw a pessimistic conclusion about the council and the way they operate, but the truth is that most people who do right by the council find themselves rewarded for it. I present my story as a cautionary tale, but also understand that I am quite a rarity.\n看看发生在我身上的事，很容易对议会及其运作方式得出悲观的结论，但事实是，大多数对议会尽心尽力的人，都会因此得到回报。我把我的故事当作一个警示来讲述，但也请明白，我是个相当罕见的例外。"

    old "Who knows. If you play your cards right, one day you might find yourself like Apolimesho here, with a seat of your own in the council chambers. Wouldn't that be fun."
    new "Who knows. If you play your cards right, one day you might find yourself like Apolimesho here, with a seat of your own in the council chambers. Wouldn't that be fun.\n谁知道呢。如果你牌打得好，总有一天，你会发现自己像这里的Apolimesho一样，在议会大厅里拥有自己的席位。那岂不是很有趣。"

    old "I'm not sure I made off any better."
    new "I'm not sure I made off any better.\n我不确定我的下场有更好。"

    old "Ha! Maybe I'm the lucky one after all. You're the one who has to deal with that group of politicians, day in and day out. Meanwhile I'm about gallivanting on the open seas."
    new "Ha! Maybe I'm the lucky one after all. You're the one who has to deal with that group of politicians, day in and day out. Meanwhile I'm about gallivanting on the open seas.\n哈！也许到头来我才是幸运的那个。日复一日跟那帮政客打交道的可是你。而我，正在公海上逍遥自在。"

    old "I'm glad to see you've taken everything in stride."
    new "I'm glad to see you've taken everything in stride.\n很高兴看到你把一切都坦然接受了。"

    old "No hard feelings, Apolimesho. I mean that completely."
    new "No hard feelings, Apolimesho. I mean that completely.\n没有怨气，Apolimesho。我是说真的。"

    old "[protag], I hope bringing my story into the open hasn't given you any reason to distrust Apolimesho. As long as I've known him, he's been a completely forthright and generous person. Just make sure that you don't forget that taking care of yourself should be your own responsibility, first and foremost."
    new "[protag], I hope bringing my story into the open hasn't given you any reason to distrust Apolimesho. As long as I've known him, he's been a completely forthright and generous person. Just make sure that you don't forget that taking care of yourself should be your own responsibility, first and foremost.\n[protag]，我希望把我的故事摊开来讲，没有让你对Apolimesho产生任何不信任的理由。自我认识他以来，他一直是个完全坦诚而慷慨的人。只是别忘了，照顾好自己，应该首先是你自己的责任。"

    old "Don't worry, Jasper. I won't forget."
    new "Don't worry, Jasper. I won't forget.\n别担心，Jasper。我不会忘的。"

    old "I find Jasper at the docks, sitting on the pier and admiring the sunset."
    new "I find Jasper at the docks, sitting on the pier and admiring the sunset.\n我在码头找到Jasper，他坐在栈桥上，欣赏着夕阳。"

    old "My favorite pirate."
    new "My favorite pirate.\n我最喜欢的海盗。"

    old "Jasper chuckles and turns his head to face me."
    new "Jasper chuckles and turns his head to face me.\nJasper轻笑着，转过头来面对我。"

    old "I'd be upset if I wasn't. It's good to see you, [protag]. Can I assume that you were lured in by the splendid sunset on display too?"
    new "I'd be upset if I wasn't. It's good to see you, [protag]. Can I assume that you were lured in by the splendid sunset on display too?\n要不是这样，我可要不高兴了。见到你真好，[protag]。我能不能假设，你也是被眼前这绚丽的日落吸引来的？"

    old "Ah, no. Though, now that you mention it, I must admit that it's quite a sight."
    new "Ah, no. Though, now that you mention it, I must admit that it's quite a sight.\n啊，不是。不过，既然你提起来，我得承认，这景色确实很美。"

    old "Come now, don't be shy. Take a seat next to me. We can enjoy the sunset and talk business at the same time."
    new "Come now, don't be shy. Take a seat next to me. We can enjoy the sunset and talk business at the same time.\n别害羞。来，坐我旁边。我们可以一边欣赏日落，一边谈正事。"

    old "Fair enough."
    new "Fair enough.\n好说。"

    old "I take a seat next to him as Jasper's gaze returns to the sunset before us. He keeps his eyes focused on the horizon, seemingly hypnotized by the light playing on the water's surface."
    new "I take a seat next to him as Jasper's gaze returns to the sunset before us. He keeps his eyes focused on the horizon, seemingly hypnotized by the light playing on the water's surface.\n我在他身旁坐下，Jasper的目光又回到我们眼前的落日上。他一直注视着地平线，似乎被水面荡漾的光迷住了。"

    old "What did you want to ask me?"
    new "What did you want to ask me?\n你想问我什么？"

    old "I was wondering about your guns."
    new "I was wondering about your guns.\n我在想你的枪。"

    old "Ah, yes, my little friends. What would you like to know?"
    new "Ah, yes, my little friends. What would you like to know?\n啊，是的，我的小伙伴们。你想知道什么？"

    old "It's very unusual to see someone fight with them. We have spellscasters, strong fighters, healers..."
    new "It's very unusual to see someone fight with them. We have spellscasters, strong fighters, healers...\n看到有人用它们作战，实在很罕见。我们有施法者、强壮的战士、治疗师……"

    old "Kusho mostly uses a bow. That's not too different from my guns."
    new "Kusho mostly uses a bow. That's not too different from my guns.\nKusho主要用弓。那跟我的枪差别也不大。"

    old "Personally, I wouldn't want to find myself in the heat of battle without ammunition."
    new "Personally, I wouldn't want to find myself in the heat of battle without ammunition.\n就我个人而言，我可不想在激战正酣时发现自己没有弹药。"

    old "Well, first off, I'm not restricted to using my guns exclusively. I can also fight with a saber if the occasion calls for it."
    new "Well, first off, I'm not restricted to using my guns exclusively. I can also fight with a saber if the occasion calls for it.\n嗯，首先，我并不局限于只用枪。如果情况需要，我也可以用军刀作战。"

    old "I admit that you're right about guns being slower than arrows. However, I usually only need one bullet to kill an enemy."
    new "I admit that you're right about guns being slower than arrows. However, I usually only need one bullet to kill an enemy.\n我承认你说得对，枪比箭慢。不过，我通常只需要一发子弹就能杀死敌人。"

    old "You can't say the same for arrows. It's much harder to kill an enemy with them too, especially if your enemy is well armored."
    new "You can't say the same for arrows. It's much harder to kill an enemy with them too, especially if your enemy is well armored.\n箭可做不到这一点。用箭杀人也要难得多，尤其是当你的敌人身披重甲的时候。"

    old "Yes, that much is true."
    new "Yes, that much is true.\n是的，那倒是真的。"

    old "Guns may take awhile to reload, but hey also do much more damage. I guess it sort of evens out."
    new "Guns may take awhile to reload, but hey also do much more damage. I guess it sort of evens out.\n枪装弹可能要花点时间，但造成的伤害也大得多。我想这算是扯平了。"

    old "Exactly. Also, try piercing plate mail with an arrow. You're not going to get very far. A bullet on the other hand..."
    new "Exactly. Also, try piercing plate mail with an arrow. You're not going to get very far. A bullet on the other hand...\n没错。还有，试试用箭射穿板甲。你根本走不了多远。反过来，一颗子弹……"

    old "Jasper grins."
    new "Jasper grins.\nJasper咧嘴一笑。"

    old "And you haven't even seen all the types of guns around."
    new "And you haven't even seen all the types of guns around.\n而且你还没见过世上的各种枪呢。"

    old "This old flintlock... I have a certain affinity for it, but it's not the best gun you can get nowadays."
    new "This old flintlock... I have a certain affinity for it, but it's not the best gun you can get nowadays.\n这把老式燧发枪……我对它有种特别的感情，但它算不上如今你能弄到的最好的枪。"

    old "There are all sorts of guns and rifles that have peculiar features."
    new "There are all sorts of guns and rifles that have peculiar features.\n各种枪和步枪都有各自的独特之处。"

    old "For example, there are rifles that shoot several bullets at once, dealing damage to an area in front of you."
    new "For example, there are rifles that shoot several bullets at once, dealing damage to an area in front of you.\n比如，有些步枪能一次射出多发子弹，对你面前的区域造成伤害。"

    old "And then there are guns with multiple barrels that can fire repeatedly, solving the problem you mentioned earlier."
    new "And then there are guns with multiple barrels that can fire repeatedly, solving the problem you mentioned earlier.\n还有多管枪，可以连续射击，正好解决你刚才提到的问题。"

    old "That does sound impressive. I'm guessing they're very difficult to procure though. Expensive too, no doubt."
    new "That does sound impressive. I'm guessing they're very difficult to procure though. Expensive too, no doubt.\n听起来确实厉害。不过我猜，它们很难弄到手。而且毫无疑问，也很昂贵。"

    old "Oh, yes. Expensive, rare, and difficult to find. Gunsmiths aren't exactly common here in Issanis either. The best ones tend to be located in Zoltar."
    new "Oh, yes. Expensive, rare, and difficult to find. Gunsmiths aren't exactly common here in Issanis either. The best ones tend to be located in Zoltar.\n哦，是的。昂贵、稀有，还难找。枪匠在Issanis这边也不常见。最好的枪匠多半在Zoltar。"

    old "Hmm. I see."
    new "Hmm. I see.\n嗯。原来如此。"

    old "You know... if I have the time, I'd like to accompany you and try to find one of these special guns."
    new "You know... if I have the time, I'd like to accompany you and try to find one of these special guns.\n你知道吗……如果我有时间，我想陪你去试试找一把这种特殊的枪。"

    old "That sounds like a good idea. I would be even more effective in battle with a better set of weapons."
    new "That sounds like a good idea. I would be even more effective in battle with a better set of weapons.\n听起来是个好主意。有了更好的武器，我在战斗中会更有效。"

    old "And we need any advantage we can get."
    new "And we need any advantage we can get.\n而且，任何优势我们都需要。"

    old "It certainly wouldn't hurt."
    new "It certainly wouldn't hurt.\n当然没有坏处。"

    old "I get up from my seated position and take one last look at the sunset."
    new "I get up from my seated position and take one last look at the sunset.\n我从坐的位置站起身，最后看了一眼落日。"

    old "I take it that it's time for you to get going?"
    new "I take it that it's time for you to get going?\n我猜，你是该走了？"

    old "Yes. It was nice watching the sunset with you for a bit though, Jasper."
    new "Yes. It was nice watching the sunset with you for a bit though, Jasper.\n是的。不过能和你一起看会儿日落，真好，Jasper。"

    old "Anytime, [protag]."
    new "Anytime, [protag].\n随时欢迎，[protag]。"

    old "We'll talk again soon."
    new "We'll talk again soon.\n我们很快再聊。"

    old "I find Jasper at the docks, leaning over some crates and speaking with a small group of other people. A few of them are dressed similarly to Jasper. I suspect those ones might be pirates like him. Some of the other members of the group are dressed differently though. Their clothes are more elegant. Merchants or nobles maybe? I wonder what they're talking about."
    new "I find Jasper at the docks, leaning over some crates and speaking with a small group of other people. A few of them are dressed similarly to Jasper. I suspect those ones might be pirates like him. Some of the other members of the group are dressed differently though. Their clothes are more elegant. Merchants or nobles maybe? I wonder what they're talking about.\n我在码头找到Jasper，他靠在几个板条箱上，正和一小群人说话。其中有几个穿得和Jasper很像。我猜那些可能是像他一样的海盗。不过，队伍里另一些人穿着不同。他们的衣服更讲究。商人或者贵族？我不知道他们在谈什么。"

    old "I wait for a few minutes and eventually they all clear away leaving Jasper by himself. With nobody left to block his vision, he catches sight of me and then waves me over."
    new "I wait for a few minutes and eventually they all clear away leaving Jasper by himself. With nobody left to block his vision, he catches sight of me and then waves me over.\n我等了几分钟，最后他们都散去了，只剩Jasper一个人。没有谁挡着他的视线后，他看到了我，然后招手让我过去。"

    old "So, Jasper, who were those people? Is there something going on that I should know about?"
    new "So, Jasper, who were those people? Is there something going on that I should know about?\n那么，Jasper，那些人是谁？有什么我该知道的事吗？"

    old "Actually, yes. [protag], do you remember awhile back when we discussed the usefulness of guns in battle? And how you mentioned the possibilty of helping me retrieve a more powerful gun?"
    new "Actually, yes. [protag], do you remember awhile back when we discussed the usefulness of guns in battle? And how you mentioned the possibilty of helping me retrieve a more powerful gun?\n其实，有。[protag]，你还记得前阵子我们讨论过枪在战斗中的用处吗？还有你提到，可能帮我弄一把更厉害的枪？"

    old "Yes. I do seem to recall something like that. Why? Have you found a viable lead?"
    new "Yes. I do seem to recall something like that. Why? Have you found a viable lead?\n是的。我好像记得有这回事。怎么？你找到靠谱的线索了？"

    old "That's exactly what I've found! The people I were talking to just now have lent me their ship, The Esmeralda, in exchange for any extra guns or gold I might find. Here, come look at this."
    new "That's exactly what I've found! The people I were talking to just now have lent me their ship, The Esmeralda, in exchange for any extra guns or gold I might find. Here, come look at this.\n正是我找到的！刚才跟我说话的那些人，把他们的船The Esmeralda借给了我，作为交换，我把找到的任何多余的枪或黄金给他们。来，看看这个。"

    old "Jasper pulls out a rough looking map and flattens it on top of one of the crates. It looks old and I'm not sure how reliable it is, but Jasper seems to trust it since he starts pointing to a couple of spots with his finger and naming locations."
    new "Jasper pulls out a rough looking map and flattens it on top of one of the crates. It looks old and I'm not sure how reliable it is, but Jasper seems to trust it since he starts pointing to a couple of spots with his finger and naming locations.\nJasper抽出一张看起来很粗糙的地图，把它摊平在其中一个板条箱上。地图看着很旧，我不确定它有多可靠，但Jasper似乎很相信它，因为他开始用手指点着几个位置，报出地名。"

    old "In practice, I know about two guns: the Blunderbuss and the Pepperbox. Which one would you like to know about?"
    new "In practice, I know about two guns: the Blunderbuss and the Pepperbox. Which one would you like to know about?\n实际上，我知道两把枪：Blunderbuss和Pepperbox。你想了解哪一把？"

    old "Back already, [protag]? I hope you're here to talk about the guns."
    new "Back already, [protag]? I hope you're here to talk about the guns.\n已经回来了，[protag]？希望你是来谈枪的。"

    old "Yes, can you remind me what our options are?"
    new "Yes, can you remind me what our options are?\n是的，你能提醒我一下，我们有哪些选择吗？"

    old "I'm terribly sorry. I just remembered something urgent I have to take care of. I'll come back as soon as I'm ready."
    new "I'm terribly sorry. I just remembered something urgent I have to take care of. I'll come back as soon as I'm ready.\n实在抱歉。我刚想起有件急事要处理。我一准备好就回来。"

    old "Bummer. Well, I'll be here, patiently waiting for your return. It's not like I can do this on my own anyway."
    new "Bummer. Well, I'll be here, patiently waiting for your return. It's not like I can do this on my own anyway.\n真扫兴。好吧，我会在这儿，耐心等你回来。反正这事我一个人也做不成。"

    old "Rumor has it that an old mercantile ship had a crate full of Blunderbuss rifles. When fired, those rifles will shoot out several bullets, covering a cone shaped area in front of the barrel. Basically, with these guns, the damage is spread out which means I can hit three enemies with one shot."
    new "Rumor has it that an old mercantile ship had a crate full of Blunderbuss rifles. When fired, those rifles will shoot out several bullets, covering a cone shaped area in front of the barrel. Basically, with these guns, the damage is spread out which means I can hit three enemies with one shot.\n有传言说，一艘旧的商船上有一整箱Blunderbuss步枪。发射时，那些步枪会射出多发子弹，覆盖枪口前方一片锥形区域。基本上，用这些枪，伤害是分散的，这意味着我能一枪打中三个敌人。"

    old "That's impressive, Jasper."
    new "That's impressive, Jasper.\n真厉害，Jasper。"

    old "It is. Of course, that feature comes at a cost. The Blunderbuss rifles do less damage and aren't nearly as accurate. Still, quickly being able to hit three targets at once is nothing to scoff at."
    new "It is. Of course, that feature comes at a cost. The Blunderbuss rifles do less damage and aren't nearly as accurate. Still, quickly being able to hit three targets at once is nothing to scoff at.\n确实。当然，这个特性是有代价的。Blunderbuss步枪伤害更小，也没那么精准。不过，能一下子击中三个目标，可不容小觑。"

    old "Rumors also say that the ship wrecked on an island not far from the Grimoire Dock. Couple hours of navigation tops. We can go there and search for the weapon. Unfortunately, it's likely we'll meet other pirates there. Unfriendly pirates."
    new "Rumors also say that the ship wrecked on an island not far from the Grimoire Dock. Couple hours of navigation tops. We can go there and search for the weapon. Unfortunately, it's likely we'll meet other pirates there. Unfriendly pirates.\n传言还说，那艘船在离Grimoire码头不远的一座岛上失事了。航行顶多几个小时。我们可以去那儿找找武器。不幸的是，我们很可能在那儿碰到其他海盗。不友好的海盗。"

    old "You mean pirates not affiliated with the Bastards Of the Sea?"
    new "You mean pirates not affiliated with the Bastards Of the Sea?\n你是说，跟Bastards Of the Sea没关系的海盗？"

    old "Exactly. Supposedly, they're after some other treasure in the area. If we encounter them, I'm afraid we might need to fight."
    new "Exactly. Supposedly, they're after some other treasure in the area. If we encounter them, I'm afraid we might need to fight.\n没错。据说，他们在这片区域找的是别的宝藏。如果我们碰上他们，恐怕免不了要打一场。"

    old "An excellent choice! Let's get on the Esmeralda."
    new "An excellent choice! Let's get on the Esmeralda.\n绝佳的选择！我们上Esmeralda吧。"

    old "I suppose you wouldn't happen to know the legend of Logan the pirate? Also known as Logan 'the Red' due to his ruthless and bloodthirsty nature?"
    new "I suppose you wouldn't happen to know the legend of Logan the pirate? Also known as Logan 'the Red' due to his ruthless and bloodthirsty nature?\n我想，你应该不知道Logan海盗的传说吧？他因为残忍嗜血的本性，又被称为“红”Logan？"

    old "Hmm. No, sorry. That name isn't familiar to me."
    new "Hmm. No, sorry. That name isn't familiar to me.\n嗯。不，抱歉。这名字我不太熟。"

    old "Well, long story short, he was one of the first people to use guns in battle. Specifically, a Pepperbox. This all happened several years ago. Logan is believed to be dead now, but some people swear that he just pretended to die."
    new "Well, long story short, he was one of the first people to use guns in battle. Specifically, a Pepperbox. This all happened several years ago. Logan is believed to be dead now, but some people swear that he just pretended to die.\n嗯，长话短说，他是最早在战斗中使用枪的人之一。具体来说，是一把Pepperbox。这些都是几年前的事了。人们相信Logan现在已经死了，但有些人发誓说，他只是装死而已。"

    old "To avoid his enemies?"
    new "To avoid his enemies?\n为了躲避他的敌人？"

    old "Ha, you are as smart as you look, [protag]. That is exactly right. At least, as far as the stories go. As Logan got older, he thought it'd be be better to fake his death so that his enemies would stop looking for him. And it seems that strategy worked, until now."
    new "Ha, you are as smart as you look, [protag]. That is exactly right. At least, as far as the stories go. As Logan got older, he thought it'd be be better to fake his death so that his enemies would stop looking for him. And it seems that strategy worked, until now.\n哈，你果然和你看起来一样聪明，[protag]。完全正确。至少，就传说的版本而言。随着Logan年纪渐长，他觉得最好假死，好让他的敌人不再找他。而那个策略似乎一直有效，直到现在。"

    old "The information I have is not very accurate. However, on an island close to the lizardmen's territory there's a small shack. I noticed it myself while circumnavigating the area when we first scouted the waters around N'Mar."
    new "The information I have is not very accurate. However, on an island close to the lizardmen's territory there's a small shack. I noticed it myself while circumnavigating the area when we first scouted the waters around N'Mar.\n我掌握的情报不太准确。不过，在靠近lizardmen领地的一座岛上，有个小棚屋。我们最初侦察N'Mar周围水域时，我在绕行那片区域时亲眼注意到了它。"

    old "I also noticed some smoke when I passed through there a few days ago so someone is definitely living there. It might be Logan."
    new "I also noticed some smoke when I passed through there a few days ago so someone is definitely living there. It might be Logan.\n几天前我经过那里时，还注意到有烟，所以肯定有人住在那儿。可能是Logan。"

    old "How old would he be now?"
    new "How old would he be now?\n他现在该多大年纪了？"

    old "Nobody knows his exact age, but he's not young anymore. He shouldn't be a match for the two of us. We should be able to overpower him if he isn't willing to part with his valuables peacefully."
    new "Nobody knows his exact age, but he's not young anymore. He shouldn't be a match for the two of us. We should be able to overpower him if he isn't willing to part with his valuables peacefully.\n没人知道他的确切年龄，但他已经不年轻了。他不该是我们俩的对手。如果他不肯和平地交出他的贵重物品，我们应该能制服他。"

    old "You're talking about the Pepperbox?"
    new "You're talking about the Pepperbox?\n你说的是Pepperbox？"

    old "And anything else that looks like it might be worth something. He's bound to have a bit of treasure hidden away somewhere. We'll need to take it in order to pay back my friends for lending me the ship. That was part of our deal."
    new "And anything else that looks like it might be worth something. He's bound to have a bit of treasure hidden away somewhere. We'll need to take it in order to pay back my friends for lending me the ship. That was part of our deal.\n还有任何看起来可能值钱的东西。他肯定在某个地方藏着点宝藏。我们得把它拿走，好还我那帮朋友借船给我的人情。那是我们交易的一部分。"

    old "Well, okay. That all sounds a little too convenient though."
    new "Well, okay. That all sounds a little too convenient though.\n嗯，好吧。不过这一切听起来有点太顺了。"

    old "What? But you promised-"
    new "What? But you promised-\n什么？可你答应过——"

    old "Don't twist my words. I did not promise you anything. I said that if I had time, I'd accompany you. Unfortunately, I don't have time for this after all."
    new "Don't twist my words. I did not promise you anything. I said that if I had time, I'd accompany you. Unfortunately, I don't have time for this after all.\n别曲解我的话。我什么都没答应过你。我说的是，如果我有时间，就陪你去。可惜，我终究没时间做这件事。"

    old "Jasper crosses his arms and looks at me with a grumpy expression on his face. It's actually kind of an endearing look."
    new "Jasper crosses his arms and looks at me with a grumpy expression on his face. It's actually kind of an endearing look.\nJasper抱起双臂，一脸不高兴地看着我。那表情其实有点可爱。"

    old "All right. I guess I have no choice but to accept you decision. But don't complain if I'm not as effective as I could be in combat!"
    new "All right. I guess I have no choice but to accept you decision. But don't complain if I'm not as effective as I could be in combat!\n好吧。我想我别无选择，只能接受你的决定。但要是我在战斗里发挥不出全力，可别抱怨！"

    old "Oh, I'm sure you'll do fine even without those guns."
    new "Oh, I'm sure you'll do fine even without those guns.\n哦，我相信就算没有那些枪，你也能干得很好。"

    old "If you say so."
    new "If you say so.\n你说了算。"

    old "As Jasper said we would, we reach the island within a few hours. Our own ship, the Esmeralda, is small enough to slip by unnoticed which turns out to be quite lucky considering that we end up spotting two large pirate vessels on the other side of the island."
    new "As Jasper said we would, we reach the island within a few hours. Our own ship, the Esmeralda, is small enough to slip by unnoticed which turns out to be quite lucky considering that we end up spotting two large pirate vessels on the other side of the island.\n正如Jasper所说，我们几个小时后就到了那座岛。我们自己的船Esmeralda小到能神不知鬼不觉地溜过去，结果这运气实在不错，因为我们最后发现，岛的另一边停着两艘大型海盗船。"

    old "Well, this isn't good. Two large pirate ships? I expected one, but not two. That means there's going to be a lot of pirates wandering around. More than we'll be able to take in a fight."
    new "Well, this isn't good. Two large pirate ships? I expected one, but not two. That means there's going to be a lot of pirates wandering around. More than we'll be able to take in a fight.\n嗯，这可不妙。两艘大型海盗船？我预料到一艘，没想到是两艘。这意味着会有很多海盗在四处游荡。比我们在战斗里能应付的还多。"

    old "Do you know where on the island the guns are supposed to be?"
    new "Do you know where on the island the guns are supposed to be?\n你知道枪应该在岛上的哪个位置吗？"

    old "Would you like to take a guess?"
    new "Would you like to take a guess?\n你想猜猜看吗？"

    old "The way Jasper asks the question makes me think that the answer must be our worst case scenario."
    new "The way Jasper asks the question makes me think that the answer must be our worst case scenario.\nJasper问这问题的方式，让我觉得答案一定是我们最坏的情形。"

    old "Mid-way between the two ships?"
    new "Mid-way between the two ships?\n两艘船正中间？"

    old "That would be correct."
    new "That would be correct.\n答对了。"

    old "I take a second to think over our options before vocalizing the two I think have the best chance of success."
    new "I take a second to think over our options before vocalizing the two I think have the best chance of success.\n我花了一会儿想我们的选择，然后说出我认为最有成功机会的两个。"

    old "I have two ideas. One, we run over there as fast as we can and grab as much as we can before running some more or, two, we approach one of the pirate groups and try to convince them the other pirates already have the treasure."
    new "I have two ideas. One, we run over there as fast as we can and grab as much as we can before running some more or, two, we approach one of the pirate groups and try to convince them the other pirates already have the treasure.\n我有两个主意。一，我们尽快冲过去，能拿多少拿多少，然后再继续跑；或者，二，我们接近其中一伙海盗，设法让他们相信，另一伙海盗已经拿到宝藏了。"

    old "Hmm. Neither of those plans sound ideal."
    new "Hmm. Neither of those plans sound ideal.\n嗯。这两个计划听着都不太理想。"

    old "I never claimed they were. Still, if we're going to get our hands on the Blunderbuss we have to try something."
    new "I never claimed they were. Still, if we're going to get our hands on the Blunderbuss we have to try something.\n我从没说过它们理想。不过，如果我们想把Blunderbuss弄到手，总得试试。"

    old "You're right about that. Well, I don't have a preference. Go ahead and choose the plan you like best."
    new "You're right about that. Well, I don't have a preference. Go ahead and choose the plan you like best.\n你说得对。嗯，我没有偏好。你自己挑个你最喜欢的计划吧。"

    old "Very well, go ahead. I'll follow your lead."
    new "Very well, go ahead. I'll follow your lead.\n很好，去吧。我跟你走。"

    old "Jasper and I make our way towards one of the pirate ships. The crew members instantly raise their weapons, unsure what to make of us as I ask to be taken to their Captain. They oblige and, soon enough, we're speaking with their leader."
    new "Jasper and I make our way towards one of the pirate ships. The crew members instantly raise their weapons, unsure what to make of us as I ask to be taken to their Captain. They oblige and, soon enough, we're speaking with their leader.\nJasper和我朝其中一艘海盗船走去。船员们立刻举起武器，不知该拿我们怎么办，这时我要求去见他们的船长。他们照办了，很快，我们就在和他们头领交谈。"

    old "Now, what is all this about?"
    new "Now, what is all this about?\n那么，这到底是怎么回事？"

    old "We know that you're searching for treasure on this island and we have some information that we think might be useful to you."
    new "We know that you're searching for treasure on this island and we have some information that we think might be useful to you.\n我们知道你们在这座岛上找宝藏，而我们有些情报，觉得也许对你们有用。"

    old "Ha! I'm afraid you're too late. We already know where the treasure is. You're of no use to us."
    new "Ha! I'm afraid you're too late. We already know where the treasure is. You're of no use to us.\n哈！恐怕你们来晚了。我们已经知道宝藏在哪儿了。你们对我们没用。"

    old "Oh? So you already know that the other pirate ship has gathered a hold full of gold and is ready to set sail?"
    new "Oh? So you already know that the other pirate ship has gathered a hold full of gold and is ready to set sail?\n哦？这么说，你们已经知道另一艘海盗船已经装满了黄金，正要起航了？"

    old "It's true. We saw it with our own eyes. Men carrying large bags of gold from the island to their ship."
    new "It's true. We saw it with our own eyes. Men carrying large bags of gold from the island to their ship.\n是真的。我们亲眼所见。那些人扛着一袋袋大金子，从岛上搬到他们的船上。"

    old "We realize that we have no chance of taking either of you on. All we ask in exchange for our information is that you leave us alone so we can at least enjoy a night on the island before we go home empty handed."
    new "We realize that we have no chance of taking either of you on. All we ask in exchange for our information is that you leave us alone so we can at least enjoy a night on the island before we go home empty handed.\n我们意识到，我们没机会跟你们任何一方较量。作为交换我们情报的代价，我们只求你们别来打扰，好让我们在空手回家前，至少能在岛上享用一个晚上。"

    old "The pirates start muttering to themselves in the background. They're predictably worried over the possibility of losing the treasure that they came for."
    new "The pirates start muttering to themselves in the background. They're predictably worried over the possibility of losing the treasure that they came for.\n海盗们在背景里开始窃窃私语。可以预料，他们在担心会失去自己来找的那份宝藏。"

    old "Whether or not the Captain believes us doesn't matter anymore. If he doesn't ease their fears, he'll have a mutiny on his hands."
    new "Whether or not the Captain believes us doesn't matter anymore. If he doesn't ease their fears, he'll have a mutiny on his hands.\n船长信不信我们已经不重要了。他要是不平息他们的恐惧，就会闹出哗变。"

    old "We'd better hurry then. Let's go! You two, stay and guard these 'adventurers'. If it turns out that they were lying to us, we'll gut them once we've dealt those other pirates!"
    new "We'd better hurry then. Let's go! You two, stay and guard these 'adventurers'. If it turns out that they were lying to us, we'll gut them once we've dealt those other pirates!\n那我们最好快点。走！你们两个，留下看守这些“冒险者”。要是发现他们在撒谎，等我们收拾完那帮海盗，就把他们开膛破肚！"

    old "The crew cheers and then follows their Captain towards the other ship. Good, the plan worked. Once we deal with these two, there shouldn't be anything left to stop us from getting that Blunderbuss."
    new "The crew cheers and then follows their Captain towards the other ship. Good, the plan worked. Once we deal with these two, there shouldn't be anything left to stop us from getting that Blunderbuss.\n船员们欢呼起来，然后跟着船长朝另一艘船去了。好，计划奏效了。等我们解决了这两个，就再没有什么能阻止我们拿到那把Blunderbuss了。"

    old "If you leave now, we'll let you live."
    new "If you leave now, we'll let you live.\n如果你们现在离开，我们就饶你们一命。"

    old "Yes! Please! We won't give you any more trouble!"
    new "Yes! Please! We won't give you any more trouble!\n是！求你们了！我们不会再给你们添麻烦了！"

    old "Run away. Now."
    new "Run away. Now.\n快跑。现在。"

    old "Good, now let's take a look at that shipwreck."
    new "Good, now let's take a look at that shipwreck.\n好，现在让我们看看那艘沉船。"

    old "We waste no time making our way to the wreckage. The crate isn't too hard to find, but there's no way that Jasper and I will be able to carry it on our own. We grab what we can carry and pocket a few other precious items such as gold trinkets and rare alchemy ingredients on our way out."
    new "We waste no time making our way to the wreckage. The crate isn't too hard to find, but there's no way that Jasper and I will be able to carry it on our own. We grab what we can carry and pocket a few other precious items such as gold trinkets and rare alchemy ingredients on our way out.\n我们片刻不耽误地朝残骸赶去。箱子不难找，但Jasper和我两个人可没法自己把它搬走。我们只拿了搬得动的几把，出去的路上，还顺手揣了些别的值钱物件，比如金饰和稀有的炼金材料。"

    old "We'll be able to verify your claims soon enough."
    new "We'll be able to verify your claims soon enough.\n我们很快就能核实你们的说法了。"

    old "He raises his voice, making sure that his crew can hear the confident tone in his voice as he reassures them."
    new "He raises his voice, making sure that his crew can hear the confident tone in his voice as he reassures them.\n他提高了嗓门，确保船员们能听出他声音里那自信的语气，好让他们安心。"

    old "Our scouts will be back shortly. They will be able to tell us if what these two have said is true or not."
    new "Our scouts will be back shortly. They will be able to tell us if what these two have said is true or not.\n我们的探子很快就会回来。他们能告诉我们，这两个家伙说的是不是真的。"

    old "The Captain's words have the desired effect. The crew calms down, ruining our chances at convincing the two groups of pirates to attack each other. This is definitely not the outcome I was hoping for. I look Jasper in the eyes and he gives me a nod of approval."
    new "The Captain's words have the desired effect. The crew calms down, ruining our chances at convincing the two groups of pirates to attack each other. This is definitely not the outcome I was hoping for. I look Jasper in the eyes and he gives me a nod of approval.\n船长的话起到了想要的效果。船员们冷静下来，我们想让两伙海盗互相打起来的机会也就泡汤了。这绝对不是我想要的结果。我望着Jasper的眼睛，他朝我点了点头，表示同意。"

    old "Sorry, but something has come up and we really need to get going now."
    new "Sorry, but something has come up and we really need to get going now.\n抱歉，出了点事，我们真的得现在就走。"

    old "That said, we bolt. The pirates chase us for a bit, but give up soon enough. We're not really their biggest concern right now, after all."
    new "That said, we bolt. The pirates chase us for a bit, but give up soon enough. We're not really their biggest concern right now, after all.\n说罢，我们拔腿就跑。海盗们追了我们一小段，但很快就放弃了。毕竟，眼下我们并不是他们最在意的。"

    old "Lucky for us, it's not worth it for them to come after us."
    new "Lucky for us, it's not worth it for them to come after us.\n对我们来说幸运的是，追我们并不值得。"

    old "Not right now anyway. Once they have their hands on the treasure though..."
    new "Not right now anyway. Once they have their hands on the treasure though...\n至少现在不值。等他们拿到宝藏之后嘛……"

    old "We'd better leave then. It's too risky to continue. It's more important that we leave here alive."
    new "We'd better leave then. It's too risky to continue. It's more important that we leave here alive.\n那我们最好离开。继续下去太冒险了。活着离开这里更重要。"

    old "Jasper and I start running towards the spot, trying to avoid the various pirate patrols. It's really hard. The island has a lot of tropical vegetation and there are a lot of plants large enough to hide behind, but there are so many pirates around that the closer we get, the harder it becomes to stay out of sight."
    new "Jasper and I start running towards the spot, trying to avoid the various pirate patrols. It's really hard. The island has a lot of tropical vegetation and there are a lot of plants large enough to hide behind, but there are so many pirates around that the closer we get, the harder it becomes to stay out of sight.\nJasper和我朝那个地点跑去，试图避开各路海盗巡逻。真的很难。岛上热带植被茂密，有很多大得足以藏身的植物，但周围海盗实在太多，我们越靠近，就越难不被发现。"

    old "Miraculously, we manage to avoid all the pirates in the area and reach the shipwreck. Knowing we only have a limited time before we're found out, we immediately begin combing through the wreckage to find the crate we're looking for."
    new "Miraculously, we manage to avoid all the pirates in the area and reach the shipwreck. Knowing we only have a limited time before we're found out, we immediately begin combing through the wreckage to find the crate we're looking for.\n奇迹般地，我们避开了那片区域所有的海盗，到达了沉船处。我们知道，在被发现之前时间有限，于是立刻开始翻找残骸，寻找我们要的那个箱子。"

    old "That must be the right one! Come, [protag]!"
    new "That must be the right one! Come, [protag]!\n那一定是了！来，[protag]！"

    old "We only grab a few of the weapons, since the two of us alone can't carry the whole crate. We also pocket as many gold trinkets and rare alchemy ingredients as we can before leaving."
    new "We only grab a few of the weapons, since the two of us alone can't carry the whole crate. We also pocket as many gold trinkets and rare alchemy ingredients as we can before leaving.\n我们只拿了几把武器，因为光靠我们两个没法搬动整箱。临走前，我们还尽量多揣了些金饰和稀有的炼金材料。"

    old "Hey! Where do you think you're going with all of that?"
    new "Hey! Where do you think you're going with all of that?\n喂！你带着那些东西要去哪儿？"

    old "See? I told you that it was worth straying away from the other patrol routes! Look what we found!"
    new "See? I told you that it was worth straying away from the other patrol routes! Look what we found!\n瞧见没？我早说了，偏离其他巡逻路线是值得的！看看我们发现了什么！"

    old "Shut up and help me kill these two so we can take their stuff!"
    new "Shut up and help me kill these two so we can take their stuff!\n闭嘴，帮我杀了这两个人，好把他们的东西抢过来！"

    old "Good, now let's hurry back to our ship before we stumble into an even bigger pirate patrol!"
    new "Good, now let's hurry back to our ship before we stumble into an even bigger pirate patrol!\n好，现在赶紧回我们船上，免得撞上更大股的海盗巡逻队！"

    old "As I'm running, my foot catches on a root. I end up tumbling to the ground and making a lot of noise in the process."
    new "As I'm running, my foot catches on a root. I end up tumbling to the ground and making a lot of noise in the process.\n我跑着跑着，脚被一条树根绊住。结果我摔倒在地，弄出了很大的动静。"

    old "Who's there? Show yourself!"
    new "Who's there? Show yourself!\n谁在那儿？现身！"

    old "Damn. I think they spotted us."
    new "Damn. I think they spotted us.\n该死。我想他们发现我们了。"

    old "I see them! Two of them, over here! Come! Let's catch them and see if they know the treasure's exact location!"
    new "I see them! Two of them, over here! Come! Let's catch them and see if they know the treasure's exact location!\n我看见他们了！两个人，在这边！来！抓住他们，看他们知不知道宝藏的确切位置！"

    old "There are too many of them. We have to get back to our ship before they surround us!"
    new "There are too many of them. We have to get back to our ship before they surround us!\n他们人太多了。我们得赶在他们包围我们之前回到船上！"

    old "Unfortunately, I agree. Let's leave. Now!"
    new "Unfortunately, I agree. Let's leave. Now!\n不幸的是，我同意。我们走。现在！"

    old "We run back to our ship as fast as we can. Luckily, the pirates give up after a bit. Their focus is on the treasure. Not us."
    new "We run back to our ship as fast as we can. Luckily, the pirates give up after a bit. Their focus is on the treasure. Not us.\n我们拼尽全力跑回船上。幸运的是，海盗们追了一小段就放弃了。他们关注的是宝藏。不是我们。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]! I still can't believe we got ourselves a Blunderbuss! It would have never happened without your help!"
    new "Thank you, [protag]! I still can't believe we got ourselves a Blunderbuss! It would have never happened without your help!\n谢谢你，[protag]！我还是不敢相信，我们弄到了一把Blunderbuss！没有你的帮助，这根本不可能！"

    old "You're welcome. This should make you stronger in battle."
    new "You're welcome. This should make you stronger in battle.\n不客气。这应该能让你在战斗中更强。"

    old "You bet it will! Now, let's get back to Grimoire so we can give the other items to my friends. I think they'll be quite pleased with our haul."
    new "You bet it will! Now, let's get back to Grimoire so we can give the other items to my friends. I think they'll be quite pleased with our haul.\n那还用说！现在，让我们回Grimoire，好把其他物品交给我朋友。我想他们会对我们的收获相当满意。"

    old "I'm really sorry, Jasper."
    new "I'm really sorry, Jasper.\n真的很抱歉，Jasper。"

    old "Well, at least we tried. I'll just have to say goodbye to getting that weapon. For now, at least."
    new "Well, at least we tried. I'll just have to say goodbye to getting that weapon. For now, at least.\n嗯，至少我们试过了。我只好跟那把武器说再见了。至少目前如此。"

    old "Let's get back to Grimoire."
    new "Let's get back to Grimoire.\n我们回Grimoire吧。"

    old "We reach the small island Jasper told me about. Honestly, I can see why a retired pirate would want to live here. It's close to the lizardmen, but not close enough for them to pose a real threat. And it's far away from everyone else with plenty of fish nearby to catch and a small pier he can use to escape quickly if needed."
    new "We reach the small island Jasper told me about. Honestly, I can see why a retired pirate would want to live here. It's close to the lizardmen, but not close enough for them to pose a real threat. And it's far away from everyone else with plenty of fish nearby to catch and a small pier he can use to escape quickly if needed.\n我们到了Jasper告诉我的那座小岛。老实说，我能理解一个退休的海盗为什么想住在这儿。这里离lizardmen很近，但也没近到让他们构成真正的威胁。而且这里远离其他所有人，附近有很多鱼可捕，还有个小码头，需要时他可以迅速驾船逃走。"

    old "I don't see any smoke coming out of the shack."
    new "I don't see any smoke coming out of the shack.\n我没看到棚屋里有烟冒出来。"

    old "He might not be home right now."
    new "He might not be home right now.\n他现在可能不在家。"

    old "Let's get a closer look."
    new "Let's get a closer look.\n我们走近点看看。"

    old "I nod and together we carefully approach the shack. I slowly take a peek inside using a small window around the side. It's very dark, but it does seem empty. Jasper approaches the main door and tries to use the keyhole to peer inside."
    new "I nod and together we carefully approach the shack. I slowly take a peek inside using a small window around the side. It's very dark, but it does seem empty. Jasper approaches the main door and tries to use the keyhole to peer inside.\n我点点头，我们一起小心翼翼地靠近棚屋。我透过侧面的一扇小窗，慢慢地往里窥探。里面很暗，但确实像是空的。Jasper走到正门前，试图透过锁孔往里看。"

    old "It's around that time that we hear a sound. We back off quickly and make it back into the foliage just in time to see an old man coming back from a successful fishing trip. This has to be Logan, right? He enters the shack and disappears from view."
    new "It's around that time that we hear a sound. We back off quickly and make it back into the foliage just in time to see an old man coming back from a successful fishing trip. This has to be Logan, right? He enters the shack and disappears from view.\n就在那时，我们听到一个声音。我们迅速退后，刚躲回树丛里，正好看到一个老人钓鱼满载而归。这一定就是Logan，对吧？他走进棚屋，从视线中消失了。"

    old "Well, now he's home. I didn't see him carrying any sort of gun though."
    new "Well, now he's home. I didn't see him carrying any sort of gun though.\n嗯，现在他到家了。不过我并没看到他带着任何枪。"

    old "He probably wouldn't go around carrying it unless he thought he needed it. If someone spots him with a gun, it would be suspicious. They might be able to figure out who he is. As he is now, he looks like a harmless hermit living alone on this small island."
    new "He probably wouldn't go around carrying it unless he thought he needed it. If someone spots him with a gun, it would be suspicious. They might be able to figure out who he is. As he is now, he looks like a harmless hermit living alone on this small island.\n除非他觉得需要，否则他大概不会随身带着它。如果有人看见他拿着枪，那就很可疑。他们也许能查出他是谁。就他现在的样子，看起来像个独自住在这座小岛上的无害隐士。"

    old "I spotted something."
    new "I spotted something.\n我发现了点东西。"

    old "I gesture to Jasper to come closer with my hand."
    new "I gesture to Jasper to come closer with my hand.\n我用手势示意Jasper靠近些。"

    old "A small chest, huh? Looks like the perfect place to hide a pepperbox gun."
    new "A small chest, huh? Looks like the perfect place to hide a pepperbox gun.\n一个小箱子，嗯？看起来正是藏一把Pepperbox枪的绝佳地方。"

    old "Do you really think it could be in there?"
    new "Do you really think it could be in there?\n你真的觉得它会在里面？"

    old "Hm. I don't know. That's where I'd hide it, but that doesn't mean that's where he hid it. Look there though, [protag]. There's a key tied at the end of that cord he's wearing around his neck."
    new "Hm. I don't know. That's where I'd hide it, but that doesn't mean that's where he hid it. Look there though, [protag]. There's a key tied at the end of that cord he's wearing around his neck.\n嗯。我不知道。那是我会藏的地方，但不代表他就藏在那儿。不过你看，[protag]。他脖子上挂着的那根绳子的末端，系着一把钥匙。"

    old "I'm betting that's the key to the chest!"
    new "I'm betting that's the key to the chest!\n我打赌那就是箱子的钥匙！"

    old "Very likely. The design does seem to match the one on the chest. But what are you planning to do, [protag]? I'm pretty sure he won't let us take it peacefully."
    new "Very likely. The design does seem to match the one on the chest. But what are you planning to do, [protag]? I'm pretty sure he won't let us take it peacefully.\n很可能。那纹样似乎确实和箱子上的一模一样。但你打算怎么办，[protag]？我很肯定，他不会让我们和平地拿走它。"

    old "Maybe we can come to some kind of compromise? After all, there are two of us. He shouldn't be eager to push his luck."
    new "Maybe we can come to some kind of compromise? After all, there are two of us. He shouldn't be eager to push his luck.\n也许我们能达成某种妥协？毕竟我们有两个人。他不该急着铤而走险。"

    old "And if he refuses? Are you ready to kill an old man? You surprise me, [protag]."
    new "And if he refuses? Are you ready to kill an old man? You surprise me, [protag].\n如果他拒绝呢？你准备好杀一个老人了吗？你让我很意外，[protag]。"

    old "First of all, if what you told me about his past is true, he's not exactly innocent. He's probably killed plenty of people of over the course of his lifetime that didn't deserve it so I'm not about to pity him. Being old doesn't absolve him of his past crimes."
    new "First of all, if what you told me about his past is true, he's not exactly innocent. He's probably killed plenty of people of over the course of his lifetime that didn't deserve it so I'm not about to pity him. Being old doesn't absolve him of his past crimes.\n首先，如果你告诉我的关于他过去的事是真的，那他并不完全无辜。他这一生多半杀过很多不该死的人，所以我不打算可怜他。年迈并不能赦免他过去的罪行。"

    old "Second, despite that, I will still try to find a compromise. He risks his life only if he doesn't leave peacefully."
    new "Second, despite that, I will still try to find a compromise. He risks his life only if he doesn't leave peacefully.\n其次，尽管如此，我仍会努力寻求妥协。只有他不肯和平离开，才会拿自己的命冒险。"

    old "Well, I don't have a better idea, so you're welcome to try."
    new "Well, I don't have a better idea, so you're welcome to try.\n嗯，我没有更好的主意，所以你尽管试试。"

    old "I think the best course of action is to try stealing the key."
    new "I think the best course of action is to try stealing the key.\n我觉得最好的做法，是试着偷钥匙。"

    old "Good, go ahead."
    new "Good, go ahead.\n好，去吧。"

    old "Why me?!"
    new "Why me?!\n为什么是我？！"

    old "It was your idea. I'll cover your back."
    new "It was your idea. I'll cover your back.\n这是你的主意。我会掩护你的后背。"

    old "Hmph."
    new "Hmph.\n哼。"

    old "I wait patiently, carefully watching him from the window. He cooks the fish he caught and eats them before going to take a nap on an improvised bed of sorts. Once I'm sure he's fallen asleep, I make my move."
    new "I wait patiently, carefully watching him from the window. He cooks the fish he caught and eats them before going to take a nap on an improvised bed of sorts. Once I'm sure he's fallen asleep, I make my move.\n我耐心等着，从窗户仔细观察他。他把自己钓到的鱼煮了吃掉，然后躺到一张凑合搭的床上打了个盹。等确定他睡着了，我才动手。"

    old "I manage to sneak inside without making any loud noises. Logan is snoring heavily as I slowly make my way towards him. Instead of trying to slide the rope over his neck, I just use a dagger to cut it. Less chance of waking him up."
    new "I manage to sneak inside without making any loud noises. Logan is snoring heavily as I slowly make my way towards him. Instead of trying to slide the rope over his neck, I just use a dagger to cut it. Less chance of waking him up.\n我设法溜了进去，没弄出任何响动。Logan鼾声如雷，我慢慢地朝他挪过去。我没有试图把绳子从他脖子上滑下来，而是直接用匕首割断了它。这样吵醒他的几率更小。"

    old "And it works. Soon enough, I have the key in my possession. I grab the chest and take it outside. Once I'm out, Jasper and I run back to the ship."
    new "And it works. Soon enough, I have the key in my possession. I grab the chest and take it outside. Once I'm out, Jasper and I run back to the ship.\n而且奏效了。很快，钥匙就到了我手里。我抓起箱子，把它拿到外面。一出来，Jasper和我就跑回了船上。"

    old "Unfortunately, as soon as I step inside the shack, my foot presses down on a loose plank and the loud squeaking sound it produces awakens Logan."
    new "Unfortunately, as soon as I step inside the shack, my foot presses down on a loose plank and the loud squeaking sound it produces awakens Logan.\n不幸的是，我刚一踏进棚屋，脚就踩上了一块松动的木板，它发出的刺耳咯吱声惊醒了Logan。"

    old "Who's there? What are you doing here?"
    new "Who's there? What are you doing here?\n谁在那儿？你在这里做什么？"

    old "From the side of his bed, Logan quickly draws a gun and points it at me."
    new "From the side of his bed, Logan quickly draws a gun and points it at me.\nLogan从床边迅速抽出一把枪，指向我。"

    old "Leave immediately or I'll shoot you in the head!"
    new "Leave immediately or I'll shoot you in the head!\n立刻离开，否则我开枪打爆你的头！"

    old "I go to the front door and knock. I hear some shuffling from inside, but don't think much of it until Jasper rushes forward and pulls me to his chest."
    new "I go to the front door and knock. I hear some shuffling from inside, but don't think much of it until Jasper rushes forward and pulls me to his chest.\n我走到前门敲门。我听到里面有些窸窣声，但没太在意，直到Jasper冲上前，把我拉到他胸前。"

    old "Bang!"
    new "Bang!\n砰！"

    old "Sorry about that, but I saw Logan through the window. He grabbed a gun and aimed it straight at the door!"
    new "Sorry about that, but I saw Logan through the window. He grabbed a gun and aimed it straight at the door!\n抱歉，但我从窗户看到了Logan。他抓起一把枪，直直瞄准了门！"

    old "I look at the old wooden door and, sure enough, there's a hole in it at the height of my head. Jasper just saved my life."
    new "I look at the old wooden door and, sure enough, there's a hole in it at the height of my head. Jasper just saved my life.\n我看着那扇旧木门，果然，在我脑袋那么高的地方有个洞。Jasper刚刚救了我一命。"

    old "Who are you? What do you want?"
    new "Who are you? What do you want?\n你们是谁？你们想干什么？"

    old "Look, we're not looking for a fight. We're here to help. We, uh... admire what you achieved when you were younger."
    new "Look, we're not looking for a fight. We're here to help. We, uh... admire what you achieved when you were younger.\n听着，我们不是来找茬的。我们是来帮忙的。我们，呃……很钦佩你年轻时的成就。"

    old "Are you calling me old?!"
    new "Are you calling me old?!\n你这是在说我老吗？！"

    old "Jasper grins, barely holding back a fit of laughter as he gives me the thumbs up sign with both hands. He's definitely making fun of me. I'm tempted to slap him, but I settle for an eye roll instead before continuing."
    new "Jasper grins, barely holding back a fit of laughter as he gives me the thumbs up sign with both hands. He's definitely making fun of me. I'm tempted to slap him, but I settle for an eye roll instead before continuing.\nJasper咧嘴笑着，几乎憋不住笑，用双手朝我竖起大拇指。他肯定是在取笑我。我真想扇他一巴掌，不过还是翻了个白眼，继续往下说。"

    old "Yes, you're old, Logan. You can't deny it. But that just makes you even more incredible. Reaching your age isn't exactly an easy feat for someone who has done as much and has made as many enemies as you have."
    new "Yes, you're old, Logan. You can't deny it. But that just makes you even more incredible. Reaching your age isn't exactly an easy feat for someone who has done as much and has made as many enemies as you have.\n是的，你老了，Logan。你没法否认。但这只会让你更加了不起。对于你这样一个干了那么多事、树了那么多敌的人来说，活到你这个岁数可不是件容易的事。"

    old "Your point, [manwoman]?"
    new "Your point, [manwoman]?\n你到底想说什么，[manwoman]？"

    old "Please, call me [protag]. We have come here to warn you and offer a solution."
    new "Please, call me [protag]. We have come here to warn you and offer a solution.\n请叫我[protag]。我们是来警告你，并提供一个解决方案的。"

    old "Ha! I already know people are after me. I've lived these last years of my life hidden away and it's worked. So far nobody has found me, except you."
    new "Ha! I already know people are after me. I've lived these last years of my life hidden away and it's worked. So far nobody has found me, except you.\n哈！我早知道有人在追我。我躲躲藏藏地过了这些年，一直管用。到目前为止，除了你们，还没人找到我。"

    old "Yes, you have been good at hiding from other outlaws like your fellow pirates. Like I said though, a lot of people want you dead. What you don't know is that the Human Empire has been added to that list."
    new "Yes, you have been good at hiding from other outlaws like your fellow pirates. Like I said though, a lot of people want you dead. What you don't know is that the Human Empire has been added to that list.\n是的，你一直很擅长躲开其他不法之徒，比如你的海盗同伙。不过，正如我所说，很多人想要你的命。你不知道的是，人类帝国也加入了这个名单。"

    old "Ah, silence. I take it he wasn't expecting that."
    new "Ah, silence. I take it he wasn't expecting that.\n啊，沉默了。我想他没料到这个。"

    old "I've heard about you, [manwoman]. The name [protag] isn't new even in this remote area. I know you're acting as the emissary of Grimoire. Did they send you to kill me?"
    new "I've heard about you, [manwoman]. The name [protag] isn't new even in this remote area. I know you're acting as the emissary of Grimoire. Did they send you to kill me?\n我听说过你，[manwoman]。[protag]这个名字，即便在这个偏远的地方也不陌生。我知道你在以Grimoire使者的身份行事。是他们派你来杀我的吗？"

    old "What if they did?"
    new "What if they did?\n如果是呢？"

    old "Then I'm afraid I would need to kill you and your quiet friend who thinks he can get away with spying on me through the window."
    new "Then I'm afraid I would need to kill you and your quiet friend who thinks he can get away with spying on me through the window.\n那恐怕我就得杀了你，还有你那位安静的朋友——他以为能从窗户偷窥我而不被发现。"

    old "What-"
    new "What-\n什么——"

    old "Look, even if you kill us, the empire will send someone else. There's a bounty on your head for 500 gold pieces."
    new "Look, even if you kill us, the empire will send someone else. There's a bounty on your head for 500 gold pieces.\n听着，就算你杀了我们，帝国也会派别的人来。你头上挂着500金币的悬赏。"

    old "500? Not bad. But when I was younger, I was worth more."
    new "500? Not bad. But when I was younger, I was worth more.\n500？不赖。不过我年轻时，身价更高。"

    old "Anyway, the point is: why should we fight and risk dying when we could both gain something?"
    new "Anyway, the point is: why should we fight and risk dying when we could both gain something?\n总之，重点是：我们双方都能有所得的时候，为什么要拼个你死我活？"

    old "Hmph. I'm listening."
    new "Hmph. I'm listening.\n哼。我听着呢。"

    old "Here's what I suggest: you give us something belonging to you, something iconic that could only have been yours."
    new "Here's what I suggest: you give us something belonging to you, something iconic that could only have been yours.\n我的建议是这样的：你给我们一件属于你的东西，一件标志性的、只可能是你的东西。"

    old "I'm really hoping that the Pepperbox is the only thing he has that fits that description."
    new "I'm really hoping that the Pepperbox is the only thing he has that fits that description.\n我真希望，Pepperbox是他唯一符合这个描述的东西。"

    old "Then, we take it back to the council as proof that we killed you. Nobody from the empire will ever look for you again. They'll take my word for it and presume that you're dead. For real, this time."
    new "Then, we take it back to the council as proof that we killed you. Nobody from the empire will ever look for you again. They'll take my word for it and presume that you're dead. For real, this time.\n然后，我们把它带回议会，作为我们杀了你的证据。帝国就不会再有人来找你了。他们会相信我的话，认定你死了。这次，是真的死了。"

    old "I already faked my death. It was a glorious funeral too, you know? Still... I think you might be right."
    new "I already faked my death. It was a glorious funeral too, you know? Still... I think you might be right.\n我已经装死过一次了。那场葬礼还很风光，你知道吗？不过……我觉得你也许说得对。"

    old "My title is good for something. If the Envoy of Grimoire says that you're dead, even the skeptics will have to believe it. And I'll do that for you as long as you give us that coffer over there."
    new "My title is good for something. If the Envoy of Grimoire says that you're dead, even the skeptics will have to believe it. And I'll do that for you as long as you give us that coffer over there.\n我的头衔还有点用。如果Grimoire的使者说你死了，连怀疑者也不得不相信。只要你把那边那个箱子给我们，我就会为你这么做。"

    old "But that's my gun in there! And...several valuable items! A ruby ring worth much more than 500 gold pieces!"
    new "But that's my gun in there! And...several valuable items! A ruby ring worth much more than 500 gold pieces!\n但里面是我的枪！还有……好几件值钱的东西！一枚红宝石戒指，价值远超500金币！"

    old "I doubt there'd be a better proof of your death than your gun. Besides, what do you need treasure for out here? Is your life worth any of those things?"
    new "I doubt there'd be a better proof of your death than your gun. Besides, what do you need treasure for out here? Is your life worth any of those things?\n我怀疑，还有什么能比你的枪更能证明你的死。再说，你在这荒郊野外要财宝做什么？你的命，值不值这些东西？"

    old "I...All right. I give up. I can't run forever. I am tired of this. I just want to be left in peace."
    new "I...All right. I give up. I can't run forever. I am tired of this. I just want to be left in peace.\n我……好吧。我认了。我不能永远逃下去。我受够了。我只想清静地过日子。"

    old "Good. We have a deal then. The Empire won't be looking for you anymore, but you may want to leave this island just to be safe."
    new "Good. We have a deal then. The Empire won't be looking for you anymore, but you may want to leave this island just to be safe.\n好。那我们成交了。帝国不会再找你了，不过为了保险起见，你也许还是离开这座岛为好。"

    old "Fine, fine. Just take the chest before I change my mind."
    new "Fine, fine. Just take the chest before I change my mind.\n行，行。趁我还没改主意，把箱子拿走吧。"

    old "Once we've gotten the chest from Logan, Jasper and I quickly head back to our ship, eager to see its contents."
    new "Once we've gotten the chest from Logan, Jasper and I quickly head back to our ship, eager to see its contents.\n从Logan那里拿到箱子后，Jasper和我迅速回到我们船上，急着想看看里面的东西。"

    old "The silence lingers a little too long. I'd initially thought that he was just lost in thought, but now I suspect he had different intentions."
    new "The silence lingers a little too long. I'd initially thought that he was just lost in thought, but now I suspect he had different intentions.\n沉默持续得有点太久了。我起初以为他只是陷入沉思，但现在我怀疑，他另有打算。"

    old "Logan?"
    new "Logan?\nLogan？"

    old "I turn to Jasper and, in a whisper, ask him if he can see Logan through the window. He shakes his head in response."
    new "I turn to Jasper and, in a whisper, ask him if he can see Logan through the window. He shakes his head in response.\n我转向Jasper，悄声问他，能不能从窗户看到Logan。他摇了摇头。"

    old "Sorry. I lost sight of him. I don't know where he went."
    new "Sorry. I lost sight of him. I don't know where he went.\n抱歉。我看不到他了。我不知道他去哪儿了。"

    old "The Empire should send better assassins."
    new "The Empire should send better assassins.\n帝国该派更好的刺客来。"

    old "Woah! He's behind us!"
    new "Woah! He's behind us!\n嚯！他在我们后面！"

    old "Now you die!"
    new "Now you die!\n现在你死定了！"

    old "Wait, we-"
    new "Wait, we-\n等等，我们——"

    old "[protag], he won't listen. He thinks we're here to kill him. He's not about to put his trust in a couple of strangers like us. We're going to have to fight him."
    new "[protag], he won't listen. He thinks we're here to kill him. He's not about to put his trust in a couple of strangers like us. We're going to have to fight him.\n[protag]，他不听的。他以为我们是来杀他的。他不会信任像我们这样的两个陌生人。我们只能跟他打一场了。"

    old "I'm going, I'm going! Don't shoot!"
    new "I'm going, I'm going! Don't shoot!\n我走，我走！别开枪！"

    old "We quickly run back to the ship. And, it's a good thing we did run. Even though I said not to shoot, Jasper and I hear bullets fly by our heads a few seconds later."
    new "We quickly run back to the ship. And, it's a good thing we did run. Even though I said not to shoot, Jasper and I hear bullets fly by our heads a few seconds later.\n我们飞快跑回船上。还好我们跑了。尽管我说了别开枪，但几秒钟后，Jasper和我还是听到子弹从我们头顶呼啸而过。"

    old "Shooting at us when we're retreating? What a bastard!"
    new "Shooting at us when we're retreating? What a bastard!\n我们撤退时还朝我们开枪？真是个混蛋！"

    old "Told you. Logan the red, he's a real bad guy."
    new "Told you. Logan the red, he's a real bad guy.\n早告诉你了。“红”Logan，他可是个真正的坏蛋。"

    old "Sorry, old man. We've come to take that gun and we won't take a 'no' for an answer."
    new "Sorry, old man. We've come to take that gun and we won't take a 'no' for an answer.\n抱歉，老家伙。我们是来拿那把枪的，可不会接受“不”字。"

    old "Come on, we've waited long enough! Open that damn chest already!"
    new "Come on, we've waited long enough! Open that damn chest already!\n快点，我们等得够久了！快打开那该死的箱子！"

    old "Somebody is impatient. Let's see... There we go. Ta dah!"
    new "Somebody is impatient. Let's see... There we go. Ta dah!\n有人等不及了。我们看看……成了。瞧！"

    old "The chest's lid clicks open, revealing the gun and some valuable looking rings as well."
    new "The chest's lid clicks open, revealing the gun and some valuable looking rings as well.\n箱盖咔嗒一声弹开，露出那把枪，还有几枚看起来很值钱的戒指。"

    old "Wow. I mean... I was here for the gun, but Logan had good taste in jewelry too! There's a quite a fortune here. My friends will be thrilled. They might even owe us one after we bring them these."
    new "Wow. I mean... I was here for the gun, but Logan had good taste in jewelry too! There's a quite a fortune here. My friends will be thrilled. They might even owe us one after we bring them these.\n哇。我是说……我本来是为枪来的，但Logan对珠宝也很有品味嘛！这里头可是相当一笔财富。我朋友会乐坏的。等我们把这些带给他们，他们说不定还欠我们一个人情。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]! I got the Pepperbox gun thanks to your help!"
    new "Thank you, [protag]! I got the Pepperbox gun thanks to your help!\n谢谢你，[protag]！多亏你的帮助，我拿到了Pepperbox枪！"

    old "You're welcome. I'm sure you'll put this to good use in the coming battles."
    new "You're welcome. I'm sure you'll put this to good use in the coming battles.\n不客气。我相信，在接下来的战斗里，你会好好用它。"

    old "I can hardly wait to try it out! Now, let's get back to Grimoire."
    new "I can hardly wait to try it out! Now, let's get back to Grimoire.\n我简直等不及要试试它了！现在，我们回Grimoire吧。"

    old "I'm really sorry, Jasper. I know you really wanted that gun. Maybe we can wait a bit and try again another day?"
    new "I'm really sorry, Jasper. I know you really wanted that gun. Maybe we can wait a bit and try again another day?\n真的很抱歉，Jasper。我知道你真的很想要那把枪。也许我们可以等一等，改天再试？"

    old "No. Logan is old but he's not stupid. He knows that we might come back. He's going to move away the first chance he gets and find an even better place to hide than this one."
    new "No. Logan is old but he's not stupid. He knows that we might come back. He's going to move away the first chance he gets and find an even better place to hide than this one.\n不。Logan虽然老了，但他不傻。他知道我们可能还会回来。他一有机会就会搬走，找个比这儿更好的藏身之处。"

    old "Unfortunately, the gun isn't worth wasting any more of our time on."
    new "Unfortunately, the gun isn't worth wasting any more of our time on.\n不幸的是，为这把枪再浪费我们的时间，不值得。"

    old "I see. I didn't think of that. Well... I guess all we can do is head back to Grimoire now."
    new "I see. I didn't think of that. Well... I guess all we can do is head back to Grimoire now.\n我明白了。我没想到这点。嗯……我想我们现在能做的，只有回Grimoire了。"

    old "Ah, I see that my favorite envoy from the council is back."
    new "Ah, I see that my favorite envoy from the council is back.\n啊，我看到，我最喜欢的议会特使回来了。"

    old "I'm also probably the only one from the council that would ever approach you."
    new "I'm also probably the only one from the council that would ever approach you.\n我也可能是议会里唯一一个会接近你的人。"

    old "You couldn't just take the compliment, could you? Why must you always ruin everything, [protag]?"
    new "You couldn't just take the compliment, could you? Why must you always ruin everything, [protag]?\n你就不能好好接受赞美吗？为什么你总要把一切都搞砸，[protag]？"

    old "Jasper laughs and then claps me on the shoulder in a friendly manner."
    new "Jasper laughs and then claps me on the shoulder in a friendly manner.\nJasper笑了，然后友好地拍了拍我的肩膀。"

    old "So what business brings you here today?"
    new "So what business brings you here today?\n那么，今天是什么事让你来这儿？"

    old "It's not really business. I was just thinking about that meeting we had with Apolimesho a while ago."
    new "It's not really business. I was just thinking about that meeting we had with Apolimesho a while ago.\n其实也不是什么正事。我只是想起了我们前阵子跟Apolimesho的那次会面。"

    old "Starting to have doubts about what will happen between you and the council once this is all over?"
    new "Starting to have doubts about what will happen between you and the council once this is all over?\n开始怀疑，等这一切结束后，你和议会之间会发生什么了？"

    old "No. I already told you my thoughts regarding that. It's not something I'm concerned about. When this is all over, I'll probably just end up wandering somewhere else."
    new "No. I already told you my thoughts regarding that. It's not something I'm concerned about. When this is all over, I'll probably just end up wandering somewhere else.\n不。关于那个，我已经告诉过你我的想法了。那不是我会担心的事。等这一切结束，我大概只会去别处流浪。"

    old "I was just wondering about... being a pirate, I guess. When you told Apolimesho that you were happy with your current situation and didn't envy him, was it true?"
    new "I was just wondering about... being a pirate, I guess. When you told Apolimesho that you were happy with your current situation and didn't envy him, was it true?\n我只是在好奇……当海盗这事，我想。你告诉Apolimesho，你对现状很满意，并不羡慕他，那是真的吗？"

    old "Of course? That's all you have to say about it? Such a short reply doesn't feel natural coming from you."
    new "Of course? That's all you have to say about it? Such a short reply doesn't feel natural coming from you.\n当然。你就这点要说的？这么短的答复，从你嘴里说出来可不太自然。"

    old "What can I say? Like all things in life there are upsides and downsides to it. For instance, as a pirate, you are an outlaw so you have to take steps to protect your identity."
    new "What can I say? Like all things in life there are upsides and downsides to it. For instance, as a pirate, you are an outlaw so you have to take steps to protect your identity.\n我能说什么呢？就像人生中所有事一样，有起有落。比如，作为海盗，你是个不法之徒，所以你得设法保护自己的身份。"

    old "And yet, here you are, sitting in the middle of Grimoire's docks without giving the city guards a second thought. It doesn't seem like you're taking that 'protecting your identity' bit seriously."
    new "And yet, here you are, sitting in the middle of Grimoire's docks without giving the city guards a second thought. It doesn't seem like you're taking that 'protecting your identity' bit seriously.\n然而，你现在就坐在这Grimoire码头正中央，对城卫兵完全不当回事。看起来，你并不怎么把“保护身份”当回事嘛。"

    old "That's where you're mistaken, [protag]. First of all, this is a rather peculiar situation. The problem at N'Mar is drawing the most attention from the city guards at the moment. They're much more concerned about spotting a zombie on the horizon than a potential pirate sitting peacefully on their docks."
    new "That's where you're mistaken, [protag]. First of all, this is a rather peculiar situation. The problem at N'Mar is drawing the most attention from the city guards at the moment. They're much more concerned about spotting a zombie on the horizon than a potential pirate sitting peacefully on their docks.\n这就是你搞错了，[protag]。首先，这是个相当特殊的情况。眼下，N'Mar的问题最吸引城卫兵的注意。他们更关心的是在地平线上发现一个僵尸，而不是一个安安静静坐在他们码头上的潜在海盗。"

    old "Still, even before this whole mess with the undead, this particular tactic has proven quite effective. There's nothing suspicious about a young man calmly sitting on the docks. I could be a fisherman, a merchant, or just a normal man enjoying a nice view of the sea. What reason would they have to suspect me?"
    new "Still, even before this whole mess with the undead, this particular tactic has proven quite effective. There's nothing suspicious about a young man calmly sitting on the docks. I could be a fisherman, a merchant, or just a normal man enjoying a nice view of the sea. What reason would they have to suspect me?\n不过，即使在这场亡灵乱子之前，这种特殊战术也相当有效。一个年轻人平静地坐在码头上，没什么可疑的。我可以是个渔夫、商人，或者只是个欣赏海景的普通人。他们有什么理由怀疑我？"

    old "Hiding in plain sight, huh? That's always seemed a bit risky to me, but I guess I can see it being beneficial in your case. Anway, back to our discussion about being a pirate. There have to be other disadvantages, right?"
    new "Hiding in plain sight, huh? That's always seemed a bit risky to me, but I guess I can see it being beneficial in your case. Anway, back to our discussion about being a pirate. There have to be other disadvantages, right?\n大隐隐于市，嗯？我一直觉得那样有点冒险，不过我想，在你这种情况下，确实有利。话说回来，回到我们关于当海盗的讨论。肯定还有别的坏处，对吧？"

    old "Why do you only want to know about the disadvantages? Oh well. I suppose it doesn't matter. Let's see... Ah, you can pretty much forget about having a stable relationship."
    new "Why do you only want to know about the disadvantages? Oh well. I suppose it doesn't matter. Let's see... Ah, you can pretty much forget about having a stable relationship.\n你为什么只想知道坏处？哦，算了。我想也无所谓。让我想想……啊，稳定的感情关系，你基本可以别想了。"

    old "How come?"
    new "How come?\n怎么说？"

    old "As a pirate, you're always on the move. You rarely stay in one place for long and, even if that wasn't a dealbreaker, you'd still need to trust that the person you were seeing wouldn't reveal that you are a pirate. I mean, you could just not tell them, but that usually comes back to haunt you later."
    new "As a pirate, you're always on the move. You rarely stay in one place for long and, even if that wasn't a dealbreaker, you'd still need to trust that the person you were seeing wouldn't reveal that you are a pirate. I mean, you could just not tell them, but that usually comes back to haunt you later.\n作为海盗，你总是在路上。你很少在一个地方久留，而且，即便这不成问题，你仍然得相信，你交往的那个人不会泄露你是海盗。我是说，你可以干脆不告诉他们，但那通常会在日后回来找你的麻烦。"

    old "Have you ever hidden something from someone close to you? And I'm not talking about something little. I'm talking about a large aspect of your life."
    new "Have you ever hidden something from someone close to you? And I'm not talking about something little. I'm talking about a large aspect of your life.\n你有没有对亲近的人隐瞒过什么？我不是说小事。我说的是你人生中很大的一部分。"

    old "Yes. I have done things like that in the past."
    new "Yes. I have done things like that in the past.\n有。我过去做过那样的事。"

    old "And present. In fact, I'm hiding something from you right now, Jasper. If you and the others knew that I accepted a deal to become a vampire..."
    new "And present. In fact, I'm hiding something from you right now, Jasper. If you and the others knew that I accepted a deal to become a vampire...\n现在也有。事实上，我此刻就在对你隐瞒着一些事，Jasper。如果你和其他人知道，我接受了一个变成吸血鬼的交易……"

    old "And I don't blame you for it. It's natural. Everyone has secrets to hide. Saying otherwise is just another lie. No matter how close you are to someone, there will always be something in your past that you don't share with them."
    new "And I don't blame you for it. It's natural. Everyone has secrets to hide. Saying otherwise is just another lie. No matter how close you are to someone, there will always be something in your past that you don't share with them.\n我不怪你。这很自然。每个人都有秘密要藏。说不是这样，不过是又一个谎言。不管你和一个人有多亲近，你的过去里总会有你不愿跟他分享的东西。"

    old "What if I really have nothing to hide? Like, I have no secrets of any sort?"
    new "What if I really have nothing to hide? Like, I have no secrets of any sort?\n如果我其实没什么可隐瞒的呢？比如，我什么秘密都没有？"

    old "Then your life is probably boring and nobody would want to stay with you anyway."
    new "Then your life is probably boring and nobody would want to stay with you anyway.\n那你的生活大概很无聊，反正也没人愿意跟你待在一起。"

    old "I laugh and then playfully punch him in the shoulder, almost making him fall over on his side."
    new "I laugh and then playfully punch him in the shoulder, almost making him fall over on his side.\n我笑了，然后开玩笑地捶了下他的肩膀，差点让他侧身摔倒。"

    old "Honestly? No. I never had to hide anything from anyone close to me."
    new "Honestly? No. I never had to hide anything from anyone close to me.\n老实说？不。我从来不用对亲近的人隐瞒任何事。"

    old "Technically that isn't a lie, right? I'm not a vampire yet. I just neglected to tell anyone that I'm going to become one soon."
    new "Technically that isn't a lie, right? I'm not a vampire yet. I just neglected to tell anyone that I'm going to become one soon.\n严格来说那不算撒谎，对吧？我还没变成吸血鬼。我只是没告诉任何人，我很快就要变成吸血鬼了。"

    old "You just did. You lied to me just now. I'm not sure about what yet, but I'll find out. I'm pretty good at knowing when someone is lying to me."
    new "You just did. You lied to me just now. I'm not sure about what yet, but I'll find out. I'm pretty good at knowing when someone is lying to me.\n你刚刚就撒谎了。你刚刚骗了我。我还不知道是为什么，但我会查出来的。我很擅长看出一个人什么时候在骗我。"

    old "You're scaring me a little now."
    new "You're scaring me a little now.\n你现在有点吓到我了。"

    old "Nah, don't worry too much. I can do it without resorting to torture. I only need to look you in the eyes."
    new "Nah, don't worry too much. I can do it without resorting to torture. I only need to look you in the eyes.\n嗐，别太担心。我不必动用酷刑也能做到。我只需要看着你的眼睛。"

    old "Getting back on topic, you could always get involved with another pirate, couldn't you? I'm pretty sure that all that time stuck on a ship together is bound to result in at least a few relationships. You can't tell me that it's never happened."
    new "Getting back on topic, you could always get involved with another pirate, couldn't you? I'm pretty sure that all that time stuck on a ship together is bound to result in at least a few relationships. You can't tell me that it's never happened.\n回到正题，你总可以和另一个海盗在一起，不是吗？我很肯定，一起困在船上的那些时间，必然至少催生出几段感情。你可别告诉我，这种事从没发生过。"

    old "Oh, it happens. Frequently, even. But you're forgetting about two important things. First of all, being in a relationship on... 'your day job' is not a good idea. For instance, let's say that you fail to assault a ship and your partner blames you for it. Or when it's time to split the loot, someone else disagrees about you or your partner's share."
    new "Oh, it happens. Frequently, even. But you're forgetting about two important things. First of all, being in a relationship on... 'your day job' is not a good idea. For instance, let's say that you fail to assault a ship and your partner blames you for it. Or when it's time to split the loot, someone else disagrees about you or your partner's share.\n哦，这种事经常发生。但你忘了两个重要的事情。首先，在……“你的日常工作”里发展关系，不是个好主意。比如，假设你们没能攻下一艘船，你的搭档为此责怪你。或者到了分赃的时候，别人对你或你搭档的那份有异议。"

    old "I could go on and on, but I imagine that you get the idea. A lot of drama can start over a petty relationship squabble and that is something you do not need in such a confined space. Especially since most of the time you won't be able to just leave seeing as you'd be out on the ocean."
    new "I could go on and on, but I imagine that you get the idea. A lot of drama can start over a petty relationship squabble and that is something you do not need in such a confined space. Especially since most of the time you won't be able to just leave seeing as you'd be out on the ocean.\n我可以一直说下去，但我想你明白我的意思。一场小小的感情争执，就可能闹出很多风波，而在这般狭小的空间里，你可不需要那种东西。尤其是大部分时候，你身在海上，根本没法一走了之。"

    old "Even if everything somehow went smoothly between you and your partner, you'd still need to consider how short the average life of a pirate is. We try to avoid conflicts with heavily armed ships, but there's always a chance the captain might decide otherwise. Senya is very prudent, but sometimes you can't avoid taking risky jobs."
    new "Even if everything somehow went smoothly between you and your partner, you'd still need to consider how short the average life of a pirate is. We try to avoid conflicts with heavily armed ships, but there's always a chance the captain might decide otherwise. Senya is very prudent, but sometimes you can't avoid taking risky jobs.\n即便你和搭档之间一切顺利，你仍得考虑，海盗的平均寿命有多短。我们尽量避免和全副武装的船只发生冲突，但船长总有可能另做决定。Senya非常谨慎，但有时你躲不开接那些冒险的活儿。"

    old "Our assault at N'Mar will be risky too... Back to the point though, you could begin a relationship with a fellow pirate and everything could be going well but there will still be that one day after a particularly hard battle. The smoke will clear and you'll find his body lying on the ground, covered in blood. And you won't be able to do anything but cry over your loss."
    new "Our assault at N'Mar will be risky too... Back to the point though, you could begin a relationship with a fellow pirate and everything could be going well but there will still be that one day after a particularly hard battle. The smoke will clear and you'll find his body lying on the ground, covered in blood. And you won't be able to do anything but cry over your loss.\n我们攻打N'Mar也会很冒险……不过回到正题，你可以和一个海盗同伴开始一段感情，一切可能都很顺利，但总会有一天，在一场格外惨烈的战斗之后，硝烟散去，你会发现他的尸体倒在地上，浑身是血。而你除了为失去他而痛哭，什么都做不了。"

    old "I get the feeling that Jasper is speaking from his own personal experience. I can't be sure, but..."
    new "I get the feeling that Jasper is speaking from his own personal experience. I can't be sure, but...\n我感觉到，Jasper是在说自己的亲身经历。我无法确定，但……"

    old "Huh? Who said that this was about me?"
    new "Huh? Who said that this was about me?\n嗯？谁说过这是关于我的？"

    old "I thought-"
    new "I thought-\n我以为——"

    old "You thought wrong, [protag]."
    new "You thought wrong, [protag].\n你想错了，[protag]。"

    old "Based on Jasper's reaction, I know that I was right. That last bit was definitely about him. Still, I let it go for now. There's no point in pushing it if he's not willing to talk about it."
    new "Based on Jasper's reaction, I know that I was right. That last bit was definitely about him. Still, I let it go for now. There's no point in pushing it if he's not willing to talk about it.\n从Jasper的反应来看，我知道我说中了。最后那段绝对是关于他自己。不过，我暂且放下了。如果他不愿谈，逼问也没有意义。"

    old "It is. I've seen it happen many times with my own eyes. Even if it's not your partner, even if it was just a friend, an aquaintance even... it's still terrible to be talking to someone in the morning only to find them dead in the evening."
    new "It is. I've seen it happen many times with my own eyes. Even if it's not your partner, even if it was just a friend, an aquaintance even... it's still terrible to be talking to someone in the morning only to find them dead in the evening.\n是的。我亲眼见过很多次。即便不是你的搭档，即便只是个朋友，甚至是点头之交……早上还在跟一个人说话，晚上却发现他已经死了，这仍然很可怕。"

    old "Hopefully that won't happen to any of us."
    new "Hopefully that won't happen to any of us.\n希望那不会发生在我们任何人身上。"

    old "Jasper nods."
    new "Jasper nods.\nJasper点了点头。"

    old "It's weird. Fighting the undead is more dangerous than most of the things we do as pirates, but somehow I still think that this will all end well for us."
    new "It's weird. Fighting the undead is more dangerous than most of the things we do as pirates, but somehow I still think that this will all end well for us.\n说来也怪。跟亡灵作战，比我们做海盗的大部分事都更危险，但不知怎的，我仍觉得这一切对我们会有个好结局。"

    old "Oh? Is that so? I like this optimistic version of Jasper."
    new "Oh? Is that so? I like this optimistic version of Jasper.\n哦？是吗？我喜欢这个乐观版的Jasper。"

    old "Haha. Just don't get too used to it."
    new "Haha. Just don't get too used to it.\n哈哈。只是别太习惯了。"

    old "Now, if you'll excuse me, [protag], I need to head back to my ship. I'll talk to you soon."
    new "Now, if you'll excuse me, [protag], I need to head back to my ship. I'll talk to you soon.\n好了，失陪了，[protag]，我得回船上去。回头再聊。"

    old "Oh hey, [protag]. Did you come to be entertained by my silly questions again?"
    new "Oh hey, [protag]. Did you come to be entertained by my silly questions again?\n哦，嘿，[protag]。你又来让我那些蠢问题逗你开心了？"

    old "Maybe. This time I thought I might ask you one though."
    new "Maybe. This time I thought I might ask you one though.\n也许吧。不过这次，我想问你一个。"

    old "Oh? I'm intrigued. Go ahead and ask your question. I'm curious to know what's going on inside that head of yours."
    new "Oh? I'm intrigued. Go ahead and ask your question. I'm curious to know what's going on inside that head of yours.\n哦？我倒来了兴致。尽管问吧。我很好奇你脑子里在想什么。"

    old "Jasper playfully pokes my head with one of his fingers. I scowl at him as he grins and raises his hands in surrender."
    new "Jasper playfully pokes my head with one of his fingers. I scowl at him as he grins and raises his hands in surrender.\nJasper用一根手指调皮地戳了戳我的头。我朝他皱眉，而他咧嘴一笑，举起双手作投降状。"

    old "So, my question is a simple one, but it is also one that can be hard to answer. What do you want? I'm not talking about any basic desires that can be fullfilled quickly either. I'm looking for something more long term. What do you, Jasper, really want out of this life? And please, don't tell me it's 'to be a pirate' because I'm not buying that."
    new "So, my question is a simple one, but it is also one that can be hard to answer. What do you want? I'm not talking about any basic desires that can be fullfilled quickly either. I'm looking for something more long term. What do you, Jasper, really want out of this life? And please, don't tell me it's 'to be a pirate' because I'm not buying that.\n那么，我的问题很简单，但也是个可能很难回答的问题。你想要什么？我说的也不是那些能很快满足的基本欲望。我要找的是更长远的东西。你，Jasper，究竟想从这人生中得到什么？还有，请别告诉我是“当海盗”，因为我不买这个账。"

    old "Hmph. That was going to be my answer too."
    new "Hmph. That was going to be my answer too.\n哼。我本来也打算那么回答。"

    old "Which is why I banned it. Now, try again."
    new "Which is why I banned it. Now, try again.\n所以我才把它禁了。好了，再来一次。"

    old "Money then. I am a pirate after all, always looking for the greatest hidden treasures."
    new "Money then. I am a pirate after all, always looking for the greatest hidden treasures.\n那就是钱。毕竟我是海盗，总在寻找最了不起的宝藏。"

    old "No. It's not that."
    new "No. It's not that.\n不。不是这个。"

    old "And why can't it be that? Why would someone bother becoming a pirate if it wasn't for the money?"
    new "And why can't it be that? Why would someone bother becoming a pirate if it wasn't for the money?\n为什么不能是这个？如果不是为了钱，谁还会费劲去当海盗？"

    old "There are a lot of safer jobs that pay better. If you were really after money, I'd think you'd at least look into some of those ones. Besides, you don't strike me as a greedy man, despite what you'd like the others to think."
    new "There are a lot of safer jobs that pay better. If you were really after money, I'd think you'd at least look into some of those ones. Besides, you don't strike me as a greedy man, despite what you'd like the others to think.\n有很多更安全、报酬更高的工作。如果你真是冲着钱，我觉得你至少会去考虑其中一些。再说，你不像个贪婪的人，尽管你希望别人那么看你。"

    old "Once again, you are correct. The last thing I want is to end up like one of those Grimoire nobles. Puah!"
    new "Once again, you are correct. The last thing I want is to end up like one of those Grimoire nobles. Puah!\n再一次，你说对了。我最不想的，就是变成那些Grimoire贵族中的一员。呸！"

    old "Why the disgust?"
    new "Why the disgust?\n为什么这么厌恶？"

    old "Don't you see what's happening? We're fighting an undead threat like no other with their small change! What the hell? If something was threatening my very existence, I would sell my house, my jewelry-- everything! I'd do anything within my power to make sure that the threat was dealt with."
    new "Don't you see what's happening? We're fighting an undead threat like no other with their small change! What the hell? If something was threatening my very existence, I would sell my house, my jewelry-- everything! I'd do anything within my power to make sure that the threat was dealt with.\n你没看见正在发生什么吗？我们在对付一场前所未有的亡灵威胁，就靠他们那点零钱！搞什么鬼？如果有什么东西威胁到我的生存，我会卖掉房子、珠宝——一切！我会尽我所能，确保威胁被解决。"

    old "But what do these nobles do instead? They try to get us to do the job for a mere pittance, hoping that they can hold on to their wealth as the world around them falls apart."
    new "But what do these nobles do instead? They try to get us to do the job for a mere pittance, hoping that they can hold on to their wealth as the world around them falls apart.\n可这些贵族做了什么呢？他们试图让我们为了那点可怜的钱去卖命，指望在世界在他们周围崩塌时，还能攥住自己的财富。"

    old "Well, money definitely isn't what you want then. Or rather, you don't want to become a rich, lazy, coward of a noble. So, back to the original question: what do you really want?"
    new "Well, money definitely isn't what you want then. Or rather, you don't want to become a rich, lazy, coward of a noble. So, back to the original question: what do you really want?\n嗯，那钱肯定不是你想要的了。或者说，你不想变成贵族那种富有、懒惰的懦夫。那么，回到最初的问题：你真正想要的是什么？"

    old "What exactly do you want me to say? What do you expect me to say?"
    new "What exactly do you want me to say? What do you expect me to say?\n你到底想让我说什么？你指望我说什么？"

    old "Why are you asking me? You're the one who is supposed to be answering the question."
    new "Why are you asking me? You're the one who is supposed to be answering the question.\n你为什么问我？该回答问题的人是你才对。"

    old "But, if I had to hazard a guess... You were aspiring for a role on the council before. No ordinary man has such ambitions. To me, you seem like someone who craves power. Am I right?"
    new "But, if I had to hazard a guess... You were aspiring for a role on the council before. No ordinary man has such ambitions. To me, you seem like someone who craves power. Am I right?\n不过，如果非要我猜的话……你以前渴望过在议会里谋得一席之位。普通人不会有这样的野心。在我看来，你像是个渴望权力的人。我说对了吗？"

    old "Heh. You're smart, [protag]. Smarter than you look."
    new "Heh. You're smart, [protag]. Smarter than you look.\n呵。你很聪明，[protag]。比看起来聪明。"

    old "Was that supposed to be a compliment? Because it's not going to work. I'm still waiting for your answer."
    new "Was that supposed to be a compliment? Because it's not going to work. I'm still waiting for your answer.\n那算恭维吗？因为这可不管用。我还在等你的答案呢。"

    old "Fine, fine. So, you're asking me about power? If I crave it? Power is a burden. That much is clear to me. It wasn't back then, but the more I sit here on this little pier, alone, watching events unfold around me, the more I'm sure of it."
    new "Fine, fine. So, you're asking me about power? If I crave it? Power is a burden. That much is clear to me. It wasn't back then, but the more I sit here on this little pier, alone, watching events unfold around me, the more I'm sure of it.\n好，好。那么，你是在问我关于权力的事？问我是否渴望它？权力是一种负担。这一点我已经很清楚了。当年不是这样，但我越是独自坐在这小码头上，看着周遭的事件展开，就越是确信。"

    old "You know, it's not all that bad. Power can buy you the tastiest food, the best company, luxurious homes..."
    new "You know, it's not all that bad. Power can buy you the tastiest food, the best company, luxurious homes...\n你知道，其实也没那么糟。权力能给你买到最美味的美食、最好的陪伴、奢华的宅邸……"

    old "And enemies. A lot of enemies. But I don't have to tell you that. I'm sure you know that pretty well by now. Still, you haven't really experienced anything yet."
    new "And enemies. A lot of enemies. But I don't have to tell you that. I'm sure you know that pretty well by now. Still, you haven't really experienced anything yet.\n还有敌人。很多敌人。不过这不用我告诉你。我相信你现在已经很清楚了。只是，你还没有真正经历过什么。"

    old "Really? Facing hordes of undead and bloodthirsty vampires doesn't count as anything to you?"
    new "Really? Facing hordes of undead and bloodthirsty vampires doesn't count as anything to you?\n是吗？面对成群亡灵和嗜血的吸血鬼，对你来说不算什么？"

    old "It counts for something. Just... think about this: at least you know who your enemies are."
    new "It counts for something. Just... think about this: at least you know who your enemies are.\n算是有那么点。只是……想想这个：至少你知道你的敌人是谁。"

    old "They're right there in front of you and you can clearly see them. And even the ones you can't see are at least known to you. You know that they're undead, vampires. You know their weaknesses and you can prepare yourself as you stay protected behind Grimoire's walls, planning a proper strategy."
    new "They're right there in front of you and you can clearly see them. And even the ones you can't see are at least known to you. You know that they're undead, vampires. You know their weaknesses and you can prepare yourself as you stay protected behind Grimoire's walls, planning a proper strategy.\n他们就在你面前，你看得清清楚楚。即便那些看不见的，也至少是你能知道的。你知道他们是亡灵、是吸血鬼。你知道他们的弱点，可以做好准备，在Grimoire的城墙后守得稳稳当当，谋划恰当的战术。"

    old "Is there a point to all this?"
    new "Is there a point to all this?\n你说这些有重点吗？"

    old "I'm getting there. Just bear with me. Now, let's imagine that you're a powerful, famous politician. A king even, if that's what you'd prefer. Do you know who your real enemies are? No. You don't know who you can trust. You can't be sure that your friends are really your friends or if your followers are loyal to you or your power. Isn't that worse?"
    new "I'm getting there. Just bear with me. Now, let's imagine that you're a powerful, famous politician. A king even, if that's what you'd prefer. Do you know who your real enemies are? No. You don't know who you can trust. You can't be sure that your friends are really your friends or if your followers are loyal to you or your power. Isn't that worse?\n我快说到了。就再忍耐一下。现在，想象你是一个有权有势、赫赫有名的政客。甚至是个国王，如果你更喜欢那样的话。你知道你真正的敌人是谁吗？不。你不知道你能信任谁。你无法确定你的朋友真是你的朋友，或者你的追随者忠于的是你这个人，还是你的权力。那难道不更糟吗？"

    old "I like the simplicity of knowing who your enemy is. Even if they're strong, it's still easier than fighting some obscure enemy that hides within your own government or court. Or even your friends."
    new "I like the simplicity of knowing who your enemy is. Even if they're strong, it's still easier than fighting some obscure enemy that hides within your own government or court. Or even your friends.\n我喜欢那种清楚敌人是谁的简单。即便他们很强，也还是比对付躲在你自己的政府或宫廷里、甚至你朋友中的某个隐晦敌人要容易。"

    old "So that's why I don't regret my life. As a pirate, I know who my enemies are. If I was still on the council? I would have to constantly watch my back. You wouldn't think so, but it's more likely that I'd have gotten literally stabbed in the back by one of them than my fellow pirates."
    new "So that's why I don't regret my life. As a pirate, I know who my enemies are. If I was still on the council? I would have to constantly watch my back. You wouldn't think so, but it's more likely that I'd have gotten literally stabbed in the back by one of them than my fellow pirates.\n所以我才不后悔自己的人生。作为海盗，我知道我的敌人是谁。如果我还在议会里？我就得时刻提防背后。你也许不这么想，但被他们中的某个人背后捅刀，比被我的海盗同伴捅刀更有可能。"

    old "Interesting. I suppose that you do have a point."
    new "Interesting. I suppose that you do have a point.\n有意思。我想你确实有道理。"

    old "I always do."
    new "I always do.\n我一向有道理。"

    old "Very funny. Still... All you plan to do is be a pirate for the rest of your life?"
    new "Very funny. Still... All you plan to do is be a pirate for the rest of your life?\n很好笑。不过……你打算余生就只当个海盗吗？"

    old "I haven't thought that far ahead. To be honest with you, [protag], I live my life day by day. I'm not making long term plans. Unless..."
    new "I haven't thought that far ahead. To be honest with you, [protag], I live my life day by day. I'm not making long term plans. Unless...\n我没想那么远。跟你说实话，[protag]，我过一天算一天。我不做长远计划。除非……"

    old "Jasper pauses for a moment and looks me in the eye.. What is he thinking? Should I say something?"
    new "Jasper pauses for a moment and looks me in the eye.. What is he thinking? Should I say something?\nJasper顿了顿，注视着我的眼睛。他在想什么？我该说点什么吗？"

    old "Uh...!"
    new "Uh...!\n呃……！"

    old "Oh, wow! Your face is so red! I never thought I'd get the chance to see you so flustered!"
    new "Oh, wow! Your face is so red! I never thought I'd get the chance to see you so flustered!\n哦，哇！你的脸好红！我从没想过能有机会看到你如此慌乱！"

    old "Well, now you have. Are you happy?"
    new "Well, now you have. Are you happy?\n现在你看到了。高兴了吗？"

    old "Very."
    new "Very.\n非常。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]. You read my mind. Are you sure you're not a shaman like Nuala?"
    new "Thank you, [protag]. You read my mind. Are you sure you're not a shaman like Nuala?\n谢谢你，[protag]。你读懂了我的心思。你确定你不是像Nuala那样的萨满吗？"

    old "I wish. It'd be nice to be as charming, strong and beautiful as she is."
    new "I wish. It'd be nice to be as charming, strong and beautiful as she is.\n我倒是想。能像她那样迷人、坚强又美丽，该多好。"

    old "Hey, don't sell yourself short. You're a good looking woman too, you know? You can trust me on that too since I'm saying that without ulterior motives. It's a sincere compliment. The kind you won't hear from men or women who want to have sex with you."
    new "Hey, don't sell yourself short. You're a good looking woman too, you know? You can trust me on that too since I'm saying that without ulterior motives. It's a sincere compliment. The kind you won't hear from men or women who want to have sex with you.\n嘿，别妄自菲薄。你也是个漂亮的女人，你知道吗？这一点你也可以信我，因为我这么说没有别的用心。这是一句真诚的赞美。那种你从想跟你上床的男人或女人嘴里听不到的赞美。"

    old "Heh. Thank you, Jasper. That's very nice of you."
    new "Heh. Thank you, Jasper. That's very nice of you.\n呵。谢谢你，Jasper。你真好。"

    old "...unless, someone or something made me change my mind, obviously."
    new "...unless, someone or something made me change my mind, obviously.\n……除非，某个人或某件事让我改变了主意，显而易见。"

    old "Someone like me?"
    new "Someone like me?\n像我这样的人？"

    old "Who knows? Perhaps."
    new "Who knows? Perhaps.\n谁知道呢？也许。"

    old "[protag], I am not going to deny it. When I'm around you, I feel good. You're great company and I'm really enjoying being a part of your team. Honestly, I haven't felt like this since... well, it's been a long time. And I haven't said something like this to anyone else either. You really do mean a lot to me."
    new "[protag], I am not going to deny it. When I'm around you, I feel good. You're great company and I'm really enjoying being a part of your team. Honestly, I haven't felt like this since... well, it's been a long time. And I haven't said something like this to anyone else either. You really do mean a lot to me.\n[protag]，我不会否认。在你身边时，我感觉很好。你是个很好的伙伴，我真的很享受成为你团队的一员。说实话，我很久没有过这种感觉了……嗯，已经很久了。而且我也没有对别的任何人说过这种话。你对我真的很重要。"

    old "However, I cannot promise anything to you right now. There's just too much going on. The undead, me being a pirate. I... I can't see how we could spend more time together after all of this is over."
    new "However, I cannot promise anything to you right now. There's just too much going on. The undead, me being a pirate. I... I can't see how we could spend more time together after all of this is over.\n不过，我现在没法向你承诺任何事。眼下有太多事在发生。亡灵，我当海盗这件事。我……我看不出这一切结束后，我们还能怎么更多地在一起。"

    old "I mean, you'll probably become an important member of the council and, in that case, it'd be in your interest to avoid people like me. Associating with pirates is a quick way to destroy your reputation."
    new "I mean, you'll probably become an important member of the council and, in that case, it'd be in your interest to avoid people like me. Associating with pirates is a quick way to destroy your reputation.\n我是说，你可能会成为议会的重要成员，那样的话，避开我这样的人对你才有利。跟海盗来往，是毁掉你名声的捷径。"

    old "I grab Jasper's hands and look him in the eyes. He wears a pained expression on his face, a mix of sadness and resignation."
    new "I grab Jasper's hands and look him in the eyes. He wears a pained expression on his face, a mix of sadness and resignation.\n我抓住Jasper的双手，直视他的眼睛。他脸上是一副痛苦的表情，混杂着悲伤与认命。"

    old "Slow down, Jasper. I don't know what I'll do after all of this is over. I don't even know if I'll survive our mission at N'Mar. It'd be really naive for us to start thinking about the future when there is so much lef to do. I say that we use the 'Jasper method' for now."
    new "Slow down, Jasper. I don't know what I'll do after all of this is over. I don't even know if I'll survive our mission at N'Mar. It'd be really naive for us to start thinking about the future when there is so much lef to do. I say that we use the 'Jasper method' for now.\n慢慢来，Jasper。我也不知道这一切结束后我会做什么。我甚至不知道，自己能否在N'Mar的任务中活下来。还有那么多事要做，现在就开始考虑未来，实在太过天真。我说，我们暂且用“Jasper方法”吧。"

    old "You'd think I'd know all about this 'Jasper method' since I'm clearly the inspiration for it, but I have no idea what you're talking about."
    new "You'd think I'd know all about this 'Jasper method' since I'm clearly the inspiration for it, but I have no idea what you're talking about.\n你该想到，我对这“Jasper方法”一清二楚，毕竟我显然是它的灵感来源，可我却完全不知道你在说什么。"

    old "Haha. I'm talking about what you said before. Live day by day. Enjoy the few moments we spend together, all of our philosophical discussions and the jokes. We don't know what the future has in store for us so, for now, let's just enjoy the present."
    new "Haha. I'm talking about what you said before. Live day by day. Enjoy the few moments we spend together, all of our philosophical discussions and the jokes. We don't know what the future has in store for us so, for now, let's just enjoy the present.\n哈哈。我说的就是你之前说过的话。过一天算一天。享受我们共处的这些时光，我们所有的哲学讨论和那些玩笑。我们不知道未来为我们准备了什么，所以，眼下就让我们享受当下吧。"

    old "Jasper remains silent for awhile. Then, he smiles and hugs me."
    new "Jasper remains silent for awhile. Then, he smiles and hugs me.\nJasper沉默了一会儿。然后，他微笑着拥抱了我。"

    old "Yes. Yes, I'd like that."
    new "Yes. Yes, I'd like that.\n好。好，我愿意。"

    old "I stay there for some time enjoying Jasper's company, but eventually, as always, I have to get back to work."
    new "I stay there for some time enjoying Jasper's company, but eventually, as always, I have to get back to work.\n我在那里待了一会儿，享受着Jasper的陪伴，但最终，和往常一样，我得回去工作了。"

    old "I received an invitation from Jasper to meet him at the docks this evening. I'm not sure what he wants, but I'm always intrigued by what he might have planned when it comes to Jasper."
    new "I received an invitation from Jasper to meet him at the docks this evening. I'm not sure what he wants, but I'm always intrigued by what he might have planned when it comes to Jasper.\n我收到Jasper的邀请，今晚到码头见他。我不知道他想要什么，但每当涉及Jasper，我总对他可能计划的事感到好奇。"

    old "[protag], you came!"
    new "[protag], you came!\n[protag]，你来了！"

    old "Of course. I couldn't ignore such a formal invitation."
    new "Of course. I couldn't ignore such a formal invitation.\n当然。这么正式的邀请，我怎能不理。"

    old "I do still remember some of the etiquette I learned while being around Apolimesho."
    new "I do still remember some of the etiquette I learned while being around Apolimesho.\n在Apolimesho身边时学到的一些礼仪，我倒还记得。"

    old "You know, now that you mention it, the writing style did remind me of a decrepit old man."
    new "You know, now that you mention it, the writing style did remind me of a decrepit old man.\n你知道吗，既然你提起来，那文风确实让我想起一个老朽的老人。"

    old "Hey! That's not a nice thing to say. Especially considering what I'm about to offer you."
    new "Hey! That's not a nice thing to say. Especially considering what I'm about to offer you.\n嘿！这话可不中听。尤其考虑到我接下来要给你的是什么。"

    old "Hm? What are you talking about?"
    new "Hm? What are you talking about?\n嗯？你在说什么？"

    old "Now, now. I don't want to spoil the surprise. Come, follow me."
    new "Now, now. I don't want to spoil the surprise. Come, follow me.\n现在先别。我可不想破坏惊喜。来，跟我来。"

    old "He leads me down the docks and eventually we get onto a smaller ship. Some time has passed, but I think I recognize it."
    new "He leads me down the docks and eventually we get onto a smaller ship. Some time has passed, but I think I recognize it.\n他领着我沿码头走去，最后我们上了一艘小一点的船。已经过去一段时间了，但我想我认出了它。"

    old "Is this the Esmeralda? The ship those friends of yours lent you when you wanted to retrieve those guns?"
    new "Is this the Esmeralda? The ship those friends of yours lent you when you wanted to retrieve those guns?\n这是Esmeralda吗？就是你想去取那些枪时，你那些朋友借给你的那艘船？"

    old "You have a good eye, [protag]. It is indeed the Esmeralda and she's mine now."
    new "You have a good eye, [protag]. It is indeed the Esmeralda and she's mine now.\n你眼力真好，[protag]。这确实是Esmeralda，现在它是我的了。"

    old "Yours?!"
    new "Yours?!\n你的？！"

    old "I mean, I remember you mentioning that they might lend you the ship again, especially after our success, but..."
    new "I mean, I remember you mentioning that they might lend you the ship again, especially after our success, but...\n我是说，我记得你提过，他们可能再把船借给你，尤其在我们成功之后，但……"

    old "What you did you do to convince them to sell you their ship?"
    new "What you did you do to convince them to sell you their ship?\n你做了什么，才说服他们把船卖给你的？"

    old "You remember the prior conversation we had? The one about power? Those men, they crave power."
    new "You remember the prior conversation we had? The one about power? Those men, they crave power.\n你还记得我们之前的谈话吗？关于权力的那次？那些人，他们渴望权力。"

    old "And how exactly does giving you a ship help those people obtain power?"
    new "And how exactly does giving you a ship help those people obtain power?\n而送你一艘船，究竟是怎么帮那些人获得权力的？"

    old "They observed me. They...observed us. They saw how close we got and they are well aware of who you are, [protag]. You're not only someone who works for the council. You also have a good relationship with the amazon's queen, with the desert tribes..."
    new "They observed me. They...observed us. They saw how close we got and they are well aware of who you are, [protag]. You're not only someone who works for the council. You also have a good relationship with the amazon's queen, with the desert tribes...\n他们观察了我。他们……观察了我们。他们看到我们走得多近，而且他们很清楚你是谁，[protag]。你不仅是为议会工作的人。你还跟Amazon女王、沙漠部落关系很好……"

    old "Basically, you're important. And, since you visit me so often, they assumed that you considered me important too. They asked me what I wanted to keep you close to me and I told them that I wanted this ship, the Esmeralda."
    new "Basically, you're important. And, since you visit me so often, they assumed that you considered me important too. They asked me what I wanted to keep you close to me and I told them that I wanted this ship, the Esmeralda.\n基本上，你很重要。而既然你经常来看我，他们就认定，你也认为我很重要。他们问我，想用什么来把你留在我身边，我告诉他们，我想要这艘船，Esmeralda。"

    old "What Jasper is saying is that he used my reputation to obtain something for himself. How do I feel about this?"
    new "What Jasper is saying is that he used my reputation to obtain something for himself. How do I feel about this?\nJasper的意思是，他利用我的名声为自己弄到了东西。我对此作何感想？"

    old "Well, I'm glad that you got something out of this."
    new "Well, I'm glad that you got something out of this.\n嗯，我很高兴你从中有所收获。"

    old "I never thought I would have my own ship. Yes, it's small but that's not a bad thing. It means that I can travel faster and it's more maneuverable... What is it? Is something bothering you?"
    new "I never thought I would have my own ship. Yes, it's small but that's not a bad thing. It means that I can travel faster and it's more maneuverable... What is it? Is something bothering you?\n我从没想过自己会有自己的船。是的，它很小，但那不是坏事。这意味着我能更快地航行，也更灵活……怎么了？有什么事困扰你吗？"

    old "[protag]? The only reason I'm telling you this is because I don't want any secrets between us! I didn't have to say a single word to you!"
    new "[protag]? The only reason I'm telling you this is because I don't want any secrets between us! I didn't have to say a single word to you!\n[protag]？我告诉你这些，唯一的原因就是我不希望我们之间有任何秘密！我本可以一个字都不对你说的！"

    old "Sorry. It's just that... I feel used. It's like if you were pretending to be my friend only to get this ship."
    new "Sorry. It's just that... I feel used. It's like if you were pretending to be my friend only to get this ship.\n抱歉。只是……我觉得被利用了。就好像你假装跟我做朋友，只是为了得到这艘船。"

    old "Absolutely not! Can't you see it? I fooled those people. I pretended to follow you only because they asked, but I enjoyed every single moment we spent together since I met you! I consider you a real friend, [protag]."
    new "Absolutely not! Can't you see it? I fooled those people. I pretended to follow you only because they asked, but I enjoyed every single moment we spent together since I met you! I consider you a real friend, [protag].\n绝对不是！你还不明白吗？我骗的是那些人。我假装追随你，只是因为他们要求，但自我遇见你以来，我们一起度过的每一刻，我都很享受！我把你当真正的朋友，[protag]。"

    old "I smile to him and we hug. I am not completely sure if he is really telling me the truth or not, but I like to believe him."
    new "I smile to him and we hug. I am not completely sure if he is really telling me the truth or not, but I like to believe him.\n我对他微笑，我们拥抱。我不完全确定他说的是不是真话，但我愿意相信他。"

    old "So, we're going to take a ride in your new ship?"
    new "So, we're going to take a ride in your new ship?\n那么，我们要坐你的新船兜兜风吗？"

    old "Absolutely! Get in. We won't go too far since night is approaching, but seeing Grimoire's city lights from the ship is a very nice view."
    new "Absolutely! Get in. We won't go too far since night is approaching, but seeing Grimoire's city lights from the ship is a very nice view.\n当然！上来吧。夜幕就要降临，我们不会走太远，但从船上看Grimoire的万家灯火，是很好的景色。"

    old "The tone of my voice is cold."
    new "The tone of my voice is cold.\n我的声音很冷。"

    old "I don't like being exploited to someone else's advantage."
    new "I don't like being exploited to someone else's advantage.\n我不喜欢被人利用来为别人谋利。"

    old "[protag], you should know well that I like to be around you. I never planned this. It just happened. There was an opportunity and I took it."
    new "[protag], you should know well that I like to be around you. I never planned this. It just happened. There was an opportunity and I took it.\n[protag]，你应该清楚，我喜欢待在你身边。我从没计划过这个。它只是发生了。正好有机会，我就抓住了。"

    old "Maybe. I'm never sure if you're telling me the truth."
    new "Maybe. I'm never sure if you're telling me the truth.\n也许吧。我从来都不确定你是不是在说真话。"

    old "What? I swear-"
    new "What? I swear-\n什么？我发誓——"

    old "Save your breath. I'm happy you got your ship. Now excuse me, but I need to go back to my home."
    new "Save your breath. I'm happy you got your ship. Now excuse me, but I need to go back to my home.\n省省吧。我很高兴你得到了你的船。现在失陪了，我得回家了。"

    old "Wait a moment-"
    new "Wait a moment-\n等一下——"

    old "Look, Jasper. Right now it's better if I'm alone. But I expect full commitment from you to our cause, after you exploited my reputation to get that ship."
    new "Look, Jasper. Right now it's better if I'm alone. But I expect full commitment from you to our cause, after you exploited my reputation to get that ship.\n听着，Jasper。现在，我最好一个人待着。但你既然利用我的名声弄到了那艘船，我希望你对我们的事业做出完全的承诺。"

    old "Of course. I owe you a lot, [protag]."
    new "Of course. I owe you a lot, [protag].\n当然。我欠你很多，[protag]。"

    old "Jasper's tone was cold too. I move away from him. I don't know if he only wanted to show me the ship or he had ulterior motives, but I don't want to stay there any minute longer right now."
    new "Jasper's tone was cold too. I move away from him. I don't know if he only wanted to show me the ship or he had ulterior motives, but I don't want to stay there any minute longer right now.\nJasper的语气也很冷。我离开了他。我不知道他只是想给我看看船，还是别有用心，但此刻，我一分钟都不想再待下去。"

    old "Maybe it would have better if you never said anything then!"
    new "Maybe it would have better if you never said anything then!\n也许你当时什么都不说，反而更好！"

    old "What's the problem? I don't understand!"
    new "What's the problem? I don't understand!\n怎么了?我不明白!"

    old "You don't understand? You just put a value on our... relationship. How much am I worth to you? A ship will do, thanks. For a ship, I'll keep the envoy of Grimoire close to me. Maybe even make him believe that I want to be more than just a friend."
    new "You don't understand? You just put a value on our... relationship. How much am I worth to you? A ship will do, thanks. For a ship, I'll keep the envoy of Grimoire close to me. Maybe even make him believe that I want to be more than just a friend.\n你不明白吗?你刚刚给我们的……我们的关系标了价。我对你来说值多少?一艘船就够了,谢谢。为了这艘船,我会把Grimoire的特使留在身边,也许还会让他相信,我想和他不只是朋友。"

    old "Jasper tries to reach me, but I slap his arm away as I get off of the ship."
    new "Jasper tries to reach me, but I slap his arm away as I get off of the ship.\nJasper想拉住我,但我在下船时甩开了他的手。"

    old "Jasper continues calling after me, but I keep walking. I am too angry to deal with him right now."
    new "Jasper continues calling after me, but I keep walking. I am too angry to deal with him right now.\nJasper在身后一直喊我,可我没有停步。我现在太生气了,不想理他。"

    old "[protag], I love you."
    new "[protag], I love you.\n[protag],我爱你。"

    old "I stop short, freezing at those words. Did Jasper really say that? He loves me?"
    new "I stop short, freezing at those words. Did Jasper really say that? He loves me?\n我猛地停住脚步,被这句话定在原地。Jasper真的这么说吗?他爱我?"

    old "I am sorry. I am so sorry. I didn't think--"
    new "I am sorry. I am so sorry. I didn't think--\n对不起,我真的很抱歉。我没想过——"

    old "I turn around and see tears streaming down his cheeks."
    new "I turn around and see tears streaming down his cheeks.\n我转过身,看见泪水顺着他的脸颊流下来。"

    old "I think that he really means it."
    new "I think that he really means it.\n我想他是认真的。"

    old "With that thought in mind, I go over to him and plant a kiss on his lips. He seems a little surprised at first, but he figures it out quickly enough and kisses me back passionately."
    new "With that thought in mind, I go over to him and plant a kiss on his lips. He seems a little surprised at first, but he figures it out quickly enough and kisses me back passionately.\n抱着这个念头,我走到他面前,在他唇上印下一吻。他起初似乎有点意外,但很快就反应过来,热情地回吻了我。"

    old "That's what I wanted to hear."
    new "That's what I wanted to hear.\n这正是我想听的话。"

    old "So you're not angry with me anymore?"
    new "So you're not angry with me anymore?\n那你不再生我的气了?"

    old "Well, we will have to talk about this a bit more, but I think I can understand why you did it."
    new "Well, we will have to talk about this a bit more, but I think I can understand why you did it.\n好吧,这件事我们还得再聊聊,不过我想我能理解你为什么那么做。"

    old "I never meant to put a price on my feelings for you. It didn't even cross my mind that I might inadvertently be doing that."
    new "I never meant to put a price on my feelings for you. It didn't even cross my mind that I might inadvertently be doing that.\n我从没想过要给我的感情标价。我甚至从没意识到,自己可能无意中做了这样的事。"

    old "In my mind, I was fooling those people, not you. They thought I needed an incentive to keep you close, but that's all I ever wanted. So, when they offered me something to do it... well, why not?"
    new "In my mind, I was fooling those people, not you. They thought I needed an incentive to keep you close, but that's all I ever wanted. So, when they offered me something to do it... well, why not?\n在我心里,我骗的是那些人,不是你。他们以为我需要点好处才肯把你留在身边,可把你留在身边本来就是我唯一想要的。所以当他们愿意为此给我点什么的时候……那何乐而不为呢?"

    old "Aren't you afraid that they might knock on your door in future, asking you for more favors once all of this is over?"
    new "Aren't you afraid that they might knock on your door in future, asking you for more favors once all of this is over?\n你就不怕将来他们来敲你的门,等这一切结束后再向你讨更多人情吗?"

    old "And why do you think I chose a ship?"
    new "And why do you think I chose a ship?\n那你觉得我为什么挑了艘船?"

    old "Ah. You plan to run away."
    new "Ah. You plan to run away.\n啊,你打算跑路。"

    old "That is a possibility. But only if you'll come with me."
    new "That is a possibility. But only if you'll come with me.\n有这种可能,不过前提是你肯跟我一起走。"

    old "Maybe I will."
    new "Maybe I will.\n也许我会的。"

    old "[protag], let me show you... the ship's hold. We'll have more privacy down there."
    new "[protag], let me show you... the ship's hold. We'll have more privacy down there.\n[protag],我带你去看看……船舱。那里更私密。"

    old "I follow Jasper down to the ship's hold. It's small, but there is more than enough room for a few people to fit in it comfortably. And, as Jasper said, there's more privacy here than there would be out on the docks."
    new "I follow Jasper down to the ship's hold. It's small, but there is more than enough room for a few people to fit in it comfortably. And, as Jasper said, there's more privacy here than there would be out on the docks.\n我跟着Jasper下到船舱。船舱不大,但足以让几个人舒服地待在里面。而且正如Jasper所说,这里比码头上私密得多。"

    old "When I turn my attention back towards Jasper, I catch him pulling off his shirt. My eyes quickly dart to his now exposed chest as Jasper casually leans against a crate, a mischievous smirk on his face."
    new "When I turn my attention back towards Jasper, I catch him pulling off his shirt. My eyes quickly dart to his now exposed chest as Jasper casually leans against a crate, a mischievous smirk on his face.\n等我把注意力转回Jasper身上时,正撞见他脱掉衬衫。我的目光飞快地落到他裸露的胸膛上,而Jasper则懒洋洋地靠在一只木箱旁,脸上挂着一丝狡黠的坏笑。"

    old "It doesn't take a genius to figure out where this is going."
    new "It doesn't take a genius to figure out where this is going.\n不用什么天才也能看出接下来会发生什么。"

    old "I turn my attention back towards Jasper and watch as he leans against a crate with a mischievous expression on his face."
    new "I turn my attention back towards Jasper and watch as he leans against a crate with a mischievous expression on his face.\n我把注意力转回Jasper身上,看着他靠在一只木箱旁,脸上带着淘气的神情。"

    old "So, what do you think, [protag]? This hold is pretty nice, isn't it?"
    new "So, what do you think, [protag]? This hold is pretty nice, isn't it?\n那么,你觉得怎么样,[protag]?这船舱挺不错吧?"

    old "I hadn't noticed. I might have gotten a little distracted by another nice thing."
    new "I hadn't noticed. I might have gotten a little distracted by another nice thing.\n我没注意。我大概是被另一件好东西分了神。"

    old "Oh? And what is this other nice thing that's caught your eye?"
    new "Oh? And what is this other nice thing that's caught your eye?\n哦?那件吸引了你的好东西是什么?"

    old "I grin and go over to him. I lean over the crate and kiss him."
    new "I grin and go over to him. I lean over the crate and kiss him.\n我咧嘴一笑,走到他面前,俯身越过木箱吻住了他。"

    old "You should be able to figure it out for yourself."
    new "You should be able to figure it out for yourself.\n你自己应该能想明白。"

    old "Jasper chuckles and then returns the kiss, gently running his hand up my neck and cupping my cheek. It feels nice. It's also a bit tame compared to what I really want from him right now."
    new "Jasper chuckles and then returns the kiss, gently running his hand up my neck and cupping my cheek. It feels nice. It's also a bit tame compared to what I really want from him right now.\nJasper轻笑一声,回应了这个吻,手温柔地滑上我的脖颈,又捧住我的脸颊。感觉很好,不过比起我现在真正想要的,还是太克制了些。"

    old "So, when are you going to get around to giving me a proper 'tour' of this hold?"
    new "So, when are you going to get around to giving me a proper 'tour' of this hold?\n那么,你打算什么时候带我好好“参观”一下这船舱?"

    old "I was just getting to that. Now, why don't you come over here, [protag]? I have something to show you that I think you'll be very interested in."
    new "I was just getting to that. Now, why don't you come over here, [protag]? I have something to show you that I think you'll be very interested in.\n我正要开始呢。现在,你何不过来,[protag]?我有个东西想给你看,我想你会很感兴趣的。"

    old "Oh, I'm definitely interested."
    new "Oh, I'm definitely interested.\n哦,我肯定感兴趣。"

    old "I head behind the crate and meet up with Jasper. I run my hands down his chest and things escalate from there."
    new "I head behind the crate and meet up with Jasper. I run my hands down his chest and things escalate from there.\n我绕到木箱后面与Jasper会合,双手抚过他的胸膛,事情便从那里一发不可收拾。"

    old "You know what? Maybe the ship was a good idea after all."
    new "You know what? Maybe the ship was a good idea after all.\n你知道吗?也许那艘船终究是个好主意。"

    old "I head to Grimoire's docks looking for Jasper. I don't see him anywhere on the pier but I do see his ship, the Esmeralda, docked there. I suppose it's possible he's taking a nap on it or something..."
    new "I head to Grimoire's docks looking for Jasper. I don't see him anywhere on the pier but I do see his ship, the Esmeralda, docked there. I suppose it's possible he's taking a nap on it or something...\n我前往Grimoire的码头找Jasper。码头上不见他的人影,但我确实看见他的船Esmeralda号停靠在那里。我想他也许正在船上打个盹什么的……"

    old "That thought in mind, I board the ship and start calling his name."
    new "That thought in mind, I board the ship and start calling his name.\n这么想着,我登上了船,开始喊他的名字。"

    old "Jasper? Are you here?"
    new "Jasper? Are you here?\nJasper?你在吗?"

    old "A few seconds pass with no response. I try again."
    new "A few seconds pass with no response. I try again.\n几秒钟过去,没有回应。我又喊了一遍。"

    old "Ah, it's you, [protag]. Sorry, I was sleeping."
    new "Ah, it's you, [protag]. Sorry, I was sleeping.\n啊,是你啊,[protag]。抱歉,我在睡觉。"

    old "I'm the one who is sorry. I didn't mean to wake you up. It's pretty uncommon for you to be asleep at this hour though, isn't it? Did something happen?"
    new "I'm the one who is sorry. I didn't mean to wake you up. It's pretty uncommon for you to be asleep at this hour though, isn't it? Did something happen?\n该道歉的是我。我不是故意吵醒你的。不过你这个时候睡觉可不多见,不是吗?出什么事了吗?"

    old "I just had some trouble sleeping. That's all."
    new "I just had some trouble sleeping. That's all.\n我只是有点睡不着,仅此而已。"

    old "No. There's definitely something else that's bothering him. I can tell from the tone in his voice. Maybe..."
    new "No. There's definitely something else that's bothering him. I can tell from the tone in his voice. Maybe...\n不,肯定还有别的事困扰着他。从他的语气里我能听得出来。也许……"

    old "Um, Japser, I don't know if it's because of me..."
    new "Um, Japser, I don't know if it's because of me...\n呃,Japser,我不知道是不是因为我……"

    old "Because of you?"
    new "Because of you?\n因为你?"

    old "I... have something to confess. I slept with someone else besides you."
    new "I... have something to confess. I slept with someone else besides you.\n我……有件事要坦白。我和除你之外的人上了床。"

    old "And that's alright with you? You don't have any questions? You don't want to know who it was?"
    new "And that's alright with you? You don't have any questions? You don't want to know who it was?\n你觉得无所谓?你没什么想问的?你不想知道那个人是谁?"

    old "I already know all that I care to know."
    new "I already know all that I care to know.\n我想知道的都已经知道了。"

    old "And I don't want to fight with you. Not now. I don't want to repeat what happened... It was too much for me. Just thinking about it hurts."
    new "And I don't want to fight with you. Not now. I don't want to repeat what happened... It was too much for me. Just thinking about it hurts.\n而且我不想和你吵架,现在不想。我不想重演发生过的事……那对我打击太大了,光是想起就心痛。"

    old "What are you talking about? Jasper?"
    new "What are you talking about? Jasper?\n你在说什么?Jasper?"

    old "It's like he's in shock. What he's talking about... Is it related to some past trauma? Has this situation made him recall something?"
    new "It's like he's in shock. What he's talking about... Is it related to some past trauma? Has this situation made him recall something?\n他像是受了惊吓。他在说的这些……和过去的创伤有关吗?是这个情形让他想起了什么?"

    old "When you asked me about losing teammates or partners... I said that it wasn't something that happened to me. That was a lie."
    new "When you asked me about losing teammates or partners... I said that it wasn't something that happened to me. That was a lie.\n你问我有没有失去过队友或同伴时……我说这种事没发生在我身上。那是谎话。"

    old "Yeah. I already knew that. I know you better than you might think, Jasper. I just didn't want to push you into telling me something you were uncomfortable with."
    new "Yeah. I already knew that. I know you better than you might think, Jasper. I just didn't want to push you into telling me something you were uncomfortable with.\n嗯,我早就知道了。我比你想象中更了解你,Jasper。我只是不想逼你说出让你难受的事。"

    old "I had this fellow pirate, Rollo. He was older than me. We got together. It wasn't anything serious. At least, that's what I thought. Long story short, one day, before a big battle, I betrayed him and fooled around with another, younger pirate."
    new "I had this fellow pirate, Rollo. He was older than me. We got together. It wasn't anything serious. At least, that's what I thought. Long story short, one day, before a big battle, I betrayed him and fooled around with another, younger pirate.\n我有个海盗同伴,叫Rollo。他比我年长。我们在一起过,不是什么认真的关系——至少我当时是这么想的。长话短说,有一天,一场大战之前,我背叛了他,和另一个更年轻的海盗厮混去了。"

    old "The day after we assaulted an island near Zoltar. Lavastorm was its name. We thought we'd find treasure, but we only found ruin there. There were so many lizardmen. Goblins and other wild races too. That island... That's where Rollo died."
    new "The day after we assaulted an island near Zoltar. Lavastorm was its name. We thought we'd find treasure, but we only found ruin there. There were so many lizardmen. Goblins and other wild races too. That island... That's where Rollo died.\n第二天,我们袭击了Zoltar附近的一座小岛。岛名叫Lavastorm。我们以为能找到宝藏,结果只找到一片废墟。那里到处都是Lizardmen,还有Goblins和其他野蛮种族。那座岛……就是Rollo死去的地方。"

    old "How did he die?"
    new "How did he die?\n他是怎么死的?"

    old "That's... the sad part. He learned that I betrayed him the night before and the next day he was fighting recklessly, as if his life didn't matter anymore. He kept jumping into battle, like some kind of berserker. It definitely wasn't his usual, calm style of fighting. Because of that, he died. Because of me."
    new "That's... the sad part. He learned that I betrayed him the night before and the next day he was fighting recklessly, as if his life didn't matter anymore. He kept jumping into battle, like some kind of berserker. It definitely wasn't his usual, calm style of fighting. Because of that, he died. Because of me.\n这……正是最让人难过的地方。他前一晚得知我背叛了他,第二天就打得不要命了,仿佛他的性命已经无关紧要。他一次次冲进战场,活像个狂战士。那绝不是他平日沉着冷静的打法。正因如此,他死了。因为我的缘故。"

    old "At the time, it really hurt me. It still hurts now. But, even if it hurt, I thought Rollo was stupid. Why risk dying over me, for what I did? But now... Now that the same thing has happened to me, I can sort of understand. I feel a strange fury inside myself, like I want to destroy everything."
    new "At the time, it really hurt me. It still hurts now. But, even if it hurt, I thought Rollo was stupid. Why risk dying over me, for what I did? But now... Now that the same thing has happened to me, I can sort of understand. I feel a strange fury inside myself, like I want to destroy everything.\n当时这件事伤透了我的心,至今仍然如此。可即便如此,我也觉得Rollo很傻。为什么要为了我、为了我做过的事去冒死的风险?但现在……现在同样的事发生在了我身上,我似乎有些明白了。我心中涌起一股莫名的怒火,像是想毁掉一切。"

    old "Jasper!"
    new "Jasper!\nJasper!"

    old "I am not Rollo. I will calm down. Luckily, we're not assaulting N'Mar today. I have time that Rollo didn't. But... I need to know if there really is something between us. Will what we have ever be more than friendship or am I deluding myself? A proper answer would help me make peace with all of this."
    new "I am not Rollo. I will calm down. Luckily, we're not assaulting N'Mar today. I have time that Rollo didn't. But... I need to know if there really is something between us. Will what we have ever be more than friendship or am I deluding myself? A proper answer would help me make peace with all of this.\n我不是Rollo。我会冷静下来的。幸好,我们今天不是去攻打N'Mar。我有Rollo所没有的时间。可是……我必须知道我们之间是否真有什么。我们所拥有的,将来会不会超越友谊?还是说我只是在自欺欺人?一个确切的答案,能帮助我和这一切和解。"

    old "Friend."
    new "Friend.\n朋友。"

    old "Yes. I'm sorry, Jasper."
    new "Yes. I'm sorry, Jasper.\n嗯,对不起,Jasper。"

    old "No, don't be. A friend is a good thing. I don't have many. I know many people who like me, who enjoy my company, but nobody that I can really call a friend, like you."
    new "No, don't be. A friend is a good thing. I don't have many. I know many people who like me, who enjoy my company, but nobody that I can really call a friend, like you.\n不,别这么说。朋友是好事。我的朋友不多。我认识很多人喜欢我、愿意和我作伴,但没有一个是我能真正称作朋友的,除了你。"

    old "If I can't be your lover, being your friend is enough. At least, it will be once I've sorted out my emotions."
    new "If I can't be your lover, being your friend is enough. At least, it will be once I've sorted out my emotions.\n如果做不成你的恋人,做你的朋友也就够了。至少,等我整理好自己的情绪之后,就足够了。"

    old "Thank you, Jasper. I do value your friendship. I was afraid I might lose it today after I confessed to you."
    new "Thank you, Jasper. I do value your friendship. I was afraid I might lose it today after I confessed to you.\n谢谢你,Jasper。我真的很珍惜你的友谊。我原本还怕,今天向你坦白之后,会失去这份友谊。"

    old "Things won't be perfect between us right away, but I will eventually come to terms with the fact that this is what you want. Time heals all things."
    new "Things won't be perfect between us right away, but I will eventually come to terms with the fact that this is what you want. Time heals all things.\n我们之间的事不会立刻圆满,但我终究会接受这个事实——这就是你想要的。时间能治愈一切。"

    old "Now, if there isn't anything else you wanted to discuss, I think I'd like to get back to my nap."
    new "Now, if there isn't anything else you wanted to discuss, I think I'd like to get back to my nap.\n好了,如果你没有别的想聊的了,我想回去继续睡我的午觉。"

    old "No, we're good Jasper. Rest well, we'll meet again soon on the battlefield as allies."
    new "No, we're good Jasper. Rest well, we'll meet again soon on the battlefield as allies.\n没有了,我们没事了,Jasper。好好休息吧,我们很快就会在战场上以盟友的身份再见。"

    old "I'm looking forward to it."
    new "I'm looking forward to it.\n我很期待。"

    old "Do you really mean that, [protag]?"
    new "Do you really mean that, [protag]?\n你真的那么想吗,[protag]?"

    old "Yes. In the moment, I thought what I did was what I wanted but afterward... I felt so guilty. And, when I came back to town and looked out of my house's window, I spotted the sails of the various ships over at the docks. My mind immediately went to the Esmeralda and the time we spent together on it."
    new "Yes. In the moment, I thought what I did was what I wanted but afterward... I felt so guilty. And, when I came back to town and looked out of my house's window, I spotted the sails of the various ships over at the docks. My mind immediately went to the Esmeralda and the time we spent together on it.\n是的。当时我以为自己所做的就是我想要的,但事后……我内疚极了。等我回到镇上,从我家窗子望出去,看到码头上那些船只的帆,我的思绪立刻飘向了Esmeralda号,飘向了我们在上面一起度过的时光。"

    old "It became transparently clear that I'd made a huge mistake. I couldn't believe how stupid I'd been! One moment of pleasure at the risk of ruining everything we had together? It wasn't worth it, but I still did it..."
    new "It became transparently clear that I'd made a huge mistake. I couldn't believe how stupid I'd been! One moment of pleasure at the risk of ruining everything we had together? It wasn't worth it, but I still did it...\n我清清楚楚地意识到,自己犯了个天大的错误。我简直不敢相信自己竟那么蠢!为了一时的欢愉,甘愿冒毁掉我们所拥有一切的风险?这不值得,可我还是那么做了……"

    old "Well... how about this? You forget that I used your position to get a ship and I forget that you slept with someone else?"
    new "Well... how about this? You forget that I used your position to get a ship and I forget that you slept with someone else?\n那么……这样如何?你忘掉我利用你的身份弄到一艘船的事,我忘掉你和别人上床的事?"

    old "I kind of already forgave you for that."
    new "I kind of already forgave you for that.\n那件事我其实已经原谅你了。"

    old "Just come here."
    new "Just come here.\n过来吧。"

    old "I move closer to him as he takes me into a hug. Then, we kiss for what seems like a blissful eternity. I'm so glad that we can still do this."
    new "I move closer to him as he takes me into a hug. Then, we kiss for what seems like a blissful eternity. I'm so glad that we can still do this.\n我靠近他,他把我拥入怀中。然后,我们吻了很久,仿佛是一段幸福的永恒。我真高兴我们还能这样。"

    old "I'm really happy right now."
    new "I'm really happy right now.\n我现在真的很开心。"

    old "Me too. Heh. And to think, when we first met, I thought you were annoying."
    new "Me too. Heh. And to think, when we first met, I thought you were annoying.\n我也是。呵。想想看,我们第一次见面时,我还觉得你很烦人呢。"

    old "Really? How is that possible?"
    new "Really? How is that possible?\n真的?这怎么可能?"

    old "Jasper's tone suggests surprise, but he's smiling as he says it. I imagine he knows exactly how annoying he can be sometimes."
    new "Jasper's tone suggests surprise, but he's smiling as he says it. I imagine he knows exactly how annoying he can be sometimes.\nJasper的语气透着惊讶,但说这话时他脸上带着笑。我想他心里清楚,自己有时候有多烦人。"

    old "All of those strange rhetorical and philosophical questions about life, purpose, myself..."
    new "All of those strange rhetorical and philosophical questions about life, purpose, myself...\n那些关于人生、关于目的、关于我自己的古怪修辞和哲学问题……"

    old "I only asked them so I could get to know you better, [protag]."
    new "I only asked them so I could get to know you better, [protag].\n我问那些问题,只是为了更了解你,[protag]。"

    old "Yes, and I got to know you better at the same time. Whenever I talk to Apolimesho or someone else on the council, I end up recalling the things we talked about."
    new "Yes, and I got to know you better at the same time. Whenever I talk to Apolimesho or someone else on the council, I end up recalling the things we talked about.\n是啊,与此同时我也更了解了你。每当我与Apolimesho或议会里的其他人谈话时,最后总会想起我们聊过的那些事。"

    old "You've wormed your way into my mind and I can't get you out of it. I think that means I love you."
    new "You've wormed your way into my mind and I can't get you out of it. I think that means I love you.\n你一点一点钻进了我的心里,我怎么也赶不走你。我想这意味着我爱你。"

    old "And I love you too, [protag]."
    new "And I love you too, [protag].\n我也爱你,[protag]。"

    old "Jasper takes my hand and together we head back to the ship's hold. I guess it's time to make up for my mistakes. I might even have something in mind already..."
    new "Jasper takes my hand and together we head back to the ship's hold. I guess it's time to make up for my mistakes. I might even have something in mind already...\nJasper牵起我的手,我们一起回到船舱。我想是时候弥补我的过错了。我甚至可能已经想好了怎么弥补……"

    old "After meeting up with Jasper at the docks, the two of us ended up taking the Esmeralda out on the water. It's a beautiful day. The breeze isn't too strong and the water is calm. And the company isn't too bad either."
    new "After meeting up with Jasper at the docks, the two of us ended up taking the Esmeralda out on the water. It's a beautiful day. The breeze isn't too strong and the water is calm. And the company isn't too bad either.\n在码头与Jasper会合后,我们俩最终把Esmeralda号开到了水面上。今天天气很好,微风不强,水面平静。而身边的人也相当不错。"

    old "Jasper smiles at me for a moment before asking his question."
    new "Jasper smiles at me for a moment before asking his question.\nJasper在问出问题之前,先对我笑了笑。"

    old "What's on your mind [protag]?"
    new "What's on your mind [protag]?\n你在想什么,[protag]?"

    old "I actually really like the ship. I'm kind of glad you asked for it."
    new "I actually really like the ship. I'm kind of glad you asked for it.\n我其实很喜欢这艘船。我很高兴你要了它。"

    old "We can get more privacy out here, away from Grimoire. And it's nice to get a bit of a break from my usual routine. It's almost like I'm on holiday."
    new "We can get more privacy out here, away from Grimoire. And it's nice to get a bit of a break from my usual routine. It's almost like I'm on holiday.\n在这里,远离Grimoire,我们能更自在些。而且能从我平日的例行事务中抽身休息一下,也很不错,简直像在度假。"

    old "And yet, we're still on the job. Don't forget that we're officially out here to scout the water around N'Mar."
    new "And yet, we're still on the job. Don't forget that we're officially out here to scout the water around N'Mar.\n不过我们还在执行任务呢。别忘了,我们名义上是出来侦察N'Mar周围水域的。"

    old "Trust me, I remember. It's not like I could actually go on vacation. Still, even if we're heading to the most dangerous place in Aravorn right now, I still feel like I'm relaxing. Here, alone with you, the sun sparkling on the waves..."
    new "Trust me, I remember. It's not like I could actually go on vacation. Still, even if we're heading to the most dangerous place in Aravorn right now, I still feel like I'm relaxing. Here, alone with you, the sun sparkling on the waves...\n相信我,我记得。我又不可能真去度假。不过,即便我们现在正前往Aravorn最危险的地方,我仍觉得自己在放松。在这里,和你独处,阳光在浪尖上闪烁……"

    old "Once we get closer to N'Mar, you can say goodbye to the sun."
    new "Once we get closer to N'Mar, you can say goodbye to the sun.\n等我们靠近N'Mar,你就得和太阳说再见了。"

    old "Sure, but until then, I plan to enjoy it."
    new "Sure, but until then, I plan to enjoy it.\n当然,但在此之前,我打算好好享受它。"

    old "The sea is calm today. Unless we plan on rowing, it will take us a few hours to get there."
    new "The sea is calm today. Unless we plan on rowing, it will take us a few hours to get there.\n今天海面平静。除非我们打算划船,否则要花上几个小时才能到那里。"

    old "I did have an idea regarding that actually."
    new "I did have an idea regarding that actually.\n关于这个,我倒真有个主意。"

    old "Oh ho ho! I have a feeling I want to hear this idea of yours."
    new "Oh ho ho! I have a feeling I want to hear this idea of yours.\n哦嚯嚯!我有种感觉,我很想听听你的这个主意。"

    old "I move closer to Jasper and kiss him. From there, we toss our clothes aside and make love right there on the deck. There's nobody around, but even if there was, I'm not sure I'd care. Actually, if I'm being honest with myself, the thought of a random ship passing by and spotting us kind of excites me."
    new "I move closer to Jasper and kiss him. From there, we toss our clothes aside and make love right there on the deck. There's nobody around, but even if there was, I'm not sure I'd care. Actually, if I'm being honest with myself, the thought of a random ship passing by and spotting us kind of excites me.\n我靠近Jasper,吻住了他。接着,我们把衣服丢到一旁,就在甲板上做起了爱。周围没有人,但即便有人,我也不确定自己会在乎。其实,若对自己坦诚点说,一想到有艘路过的船可能撞见我们,我竟还有点兴奋。"

    old "I let out a yawn and stretch as I come to. I must have fallen asleep."
    new "I let out a yawn and stretch as I come to. I must have fallen asleep.\n我醒来时打了个哈欠,伸了伸懒腰。我一定是睡着了。"

    old "Jasper, where are we? Are we close to-"
    new "Jasper, where are we? Are we close to-\nJasper,我们到哪儿了?是不是快到——"

    old "Did you enjoy your nap, [protag]?"
    new "Did you enjoy your nap, [protag]?\n你的小睡睡得好吗,[protag]?"

    old "Jasper is scouting ahead, a spyglass in one hand as he holds onto one of the ship's ropes with the other."
    new "Jasper is scouting ahead, a spyglass in one hand as he holds onto one of the ship's ropes with the other.\nJasper正在前方瞭望,一手拿着望远镜,另一手抓着船上的一根绳索。"

    old "He's also completely naked! I've obviously seen his body before, but this... It's the sort of image I'd expect a raunchy romance novel to conjure up."
    new "He's also completely naked! I've obviously seen his body before, but this... It's the sort of image I'd expect a raunchy romance novel to conjure up.\n他还一丝不挂!他的身体我自然早就见过,可这……这简直是我会指望低俗言情小说才有的画面。"

    old "What are you doing standing up there?! What if someone spots you?"
    new "What are you doing standing up there?! What if someone spots you?\n你站在那上面干什么?!要是被人看见怎么办?"

    old "Relax, there's nobody around."
    new "Relax, there's nobody around.\n放心,周围没人。"

    old "The only piece of clothing he has on are his trousers, leaving his chest bared for me to enjoy. He's on the slim side, but that doesn't mean he doesn't have a bit of muscle to him."
    new "The only piece of clothing he has on are his trousers, leaving his chest bared for me to enjoy. He's on the slim side, but that doesn't mean he doesn't have a bit of muscle to him.\n他身上唯一的衣物就是裤子,胸膛就这么裸露着任我欣赏。他偏瘦,但这不意味着他身上没有一点肌肉。"

    old "All in all, it's a very pleasing sight."
    new "All in all, it's a very pleasing sight.\n总而言之,这是一幕令人赏心悦目的景象。"

    old "Hmm. I think we're about there. I can see some mist on the horizon."
    new "Hmm. I think we're about there. I can see some mist on the horizon.\n嗯,我想我们差不多到了。我能看到地平线上有些雾气。"

    old "And so my 'vacation' comes to an end. I can't help but be a bit sad about it. I knew this was coming, but for a moment I was able to log that away in the back of my mind."
    new "And so my 'vacation' comes to an end. I can't help but be a bit sad about it. I knew this was coming, but for a moment I was able to log that away in the back of my mind.\n于是我的“假期”就此结束了。我难免有些难过。我早知道会有这一刻,但方才那一会儿,我总算能把它抛到脑后。"

    old "Still, I'm thankful that I got to spend this time with Jasper. It turned out to be a much needed break. And... it served as a reminder of what I might have to look forward to once this is all over."
    new "Still, I'm thankful that I got to spend this time with Jasper. It turned out to be a much needed break. And... it served as a reminder of what I might have to look forward to once this is all over.\n不过,我仍感激能与Jasper共度这段时光。事实证明,这是一次非常需要的休息。而且……它也提醒着我,等这一切结束后,我或许可以期待些什么。"

    old "I'll join you as soon as I'm dressed. Remember, we need to avoid fighting. This is only a reconaissance mission."
    new "I'll join you as soon as I'm dressed. Remember, we need to avoid fighting. This is only a reconaissance mission.\n我穿好衣服就去找你。记住,我们得避免交战。这只是一次侦察任务。"

    old "Aye aye, Captain!"
    new "Aye aye, Captain!\n遵命,船长!"

    old "Shut up."
    new "Shut up.\n闭嘴。"

    old "We scout the area. While we don't take any big risks, we're still able to collect some important information before we make our way back to Grimoire."
    new "We scout the area. While we don't take any big risks, we're still able to collect some important information before we make our way back to Grimoire.\n我们侦察了那片区域。虽然没冒什么大险,但在返回Grimoire之前,我们还是收集到了一些重要情报。"

    old "As much as I'd love to stay there on the ship with Jasper, I need to continue my mission."
    new "As much as I'd love to stay there on the ship with Jasper, I need to continue my mission.\n虽然我很想和Jasper留在船上,但我得继续执行任务。"

    old "Just a few days. Just a few more days and all of this will be over. I can't deny that I'm worried. For my whole team, of course, but mostly for me and for Jasper."
    new "Just a few days. Just a few more days and all of this will be over. I can't deny that I'm worried. For my whole team, of course, but mostly for me and for Jasper.\n就几天了。再过几天,这一切都会结束。我不能否认自己的担忧——当然是为了整个团队,但主要还是为了我自己,以及Jasper。"

    old "If someone had told me that I would fall in love with a pirate before all of this I would have laughed in their face. The idea would have been too absurd."
    new "If someone had told me that I would fall in love with a pirate before all of this I would have laughed in their face. The idea would have been too absurd.\n如果在这一切发生之前,有人告诉我,我会爱上一个海盗,我一定会当面嘲笑他。这想法太荒唐了。"

    old "And yet, here I am. I guess that I always had an inkling that there was something about Jasper that intrigued me. Even on that first day when I met him on the docks."
    new "And yet, here I am. I guess that I always had an inkling that there was something about Jasper that intrigued me. Even on that first day when I met him on the docks.\n然而,我就站在这里。我想,我内心深处一直隐隐觉得,Jasper身上有什么吸引着我。即便是在码头上第一次见到他的那天起。"

    old "Maybe it was the way he looked at me. His eyes. Or how his long, curly hair swayed in the breeze."
    new "Maybe it was the way he looked at me. His eyes. Or how his long, curly hair swayed in the breeze.\n也许是他看我的眼神。他的眼睛。或者是他那长长的卷发在微风中摇曳的样子。"

    old "You're dreaming about me now, [protag]? I'm flattered."
    new "You're dreaming about me now, [protag]? I'm flattered.\n你现在在梦见我了,[protag]?我受宠若惊。"

    old "I'm always dreaming about you. It's just... this time feels more real than the others."
    new "I'm always dreaming about you. It's just... this time feels more real than the others.\n我一直都在梦见你。只是……这一次比以往都更真实。"

    old "Come, let's get in the boat."
    new "Come, let's get in the boat.\n来吧,我们上船。"

    old "The Esmeralda?"
    new "The Esmeralda?\nEsmeralda号?"

    old "No. You're dreaming about the first time we met, right? I didn't have the Esmeralda yet. When I brought you to Senya, it was with that small row boat."
    new "No. You're dreaming about the first time we met, right? I didn't have the Esmeralda yet. When I brought you to Senya, it was with that small row boat.\n不,你梦见的是我们第一次见面,对吧?那时我还没有Esmeralda号。我带你去Senya时,用的就是那条小船。"

    old "But this time, let's try something a little different."
    new "But this time, let's try something a little different.\n但这一次,我们换个花样试试。"

    old "Jasper! You...you're naked! How did you get naked so fast?"
    new "Jasper! You...you're naked! How did you get naked so fast?\nJasper!你……你光着身子!你怎么这么快就脱光了?"

    old "Who cares? This is a dream. There's nobody around us. It's just you, me, and the sea."
    new "Who cares? This is a dream. There's nobody around us. It's just you, me, and the sea.\n管它呢?这是梦。我们周围没人,只有你、我和大海。"

    old "You're right. I should stop worrying and just enjoy the moment."
    new "You're right. I should stop worrying and just enjoy the moment.\n你说得对。我别再胡思乱想了,好好享受这一刻。"

    old "Now you're getting it."
    new "Now you're getting it.\n现在你终于开窍了。"

    old "I remember that moment well. We sat across from each other in a confined space. It didn't occur to me then, but now... It's actually an embarrassingly close situation, isn't it? You either look at the sea around you or stare straight ahead, meeting the eyes of the person you're sharing the boat with."
    new "I remember that moment well. We sat across from each other in a confined space. It didn't occur to me then, but now... It's actually an embarrassingly close situation, isn't it? You either look at the sea around you or stare straight ahead, meeting the eyes of the person you're sharing the boat with.\n我记得那一刻很清楚。我们面对面坐在一个狭小的空间里。当时我还没意识到,但现在想来……那其实是个尴尬到令人脸红的近距离场面,不是吗?你要么看周围的海,要么直视前方,与和你同船的人四目相对。"

    old "That's why I chose to bring you with me. You can learn a lot about a person by simply looking them in the eyes."
    new "That's why I chose to bring you with me. You can learn a lot about a person by simply looking them in the eyes.\n所以我才会选择带你同行。只要凝视一个人的眼睛,你就能了解他很多。"

    old "You know, Jasper. You have really beautiful eyes."
    new "You know, Jasper. You have really beautiful eyes.\n你知道吗,Jasper,你的眼睛真的很漂亮。"

    old "And what are my beautiful eyes trying to tell you right now?"
    new "And what are my beautiful eyes trying to tell you right now?\n那我这双漂亮的眼睛,现在想对你说什么?"

    old "That I should stop worrying and enjoy this stolen moment with you."
    new "That I should stop worrying and enjoy this stolen moment with you.\n它在说,我别再担心了,好好和你享受这偷来的时光。"

    old "You are smarter than you look, [protag]."
    new "You are smarter than you look, [protag].\n你比你看起来聪明,[protag]。"

    old "The dream quickly escalates into more physical activities and I end up touching myself. For a blissful moment, all my fears are gone. I'm sure they'll come flooding back in the morning but, at least for one peaceful night, I can be free of them."
    new "The dream quickly escalates into more physical activities and I end up touching myself. For a blissful moment, all my fears are gone. I'm sure they'll come flooding back in the morning but, at least for one peaceful night, I can be free of them.\n这场梦很快就升级成了更激烈的肢体活动,最后我抚摸起了自己。在那一小段幸福的时光里,我所有的恐惧都消失了。我知道它们明早还会如潮水般涌来,但至少在这平静的一夜,我能从其中解脱。"

    old "[protag], I'm glad you stopped by. There's something that's been on my mind lately. Regarding N'Mar, specifically."
    new "[protag], I'm glad you stopped by. There's something that's been on my mind lately. Regarding N'Mar, specifically.\n[protag],很高兴你能顺路过来。有件事近来一直压在我心上,具体来说,是关于N'Mar的。"

    old "Lately I've been thinking about the structure and location of N'mar's castle. It's really not so different from the Amazon citadel, in many respects."
    new "Lately I've been thinking about the structure and location of N'mar's castle. It's really not so different from the Amazon citadel, in many respects.\n最近我一直在琢磨N'Mar城堡的构造和位置。说真的,它在很多方面都和Amazon要塞差别不大。"

    old "How do you figure?"
    new "How do you figure?\n这话怎么说?"

    old "I'm sure you've seen it yourself. One of the greatest strategic advantages that the citadel has is its location. A land invasion would force enemy soldiers through a choke point to get to the citadel. It's all thanks to the fact that the citadel is situated on a peninsula."
    new "I'm sure you've seen it yourself. One of the greatest strategic advantages that the citadel has is its location. A land invasion would force enemy soldiers through a choke point to get to the citadel. It's all thanks to the fact that the citadel is situated on a peninsula.\n我想你自己也见过。那座要塞最大的战略优势之一就是它的位置。从陆路进攻,敌军就会被逼着通过一处咽喉要道才能抵达要塞。这全靠要塞坐落在一座半岛上。"

    old "It certainly doesn't help that the terrain is rocky and treacherous."
    new "It certainly doesn't help that the terrain is rocky and treacherous.\n更何况这里地形崎岖险恶,更是雪上加霜。"

    old "True, true. Invading the castle of N'mar is a much easier task than accessing the Amazon citadel. The land route is much wider, enough for an army regiment to pass through. And the terrain is mostly flat."
    new "True, true. Invading the castle of N'mar is a much easier task than accessing the Amazon citadel. The land route is much wider, enough for an army regiment to pass through. And the terrain is mostly flat.\n没错,没错。攻打N'Mar城堡比进入Amazon要塞要容易得多。陆路宽阔许多,足以让一个军团通过,而且地形大多是平地。"

    old "It's difficult to get ambushed, or at least that would be the case if it weren't for the damned mist covering those plains. However, there are other advantages of being located on a peninsula."
    new "It's difficult to get ambushed, or at least that would be the case if it weren't for the damned mist covering those plains. However, there are other advantages of being located on a peninsula.\n在那里很难遭到伏击——至少,要不是那该死的迷雾笼罩着平原,情况本该如此。不过,坐落在半岛上还有其他好处。"

    old "Of course. Realistically we can only approach the castle from the front. We could try circling around to the rear of the castle, but positioning an entire army around it when it has its back to the sea is untenable."
    new "Of course. Realistically we can only approach the castle from the front. We could try circling around to the rear of the castle, but positioning an entire army around it when it has its back to the sea is untenable.\n当然。实际上我们只能从正面逼近城堡。我们可以尝试绕到城堡后方,但城堡背靠大海,要把一整支军队部署在它周围是行不通的。"

    old "You say that assuming an assault by land. But there are other vectors of attack we can take."
    new "You say that assuming an assault by land. But there are other vectors of attack we can take.\n你说这话,前提是假设只能从陆路进攻。但我们还有其他可以采取的进攻途径。"

    old "You're talking about your griffons."
    new "You're talking about your griffons.\n你指的是你的狮鹫。"

    old "Partly, yes. We're assaulting by land, and by air. But for a castle with its back to the sea, wouldn't it make sense to assault by water as well?"
    new "Partly, yes. We're assaulting by land, and by air. But for a castle with its back to the sea, wouldn't it make sense to assault by water as well?\n这只是一部分。我们会从陆路和空中进攻。但对一座背靠大海的城堡来说,从水上进攻不也顺理成章吗?"

    old "That's a good idea, Karen. We can take the geography of N'mar and use it to our advantage. Travel by sea is more rapid than travel by land."
    new "That's a good idea, Karen. We can take the geography of N'mar and use it to our advantage. Travel by sea is more rapid than travel by land.\n这是个好主意,Karen。我们可以利用N'Mar的地形,让它为我们所用。海路行军比陆路更快。"

    old "That said, travel time is not the issue here. Whether it takes you two days or two weeks to position your men around N'mar, the difference seems immaterial to me. Either way, you will be engaging them at a known date. I've given the idea some thought, and I still find myself unsure of how one might execute an assault by sea effectively."
    new "That said, travel time is not the issue here. Whether it takes you two days or two weeks to position your men around N'mar, the difference seems immaterial to me. Either way, you will be engaging them at a known date. I've given the idea some thought, and I still find myself unsure of how one might execute an assault by sea effectively.\n话虽如此,行军时间并不是问题所在。不管你需要两天还是两周才能把兵力部署到N'Mar周围,在我看来差别都无关紧要。无论如何,你都会在既定的日子与他们交战。我仔细想过这个主意,但仍不确定如何才能有效地从海上发动进攻。"

    old "It is one of those ideas that seems intuitive at first, but when it comes to the realities of battle, it may not be the solution you need. After all, you have to question what benefit you'd get from a ship that you couldn't get with a ground-based regiment."
    new "It is one of those ideas that seems intuitive at first, but when it comes to the realities of battle, it may not be the solution you need. After all, you have to question what benefit you'd get from a ship that you couldn't get with a ground-based regiment.\n这是那种乍一听很直观的想法,可一旦落到实战的现实里,它未必就是你需要的方案。说到底,你必须问一问,一艘船能带来的好处,有哪些是陆上军团无法带来的。"

    old "True, true. But I think it's still worth looking into. Do you have any suggestions for where I might begin investigating?"
    new "True, true. But I think it's still worth looking into. Do you have any suggestions for where I might begin investigating?\n没错,没错。但我觉得仍值得深究。你能不能给我点建议,告诉我该从哪里着手调查?"

    old "The Grimoire docks seem like an obvious place to look. If you want to know the specifics of sailing, ask a sailor."
    new "The Grimoire docks seem like an obvious place to look. If you want to know the specifics of sailing, ask a sailor.\nGrimoire的码头显然是个合适的起点。想了解航海的门道,就去问水手。"

    old "Good idea. I'll try to make my way out there. Even if using Grimoire's naval resources turns out to not be practical, I may learn something useful."
    new "Good idea. I'll try to make my way out there. Even if using Grimoire's naval resources turns out to not be practical, I may learn something useful.\n好主意。我会想办法去一趟。即便最后证明动用Grimoire的海军资源并不实际,我也许仍能学到些有用的东西。"

    old "I'm not sure I agree, Karen."
    new "I'm not sure I agree, Karen.\n我不确定我同意,Karen。"

    old "My understanding of naval warfare is that ships do one of two things: battle other ships at sea, or deposit soldiers on an enemy's shore to enable assault from a new front. Would assaulting N'mar by sea allow us to do anything we couldn't already to with our ground troops?"
    new "My understanding of naval warfare is that ships do one of two things: battle other ships at sea, or deposit soldiers on an enemy's shore to enable assault from a new front. Would assaulting N'mar by sea allow us to do anything we couldn't already to with our ground troops?\n我对海战的理解是,船只只做两件事之一:在海上与敌船交战,或者把士兵送上敌方的海岸,好从新的战线发起进攻。从海上攻打N'Mar,能让我们做到陆上部队原本做不到的事吗?"

    old "You're right, it may be nothing. It was just a thought of mine. Of course, whether or not it's worth investigating is entirely up to you."
    new "You're right, it may be nothing. It was just a thought of mine. Of course, whether or not it's worth investigating is entirely up to you.\n你说得对,也许这根本行不通。这只是我的一个想法。当然,值不值得深究,完全由你决定。"

    old "You can dismiss my remark as nothing but an errant thought. Still, if the ideal appeals to you, it may be worth taking the time to question someone who does understand naval combat and land-to-sea assaults. I'm sure you'd find information at the Grimorie docks."
    new "You can dismiss my remark as nothing but an errant thought. Still, if the ideal appeals to you, it may be worth taking the time to question someone who does understand naval combat and land-to-sea assaults. I'm sure you'd find information at the Grimorie docks.\n你可以把我的话当作一个不着边际的念头一笑置之。不过,如果这个构想对你有吸引力,也许值得花时间去请教一位真正懂得海战和陆海协同突击的人。我相信你在Grimoire的码头能找到这样的信息。"

    old "I appreciate the suggestion. I'm not sure how useful Grimoire's naval resources will be in my battle, but in all my journeys, I've found that what appears to be a dead end at first glance can sometimes turn up useful information."
    new "I appreciate the suggestion. I'm not sure how useful Grimoire's naval resources will be in my battle, but in all my journeys, I've found that what appears to be a dead end at first glance can sometimes turn up useful information.\n我很感谢这个建议。我不确定Grimoire的海军资源在我的战斗里能派上多大用场,但在我所有的旅程中,我发现乍看是死胡同的地方,有时反而会带来有用的信息。"

    old "Karen wants to speak with me again, so I reach her at the Citadel."
    new "Karen wants to speak with me again, so I reach her at the Citadel.\nKaren又想和我谈谈,于是我到要塞去找她。"

    old "I hear that your efforts to assemble an elite task force have been quite fruitful."
    new "I hear that your efforts to assemble an elite task force have been quite fruitful.\n我听说你组建精锐特遣队的努力颇有成效。"

    old "How elite they are is yet to be proved. But yes, my recruitment efforts have been quite succesful so far."
    new "How elite they are is yet to be proved. But yes, my recruitment efforts have been quite succesful so far.\n他们到底有多精锐还有待证明,不过没错,我的招募工作到目前为止相当成功。"

    old "'So far' would imply that you intend to continue your recruitment efforts. Are you sure that's wise?"
    new "'So far' would imply that you intend to continue your recruitment efforts. Are you sure that's wise?\n“到目前为止”这个词,意味着你打算继续招募。你确定这样明智吗?"

    old "You don't think I should?"
    new "You don't think I should?\n你觉得我不该继续?"

    old "I am simply saying that you only have so much time to work with. If you have a full party ready to take on the castle, I would think your time would be better spent working with those individuals you've already met, rather than trying to recruit more individuals. Think more about ways to improve the combat readiness of the followers you already have."
    new "I am simply saying that you only have so much time to work with. If you have a full party ready to take on the castle, I would think your time would be better spent working with those individuals you've already met, rather than trying to recruit more individuals. Think more about ways to improve the combat readiness of the followers you already have.\n我只是说,你能支配的时间有限。如果你已经有一支完整的队伍,可以随时进攻城堡,那我认为你的时间更应该花在那些已经见过的人身上,而不是再招募更多人。多想想怎么提高你现有追随者的战备水平吧。"

    old "I see. So you're saying that after a certain date, I won't be able to recruit them anymore."
    new "I see. So you're saying that after a certain date, I won't be able to recruit them anymore.\n我明白了。你是说,过了某个时间点,我就再也招募不了他们了。"

    old "Exactly. Well, you might, but could be too late for them to be useful in battle."
    new "Exactly. Well, you might, but could be too late for them to be useful in battle.\n正是。唔,也许还能招,但可能为时已晚,赶不上在战斗中派上用场了。"

    old "And if you haven't already, take the time to communicate the plans of your mission to your team. I'm sure you've spoken about it with all of them, in broad terms, but a series of one-on-one encounters is no way to form and communicate a strategy. You're dealing with matters of great importance, and you should assemble everyone to speak with them."
    new "And if you haven't already, take the time to communicate the plans of your mission to your team. I'm sure you've spoken about it with all of them, in broad terms, but a series of one-on-one encounters is no way to form and communicate a strategy. You're dealing with matters of great importance, and you should assemble everyone to speak with them.\n还有,如果你还没做的话,请抽时间把你的任务计划传达给团队。我相信你已经和他们每个人都大致谈过,但一连串一对一的碰面,无法形成并传达一套战略。你处理的是至关重要的大事,你应该把所有人召集起来,和他们好好谈谈。"

    old "That sounds like a good idea, Karen."
    new "That sounds like a good idea, Karen.\n听起来是个好主意,Karen。"

    old "Oh, and [protag], one more thing. There's another reason I suggested that you form an assembly. I'd like to meet your team members."
    new "Oh, and [protag], one more thing. There's another reason I suggested that you form an assembly. I'd like to meet your team members.\n哦,还有,[protag],再有一件事。我建议你召集会面,还有另一个原因——我想见见你的团队成员。"

    old "What for?"
    new "What for?\n为什么呢?"

    old "If you've judged these people worthy of joining your cause, then surely they must be people worth knowing. Also, there is a distinct possibility that my own Amazon warriors might one day fight in tandem with your little task force, depending on the scope of battle. If that were ever to happen, I think it would put me at ease to know exactly who my allies would be."
    new "If you've judged these people worthy of joining your cause, then surely they must be people worth knowing. Also, there is a distinct possibility that my own Amazon warriors might one day fight in tandem with your little task force, depending on the scope of battle. If that were ever to happen, I think it would put me at ease to know exactly who my allies would be.\n如果你认定这些人值得加入你的事业,那他们一定也值得认识。此外,我的Amazon战士将来很有可能与你的小特遣队并肩作战,这取决于战斗的规模。倘若真有那一天,我想,确切知道自己的盟友是谁,会让我安心许多。"

    old "You'd fight alongside us?"
    new "You'd fight alongside us?\n你会和我们并肩作战?"

    old "Or above you, as the case may be. As I recall, the first time I saw you it was from the back of my griffon. But the truth is, my request is more rooted in curiosity than anything. So if you wouldn't mind indulging me, I would like to see the group of individuals that you've chosen to call allies."
    new "Or above you, as the case may be. As I recall, the first time I saw you it was from the back of my griffon. But the truth is, my request is more rooted in curiosity than anything. So if you wouldn't mind indulging me, I would like to see the group of individuals that you've chosen to call allies.\n或者是在你们上方作战,视情况而定。我记得,我第一次见到你,就是从我的狮鹫背上。不过说实话,我的请求更多出于好奇。所以,如果你不介意迁就我一下,我想见见你选作盟友的那群人。"

    old "Alright, Karen. I'll bring them to the citadel some time."
    new "Alright, Karen. I'll bring them to the citadel some time.\n好的,Karen。我改天带他们来要塞。"

    old "Actually, I think perhaps it would be best if I met them outside of the citadel."
    new "Actually, I think perhaps it would be best if I met them outside of the citadel.\n其实,我想,也许在要塞外面见他们更好。"

    old "My sentries might not respond too well to seeing a ragtag group of individuals making their way here, and besides, the citadel is quite far to travel for those living near the center of the continent. Besides, I don't mean to make the event more formal than it needs to be."
    new "My sentries might not respond too well to seeing a ragtag group of individuals making their way here, and besides, the citadel is quite far to travel for those living near the center of the continent. Besides, I don't mean to make the event more formal than it needs to be.\n我的哨兵们看到一群乌合之众往这里来,反应恐怕不会太好。再说,对住在大陆中心附近的人来说,这要塞也实在太远。况且,我并不想让这件事变得比必要的更正式。"

    old "A camp in a neutral area seems like a much better approach than a formal audience in the citadel."
    new "A camp in a neutral area seems like a much better approach than a formal audience in the citadel.\n在中立地区扎个营地,似乎比在要塞里正式觐见要好得多。"

    old "Interesting. We'll make it happen, then."
    new "Interesting. We'll make it happen, then.\n有意思。那我们就这么办。"

    old "Excellent. I look forward to it, [protag]. When you find the time, you can make arrangements through Leena. Simply assemble your group for a meeting, and I'll accompany Leena."
    new "Excellent. I look forward to it, [protag]. When you find the time, you can make arrangements through Leena. Simply assemble your group for a meeting, and I'll accompany Leena.\n太好了。我很期待,[protag]。等你方便时,可以通过Leena来安排。只需把你的队伍召集起来开个会,我会随Leena一同前来。"

    old "Karen wants to speak with all of us, so my companions and I meet up with her at the Citadel."
    new "Karen wants to speak with all of us, so my companions and I meet up with her at the Citadel.\nKaren想和我们大家谈谈,于是我和同伴们到要塞去见她。"

    old "I must say, you have impressed me, [protag]."
    new "I must say, you have impressed me, [protag].\n不得不说,你给我留下了深刻印象,[protag]。"

    old "Thank you, Karen, but, um, may I ask how exactly?"
    new "Thank you, Karen, but, um, may I ask how exactly?\n谢谢,Karen,不过,呃,能问问具体是什么吗?"

    old "You've managed to recruit quite a few people for our cause."
    new "You've managed to recruit quite a few people for our cause.\n你为我们的事业招募到了不少人。"

    old "Karen's gaze drifts towards the companions who've joined me in the hall."
    new "Karen's gaze drifts towards the companions who've joined me in the hall.\nKaren的目光飘向那些随我进入大厅的同伴。"

    old "I see that you followed my advice and collected the very best from all corners of Aravorn. Well done."
    new "I see that you followed my advice and collected the very best from all corners of Aravorn. Well done.\n看来你听从了我的建议,从Aravorn的四面八方网罗了最出色的人手。干得漂亮。"

    old "Karen's words are met with approval from the others. Though most of their responses get lost in all of the murmuring, I am able to make out bits and pieces."
    new "Karen's words are met with approval from the others. Though most of their responses get lost in all of the murmuring, I am able to make out bits and pieces.\nKaren的话得到了其他人的认同。虽然大部分回应都淹没在一片低语声中,但我还是能听清只言片语。"

    old "Damn. Karen. She's hot."
    new "Damn. Karen. She's hot.\n天哪,Karen,她真辣。"

    old "Shhh! Sylrissa."
    new "Shhh! Sylrissa.\n嘘!Sylrissa。"

    old "I'm surprised when the intense glare etched on Leena's face doesn't instantly kill Sylrissa. I don't think I've ever seen a look that powerful."
    new "I'm surprised when the intense glare etched on Leena's face doesn't instantly kill Sylrissa. I don't think I've ever seen a look that powerful.\n令我惊讶的是,Leena脸上那道凌厉的目光竟然没能当场把Sylrissa瞪死。我想我从未见过那么有杀伤力的眼神。"

    old "Karen resumes speaking as if nothing had happened. Of course, it's always possible that she simply didn't hear what Sylrissa said in the first place."
    new "Karen resumes speaking as if nothing had happened. Of course, it's always possible that she simply didn't hear what Sylrissa said in the first place.\nKaren若无其事地继续讲话。当然,也说不定她一开始就根本没听见Sylrissa说了什么。"

    old "I wanted to apologize for not coming to your first meeting which is why I invited you all here."
    new "I wanted to apologize for not coming to your first meeting which is why I invited you all here.\n我想为没能出席你们的第一次会议而道歉,这也是我邀请你们大家到这里来的原因。"

    old "Ah, that explains it. I was surprised. I mean, it's not like the amazons are known for welcoming guests into their Citadel."
    new "Ah, that explains it. I was surprised. I mean, it's not like the amazons are known for welcoming guests into their Citadel.\n啊,原来如此。我还纳闷呢。我是说,Amazon可不是以欢迎客人进入她们的要塞而闻名的。"

    old "If you continue saying disrespectful things in front of our Queen, this will be the last time you're welcomed anywhere."
    new "If you continue saying disrespectful things in front of our Queen, this will be the last time you're welcomed anywhere.\n如果你继续在女王陛下面前说这些不敬的话,这将是你最后一次在任何地方受到欢迎。"

    old "Leena, please. What is your name, young man?"
    new "Leena, please. What is your name, young man?\nLeena,算了吧。你叫什么名字,年轻人?"

    old "I'm Jasper."
    new "I'm Jasper.\n我是Jasper。"

    old "Ah, the pirate. Leena told me much about you."
    new "Ah, the pirate. Leena told me much about you.\n啊,那个海盗。Leena跟我说了不少你的事。"

    old "She did, did she? Good things I hope."
    new "She did, did she? Good things I hope.\n她说了?但愿都是好话。"

    old "Only the truth."
    new "Only the truth.\n只有实话。"

    old "Ouch. I'm screwed then."
    new "Ouch. I'm screwed then.\n哎哟,那我可完蛋了。"

    old "We laugh. Then Larik steps forward and bows to Karen."
    new "We laugh. Then Larik steps forward and bows to Karen.\n我们都笑了。接着Larik走上前,向Karen鞠躬。"

    old "It is a honor to meet you."
    new "It is a honor to meet you.\n很荣幸见到您。"

    old "Finally, someone who knows how to behave."
    new "Finally, someone who knows how to behave.\n终于有个懂规矩的人了。"

    old "Ah, you must be the Warchief of the Dunemarchers. Rise up, my friend."
    new "Ah, you must be the Warchief of the Dunemarchers. Rise up, my friend.\n啊,你一定是Dunemarchers的战酋。起来吧,我的朋友。"

    old "And you, handsome young woman? What is your name?"
    new "And you, handsome young woman? What is your name?\n而你,漂亮的年轻女士,你叫什么名字?"

    old "Nuala, my Queen. Ehm, I mean, Queen Karen."
    new "Nuala, my Queen. Ehm, I mean, Queen Karen.\nNuala,我的女王。呃,我是说,Karen女王。"

    old "Did Nuala just blush? She seems flustered. Well, considering how Karen is looking at her, I can understand it."
    new "Did Nuala just blush? She seems flustered. Well, considering how Karen is looking at her, I can understand it.\nNuala刚才是脸红了吗?她看起来局促不安。嗯,想想Karen看她的眼神,我也能理解。"

    old "Your build is excellent, Nuala. You put some of my amazons to shame."
    new "Your build is excellent, Nuala. You put some of my amazons to shame.\n你的体格真棒,Nuala。你让我的不少Amazon战士都自愧不如。"

    old "Th-thank you."
    new "Th-thank you.\n谢、谢谢。"

    old "Haha, she is melting right now. Leena doesn't look too happy though."
    new "Haha, she is melting right now. Leena doesn't look too happy though.\n哈哈,她这会儿都要化了。不过Leena看起来可不太高兴。"

    old "She's young. Your build is even better, queen Karen."
    new "She's young. Your build is even better, queen Karen.\n她还年轻。你的身材更好,Karen女王。"

    old "Karen laughs, and then gestures for the two nagas to come forward."
    new "Karen laughs, and then gestures for the two nagas to come forward.\nKaren笑了,然后示意那两位Naga走上前来。"

    old "Normally, you two would be killed on sight by my guards."
    new "Normally, you two would be killed on sight by my guards.\n正常情况下,你们两个会被我的卫兵当场格杀。"

    old "Ouch. You amazons really need to improve on your hospitality."
    new "Ouch. You amazons really need to improve on your hospitality.\n哎哟。你们Amazon真该好好改善一下待客之道了。"

    old "But [protag] told me about you first and then Leena. You two seem very different from the nagas we've met in the past."
    new "But [protag] told me about you first and then Leena. You two seem very different from the nagas we've met in the past.\n但[protag]先跟我讲了你们的事,然后是Leena。你们俩和我们过去见过的Naga很不一样。"

    old "We are, Queen Karen. That's why we were exiled."
    new "We are, Queen Karen. That's why we were exiled.\n我们确实不一样,Karen女王。这正是我们被放逐的原因。"

    old "I'm sorry to hear that, of course. But I'd be lying if I said that I wasn't happy that this turn of events brought both of you to us. Your help has been invaluable."
    new "I'm sorry to hear that, of course. But I'd be lying if I said that I wasn't happy that this turn of events brought both of you to us. Your help has been invaluable.\n我当然为你们感到难过。但如果我说,我并不为这个转折把你们俩带到我们身边而高兴,那就是在说谎了。你们的帮助非常宝贵。"

    old "Fighting the undead alongside Leena has been a real honor."
    new "Fighting the undead alongside Leena has been a real honor.\n能与Leena并肩对抗亡灵,是莫大的荣幸。"

    old "Leena smiles and looks at Enok fondly. If I wasn't so sure that she only liked women, I might think that there was something there."
    new "Leena smiles and looks at Enok fondly. If I wasn't so sure that she only liked women, I might think that there was something there.\nLeena微笑着,满怀怜爱地看着Enok。要不是我十分确定她只喜欢女人,我或许会以为他们之间有点什么。"

    old "And you two, little ones?"
    new "And you two, little ones?\n那你们两个小家伙呢?"

    old "Your manners, Dasyra!"
    new "Your manners, Dasyra!\n注意你的礼数,Dasyra!"

    old "Oops, ehm, sorry your highness. I guess I got a little too excited and forgot the proper etiquette."
    new "Oops, ehm, sorry your highness. I guess I got a little too excited and forgot the proper etiquette.\n哎呀,呃,抱歉,陛下。我想我是太兴奋了,把应有的礼节给忘了。"

    old "Karen laughs and Leena relaxes a bit in turn."
    new "Karen laughs and Leena relaxes a bit in turn.\nKaren笑了,Leena也随之放松了些。"

    old "Haha, don't worry Dasyra. This is more of an informal meeting. I promise not to be too harsh on my guests."
    new "Haha, don't worry Dasyra. This is more of an informal meeting. I promise not to be too harsh on my guests.\n哈哈,别担心,Dasyra。这更像是一次非正式的会面。我保证不会对我的客人太苛刻。"

    old "And you must be Galan."
    new "And you must be Galan.\n那你一定是Galan了。"

    old "Your majesty. How is Loren's training going? I am sorry that our little experiment didn't work."
    new "Your majesty. How is Loren's training going? I am sorry that our little experiment didn't work.\n陛下。Loren的训练进展如何?很抱歉,我们的小实验没有成功。"

    old "Well, she's still a little rebel. I hope she'll change as she grows up. She'll have to if she wants to be a good queen."
    new "Well, she's still a little rebel. I hope she'll change as she grows up. She'll have to if she wants to be a good queen.\n唉,她还是个小叛逆。我希望她长大后能有所改变。若想成为一位好女王,她就必须改变。"

    old "In any case, that's a matter for another time. I didn't invite you all here just to talk, after all. Come, follow me."
    new "In any case, that's a matter for another time. I didn't invite you all here just to talk, after all. Come, follow me.\n无论如何,那是另一回事了。我请你们大家来,毕竟不是光为了聊天。来,跟我走。"

    old "Karen leads us to the dining room and offers us some Amazon wine. Once everyone is seated, a few amazons start pouring our drinks."
    new "Karen leads us to the dining room and offers us some Amazon wine. Once everyone is seated, a few amazons start pouring our drinks.\nKaren带我们到餐厅,请我们喝Amazon葡萄酒。等大家都落座后,几个Amazon上前为我们斟酒。"

    old "The wine's enticing, aromatic scent is only surpassed by it's exquisite taste. I'd say its fame is rightly earned."
    new "The wine's enticing, aromatic scent is only surpassed by it's exquisite taste. I'd say its fame is rightly earned.\n这酒诱人的芳香,只有它精美的口感才配得上。我想它声名远扬确是实至名归。"

    old "After a bit, Karen approaches me with two guards following her at a distance."
    new "After a bit, Karen approaches me with two guards following her at a distance.\n过了一会儿,Karen朝我走来,两名卫兵远远跟在她身后。"

    old "I must admit, I wasn't expecting this."
    new "I must admit, I wasn't expecting this.\n我得承认,我没想到会这样。"

    old "Oh? You didn't think Amazons would have a basic understanding of good manners?"
    new "Oh? You didn't think Amazons would have a basic understanding of good manners?\n哦?你以为Amazon连基本的礼貌都不懂吗?"

    old "No! I didn't mean it like that. I just... Well, it was a nice surprise."
    new "No! I didn't mean it like that. I just... Well, it was a nice surprise.\n不!我不是那个意思。我只是……嗯,这是个惊喜。"

    old "Oh, [protag], you should know that I'm a woman full of surprises."
    new "Oh, [protag], you should know that I'm a woman full of surprises.\n哦,[protag],你该知道,我是个充满惊喜的女人。"

    old "Without adding anything else, she turns to leave. Wait, did she just wink at me? No... She wouldn't, right? It must have been my imagination."
    new "Without adding anything else, she turns to leave. Wait, did she just wink at me? No... She wouldn't, right? It must have been my imagination.\n她没再多说什么,转身就要离开。等等,她刚才是对我眨眼了吗?不……她不会吧,对吗?一定是我的错觉。"

    old "Is it just me, or is it getting hot in here? I'd better go grab some more wine... or maybe I'll just drink water tonight."
    new "Is it just me, or is it getting hot in here? I'd better go grab some more wine... or maybe I'll just drink water tonight.\n是我的错觉,还是这里越来越热了?我最好再去倒点酒……或者,今晚我还是喝白水吧。"

    old "The wine could be the reason behind all of these strange thoughts, after all."
    new "The wine could be the reason behind all of these strange thoughts, after all.\n毕竟,这些古怪念头背后的原因,说不定就是那酒。"

    old "Outside Grimoire, I get ready to pick my team for tonight's mission. Who to choose?"
    new "Outside Grimoire, I get ready to pick my team for tonight's mission. Who to choose?\n在Grimoire城外,我准备为今晚的任务挑选我的队伍。该选谁呢?"

    old "Hold up."
    new "Hold up.\n等一下。"

    old "What is it, Leena?"
    new "What is it, Leena?\n怎么了,Leena?"

    old "Look above. Griffon."
    new "Look above. Griffon.\n看天上。狮鹫。"

    old "I cast my eye skyward, and through the misty fog, I can see a figure moving overhead, swooping nearer to the earth before landing on a nearby hill."
    new "I cast my eye skyward, and through the misty fog, I can see a figure moving overhead, swooping nearer to the earth before landing on a nearby hill.\n我把目光投向天空,透过迷雾,看见一个人影在头顶移动,向下俯冲,落到了附近的一座山丘上。"

    old "Who might that be?"
    new "Who might that be?\n那会是谁呢?"

    old "It came from the direction of the Amazon Citadel. Likely a courier, come to deliver some sort of message. Perhaps valuable intelligence came through."
    new "It came from the direction of the Amazon Citadel. Likely a courier, come to deliver some sort of message. Perhaps valuable intelligence came through.\n它来自Amazon要塞的方向。很可能是信使,前来传递某种消息。也许是宝贵的情报送到了。"

    old "Let's hurry to meet them, then."
    new "Let's hurry to meet them, then.\n那我们快去见见他们吧。"

    old "I rush over to the spot where the griffon landed, and as I approach, I see the familiar face of the Amazon Queen."
    new "I rush over to the spot where the griffon landed, and as I approach, I see the familiar face of the Amazon Queen.\n我赶到狮鹫降落的地方,走近时,看到了Amazon女王那张熟悉的面孔。"

    old "Karen? Is that you?"
    new "Karen? Is that you?\nKaren?是你吗?"

    old "Hello, [protag]. You probably didn't expect to see me here tonight."
    new "Hello, [protag]. You probably didn't expect to see me here tonight.\n你好,[protag]。你大概没想到今晚会在这里见到我。"

    old "Karen..."
    new "Karen...\nKaren……"

    old "It's good to see you."
    new "It's good to see you.\n见到你真好。"

    old "Unfortunately, I wish I could say the same. If all were well, I would not be here right now, but unfortunate circumstances forced me here."
    new "Unfortunately, I wish I could say the same. If all were well, I would not be here right now, but unfortunate circumstances forced me here.\n可惜,我也希望能说同样的话。如果一切安好,我现在就不会在这里了。是不幸的境况把我逼到了这里。"

    old "You shouldn't be here."
    new "You shouldn't be here.\n你不该来这里。"

    old "You're right, I shouldn't be here. My appearance before you tonight is, I must confess, the culmination in a series of blunders."
    new "You're right, I shouldn't be here. My appearance before you tonight is, I must confess, the culmination in a series of blunders.\n你说得对,我不该来。我必须承认,今晚出现在你面前,是一连串失误酿成的结果。"

    old "What are you talking about?"
    new "What are you talking about?\n你在说什么?"

    old "Last night, several Amazons left the citadel. They went to castle N'Mar."
    new "Last night, several Amazons left the citadel. They went to castle N'Mar.\n昨晚,几个Amazon离开了要塞。他们去了N'Mar城堡。"

    old "What? Why would they do that?"
    new "What? Why would they do that?\n什么?他们为什么要那么做?"

    old "One of them was a mother. Her daughter had gone missing, and was last reported near the plains. And there are fewer forces more formidable than a mother who believes her child is in danger."
    new "One of them was a mother. Her daughter had gone missing, and was last reported near the plains. And there are fewer forces more formidable than a mother who believes her child is in danger.\n其中一位是位母亲。她的女儿失踪了,最后一次有消息是在平原附近。而世间没有多少力量,比一个坚信自己孩子身处险境的母亲更强大。"

    old "She managed to persuade several other Amazons to accompany her to find her daughter."
    new "She managed to persuade several other Amazons to accompany her to find her daughter.\n她说服了另外几个Amazon陪她一起去找女儿。"

    old "This...is deeply troubling, for a number of reasons. For one..."
    new "This...is deeply troubling, for a number of reasons. For one...\n这……令人深感不安,原因有很多。其一……"

    old "Why would they march into the face of danger like that? Going to the castle with no information other than that a girl was missing...the risks are far too great."
    new "Why would they march into the face of danger like that? Going to the castle with no information other than that a girl was missing...the risks are far too great.\n他们为什么要那样冲向险境?仅仅因为一个女孩失踪,就毫无情报地直奔城堡……风险实在太大了。"

    old "That was a foolish decision. The most effective attacks take time to plan. I should know, having been tasked with assembling a team to invade Castle N'Mar myself. I've spent weeks and weeks preparing for this...for someone to try and attempt the same thing with not even a day of preparation seems like absolute folly."
    new "That was a foolish decision. The most effective attacks take time to plan. I should know, having been tasked with assembling a team to invade Castle N'Mar myself. I've spent weeks and weeks preparing for this...for someone to try and attempt the same thing with not even a day of preparation seems like absolute folly.\n那是个愚蠢的决定。最有效的进攻需要时间谋划。我自己就受命组建一支队伍入侵N'Mar城堡,对此再清楚不过。我花了好几周又好几周来准备……而有人连一天的准备都没有,就试图做同样的事,这简直是彻头彻尾的疯狂。"

    old "Why wasn't I consulted? From the fact that nobody from the council told me this, I assume none of them know. You knew that the council had a plan and a strategy to deal with N'Mar, and this spur-of-the-moment decision threatens to undermine all of that."
    new "Why wasn't I consulted? From the fact that nobody from the council told me this, I assume none of them know. You knew that the council had a plan and a strategy to deal with N'Mar, and this spur-of-the-moment decision threatens to undermine all of that.\n为什么没人来问过我?议会里没人告诉我这件事,我由此推断他们对此一无所知。你明知道议会有一套应对N'Mar的计划和策略,而这一时冲动的决定,很可能把这一切全部毁掉。"

    old "I'm equally upset, [protag]. Believe me, if I had known that any of this was happening, I would have stopped it immediately. It was not until earlier today that we learned that several Amazons had left the night before."
    new "I'm equally upset, [protag]. Believe me, if I had known that any of this was happening, I would have stopped it immediately. It was not until earlier today that we learned that several Amazons had left the night before.\n我也同样愤怒,[protag]。相信我,如果我早知道发生了这种事,一定会立即阻止。直到今天早些时候,我们才得知有几个Amazon在前一天夜里离开了。"

    old "Queen Karen, this is my first time hearing of this as well. I apologize for not being attendant in my duties of discovering and reporting those who have gone missing."
    new "Queen Karen, this is my first time hearing of this as well. I apologize for not being attendant in my duties of discovering and reporting those who have gone missing.\nKaren女王,我也是头一次听说此事。我为自己没有尽到职责,发现并上报那些失踪的人而道歉。"

    old "Nonsense, Leena. There is no need for you to apologize for this. Your priorities were with preparing to assist [protag] tonight, not with keeping the warriors of the citadel in check. The blame falls squarely on my shoulders."
    new "Nonsense, Leena. There is no need for you to apologize for this. Your priorities were with preparing to assist [protag] tonight, not with keeping the warriors of the citadel in check. The blame falls squarely on my shoulders.\n胡说什么,Leena。你无须为此道歉。你的当务之急是准备今晚协助[protag],而不是盯住要塞里的战士们。这责任完全在我肩上。"

    old "That is why I came to tell you directly. You are the first person outside the citadel to find out."
    new "That is why I came to tell you directly. You are the first person outside the citadel to find out.\n所以我才会亲自来告诉你。你是要塞之外第一个知道的人。"

    old "The council doesn't know."
    new "The council doesn't know.\n议会还不知道。"

    old "That is correct."
    new "That is correct.\n没错。"

    old "The council needs to know this."
    new "The council needs to know this.\n议会需要知道这件事。"

    old "You're right to think that, [protag]. You have a duty to the council, and it is incumbent on you to inform them of critical information like this."
    new "You're right to think that, [protag]. You have a duty to the council, and it is incumbent on you to inform them of critical information like this.\n你这么想是对的,[protag]。你对议会负有责任,把这样的关键信息告知他们,是你的义务。"

    old "However...I have but one request. If you are going to tell the council, do not tell them until after you have completed the mission."
    new "However...I have but one request. If you are going to tell the council, do not tell them until after you have completed the mission.\n不过……我只有一个请求。如果你要告诉议会,请在你完成任务之后再告诉他们。"

    old "If the council doesn't know, then I'd prefer to keep it that way."
    new "If the council doesn't know, then I'd prefer to keep it that way.\n如果议会不知道,那我宁愿保持现状。"

    old "That was my thinking as well, [protag]. But it is reassuring to hear you say the same thing."
    new "That was my thinking as well, [protag]. But it is reassuring to hear you say the same thing.\n我也是这么想的,[protag]。但听到你也这么说,令人安心。"

    old "The truth is, things have always been tense between the Amazons and the human empire."
    new "The truth is, things have always been tense between the Amazons and the human empire.\n事实是,Amazon与人类帝国之间的关系一直很紧张。"

    old "You fear the political consequences if they find out?"
    new "You fear the political consequences if they find out?\n你担心他们发现后会带来政治后果?"

    old "Make no mistake, [protag]. It is very likely that they will find out. But right now, tonight, you are the one who needs to take action. Bringing this information to the council will likely force them to cancel your mission."
    new "Make no mistake, [protag]. It is very likely that they will find out. But right now, tonight, you are the one who needs to take action. Bringing this information to the council will likely force them to cancel your mission.\n别弄错了,[protag]。他们很可能会发现。但此时此刻,今晚,你才是需要采取行动的人。把这条情报呈给议会,很可能会迫使他们取消你的任务。"

    old "I can only imagine some overly-cautious council member telling you that they need more time to prepare in light of changing circumstances."
    new "I can only imagine some overly-cautious council member telling you that they need more time to prepare in light of changing circumstances.\n我几乎可以想象,某个过分谨慎的议员会对你说,鉴于局势有变,他们需要更多时间来准备。"

    old "That argument might be justified in some situations. But right now, there is no time to delay. Time is too precious. You need to go on the mission tonight. So keep this information to yourself, for the time being."
    new "That argument might be justified in some situations. But right now, there is no time to delay. Time is too precious. You need to go on the mission tonight. So keep this information to yourself, for the time being.\n在某些情况下,这种说法或许有道理。但现在,没有时间可以拖延。时间太宝贵了。你今晚必须去执行任务。所以,暂时把这条情报藏在心里。"

    old "Is that why you came to tell me yourself instead of sending a scout?"
    new "Is that why you came to tell me yourself instead of sending a scout?\n所以你才亲自来告诉我,而不是派个侦察兵?"

    old "Well observed, [protag]. You are correct. I wanted to give you this information myself to avoid it leaking out. Although, I feel I should point out a much more obvious reason for me to come myself."
    new "Well observed, [protag]. You are correct. I wanted to give you this information myself to avoid it leaking out. Although, I feel I should point out a much more obvious reason for me to come myself.\n观察得不错,[protag]。你说得对。我想亲自把这条情报交给你,以免走漏。不过,我觉得我还是应该指出一个更明显、让我亲自前来的理由。"

    old "And that is?"
    new "And that is?\n那是什么?"

    old "It's difficult enough to see people on the ground from the back of a griffon, even without mist, and I know your face better than anyone in the citadel. The truth is, I had to come here myself, not because I didn't trust a scout or courier not to leak it, but because I couldn't trust them to find you."
    new "It's difficult enough to see people on the ground from the back of a griffon, even without mist, and I know your face better than anyone in the citadel. The truth is, I had to come here myself, not because I didn't trust a scout or courier not to leak it, but because I couldn't trust them to find you.\n即便没有雾,从狮鹫背上看清地上的人也很困难,而我比要塞里的任何人都更熟悉你的脸。事实上,我必须亲自来,不是因为信不过侦察兵或信使不会走漏消息,而是因为我信不过他们能找到你。"

    old "There is also the fact that the council wouldn't take too kindly to a random Amazon appearing this close to their territory..."
    new "There is also the fact that the council wouldn't take too kindly to a random Amazon appearing this close to their territory...\n还有一个事实,那就是议会对一个Amazon贸然出现在他们领地附近,可不会有什么好脸色……"

    old "Yes, that too. Although, I can assure you that the political consequences of this meeting are only of interest to me insofar as they affect your ability to perform your responsibilities tonight."
    new "Yes, that too. Although, I can assure you that the political consequences of this meeting are only of interest to me insofar as they affect your ability to perform your responsibilities tonight.\n对,这也是。不过,我可以向你保证,这次会面的政治后果,只有影响到你今晚履行职责的能力时,才是我关心的。"

    old "Let's talk about the mission, then. What should I know, going forward? How will the incident with the Amazons who decided to launch their own mission affect things?"
    new "Let's talk about the mission, then. What should I know, going forward? How will the incident with the Amazons who decided to launch their own mission affect things?\n那我们来谈谈任务吧。接下来我该知道些什么?那些Amazon自行发起的行动,会怎样影响局势?"

    old "From the fact that we have not heard from them, I can only surmise that their mission was a failure. They were likely caught and captured."
    new "From the fact that we have not heard from them, I can only surmise that their mission was a failure. They were likely caught and captured.\n从我们没有收到他们任何消息这一点来看,我只能推测他们的行动失败了。他们很可能被抓住并俘虏了。"

    old "I don't think vampires are the type to take prisoners. As much as it pains me to say it, they may already be dead."
    new "I don't think vampires are the type to take prisoners. As much as it pains me to say it, they may already be dead.\n我觉得吸血鬼不是会留俘虏的类型。虽然我很不想这么说,但他们可能已经死了。"

    old "I was thinking the opposite, [protag]. A living prisoner has all sorts of uses to a vampire clan. They drink blood, and they like it best when it comes fresh. I've heard tale of many vampires keeping prisoners alive to feed on."
    new "I was thinking the opposite, [protag]. A living prisoner has all sorts of uses to a vampire clan. They drink blood, and they like it best when it comes fresh. I've heard tale of many vampires keeping prisoners alive to feed on.\n我的想法正相反,[protag]。一个活着的俘虏,对吸血鬼部族有各种用途。他们吸血,而且最喜欢新鲜的血液。我听过不少传闻,说许多吸血鬼会把俘虏养着活口,以便吸血。"

    old "I would not expect them to survive a particularly long imprisonment. But given that they have been gone only a day, I have high hopes that they are still living."
    new "I would not expect them to survive a particularly long imprisonment. But given that they have been gone only a day, I have high hopes that they are still living.\n我并不指望他们能熬过特别漫长的囚禁。但考虑到他们才离开一天,我很希望他们仍活着。"

    old "Knowing vampires, they're probably still alive. If we manage to find them, there is certainly the possibility that they could be returned the citadel, albeit with perhaps slightly less blood than when the vampires find them."
    new "Knowing vampires, they're probably still alive. If we manage to find them, there is certainly the possibility that they could be returned the citadel, albeit with perhaps slightly less blood than when the vampires find them.\n以我对吸血鬼的了解,他们很可能还活着。如果我们能找到他们,他们当然有可能被送回要塞,尽管血液也许比吸血鬼找到他们时少了那么一点。"

    old "That is a macabre way to put it, but I agree with your suspicions, [protag]. I would be surprised if the vampires killed them outright."
    new "That is a macabre way to put it, but I agree with your suspicions, [protag]. I would be surprised if the vampires killed them outright.\n这说法可真够阴森的,不过我同意你的推测,[protag]。如果吸血鬼直接杀了他们,我倒会感到意外。"

    old "So, you're suggesting a rescue mission?"
    new "So, you're suggesting a rescue mission?\n所以,你是在建议一次营救任务?"

    old "The possibility certainly exists, [protag]. However, I know that I cannot force you to correct the mistakes that my warriors have made. You ultimately report to the council, not me."
    new "The possibility certainly exists, [protag]. However, I know that I cannot force you to correct the mistakes that my warriors have made. You ultimately report to the council, not me.\n这种可能当然存在,[protag]。不过,我知道自己不能强迫你去弥补我的战士们犯下的过错。你终究是向议会报告,而不是向我。"

    old "Karen, there are people in peril. I know I have responsibilities to the council, but if there are prisoners, the lives of those prisoners need to come first."
    new "Karen, there are people in peril. I know I have responsibilities to the council, but if there are prisoners, the lives of those prisoners need to come first.\nKaren,有人正身处险境。我知道自己对议会负有责任,但如果有俘虏,那些俘虏的生命必须放在首位。"

    old "Karen, I've been tasked by the council to discover the source of the corruption spreading from the castle. Ultimately, the fate of cities, or perhaps an entire empire, may depend on my ability to determine what is afoot there. That needs to be my priority."
    new "Karen, I've been tasked by the council to discover the source of the corruption spreading from the castle. Ultimately, the fate of cities, or perhaps an entire empire, may depend on my ability to determine what is afoot there. That needs to be my priority.\nKaren,议会派我去查明从城堡蔓延开来的腐化之源。最终,许多城市,乃至整个帝国的命运,都可能取决于我能否弄清那里正在发生什么。这必须是我的首要任务。"

    old "Perhaps you do not need to choose one or the other. The council wants you to obtain information about what is going on in N'Mar, and I would appreciate the return of any Amazons being held there. It seems likely to me that anyone being held prisoner in castle N'Mar is likely to be a source of information about it."
    new "Perhaps you do not need to choose one or the other. The council wants you to obtain information about what is going on in N'Mar, and I would appreciate the return of any Amazons being held there. It seems likely to me that anyone being held prisoner in castle N'Mar is likely to be a source of information about it.\n也许你并不需要二选一。议会想让你获取N'Mar内部情况的情报,而我则希望任何被关押在那里的Amazon能被送回来。在我看来,任何被囚禁在N'Mar城堡里的人,都很可能是关于那里的情报来源。"

    old "You think the prisoners would have good information?"
    new "You think the prisoners would have good information?\n你觉得俘虏们会掌握有价值的情报?"

    old "Why not? For one thing, they'd likely have a lay of the land. At the very least, it would be useful intel for future scouting. And I would also not be surprised if they happened to overhear things inside the castle."
    new "Why not? For one thing, they'd likely have a lay of the land. At the very least, it would be useful intel for future scouting. And I would also not be surprised if they happened to overhear things inside the castle.\n为什么不呢?首先,她们很可能熟悉当地地形。至少,这对日后的侦察是有用的情报。而且,如果她们碰巧在城堡里听到了什么,我也不会感到惊讶。"

    old "You think that vampires would discuss secrets openly around prisoners?"
    new "You think that vampires would discuss secrets openly around prisoners?\n你觉得吸血鬼会当着俘虏的面公开讨论秘密?"

    old "If they're confident that the prisoners will never escape—and, knowing vampires, they probably are—I wouldn't be surprised if they happened to divulge information they never expected to leave those walls."
    new "If they're confident that the prisoners will never escape—and, knowing vampires, they probably are—I wouldn't be surprised if they happened to divulge information they never expected to leave those walls.\n如果他们确信俘虏永远逃不出去——而且以吸血鬼的性子,他们多半很确信——那么,如果他们随口泄露了那些本以为绝不会传出高墙的信息,我也不会惊讶。"

    old "Of course, I cannot promise that the prisoners hold the keys to the mysteries you hope to unravel. But it seems very likely to be beneficial to you."
    new "Of course, I cannot promise that the prisoners hold the keys to the mysteries you hope to unravel. But it seems very likely to be beneficial to you.\n当然,我不能保证俘虏们掌握着你希望解开谜团的关键。但这看起来极有可能对你有益。"

    old "Hmm..."
    new "Hmm...\n嗯……"

    old "Well then. It seems that our reconnaissance mission has become a rescue mission. Karen, I can make no promises regarding the fate of any Amazons that might have been captured, but I think it will serve the interests of all involved if I try to locate them. I will certainly make an effort."
    new "Well then. It seems that our reconnaissance mission has become a rescue mission. Karen, I can make no promises regarding the fate of any Amazons that might have been captured, but I think it will serve the interests of all involved if I try to locate them. I will certainly make an effort.\n那么好吧。看来我们的侦察任务变成了营救任务。Karen,我无法保证任何可能被俘的Amazon的命运,但我认为,尽力寻找他们,符合所有相关方的利益。我一定会尽力而为。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]. An effort is all that I can ask for."
    new "Thank you, [protag]. An effort is all that I can ask for.\n谢谢你,[protag]。尽力,就是我所能要求的全部了。"

    old "I walk to the citadel. It's certainly not the first time I've walked along this stretch of land, and I find myself noticing several Amazon sentries looking at me from a distance. Several of them give me a nod of assent as I walk."
    new "I walk to the citadel. It's certainly not the first time I've walked along this stretch of land, and I find myself noticing several Amazon sentries looking at me from a distance. Several of them give me a nod of assent as I walk.\n我走向要塞。这绝不是我第一次走这条路了,我发现自己注意到远处有几个Amazon哨兵在看着我。我走过时,其中几位朝我点头示意。"

    old "I'm not sure if there are more Amazon sentries out today than the last time I came through here, or whether this is just the first time I'm seeing so many of them. It could be that in the past, most of them just watched me from a concealed position, and now they don't bother to conceal themselves now that they know I'm not a threat."
    new "I'm not sure if there are more Amazon sentries out today than the last time I came through here, or whether this is just the first time I'm seeing so many of them. It could be that in the past, most of them just watched me from a concealed position, and now they don't bother to conceal themselves now that they know I'm not a threat.\n我不确定今天外出的Amazon哨兵是否比上次经过时更多,还是说这只是我第一次看到这么多。也许过去她们大多藏在隐蔽处盯着我,如今知道我不构成威胁,便懒得再躲了。"

    old "It does seem odd to see so many sentries, though. The citadel is ever vigilant. I wonder if attackers ever come to their walls? It seems like it would take a crazy person to try and penetrate their defenses."
    new "It does seem odd to see so many sentries, though. The citadel is ever vigilant. I wonder if attackers ever come to their walls? It seems like it would take a crazy person to try and penetrate their defenses.\n不过看到这么多哨兵,确实有些奇怪。这座要塞时刻戒备森严。我很好奇,是否曾有进攻者兵临城下?要想穿透她们的防御,似乎得是个疯子才行。"

    old "Then again, it could be the reason that no one ever tries to attack them is that they're so on guard. They avoid danger by not making themselves a target. And now that I think about it, the Amazons probably control quite a bit of wealth. At the very least, they probably have a lot of weapons that are worth stealing. Perhaps they're right to always be on their guard."
    new "Then again, it could be the reason that no one ever tries to attack them is that they're so on guard. They avoid danger by not making themselves a target. And now that I think about it, the Amazons probably control quite a bit of wealth. At the very least, they probably have a lot of weapons that are worth stealing. Perhaps they're right to always be on their guard.\n话又说回来,也许正因她们如此戒备,才从没人敢攻打她们。她们不让自己成为靶子,从而避开了危险。现在我细想,Amazon大概掌握着相当多的财富。至少,她们多半拥有大量值得一偷的武器。也许她们时刻保持警惕是对的。"

    old "I enter the citadel and head to Karen's chamber."
    new "I enter the citadel and head to Karen's chamber.\n我进入要塞,前往Karen的房间。"

    old "[protag], the returning hero."
    new "[protag], the returning hero.\n[protag],归来的英雄。"

    old "Hero, eh? I think I like that title."
    new "Hero, eh? I think I like that title.\n英雄,嗯?我想我喜欢这个头衔。"

    old "Among Amazons, a title is something that you have to keep earning. Officers can lose their standing if they don't maintain their skills. If you want to keep being called a hero, then keep doing heroic acts."
    new "Among Amazons, a title is something that you have to keep earning. Officers can lose their standing if they don't maintain their skills. If you want to keep being called a hero, then keep doing heroic acts.\n在Amazon之中,头衔是必须不断挣取的。军官若不保持技艺,就会失去地位。你若想继续被人称作英雄,那就继续行英雄之举。"

    old "Ah, so it's a title I need to keep living up to? Well, I hadn't planned on abandoning the people in their time of need, anyway."
    new "Ah, so it's a title I need to keep living up to? Well, I hadn't planned on abandoning the people in their time of need, anyway.\n啊,所以我得不断配得上这个头衔?嗯,反正我本就没打算在人们需要之时弃他们而去。"

    old "It's good to see that spirit in you."
    new "It's good to see that spirit in you.\n很高兴看到你身上有这股精神。"

    old "I'm not sure that I ought to be called a hero."
    new "I'm not sure that I ought to be called a hero.\n我不确定自己配不配被称作英雄。"

    old "Ah, humility. Yet another mark of a true hero."
    new "Ah, humility. Yet another mark of a true hero.\n啊,谦逊。真英雄的又一印记。"

    old "There were several other people that night with me who exhibited just as much courage, or whatever other merit you want to ascribe to me."
    new "There were several other people that night with me who exhibited just as much courage, or whatever other merit you want to ascribe to me.\n那晚还有其他几个人和我在一起,表现出了同样的勇气,或是你想加在我身上的任何其他优点。"

    old "Besides, the word 'hero' sounds like a title that I have to live up to. And many of my days are utterly mundane with nothing heroic at all going on."
    new "Besides, the word 'hero' sounds like a title that I have to live up to. And many of my days are utterly mundane with nothing heroic at all going on.\n再说,“英雄”这个词听起来像个我必须去配得上的头衔。而我的许多日子都平淡无奇,毫无英雄事迹可言。"

    old "Then we'll have to settle for referring to you as one of many individuals who's accomplished heroic deeds."
    new "Then we'll have to settle for referring to you as one of many individuals who's accomplished heroic deeds.\n那我们只好把你说成是众多成就英雄之举的人之一了。"

    old "Thank you for rescuing the amazons held prisoner in the dungeons of N'Mar."
    new "Thank you for rescuing the amazons held prisoner in the dungeons of N'Mar.\n感谢你救出了被囚禁在N'Mar地牢里的Amazon。"

    old "Karen seems to be in quite a good mood."
    new "Karen seems to be in quite a good mood.\nKaren似乎心情很好。"

    old "I wish this were just a social visit, but I bring news from the council."
    new "I wish this were just a social visit, but I bring news from the council.\n我倒希望这只是次社交拜访,但我带来了议会的消息。"

    old "And what would that news be?"
    new "And what would that news be?\n那是什么消息?"

    old "The council is expecting a vampire attack next month, on the night of the full moon."
    new "The council is expecting a vampire attack next month, on the night of the full moon.\n议会预计下个月满月之夜,会有吸血鬼来袭。"

    old "Yes, we had gathered as much from the Amazons who were taken prisoner at N'Mar."
    new "Yes, we had gathered as much from the Amazons who were taken prisoner at N'Mar.\n是的,我们从被俘于N'Mar的Amazon那里,也拼凑出了大致情况。"

    old "They're preparing to defend Grimoire against that attack."
    new "They're preparing to defend Grimoire against that attack.\n他们正准备保卫Grimoire,抵御那次袭击。"

    old "A reasonable course of action."
    new "A reasonable course of action.\n合理的应对。"

    old "I'm still working on the council's behalf. As a facilitator, of sorts."
    new "I'm still working on the council's behalf. As a facilitator, of sorts.\n我仍在为议会效力。算是某种协调人吧。"

    old "Given what you've accomplished so far, I don't think they could have picked anyone better for the job."
    new "Given what you've accomplished so far, I don't think they could have picked anyone better for the job.\n鉴于你迄今取得的成就,我想他们再也挑不出比你更合适的人选了。"

    old "Does this change our relationship?"
    new "Does this change our relationship?\n这会不会改变我们的关系?"

    old "That's an interesting question, [protag]. Do you think it does?"
    new "That's an interesting question, [protag]. Do you think it does?\n这是个有趣的问题,[protag]。你觉得会吗?"

    old "Well, I certainly don't expect our relationship to change. It is a working relationship, after all, but the nature of that work has changed. We have a different mission objective, and it's a mission objective that doesn't necessarily line up perfectly with the interests of the Amazons."
    new "Well, I certainly don't expect our relationship to change. It is a working relationship, after all, but the nature of that work has changed. We have a different mission objective, and it's a mission objective that doesn't necessarily line up perfectly with the interests of the Amazons.\n嗯,我当然不希望我们的关系改变。毕竟这是工作关系,但工作的性质已经变了。我们的任务目标不同了,而这个新目标,未必与Amazon的利益完全一致。"

    old "The Grimoire council fears an attack on the city walls, but the Amazon citadel isn't at target."
    new "The Grimoire council fears an attack on the city walls, but the Amazon citadel isn't at target.\nGrimoire议会担心城墙遭到攻击,但Amazon要塞并非目标。"

    old "I don't think that the nature of our relationship has changed, [protag]. When we first met, I was in the midst of bringing my concerns to Grimoire's council regarding the nature of the mists that were creeping over N'Mar. I wanted them to take it seriously."
    new "I don't think that the nature of our relationship has changed, [protag]. When we first met, I was in the midst of bringing my concerns to Grimoire's council regarding the nature of the mists that were creeping over N'Mar. I wanted them to take it seriously.\n我不认为我们关系的性质变了,[protag]。我们初次见面时,我正忙着向Grimoire议会陈情,关于笼罩N'Mar的迷雾的本质。我希望他们认真对待此事。"

    old "Now, they are taking it seriously. It would be remarkably stupid of me to back out now."
    new "Now, they are taking it seriously. It would be remarkably stupid of me to back out now.\n如今,他们认真对待了。此刻退缩,就太愚蠢了。"

    old "No, I don't think that things have changed. The mission is different. We were in fact-finding mode, and now Grimoire's leadership is preparing to defend against an attack. They're gearing up for war against the undead. But ultimately, our interests should still be aligned."
    new "No, I don't think that things have changed. The mission is different. We were in fact-finding mode, and now Grimoire's leadership is preparing to defend against an attack. They're gearing up for war against the undead. But ultimately, our interests should still be aligned.\n不,我不认为事情变了。任务不同了。我们原先处于查明真相的阶段,现在Grimoire的领袖们正准备抵御袭击。他们在为对抗亡灵备战。但归根结底,我们的利益应该仍是一致的。"

    old "I think so too, [protag]. Though some leaders might selfishly choose to ignore the peril of the human empire, a threat to the humans could just as easily turn into a threat against the Amazons."
    new "I think so too, [protag]. Though some leaders might selfishly choose to ignore the peril of the human empire, a threat to the humans could just as easily turn into a threat against the Amazons.\n我也这么想,[protag]。虽然有些领袖可能会自私地选择无视人类帝国的危难,但威胁到人类的,同样很容易变成威胁到Amazon。"

    old "The creeping mists around N'Mar are what caused me to become invested in this situation, and now that we've confirmed that there are in fact sinister deeds afoot in N'Mar, I don't intend to rest until we've stopped the problem at its source."
    new "The creeping mists around N'Mar are what caused me to become invested in this situation, and now that we've confirmed that there are in fact sinister deeds afoot in N'Mar, I don't intend to rest until we've stopped the problem at its source.\n正是N'Mar周围蔓延的迷雾,让我卷入这桩事。如今我们已确认N'Mar确实在酝酿邪恶的勾当,我打算在从根源上解决这个问题之前,绝不停歇。"

    old "That being said, the situation between the Amazons and the human empire remains politically complicated. I won't be sending regiments of my Amazon warriors to defend your city gates."
    new "That being said, the situation between the Amazons and the human empire remains politically complicated. I won't be sending regiments of my Amazon warriors to defend your city gates.\n话虽如此,Amazon与人类帝国之间的局势在政治上依然复杂。我不会派我的Amazon战士团去守卫你的城门。"

    old "Why is that?"
    new "Why is that?\n这是为什么?"

    old "Grimoire's leadership won't stand for any foreign power amassing military forces at their border. It might look like an Amazon invasion. They don't want to be stabbed in the back."
    new "Grimoire's leadership won't stand for any foreign power amassing military forces at their border. It might look like an Amazon invasion. They don't want to be stabbed in the back.\nGrimoire的领袖们不会容忍任何外国势力在他们边境集结军队。那看起来可能像一场Amazon入侵。他们不想被人从背后捅刀子。"

    old "And so they'd refuse help when the city needs it most?"
    new "And so they'd refuse help when the city needs it most?\n所以当城市最需要帮助时,他们反而会拒绝援手?"

    old "I know. It is deeply frustrating. However, despite the obstinate of Grimoire's leadership, we are looking into other ways to assist them. Providing supplies and the like."
    new "I know. It is deeply frustrating. However, despite the obstinate of Grimoire's leadership, we are looking into other ways to assist them. Providing supplies and the like.\n我知道,这实在令人沮丧。不过,尽管Grimoire的领袖们固执己见,我们仍在寻找其他方式协助他们,比如提供补给之类。"

    old "That's very generous of you."
    new "That's very generous of you.\n你真是慷慨。"

    old "Unfortunately, it won't amount to much. The Amazons are, pound for pound, stronger than any city in the human empire. But the sheer size of the human empire means that we could send them every weapon that we have and it still woundn't be enough for the battles they have to face."
    new "Unfortunately, it won't amount to much. The Amazons are, pound for pound, stronger than any city in the human empire. But the sheer size of the human empire means that we could send them every weapon that we have and it still woundn't be enough for the battles they have to face.\n可惜这起不了太大作用。Amazon论单兵战力,比人类帝国的任何城市都强。但人类帝国疆域辽阔,即便我们把拥有的每一件武器都送给他们,也不足以应付他们必须面对的战斗。"

    old "But even if we can only make a modest dent in their needs, it is at least something."
    new "But even if we can only make a modest dent in their needs, it is at least something.\n但即便只能在他们的需求上留下一点微小的印记,也聊胜于无。"

    old "Of course, I'll continue to provide whatever moral support I can directly to you, [protag]. I'll give you what words of advice I can, and of course you'll continue to have the direct support of Leena in battle."
    new "Of course, I'll continue to provide whatever moral support I can directly to you, [protag]. I'll give you what words of advice I can, and of course you'll continue to have the direct support of Leena in battle.\n当然,我会继续尽我所能,直接给你道义上的支持,[protag]。我会给你我所能给出的建议,当然,你在战斗中也会继续得到Leena的直接支援。"

    old "I hope you won't mind if you're excluded from most of my talks with Grimoire's leadership. Due to the need for political expediency, there simply isn't enough time to make sure that you're included in every conversation."
    new "I hope you won't mind if you're excluded from most of my talks with Grimoire's leadership. Due to the need for political expediency, there simply isn't enough time to make sure that you're included in every conversation.\n希望你不会介意,我大多数与Grimoire领袖们的会谈都不带上你。出于政治上的权宜,实在没有时间确保每场谈话都让你在场。"

    old "And I suspect that Grimoire's leadership also tries to keep the details away from lower-ranking members of their own organization."
    new "And I suspect that Grimoire's leadership also tries to keep the details away from lower-ranking members of their own organization.\n而且我怀疑,Grimoire的领袖们也在刻意对自家组织里级别较低的成员隐瞒细节。"

    old "Members like me."
    new "Members like me.\n就像我这样的成员。"

    old "Yes, even you, the emissary of Grimoire. Who knows, perhaps if you continue to serve them loyally and faithfully, you may one day be more than just an emissary. You might be the one giving orders instead of receiving them."
    new "Yes, even you, the emissary of Grimoire. Who knows, perhaps if you continue to serve them loyally and faithfully, you may one day be more than just an emissary. You might be the one giving orders instead of receiving them.\n对,连你这位Grimoire的特使也不例外。谁知道呢,也许只要你继续忠诚勤恳地为他们效力,有朝一日你会不止是特使。你也许会发号施令,而不是听命于人。"

    old "Then it sounds like you have something to aspire to. Just make sure that your aspirations don't distract you from your current mission."
    new "Then it sounds like you have something to aspire to. Just make sure that your aspirations don't distract you from your current mission.\n那听起来你倒是有了可以追求的目标。只是要确保你的抱负不会让你偏离眼下的任务。"

    old "You've already amassed quite a bit of influence. Just look at who you're talking to."
    new "You've already amassed quite a bit of influence. Just look at who you're talking to.\n你已经积累了不少影响力。看看你现在正和谁说话。"

    old "I'd hate that."
    new "I'd hate that.\n我会很讨厌那样。"

    old "Ha! Is that out of a distaste for the council specifically, or politics in general?"
    new "Ha! Is that out of a distaste for the council specifically, or politics in general?\n哈!这是因为你对议会本身反感,还是对政治总体上反感?"

    old "I just don't think I'd enjoy the life of sitting in council chambers, one voting member out of many, spending all of my time trying to persuade others of my viewpoint, or trying to stay informed about important issues in the empire. It sounds like a job that is somehow both demanding and boring at the same time."
    new "I just don't think I'd enjoy the life of sitting in council chambers, one voting member out of many, spending all of my time trying to persuade others of my viewpoint, or trying to stay informed about important issues in the empire. It sounds like a job that is somehow both demanding and boring at the same time.\n我只是不觉得我会喜欢那种坐在议会厅里的生活,在众多议员中做一个表决者,把所有时间都花在说服别人接受我的观点,或是努力跟进帝国的重要议题上。那听起来是一份既累人又无聊的工作。"

    old "The world is full of jobs like that, [protag]. But it seems you've managed one that avoids most of the boring parts."
    new "The world is full of jobs like that, [protag]. But it seems you've managed one that avoids most of the boring parts.\n世上这样的工作多了去了,[protag]。不过你似乎已经找到了一份能避开大部分无聊之处的工作。"

    old "Yes, I get to do all sorts of interesting things."
    new "Yes, I get to do all sorts of interesting things.\n是啊,我能做各种有趣的事。"

    old "I mean, here I am, conversing with the Amazon Queen. A year ago I don't think I would have imagined this life for myself, and yet, here I am."
    new "I mean, here I am, conversing with the Amazon Queen. A year ago I don't think I would have imagined this life for myself, and yet, here I am.\n我是说,此刻我正与Amazon女王交谈。一年前,我想我绝想象不到自己会过上这样的生活,然而我就在这里。"

    old "Sorry, I don't mean to distract us from business. I believe I've reported all of the essentials from Grimoire's meeting. Did you have anything you needed to convey to me?"
    new "Sorry, I don't mean to distract us from business. I believe I've reported all of the essentials from Grimoire's meeting. Did you have anything you needed to convey to me?\n抱歉,我不是有意把话题带偏。我想我已经汇报完Grimoire会议的所有要点。你还有什么需要向我转达的吗?"

    old "It sounds like you have your work cut out for you, [protag]. It seems like the people you've met and the bonds you've formed have allowed you to accomplish quite a lot in such a short time. I trust that you'll continue to cultivate those relationships."
    new "It sounds like you have your work cut out for you, [protag]. It seems like the people you've met and the bonds you've formed have allowed you to accomplish quite a lot in such a short time. I trust that you'll continue to cultivate those relationships.\n听起来你的工作够你忙的,[protag]。你认识的人、结下的情谊,似乎让你在这么短的时间里成就了不少。我相信你会继续经营好这些关系。"

    old "I certainly will."
    new "I certainly will.\n我当然会的。"

    old "Apart from that, I have two gifts to share with you."
    new "Apart from that, I have two gifts to share with you.\n除此之外,我有两份礼物要送给你。"

    old "What sort of gifts?"
    new "What sort of gifts?\n什么样的礼物?"

    old "The first is a spear. Not just a normal spear, but one wielded by our Great-Mothers."
    new "The first is a spear. Not just a normal spear, but one wielded by our Great-Mothers.\n第一份是一柄长矛。不是普通的长矛,而是我们Great-Mothers使用过的长矛。"

    old "Great-Mothers?"
    new "Great-Mothers?\nGreat-Mothers?"

    old "Past amazon queens. Of course this wasn't their personal weapon, but one they used during training. I'm sure you'll find it very useful in your quest."
    new "Past amazon queens. Of course this wasn't their personal weapon, but one they used during training. I'm sure you'll find it very useful in your quest.\n往昔的Amazon女王们。当然,这不是她们个人的武器,而是她们训练时用过的。我相信你在征途中会发现它非常有用。"

    old "Thank you, queen Karen. What is the other gift?"
    new "Thank you, queen Karen. What is the other gift?\n谢谢,Karen女王。另一份礼物是什么?"

    old "It's a tome of knowledge."
    new "It's a tome of knowledge.\n是一卷知识典籍。"

    old "Ah, that's quite the gift! I must admit, I didn't come here expecting you to be so generous. First this spear, and then the tome."
    new "Ah, that's quite the gift! I must admit, I didn't come here expecting you to be so generous. First this spear, and then the tome.\n啊,这可真是份大礼!我得承认,我来时没想到你会如此慷慨。先是这柄长矛,再是这卷典籍。"

    old "This tome has sat unused for a very, very long time, [protag]. I thought it might go a hundred years unused."
    new "This tome has sat unused for a very, very long time, [protag]. I thought it might go a hundred years unused.\n这卷典籍已经闲置了很久很久,[protag]。我原以为它也许会闲置上一百年。"

    old "Amazons are generally guarded in the way that we pass down knowledge. Often, an Amazon learns from years of training. It is a slow process."
    new "Amazons are generally guarded in the way that we pass down knowledge. Often, an Amazon learns from years of training. It is a slow process.\nAmazon在传承知识方面向来谨慎。通常,一名Amazon要从多年的训练中学习。这是个缓慢的过程。"

    old "Quite a bit different from how scholars and scribes pass on information, I imagine."
    new "Quite a bit different from how scholars and scribes pass on information, I imagine.\n我想,这和学者与文士传递信息的方式大不相同。"

    old "Our method of passing on what we've learned is quite different, yes."
    new "Our method of passing on what we've learned is quite different, yes.\n没错,我们传承所学的方式截然不同。"

    old "There's a reason that Amazons value discipline so highly. Power is something that comes with responsibility, and many choose to misuse it."
    new "There's a reason that Amazons value discipline so highly. Power is something that comes with responsibility, and many choose to misuse it.\nAmazon如此看重纪律,是有原因的。力量伴随着责任而来,而许多人却选择滥用它。"

    old "[protag], have you ever thought about why it is that so few muggers and thieves threaten their victims with fists? Nearly every time you have someone threatening your life demanding that you empty your pockets of coin, they are using a weapon, rather than their fists to threaten."
    new "[protag], have you ever thought about why it is that so few muggers and thieves threaten their victims with fists? Nearly every time you have someone threatening your life demanding that you empty your pockets of coin, they are using a weapon, rather than their fists to threaten.\n[protag],你有没有想过,为什么很少有劫匪和小偷会用拳头威胁受害者?几乎每次有人以性命相逼,要你掏空钱袋时,他们用的都是武器,而不是拳头。"

    old "Well, I imagine the threat is much greater when you have a weapon."
    new "Well, I imagine the threat is much greater when you have a weapon.\n嗯,我想有武器在手,威胁要大得多。"

    old "And yet there are many with the strength to kill using only their hands. I know many such warriors who could easily maim you beyond recognition using only their fists. Others have trained in martial arts for years to make their palms as deadly as any weapon."
    new "And yet there are many with the strength to kill using only their hands. I know many such warriors who could easily maim you beyond recognition using only their fists. Others have trained in martial arts for years to make their palms as deadly as any weapon.\n然而许多人单凭双手就有杀人的力气。我认识许多这样的战士,他们光用拳头就能轻而易举地把你揍得面目全非。还有些人习武多年,练就了一双与任何武器同样致命的手掌。"

    old "You're talking about the Disciples Of Truth on Mount Kronos?"
    new "You're talking about the Disciples Of Truth on Mount Kronos?\n你说的是Kronos山上的Disciples Of Truth?"

    old "Yes, that's a good example. But there are many more like them all around Aravorn."
    new "Yes, that's a good example. But there are many more like them all around Aravorn.\n对,这是个好例子。不过Aravorn各地还有许多像他们一样的人。"

    old "Why don't you suppose any of those people—the ones with hands strong enough to kill—make their money by threatening victims in alleyways?"
    new "Why don't you suppose any of those people—the ones with hands strong enough to kill—make their money by threatening victims in alleyways?\n那你觉得,为什么那些人——那些双手有力足以杀人的人——没有一个靠在小巷里威胁受害者赚钱呢?"

    old "Because they don't have that kind of malice in them."
    new "Because they don't have that kind of malice in them.\n因为他们心里没有那种恶意。"

    old "Yes. As paradoxical as it might seem, the people who are most personally skilled at the art of killing are often the least likely to misuse that power."
    new "Yes. As paradoxical as it might seem, the people who are most personally skilled at the art of killing are often the least likely to misuse that power.\n对。虽然听起来矛盾,但个人最精通杀戮之术的人,往往最不可能滥用那种力量。"

    old "Because they have better ways to make money."
    new "Because they have better ways to make money.\n因为他们有更好的赚钱门路。"

    old "Better ways to make money?"
    new "Better ways to make money?\n更好的赚钱门路?"

    old "If you have that kind of strength, you could be a mercenary and get paid more than you could make from mugging people."
    new "If you have that kind of strength, you could be a mercenary and get paid more than you could make from mugging people.\n有那种力气,你可以去当雇佣兵,赚得比抢劫路人还多。"

    old "I imagine they could make quite a lot of money by threatening or serving rich people."
    new "I imagine they could make quite a lot of money by threatening or serving rich people.\n我想他们靠威胁富人,或为富人效力,也能赚不少钱。"

    old "Well, I suppose."
    new "Well, I suppose.\n嗯,或许吧。"

    old "When you spend years of time training to become a strong fighter, it breeds in you a sort of discipline. The cowardly, those who might make their money by taking from the week, don't survive the years of training that it takes. One who has dedicated their life to study knows how to wield that power responsibly."
    new "When you spend years of time training to become a strong fighter, it breeds in you a sort of discipline. The cowardly, those who might make their money by taking from the week, don't survive the years of training that it takes. One who has dedicated their life to study knows how to wield that power responsibly.\n当你花上多年时间训练成为一名强大的战士,这会磨砺出某种纪律。那些懦弱之辈,那些想靠欺压弱者赚钱的人,熬不过那多年训练的苦。一个毕生致力于修习的人,懂得如何负责任地运用那种力量。"

    old "The dangerous ones are the ones who haven't earned their power. Any street ruffian can simply buy a life, and just like that, he has power over any victim that he can corner in a dark alleyway. There's a reason that they choose to prey on the weak."
    new "The dangerous ones are the ones who haven't earned their power. Any street ruffian can simply buy a life, and just like that, he has power over any victim that he can corner in a dark alleyway. There's a reason that they choose to prey on the weak.\n危险的是那些未曾赢得力量的人。任何街头无赖都能随手买条性命,于是乎,他对任何被他逼进暗巷角落的受害者便有了生杀之权。他们专挑弱者下手,是有原因的。"

    old "Hence, when it comes to items of importance, items like this tome of knowledge, I hesitate to give them out freely. I need to make sure to give them to someone who won't misuse that power."
    new "Hence, when it comes to items of importance, items like this tome of knowledge, I hesitate to give them out freely. I need to make sure to give them to someone who won't misuse that power.\n因此,对于重要之物,比如这卷知识典籍,我迟疑着不愿随意赠出。我得确保把它交给不会滥用那力量的人。"

    old "You want me to use this on myself?"
    new "You want me to use this on myself?\n你想让我把它用在自己身上?"

    old "No, but I trust you to give it to someone deserving. Someone who will really know what to do with that power."
    new "No, but I trust you to give it to someone deserving. Someone who will really know what to do with that power.\n不,但我相信你会把它交给值得的人。一个真正懂得如何运用那力量的人。"

    old "Of course, anyone who is of the moral inclination to dedicate themselves to a cause like fighting the vampires at N'Mar has probably demonstrated a certain amount of selflessness."
    new "Of course, anyone who is of the moral inclination to dedicate themselves to a cause like fighting the vampires at N'Mar has probably demonstrated a certain amount of selflessness.\n当然,任何在道义上倾向于投身如抗击N'Mar吸血鬼这般事业的人,大概都已展现出了一定程度的无私。"

    old "But when it comes to using that tome of knowledge, my personal recommendation would be to give it to someone who has already demonstrated their prowess as a fighter."
    new "But when it comes to using that tome of knowledge, my personal recommendation would be to give it to someone who has already demonstrated their prowess as a fighter.\n不过说到使用那卷知识典籍,我个人的建议是,把它交给一个已经展现出战士实力的人。"

    old "So allow the strong to become even stronger."
    new "So allow the strong to become even stronger.\n也就是让强者变得更强。"

    old "In a sense, yes. All of your allies are assisting you in your travels, [protag]. But I am sure that by now, you've found certain allies to be more helpful than others. It may be wise of you to consider who you are investing your time and resources in."
    new "In a sense, yes. All of your allies are assisting you in your travels, [protag]. But I am sure that by now, you've found certain allies to be more helpful than others. It may be wise of you to consider who you are investing your time and resources in.\n某种意义上,是的。你的所有盟友都在协助你的旅途,[protag]。但我相信,如今你已经发现,某些盟友比其他人更有帮助。明智的做法,或许是想想你在谁身上投入时间和资源。"

    old "Make sure that the people that you're taking the time to train and practice with are the ones who will be most important to helping your mission succeed."
    new "Make sure that the people that you're taking the time to train and practice with are the ones who will be most important to helping your mission succeed.\n务必确保你花时间一起训练、一起切磋的人,是对你任务的成功最重要的人。"

    old "That is my personal take on it, anyway. But knowing what I know about you, whatever choice you make will probably turn out to be the right one, just so long as you trust your instincts."
    new "That is my personal take on it, anyway. But knowing what I know about you, whatever choice you make will probably turn out to be the right one, just so long as you trust your instincts.\n总之这是我个人的看法。但以我对你的了解,无论你作何选择,大概都会是对的,只要你相信自己的直觉。"

    old "That's quite a compliment, Karen. I hope it turns out to be true."
    new "That's quite a compliment, Karen. I hope it turns out to be true.\n这评价可真高,Karen。但愿它成真。"

    old "I hope so too, [protag]. I hope so too."
    new "I hope so too, [protag]. I hope so too.\n我也希望如此,[protag]。我也希望如此。"

    old "Ah, before you leave, I think there's someone who would like to thank you."
    new "Ah, before you leave, I think there's someone who would like to thank you.\n啊,在你离开之前,我想有个人想向你道谢。"

    old "I turn around and look toward the door of Queen Karen's chambers. I think I recognize that girl..."
    new "I turn around and look toward the door of Queen Karen's chambers. I think I recognize that girl...\n我转过身,看向Karen女王房间的门。我想我认出了那个女孩……"

    old "Breza, you can come forward."
    new "Breza, you can come forward.\nBreza,你可以过来了。"

    old "The girl takes several steps forward. She moves cautiously, but there's no timidity in her; it almost seems like she's moving in defensive manner because she's not quite sure of how she should be acting around me."
    new "The girl takes several steps forward. She moves cautiously, but there's no timidity in her; it almost seems like she's moving in defensive manner because she's not quite sure of how she should be acting around me.\n那女孩向前走了几步。她动作谨慎,但身上没有怯意;她几乎像是在以防御的姿态移动,因为她不太确定在我面前该如何表现。"

    old "Hello, Breza."
    new "Hello, Breza.\n你好,Breza。"

    old "Hello."
    new "Hello.\n你好。"

    old "Thank you for coming to rescue us."
    new "Thank you for coming to rescue us.\n谢谢你来救我们。"

    old "It was my pleasure."
    new "It was my pleasure.\n这是我的荣幸。"

    old "Was it really, though?"
    new "Was it really, though?\n真的吗?"

    old "...I didn't expect such a young girl to challenge me on that."
    new "...I didn't expect such a young girl to challenge me on that.\n……我没想到这么年轻的女孩会这样质问我。"

    old "You risked your own safety to free us. Most people wouldn't do such a thing just for the pleasure of it."
    new "You risked your own safety to free us. Most people wouldn't do such a thing just for the pleasure of it.\n你冒着自身安危来解救我们。大多数人不会只为了乐意就做这种事。"

    old "There's a saying, 'virtue is its own reward.' Doing good for others is a gratifying thing, Breza. I think it's a responsibility of the strong to help the weak."
    new "There's a saying, 'virtue is its own reward.' Doing good for others is a gratifying thing, Breza. I think it's a responsibility of the strong to help the weak.\n有句谚语说,“美德本身就是回报”。为他人行善是件令人欣慰的事,Breza。我认为,强者有责任帮助弱者。"

    old "One day, I'll be strong enough that no one will need to come to my rescue."
    new "One day, I'll be strong enough that no one will need to come to my rescue.\n总有一天,我会变得足够强大,不再需要任何人来救我。"

    old "It was the right thing to do."
    new "It was the right thing to do.\n这么做是对的。"

    old "Breza nods."
    new "Breza nods.\nBreza点了点头。"

    old "I understand. Those in need must be protected. And I turned out to be the one in need."
    new "I understand. Those in need must be protected. And I turned out to be the one in need.\n我明白。身处困境的人必须受到保护。而结果,我成了那个身处困境的人。"

    old "I get the feeling that it won't always be that way, though."
    new "I get the feeling that it won't always be that way, though.\n不过我有种感觉,事情不会总是如此。"

    old "That's right. I'm going to become strong so that when trials come, I won't be the one asking for help."
    new "That's right. I'm going to become strong so that when trials come, I won't be the one asking for help.\n没错。我要变强,这样当考验来临时,我才不会成为那个开口求助的人。"

    old "I owed Queen Karen a favor. You're one of the subjects under her protection, aren't you? She deserves your thanks just as much as I do. If it hadn't been me saving you, it would have been someone else."
    new "I owed Queen Karen a favor. You're one of the subjects under her protection, aren't you? She deserves your thanks just as much as I do. If it hadn't been me saving you, it would have been someone else.\n我欠Karen女王一个人情。你是她庇护下的子民之一,不是吗?她和我一样,值得你的感谢。如果救你的不是我,也会是别人。"

    old "Do you serve directly under Queen Karen?"
    new "Do you serve directly under Queen Karen?\n你直接在Karen女王麾下效力吗?"

    old "Not exactly. I'm not an Amazon like you. But I do sometimes do things at her behest."
    new "Not exactly. I'm not an Amazon like you. But I do sometimes do things at her behest.\n不算。我不像你,不是Amazon。但我有时确实会按她的吩咐做事。"

    old "It's a great honor to serve the queen directly. I'm going to do the same thing too, one day."
    new "It's a great honor to serve the queen directly. I'm going to do the same thing too, one day.\n直接侍奉女王是莫大的荣耀。总有一天,我也要做同样的事。"

    old "I hope you're able to live up to that goal, Breza."
    new "I hope you're able to live up to that goal, Breza.\n我希望你能实现那个目标,Breza。"

    old "Breza looks like she's not quite sure how to respond, so she gives me a nod."
    new "Breza looks like she's not quite sure how to respond, so she gives me a nod.\nBreza看起来不太确定该如何回应,于是向我点了点头。"

    old "You're dismissed, Breza. It was good of you to come and give our visitor a proper thank you."
    new "You're dismissed, Breza. It was good of you to come and give our visitor a proper thank you.\n你可以退下了,Breza。你能来向我们的客人好好道谢,这很好。"

    old "She's quite determined and ambitious for someone so young."
    new "She's quite determined and ambitious for someone so young.\n对这么年轻的人来说,她相当有决心、有抱负。"

    old "She is, isn't she? Despite what an ordeal all of this has been, there's something in that girl that makes me think she's special."
    new "She is, isn't she? Despite what an ordeal all of this has been, there's something in that girl that makes me think she's special.\n可不是吗?尽管这一切磨难重重,但那女孩身上有种东西,让我觉得她很特别。"

    old "She seems to be brimming with potential. She has a lot to learn, but she's young. She has time to learn it."
    new "She seems to be brimming with potential. She has a lot to learn, but she's young. She has time to learn it.\n她似乎浑身充满潜力。她有很多要学的,但她还年轻,有足够的时间去学。"

    old "It's a bit surprising, to see that attitude after her experience at the castle. It must have been quite traumatic."
    new "It's a bit surprising, to see that attitude after her experience at the castle. It must have been quite traumatic.\n经历过城堡里那件事之后,还能有这样的态度,实在有些出人意料。那一定给她留下了很大的创伤。"

    old "Indeed. But I think it may ultimately be to her benefit. While I wouldn't wish harm upon someone so young, I do believe that encountering hardship at such an early age will give her the determination to be stronger. If anything, the fact that she's survived it seems to have given her a notion that she's made of stronger stuff. It'll be interesting to see."
    new "Indeed. But I think it may ultimately be to her benefit. While I wouldn't wish harm upon someone so young, I do believe that encountering hardship at such an early age will give her the determination to be stronger. If anything, the fact that she's survived it seems to have given her a notion that she's made of stronger stuff. It'll be interesting to see.\n确实。但我想这最终或许对她有益。虽然我不愿看到这么年轻的人受苦,但我确实相信,在如此幼小的年纪历经磨难,会给予她变强的决心。可以说,她能挺过来这一点,似乎让她意识到自己是由更坚韧的材料铸成的。这将很有趣。"

    old "Do you usually take such an interest in the younger members of the citadel? I imagine there must be more children than just Breza."
    new "Do you usually take such an interest in the younger members of the citadel? I imagine there must be more children than just Breza.\n你一向对要塞里的年轻成员这么上心吗?我想这里肯定不止Breza一个孩子。"

    old "I must admit that I initially took interest in Breza simply through my own daughter."
    new "I must admit that I initially took interest in Breza simply through my own daughter.\n我得承认,我最初关注Breza,仅仅是因为我自己的女儿。"

    old "Princess Loren is friends with Breza?"
    new "Princess Loren is friends with Breza?\nLoren公主和Breza是朋友?"

    old "Yes. Loren and Breza are somewhat similarly matched in terms of their physical abilities, given that they're of similar ages, which makes them good sparring partners. I think Loren appreciates having someone her own height to practice against. And Breza seems to have taken a keen liking to Loren."
    new "Yes. Loren and Breza are somewhat similarly matched in terms of their physical abilities, given that they're of similar ages, which makes them good sparring partners. I think Loren appreciates having someone her own height to practice against. And Breza seems to have taken a keen liking to Loren.\n是的。Loren和Breza年纪相仿,体能也大致相当,这让她们成了很好的对练伙伴。我想Loren很乐意有个和自己身高相仿的人陪练。而Breza似乎对Loren也格外喜欢。"

    old "That being said, even were it not for my own daughter, I think it's important to ensure that children are learning to be all that they can be. One of my responsibilities as queen is to ensure the wellfare of the Amazons, not just in the immediate future, but a generation or more from now."
    new "That being said, even were it not for my own daughter, I think it's important to ensure that children are learning to be all that they can be. One of my responsibilities as queen is to ensure the wellfare of the Amazons, not just in the immediate future, but a generation or more from now.\n话虽如此,即便不是为了我自己的女儿,我也认为,确保孩子们成长为她们所能成为的一切,十分重要。作为女王,我的职责之一就是保障Amazon的福祉,不只是眼下,更是一代乃至更久之后。"

    old "Fifty years from now, I and the warriors that serve directly under me will not be what keeps the citadel safe. Whether the Amazons persevere will depend entirely on the generation that follows us. Girls like Breza, and my own daughter Loren—they will one day be responsible for this citadel. I try to always remain cognizant of that."
    new "Fifty years from now, I and the warriors that serve directly under me will not be what keeps the citadel safe. Whether the Amazons persevere will depend entirely on the generation that follows us. Girls like Breza, and my own daughter Loren—they will one day be responsible for this citadel. I try to always remain cognizant of that.\n五十年后,我和直接效命于我的战士们,将不再是这座要塞的守护者。Amazon能否长存,完全取决于我们之后的下一代。像Breza这样的女孩,还有我的女儿Loren——她们总有一天要为这座要塞负责。我努力时刻牢记这一点。"

    old "But enough about my daughter. I know you're a busy person, and I've already taken enough of your time. Let me know if I can be of service to you. But I think you already know what to do."
    new "But enough about my daughter. I know you're a busy person, and I've already taken enough of your time. Let me know if I can be of service to you. But I think you already know what to do.\n关于我女儿就说这些吧。我知道你很忙,我已经占用你不少时间了。如果有什么我能效劳的,请告诉我。不过我想,你已经知道自己该怎么做了。"

    old "I roll over in my bed, unable to sleep."
    new "I roll over in my bed, unable to sleep.\n我在床上翻了个身,睡不着。"

    old "Even if in public I try to appear to be a strong, decisive person, it's no secret that I have a lot of responsibility on my shoulders."
    new "Even if in public I try to appear to be a strong, decisive person, it's no secret that I have a lot of responsibility on my shoulders.\n即便我在人前努力表现得坚强果决,但我肩上担着许多责任,这已不是什么秘密。"

    old "The future of a whole city, Grimoire, and possibly this whole region... It's in my hands."
    new "The future of a whole city, Grimoire, and possibly this whole region... It's in my hands.\n整座城市Grimoire的未来,或许还有这整个地区的未来……都握在我手中。"

    old "Luckily, I am not alone in this. My team, the wise Apolimesho, and Karen..."
    new "Luckily, I am not alone in this. My team, the wise Apolimesho, and Karen...\n幸好,我并非孤身一人。我的团队、睿智的Apolimesho,还有Karen……"

    old "[protag], finally you have come!"
    new "[protag], finally you have come!\n[protag],你终于来了!"

    old "My queen? I... what I am supposed to do here?"
    new "My queen? I... what I am supposed to do here?\n我的女王?我……我该在这里做什么?"

    old "We need to defeat the evil that lurks in N'Mar! Have you forgotten?"
    new "We need to defeat the evil that lurks in N'Mar! Have you forgotten?\n我们必须打败潜伏在N'Mar的邪恶!你忘了吗?"

    old "No I haven't, but... why I am here, alone with you?"
    new "No I haven't, but... why I am here, alone with you?\n不,我没有,可是……为什么我会在这里,和你独处?"

    old "You know why."
    new "You know why.\n你知道为什么。"

    old "Karen moves in close. Before I can process what's happening, her lips are on mine."
    new "Karen moves in close. Before I can process what's happening, her lips are on mine.\nKaren凑上前来。我还没反应过来发生了什么,她的唇已经贴上了我的唇。"

    old "Hmpf-"
    new "Hmpf-\n唔——"

    old "Karen leans into the kiss for a brief moment and then pulls away, leaving me in a stunned stupor."
    new "Karen leans into the kiss for a brief moment and then pulls away, leaving me in a stunned stupor.\nKaren短暂地投入这个吻,随后便抽身离开,留我怔怔地愣在原地。"

    old "From there, Karen confidently strides over to the side of a fierce griffon."
    new "From there, Karen confidently strides over to the side of a fierce griffon.\n接着,Karen信心十足地大步走到一头凶猛的狮鹫身旁。"

    old "It beats its wings powerfully, indicating its readiness to take flight."
    new "It beats its wings powerfully, indicating its readiness to take flight.\n它有力地拍打着翅膀,表明自己已准备好起飞。"

    old "In case we won't meet again, I wanted you to remember me."
    new "In case we won't meet again, I wanted you to remember me.\n万一我们再也不能相见,我希望你能记得我。"

    old "Where are you going?"
    new "Where are you going?\n你要去哪里?"

    old "I'm flying to N'Mar with my amazon army. We're in this together, [protag]."
    new "I'm flying to N'Mar with my amazon army. We're in this together, [protag].\n我要带着我的Amazon大军飞往N'Mar。我们是一起的,[protag]。"

    old "Strangely enough, Karen is completely naked. I'm not sure how I didn't notice before..."
    new "Strangely enough, Karen is completely naked. I'm not sure how I didn't notice before...\n说来奇怪,Karen竟然全身赤裸。我不知道自己之前怎么没注意到……"

    old "I'm certainly noticing now."
    new "I'm certainly noticing now.\n现在我当然注意到了。"

    old "For an older woman- I immediately put a halt to that thought. It's definitely not the sort of thing I should be thinking about before an important battle."
    new "For an older woman- I immediately put a halt to that thought. It's definitely not the sort of thing I should be thinking about before an important battle.\n对一个上了年纪的女人——我立刻打住了这个念头。这绝不该是一场重要战斗之前该想的事。"

    old "I should try to be as oblivious about it as she seems to be."
    new "I should try to be as oblivious about it as she seems to be.\n我该尽量像她那样,对此毫不在意。"

    old "I can't help but admire Karen as she mounts her griffon, spear in hand."
    new "I can't help but admire Karen as she mounts her griffon, spear in hand.\n看着Karen手持长矛跨上狮鹫,我忍不住心生钦佩。"

    old "Everything about her radiates power."
    new "Everything about her radiates power.\n她的一切都散发着力量。"

    old "She's ready to fight and, as I bask in her glory, I feel my own morale soar. She is truly a Queen worthy of the title."
    new "She's ready to fight and, as I bask in her glory, I feel my own morale soar. She is truly a Queen worthy of the title.\n她已准备好战斗,而我沐浴在她的荣光中,感到自己的士气也随之高涨。她真是一位名副其实的女王。"

    old "Farewell, my love."
    new "Farewell, my love.\n再会了,我的爱人。"

    old "I wake up in a sweat."
    new "I wake up in a sweat.\n我浑身是汗地惊醒过来。"

    old "What a strange dream; Not unpleasant by any means, but... it'd probably be best if I didn't mention it to [chosen_romance]."
    new "What a strange dream; Not unpleasant by any means, but... it'd probably be best if I didn't mention it to [chosen_romance].\n多么奇怪的梦;绝非不愉快,只是……最好还是别向[chosen_romance]提起。"

    old "Get those ideas out of your head, [protag]. Karen is an amazon. They like women."
    new "Get those ideas out of your head, [protag]. Karen is an amazon. They like women.\n把那些念头赶出你的脑袋,[protag]。Karen是Amazon。她们喜欢女人。"

    old "Get those ideas out of your head, [protag]. Karen is the amazon queen! She has no time for you. You're an outsider too. There's no chance."
    new "Get those ideas out of your head, [protag]. Karen is the amazon queen! She has no time for you. You're an outsider too. There's no chance.\n把那些念头赶出你的脑袋,[protag]。Karen是Amazon女王!她没有时间理你。你也不过是个外人。没戏的。"

    old "I decide to get back to sleep, but not before taking a hot bath to relax myself."
    new "I decide to get back to sleep, but not before taking a hot bath to relax myself.\n我决定回去睡觉,但先洗个热水澡放松一下。"

    old "[protag]. How may I be of service? Do you happen to need anyone killed? Don't hesitate to let me know if you do. Killing is my specialty, after all. I try to be humble, but it's hard to be honest about my talent as a killer without boasting."
    new "[protag]. How may I be of service? Do you happen to need anyone killed? Don't hesitate to let me know if you do. Killing is my specialty, after all. I try to be humble, but it's hard to be honest about my talent as a killer without boasting.\n[protag]。有什么我可以效劳的吗?你碰巧需要杀什么人吗?若是有,请尽管告诉我。毕竟,杀人是我最拿手的。我尽量保持谦逊,但要老老实实谈我杀人的天赋而不显自夸,实在很难。"

    old "You may be an assassin, Kusho, but you're hardly the only fighter I know who's ever killed someone. I'm building a small army. You think a soldier doesn't know how to kill?"
    new "You may be an assassin, Kusho, but you're hardly the only fighter I know who's ever killed someone. I'm building a small army. You think a soldier doesn't know how to kill?\n你也许是个刺客,Kusho,但你远不是我认识的唯一杀过人的人。我在组建一支小军队。你以为士兵就不懂得杀人吗?"

    old "In fact, a trained footsoldier probably has a lot more experience with killing than an assassin does. A soldier on the battlefield could face many foes. Most of what you do is hiding, stalking, and then killing a single target."
    new "In fact, a trained footsoldier probably has a lot more experience with killing than an assassin does. A soldier on the battlefield could face many foes. Most of what you do is hiding, stalking, and then killing a single target.\n事实上,一名训练有素的步兵,杀人的经验大概比刺客还多得多。战场上的士兵要面对众多敌人。而你做的多半是躲藏、跟踪,然后杀掉一个目标。"

    old "In a manner of speaking, your reasoning is logical. It is also wrong."
    new "In a manner of speaking, your reasoning is logical. It is also wrong.\n从某种意义上说,你的推理合乎逻辑。但它也是错的。"

    old "I suppose you imagine a soldier charging into battle, sword drawn, and slaying dozens of enemies. Clearly, a soldier is better cut out for killing than someone like me, who may kill in the span of a year the same number of people that a soldier kills in a single day."
    new "I suppose you imagine a soldier charging into battle, sword drawn, and slaying dozens of enemies. Clearly, a soldier is better cut out for killing than someone like me, who may kill in the span of a year the same number of people that a soldier kills in a single day.\n我想象得到,你脑中浮现的是一名士兵拔剑冲入战阵、斩杀数十敌人的画面。显然,士兵比我这种人更擅长杀人——我一年里杀的人,可能只顶得上士兵一天杀的量。"

    old "After all, to an assassin, what matters is the quality of killing, not the quantity. In fact, one of the marks of a good assassin is that he doesn't cause unnecessary casualties. They are sometimes unavoidable, but in an ideal world, only the designated target dies."
    new "After all, to an assassin, what matters is the quality of killing, not the quantity. In fact, one of the marks of a good assassin is that he doesn't cause unnecessary casualties. They are sometimes unavoidable, but in an ideal world, only the designated target dies.\n毕竟,对刺客而言,重要的是杀人的质量,而非数量。事实上,好刺客的标志之一,就是不会造成不必要的伤亡。伤亡有时不可避免,但在理想情形下,死去的只有指定目标。"

    old "Here's something you need to realize, [protag]. Real soldiers do very little in the way of actual killing."
    new "Here's something you need to realize, [protag]. Real soldiers do very little in the way of actual killing.\n有件事你得明白,[protag]。真正的士兵,在实际杀戮上做得很少。"

    old "You may have this mental image of battlefield casualties being this glorious thing. A soldier decapitates a foe here, slits a throat there, and then turns around and kills another enemy with a well-placed stab to the gut. All very heroic and bloody."
    new "You may have this mental image of battlefield casualties being this glorious thing. A soldier decapitates a foe here, slits a throat there, and then turns around and kills another enemy with a well-placed stab to the gut. All very heroic and bloody.\n你脑中也许有战场伤亡颇为壮烈的画面。士兵在此处斩首敌人,在彼处割开喉咙,然后转身用一记精准的刺击捅进另一个敌人的肚子。既英勇又血腥。"

    old "The reality is, most soldiers who die from combat aren't slain in this matter. Most of them suffer one cut too many, and are left to bleed out over the course of many painful minutes or hours. By the time they finally take their last breath, the man who dealt them the last blow may be long gone."
    new "The reality is, most soldiers who die from combat aren't slain in this matter. Most of them suffer one cut too many, and are left to bleed out over the course of many painful minutes or hours. By the time they finally take their last breath, the man who dealt them the last blow may be long gone.\n现实是,大多数死于战斗的士兵并非这样被杀的。他们中大多数人是多挨了几刀,然后在漫长而痛苦的几分钟或几小时里慢慢流血而亡。等他们终于咽下最后一口气时,那个给了他们最后一击的人,可能早已离去。"

    old "Many soldiers don't even die on the battlefield. They're carried off the battlefield by their comrades, and then later succumb to their wounds. Sometimes, it's something as simple and inglorious as an infection that takes their life."
    new "Many soldiers don't even die on the battlefield. They're carried off the battlefield by their comrades, and then later succumb to their wounds. Sometimes, it's something as simple and inglorious as an infection that takes their life.\n许多士兵甚至不是死在战场上。他们被战友抬下战场,之后才伤重不治。有时,夺走他们性命的,是感染这类既简单又不光彩的事。"

    old "Many soldiers, even competent soldiers who have taken many lives, don't have much experience in the way of killing in the same way I have. It's one thing to stab a man and then ride off on your horse as he bleeds out."
    new "Many soldiers, even competent soldiers who have taken many lives, don't have much experience in the way of killing in the same way I have. It's one thing to stab a man and then ride off on your horse as he bleeds out.\n许多士兵,即便是身经百战、夺走过许多性命的精兵,在杀人这件事上的亲身体验,也不如我这般深刻。捅一个人一刀,然后趁他流血时策马离去,是一回事。"

    old "It's quite another to slice a man's throat with one hand while you cover his mouth with the other, holding his struggling body in your arms until finally he can struggle no more."
    new "It's quite another to slice a man's throat with one hand while you cover his mouth with the other, holding his struggling body in your arms until finally he can struggle no more.\n用一只手割开一个人的喉咙,同时用另一只手捂住他的嘴,把他挣扎的身体抱在怀里,直到他终于再也挣扎不动——那完全是另一回事。"

    old "I'm sure that you, or many of your other companions, have at one time or another been directly responsible for the death of another person. I don't question those credentials."
    new "I'm sure that you, or many of your other companions, have at one time or another been directly responsible for the death of another person. I don't question those credentials.\n我相信,你或你的许多同伴,都曾在某个时刻对另一个人的死亡负有直接责任。我并不质疑这些资历。"

    old "What I'm asking you is this: are you really prepared to kill a man? If all you had were your bare hands, could you find it in yourself to place your hands around his throat and squeeze until you'd crushed the life out of him?"
    new "What I'm asking you is this: are you really prepared to kill a man? If all you had were your bare hands, could you find it in yourself to place your hands around his throat and squeeze until you'd crushed the life out of him?\n我要问你的,是这个:你真的准备好杀一个人了吗?如果你赤手空拳,你能下得了决心,把双手掐上他的喉咙,一直勒到他断气吗?"

    old "You 'think so?'"
    new "You 'think so?'\n你“觉得可以?”"

    old "Well, it's hard to predict future behavior. If it ever came to that, my hands around someone's throat, how would I act? I'd be lying if I said I knew for certain. But I've been around these lands, and seen quite a bit. I think I'd be up to the task."
    new "Well, it's hard to predict future behavior. If it ever came to that, my hands around someone's throat, how would I act? I'd be lying if I said I knew for certain. But I've been around these lands, and seen quite a bit. I think I'd be up to the task.\n嗯,未来的行为很难预测。若真到了那一步,我的双手掐在某人的喉咙上,我会怎么做?如果说我确知答案,那就是在说谎。但我走南闯北,见识了不少。我想我能胜任。"

    old "I've got a chance for you to prove it, if you'd like to help me with a job."
    new "I've got a chance for you to prove it, if you'd like to help me with a job.\n如果你愿意帮我办件事,我倒有个机会让你证明自己。"

    old "I don't think I could, Kusho. Killing with a blade is one thing. Literally squeezing the life out of someone is quite another."
    new "I don't think I could, Kusho. Killing with a blade is one thing. Literally squeezing the life out of someone is quite another.\n我想我做不到,Kusho。用刀杀人是一回事。真真切切地扼杀一个人的生命,完全是另一回事。"

    old "Besides, when it comes to any task, I'm going to want the tool that's best suited to the job. And my hands seem poorly suited to killing."
    new "Besides, when it comes to any task, I'm going to want the tool that's best suited to the job. And my hands seem poorly suited to killing.\n再说,无论什么任务,我都想要最适合它的工具。而我这双手,似乎不太适合杀人。"

    old "Well, you'll never know unless you try. How'd you like to try your own hand at things? Accompany me on an assassination? You might learn a thing or two about yourself."
    new "Well, you'll never know unless you try. How'd you like to try your own hand at things? Accompany me on an assassination? You might learn a thing or two about yourself.\n嗯,不试试永远不知道。你想不想亲自动手试试?陪我走一趟暗杀?你也许能更了解自己。"

    old "The answer to your question is 'yes.'"
    new "The answer to your question is 'yes.'\n你那个问题的答案是“能”。"

    old "And you know this how?"
    new "And you know this how?\n你又怎么知道?"

    old "Through experience, of course."
    new "Through experience, of course.\n当然是通过经验。"

    old "Really. You killed a man with your bare hands? Now that's a story I'd like to hear."
    new "Really. You killed a man with your bare hands? Now that's a story I'd like to hear.\n真的?你徒手杀过人?这故事我倒想听听。"

    old "Stay with me long enough and you might hear that story some day."
    new "Stay with me long enough and you might hear that story some day.\n跟我待得够久,有一天你也许会听到那个故事。"

    old "Is that a promise?"
    new "Is that a promise?\n这算承诺吗?"

    old "Sure. But I never said how long."
    new "Sure. But I never said how long.\n当然。但我可从没说过要等多久。"

    old "A grin flashes across Kusho's face and he begins cackling."
    new "A grin flashes across Kusho's face and he begins cackling.\nKusho脸上闪过一丝笑容,接着咯咯笑了起来。"

    old "Sly, sly. Well, I'm not sure how long we'll be together. I've never been one to maintain lasting relationships for too long. After all, you never know when a former client might become your next target."
    new "Sly, sly. Well, I'm not sure how long we'll be together. I've never been one to maintain lasting relationships for too long. After all, you never know when a former client might become your next target.\n狡猾,真狡猾。不过,我不知道我们还会在一起多久。我从来就不是个能维持长久关系的人。毕竟,你永远不知道哪个老主顾,有朝一日会变成你的下一个目标。"

    old "Is that a threat?"
    new "Is that a threat?\n这是在威胁我吗?"

    old "My, growing paranoid, are we? I don't see any reason someone would hire an assassin to take you out. After all, you mentioned that your foes are undead. Zombies, vampires, and ghouls generally don't strike me as the type who would hire an elf assassin."
    new "My, growing paranoid, are we? I don't see any reason someone would hire an assassin to take you out. After all, you mentioned that your foes are undead. Zombies, vampires, and ghouls generally don't strike me as the type who would hire an elf assassin.\n哟,疑心病见长啊?我看不出有什么理由会有人雇刺客来取你性命。毕竟你自己说过,你的敌人是亡灵。僵尸、吸血鬼和食尸鬼,在我印象里可不是会雇精灵刺客的那种主。"

    old "But you're more than just a client, [protag]. You didn't pay for my services with cash. I owe you a favor for what you did about Vaeril."
    new "But you're more than just a client, [protag]. You didn't pay for my services with cash. I owe you a favor for what you did about Vaeril.\n但你不只是客户,[protag]。你没有用现金支付我的服务。为了Vaeril那件事,我欠你一个人情。"

    old "So. You have what it takes to be a killer, do you? How about putting those skills to use once again? Care to assist me with an assassination?"
    new "So. You have what it takes to be a killer, do you? How about putting those skills to use once again? Care to assist me with an assassination?\n那么,你确实有当杀手的料,是吧?何不再把这些本事派上用场一次?愿不愿意协助我完成一次暗杀?"

    old "What kind of job are you talking about?"
    new "What kind of job are you talking about?\n你说的是什么活儿?"

    old "If you're asking me to lay out the hit for you, then I assume you're ready to swear to silence. Not that I ever take anyone at their word, but even the most dishonest of folks tend to do a good job of keeping their oath when it's sworn to an assassin."
    new "If you're asking me to lay out the hit for you, then I assume you're ready to swear to silence. Not that I ever take anyone at their word, but even the most dishonest of folks tend to do a good job of keeping their oath when it's sworn to an assassin.\n如果你要我为你道出这次刺杀的内情,那我便假定你已准备好发誓守密。倒不是说我轻信任何人的口头承诺,但即便是最不老实的人,向一个刺客发誓时,通常也会把誓言守得不错。"

    old "Making promises to an assassin and then breaking them can lead to...well, let's not go there, I think you know well enough already."
    new "Making promises to an assassin and then breaking them can lead to...well, let's not go there, I think you know well enough already.\n对刺客许下承诺然后又背弃,会导致……算了,我们别往那处想,我想你已经很清楚了。"

    old "So, do you really want to hear about this hit? I'm not asking for your cooperation, just your silence."
    new "So, do you really want to hear about this hit? I'm not asking for your cooperation, just your silence.\n那么,你真的想听听这次刺杀的内情吗?我不求你的合作,只求你的沉默。"

    old "I can't make that kind of promise, Kusho. If you don't want me repeating what you say, you should just not tell me in the first place."
    new "I can't make that kind of promise, Kusho. If you don't want me repeating what you say, you should just not tell me in the first place.\n我无法作那样的承诺,Kusho。若你不想让我复述你的话,那一开始就不该告诉我。"

    old "That's not the response I expected. But I can respect that. You don't want to get involved with a hit. Well, I can't very well ask for your help if you're not even willing to hear what I have to say, so I guess that means we're done here."
    new "That's not the response I expected. But I can respect that. You don't want to get involved with a hit. Well, I can't very well ask for your help if you're not even willing to hear what I have to say, so I guess that means we're done here.\n这倒不是我预期的回应。但我敬重这一点。你不想卷入一次刺杀。嗯,如果你连听都不愿听,我自然无法请你帮忙,那么我想,我们就到此为止吧。"

    old "Done?"
    new "Done?\n到此为止?"

    old "I mean that my time is valuable, and you've taken up quite enough of it for today. If you're not helping me, then you're hindering me. That's a rule I have for everyone, so I hope you don't take it personally."
    new "I mean that my time is valuable, and you've taken up quite enough of it for today. If you're not helping me, then you're hindering me. That's a rule I have for everyone, so I hope you don't take it personally.\n我是说,我的时间很宝贵,而今天你已经占用得够多了。你不帮我,就是在碍我的事。这是我对每个人一视同仁的规矩,希望你别往心里去。"

    old "Of course not."
    new "Of course not.\n当然不会。"

    old "You can feel free to come bother me some other time. I am in your debt for your assistance with Vaeril, after all. But today, I have things to do. Farewell."
    new "You can feel free to come bother me some other time. I am in your debt for your assistance with Vaeril, after all. But today, I have things to do. Farewell.\n改天你尽管来烦我。毕竟,Vaeril那件事上我欠你人情。但今天,我还有事要做。再会。"

    old "Kusho leaps into the air, grabbing hold of a low-hanging branch, and hoists himself onto it. Within seconds, he's ascended into the canopy, scurrying away faster than my eyes can follow."
    new "Kusho leaps into the air, grabbing hold of a low-hanging branch, and hoists himself onto it. Within seconds, he's ascended into the canopy, scurrying away faster than my eyes can follow.\nKusho纵身跃起,抓住一根低垂的树枝,把自己荡了上去。几秒之内,他已没入树冠,逃窜之快,连我的眼睛都跟不上。"

    old "I swear, Kusho. I swear on my life."
    new "I swear, Kusho. I swear on my life.\n我发誓,Kusho。我以我的性命发誓。"

    old "Swearing on your life seems a little redundant, but okay."
    new "Swearing on your life seems a little redundant, but okay.\n以性命发誓似乎有点多余,不过行吧。"

    old "So, let me start by giving you the lowdown on this man. The target, I mean. He's an elf."
    new "So, let me start by giving you the lowdown on this man. The target, I mean. He's an elf.\n那么,我先给你讲讲这个人的底细。我是说,目标。他是个精灵。"

    old "Working close to home?"
    new "Working close to home?\n在离家这么近的地方动手?"

    old "Actually, no. He's an elf noble from Triberg."
    new "Actually, no. He's an elf noble from Triberg.\n其实不是。他是Triberg的一位精灵贵族。"

    old "The lord of house Nox. Clement is his name."
    new "The lord of house Nox. Clement is his name.\nNox家族的家主。他叫Clement。"

    old "The name Nox is familiar, but I can't for the life of me recall what business they're in."
    new "The name Nox is familiar, but I can't for the life of me recall what business they're in.\nNox这个名字很耳熟,但我怎么也想不起他们是做什么生意的。"

    old "House Nox is in the business of being rich. They're what you might call 'old money.' Clement Nox is rich because his father is rich. And Clement's father was rich because {i}his{/i} father was rich."
    new "House Nox is in the business of being rich. They're what you might call 'old money.' Clement Nox is rich because his father is rich. And Clement's father was rich because {i}his{/i} father was rich.\nNox家族做的,是有钱的生意。他们就是人们所说的“老钱”。Clement Nox富有,是因为他父亲富有。而Clement的父亲富有,是因为{i}他{/i}的父亲富有。"

    old "And so on and so forth. Nox is a very old family, dating back to the founding days of Triberg. At one point they controlled more than one fifth of the property in the city."
    new "And so on and so forth. Nox is a very old family, dating back to the founding days of Triberg. At one point they controlled more than one fifth of the property in the city.\n如此代代相传。Nox是个非常古老的家族,可追溯到Triberg建城之初。他们一度掌控了城中五分之一以上的地产。"

    old "They have no new income, apart from lending money, which they're actually quite bad at. They tend to give out high-interest loans to people who have neither the intention nor the means to pay it back."
    new "They have no new income, apart from lending money, which they're actually quite bad at. They tend to give out high-interest loans to people who have neither the intention nor the means to pay it back.\n除了放贷,他们没有任何新进项,而放贷他们其实还很不在行。他们总爱把高利贷借给那些既无意也无力偿还的人。"

    old "Not much money to be made in lending to such people, I imagine, though I suppose we should all be thanking Nox for helping to fuel the bustling Triberg economy."
    new "Not much money to be made in lending to such people, I imagine, though I suppose we should all be thanking Nox for helping to fuel the bustling Triberg economy.\n我想,借钱给这种人赚不到什么钱,不过我想我们都该感谢Nox,为繁荣的Triberg经济添了把火。"

    old "So they're in a bad place financially?"
    new "So they're in a bad place financially?\n这么说他们财政吃紧了?"

    old "Ha! Of course not. [protag], you must realize that when you have a large mountain, and stone cutters carve away at that mountain year after year, at the end of a century or two, you still have a very large mountain."
    new "Ha! Of course not. [protag], you must realize that when you have a large mountain, and stone cutters carve away at that mountain year after year, at the end of a century or two, you still have a very large mountain.\n哈!当然不是。[protag],你得明白,当你拥有一座大山,而采石人年复一年地凿那座山,过了一两个世纪,你依然拥有一座非常大的山。"

    old "Nox could continue to bleed money at its current rate and that family's descendants would continue to be wealthy for a dozen or so generations. That's the nature of old money."
    new "Nox could continue to bleed money at its current rate and that family's descendants would continue to be wealthy for a dozen or so generations. That's the nature of old money.\n即便Nox按现在的速度继续失血,那家族的后人也还能富上十几代。这就是老钱的本质。"

    old "In fact, many suspect that Clement makes bad loans deliberately. You see, the few defaulting debtors who are caught are bound by contract to work as indentured servants for house Nox. Clement is a cruel man, and servanthood under him is far from enviable."
    new "In fact, many suspect that Clement makes bad loans deliberately. You see, the few defaulting debtors who are caught are bound by contract to work as indentured servants for house Nox. Clement is a cruel man, and servanthood under him is far from enviable.\n事实上,许多人怀疑Clement是故意放坏账的。你看,少数被抓到的违约债务人,按契约要为Nox家族当契约仆人。Clement是个残忍的人,在他手下做仆人,可绝非什么令人羡慕的事。"

    old "Making bad loans is a way for Clement to effectively obtain slaves that he can abuse as much as he likes. It's not rational from any point of view. But cruel men with old money often lack a taste for the rational."
    new "Making bad loans is a way for Clement to effectively obtain slaves that he can abuse as much as he likes. It's not rational from any point of view. But cruel men with old money often lack a taste for the rational.\n放坏账是Clement有效获取奴隶的方式,好让他随心所欲地虐待。从任何角度看,这都不合常理。但坐拥老钱的残忍之辈,往往就不喜欢讲常理。"

    old "Killing Clement Nox is an opportunity for us to rescue those slaves from abuse, though of course my main interest is in helping myself to some of that old money. It's the kind of kill that hopefully won't weigh too heavily on your conscience, and it should pay out quite well."
    new "Killing Clement Nox is an opportunity for us to rescue those slaves from abuse, though of course my main interest is in helping myself to some of that old money. It's the kind of kill that hopefully won't weigh too heavily on your conscience, and it should pay out quite well.\n杀掉Clement Nox,是让我们把那些奴隶从虐待中解救出来的机会,当然,我主要的兴趣,是分一点那老钱。这种杀法,但愿不会太重地压在你的良心上,而且报酬应该相当可观。"

    old "So, do you want a part of this job? Are you in or are you out?"
    new "So, do you want a part of this job? Are you in or are you out?\n那么,你想参与这份活儿吗?你入伙,还是退出?"

    old "I'm in, Kusho. If this man is as you say he is, then seeing him dead might actually help me rest easier at night."
    new "I'm in, Kusho. If this man is as you say he is, then seeing him dead might actually help me rest easier at night.\n我入伙,Kusho。如果这个人真如你所说,那么看着他死,也许反倒能让我夜里睡得更安稳。"

    old "Excellent. I think that our time would be well-spent traveling to stake out the location. Planning and reconnaissance is a critical part of any mission, and while I've already spent plenty of time scouting the location myself, I think it's best that you get acquainted with the premises."
    new "Excellent. I think that our time would be well-spent traveling to stake out the location. Planning and reconnaissance is a critical part of any mission, and while I've already spent plenty of time scouting the location myself, I think it's best that you get acquainted with the premises.\n好极了。我想我们的时间值得花在前往踩点上面。筹划与侦察是任何任务的关键部分,虽然我自己已经花了不少时间勘察那处,但我认为你最好也熟悉一下那栋宅子。"

    old "Simply being comfortable and familiar with the territory is a huge part of what makes an operation go smoothly—and it could save your life if circumstances go awry."
    new "Simply being comfortable and familiar with the territory is a huge part of what makes an operation go smoothly—and it could save your life if circumstances go awry.\n对环境感到自在熟悉,是行动顺利进行的一大关键——若情势生变,它还可能救你一命。"

    old "Let's go pay Clement Nox a visit, then."
    new "Let's go pay Clement Nox a visit, then.\n那我们这就去拜访Clement Nox吧。"

    old "I'd rather not get involved, Kusho."
    new "I'd rather not get involved, Kusho.\n我宁愿不掺和进来,Kusho。"

    old "If you're worried about having that man's death on your conscience, you should know that he's going to die, whether or not you choose to help."
    new "If you're worried about having that man's death on your conscience, you should know that he's going to die, whether or not you choose to help.\n如果你担心那人的死会压在你良心上,那你该知道,不管你是否帮忙,他都死定了。"

    old "That may be the case, Kusho. But as you yourself said, it's easier to rationalize a man's death when he's far away. I hold no disdain for what you plan to do, but the further away I stand from it, the easier it is for me to tolerate it."
    new "That may be the case, Kusho. But as you yourself said, it's easier to rationalize a man's death when he's far away. I hold no disdain for what you plan to do, but the further away I stand from it, the easier it is for me to tolerate it.\n也许是这样,Kusho。但正如你自己说过的,一个人死在远方时,更容易为他的死找到开脱。我不鄙视你打算做的事,但我离它站得越远,就越容易容忍它。"

    old "Suit yourself. Well, I've got preparations to attend to, and if you're not going to be part of them, I'd prefer your absence. Not that I dislike your company, you understand, but I'm a busy man."
    new "Suit yourself. Well, I've got preparations to attend to, and if you're not going to be part of them, I'd prefer your absence. Not that I dislike your company, you understand, but I'm a busy man.\n随你便。嗯,我还有准备工作要忙,如果你不打算参与,我倒希望你别在场。别误会,不是不喜欢你作陪,你懂的,只是我是个忙人。"

    old "No disrespect taken, Kusho. I'll leave you to your business."
    new "No disrespect taken, Kusho. I'll leave you to your business.\n我并无不敬,Kusho。我就不打扰你办事了。"

    old "Come by to chat some time. Who knows, if the hit goes well, I may be able to regale you with tales of how it went."
    new "Come by to chat some time. Who knows, if the hit goes well, I may be able to regale you with tales of how it went.\n改天来聊聊。谁知道呢,要是这次刺杀顺利,我也许还能给你讲讲它的经过。"

    old "It takes us a full day to reach Triberg. The sun is beginning to get lower in the sky by the time that we arrive at the large fence surrounding the Nox estate."
    new "It takes us a full day to reach Triberg. The sun is beginning to get lower in the sky by the time that we arrive at the large fence surrounding the Nox estate.\n我们花了整整一天才到Triberg。等我们抵达Nox庄园周围那道高大的栅栏时,太阳已开始西沉。"

    old "Well, here we are. The mansion where Clement Nox sleeps."
    new "Well, here we are. The mansion where Clement Nox sleeps.\n好了,我们到了。Clement Nox酣睡其中的那座豪宅。"

    old "Odd for a man so wealthy to have a metal fence surrounding his estate. Are brick walls out of fashion?"
    new "Odd for a man so wealthy to have a metal fence surrounding his estate. Are brick walls out of fashion?\n这么有钱的人,庄园四周却是金属栅栏,真怪。砖墙难道过时了?"

    old "Solid brick walls don't let you share the sight of your luxurious manor with the neighborhood. Look at that grass."
    new "Solid brick walls don't let you share the sight of your luxurious manor with the neighborhood. Look at that grass.\n实心砖墙可没法让你与街坊四邻分享你豪华宅邸的风光。瞧瞧那片草。"

    old "That's grass? But it's so short."
    new "That's grass? But it's so short.\n那是草?可它也太短了。"

    old "Clement has grounds keepers who trim the grass every day to keep it short and watered. You could walk on that grass in bare feet and it would be soft to the touch. He calls it a 'lawn.'"
    new "Clement has grounds keepers who trim the grass every day to keep it short and watered. You could walk on that grass in bare feet and it would be soft to the touch. He calls it a 'lawn.'\nClement有园丁,每天修剪草坪,好让它既短又浇足了水。你可以赤脚走在那草地上,触感柔软。他管它叫“草坪”。"

    old "I must say, the green grass is quite beautiful."
    new "I must say, the green grass is quite beautiful.\n不得不说,那青草真的很美。"

    old "Well, being 'beautiful' as you describe it is that lawn's sole function."
    new "Well, being 'beautiful' as you describe it is that lawn's sole function.\n嗯,如你所说的“美”,就是那草坪唯一的功能。"

    old "It's aesthetic. And it's primary aesthetic property is that it serves no use."
    new "It's aesthetic. And it's primary aesthetic property is that it serves no use.\n它关乎审美。而它最主要的审美特性,恰恰在于它毫无用处。"

    old "It's Clement's way of saying, 'look at me! I'm so rich that I have all of this fertile land, but rather than use it to support an orchard or some kind of crops, I've instead chosen to fill it with grass that serves no practical use, and is expensive to maintain!'"
    new "It's Clement's way of saying, 'look at me! I'm so rich that I have all of this fertile land, but rather than use it to support an orchard or some kind of crops, I've instead chosen to fill it with grass that serves no practical use, and is expensive to maintain!'\n这是Clement在说:“看看我!我富得拥有这么多肥沃的土地,却不用它来种果园或庄稼,反倒用毫无实际用途、维护还贵的草把它填满!”"

    old "The fashions of the rich will never cease to amuse me."
    new "The fashions of the rich will never cease to amuse me.\n有钱人的风尚,永远都能逗我发笑。"

    old "What a waste of land. If the ground is fertile enough to support green grass, surely it could have supported an orchard, or even a simple vegetable garden. Why spend so much land and so much effort to maintain something as useless as grass?"
    new "What a waste of land. If the ground is fertile enough to support green grass, surely it could have supported an orchard, or even a simple vegetable garden. Why spend so much land and so much effort to maintain something as useless as grass?\n真是糟蹋土地。如果这片地肥沃得能种青草,那它肯定也能种果园,哪怕是个简单的菜园呢。为什么要花这么多地、这么多力气,去维护草这种毫无用处的东西?"

    old "Kusho laughs."
    new "Kusho laughs.\nKusho笑了。"

    old "People like you and I have little hope of understanding what goes on inside the head of the extravagantly wealthy. It's almost as if they consider wastefulness a virtue."
    new "People like you and I have little hope of understanding what goes on inside the head of the extravagantly wealthy. It's almost as if they consider wastefulness a virtue.\n像你我这样的人,几乎别想弄懂那些富得流油的人脑子里在想什么。他们几乎把挥霍当成一种美德了。"

    old "In a way, wastefulness is Clement's way of bragging about his wealth. As you said, this land could have been purposed as an orchard or a garden, but instead it's supporting something as inane as a grass lawn."
    new "In a way, wastefulness is Clement's way of bragging about his wealth. As you said, this land could have been purposed as an orchard or a garden, but instead it's supporting something as inane as a grass lawn.\n某种程度上,挥霍是Clement炫耀财富的方式。正如你所说,这片地本可用作果园或花园,结果却养着一片草地这样毫无意义的东西。"

    old "It's just one of many reasons that Nox has been bleeding money ever since Clement inherited the estate from his father, but that pile of wealth is so massive that even with Clement's wastefulness, it will never be exhausted during his lifetime."
    new "It's just one of many reasons that Nox has been bleeding money ever since Clement inherited the estate from his father, but that pile of wealth is so massive that even with Clement's wastefulness, it will never be exhausted during his lifetime.\n这只是Nox自Clement从父亲手中继承庄园以来一直不断失血的众多原因之一,但那堆财富实在庞大,即便Clement如此挥霍,他这辈子也挥霍不完。"

    old "Those guards look intimidating."
    new "Those guards look intimidating.\n那些卫兵看起来怪唬人的。"

    old "They do, don't they? And that's exactly the way that Clement likes things. But the best security systems tend to be the ones that don't draw attention to themselves."
    new "They do, don't they? And that's exactly the way that Clement likes things. But the best security systems tend to be the ones that don't draw attention to themselves.\n可不是吗?这正是Clement喜欢的样子。不过最好的安保系统,往往是那些不引人注目的。"

    old "After all, for a sneak like me, a guard following a predictable route, whose main job is to carry a big lance and look intimidating, is nothing more than something to plan around. And the more ostentatious they are, the easier they are to plan around."
    new "After all, for a sneak like me, a guard following a predictable route, whose main job is to carry a big lance and look intimidating, is nothing more than something to plan around. And the more ostentatious they are, the easier they are to plan around.\n毕竟,对我这种潜行者来说,一个沿可预测路线巡逻、主要职责是扛着长枪摆出唬人模样的卫兵,不过是个需要绕开的因素罢了。他们越是招摇,越容易绕开。"

    old "That's the thing about supreme wealth. It tends to make people arrogant. People assume that parading their wealth in this manner will deter invaders. It deters dumb invaders, people who would go in through the front door. But my attention isn't on the front door."
    new "That's the thing about supreme wealth. It tends to make people arrogant. People assume that parading their wealth in this manner will deter invaders. It deters dumb invaders, people who would go in through the front door. But my attention isn't on the front door.\n这就是巨额财富的问题所在。它容易让人变得傲慢。人们以为这样炫耀财富能吓退入侵者。它能吓退愚蠢的入侵者,那些会从前门闯进来的人。可我的注意力不在前门。"

    old "So, the back door, then?"
    new "So, the back door, then?\n那么,是后门了?"

    old "Not a door. Look up. Do you see that east-facing window?"
    new "Not a door. Look up. Do you see that east-facing window?\n不是门。往上看。看到那扇朝东的窗户了吗?"

    old "That's where Clement sleeps. He likes the east-facing window, because it lets the morning sun in to wake him up naturally. That's our entry point."
    new "That's where Clement sleeps. He likes the east-facing window, because it lets the morning sun in to wake him up naturally. That's our entry point.\nClement就睡在那里。他喜欢那扇朝东的窗,因为晨光能透进来,让他自然醒来。那就是我们的入口。"

    old "So, you're going to scale the fence, then scale the entire building? That must be three stories up."
    new "So, you're going to scale the fence, then scale the entire building? That must be three stories up.\n所以,你要翻过栅栏,再攀上整栋楼?那得有三层楼高。"

    old "I'm an elf. I grew up in the woods. We don't have many fences or stone buildings there. What we do have are trees."
    new "I'm an elf. I grew up in the woods. We don't have many fences or stone buildings there. What we do have are trees.\n我是精灵。我在林子里长大。那里没有多少栅栏或石砌建筑。我们有的是树。"

    old "Kusho gestures to a nearby tree."
    new "Kusho gestures to a nearby tree.\nKusho朝附近的一棵树比了比。"

    old "The branches of that tree have been my perch for several weeks now. From that tree, I've observed what goes on in that estate. And from that tree, I will descend into Clement's east-facing third-story window."
    new "The branches of that tree have been my perch for several weeks now. From that tree, I've observed what goes on in that estate. And from that tree, I will descend into Clement's east-facing third-story window.\n那棵树的树枝,几周来一直是我的栖身处。从那儿,我观察着那座庄园里发生的一切。也是从那儿,我将潜入Clement那扇朝东的三楼窗户。"

    old "But how? You can't jump. The distance from those tree branches to the window must be at least a hundred feet. Don't tell me you've found a way to fly."
    new "But how? You can't jump. The distance from those tree branches to the window must be at least a hundred feet. Don't tell me you've found a way to fly.\n可怎么过去?你跳不过去的。从那些树枝到窗户,少说也有一百英尺。别告诉我你找到了会飞的办法。"

    old "Flying, eh? That's a talent I've yet to master, though I can't deny that it would come in handy for a man of my vocation."
    new "Flying, eh? That's a talent I've yet to master, though I can't deny that it would come in handy for a man of my vocation.\n飞,嗯?这本事我还没练成,虽说我不能否认,它对我这种行当的人会很有用。"

    old "As for how I intend to travel through the air and enter that window, I think that's a question best answered by showing rather than telling. And today isn't the day to show it. It's going to be dark soon."
    new "As for how I intend to travel through the air and enter that window, I think that's a question best answered by showing rather than telling. And today isn't the day to show it. It's going to be dark soon.\n至于我打算如何穿空而过,进入那扇窗,我想这问题与其说给你听,不如演示给你看。而今天不是演示的日子。天快黑了。"

    old "I don't understand. Wouldn't that be the perfect time to strike? After sunset?"
    new "I don't understand. Wouldn't that be the perfect time to strike? After sunset?\n我不明白。日落之后,不正是动手的最佳时机吗?"

    old "You might think that. And I expect Clement thinks that, too. Paranoid people always fear an assassin sneaking into their room and killing them in their sleep."
    new "You might think that. And I expect Clement thinks that, too. Paranoid people always fear an assassin sneaking into their room and killing them in their sleep.\n你也许会这么想。而我想,Clement也会这么想。偏执的人总是害怕有刺客潜入房间,趁他们熟睡时痛下杀手。"

    old "But nobody ever fears being assassinated in the safety of their home during daylight hours. I plan to give Clement a surprise. So this hit will have to wait for another day."
    new "But nobody ever fears being assassinated in the safety of their home during daylight hours. I plan to give Clement a surprise. So this hit will have to wait for another day.\n但没人会担心,光天化日之下,在自己安全的家中被暗杀。我打算给Clement一个惊喜。所以这次刺杀得等到另一天。"

    old "We need to strike earlier in the day, when the sun is higher and shining."
    new "We need to strike earlier in the day, when the sun is higher and shining.\n我们得在白天早些动手,趁太阳高照的时候。"

    old "You pick the day, [protag]. I've gathered all the information I need. Whenever you're ready to make this happen, just let me know."
    new "You pick the day, [protag]. I've gathered all the information I need. Whenever you're ready to make this happen, just let me know.\n日子你来挑,[protag]。我需要的情报都已收集齐。你什么时候准备好动手,就告诉我一声。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. It's good to see you."
    new "Ah, [protag]. It's good to see you.\n啊,[protag]。见到你真好。"

    old "I've been hearing a lot of chatter around Grimoire. What news am I missing out on?"
    new "I've been hearing a lot of chatter around Grimoire. What news am I missing out on?\n我听到Grimoire这边有不少闲言碎语。我错过了什么消息?"

    old "Recently there's been a bit of a power shift in Triberg. Geographically, it's disconnected from Grimoire, but things that affect Triberg's economy tend to have a ripple effect that extends across the land."
    new "Recently there's been a bit of a power shift in Triberg. Geographically, it's disconnected from Grimoire, but things that affect Triberg's economy tend to have a ripple effect that extends across the land.\n最近Triberg发生了一点权力更迭。地理上,它和Grimoire并不相连,但影响Triberg经济的事,往往会波及整片大地。"

    old "What happened?"
    new "What happened?\n出了什么事?"

    old "As best we can tell, there was a small rebellion. The lord of one of the city's larger noble houses was killed in his own mansion, and though they have yet to finger a perpetrator, it seems to be something that originated from within his own house. The deceased Clement Nox is now succeeded by his son."
    new "As best we can tell, there was a small rebellion. The lord of one of the city's larger noble houses was killed in his own mansion, and though they have yet to finger a perpetrator, it seems to be something that originated from within his own house. The deceased Clement Nox is now succeeded by his son.\n据我们所知,发生了一场小规模叛乱。城中一个较大贵族家族的家主,死在了自己的宅邸里,虽然他们尚未指认凶手,但这事似乎源于他自己家族内部。已故的Clement Nox如今由其子继任。"

    old "Clement Nox. If I recall, Nox is one of Triberg's oldest noble houses."
    new "Clement Nox. If I recall, Nox is one of Triberg's oldest noble houses.\nClement Nox。如果我没记错,Nox是Triberg最古老的贵族家族之一。"

    old "That it is. Clement's death has caused a bit of a stir. Rebellion is something that always put people in a state of unease, particularly people in positions of power. However, I can't say that I'm sad to see Clement go. He had quite a reputation for being an abusive master."
    new "That it is. Clement's death has caused a bit of a stir. Rebellion is something that always put people in a state of unease, particularly people in positions of power. However, I can't say that I'm sad to see Clement go. He had quite a reputation for being an abusive master.\n正是。Clement的死引起了一阵骚动。叛乱总是让人们心神不宁,尤其是当权者。不过,我不能说看到Clement离去我会难过。他虐待主人是出了名的。"

    old "His abuse bordered on cruelty, but it was just shy enough of criminal that his house could never be opened up to serious criminal investigation, and he was large and influential enough to never have his estate threatened. When you have as much money has he did, people tend to forgive any moral transgressions up to a certain point."
    new "His abuse bordered on cruelty, but it was just shy enough of criminal that his house could never be opened up to serious criminal investigation, and he was large and influential enough to never have his estate threatened. When you have as much money has he did, people tend to forgive any moral transgressions up to a certain point.\n他的虐待近乎残忍,却刚好够不上刑事犯罪,以致他的家族从未被立案严查;而他位高权重、势力庞大,庄园也从未受到威胁。当一个人有他那般多的钱财时,人们往往会原谅他一定程度内的任何道德劣迹。"

    old "What's the follow-up? Has any armed conflict followed the rebellion?"
    new "What's the follow-up? Has any armed conflict followed the rebellion?\n后续如何?叛乱之后有没有爆发武装冲突?"

    old "No, that's what's odd. No one has claimed credit for his death. In fact, if I had to guess, I'd say that whoever killed him was motivated more by personal anger than any larger grander scheme to topple the throne. It wouldn't surprise me if one of his own staff, maltreated one time too many, decided to do unto Clement as he did unto others."
    new "No, that's what's odd. No one has claimed credit for his death. In fact, if I had to guess, I'd say that whoever killed him was motivated more by personal anger than any larger grander scheme to topple the throne. It wouldn't surprise me if one of his own staff, maltreated one time too many, decided to do unto Clement as he did unto others.\n没有,这正是奇怪之处。没有人宣称对他的死负责。事实上,若要我猜,我会说杀他的人,更多是出于个人愤怒,而非任何推翻王权的宏大阴谋。若说是他手下的某个人,被虐待了太多次,决定以其人之道还治其人之身,我也不会意外。"

    old "I wanted to ask you. I don't know how well-connected you are in Triberg, but I know that you seem to have your finger on the pulse of this continent."
    new "I wanted to ask you. I don't know how well-connected you are in Triberg, but I know that you seem to have your finger on the pulse of this continent.\n我想问问你。我不知道你在Triberg的人脉如何,但我知道你似乎对这个大陆的脉搏了如指掌。"

    old "Of course, this lies entirely outside of your responsibilities to the council of Grimoire. I don't mean to heap another task on your plate, but I thought this information might be relevant to you."
    new "Of course, this lies entirely outside of your responsibilities to the council of Grimoire. I don't mean to heap another task on your plate, but I thought this information might be relevant to you.\n当然,这完全超出了你对Grimoire议会的职责范围。我不是想再给你添一桩差事,只是觉得这消息可能与你有关。"

    old "Hmm. A dead nobleman, with no killer apparent. That's a quandary you don't face every day."
    new "Hmm. A dead nobleman, with no killer apparent. That's a quandary you don't face every day.\n嗯。一个死去的贵族,凶手却毫无踪迹。这可不是天天能碰上的谜题。"

    old "It's a bit of a shot in the dark, but I was wondering if you had any knowledge that you think might be relevant to this case."
    new "It's a bit of a shot in the dark, but I was wondering if you had any knowledge that you think might be relevant to this case.\n这有点碰运气的成分,但我想问问,你是否知道些什么你认为与此案有关的?"

    old "I must confess that I'm not as well-connected with the affairs of Triberg as I am with the northern half of the continent. I wish I could offer you a theory, but I don't have any."
    new "I must confess that I'm not as well-connected with the affairs of Triberg as I am with the northern half of the continent. I wish I could offer you a theory, but I don't have any.\n我得承认,我对Triberg事务的了解,不如对大陆北半部那样深入。我倒希望能给你一个推测,可惜我没有。"

    old "Anyway based on what you said, it doesn't sound like there are a lot of people mourning this man's death. It could very well be that there were people who witnessed his murder, but don't have any interest in revealing the killer."
    new "Anyway based on what you said, it doesn't sound like there are a lot of people mourning this man's death. It could very well be that there were people who witnessed his murder, but don't have any interest in revealing the killer.\n总之,照你所说,听起来没多少人为这人的死而哀悼。很可能有人目睹了他的谋杀,却无意指认凶手。"

    old "Hmm. That may very well be the case. I suppose it is a mystery that will go unsolved as far as official reports are concerned, but I think that in their heart of hearts, most of the involved parties have a good idea of what happened."
    new "Hmm. That may very well be the case. I suppose it is a mystery that will go unsolved as far as official reports are concerned, but I think that in their heart of hearts, most of the involved parties have a good idea of what happened.\n嗯,很可能是这样。我想,就官方报告而言,这会是个悬而未决的谜团,但我想,在内心深处,大多数相关的人对发生了什么都有数。"

    old "I recall a certain someone telling me not too long ago that he intended to carry out an assassination. Could this be it?"
    new "I recall a certain someone telling me not too long ago that he intended to carry out an assassination. Could this be it?\n我记得不久前,有个人告诉我,他打算执行一次暗杀。会不会就是这事?"

    old "I do have a theory, but I think it would be premature to share it."
    new "I do have a theory, but I think it would be premature to share it.\n我确实有个推测,但我觉得现在分享它还太早。"

    old "Interesting. Well, as I said, this whole ordeal is entirely outside the bounds of your responsibilities. But if you do have a hunch, I hope you'll have the time to follow up on it."
    new "Interesting. Well, as I said, this whole ordeal is entirely outside the bounds of your responsibilities. But if you do have a hunch, I hope you'll have the time to follow up on it.\n有意思。嗯,如我所说,这整桩磨难完全超出了你的职责范围。但如果你真有什么预感,希望你能抽出时间追查下去。"

    old "I need to go now, Apolimesho. Thanks for telling me this."
    new "I need to go now, Apolimesho. Thanks for telling me this.\n我得走了,Apolimesho。谢谢你告诉我这些。"

    old "Anytime."
    new "Anytime.\n随时奉陪。"

    old "Kusho brings me to the fence of the Nox estate in Triberg. We stand off the main road, but the hustle and bustle of people carrying about their morning business is still clearly audible from where we stand."
    new "Kusho brings me to the fence of the Nox estate in Triberg. We stand off the main road, but the hustle and bustle of people carrying about their morning business is still clearly audible from where we stand.\nKusho带我来到Triberg的Nox庄园栅栏前。我们站在大道旁,但人们忙碌张罗晨间事务的喧闹声,从我们所站之处仍清晰可闻。"

    old "Well, Clement is ready to meet his maker. The question is, are you ready to send him there?"
    new "Well, Clement is ready to meet his maker. The question is, are you ready to send him there?\n好了,Clement已准备好去见他的造物主。问题是,你准备好送他上路了吗?"

    old "I suppose I'm mentally ready, but I'm still a bit uneasy with this 'infiltration by daylight' plan that you have."
    new "I suppose I'm mentally ready, but I'm still a bit uneasy with this 'infiltration by daylight' plan that you have.\n我想我心理上准备好了,但对你那个“白天潜入”的计划,我还是有点不放心。"

    old "I understand that you want to strike when we're least expected, but isn't an infiltration like this something best done under cover of darkness? Even if people are more paranoid at night, I would think that sneaking about would be easier without daylight exposing our every movement."
    new "I understand that you want to strike when we're least expected, but isn't an infiltration like this something best done under cover of darkness? Even if people are more paranoid at night, I would think that sneaking about would be easier without daylight exposing our every movement.\n我理解你想趁我们最不被料到的时机动手,但这样的潜入,不是最好在夜幕掩护下进行吗?即便人们夜里更警觉,我也觉得,没有日光暴露我们的一举一动,偷偷摸摸会更容易些。"

    old "Your suggestion that infiltration by night is less-easily detected is both logical and intuitive. And, like many logical and intuitive assumptions, it is wrong."
    new "Your suggestion that infiltration by night is less-easily detected is both logical and intuitive. And, like many logical and intuitive assumptions, it is wrong.\n你认为夜间潜入更难被察觉,这既合逻辑又合直觉。而正如许多合逻辑又合直觉的假设一样,它是错的。"

    old "Look around us. What do you see?"
    new "Look around us. What do you see?\n看看我们周围。你看到了什么?"

    old "Lots of people. Lots of potential witnesses."
    new "Lots of people. Lots of potential witnesses.\n很多人。很多潜在的目击者。"

    old "No, not witnesses. They won't see us do the deed. The people that you see walking the streets? These are distractions. If we find ourselves needing to flee, they will be a place to get lost."
    new "No, not witnesses. They won't see us do the deed. The people that you see walking the streets? These are distractions. If we find ourselves needing to flee, they will be a place to get lost.\n不,不是目击者。他们不会看到我们动手。你在街上看到的那些人?他们只是障眼。如果我们需要逃跑,他们就是我们藏身的地方。"

    old "Think about it this way. What kind of people slink around in the shadows at night? People who are up to no good, that's who. At night, even the most minor of disturbances is investigated with some amount of rigor. But if someone hears a din outside during the daytime, they don't bat an eye."
    new "Think about it this way. What kind of people slink around in the shadows at night? People who are up to no good, that's who. At night, even the most minor of disturbances is investigated with some amount of rigor. But if someone hears a din outside during the daytime, they don't bat an eye.\n这么想。什么样的人会在夜里于阴影中潜行?图谋不轨的人,就是那种人。夜里,哪怕是最轻微的异动,也会被颇为认真地查个究竟。但若有人在白天听到外面的动静,他们连眼皮都不会抬一下。"

    old "That's why daytime is the best time to infiltrate. Morning, best of all, since we're infiltrating through an east-facing window. We'll have the sun at our backs."
    new "That's why daytime is the best time to infiltrate. Morning, best of all, since we're infiltrating through an east-facing window. We'll have the sun at our backs.\n所以白天才是潜入的最佳时机。而早晨最好,因为我们是从朝东的窗户潜入,太阳会正好在我们背后。"

    old "Guards inside the estate won't be watching the top of the eastern wall. And even if they do happen to glance our direction, the sun will be in their eyes. They may see motion, but in the daytime, that motion could be anything. Birds, a child's kite, whatever excuse they want."
    new "Guards inside the estate won't be watching the top of the eastern wall. And even if they do happen to glance our direction, the sun will be in their eyes. They may see motion, but in the daytime, that motion could be anything. Birds, a child's kite, whatever excuse they want.\n庄园里的卫兵不会盯着东墙顶端看。就算他们碰巧朝我们这个方向瞥一眼,阳光也会晃他们的眼。他们可能看到动静,但在白天,那动静可能是任何东西。鸟,孩子的风筝,随他们怎么找借口。"

    old "Besides, you said it yourself: the prevailing notion is that infitration is a crime best performed under cover of darkness. In the bright morning sun, nobody will be expecting a sneak attack. You want to surprise someone? Attack them when and where they feel safest."
    new "Besides, you said it yourself: the prevailing notion is that infitration is a crime best performed under cover of darkness. In the bright morning sun, nobody will be expecting a sneak attack. You want to surprise someone? Attack them when and where they feel safest.\n再说,你自己也说了:普遍的认知是,潜入最好在夜幕掩护下进行。在明亮的晨光里,没人会料到一场偷袭。你想给某人一个惊喜?就在他们感觉最安全的时间和地点下手。"

    old "Kusho leads me off the main roadway to the tree he showed me yesterday. Kusho ducks behind the tree to hide from the pedestrians on the main roadway, and gestures for me to follow him."
    new "Kusho leads me off the main roadway to the tree he showed me yesterday. Kusho ducks behind the tree to hide from the pedestrians on the main roadway, and gestures for me to follow him.\nKusho领我离开大道,来到昨天他指给我看的那棵树旁。Kusho躲到树后,避开大道上的行人,并示意我跟上。"

    old "You know how to climb a tree?"
    new "You know how to climb a tree?\n你会爬树吗?"

    old "Of course I do."
    new "Of course I do.\n当然会。"

    old "Good. Follow me."
    new "Good. Follow me.\n好。跟我来。"

    old "Kusho scrambles up the tree's trunk, and within moment's he's concealed in the foliage. I follow behind as quickly as I can."
    new "Kusho scrambles up the tree's trunk, and within moment's he's concealed in the foliage. I follow behind as quickly as I can.\nKusho攀上树干,转瞬便隐没在枝叶中。我以最快的速度跟在后面。"

    old "Quite fortuitous for this tree to be right outside the estate walls."
    new "Quite fortuitous for this tree to be right outside the estate walls.\n这棵树恰好长在庄园墙外,真是走运。"

    old "Nox is a man who prizes things like beauty more than safety. Even the guards patrolling the front of the estate are there mostly for aesthetic purposes. They're for intimidation, not fighting."
    new "Nox is a man who prizes things like beauty more than safety. Even the guards patrolling the front of the estate are there mostly for aesthetic purposes. They're for intimidation, not fighting.\nNox这个人,看重美胜过安全。即便是庄园前方巡逻的卫兵,也多半是摆在那儿的点缀。他们是用来唬人的,不是用来打仗的。"

    old "Just look at the size of the weapons they're carrying. They look deadly, but a lance like that is best suited to the battlefield, not a yard where they could face close-quarters combat."
    new "Just look at the size of the weapons they're carrying. They look deadly, but a lance like that is best suited to the battlefield, not a yard where they could face close-quarters combat.\n看看他们拿的武器有多大。那些看起来致命,但那样的长枪最适合战场,而不是可能爆发近身搏斗的庭院。"

    old "I doubt any of those men have seen real combat at all during their time with Nox. I don't intend to get caught, but if we do, I think we have the means to fight our way out."
    new "I doubt any of those men have seen real combat at all during their time with Nox. I don't intend to get caught, but if we do, I think we have the means to fight our way out.\n我怀疑那些人里,有谁在Nox手下真见过实战。我并不想被抓,但若真被抓住,我想我们有办法杀出去。"

    old "So, we have a backup exit strategy. You still haven't told me what the entry strategy is."
    new "So, we have a backup exit strategy. You still haven't told me what the entry strategy is.\n这么说,我们有了备用的撤退方案。你还没告诉我进入的方案是什么。"

    old "Ah, of course."
    new "Ah, of course.\n啊,当然。"

    old "Kusho draws my attention to a crossbow that is mounted on one of the tree branches."
    new "Kusho draws my attention to a crossbow that is mounted on one of the tree branches.\nKusho把我的注意力引向一把架在其中一根树枝上的弩。"

    old "You've been storing this thing up here?"
    new "You've been storing this thing up here?\n你一直把这东西藏在这儿?"

    old "What can I say? I'm an elf. When I see a tree, I feel obliged to make myself at home. And the foliage of this tree is dense enough to hide both us and any gadgets and tools I might want to store here."
    new "What can I say? I'm an elf. When I see a tree, I feel obliged to make myself at home. And the foliage of this tree is dense enough to hide both us and any gadgets and tools I might want to store here.\n我能说什么呢?我是精灵。看见树,我就忍不住想安家。而这棵树的枝叶浓密,足以藏住我们俩,以及我想存放在这儿的任何物件和工具。"

    old "Kusho lays himself out on the tree branch and aims the crossbow."
    new "Kusho lays himself out on the tree branch and aims the crossbow.\nKusho伏在树枝上,端起弩瞄准。"

    old "You're going to shoot him with that thing?"
    new "You're going to shoot him with that thing?\n你要用那东西射他?"

    old "Unfortunately, no. Although I consider myself an accomplished sniper, and I often take great pride in claiming credit for my kills, this is a special job. I don't want this to look like the work of an outsider. A crossbow bolt fired through a window just won't do. The kill is going to have to be more intimate than that."
    new "Unfortunately, no. Although I consider myself an accomplished sniper, and I often take great pride in claiming credit for my kills, this is a special job. I don't want this to look like the work of an outsider. A crossbow bolt fired through a window just won't do. The kill is going to have to be more intimate than that.\n很遗憾,不是。虽然我自认是名出色的狙击手,也常为自己杀人的功劳引以为傲,但这是桩特殊的活儿。我不想让它看起来像外人所为。从窗外射进一支弩箭可不行。这次动手,必须比那更贴身。"

    old "So what's the crossbow for, then?"
    new "So what's the crossbow for, then?\n那这弩是干什么用的?"

    old "[protag], do you know what a harpoon is?"
    new "[protag], do you know what a harpoon is?\n[protag],你知道鱼叉是什么吗?"

    old "Yes, I once met a whaler who acquainted me with the device. It seems like a brutal way to kill sea animals. My understanding is that the beast would often remain alive as the harpoon remained embedded in its flesh, and it would bleed out as it was dragged back to shore."
    new "Yes, I once met a whaler who acquainted me with the device. It seems like a brutal way to kill sea animals. My understanding is that the beast would often remain alive as the harpoon remained embedded in its flesh, and it would bleed out as it was dragged back to shore.\n知道,我曾遇到过一个捕鲸人,是他让我认识了这个器具。那似乎是种残忍的猎杀海兽之法。据我所知,鱼叉嵌在猎物体内时,那畜生往往还活着,被拖回岸边时才慢慢流血而亡。"

    old "Sorry, Kusho. You'll have to enlighten me."
    new "Sorry, Kusho. You'll have to enlighten me.\n抱歉,Kusho。你得给我讲讲。"

    old "Kusho points to the bolt that's mounted on his crossbow."
    new "Kusho points to the bolt that's mounted on his crossbow.\nKusho指了指装在他弩上的那支箭。"

    old "See this hooked end? Fishermen and whalers use these when hunting. They fire the harpoon at a whale or seal, and the hook embeds itself in the beast. The barbs around it dig into the animal's flesh, allowing them to secure hold of it and drag it with them back to shore. That's what the rope is for."
    new "See this hooked end? Fishermen and whalers use these when hunting. They fire the harpoon at a whale or seal, and the hook embeds itself in the beast. The barbs around it dig into the animal's flesh, allowing them to secure hold of it and drag it with them back to shore. That's what the rope is for.\n看到这带钩的头了吗?渔夫和捕鲸人打猎时就用这个。他们把鱼叉射向鲸或海豹,钩子便嵌进猎物体内。周围的倒刺扎进它的肉里,让他们能牢牢钩住它,再把它拖回岸边。绳子就是干这个用的。"

    old "As it turns out, these hooks and barbs are good at catching things besides just flesh. Watch."
    new "As it turns out, these hooks and barbs are good at catching things besides just flesh. Watch.\n事实证明,这些钩子和倒刺除了钩肉,还很擅长钩住别的东西。瞧好了。"

    old "Kusho fires the harpoon, and it flies through the air, embedding itself above Clement's open window."
    new "Kusho fires the harpoon, and it flies through the air, embedding itself above Clement's open window.\nKusho射出鱼叉,它破空而去,嵌在了Clement敞开的窗户上方。"

    old "Nobody heard that?"
    new "Nobody heard that?\n没人听见?"

    old "It's broad daylight. Loud sounds during daylight hours aren't an unusual thing."
    new "It's broad daylight. Loud sounds during daylight hours aren't an unusual thing.\n这是大白天。白天有响动,不是什么稀奇事。"

    old "Kusho yanks the rope connected to the harpoon, pulling it taut before tying it to one of the branches of the tree."
    new "Kusho yanks the rope connected to the harpoon, pulling it taut before tying it to one of the branches of the tree.\nKusho拽了拽系在鱼叉上的绳子,把它绷紧,再系到树的一根树枝上。"

    old "Now we have our entry point. And escape route."
    new "Now we have our entry point. And escape route.\n现在我们有入口了。还有退路。"

    old "Escape route?"
    new "Escape route?\n退路?"

    old "Right now the rope is angled downward, sloped toward Clement's window. I'll use this rope to descend into his room. Once I'm across, you'll untie this rope, and re-affix it to a lower branch, creating a sloped incline from Clement's window back to this tree. I'll be in and out like nothing happened."
    new "Right now the rope is angled downward, sloped toward Clement's window. I'll use this rope to descend into his room. Once I'm across, you'll untie this rope, and re-affix it to a lower branch, creating a sloped incline from Clement's window back to this tree. I'll be in and out like nothing happened.\n眼下绳子向下倾斜,斜向Clement的窗户。我会顺着这根绳子下到他的房间。等我过去后,你解开绳子,重新系到更低的树枝上,形成一条从Clement窗户斜回这棵树的坡道。我进出就神不知鬼不觉了。"

    old "Of course, if you'd like to do the honors yourself, you're welcome to do so."
    new "Of course, if you'd like to do the honors yourself, you're welcome to do so.\n当然,如果你想亲自代劳,也欢迎。"

    old "I mean that I can stay watch if you want to be the one who goes across and does the deed."
    new "I mean that I can stay watch if you want to be the one who goes across and does the deed.\n我是说,如果你想当那个过去动手的人,我可以留在这儿望风。"

    old "I think I need more information if I'm going to commit to that."
    new "I think I need more information if I'm going to commit to that.\n要我真接下这差事,我想我需要更多信息。"

    old "What if I decide to let you do the dirty work?"
    new "What if I decide to let you do the dirty work?\n如果我说让你去干这脏活呢?"

    old "That's the contingency I had planned on. I'm good at what I do, and I don't expect you to do my work for me. I was just giving you the option."
    new "That's the contingency I had planned on. I'm good at what I do, and I don't expect you to do my work for me. I was just giving you the option.\n那本就是我计划中的预备方案。我擅长自己的本行,也没指望你替我干活。我只是给你这个选项。"

    old "That being said, I did bring you here for a reason. You see, as well as I've planned this, I always like to have contingencies, and should you choose to stay in this tree, I'll be relying on you to act as an insurance policy of sorts."
    new "That being said, I did bring you here for a reason. You see, as well as I've planned this, I always like to have contingencies, and should you choose to stay in this tree, I'll be relying on you to act as an insurance policy of sorts.\n话虽如此,我带你来是有原因的。你看,尽管我计划周密,但我总喜欢留些后手。如果你选择留在这棵树上,我就得靠你充当某种保险。"

    old "What do you mean by that?"
    new "What do you mean by that?\n你这话什么意思?"

    old "Kusho points to the crossbow."
    new "Kusho points to the crossbow.\nKusho指了指那把弩。"

    old "I'm not sure I'm a good enough marksman to support you with this thing. I don't think you should be trusting me to accurately hit a target through that window."
    new "I'm not sure I'm a good enough marksman to support you with this thing. I don't think you should be trusting me to accurately hit a target through that window.\n我不确定自己枪法够好,能用这东西掩护你。我觉得你不该指望我能隔着那扇窗精准命中目标。"

    old "I'm not asking you to."
    new "I'm not asking you to.\n我没要你那么做。"

    old "Kusho picks up a crossbow bolt with something affixed to the end."
    new "Kusho picks up a crossbow bolt with something affixed to the end.\nKusho拾起一支弩箭,箭尾装着什么东西。"

    old "When this tip strikes a hard surface, it will emit thick black smoke. That should provide enough of a distraction for me to escape, should circumstances require it."
    new "When this tip strikes a hard surface, it will emit thick black smoke. That should provide enough of a distraction for me to escape, should circumstances require it.\n这箭头撞上硬面,就会放出浓黑的烟。若情势需要,那应该足以制造混乱,让我脱身。"

    old "The crossbow is already aimed at the window. All you need to do is pull the trigger."
    new "The crossbow is already aimed at the window. All you need to do is pull the trigger.\n弩已经瞄准窗户。你只需扣下扳机。"

    old "That sounds reasonable enough."
    new "That sounds reasonable enough.\n这听起来挺合理。"

    old "Let's say I descend down that rope and enter Clement's room. Then what?"
    new "Let's say I descend down that rope and enter Clement's room. Then what?\n假设我顺着绳子下去,进了Clement的房间。然后呢?"

    old "Simple. He's out of his room, attending to the affairs of his estate, but he'll soon be back to visit his wardrobe, as man of his means are often wont to do in the late morning hours."
    new "Simple. He's out of his room, attending to the affairs of his estate, but he'll soon be back to visit his wardrobe, as man of his means are often wont to do in the late morning hours.\n简单。他现在不在房里,正忙着打理庄园事务,但很快就会回来看他的衣橱——像他这般身家的人,往往喜欢在上午晚些时候这么做。"

    old "You find a place to hide, either under his bed, or in a closet if you find one convenient. You wait for him to re-enter the room, and when the opportunity arises, you pop out and kill him."
    new "You find a place to hide, either under his bed, or in a closet if you find one convenient. You wait for him to re-enter the room, and when the opportunity arises, you pop out and kill him.\n你找个地方藏起来,床底下,或者壁橱里,只要你觉得方便。你等他重新进房,一旦机会出现,你就窜出来杀了他。"

    old "Kill him how?"
    new "Kill him how?\n怎么杀?"

    old "Kusho pulls out a knife, wrapped in a leather sheath."
    new "Kusho pulls out a knife, wrapped in a leather sheath.\nKusho掏出一把刀,裹在皮鞘里。"

    old "This should do the job nicely. It's just like the ones that his guards use, so killing him with this will make the hit look like an inside job. Plant this blade between his shoulder blades, or slide it behind his ribs."
    new "This should do the job nicely. It's just like the ones that his guards use, so killing him with this will make the hit look like an inside job. Plant this blade between his shoulder blades, or slide it behind his ribs.\n这把会很顺手。它和他卫兵用的刀一模一样,用它杀他,会让这次刺杀看起来像是内鬼所为。把刀插进他的肩胛骨之间,或者从肋骨后面捅进去。"

    old "Or you can slice his throat, or stab him in the neck. Whatever suits your fancy. The possibilities are endless, really."
    new "Or you can slice his throat, or stab him in the neck. Whatever suits your fancy. The possibilities are endless, really.\n或者割开他的喉咙,或者刺进他的脖子。随你喜欢。可能性多得是,真的。"

    old "Of course, if you go through the window, I'll be back here, keeping watch from afar."
    new "Of course, if you go through the window, I'll be back here, keeping watch from afar.\n当然,如果你穿窗进去,我会留在这里,远远地望风。"

    old "Kusho gestures to the crossbow."
    new "Kusho gestures to the crossbow.\nKusho朝那把弩比了比。"

    old "This thing is good for shooting more than just harpoons. If you run into any snags, or find yourself in a bind, I'll give you the cover you need to escape."
    new "This thing is good for shooting more than just harpoons. If you run into any snags, or find yourself in a bind, I'll give you the cover you need to escape.\n这东西可不只能射鱼叉。如果你遇到麻烦,或者陷入困境,我会给你提供脱身所需的掩护。"

    old "I'll cover you while you go and get your hands dirty."
    new "I'll cover you while you go and get your hands dirty.\n你去弄脏双手,我来掩护你。"

    old "Excellent. Once I'm across, secure that rope two branches down."
    new "Excellent. Once I'm across, secure that rope two branches down.\n好极了。我过去之后,把绳子往下两枝树枝处系好。"

    old "You got it."
    new "You got it.\n没问题。"

    old "Kusho pulls a length of chain from his pocket, and wraps it around both of his hands after looping it around the rope."
    new "Kusho pulls a length of chain from his pocket, and wraps it around both of his hands after looping it around the rope.\nKusho从口袋里掏出一段链子,先绕过绳子,再缠住自己双手。"

    old "Kusho releases his hold of the tree branch, and allows gravity to pull him toward Clement's window as he slides down the rope. He climbs through without much difficulty and gives me a nod."
    new "Kusho releases his hold of the tree branch, and allows gravity to pull him toward Clement's window as he slides down the rope. He climbs through without much difficulty and gives me a nod.\nKusho松开抓住树枝的手,任重力把自己拉向Clement的窗户,同时沿绳滑下。他毫不费力地爬了进去,向我点了点头。"

    old "I untie the rope from where it's affixed, and climb several branches lower, until I'm below the level of the window. At this height, he should be able to slide down the rope while still clearing the wall. I tie the rope, give it a tug to ensure it's securely fashioned, and return to the crossbow to keep watch."
    new "I untie the rope from where it's affixed, and climb several branches lower, until I'm below the level of the window. At this height, he should be able to slide down the rope while still clearing the wall. I tie the rope, give it a tug to ensure it's securely fashioned, and return to the crossbow to keep watch.\n我解开系绳之处,往下爬了几枝树枝,直到低于窗户的高度。在这个高度,他应该能顺绳滑下,同时还能越过围墙。我系好绳子,拽了拽确认系牢,然后回到弩旁望风。"

    old "I can't see much through the window, apart from the door to the room. Kusho seems to have hidden himself quite well. I guess it's just a matter of waiting for the assassination target to reveal himself."
    new "I can't see much through the window, apart from the door to the room. Kusho seems to have hidden himself quite well. I guess it's just a matter of waiting for the assassination target to reveal himself.\n除了房门,我从窗户里看不到太多东西。Kusho似乎把自己藏得很好。我想,现在只需等待暗杀目标现身了。"

    old "To pass the time, I scan the courtyard and observe the movement of the guards."
    new "To pass the time, I scan the courtyard and observe the movement of the guards.\n为打发时间,我扫视庭院,观察卫兵的动向。"

    old "I've often heard it said that most professions that involve killing consist mostly of boredom, punctuated by moments of supreme terror. Now that I think about it, Kusho says he's spent weeks planning this hit. Several minutes—or hours—of lying in hiding is probably nothing to him."
    new "I've often heard it said that most professions that involve killing consist mostly of boredom, punctuated by moments of supreme terror. Now that I think about it, Kusho says he's spent weeks planning this hit. Several minutes—or hours—of lying in hiding is probably nothing to him.\n我常听人说,大多数涉及杀戮的行当,大半时间都在无聊中度过,只在偶尔的极度恐怖瞬间才有事发生。如今想来,Kusho说这次刺杀他筹划了好几周。对他来说,躲藏几分钟——或者几小时——大概根本算不了什么。"

    old "Ah, well. Nothing to do now but be patient."
    new "Ah, well. Nothing to do now but be patient.\n啊,算了。现在除了耐心等待,别无他法。"

    old "To keep myself alert, I keep my eyes trained on the window and try to count the individual bricks and boards in the building's construction. My boredom is finally interrupted when the door opens."
    new "To keep myself alert, I keep my eyes trained on the window and try to count the individual bricks and boards in the building's construction. My boredom is finally interrupted when the door opens.\n为了保持警觉,我一直盯着窗户,试着数清建筑上的一块块砖和板。门打开时,我的无聊终于被打断。"

    old "I steady my grip in the crossbow, and rest my finger against the trigger. Do your worst, Kusho."
    new "I steady my grip in the crossbow, and rest my finger against the trigger. Do your worst, Kusho.\n我握稳弩,手指搭上扳机。放手干吧,Kusho。"

    old "A slight man steps through the door and walks to the bed. I think I can make out the shape of his elvish ears."
    new "A slight man steps through the door and walks to the bed. I think I can make out the shape of his elvish ears.\n一个瘦小的男人推门而入,走向床边。我想我认得出他精灵耳朵的轮廓。"

    old "Before I've even registered it, Kusho emerges behind him, grabbing him by the throat. I see a flash of metal, and blood begins flowing from the man's neck."
    new "Before I've even registered it, Kusho emerges behind him, grabbing him by the throat. I see a flash of metal, and blood begins flowing from the man's neck.\n我还没反应过来,Kusho已从他身后出现,掐住了他的喉咙。我瞥见一道金属寒光,鲜血开始从那人的脖颈涌出。"

    old "Kusho allows the man's limp body to drop to the ground, then turns around and straddles the body."
    new "Kusho allows the man's limp body to drop to the ground, then turns around and straddles the body.\nKusho任那人瘫软的身体倒在地上,随即转身跨坐在尸体上。"

    old "I watch as Kusho drives his knife into the man's chest repeatedly, delivering blow after blow. Any one of those stabs could have been fatal, in and of itself, but he continues stabbing away."
    new "I watch as Kusho drives his knife into the man's chest repeatedly, delivering blow after blow. Any one of those stabs could have been fatal, in and of itself, but he continues stabbing away.\n我看着Kusho把刀一次次捅进那人胸口,一击接着一击。任何一刀都足以致命,但他仍不停地捅着。"

    old "Kusho leaves the knife in the man's chest, and heads to the window. With a flourish of the chain, he begins descending from the window back to the tree, and within seconds he's hanging from a branch beneath me."
    new "Kusho leaves the knife in the man's chest, and heads to the window. With a flourish of the chain, he begins descending from the window back to the tree, and within seconds he's hanging from a branch beneath me.\nKusho把刀留在那人胸口,走向窗户。他挥了挥链子,开始从窗户回落向树,几秒之内就悬在了我下方的一根树枝上。"

    old "Time for you to get lost."
    new "Time for you to get lost.\n你该走了。"

    old "What about you?"
    new "What about you?\n那你呢?"

    old "Me? I've got this setup to clean up."
    new "Me? I've got this setup to clean up.\n我?我得收拾这里的家伙什。"

    old "He points to the mounted crossbow."
    new "He points to the mounted crossbow.\n他指了指架起的弩。"

    old "Besides, we should leave separately. We can meet back in the forest in a few days once the dust has settled."
    new "Besides, we should leave separately. We can meet back in the forest in a few days once the dust has settled.\n再说,我们该分开离开。等尘埃落定,几天后在林子里碰头。"

    old "All right."
    new "All right.\n好。"

    old "I'll make the hit. As long as you have my back, I feel confident in my ability to pull this off."
    new "I'll make the hit. As long as you have my back, I feel confident in my ability to pull this off.\n这次动手由我来。只要你掩护我,我对自己成功就有信心。"

    old "Kusho hands me the knife."
    new "Kusho hands me the knife.\nKusho把刀递给我。"

    old "When you're done, leave the knife behind. They'll want to know how this crime was executed, and we don't want to leave too much to the imagination."
    new "When you're done, leave the knife behind. They'll want to know how this crime was executed, and we don't want to leave too much to the imagination.\n完事后把刀留下。他们会想弄清这案子是怎么下的手,我们别给他们留下太多想象空间。"

    old "Got it."
    new "Got it.\n明白。"

    old "As for zip-lining, take this."
    new "As for zip-lining, take this.\n至于滑索,拿着这个。"

    old "Kusho hands me a small length of chain."
    new "Kusho hands me a small length of chain.\nKusho递给我一小段链子。"

    old "Loop the chain over the rope, then wrap it around each of your hands to make sure you have a solid grip on it. Ease yourself on the branch, so that your weight shifts to the rope gradually. Your legs will naturally swing downward. Most importantly, when you hit the window, bend your knees, don't lock them."
    new "Loop the chain over the rope, then wrap it around each of your hands to make sure you have a solid grip on it. Ease yourself on the branch, so that your weight shifts to the rope gradually. Your legs will naturally swing downward. Most importantly, when you hit the window, bend your knees, don't lock them.\n把链子套在绳子上,再绕住你的双手,确保抓得牢。在树枝上缓缓移动身体,让重量逐渐转移到绳子上。双腿会自然下摆。最重要的是,撞到窗户时要屈膝,别把膝盖绷死。"

    old "Following Kusho's advice, I loop the chain over the zip-line rope, then wrap each end of the chain around my hands several time, securing my grip before shifting my weight off the tree branch and on to the rope. I slide down the rope, slowly accelerating as I go."
    new "Following Kusho's advice, I loop the chain over the zip-line rope, then wrap each end of the chain around my hands several time, securing my grip before shifting my weight off the tree branch and on to the rope. I slide down the rope, slowly accelerating as I go.\n我照Kusho的建议,把链子套在滑索绳上,再把链子两端在手上缠了几圈,先抓稳,才把重心从树枝移到绳上。我顺绳滑下,越滑越快。"

    old "I bend my knees as my feet clip the bottom of the window, and release my grip on the chain as my momentum carries me through the window. I hit the floor and stumble, and the chain clatters to the floor beside me. Did anyone hear me?"
    new "I bend my knees as my feet clip the bottom of the window, and release my grip on the chain as my momentum carries me through the window. I hit the floor and stumble, and the chain clatters to the floor beside me. Did anyone hear me?\n双脚擦过窗底时我屈起膝,趁冲劲把我带过窗时松开了链子。我摔到地上,踉跄了一下,链子咣当落在我身旁的地板上。有人听见我吗?"

    old "I scan the room. The closet looks to small to hide in. The bed is the only place big enough to conceal me, so I drop to the floor and slide underneath it. From here, I can see only the bottom of the door, but that's all I need to see. Now there's nothing to do but wait."
    new "I scan the room. The closet looks to small to hide in. The bed is the only place big enough to conceal me, so I drop to the floor and slide underneath it. From here, I can see only the bottom of the door, but that's all I need to see. Now there's nothing to do but wait.\n我扫视房间。壁橱太小,藏不下人。床是唯一大得能藏住我的地方,于是我伏到地上,钻到床底。从这里我只能看到门的下沿,但也只需看到这些。现在除了等,无事可做。"

    old "As I concentrate on the door, I take note of my breathing, and realize that my heart is racing. I concentrate on taking slow-even breaths, and press a finger against my neck to track my own pulse."
    new "As I concentrate on the door, I take note of my breathing, and realize that my heart is racing. I concentrate on taking slow-even breaths, and press a finger against my neck to track my own pulse.\n我盯着门,留意自己的呼吸,意识到心脏正狂跳不止。我专注于放慢、放匀呼吸,并伸出一根手指按在颈侧,追踪自己的脉搏。"

    old "Several minutes pass without any sign of motion at the door, and I find myself somewhat grateful for the lull. With any luck, by the time Clement opens that door, any feelings of anxiety will be completely replaced with boredom."
    new "Several minutes pass without any sign of motion at the door, and I find myself somewhat grateful for the lull. With any luck, by the time Clement opens that door, any feelings of anxiety will be completely replaced with boredom.\n几分钟过去,门口毫无动静,我竟有些感激这份平静。运气好的话,等Clement推开那扇门时,任何不安都已完全被无聊取代。"

    old "I hear the door creak before I see it open. A man's bare feet are all that's visible to me from beneath the bed, and I wait until I hear the door slam shut before I slide out, positioning myself behind the man."
    new "I hear the door creak before I see it open. A man's bare feet are all that's visible to me from beneath the bed, and I wait until I hear the door slam shut before I slide out, positioning myself behind the man.\n我先听见门吱呀一声,才看见它打开。从床底,我只能看到一双男人赤裸的脚。我等到听见门砰地关上,才滑出去,站到那男人身后。"

    old "Clement is a slight man, with his long elvish ears being his most prominent features. I'm amazed at how old and feeble he looks. He's hunched over, and even from behind him I can hear his labored breathing."
    new "Clement is a slight man, with his long elvish ears being his most prominent features. I'm amazed at how old and feeble he looks. He's hunched over, and even from behind him I can hear his labored breathing.\nClement是个瘦小的男人,长长的精灵耳是他最显眼的特征。我惊讶于他看上去如此苍老虚弱。他佝偻着背,即便在他身后,我都能听见他吃力的呼吸声。"

    old "I draw the knife from it's sheath, and hold it inches from his back."
    new "I draw the knife from it's sheath, and hold it inches from his back.\n我从鞘中抽出刀,举到他背脊几寸之处。"

    old "I place both hands around the handle of the knife and drive it into his back. It penetrates his flesh with frightening ease."
    new "I place both hands around the handle of the knife and drive it into his back. It penetrates his flesh with frightening ease.\n我双手握住刀柄,把刀捅进他的后背。刀刃穿透他的皮肉,轻松得令人心惊。"

    old "A noise begins emanating from his mouth, some kind of abominable wheezing sound. I twist the knife in his back, and blood begins to erupt from the wound as I twist it."
    new "A noise begins emanating from his mouth, some kind of abominable wheezing sound. I twist the knife in his back, and blood begins to erupt from the wound as I twist it.\n他嘴里开始发出声响,某种可怖的喘息声。我在他背上拧动刀子,鲜血随之从伤口喷涌而出。"

    old "Clement falls forward, knife still lodged in his back, and blood begins to pool around him. I place a finger on the side of his neck to check for a pulse, and feel nothing."
    new "Clement falls forward, knife still lodged in his back, and blood begins to pool around him. I place a finger on the side of his neck to check for a pulse, and feel nothing.\nClement向前栽倒,刀仍插在他背上,血开始在他身周汇成一片。我伸出手指探他颈侧,想查脉搏,却什么也摸不到。"

    old "Time for me to go."
    new "Time for me to go.\n我该走了。"

    old "I walk to the window. Kusho's already adjusted the height of the rope on the other side, and the rope is low angled downward toward the tree's lower branches, still high enough for me to clear the wall surrounding Clement's estate."
    new "I walk to the window. Kusho's already adjusted the height of the rope on the other side, and the rope is low angled downward toward the tree's lower branches, still high enough for me to clear the wall surrounding Clement's estate.\n我走到窗边。Kusho已在对侧调好了绳子的高度,绳子低低地向树下枝斜伸过去,高度仍足以让我越过Clement庄园的围墙。"

    old "I glance down at the courtyard below us, but the guards beneath seem completely oblivious to what is happening above them, and the fate that has just befallen their master."
    new "I glance down at the courtyard below us, but the guards beneath seem completely oblivious to what is happening above them, and the fate that has just befallen their master.\n我低头瞥了一眼下方的庭院,但底下的卫兵似乎对头顶发生的事,以及刚刚降临他们主人身上的命运,浑然不觉。"

    old "As I'm about to strike, Clement coughs. His rapid movement makes me miss the vital spot."
    new "As I'm about to strike, Clement coughs. His rapid movement makes me miss the vital spot.\n我正要动手,Clement咳嗽了一声。他身体猛地一动,让我错失了要害。"

    old "Before this man meets his maker, he at least deserves to see the face of his killer. I grab his shoulder and spin him around."
    new "Before this man meets his maker, he at least deserves to see the face of his killer. I grab his shoulder and spin him around.\n这个人去见造物主之前,至少该看看杀他之人的脸。我抓住他的肩膀,把他转了过来。"

    old "Terrance, wh-"
    new "Terrance, wh-\nTerrance,什——"

    old "He stops short at seeing my face, and his eyes look down to the knife in my hands."
    new "He stops short at seeing my face, and his eyes look down to the knife in my hands.\n看到我的脸,他骤然停住,目光落到我手中的刀上。"

    old "Oh gods. Oh gods, no. Not like this."
    new "Oh gods. Oh gods, no. Not like this.\n天哪。天哪,不。不要这样。"

    old "Clement lets out a wail, and I push him to the floor, covering his mouth with one hand and driving the knife into his chest with the other."
    new "Clement lets out a wail, and I push him to the floor, covering his mouth with one hand and driving the knife into his chest with the other.\nClement发出一声哀嚎,我把他推倒在地,一手捂住他的嘴,另一手把刀捅进他的胸膛。"

    old "Master Clement?"
    new "Master Clement?\nClement老爷?"

    old "I hear the voice of a young guard outside the door. I hold Clement down as he bleeds out, but the sounds of our struggle and his choking must be audible on the other side of the door."
    new "I hear the voice of a young guard outside the door. I hold Clement down as he bleeds out, but the sounds of our struggle and his choking must be audible on the other side of the door.\n我听见门外传来一个年轻卫兵的声音。我按住Clement,任他流血,但我们厮打和他窒息的声响,门那边一定听得见。"

    old "I pull the knife out of Clement's chest, and slash it across his throat to be sure the deed is done. As I stand, blade in hand, I hear the door open behind me."
    new "I pull the knife out of Clement's chest, and slash it across his throat to be sure the deed is done. As I stand, blade in hand, I hear the door open behind me.\n我把刀从Clement胸口拔出,又横着割过他的喉咙,确保事情办妥。我手握刀刃站起身时,听见身后的门开了。"

    old "Master—"
    new "Master—\n老爷——"

    old "I spin around and catch sight of a young guard. His gaze shifts from the blooded corpse on the floor to the knife in my hand."
    new "I spin around and catch sight of a young guard. His gaze shifts from the blooded corpse on the floor to the knife in my hand.\n我转身,看见一个年轻的卫兵。他的目光从地板上血淋淋的尸体,移到我手中的刀上。"

    old "The young man's face turns white, and his hands begin shaking. He reaches for his scabbard, and draws his sword, but his hands are shaking too much to grasp it, and his blade clatters to the ground. He stands before me, petrified and defenseless."
    new "The young man's face turns white, and his hands begin shaking. He reaches for his scabbard, and draws his sword, but his hands are shaking too much to grasp it, and his blade clatters to the ground. He stands before me, petrified and defenseless.\n年轻人的脸唰地白了,双手开始发抖。他伸手去摸剑鞘,抽出剑来,可双手抖得太厉害,握不住剑,剑哐当掉到地上。他站在我面前,惊恐无助。"

    old "This boy is no threat to my safety, and he clearly too shocked to offer any kind of pursuit. I turn around and head to the window."
    new "This boy is no threat to my safety, and he clearly too shocked to offer any kind of pursuit. I turn around and head to the window.\n这男孩威胁不到我的安全,也显然震惊得无力追来。我转身走向窗户。"

    old "As I'm about to leave, something whizzes past my head, and I flinch as it clips the edge of my ear."
    new "As I'm about to leave, something whizzes past my head, and I flinch as it clips the edge of my ear.\n我正要离开,有东西嗖地从我头边掠过,擦过耳沿,我不禁一缩。"

    old "I turn around. The young guard lies bleeding, a crossbow bolt stuck through his neck."
    new "I turn around. The young guard lies bleeding, a crossbow bolt stuck through his neck.\n我转过身。那年轻卫兵倒在地上流着血,一支弩箭贯穿了他的脖颈。"

    old "I look out the window, and see Kusho beckoning me. I guess you did have my back after all, Kusho."
    new "I look out the window, and see Kusho beckoning me. I guess you did have my back after all, Kusho.\n我朝窗外望去,看见Kusho在向我示意。我想你终究还是掩护了我,Kusho。"

    old "If Kusho and I are to escape this city, we can't have a group of guards chasing us. Even if we escape, the consequences of a crime this grave will eventually catch up to us if we are seen and identified. This guard is no threat to my immediate safety, but there's no telling what will happen if I allow him to live."
    new "If Kusho and I are to escape this city, we can't have a group of guards chasing us. Even if we escape, the consequences of a crime this grave will eventually catch up to us if we are seen and identified. This guard is no threat to my immediate safety, but there's no telling what will happen if I allow him to live.\n如果Kusho和我要逃出这座城市,就不能让一群卫兵追着我们跑。即便我们逃了,一旦被看见并被认出来,这桩重罪的后果终究会追上我们。这名卫兵威胁不到我眼前的安全,但若放他活命,谁也不知道会发生什么。"

    old "I lunge toward the boy, who crumbles to the ground as I drive the knife into his chest."
    new "I lunge toward the boy, who crumbles to the ground as I drive the knife into his chest.\n我扑向那男孩,把刀捅进他胸口时,他瘫倒在地。"

    old "Sorry."
    new "Sorry.\n对不起。"

    old "I pull the knife from his chest and slash his throat, just as I did with Clement. His body falls lifeless to the floor, and the room is silent as another pool of blood begins to form."
    new "I pull the knife from his chest and slash his throat, just as I did with Clement. His body falls lifeless to the floor, and the room is silent as another pool of blood begins to form.\n我从他胸口拔出刀,又割过他的喉咙,就像对Clement做的那样。他的身体毫无生气地倒在地上,又一片血泊开始蔓延,房间里一片死寂。"

    old "It's time for me to go now."
    new "It's time for me to go now.\n现在我真的该走了。"

    old "I grab the chain that I zipped in on, and loop it over the rope. I grab on tight and slide down the rope, into the waiting branches of the tree where Kusho remains perched."
    new "I grab the chain that I zipped in on, and loop it over the rope. I grab on tight and slide down the rope, into the waiting branches of the tree where Kusho remains perched.\n我抓起滑进来的那段链子,套在绳子上。我紧紧抓牢,顺绳滑下,落入Kusho仍栖身守候的树枝间。"

    old "You need to leave now. We'll split up. I'm headed back to the forest. You can meet me there in several days' time."
    new "You need to leave now. We'll split up. I'm headed back to the forest. You can meet me there in several days' time.\n你现在就得离开。我们分头走。我回林子里去,几天后你可以在那里和我碰面。"

    old "While I consider stealth and subtlety to be my greatest gifts, I don't want to tiptoe around the subject too tenderly, so I'll just come right out and ask. You have blood on your hands. How do you feel about that?"
    new "While I consider stealth and subtlety to be my greatest gifts, I don't want to tiptoe around the subject too tenderly, so I'll just come right out and ask. You have blood on your hands. How do you feel about that?\n虽然我把隐秘和机敏视作自己最了不起的天赋,但我不想在这话题上绕得太委婉,所以我就直说了。你手上沾了血。对此你感觉如何?"

    old "About killing Clement? Not the slightest hint of guilt. I consciously decided to do the deed myself, and I'd do it again. But that boy you killed...he didn't deserve that."
    new "About killing Clement? Not the slightest hint of guilt. I consciously decided to do the deed myself, and I'd do it again. But that boy you killed...he didn't deserve that.\n关于杀Clement?一点愧疚都没有。我是有意识地决定亲自下手,再让我选,我还会这么做。但你杀的那个男孩……他不该死。"

    old "That's part of being an assassin, [protag]. You don't always have the luxury of killing people who deserve to die. Assassins are not moral crusaders."
    new "That's part of being an assassin, [protag]. You don't always have the luxury of killing people who deserve to die. Assassins are not moral crusaders.\n这就是当刺客的一部分,[protag]。你并不总有余裕只杀该死之人。刺客不是道德十字军。"

    old "In fact, the dispassionate discipline of a paid assassin is about as far away from moral discipline as you can get. Some people say assassins are immoral people. I say they're amoral people."
    new "In fact, the dispassionate discipline of a paid assassin is about as far away from moral discipline as you can get. Some people say assassins are immoral people. I say they're amoral people.\n事实上,一个受雇刺客冷血的纪律,与道德纪律相去甚远。有人说刺客是不道德的人。我说他们是不讲道德的人。"

    old "Saying that an assassin is responsible for a man's death is no different than saying that the sword was. Ultimately, assassins are a tool, and moral must be laid on the person who originally sought to wield it."
    new "Saying that an assassin is responsible for a man's death is no different than saying that the sword was. Ultimately, assassins are a tool, and moral must be laid on the person who originally sought to wield it.\n说一个刺客对一个人的死负有责任,和说那把剑负有责任没什么两样。归根结底,刺客是工具,道德必须归于最初想使用这工具的人。"

    old "Do you know the real reason we killed Clement Nox? It has nothing to do with the fact that he beat his servants."
    new "Do you know the real reason we killed Clement Nox? It has nothing to do with the fact that he beat his servants.\n你知道我们杀Clement Nox的真正原因吗?和他殴打仆人毫无关系。"

    old "You lied to me?"
    new "You lied to me?\n你骗了我?"

    old "Everything I told you was true. Clement was an abusive master. But ending his abuse is little more than a pleasant side-effect."
    new "Everything I told you was true. Clement was an abusive master. But ending his abuse is little more than a pleasant side-effect.\n我告诉你的每句话都是真的。Clement是个虐待人的主子。但终结他的虐待,不过是个令人愉快的附带效果。"

    old "Clement Nox was like any other target. Someone wanted him dead, and they were willing to pay a generous sum to see him dead."
    new "Clement Nox was like any other target. Someone wanted him dead, and they were willing to pay a generous sum to see him dead.\nClement Nox和其他任何目标一样。有人想让他死,并愿意付一大笔钱看他死。"

    old "Who hired you?"
    new "Who hired you?\n谁雇的你?"

    old "Clement's son. Or, as he's now known, Lord Nox. He inherited the title when is father was killed."
    new "Clement's son. Or, as he's now known, Lord Nox. He inherited the title when is father was killed.\nClement的儿子。或者说,如今人们口中的Nox领主。他父亲被杀后,他继承了爵位。"

    old "Clement was the epitome of excessive living. The Nox estate was bleeding money with him at the helm. His son thought he could do a better job of steering the ship. So he hired me."
    new "Clement was the epitome of excessive living. The Nox estate was bleeding money with him at the helm. His son thought he could do a better job of steering the ship. So he hired me.\nClement是穷奢极欲的化身。有他掌舵,Nox庄园一直在失血。他儿子觉得自己能把船驶得更好,于是雇了我。"

    old "Make no mistake. We killed a wretched, abusive man. But his wretchedness and abusiveness is not the reason we killed him."
    new "Make no mistake. We killed a wretched, abusive man. But his wretchedness and abusiveness is not the reason we killed him.\n别弄错。我们杀了一个卑劣、暴虐的人。但他的卑劣与暴虐,不是我们杀他的原因。"

    old "And now he's been replaced with a pragmatic-minded killer, a man who desired wealth enough to kill his own father over it."
    new "And now he's been replaced with a pragmatic-minded killer, a man who desired wealth enough to kill his own father over it.\n如今他已被一个务实冷酷的杀手取代,一个贪图财富到足以为此弑父的人。"

    old "[protag], look at it from the perspective of the servants. For years, they tolerated a master who would beat them. Now, they have a master who is too profit-minded to waste time on spiteful activities like abuse. Which do you prefer? Is Clement's son really an evil man for what he did?"
    new "[protag], look at it from the perspective of the servants. For years, they tolerated a master who would beat them. Now, they have a master who is too profit-minded to waste time on spiteful activities like abuse. Which do you prefer? Is Clement's son really an evil man for what he did?\n[protag],从仆人的角度看吧。多年来,他们忍受着一个会殴打他们的主子。如今,他们有了个太精于逐利、不屑把时间浪费在虐待这种泄愤勾当上的主子。你更想要哪个?Clement的儿子真的就因为所做之事成了恶人吗?"

    old "[protag], I want you to be honest with me. I agreed to assist you in banishing the evil that surrounds N'Mar. I'm prepared to devote my attention to that goal. And, as a commanding officer of sorts, I feel I owe you a certain level of accountability, perhaps more than I've given you."
    new "[protag], I want you to be honest with me. I agreed to assist you in banishing the evil that surrounds N'Mar. I'm prepared to devote my attention to that goal. And, as a commanding officer of sorts, I feel I owe you a certain level of accountability, perhaps more than I've given you.\n[protag],我要你对我坦诚。我答应协助你驱逐N'Mar周围的邪恶。我已准备把精力投入那个目标。而作为某种意义上的指挥官,我觉得自己欠你一份交代,也许比我给过的更多。"

    old "I think that I can be an assassin and still fulfill my duties to you. After all, you wanted my help because I'm good at killing. I can't allow those skills to dull."
    new "I think that I can be an assassin and still fulfill my duties to you. After all, you wanted my help because I'm good at killing. I can't allow those skills to dull.\n我想我可以既当刺客,又履行对你的职责。毕竟,你需要我帮忙,是因为我擅长杀人。我不能让那些技艺荒废。"

    old "But if you think that I should abandon my career as an assassin, I will drop it, and make slaying the undead my sole focus, until the day that we see them vanquished."
    new "But if you think that I should abandon my career as an assassin, I will drop it, and make slaying the undead my sole focus, until the day that we see them vanquished.\n但如果你认为我该放弃刺客的生涯,我会放下它,把斩杀亡灵当作我唯一的重心,直到我们看着它们被消灭的那一天。"

    old "What would you have me do, [protag]?"
    new "What would you have me do, [protag]?\n你要我怎么做,[protag]?"

    old "I need you at your very best, Kusho. And in your case, being your very best means keeping your killer instinct sharp."
    new "I need you at your very best, Kusho. And in your case, being your very best means keeping your killer instinct sharp.\n我需要你拿出最佳状态,Kusho。而对你来说,拿出最佳状态,就意味着保持你杀手的本能锋锐。"

    old "Your profession as an assassin was enough to catch my eye and make you a target for recruitment. I feel that I would be a fool to give that up."
    new "Your profession as an assassin was enough to catch my eye and make you a target for recruitment. I feel that I would be a fool to give that up.\n你刺客的行当,足以让我注意到你,把你列为招募目标。我觉得放弃它才是愚蠢。"

    old "Kusho, you're a skilled assassin. That's how you caught my attention in the first place, and I won't deny that every time I see you work, I'm impressed with your skill."
    new "Kusho, you're a skilled assassin. That's how you caught my attention in the first place, and I won't deny that every time I see you work, I'm impressed with your skill.\nKusho,你是个技艺娴熟的刺客。这正是你最初引起我注意的原因,我也不否认,每次看你出手,我都被你的身手折服。"

    old "That being said, I feel that a man cannot serve two masters. If you really intend to give everything that you have to slay the undead, then you must forsake all other passions and pursuits until we achieve that goal."
    new "That being said, I feel that a man cannot serve two masters. If you really intend to give everything that you have to slay the undead, then you must forsake all other passions and pursuits until we achieve that goal.\n话虽如此,我觉得一个人不能侍奉两个主人。如果你真打算为斩杀亡灵倾尽所有,那就必须舍弃其他一切激情与追求,直到我们达成目标。"

    old "I want your focus on the mission at N'Mar. That is our purpose."
    new "I want your focus on the mission at N'Mar. That is our purpose.\n我要你把心思放在N'Mar的任务上。那是我们的目标。"

    old "Alright. I'll do it."
    new "Alright. I'll do it.\n好。我照做。"

    old "Oh, I almost forgot."
    new "Oh, I almost forgot.\n哦,我差点忘了。"

    old "Kusho pulls out a bag of coin and tosses it to me."
    new "Kusho pulls out a bag of coin and tosses it to me.\nKusho掏出一袋钱币,抛给了我。"

    old "Two thousand gold. I split the bounty two ways between us. You killed Clement, but I did the planning and had to get my own hands dirty in the end, so an even split down the middle seems fair."
    new "Two thousand gold. I split the bounty two ways between us. You killed Clement, but I did the planning and had to get my own hands dirty in the end, so an even split down the middle seems fair.\n两千金币。我把赏金分成了两份。Clement是你杀的,但计划是我定的,最后也不得不弄脏自己的手,所以对半分,似乎公平。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. It's good to see you. I have something for you."
    new "Ah, [protag]. It's good to see you. I have something for you.\n啊,[protag]。见到你真好。我有东西给你。"

    old "Kusho pulls a bag of coin out of his pocket and tosses it to me. I catch the bag and heft it."
    new "Kusho pulls a bag of coin out of his pocket and tosses it to me. I catch the bag and heft it.\nKusho从口袋里掏出一袋钱币抛给我。我接住钱袋,掂了掂。"

    old "What's this?"
    new "What's this?\n这是什么?"

    old "Your share. You assisted with the hit, so you get part of the commission. I thought a fifty-fifty split would be fair. That's two thousand gold for each of us."
    new "Your share. You assisted with the hit, so you get part of the commission. I thought a fifty-fifty split would be fair. That's two thousand gold for each of us.\n你的那份。你协助了这次刺杀,所以佣金有你一份。我想五五分成公平。我们每人两千金币。"

    old "Where did you get this money? Did you steal it from Clement's estate when you killed him?"
    new "Where did you get this money? Did you steal it from Clement's estate when you killed him?\n这钱你哪来的?是你杀他时从Clement的庄园里偷的?"

    old "I'm an assassin, not a burglar. I don't kill people so that I can steal from them. I kill for money. A client paid me to kill Clement Nox."
    new "I'm an assassin, not a burglar. I don't kill people so that I can steal from them. I kill for money. A client paid me to kill Clement Nox.\n我是刺客,不是窃贼。我杀人不是为了偷东西。我杀人是为了赚钱。是一个客户付钱让我杀Clement Nox。"

    old "I thought that we killed Clement Nox because of his cruelty to his servants."
    new "I thought that we killed Clement Nox because of his cruelty to his servants.\n我还以为我们杀Clement Nox,是因为他虐待仆人。"

    old "Ending the suffering of his underlings is just a side-effect. The real reason we killed Clement is that his son wanted him dead."
    new "Ending the suffering of his underlings is just a side-effect. The real reason we killed Clement is that his son wanted him dead.\n终结他手下的苦难,只是附带效果。我们杀Clement的真正原因,是他儿子想让他死。"

    old "Is there some father-son feud that I should know about?"
    new "Is there some father-son feud that I should know about?\n这里头有什么我该知道的父子恩怨吗?"

    old "Well, Clement was the lord of the Nox estate. His son wanted that title for himself. That about sums it up."
    new "Well, Clement was the lord of the Nox estate. His son wanted that title for himself. That about sums it up.\n嗯,Clement是Nox庄园的家主。他儿子想自己坐上那个位子。差不多就是这么回事。"

    old "His son is really quite a reasonable man. He's actually got a knack for accounting, and when he looked at the money his father was squandering foolishly year after year through poor management, and weighed it against my fee, the choice was obvious."
    new "His son is really quite a reasonable man. He's actually got a knack for accounting, and when he looked at the money his father was squandering foolishly year after year through poor management, and weighed it against my fee, the choice was obvious.\n他儿子其实是个相当通情达理的人。他真有记账的天赋,当他看着父亲年复一年因经营不善而愚蠢地挥霍掉的钱,再拿这笔钱与我的佣金一权衡,选择便显而易见了。"

    old "We killed a man for nothing more than profit?"
    new "We killed a man for nothing more than profit?\n我们杀一个人,仅仅是为了赚钱?"

    old "Killing people for profit is what assassins do, [protag]. I hope you're not realizing this just now."
    new "Killing people for profit is what assassins do, [protag]. I hope you're not realizing this just now.\n为钱杀人,正是刺客的本行,[protag]。我希望你不是现在才意识到这点。"

    old "I meant your client. All the while, I thought we were doing this to lift the yoke from the shoulders of abused servants, when in fact the only benefactor was a man so greedy that he'd kill his own father in the interest of saving money."
    new "I meant your client. All the while, I thought we were doing this to lift the yoke from the shoulders of abused servants, when in fact the only benefactor was a man so greedy that he'd kill his own father in the interest of saving money.\n我是指你的委托人。一直以来,我以为我们这么做,是为了卸下受虐仆人肩上的枷锁,可事实上,唯一的受益者是个贪婪到为了省钱不惜弑父的人。"

    old "I wouldn't say that's true. While the Nox servants are certainly not directly involved with the transaction that was carried out, they are certainly interested parties. And as far as they're concerned, Clement may as well have been killed by a disgruntled servant."
    new "I wouldn't say that's true. While the Nox servants are certainly not directly involved with the transaction that was carried out, they are certainly interested parties. And as far as they're concerned, Clement may as well have been killed by a disgruntled servant.\n我不会说那是真的。虽然Nox的仆人们当然没有直接参与这笔已完成的交易,但他们无疑是利益相关方。就他们而言,Clement完全可能是被一个心怀不满的仆人杀死的。"

    old "But he wasn't. You and I know the truth."
    new "But he wasn't. You and I know the truth.\n但他不是。你我都知道真相。"

    old "Suppose you were one of the servants. One day, your master who beats you is slain, and a new master, one who doesn't abuse you, steps up to take his place. Does it really matter to you whether the man who killed your old master did it for noble or selfish reasons?"
    new "Suppose you were one of the servants. One day, your master who beats you is slain, and a new master, one who doesn't abuse you, steps up to take his place. Does it really matter to you whether the man who killed your old master did it for noble or selfish reasons?\n假设你是仆人之一。有一天,殴打你的主子被杀了,一个不再虐待你的新主子接替了他的位置。那个杀掉你旧主子的人,是出于高尚还是自私的原因,对你来说真的重要吗?"

    old "Do you think that those servants would protest the death of their old abusive master if they knew the truth?"
    new "Do you think that those servants would protest the death of their old abusive master if they knew the truth?\n你觉得那些仆人,如果知道了真相,会为旧主子之死鸣不平吗?"

    old "No, but their new master is a killer. He killed to make himself rich."
    new "No, but their new master is a killer. He killed to make himself rich.\n不会,但他们的新主子是个杀手。他杀人是为了让自己发财。"

    old "You say that like it's a bad thing. [protag], do you even know who you're talking to? Killing people for money is literally my job. You were a part of that hit too, lest you forget. What you've just learned doesn't change things at all."
    new "You say that like it's a bad thing. [protag], do you even know who you're talking to? Killing people for money is literally my job. You were a part of that hit too, lest you forget. What you've just learned doesn't change things at all.\n你说得好像那是坏事。[protag],你知道你在跟谁说话吗?为了钱杀人,说白了就是我的工作。那次刺杀你也有份,别忘喽。你刚刚得知的事,根本改变不了什么。"

    old "Any pretenses under which you accepted that job, those were real. I never lied to you about the nature of Clement's relationship with his underlings."
    new "Any pretenses under which you accepted that job, those were real. I never lied to you about the nature of Clement's relationship with his underlings.\n你当初接受那活儿时所依凭的理由,都是真的。关于Clement与他手下的关系,我从没骗过你。"

    old "To be honest, I'm a bit surprised we're even having this conversation. You know that I'm an assassin. I kill the marks I'm paid to kill."
    new "To be honest, I'm a bit surprised we're even having this conversation. You know that I'm an assassin. I kill the marks I'm paid to kill.\n说实话,我们居然会聊起这个,我有点意外。你知道我是刺客。我杀那些付钱要我杀的目标。"

    old "I thought I'd check in on you. Since you seem to be an expert in the realm of death, I thought I'd consult you on something."
    new "I thought I'd check in on you. Since you seem to be an expert in the realm of death, I thought I'd consult you on something.\n我想来看看你。既然你似乎是死亡领域的行家,我想就某件事请教你。"

    old "Well, I'm not sure how helpful I will be, but feel free to query me."
    new "Well, I'm not sure how helpful I will be, but feel free to query me.\n嗯,我不确定能帮上多少忙,但你尽管问。"

    old "A few days back, a Triberg nobleman was found dead in his estate. All signs point to some kind of internal feud. It seems that one of his own men killed him, probably out of spite or hatred for their cruel master."
    new "A few days back, a Triberg nobleman was found dead in his estate. All signs point to some kind of internal feud. It seems that one of his own men killed him, probably out of spite or hatred for their cruel master.\n几天前,一位Triberg贵族被发现死在自己的庄园里。种种迹象都指向某种内部恩怨。似乎是他的一个手下杀了他,多半是出于对那位残忍主子的怨恨或憎恶。"

    old "And what do you think?"
    new "And what do you think?\n那你怎么看?"

    old "I think that maybe you might know something about what happened there."
    new "I think that maybe you might know something about what happened there.\n我想,你也许知道那里发生了什么。"

    old "So, the question is: do you?"
    new "So, the question is: do you?\n那么,问题来了:你知道吗?"

    old "Well, before I answer your question, I'd like to point a question back at you. Do you want to know? Suppose that you found out that someone you associate was responsible for killing an unarmed man, a nobleman, a weak and defenseless civilian who was caught unawares in his own home. Could you deal with that?"
    new "Well, before I answer your question, I'd like to point a question back at you. Do you want to know? Suppose that you found out that someone you associate was responsible for killing an unarmed man, a nobleman, a weak and defenseless civilian who was caught unawares in his own home. Could you deal with that?\n嗯,在我回答你的问题之前,我想先回敬一个问题。你想知道吗?假设你发现你认识的某个人,要为杀死一个手无寸铁的人负责——一个贵族,一个在自己家中毫无防备、虚弱无力的平民。你能承受得了吗?"

    old "Do I strike you as the kind of person who's made weak in the knees when staring into the face of a known killer? You're an assassin, Kusho. That's what you do. Do you think that adding one more to your body count would really upset me that much?"
    new "Do I strike you as the kind of person who's made weak in the knees when staring into the face of a known killer? You're an assassin, Kusho. That's what you do. Do you think that adding one more to your body count would really upset me that much?\n我看起来像是那种,直面一个众所周知杀手时就会吓得腿软的人吗?你是刺客,Kusho。这就是你的本行。你以为再往你的杀人名单上添一个,真会让我那么不安吗?"

    old "No, I don't suppose it would."
    new "No, I don't suppose it would.\n不,我想不会。"

    old "Well, I'll tell you, then. I killed Clement Nox. I stabbed him with a knife taken from his own armory, identical to the one each of his men carry. I stabbed him repeatedly, multiple times, a very sloppy job, to make it look like an act of passion, rather than the act of a trained killer."
    new "Well, I'll tell you, then. I killed Clement Nox. I stabbed him with a knife taken from his own armory, identical to the one each of his men carry. I stabbed him repeatedly, multiple times, a very sloppy job, to make it look like an act of passion, rather than the act of a trained killer.\n那我就告诉你。Clement Nox是我杀的。我用一把从他自家军械库取来的刀捅了他,那刀和他的手下人人所佩的一模一样。我反复捅了他好几次,手法十分粗糙,好让它看起来像一时冲动所为,而非训练有素的杀手所为。"

    old "Why did you do it?"
    new "Why did you do it?\n你为什么这么做?"

    old "Why did I kill Clement Nox? Killing is what I do. I'm an assassin, [protag]."
    new "Why did I kill Clement Nox? Killing is what I do. I'm an assassin, [protag].\n为什么杀Clement Nox?杀人就是我的本行。我是刺客,[protag]。"

    old "This isn't what you normally do. You're normally the type to leave a calling card."
    new "This isn't what you normally do. You're normally the type to leave a calling card.\n这不像你平常的作风。你通常都会留下招牌的。"

    old "It's true. Killing a man like Clement Nox, in the way I killed him, is a bit different from what I'm used to doing as a paid assassin. In fact, since the hit, I've decided that it will be my last for awhile."
    new "It's true. Killing a man like Clement Nox, in the way I killed him, is a bit different from what I'm used to doing as a paid assassin. In fact, since the hit, I've decided that it will be my last for awhile.\n不错。用我杀他的那种方式,杀Clement Nox这样的人,与我当受雇刺客的惯常做法有些不同。事实上,自那次刺杀起,我已决定,这将是未来一段时间内的最后一单。"

    old "Killing is my profession, but I am not a man who is driven solely by money. For many years, killing was a passion. And I considered myself a fortunate man, to find myself in a position where I could be paid for doing something which I enjoyed very much."
    new "Killing is my profession, but I am not a man who is driven solely by money. For many years, killing was a passion. And I considered myself a fortunate man, to find myself in a position where I could be paid for doing something which I enjoyed very much.\n杀人是我的职业,但我不是个只受金钱驱使的人。多年来,杀人是一种激情。我也自认幸运,竟能置身于靠做自己乐在其中的事来赚钱的境地。"

    old "A man needs a mission. A purpose in life. And odd is it may seem, during my last hit I realized that a new passion consumed my attention. I have you to blame for that."
    new "A man needs a mission. A purpose in life. And odd is it may seem, during my last hit I realized that a new passion consumed my attention. I have you to blame for that.\n一个人需要使命,需要人生的目标。说来也许奇怪,但在上一次刺杀中,我意识到一股新的激情攫住了我的全部心神。这都得怪你。"

    old "Bringing unrest to the undead is now my mission. My days of stalking the living are over, at least for the time being."
    new "Bringing unrest to the undead is now my mission. My days of stalking the living are over, at least for the time being.\n给亡灵带去不安,如今成了我的使命。我跟踪活人的日子结束了,至少暂时如此。"

    old "You know, it's quite funny. My entire life, I've been obsessed with the puzzle of how to most effectively end a man's life. And with that goal in mind, I've amassed a rather substantial collection of tools to aid in that pursuit. In fact, much of what I've earned from killing, I've invested in myself, aiming to become a more effective killer."
    new "You know, it's quite funny. My entire life, I've been obsessed with the puzzle of how to most effectively end a man's life. And with that goal in mind, I've amassed a rather substantial collection of tools to aid in that pursuit. In fact, much of what I've earned from killing, I've invested in myself, aiming to become a more effective killer.\n你知道吗,挺有意思的。我这一生,都痴迷于如何最有效地终结一个人的性命这个难题。怀着这个目标,我攒下了一大批工具,来助力这份追求。事实上,我杀人挣来的钱,大多投在了自己身上,只为成为更厉害的杀手。"

    old "But ever since I joined your mission, I've had a chance to open my eyes to a much wider array of tools. And considering that I am, at least tentatively, retiring as an assassin, I've decided to devote some of my resources to that end."
    new "But ever since I joined your mission, I've had a chance to open my eyes to a much wider array of tools. And considering that I am, at least tentatively, retiring as an assassin, I've decided to devote some of my resources to that end.\n但自从加入你的任务,我有机会见识了广得多的工具。考虑到我——至少暂时——从刺客一行退休了,我决定把一部分资源投向那个方向。"

    old "How, exactly?"
    new "How, exactly?\n具体怎么投?"

    old "What I'm saying is that I've bought myself a new toy."
    new "What I'm saying is that I've bought myself a new toy.\n我是说,我给自己买了件新玩具。"

    old "Kusho holds up a cloth, and adorns his arm with it for effect."
    new "Kusho holds up a cloth, and adorns his arm with it for effect.\nKusho举起一块布,为展示效果,把它缠在了自己手臂上。"

    old "What does someone like you want with something like this? What is it, exactly?"
    new "What does someone like you want with something like this? What is it, exactly?\n像你这样的人,要这种东西做什么?这到底是什么?"

    old "It's a bracer."
    new "It's a bracer.\n是个护腕。"

    old "I can understand why a bowman like you would have a bracer. In fact, I'm surprised that you don't wear one more regularly, and I'm even more curious about the lack of scarring on your forearm if you do all of your shooting with bare arms."
    new "I can understand why a bowman like you would have a bracer. In fact, I'm surprised that you don't wear one more regularly, and I'm even more curious about the lack of scarring on your forearm if you do all of your shooting with bare arms.\n我能理解你这样的弓手会配护腕。事实上,我惊讶的是你竟不常戴,而我更好奇的是,如果你一直光着前臂射箭,前臂上怎么没有疤痕。"

    old "While I'm certainly glad to see you taking personal safety seriously, this 'bracer' as you call it hardly seems something I would trust to protect your arm. Any arrow that hits it would rip it to shreds. If you want a bracer, might I suggest leather?"
    new "While I'm certainly glad to see you taking personal safety seriously, this 'bracer' as you call it hardly seems something I would trust to protect your arm. Any arrow that hits it would rip it to shreds. If you want a bracer, might I suggest leather?\n我当然很高兴看到你认真对待个人安全,但这个你所谓的“护腕”,我看未必能护住你的手臂。任何箭射上去都会把它撕成碎片。若你想要护腕,要不要我建议用皮革的?"

    old "Perhaps calling it a bracer is a bit deceptive. It's not intended to protect my arm. As you noted, I can handle a bow well enough to shoot an arrow without clipping my forearm."
    new "Perhaps calling it a bracer is a bit deceptive. It's not intended to protect my arm. As you noted, I can handle a bow well enough to shoot an arrow without clipping my forearm.\n也许叫它护腕有点误导。它并不是用来护我手臂的。正如你所指出的,我弓术够好,射箭不会擦到前臂。"

    old "So what's it for, then?"
    new "So what's it for, then?\n那它是干什么用的?"

    old "This cloth once belonged to a monk."
    new "This cloth once belonged to a monk.\n这块布,曾属于一位僧侣。"

    old "Did you..."
    new "Did you...\n你不会……"

    old "Don't worry, he parted with the cloth willingly. I'm an assassin, not a robber. He traded the cloth to a merchant, who traded it to another merchant, and so on and so forth until it eventually made its way to me."
    new "Don't worry, he parted with the cloth willingly. I'm an assassin, not a robber. He traded the cloth to a merchant, who traded it to another merchant, and so on and so forth until it eventually made its way to me.\n别担心,他是自愿与这块布分开的。我是刺客,不是强盗。他把布卖给了商人,商人又卖给了另一个商人,如此辗转,最终到了我手上。"

    old "I'm not adept in the ways of magic, but the monk who owned it before me must have known a thing or two about vanquishing the foul, because when I wear this bracer, if I knock my arrow just right so that it all but grazes the cloth, it gains a certain luminescence. You might say that it allows me to shoot holy arrows."
    new "I'm not adept in the ways of magic, but the monk who owned it before me must have known a thing or two about vanquishing the foul, because when I wear this bracer, if I knock my arrow just right so that it all but grazes the cloth, it gains a certain luminescence. You might say that it allows me to shoot holy arrows.\n我虽不谙魔法之道,但在我之前拥有它的那位僧侣,想必对除魔驱邪略知一二,因为当我戴上这个护腕,只要把箭恰到好处地搭好,让它几乎擦过这块布,它就会泛起某种微光。你大可以说,它让我能射出神圣之箭。"

    old "That's quite a useful trick."
    new "That's quite a useful trick.\n这招倒真有用。"

    old "Indeed it is, and unfortunately it will have to remain a trick. I can't reproduce the holy arrows with any sense of regularity. Sometimes, even the slightest breeze, or a single drop of sweat, causes me to just barely miss that sweet spot—or hit it."
    new "Indeed it is, and unfortunately it will have to remain a trick. I can't reproduce the holy arrows with any sense of regularity. Sometimes, even the slightest breeze, or a single drop of sweat, causes me to just barely miss that sweet spot—or hit it.\n确实,只可惜它终究只能是个小把戏。我没法稳定地再现神圣之箭。有时,哪怕一丝微风,或者一滴汗,都会让我差之毫厘地错过——或击中——那个恰到好处的点。"

    old "Still, a bracer that allows you to shoot holy arrows even a small portion of the time—that's got to be a useful weapon against the undead, don't you think?"
    new "Still, a bracer that allows you to shoot holy arrows even a small portion of the time—that's got to be a useful weapon against the undead, don't you think?\n不过,一个能让你即便只有一小部分时间射出神圣之箭的护腕——那对付亡灵一定很有用,你不觉得吗?"

    old "It sounds intriguing, Kusho. Only time will tell, but my intuition tells me that you've just made a very worthwhile investment."
    new "It sounds intriguing, Kusho. Only time will tell, but my intuition tells me that you've just made a very worthwhile investment.\n听起来很诱人,Kusho。只有时间能证明,但我的直觉告诉我,你刚做了一笔非常值得的投资。"

    old "Kusho. Up to anything new recently?"
    new "Kusho. Up to anything new recently?\nKusho。最近有什么新动静吗?"

    old "No new jobs as of late. But I did recently acquire some new hardware, purchased from the gray market with some of the earnings of my most recent kill."
    new "No new jobs as of late. But I did recently acquire some new hardware, purchased from the gray market with some of the earnings of my most recent kill.\n近来没有新活儿。不过我最近从灰市上添置了些新装备,用的是我最近一单杀人的部分收入。"

    old "You assassinate people, to get better gear, to make yourself better at assassinating people."
    new "You assassinate people, to get better gear, to make yourself better at assassinating people.\n你靠暗杀赚钱,买更好的装备,好让自己更擅长暗杀。"

    old "Of course. The best investment that a man can make is in himself, but the second best investment that he can make is in his tools."
    new "Of course. The best investment that a man can make is in himself, but the second best investment that he can make is in his tools.\n当然。一个人能做的最好投资,是投资自己;而第二好的投资,是投资他的工具。"

    old "So, what's your newest acquisition?"
    new "So, what's your newest acquisition?\n那么,你最新的收获是什么?"

    old "Kusho points to his feet, which are adorned in what appears to be a pair of thick socks."
    new "Kusho points to his feet, which are adorned in what appears to be a pair of thick socks.\nKusho指了指自己的脚,脚上穿着一双看起来挺厚的袜子。"

    old "Nice socks."
    new "Nice socks.\n袜子不错。"

    old "They're called tabi, or so the merchant I purchased them from claims. They're spun by craftsman hailing from the far east. Note the separated toes. They're really quite marvelous."
    new "They're called tabi, or so the merchant I purchased them from claims. They're spun by craftsman hailing from the far east. Note the separated toes. They're really quite marvelous.\n它们叫足袋,至少卖给我的商人是这么说的。由来自远东的工匠织就。看这分开的脚趾。真是妙极了。"

    old "They provide flexibility of movement while cushioning against rough or jagged surfaces, and the padding also allows me to move silently in them."
    new "They provide flexibility of movement while cushioning against rough or jagged surfaces, and the padding also allows me to move silently in them.\n它们让动作更灵活,又能缓冲粗糙崎岖的地面,这层软垫也让我能穿着它们悄无声息地行走。"

    old "Moving silently is great. Being agile as you move silently is even better. I've fallen in love with this pair of tabi. It took some time for me to learn how to walk in them, but it's time well spent."
    new "Moving silently is great. Being agile as you move silently is even better. I've fallen in love with this pair of tabi. It took some time for me to learn how to walk in them, but it's time well spent.\n悄无声息地行动很棒。在悄无声息的同时保持敏捷,就更棒了。我爱上了这双足袋。我花了些时间才学会穿着它走路,但这时间花得值。"

    old "Look at this. I can even grasp things with my feet while wearing these. I can actually feel the texture of the surfaces that I walk on. My gratitude to whoever came up with the idea for these."
    new "Look at this. I can even grasp things with my feet while wearing these. I can actually feel the texture of the surfaces that I walk on. My gratitude to whoever came up with the idea for these.\n瞧这个。穿着它们,我甚至能用脚抓住东西。我还能真切感受到所走地面的质地。我得感谢想出这玩意儿的人。"

    old "They look rather odd."
    new "They look rather odd.\n它们看起来怪怪的。"

    old "The entire point of wearing these is that I don't have to care how I look, because I'm so silent. They should assist me both in striking foes unawares, and avoiding damaging blows in combat if I find myself forced to defend."
    new "The entire point of wearing these is that I don't have to care how I look, because I'm so silent. They should assist me both in striking foes unawares, and avoiding damaging blows in combat if I find myself forced to defend.\n穿它们的全部意义,就在于我不必在乎自己看起来如何,因为我实在太安静了。它们既能帮我偷袭敌人,也能在我被迫防守时,帮我避开致命的打击。"

    old "I can't say that I'm jealous of your new toy. But I am glad to see that you're acquiring new tools."
    new "I can't say that I'm jealous of your new toy. But I am glad to see that you're acquiring new tools.\n我不敢说羡慕你的新玩具。但我很高兴看到你在添置新工具。"

    old "I find Kusho in the forest, bow in hand, engaging in some old-fashioned target practice."
    new "I find Kusho in the forest, bow in hand, engaging in some old-fashioned target practice.\n我在林子里找到Kusho,他手持弓箭,正进行着老式的打靶练习。"

    old "Good to see you're still staying sharp."
    new "Good to see you're still staying sharp.\n很高兴看到你仍保持身手。"

    old "Indeed. I've got a new toy to play with, and I want to make sure I'm prepared to use it effectively before we carry it into battle."
    new "Indeed. I've got a new toy to play with, and I want to make sure I'm prepared to use it effectively before we carry it into battle.\n确实。我有件新玩具要试,我想确保在带上它上战场前,能熟练运用。"

    old "What's your new toy?"
    new "What's your new toy?\n你的新玩具是什么?"

    old "Indeed it is, and unfortunately it will have to remain a trick. I can't reproduce the holy arrows with any sense of regularity. Sometimes, even the slightest breeze, or a single drop of sweat, causes me to just barely miss that sweet spot-or hit it."
    new "Indeed it is, and unfortunately it will have to remain a trick. I can't reproduce the holy arrows with any sense of regularity. Sometimes, even the slightest breeze, or a single drop of sweat, causes me to just barely miss that sweet spot-or hit it.\n确实,只可惜它终究只能是个小把戏。我没法稳定地再现神圣之箭。有时,哪怕一丝微风,或者一滴汗,都会让我差之毫厘地错过——或击中——那个恰到好处的点。"

    old "Still, a bracer that allows you to shoot holy arrows even a small portion of the time-that's got to be a useful weapon against the undead, don't you think?"
    new "Still, a bracer that allows you to shoot holy arrows even a small portion of the time-that's got to be a useful weapon against the undead, don't you think?\n不过,一个能让你即便只有一小部分时间射出神圣之箭的护腕——那对付亡灵一定很有用,你不觉得吗?"

    old "Kusho?"
    new "Kusho?\nKusho?"

    old "Kusho turns to face me and nods."
    new "Kusho turns to face me and nods.\nKusho转过身面向我,点了点头。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. It's you."
    new "Ah, [protag]. It's you.\n啊,[protag]。是你啊。"

    old "What are you doing?"
    new "What are you doing?\n你在做什么?"

    old "Hunting."
    new "Hunting.\n狩猎。"

    old "Really? Because to me, it looks like you're sitting alone doing nothing."
    new "Really? Because to me, it looks like you're sitting alone doing nothing.\n真的?因为在我看来,你只是独自坐着,什么都没干。"

    old "[protag], I want you to come close, stop talking and listen."
    new "[protag], I want you to come close, stop talking and listen.\n[protag],我想让你靠近点,别说话,仔细听。"

    old "Listen to what?"
    new "Listen to what?\n听什么?"

    old "Just be silent for a moment, and tell me what you hear."
    new "Just be silent for a moment, and tell me what you hear.\n先安静一会儿,然后告诉我你听到了什么。"

    old "Alright, Kusho."
    new "Alright, Kusho.\n好吧,Kusho。"

    old "What do you hear?"
    new "What do you hear?\n你听到了什么?"

    old "I hear nothing."
    new "I hear nothing.\n我什么也没听到。"

    old "Then you're not really listening. Close your eyes and tell me what you hear."
    new "Then you're not really listening. Close your eyes and tell me what you hear.\n那你并没有真的在听。闭上眼睛,告诉我你听到了什么。"

    old "I shut my eyes and listen for any sounds around me. I hear the sound of rustling leaves overhead."
    new "I shut my eyes and listen for any sounds around me. I hear the sound of rustling leaves overhead.\n我闭上眼,聆听四周的一切声响。我听见头顶树叶沙沙作响的声音。"

    old "I hear the sound of the wind blowing through the tree branches above us."
    new "I hear the sound of the wind blowing through the tree branches above us.\n我听见风穿过我们头顶树枝的声音。"

    old "Very good. Listen more."
    new "Very good. Listen more.\n很好。继续听。"

    old "I stay still, and after several moments I can hear the sounds of birds chirping and wildlife moving through the forest."
    new "I stay still, and after several moments I can hear the sounds of birds chirping and wildlife moving through the forest.\n我静静不动,片刻之后,能听见鸟鸣声和野生动物在林中穿行的声音。"

    old "I hear birds and small animals."
    new "I hear birds and small animals.\n我听到了鸟和许多小动物的声音。"

    old "Good, good. You can open your eyes now."
    new "Good, good. You can open your eyes now.\n好,很好。现在可以睁开眼睛了。"

    old "What was the point of that?"
    new "What was the point of that?\n这有什么意义?"

    old "The birds and other small woodland animals are a signal. When a possible threat approaches, they get quiet."
    new "The birds and other small woodland animals are a signal. When a possible threat approaches, they get quiet.\n鸟类和其他小型林间动物是一种信号。当可能的威胁逼近时,它们会安静下来。"

    old "You may recall that at first, you heard nothing, not even the chirping of birds. Do you know why that was?"
    new "You may recall that at first, you heard nothing, not even the chirping of birds. Do you know why that was?\n你也许还记得,起初你什么都没听到,连鸟鸣都没有。你知道那是为什么吗?"

    old "They heard something that threatened them?"
    new "They heard something that threatened them?\n它们听到了什么威胁它们的东西?"

    old "Yes. Specifically, they heard you. That's how I could sense your approach so easily. Even before you were close enough to hear me, I could tell that something was approaching just by the absence of sound around me."
    new "Yes. Specifically, they heard you. That's how I could sense your approach so easily. Even before you were close enough to hear me, I could tell that something was approaching just by the absence of sound around me.\n对。具体地说,它们听到了你。正因如此,我才能那么轻易地察觉你靠近。甚至在你近到能听见我之前,仅凭周围声音的消失,我就知道有东西正在靠近。"

    old "This is what I was doing before you arrived. Hearing the sounds of the forest. Listening to what it has to tell me."
    new "This is what I was doing before you arrived. Hearing the sounds of the forest. Listening to what it has to tell me.\n这就是你到来之前我在做的事。聆听森林的声音。倾听它要告诉我的事。"

    old "To you, it may look like I am doing nothing. But this is part of how I hunt."
    new "To you, it may look like I am doing nothing. But this is part of how I hunt.\n在你看来,我可能像是什么都没做。但这正是我狩猎方式的一部分。"

    old "What are you hunting, exactly?"
    new "What are you hunting, exactly?\n你究竟在猎什么?"

    old "I've encountered several bears in this part of the forest, and bears always make for a good kill. Plenty of meat, and bear skins always make a nice trophy."
    new "I've encountered several bears in this part of the forest, and bears always make for a good kill. Plenty of meat, and bear skins always make a nice trophy.\n我在这片林子遇到过好几头熊,而熊总是不错的猎物。肉多,熊皮也总能做成漂亮的战利品。"

    old "So you're just waiting for a bear to creep up on you? That sounds...stressful."
    new "So you're just waiting for a bear to creep up on you? That sounds...stressful.\n所以你只是等着熊悄悄靠近你?这听起来……压力不小。"

    old "There's nothing stressful about it. I know that if a bear and I come to blows, I'll be the one to win."
    new "There's nothing stressful about it. I know that if a bear and I come to blows, I'll be the one to win.\n没什么可紧张的。我知道,若我与熊正面交锋,赢的会是我。"

    old "Do you ever find yourself overcome by anxiety, though? All you're doing is waiting for the moment when your adversary will make their presence known."
    new "Do you ever find yourself overcome by anxiety, though? All you're doing is waiting for the moment when your adversary will make their presence known.\n不过,你有没有感到过焦虑呢?你所做的,只是等待对手现身的那一刻。"

    old "No, I don't find myself getting anxious. The forest often speaks to me in reassuring tones as I wait."
    new "No, I don't find myself getting anxious. The forest often speaks to me in reassuring tones as I wait.\n不,我不会感到焦虑。我等待时,森林常以令人安心的语调与我交谈。"

    old "Just waiting here for your prey to walk by seems quite boring."
    new "Just waiting here for your prey to walk by seems quite boring.\n只是坐在这里等猎物经过,似乎挺无聊的。"

    old "I don't find it boring. I have the forest here to keep me company."
    new "I don't find it boring. I have the forest here to keep me company.\n我不觉得无聊。有森林在这里陪着我。"

    old "I already told you, [protag]. When I sit and listen to what the forest has to tell me, it is much like sitting down with a friend and listening to what they have to say."
    new "I already told you, [protag]. When I sit and listen to what the forest has to tell me, it is much like sitting down with a friend and listening to what they have to say.\n我已经告诉过你了,[protag]。当我坐下倾听森林要对我说的话时,那很像与朋友坐在一起,听他诉说。"

    old "I thought you were just waiting on the forest to tell you when someone or something had shown up."
    new "I thought you were just waiting on the forest to tell you when someone or something had shown up.\n我还以为你只是在等森林告诉你,是否有人或什么东西出现了。"

    old "The forest tells me lots of things. Sometimes it's telling me that a large predatory has arrived. Other times, the forest is just telling me what is happening today."
    new "The forest tells me lots of things. Sometimes it's telling me that a large predatory has arrived. Other times, the forest is just telling me what is happening today.\n森林告诉我许多事。有时它告诉我,有头大型猛兽来了。另一些时候,森林只是告诉我今天正发生着什么。"

    old "The birds have many different songs, you know. You can tell their mood by the songs they sing."
    new "The birds have many different songs, you know. You can tell their mood by the songs they sing.\n你知道吗,鸟儿有许多不同的歌。通过它们唱的歌,你能听出它们的心情。"

    old "What's today's song like?"
    new "What's today's song like?\n今天的歌怎么样?"

    old "It's one of the more melancholy ones, unfortunately. It seems to be a recent trend. Coincidentally, I noticed the birds seemed to be more pessimistic around the time that you first showed up..."
    new "It's one of the more melancholy ones, unfortunately. It seems to be a recent trend. Coincidentally, I noticed the birds seemed to be more pessimistic around the time that you first showed up...\n很不巧,是较为忧伤的一首。这似乎是近来的一种趋势。巧合的是,我注意到大约在你头一回出现的时候,鸟儿们似乎就变得更悲观了……"

    old "You don't think I'm responsible, do you?"
    new "You don't think I'm responsible, do you?\n你不会觉得这是我的责任吧?"

    old "No, of course not. The birds changed their tune shortly before you became a regular visitor to this forest. But hearing the birds sing to each other in upset tones, it does fill me with a certain sense of determination."
    new "No, of course not. The birds changed their tune shortly before you became a regular visitor to this forest. But hearing the birds sing to each other in upset tones, it does fill me with a certain sense of determination.\n不,当然不是。鸟儿们在你成为这片林子的常客之前不久,就改了调子。但听到鸟儿们用不安的调子彼此鸣唱,我内心确实涌起某种决心。"

    old "I don't think it's any coincidence that the birds changed their tune when the blight began creeping across the land. It makes me all the more certain that volunteering to join you and fight by your side in N'Mar was the right choice."
    new "I don't think it's any coincidence that the birds changed their tune when the blight began creeping across the land. It makes me all the more certain that volunteering to join you and fight by your side in N'Mar was the right choice.\n我不认为疫病开始在大地上蔓延时,鸟儿们改调子是巧合。这让我更加确信,自愿加入你们,在N'Mar与你并肩作战,是正确的选择。"

    old "I'm glad to hear it, Kusho."
    new "I'm glad to hear it, Kusho.\n听你这么说我很高兴,Kusho。"

    old "I spot Kusho in the distance. He seems to be training with his bow."
    new "I spot Kusho in the distance. He seems to be training with his bow.\n我望见远处的Kusho。他似乎正用弓训练。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. Come close and watch. You might learn a thing or two."
    new "Ah, [protag]. Come close and watch. You might learn a thing or two.\n啊,[protag]。走近来看。你也许能学上一两招。"

    old "Bows aren't really my thing. I prefer more close combat."
    new "Bows aren't really my thing. I prefer more close combat.\n弓不是我的菜。我更喜欢近身格斗。"

    old "To each his own. Personally, I like to watch those undead fall into pieces at a safe distance from me. I've never been fond of the 'up close and personal' approach that some assassins take."
    new "To each his own. Personally, I like to watch those undead fall into pieces at a safe distance from me. I've never been fond of the 'up close and personal' approach that some assassins take.\n各有所好吧。就我个人而言,我喜欢看着那些亡灵在离我安全距离之外碎成片。有些刺客爱用的“贴身亲近”打法,我从来都不感冒。"

    old "Kusho shots three arrows in rapid succession. Each one hits the center of the target."
    new "Kusho shots three arrows in rapid succession. Each one hits the center of the target.\nKusho连射三箭,箭箭命中靶心。"

    old "Ha! I'd thank you for the compliment, but you simply witnessed my skills at work. This is nothing exceptional for me."
    new "Ha! I'd thank you for the compliment, but you simply witnessed my skills at work. This is nothing exceptional for me.\n哈!我倒要谢谢你的夸奖,但你不过是亲眼目睹了我的本事。这对我来说稀松平常。"

    old "Modesty isn't really one of your strength, isn't it Kusho?"
    new "Modesty isn't really one of your strength, isn't it Kusho?\n谦虚实在不是你的强项之一,不是吗,Kusho?"

    old "[protag], you hurt me. Is it really that hard for you to believe I might be that skilled?"
    new "[protag], you hurt me. Is it really that hard for you to believe I might be that skilled?\n[protag],你伤到我了。要你相信我这么厉害,真有那么难吗?"

    old "If you think that's unbelievable, you should be aware that this is nothing special. It's just my training routine."
    new "If you think that's unbelievable, you should be aware that this is nothing special. It's just my training routine.\n如果你觉得这难以置信,那你该知道,这根本不算什么。不过是我的日常训练。"

    old "Watch now!"
    new "Watch now!\n看好了!"

    old "Kusho closes his eyes, and shoots again with his bow. In the same instant, I spot a shadow, someone moving near the target."
    new "Kusho closes his eyes, and shoots again with his bow. In the same instant, I spot a shadow, someone moving near the target.\nKusho闭上眼睛,又用弓射了一箭。同一瞬间,我瞥见一个影子,有人在靶子附近移动。"

    old "Wha-?"
    new "Wha-?\n什——?"

    old "Everything happens so quickly that I don't have time to talk. Luckily, that mysterious red head girl casts a spell just in time and the arrows are pushed away from a gust of wind."
    new "Everything happens so quickly that I don't have time to talk. Luckily, that mysterious red head girl casts a spell just in time and the arrows are pushed away from a gust of wind.\n一切发生得太快,我根本来不及开口。幸好,那个神秘的红发女孩及时施了法术,箭被一阵风吹偏了。"

    old "Elder Myrth! You're all right? I'm sorry, I-"
    new "Elder Myrth! You're all right? I'm sorry, I-\nMyrth长老!你没事吧?对不起,我——"

    old "You were shooting arrows with your eyes closed."
    new "You were shooting arrows with your eyes closed.\n你刚才闭着眼睛射箭。"

    old "It was only a demonstration-"
    new "It was only a demonstration-\n那只是个演示——"

    old "Silence! My brother Rei is already giving me enough headaches. Don't do this again."
    new "Silence! My brother Rei is already giving me enough headaches. Don't do this again.\n住口!我哥哥Rei已经够让我头疼的了。别再有下次。"

    old "Of course. My apologies again."
    new "Of course. My apologies again.\n当然。再次向您道歉。"

    old "I look at her. Elder druid? Well, surely she doesn't look old."
    new "I look at her. Elder druid? Well, surely she doesn't look old.\n我看着她。德鲁伊长老?唔,她看起来确实一点也不老。"

    old "You must be the envoy from Grimoire everyone is talking about."
    new "You must be the envoy from Grimoire everyone is talking about.\n你一定就是人人都在谈论的那位Grimoire特使。"

    old "Pleasure, ehm...Elder Druid Myrth?"
    new "Pleasure, ehm...Elder Druid Myrth?\n幸会,呃……Myrth德鲁伊长老?"

    old "Just call me Myrth. I'm sorry, I need to go now, the other Elders are waiting."
    new "Just call me Myrth. I'm sorry, I need to go now, the other Elders are waiting.\n叫我Myrth就好。抱歉,我得走了,其他长老还在等着。"

    old "Well, that was...interesting. And no, I'm not talking about your skills demonstration."
    new "Well, that was...interesting. And no, I'm not talking about your skills demonstration.\n嗯,刚才真是……有趣。而且,不,我说的不是你的技艺演示。"

    old "Don't get any ideas. First, she's the only Elder Druid with that look. Second, her brother Rei is very jealous."
    new "Don't get any ideas. First, she's the only Elder Druid with that look. Second, her brother Rei is very jealous.\n别动歪脑筋。首先,她是唯一一位长得那般模样的德鲁伊长老。其次,她哥哥Rei醋劲大得很。"

    old "And I suppose he is also a skilled assassin like you?"
    new "And I suppose he is also a skilled assassin like you?\n我想,他也和你一样,是个技艺娴熟的刺客?"

    old "Pff. He only talks. He has no remarkable feats to his name yet."
    new "Pff. He only talks. He has no remarkable feats to his name yet.\n切。他只会耍嘴皮子。到目前还没有什么拿得出手的功绩。"

    old "Who knows. Maybe one day he'll be more famous than you."
    new "Who knows. Maybe one day he'll be more famous than you.\n谁知道呢。也许有朝一日他会比你更出名。"

    old "I doubt it."
    new "I doubt it.\n我表示怀疑。"

    old "Anyway, was nice talking with you and... looking at your demonstration, but now I need to go."
    new "Anyway, was nice talking with you and... looking at your demonstration, but now I need to go.\n总之,很高兴和你聊天,还有……欣赏你的演示,不过现在我得走了。"

    old "Just let me know when you need my skills, [protag]."
    new "Just let me know when you need my skills, [protag].\n需要我的本事时,说一声就行,[protag]。"

    old "I spot Kusho in the distance. Before I have a chance to call out to him, his eyes fix on me. From there, Kusho quickly makes his way towards me. Something's definitely going on. The urgency in Kusho's movements tell me that much."
    new "I spot Kusho in the distance. Before I have a chance to call out to him, his eyes fix on me. From there, Kusho quickly makes his way towards me. Something's definitely going on. The urgency in Kusho's movements tell me that much.\n我望见远处的Kusho。我还没来得及喊他,他的目光就锁定了我。接着,Kusho快步朝我走来。肯定出事了,Kusho动作中的急切说明了这一点。"

    old "This is a rare sight. A scared assassin isn't something you see every day."
    new "This is a rare sight. A scared assassin isn't something you see every day.\n这景象可真罕见。一个吓坏了的刺客,可不是天天都能见到的。"

    old "[protag], I am... in trouble."
    new "[protag], I am... in trouble.\n[protag],我……有麻烦了。"

    old "Okay. We'll figure this out, but first you need to tell me what's going on."
    new "Okay. We'll figure this out, but first you need to tell me what's going on.\n好。我们会想出办法的,但首先你得告诉我发生了什么。"

    old "Well, the short version of it is that someone wants me dead."
    new "Well, the short version of it is that someone wants me dead.\n嗯,简而言之,有人想要我死。"

    old "So, you're saying..."
    new "So, you're saying...\n所以,你是说……"

    old "Yes. Someone is paying to have me assassinated."
    new "Yes. Someone is paying to have me assassinated.\n对。有人出钱雇人暗杀我。"

    old "An assassin getting assassinated by another assassin."
    new "An assassin getting assassinated by another assassin.\n一个刺客被另一个刺客暗杀。"

    old "No. If I was just being hunted by one assassin, it wouldn't be a problem. There are three. And they happen to be the best dwarven assassins Hammerhands has to offer."
    new "No. If I was just being hunted by one assassin, it wouldn't be a problem. There are three. And they happen to be the best dwarven assassins Hammerhands has to offer.\n不。如果只有一个刺客在猎杀我,那倒不是问题。一共有三个。而且他们碰巧是Hammerhands最顶尖的矮人刺客。"

    old "Dwarven assassins?"
    new "Dwarven assassins?\n矮人刺客?"

    old "Why the surprise? They're small, agile. It's true that they can't run as fast as other races, but to be a good assassin you don't need to run. You need to stay hidden and move quietly."
    new "Why the surprise? They're small, agile. It's true that they can't run as fast as other races, but to be a good assassin you don't need to run. You need to stay hidden and move quietly.\n有什么好惊讶的?他们身材矮小、动作敏捷。他们确实跑得没别的种族快,但要当个好刺客,你不需要会跑。你需要的是藏得住、走得静。"

    old "You're sure about this though? How do you know they want you dead?"
    new "You're sure about this though? How do you know they want you dead?\n但你确定吗?你怎么知道他们想要你的命?"

    old "An aquaintance in Hammerhands owed me a favor and sent along a warning."
    new "An aquaintance in Hammerhands owed me a favor and sent along a warning.\nHammerhands的一个熟人欠我人情,给我递了警告。"

    old "And you trust this aquaintance?"
    new "And you trust this aquaintance?\n而这个熟人你信得过?"

    old "Kusho nods."
    new "Kusho nods.\nKusho点了点头。"

    old "The source is reliable. This threat is very real."
    new "The source is reliable. This threat is very real.\n消息来源可靠。这威胁千真万确。"

    old "All right, so what can I do to help?"
    new "All right, so what can I do to help?\n好,那我能帮上什么忙?"

    old "The only thing to do is to strike first. The three of them frequent a tavern-"
    new "The only thing to do is to strike first. The three of them frequent a tavern-\n唯一的办法是先下手为强。他们三个常去一家酒馆——"

    old "Oh, for the love of-- not a tavern in Hammerhands! I already have enough troubles there..."
    new "Oh, for the love of-- not a tavern in Hammerhands! I already have enough troubles there...\n哦,看在老天的份上——可别是Hammerhands的酒馆!我在那儿的麻烦已经够多了……"

    old "No, not in Hammerhands. In Thorga, a small settlement south of Hammerhands, near the Orcish Wastes border. We're going to go there, strike fast, and then slip away quietly. Nobody else needs to get hurt."
    new "No, not in Hammerhands. In Thorga, a small settlement south of Hammerhands, near the Orcish Wastes border. We're going to go there, strike fast, and then slip away quietly. Nobody else needs to get hurt.\n不,不在Hammerhands。在Thorga,Hammerhands南边的一个小村落,靠近Orcish Wastes边界。我们要去那儿,速战速决,然后悄悄撤离。不必再伤及任何人。"

    old "Okay. That sounds doable. I suppose I should bring help?"
    new "Okay. That sounds doable. I suppose I should bring help?\n好。听起来可行。我想我应该带些帮手?"

    old "I hate to admit it, but these three are good. Very good. Besides you and me, I think we should bring two more people."
    new "I hate to admit it, but these three are good. Very good. Besides you and me, I think we should bring two more people.\n我不想承认,但这三个人确实厉害,非常厉害。除了你和我,我想我们应该再带两个人。"

    old "I'll find a few people to help then. When we need to go?"
    new "I'll find a few people to help then. When we need to go?\n那我去找几个人来帮忙。我们什么时候出发?"

    old "As soon as possible. This needs to be done within three days or else I'll have to seek outside help. I'm sorry, but I can't wait any longer than that. I'm sure you can understand why."
    new "As soon as possible. This needs to be done within three days or else I'll have to seek outside help. I'm sorry, but I can't wait any longer than that. I'm sure you can understand why.\n越快越好。这事必须在三天内办成,否则我就得去外面求助了。抱歉,我不能再等更久了。我想你能理解其中缘由。"

    old "All right, Kusho. I'll see what I can do."
    new "All right, Kusho. I'll see what I can do.\n好的,Kusho。我看看能做什么。"

    old "We meet up with Kusho near Thorga and prepare for the mission."
    new "We meet up with Kusho near Thorga and prepare for the mission.\n我们在Thorga附近与Kusho会合,为任务做准备。"

    old "Thank you for coming."
    new "Thank you for coming.\n谢谢你们能来。"

    old "I still can't believe [protag] convinced me to come."
    new "I still can't believe [protag] convinced me to come.\n我到现在都不敢相信,[protag]竟说服了我来。"

    old "I've never killed a dwarf before. This should be fun."
    new "I've never killed a dwarf before. This should be fun.\n我还没杀过矮人呢。这应该会很有趣。"

    old "Ahem..."
    new "Ahem...\n咳咳……"

    old "Oh, um..."
    new "Oh, um...\n哦,呃……"

    old "Sylrissa... Please try to be more considerate of our other party members."
    new "Sylrissa... Please try to be more considerate of our other party members.\nSylrissa……请多体谅一下我们队里的其他成员。"

    old "Oops. Sorry, I mean evil dwarves. Totally, completely evil. Not like our team's adorable ones!"
    new "Oops. Sorry, I mean evil dwarves. Totally, completely evil. Not like our team's adorable ones!\n哎呀。抱歉,我是说邪恶的矮人。彻头彻尾的邪恶。才不像我们队里那些可爱的矮人呢!"

    old "Let's just get this over with. I don't like this."
    new "Let's just get this over with. I don't like this.\n我们快把这事了结吧。我不喜欢这样。"

    old "Agreed. There's no honor in what we're about to do. Kusho, consider yourself lucky that [protag] asked me. I wouldn't have come otherwise."
    new "Agreed. There's no honor in what we're about to do. Kusho, consider yourself lucky that [protag] asked me. I wouldn't have come otherwise.\n同意。我们接下来要做的事毫无荣誉可言。Kusho,算你走运,[protag]开口请了我。否则我是不会来的。"

    old "Remember, those dwarves are assassins. We're doing Aravorn a favor by killing them."
    new "Remember, those dwarves are assassins. We're doing Aravorn a favor by killing them.\n记住,那些矮人是刺客。杀了他们,是在帮Aravorn一个忙。"

    old "Killing three assassins to save the life of one... Perhaps it is a fair trade."
    new "Killing three assassins to save the life of one... Perhaps it is a fair trade.\n杀三个刺客,救一个人的命……也许还算公平的交易。"

    old "The air is so dry here... I'm not used to it."
    new "The air is so dry here... I'm not used to it.\n这里的空气好干燥……我有点不习惯。"

    old "It is rather uncomfortable. There aren't any nice smells here like there are back home either."
    new "It is rather uncomfortable. There aren't any nice smells here like there are back home either.\n确实挺难受的。这里也没有家乡那种好闻的气味。"

    old "There are so many things in the desert that can kill you. The air being dry should be the least of your concerns."
    new "There are so many things in the desert that can kill you. The air being dry should be the least of your concerns.\n沙漠里能要你命的东西多了去了。空气干燥,应该是最不该让你们操心的事。"

    old "Why, thank you, Nuala. That was very reassuring. I clearly made the correct choice when I agreed to tag along."
    new "Why, thank you, Nuala. That was very reassuring. I clearly made the correct choice when I agreed to tag along.\n哎呀,多谢你啊,Nuala。这话真让人安心。我当初同意跟着来,显然是个正确的决定。"

    old "Don't worry, Jasper, we won't be here long."
    new "Don't worry, Jasper, we won't be here long.\n别担心,Jasper,我们不会在这儿待太久的。"

    old "All right, listen. Here is the plan."
    new "All right, listen. Here is the plan.\n好,听我说。计划是这样的。"

    old "I have already scouted the village: it's a small hamlet, so not many people live here. There shouldn't be any problems getting inside the tavern, completing our objective, and escaping before anyone asks any questions."
    new "I have already scouted the village: it's a small hamlet, so not many people live here. There shouldn't be any problems getting inside the tavern, completing our objective, and escaping before anyone asks any questions.\n我已经侦察过那个村子了:它是个小村落,住的人不多。进入酒馆、完成任务,再在任何人起疑之前撤离,应该不成问题。"

    old "However, killing in a public place always carries a certain amount of risk."
    new "However, killing in a public place always carries a certain amount of risk.\n不过,在公共场所杀人,总伴随着一定的风险。"

    old "Is there another way?"
    new "Is there another way?\n还有别的办法吗?"

    old "Yes. A couple even. We could spread a rumor that I'm traveling here for some assignment. If done correctly, that might be enough to lure them outside of the village, near the desert."
    new "Yes. A couple even. We could spread a rumor that I'm traveling here for some assignment. If done correctly, that might be enough to lure them outside of the village, near the desert.\n有。甚至还有几个。我们可以散布谣言,说我是为某桩差事到此地来。若办得妥当,也许足以把他们引出村外,引到沙漠附近。"

    old "But they're not stupid. They might wonder why I am here, right when they have been hired to assassinate me. It would be very suspicious."
    new "But they're not stupid. They might wonder why I am here, right when they have been hired to assassinate me. It would be very suspicious.\n但他们不傻。他们可能会纳闷,为什么偏偏在他们受雇暗杀我的当口,我会出现在这里。那样就太可疑了。"

    old "I think we'd stand a better chance if [protag] goes to the tavern and pretends to be looking to hire some assassins."
    new "I think we'd stand a better chance if [protag] goes to the tavern and pretends to be looking to hire some assassins.\n我想,若让[protag]去酒馆,假装想雇几个刺客,我们的胜算会更大。"

    old "So you want me to pretend that I'm looking to use their 'services' myself?"
    new "So you want me to pretend that I'm looking to use their 'services' myself?\n所以你想让我假装,我自己也想用他们的“服务”?"

    old "You're the Envoy of Grimoire and you're moderately famous. They will smell money. Even if they haven't... finished their current task, they shouldn't be opposed to accepting another job."
    new "You're the Envoy of Grimoire and you're moderately famous. They will smell money. Even if they haven't... finished their current task, they shouldn't be opposed to accepting another job.\n你是Grimoire的特使,小有名气。他们会嗅到钱的味道。即便他们还没……完成手头的任务,也不至于拒绝再接一单。"

    old "Hm. Well, okay. I guess that sounds like it could work. And once I've 'hired' them, you want me to lure them outside where you'll be waiting to ambush them, right?"
    new "Hm. Well, okay. I guess that sounds like it could work. And once I've 'hired' them, you want me to lure them outside where you'll be waiting to ambush them, right?\n嗯。好吧,我想这听起来可行。而一旦我“雇”下他们,你就想让我把他们引到外面,你埋伏在那里,对吧?"

    old "Exactly. So, [protag], what do you think is the best strategy?"
    new "Exactly. So, [protag], what do you think is the best strategy?\n正是。那么,[protag],你觉得最佳策略是什么?"

    old "I still think attacking them in the tavern is our best option."
    new "I still think attacking them in the tavern is our best option.\n我仍认为在酒馆里动手是我们最好的选择。"

    old "Both the authorities of Hammerhands and of the Empire will think it's just another tavern brawl that ended badly. Nobody will ask any questions."
    new "Both the authorities of Hammerhands and of the Empire will think it's just another tavern brawl that ended badly. Nobody will ask any questions.\nHammerhands和帝国的当局,都会以为这不过是又一场收场糟糕的酒馆斗殴。没人会问东问西。"

    old "We just have to make sure no innocents are harmed in the process."
    new "We just have to make sure no innocents are harmed in the process.\n我们只需确保过程中没有无辜者受到伤害。"

    old "Your plan sounds good enough to me."
    new "Your plan sounds good enough to me.\n你的计划对我来说足够好了。"

    old "They probably don't know that you work for me-- or that we even know each other. They shouldn't suspect anything. We can strike them by surprise this way."
    new "They probably don't know that you work for me-- or that we even know each other. They shouldn't suspect anything. We can strike them by surprise this way.\n他们多半不知道你为我做事——甚至不知道我们彼此认识。他们不该起疑。这样我们就能出其不意地袭击他们。"

    old "Then it's decided. We'll wait until nightfall and then execute the plan."
    new "Then it's decided. We'll wait until nightfall and then execute the plan.\n那就这么定了。我们等到天黑,再执行计划。"

    old "One last thing: they're famous assassins, so they're likely to be well equipped."
    new "One last thing: they're famous assassins, so they're likely to be well equipped.\n最后一件事:他们是出名的刺客,所以很可能装备精良。"

    old "Ooh. Let's hope they have some nice rings!"
    new "Ooh. Let's hope they have some nice rings!\n哦哦。但愿他们戴着些漂亮的戒指!"

    old "Good. More loot for us."
    new "Good. More loot for us.\n好。更多战利品归我们了。"

    old "Gasp. Let's hope they're not too well-equipped for us!"
    new "Gasp. Let's hope they're not too well-equipped for us!\n天哪。但愿他们的装备别好到我们对付不了!"

    old "Equipment means nothing if you aren't skilled enough to use it."
    new "Equipment means nothing if you aren't skilled enough to use it.\n若你技艺不够,装备再精良也白搭。"

    old "That decided, we wait. Once darkness falls over the small hamlet, we put our plan in motion."
    new "That decided, we wait. Once darkness falls over the small hamlet, we put our plan in motion.\n商议既定,我们开始等待。等夜幕笼罩小村,我们便付诸行动。"

    old "We enter the tavern. Kusho immediately spots the three dwarves amongst the crowd."
    new "We enter the tavern. Kusho immediately spots the three dwarves amongst the crowd.\n我们走进酒馆。Kusho立刻在人群中认出了那三个矮人。"

    old "I walk across the room and make my way to the bartender."
    new "I walk across the room and make my way to the bartender.\n我穿过房间,走向吧台后的酒保。"

    old "Ahem. Excuse me. I was told that this tavern was a place where I'd be able to find people with... 'special talents'."
    new "Ahem. Excuse me. I was told that this tavern was a place where I'd be able to find people with... 'special talents'.\n咳咳。打扰一下。有人告诉我,这家酒馆是个能找着有……“特殊才能”之人的地方。"

    old "The bartender doesn't reply verbally. Instead, he subtly nods and looks behind me."
    new "The bartender doesn't reply verbally. Instead, he subtly nods and looks behind me.\n酒保没有出声回答,而是微微点头,并朝我身后看去。"

    old "I look over my shoulder and follow his gaze to a scantily clad woman in the far corner. I blush a bright red as I realize what the bartender thought I meant."
    new "I look over my shoulder and follow his gaze to a scantily clad woman in the far corner. I blush a bright red as I realize what the bartender thought I meant.\n我扭头顺着他的目光,望向远处角落里一个衣着暴露的女子。意识到酒保以为我是什么意思后,我的脸涨得通红。"

    old "Er, that's not... Um, I'm sure she's very talented, but I was looking for... a different talent. More of a practical..."
    new "Er, that's not... Um, I'm sure she's very talented, but I was looking for... a different talent. More of a practical...\n呃,不是那个……嗯,我相信她确实很有才华,但我要找的是……另一种才能。更实际一点的……"

    old "Oh, screw it. I'll be more direct."
    new "Oh, screw it. I'll be more direct.\n哦,去他的。我直说好了。"

    old "I need someone who is good at making problems disappear. Understand?"
    new "I need someone who is good at making problems disappear. Understand?\n我需要一个擅长让麻烦消失的人。明白吗?"

    old "Once more, the bartender responds with a nod and a look. This time, however, he seems to get my meaning as he directs me towards the dwarves."
    new "Once more, the bartender responds with a nod and a look. This time, however, he seems to get my meaning as he directs me towards the dwarves.\n酒保再次以点头和眼神回应。不过这一次,他似乎明白了我的意思,把我引向了那几个矮人。"

    old "Hm. Never thought we'd run into someone like you here of all places."
    new "Hm. Never thought we'd run into someone like you here of all places.\n嗯。真没想到,会在这地方撞见你这号人物。"

    old "Question is, what does the Envoy of Grimoire wants from the likes of us?"
    new "Question is, what does the Envoy of Grimoire wants from the likes of us?\n问题是,Grimoire的特使,想从我们这种人这儿得到什么?"

    old "I see that you know me."
    new "I see that you know me.\n看来你们认得我。"

    old "We know a lot of things."
    new "We know a lot of things.\n我们知道的事多了。"

    old "Hopefully that works in my favor."
    new "Hopefully that works in my favor.\n但愿那对我有利。"

    old "Then you know I'm currently dealing with the situation at N'Mar. Unfortunately, that's not the only business I find myself needing to take care of."
    new "Then you know I'm currently dealing with the situation at N'Mar. Unfortunately, that's not the only business I find myself needing to take care of.\n那你们也知道,我目前正在处理N'Mar的局势。可惜,那不是我需要操办的唯一一桩事。"

    old "I take it that this other business is unofficial business?"
    new "I take it that this other business is unofficial business?\n我猜,这另一桩事,是非官方的?"

    old "You could call it that, yes."
    new "You could call it that, yes.\n你可以这么说,没错。"

    old "I would be happy to tell you more if you'd be willing to follow me back to my tent. I don't like to speak openly in taverns."
    new "I would be happy to tell you more if you'd be willing to follow me back to my tent. I don't like to speak openly in taverns.\n如果你们愿意跟我回我的帐篷,我很乐意多告诉你们一些。我不喜欢在酒馆里公开谈事。"

    old "Neither do we. You never know who might be eavesdropping."
    new "Neither do we. You never know who might be eavesdropping.\n我们也是。谁知道会不会有人在偷听。"

    old "I head outside with the three dwarves in tow. I must admit that the thought of turning my back to such dangerous people sends a chill down my spine."
    new "I head outside with the three dwarves in tow. I must admit that the thought of turning my back to such dangerous people sends a chill down my spine.\n我带着三个矮人朝外走。我必须承认,一想到背对着这么危险的人物,我的脊背就一阵发凉。"

    old "We're almost there."
    new "We're almost there.\n我们快到了。"

    old "As I talk, I spot Kusho sneaking behind them. His movements are completely silent as far as I can tell, but somehow one of the dwarves still manages to notice him."
    new "As I talk, I spot Kusho sneaking behind them. His movements are completely silent as far as I can tell, but somehow one of the dwarves still manages to notice him.\n我一边说着,一边瞥见Kusho悄悄潜到他们身后。就我所能分辨,他的动作毫无声息,可不知怎的,其中一个矮人还是察觉到了他。"

